INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glenmoril_witches', 'The Glenmoril Wyrd, also known as the Glenmoril Coven or Glenmoril Witches, is a loose network of female-dominated Bretonic covens scattered across Tamriel. Revering nature and often associating with Daedric Princes like Hircine, the Wyrd enforces laws of nature known only to them, frequently leaning into its darker aspects. Their members, while primarily human, sometimes include beastfolk like hagravens and lamias, who often hold leadership roles. These covens are known for their unique practices, such as curing lycanthropy and vampirism, and their ability to transform into animals, including wolves and ravens. Historically linked to the Druids of Galen, the Glenmoril Wyrd broke away due to differing philosophies, choosing to live as reclusive protectors of the wilds. They see themselves as part of nature itself, drawing their power from the land and maintaining a delicate balance between life and death.

The covens are spread across regions such as High Rock, Skyrim, and Bangkorai, each with distinct beliefs and practices. While many covens venerate Hircine, others align with Daedric Princes like Namira or Molag Bal, creating both alliances and rivalries with groups like the Reachmen. The Glenmoril Wyrd has been influential in major events throughout history, such as assisting in the Bloodmoon Prophecy on Solstheim and making a pact with the Companions of Whiterun that introduced lycanthropy into their ranks. Over time, some covens have dwindled, such as the hagraven-led Glenmoril witches in Falkreath Hold, who became the last of their kind in Skyrim by the Fourth Era. Despite their mysterious and often dark reputation, the Glenmoril Wyrd remains a significant force in Tamriel, embodying the raw, untamed power of nature and its enduring connection to the supernatural.', '''abil'':87B ''across'':26B,148B ''align'':169B ''allianc'':180B ''also'':6B ''anim'':91B ''aspect'':53B ''assist'':201B ''associ'':32B ''away'':107B ''bal'':177B ''balanc'':139B ''bangkorai'':156B ''beastfolk'':61B ''becam'':241B ''belief'':160B ''bloodmoon'':204B ''breton'':23B ''broke'':106B ''choos'':112B ''companion'':214B ''connect'':279B ''coven'':11B,24B,72B,145B,165B,226B ''creat'':178B ''cure'':81B ''daedric'':34B,171B ''dark'':258B ''darker'':52B ''death'':143B ''delic'':138B ''despit'':253B ''differ'':110B ''distinct'':159B ''domin'':22B ''draw'':129B ''druid'':100B ''due'':108B ''dwindl'':228B ''embodi'':269B ''endur'':278B ''enforc'':40B ''era'':252B ''event'':196B ''falkreath'':238B ''femal'':21B ''female-domin'':20B ''forc'':266B ''fourth'':251B ''frequent'':48B ''galen'':102B ''glenmoril'':1A,4B,10B,13B,104B,189B,235B,261B ''group'':184B ''hagraven'':63B,233B ''hagraven-l'':232B ''high'':152B ''hircin'':37B,167B ''histor'':96B ''histori'':198B ''hold'':68B,239B ''human'':58B ''includ'':60B,92B ''influenti'':193B ''introduc'':218B ''kind'':246B ''known'':7B,44B,74B ''lamia'':65B ''land'':134B ''last'':243B ''law'':41B ''leadership'':69B ''lean'':49B ''led'':234B ''life'':141B ''like'':36B,62B,173B,185B ''link'':97B ''live'':114B ''loos'':17B ''lycanthropi'':82B,219B ''maintain'':136B ''major'':195B ''make'':209B ''mani'':164B ''member'':55B ''molag'':176B ''mysteri'':255B ''namira'':174B ''natur'':29B,43B,127B,275B ''network'':18B ''often'':31B,67B,257B ''other'':168B ''pact'':211B ''part'':125B ''philosophi'':111B ''power'':131B,273B ''practic'':78B,162B ''primarili'':57B ''princ'':35B,172B ''propheci'':205B ''protector'':117B ''rank'':222B ''raven'':95B ''raw'':271B ''reachmen'':187B ''reclus'':116B ''region'':149B ''remain'':263B ''reput'':259B ''rever'':28B ''rivalri'':182B ''rock'':153B ''role'':70B ''scatter'':25B ''see'':122B ''signific'':265B ''skyrim'':154B,248B ''solstheim'':207B ''sometim'':59B ''spread'':147B ''supernatur'':282B ''tamriel'':27B,268B ''throughout'':197B ''time'':224B ''transform'':89B ''uniqu'':77B ''untam'':272B ''vampir'':84B ''vener'':166B ''whiterun'':216B ''wild'':120B ''witch'':2A,14B,236B ''wolv'':93B ''wyrd'':5B,39B,105B,190B,262B', 'scholar,breton, wtich, forsworn', 'The Glenmoril Wyrd, or Glenmoril Coven, is a network of female-dominated Bretonic covens across Tamriel, known for their reverence of nature and association with Daedric Princes like Hircine. These covens, often led by beastfolk such as hagravens, practice unique rites like curing lycanthropy and vampirism and shape-shifting into animals. Originally linked to the Druids of Galen, they became reclusive protectors of the wilds. Their covens, spread across High Rock, Skyrim, and Bangkorai, are influenced by various Daedric Princes, creating both alliances and rivalries. They played key roles in events like the Bloodmoon Prophecy and the introduction of lycanthropy to the Companions of Whiterun. Despite their decline, the Glenmoril Wyrd remains a powerful and mysterious force tied to the natural and supernatural realms.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('namira_rot', 'Namira''s Rot is a brown capped fungus found on cave floors, named after the Daedric Prince Namira. Alchemy effects: Damage Magicka, Fortify Lockpicking, Fear, and Regenerate Health.', '''alchemi'':21B ''brown'':8B ''cap'':9B ''cave'':13B ''daedric'':18B ''damag'':23B ''effect'':22B ''fear'':27B ''floor'':14B ''fortifi'':25B ''found'':11B ''fungus'':10B ''health'':30B ''lockpick'':26B ''magicka'':24B ''name'':15B ''namira'':1A,3B,20B ''princ'':19B ''regener'':29B ''rot'':2A,5B', 'alchemist', 'Namira''s Rot is a brown capped fungus found on cave floors, named after the Daedric Prince Namira. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tundra_cotton', 'Tundra Cotton is a plant that mostly grows in the plains of Whiterun Hold, known for its resilience in the region''s climate. It is a common ingredient in potions that fortify magicka and resist spells, often valued for its subtle yet effective properties. Alchemy effects: Resist Magic, Fortify Magicka, Fortify Block, and Fortify Barter.', '''alchemi'':47B ''barter'':57B ''block'':54B ''climat'':25B ''common'':29B ''cotton'':2A,4B ''effect'':45B,48B ''fortifi'':34B,51B,53B,56B ''grow'':10B ''hold'':16B ''ingredi'':30B ''known'':17B ''magic'':50B ''magicka'':35B,52B ''most'':9B ''often'':39B ''plain'':13B ''plant'':7B ''potion'':32B ''properti'':46B ''region'':23B ''resili'':20B ''resist'':37B,49B ''spell'':38B ''subtl'':43B ''tundra'':1A,3B ''valu'':40B ''whiterun'':15B ''yet'':44B', 'alchemist', 'Tundra Cotton is a plant that mostly grows in the plains of Whiterun Hold, known for its resilience in the region''s climate. It is a common ingredient in potions that fortify magicka and resist spells, often valued for its subtle yet effective properties. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('su_grah_dun', 'Elemental Fury is a Shout that imbues your arms with the speed of wind, allowing for faster weapon strikes. The three words of power in this Shout are Su (Air), which grants you the swiftness of wind; Grah (Battle), which enhances your combat prowess; and Dun (Grace), which allows for more fluid and rapid attacks.', '''air'':33B ''allow'':18B,52B ''arm'':12B ''attack'':58B ''battl'':42B ''combat'':46B ''dun'':3A,49B ''element'':4B ''enhanc'':44B ''faster'':20B ''fluid'':55B ''furi'':5B ''grace'':50B ''grah'':2A,41B ''grant'':35B ''imbu'':10B ''power'':27B ''prowess'':47B ''rapid'':57B ''shout'':8B,30B ''speed'':15B ''strike'':22B ''su'':1A,32B ''swift'':38B ''three'':24B ''weapon'':21B ''wind'':17B,40B ''word'':25B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('summon_durnehviir', 'Summon Durnehviir is a Shout that calls upon Durnehviir, summoning him from the Soul Cairn to aid you in your time of need. The three words of power in this Shout are Dur (Curse), which invokes the dark power of the Soul Cairn; Neh (Never), which calls Durnehviir from his eternal rest; and Viir (Dying), which brings him forth from the afterlife to fight alongside you.', '''afterlif'':64B ''aid'':19B ''alongsid'':67B ''bring'':59B ''cairn'':17B,45B ''call'':9B,49B ''curs'':36B ''dark'':40B ''die'':57B ''dur'':35B ''durnehviir'':2A,4B,11B,50B ''etern'':53B ''fight'':66B ''forth'':61B ''invok'':38B ''need'':25B ''neh'':46B ''never'':47B ''power'':30B,41B ''rest'':54B ''shout'':7B,33B ''soul'':16B,44B ''summon'':1A,3B,12B ''three'':27B ''time'':23B ''upon'':10B ''viir'':56B ''word'':28B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwemer_sphere', 'Dwarven Spheres, also referred to as Centurion Spheres or Dwarven Centurions, are formidable automatons crafted by the Dwemer, known for their agility and combat strength. These constructs typically patrol ancient ruins in a spherical form, remaining dormant until they detect intruders. Upon encountering an opponent, they emerge from their protective shells to engage in combat.', '''agil'':24B ''also'':5B ''ancient'':32B ''automaton'':16B ''centurion'':9B,13B ''combat'':26B,57B ''construct'':29B ''craft'':17B ''detect'':42B ''dormant'':39B ''dwarven'':3B,12B ''dwemer'':1A,20B ''emerg'':49B ''encount'':45B ''engag'':55B ''form'':37B ''formid'':15B ''intrud'':43B ''known'':21B ''oppon'':47B ''patrol'':31B ''protect'':52B ''refer'':6B ''remain'':38B ''ruin'':33B ''shell'':53B ''sphere'':2A,4B,10B ''spheric'':36B ''strength'':27B ''typic'':30B ''upon'':44B', 'dwemer', '
Dwarven Spheres are powerful automatons created by the Dwemer, that will attack anyone foolish enough to enter a dwemer ruin.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glow_dust', 'Glow Dust is a glowing green dust  found on dead wisps and wispmothers, along with wisp wrappings, and is valued for its magical properties. Alchemy effects: Damage Magicka, Damage Magicka Regen, Fortify Destruction, and Resist Shock.', '''alchemi'':27B ''along'':16B ''damag'':29B,31B ''dead'':12B ''destruct'':35B ''dust'':2A,4B,9B ''effect'':28B ''fortifi'':34B ''found'':10B ''glow'':1A,3B,7B ''green'':8B ''magic'':25B ''magicka'':30B,32B ''properti'':26B ''regen'':33B ''resist'':37B ''shock'':38B ''valu'':22B ''wisp'':13B,18B ''wispmoth'':15B ''wrap'':19B', 'alchemist', 'Glow Dust is a glowing green dust  found on dead wisps and wispmothers, along with wisp wrappings, and is valued for its magical properties. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('slaughterfish', 'Slaughterfish are aggressive predatory fish found in diverse aquatic environments across Nirn. Known for their sharp teeth and swift, lethal attacks, they form dense schools and grow exceptionally large when well-fed. Variants such as the Rumare Slaughterfish, Blind Slaughterfish, and the legendary Crab-Slaughter-Crane highlight their adaptability. While their bites can cause severe injuries and transmit diseases like Greenspore, slaughterfish are valuable for their alchemical properties, crafting materials, and culinary uses. Regions like Vvardenfell consume their dried scales as treats, while Nords favor stone-cooked slaughterfish as a delicacy. Their prevalence has spurred preventative measures, such as enchanted bobbers and repellents, reflecting their dual role as both a threat and a resource in Tamrielic life.', '''across'':12B ''adapt'':52B ''aggress'':4B ''alchem'':70B ''aquat'':10B ''attack'':22B ''bite'':55B ''blind'':41B ''bobber'':105B ''caus'':57B ''consum'':80B ''cook'':91B ''crab'':47B ''crab-slaughter-cran'':46B ''craft'':72B ''crane'':49B ''culinari'':75B ''delicaci'':95B ''dens'':25B ''diseas'':62B ''divers'':9B ''dri'':82B ''dual'':110B ''enchant'':104B ''environ'':11B ''except'':29B ''favor'':88B ''fed'':34B ''fish'':6B ''form'':24B ''found'':7B ''greenspor'':64B ''grow'':28B ''highlight'':50B ''injuri'':59B ''known'':14B ''larg'':30B ''legendari'':45B ''lethal'':21B ''life'':121B ''like'':63B,78B ''materi'':73B ''measur'':101B ''nirn'':13B ''nord'':87B ''predatori'':5B ''preval'':97B ''prevent'':100B ''properti'':71B ''reflect'':108B ''region'':77B ''repel'':107B ''resourc'':118B ''role'':111B ''rumar'':39B ''scale'':83B ''school'':26B ''sever'':58B ''sharp'':17B ''slaughter'':48B ''slaughterfish'':1A,2B,40B,42B,65B,92B ''spur'':99B ''stone'':90B ''stone-cook'':89B ''swift'':20B ''tamriel'':120B ''teeth'':18B ''threat'':115B ''transmit'':61B ''treat'':85B ''use'':76B ''valuabl'':67B ''variant'':35B ''vvardenfel'':79B ''well'':33B ''well-f'':32B', 'hunter', 'Slaughterfish are small, aggressive aquatic predators found in nearly all waters of Nirn. Recognizable by their razor-sharp teeth, these fish often swim in large groups, quickly overwhelming and attacking unsuspecting prey.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('scrib_jelly', 'Scrib Jelly, a red jelly originating from Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Fortify Stamina, Paralysis, and Waterbreathing.', '''alchemi'':21B ''caravan'':20B ''effect'':22B ''fortifi'':25B ''ingredi'':13B ''jelli'':2A,4B,7B ''khajiit'':19B ''origin'':8B ''paralysi'':27B ''purchas'':17B ''red'':6B ''restor'':23B ''scrib'':1A,3B ''stamina'':24B,26B ''vvardenfel'':10B ''waterbreath'':29B', 'alchemist', 'Scrib Jelly, a red jelly originating from Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chicken_egg', 'Chicken''s Eggs can be harvested from chickens'' nests, commonly found at most farms. Alchemy effects: Resist Magic, Damage Magicka Regen, Waterbreathing, and Lingering Damage Stamina.', '''alchemi'':17B ''chicken'':1A,3B,10B ''common'':12B ''damag'':21B,27B ''effect'':18B ''egg'':2A,5B ''farm'':16B ''found'':13B ''harvest'':8B ''linger'':26B ''magic'':20B ''magicka'':22B ''nest'':11B ''regen'':23B ''resist'':19B ''stamina'':28B ''waterbreath'':24B', 'alchemist', 'Chicken''s Eggs can be harvested from chickens'' nests, commonly found at most farms 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('niranye''s_house', 'Niranye''s House is a large, single-story residence located in Windhelm, immediately to the east of the main city gates. The rear of the house is part of the city''s surrounding walls. It features a small yard between the side entrance and Calixto''s House of Curiosities.', '''calixto'':49B ''citi'':24B,35B ''curios'':53B ''east'':20B ''entranc'':47B ''featur'':40B ''gate'':25B ''hous'':3A,6B,30B,51B ''immedi'':17B ''larg'':9B ''locat'':14B ''main'':23B ''nirany'':1A,4B ''part'':32B ''rear'':27B ''resid'':13B ''side'':46B ''singl'':11B ''single-stori'':10B ''small'':42B ''stori'':12B ''surround'':37B ''wall'':38B ''windhelm'':16B ''yard'':43B', 'eastmarch', 'Niranye''s House is a large, single-story residence located in Windhelm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_the_knight', 'This potion bolsters the wearer''s proficiency in heavy armor, enhancing resilience and durability in combat. Improves heavy armor skills slightly, with stronger potions offering greater boosts to resilience in battle. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':47B ''armor'':14B,23B ''battl'':35B ''bolster'':7B ''boost'':31B ''combat'':20B ''draught'':57B ''durabl'':18B ''elixir'':60B ''enhanc'':15B ''found'':40B ''greater'':30B ''heavi'':13B,22B ''improv'':21B ''knight'':4A ''loot'':43B ''offer'':29B ''philter'':58B ''potion'':1A,6B,28B,37B,56B ''profici'':11B ''purchas'':45B ''random'':42B ''resili'':16B,33B ''sever'':50B ''skill'':24B ''slight'':25B ''stronger'':27B ''strongest'':55B ''tier'':51B ''weakest'':53B ''wearer'':9B', 'warrior, alchemist, companions, guard', 'The Potion of the Knight boosts heavy armor skills, improving resilience in combat. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_illusion', 'A mage''s tool for manipulation, this potion amplifies the effects of illusion magic, making spells of fear, calm, and frenzy more effective. Slightly enhances illusion magic, with higher-grade potions providing significant boosts to manipulation spells. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':53B ''amplifi'':12B ''boost'':38B ''calm'':22B ''draught'':63B ''effect'':14B,26B ''elixir'':66B ''enhanc'':28B ''fear'':21B ''found'':46B ''frenzi'':24B ''grade'':34B ''higher'':33B ''higher-grad'':32B ''illus'':3A,16B,29B ''loot'':49B ''mage'':5B ''magic'':17B,30B ''make'':18B ''manipul'':9B,40B ''philter'':64B ''potion'':1A,11B,35B,43B,62B ''provid'':36B ''purchas'':51B ''random'':48B ''sever'':56B ''signific'':37B ''slight'':27B ''spell'':19B,41B ''strongest'':61B ''tier'':57B ''tool'':7B ''weakest'':59B', 'mage, alchemist, scholar, collegeofwinterhold, psijic', 'The Potion of Illusion makes manipulation spells like fear and calm more effective. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mort_flesh', 'Mort Flesh, rotting human flesh originating from Cyrodiil, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. You are bewildered why they would see this in Skyrim. Alchemy effects: Damage Health, Damage Magicka, Damage Magicka Regen, and Frenzy.', '''alchemi'':31B ''bewild'':23B ''caravan'':20B ''cyrodiil'':10B ''damag'':33B,35B,37B ''effect'':32B ''flesh'':2A,4B,7B ''frenzi'':41B ''health'':34B ''human'':6B ''ingredi'':13B ''khajiit'':19B ''magicka'':36B,38B ''mort'':1A,3B ''origin'':8B ''purchas'':17B ''regen'':39B ''rot'':5B ''see'':27B ''skyrim'':30B ''would'':26B', 'alchemist', 'Mort Flesh, rotting human flesh originating from Cyrodiil, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. You are bewildered why they would see this in Skyrim.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cyrodilic_spadetail', 'Cyrodilic Spadetail are long brown fish found around Skyrim and can be caught with your hands. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Damage Stamina, Fortify Restoration, Fear and Ravage Health.', '''around'':10B ''brown'':7B ''caught'':15B ''cyrodil'':1A,3B ''damag'':32B ''effect'':29B ''fear'':36B ''fish'':8B ''fortifi'':34B ''found'':9B ''hand'':18B ''health'':39B ''ingredi'':23B ''long'':6B ''make'':26B ''offer'':28B ''potion'':25B ''ravag'':38B ''restor'':35B ''skyrim'':11B ''spadetail'':2A,4B ''stamina'':33B ''use'':20B', 'fisher', 'Cyrodilic Spadetail are long brown fish found around Skyrim.  You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('telekinesis', 'Telekinesis is an Alteration spell that allows the caster to lift, move, and manipulate objects from a distance. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':23B ''allow'':8B ''alter'':5B ''cast'':27B ''caster'':10B ''distanc'':19B ''level'':25B ''lift'':12B ''manipul'':15B ''move'':13B ''object'':16B ''requir'':21B ''skill'':24B ''spell'':6B ''telekinesi'':1A,2B', 'mage', 'Telekinesis is a spell that lets the caster move things from far away, like lifting objects or pulling them closer without touching them. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dark_brotherhood', 'The Dark Brotherhood is a clandestine guild of assassins in Skyrim, renowned for carrying out murders for hire. Historically powerful, the guild has seen a significant decline in recent years. Unlike the more legally sanctioned Morag Tong in Morrowind, the Dark Brotherhood operates entirely outside the law, often feared and loathed by the general population. The organization was traditionally led by the Night Mother, but in Skyrim, Astrid has assumed control. The Brotherhood''s operations are based out of their Sanctuary, hidden deep within the wilderness, and they maintain a connection with the Thieves Guild in Riften.', '''assassin'':11B ''assum'':72B ''astrid'':70B ''base'':79B ''brotherhood'':2A,5B,44B,75B ''carri'':16B ''clandestin'':8B ''connect'':93B ''control'':73B ''dark'':1A,4B,43B ''declin'':29B ''deep'':85B ''entir'':46B ''fear'':51B ''general'':56B ''guild'':9B,24B,97B ''hidden'':84B ''hire'':20B ''histor'':21B ''law'':49B ''led'':62B ''legal'':36B ''loath'':53B ''maintain'':91B ''morag'':38B ''morrowind'':41B ''mother'':66B ''murder'':18B ''night'':65B ''often'':50B ''oper'':45B,77B ''organ'':59B ''outsid'':47B ''popul'':57B ''power'':22B ''recent'':31B ''renown'':14B ''riften'':99B ''sanction'':37B ''sanctuari'':83B ''seen'':26B ''signific'':28B ''skyrim'':13B,69B ''thiev'':96B ''tong'':39B ''tradit'':61B ''unlik'':33B ''wilder'':88B ''within'':86B ''year'':32B', 'darkbrotherhood', 'The Dark Brotherhood is a secretive guild of assassins in Skyrim, specializing in murder-for-hire. Once powerful, it has declined in recent years and operates outside the law, feared by many. They are known to send notes with vague threats with a blackhand drawn on them. It is also rumored that you can summon the Dark Brotherhood to perform an assination using a secret dark ritual.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sload_soap', 'Sload Soap, a grey soap popular in Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Resist Fire, Fear, Fortify Conjuration, and Fortify Alteration.', '''alchemi'':21B ''alter'':30B ''caravan'':20B ''conjur'':27B ''effect'':22B ''fear'':25B ''fire'':24B ''fortifi'':26B,29B ''grey'':6B ''ingredi'':13B ''khajiit'':19B ''popular'':8B ''purchas'':17B ''resist'':23B ''sload'':1A,3B ''soap'':2A,4B,7B ''vvardenfel'':10B', 'alchemist', 'Sload Soap, a grey soap popular in Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('oakflesh', 'Oakflesh is an Alteration spell that increases the caster''s armor rating for a short duration, providing additional protection. It requires a Novice skill level to cast.', '''addit'':19B ''alter'':5B ''armor'':12B ''cast'':28B ''caster'':10B ''durat'':17B ''increas'':8B ''level'':26B ''novic'':24B ''oakflesh'':1A,2B ''protect'':20B ''provid'':18B ''rate'':13B ''requir'':22B ''short'':16B ''skill'':25B ''spell'':6B', 'mage', 'Oakflesh is a spell that makes the caster''s skin tougher, like armor, for a little while, helping them take less damage in a fight. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('riverwood', 'Riverwood is a small milling town in southern Whiterun Hold, nestled at the foot of the Throat of the World and situated along the banks of the White River. Located just south of Whiterun and east of Bleak Falls Barrow.

Despite its modest size, Riverwood offers essential facilities, including a sawmill, a general goods store known as the Riverwood Trader, and the Sleeping Giant Inn, a cozy tavern ideal for rest and socializing.', '''along'':24B ''bank'':26B ''barrow'':41B ''bleak'':39B ''cozi'':68B ''despit'':42B ''east'':37B ''essenti'':48B ''facil'':49B ''fall'':40B ''foot'':15B ''general'':54B ''giant'':65B ''good'':55B ''hold'':11B ''ideal'':70B ''includ'':50B ''inn'':66B ''known'':57B ''locat'':31B ''mill'':6B ''modest'':44B ''nestl'':12B ''offer'':47B ''rest'':72B ''river'':30B ''riverwood'':1A,2B,46B,60B ''sawmil'':52B ''situat'':23B ''size'':45B ''sleep'':64B ''small'':5B ''social'':74B ''south'':33B ''southern'':9B ''store'':56B ''tavern'':69B ''throat'':18B ''town'':7B ''trader'':61B ''white'':29B ''whiterun'':10B,35B ''world'':21B', 'whiterun', 'Riverwood is a small milling town in southern Whiterun Hold, nestled at the foot of the Throat of the World and situated along the banks of the White River. Located just south of Whiterun and east of Bleak Falls Barrow.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragontooth_crater', 'Dragontooth Crater is a dragon lair located north-northwest of Karthwasten and southwest of Harmugstahl in the Reach. The lair is perched atop a mountain, making it a prominent landmark in the rugged terrain.

To reach Dragontooth Crater from Karthwasten, navigate east around the mountain and approach the site from the north.', '''approach'':50B ''around'':46B ''atop'':26B ''crater'':2A,4B,41B ''dragon'':7B ''dragontooth'':1A,3B,40B ''east'':45B ''harmugstahl'':18B ''karthwasten'':14B,43B ''lair'':8B,23B ''landmark'':33B ''locat'':9B ''make'':29B ''mountain'':28B,48B ''navig'':44B ''north'':11B,55B ''north-northwest'':10B ''northwest'':12B ''perch'':25B ''promin'':32B ''reach'':21B,39B ''rug'':36B ''site'':52B ''southwest'':16B ''terrain'':37B', 'reach', 'Dragontooth Crater is a dragon lair located north-northwest of Karthwasten in the Reach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cod', 'Cod are a large yellow fish found in freezing waters during any weather. They can be eaten with a mild, delicate, and slightly sweet flavor with a flaky texture.', '''cod'':1A,2B ''delic'':22B ''eaten'':18B ''fish'':7B ''flaki'':29B ''flavor'':26B ''found'':8B ''freez'':10B ''larg'':5B ''mild'':21B ''slight'':24B ''sweet'':25B ''textur'':30B ''water'':11B ''weather'':14B ''yellow'':6B', 'fisher', 'Cod are a large yellow fish. They can be eaten with a mild, delicate, and slightly sweet flavor with a flaky texture. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chillfurrow_farm', 'Chillfurrow Farm is a modest agricultural holding located just east of Whiterun, south of Battle-Born Farm, nestled within the fertile lands of Whiterun Hold. Owned by the affluent but often absent Nazeem, the farm''s daily operations are entrusted to Wilmuth, a hardworking caretaker who resides in the farmhouse.

Despite Nazeem’s lack of presence, Chillfurrow Farm is well-maintained, with a Whiterun Guard stationed on-site to ensure its security. Another guard regularly patrols the yard, reflecting its importance as part of the region''s agricultural network. The farm stands as a quiet yet vital contributor to the prosperity of Whiterun Hold, its fields and farmhouse embodying the steady rhythm of Skyrim’s agrarian life.', '''absent'':35B ''affluent'':32B ''agrarian'':119B ''agricultur'':8B,92B ''anoth'':77B ''battl'':18B ''battle-born'':17B ''born'':19B ''caretak'':48B ''chillfurrow'':1A,3B,59B ''contributor'':102B ''daili'':40B ''despit'':54B ''east'':12B ''embodi'':113B ''ensur'':74B ''entrust'':43B ''farm'':2A,4B,20B,38B,60B,95B ''farmhous'':53B,112B ''fertil'':24B ''field'':110B ''guard'':68B,78B ''hardwork'':47B ''hold'':9B,28B,108B ''import'':85B ''lack'':56B ''land'':25B ''life'':120B ''locat'':10B ''maintain'':64B ''modest'':7B ''nazeem'':36B ''nazeem’'':55B ''nestl'':21B ''network'':93B ''often'':34B ''on-sit'':70B ''oper'':41B ''own'':29B ''part'':87B ''patrol'':80B ''presenc'':58B ''prosper'':105B ''quiet'':99B ''reflect'':83B ''region'':90B ''regular'':79B ''resid'':50B ''rhythm'':116B ''secur'':76B ''site'':72B ''skyrim’'':118B ''south'':15B ''stand'':96B ''station'':69B ''steadi'':115B ''vital'':101B ''well'':63B ''well-maintain'':62B ''whiterun'':14B,27B,67B,107B ''wilmuth'':45B ''within'':22B ''yard'':82B ''yet'':100B', 'whiterun', 'Chillfurrow Farm is a modest agricultural holding located just east of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vampire_armor', '
Vampire Armor has basic protection quality. Its visual design is dark and gothic, featuring sleek leather with subtle, blood-red accents. It can not be crafted. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''accent'':24B ''adept'':31B ''armor'':2A,4B ''basic'':6B ''blood'':22B ''blood-r'':21B ''craft'':29B,34B ''dark'':13B ''design'':11B ''featur'':16B ''gothic'':15B ''it.it'':35B ''leather'':18B,41B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''red'':23B ''sleek'':17B ''smith'':32B ''subtl'':20B ''tempered/improved'':38B ''use'':40B ''vampir'':1A,3B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':44B', 'blacksmith', '
