INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lesser_ward', 'Lesser Ward is a Restoration spell that creates a magical shield around the caster, absorbing a small amount of magic damage. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''absorb'':17B ''amount'':20B ''apprentic'':27B ''around'':14B ''cast'':31B ''caster'':16B ''creat'':10B ''damag'':23B ''lesser'':1A,3B ''level'':29B ''magic'':12B,22B ''requir'':25B ''restor'':7B ''shield'':13B ''skill'':28B ''small'':19B ''spell'':8B ''ward'':2A,4B', 'mage', 'Lesser Ward is a spell that creates a magical shield around the caster, absorbing a small amount of magic damage. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lost_valkygg', 'Lost Valkygg is a small Nordic ruin located northeast of Labyrinthian and west of Skyborn Altar in Hjaalmarch. The ruin is inhabited by draugr.', '''altar'':18B ''draugr'':26B ''hjaalmarch'':20B ''inhabit'':24B ''labyrinthian'':13B ''locat'':10B ''lost'':1A,3B ''nordic'':8B ''northeast'':11B ''ruin'':9B,22B ''skyborn'':17B ''small'':7B ''valkygg'':2A,4B ''west'':15B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Lost Valkygg is a small Nordic ruin located northeast of Labyrinthi in Hjaalmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bow_of_shadows', 'The Bow of Shadows is a Daedric artifact attributed to Nocturnal, granting its wielder invisibility and increased speed. Originally given to the ranger Raerlas Ghile for a failed mission, the bow was lost, though legends say Raerlas used it to vanquish many foes before his demise.', '''artifact'':11B ''attribut'':12B ''bow'':1A,5B,34B ''daedric'':10B ''demis'':49B ''fail'':31B ''foe'':46B ''ghile'':28B ''given'':23B ''grant'':15B ''increas'':20B ''invis'':18B ''legend'':38B ''lost'':36B ''mani'':45B ''mission'':32B ''nocturn'':14B ''origin'':22B ''raerla'':27B,40B ''ranger'':26B ''say'':39B ''shadow'':3A,7B ''speed'':21B ''though'':37B ''use'':41B ''vanquish'':44B ''wielder'':17B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', 'The Bow of Shadows is a Daedric artifact from Nocturnal, granting invisibility and increased speed. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_apprentice''s_assistant', 'The Apprentice''s Assistant, written by Aramril, provides practical advice for aspiring mages, delivered with a touch of arrogance and humor by Valenwood''s most celebrated spellcaster. Framed as a guide to achieving fame and fortune through magical duels, the book outlines five key principles for success: understanding an opponent’s weaknesses, recognizing one’s own limitations, using wards judiciously, balancing spellcasting techniques, and strategically engaging with challenges. Aramril emphasizes both the technical and performative aspects of spellcasting, highlighting the importance of pleasing spectators to sustain a mage’s reputation and livelihood.

Themes of self-awareness, strategy, and showmanship run throughout the text, underscoring the balance between practical survival skills and the theatrical nature of public dueling. Aramril’s tone combines playful egotism with genuine wisdom, making this single-volume work as much a reflection of the author’s personality as it is a manual for mastering the arcane arts.', '''achiev'':37B ''advic'':14B ''apprentic'':2A,6B ''aramril'':11B,71B ''aramril’'':120B ''arcan'':150B ''arrog'':23B ''art'':151B ''aspect'':78B ''aspir'':16B ''assist'':4A,8B ''author’'':140B ''awar'':98B ''balanc'':63B,108B ''book'':45B ''celebr'':30B ''challeng'':70B ''combin'':122B ''deliv'':18B ''duel'':43B,119B ''egot'':124B ''emphas'':72B ''engag'':68B ''fame'':38B ''five'':47B ''fortun'':40B ''frame'':32B ''genuin'':126B ''guid'':35B ''highlight'':81B ''humor'':25B ''import'':83B ''judici'':62B ''key'':48B ''limit'':59B ''livelihood'':93B ''mage'':17B ''mage’'':90B ''magic'':42B ''make'':128B ''manual'':146B ''master'':148B ''much'':135B ''natur'':116B ''one’'':57B ''opponent’'':54B ''outlin'':46B ''perform'':77B ''person'':141B ''play'':123B ''pleas'':85B ''practic'':13B,110B ''principl'':49B ''provid'':12B ''public'':118B ''recogn'':56B ''reflect'':137B ''reput'':91B ''run'':102B ''self'':97B ''self-awar'':96B ''showmanship'':101B ''singl'':131B ''single-volum'':130B ''skill'':112B ''spectat'':86B ''spellcast'':31B,64B,80B ''strateg'':67B ''strategi'':99B ''success'':51B ''surviv'':111B ''sustain'':88B ''technic'':75B ''techniqu'':65B ''text'':105B ''theatric'':115B ''theme'':94B ''throughout'':103B ''tone'':121B ''touch'':21B ''underscor'':106B ''understand'':52B ''use'':60B ''valenwood'':27B ''volum'':132B ''ward'':61B ''weak'':55B ''wisdom'':127B ''work'':133B ''written'':9B', 'scholar', '
The Apprentice''s Assistant, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, offers advice for aspiring mages, blending practical strategies with theatrical tips for success in magical duels. Thematically, it emphasizes self-awareness, strategy, and showmanship, illustrating the balance between magical skill and the performance aspect required for maintaining a mage''s reputation.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bone_meal', 'Bone Meal is an ingredient dropped by most undead creatures, commonly used in various alchemical concoctions. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina, Resist Fire, Fortify Conjuration, and Ravage Stamina.', '''alchem'':17B ''alchemi'':19B ''bone'':1A,3B ''common'':13B ''concoct'':18B ''conjur'':26B ''creatur'':12B ''damag'':21B ''drop'':8B ''effect'':20B ''fire'':24B ''fortifi'':25B ''ingredi'':7B ''meal'':2A,4B ''ravag'':28B ''resist'':23B ''stamina'':22B,29B ''undead'':11B ''use'':14B ''various'':16B', 'alchemist', 'Bone Meal is an ingredient dropped by most undead creatures, commonly used in various alchemical concoctions.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nordic_helmet', 'Nordic Carved Helmet is a basic Nordic carved helmet with great protection quality. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. To craft it: 1 ebony ingot, 1 quicksilver ingot, 2 leather strips, and 4 steel ingots at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using quicksilver at a workbench.', '''1'':40B,43B ''2'':46B ''4'':50B ''adept'':58B ''ancient'':35B ''basic'':8B ''blacksmith'':55B ''carv'':4B,10B ''craft'':38B,61B ''craftsmanship'':36B ''design'':18B ''eboni'':41B ''engrav'':32B ''evok'':34B ''finish'':28B ''forg'':56B ''gray'':27B ''great'':13B ''helmet'':2A,5B,11B ''ingot'':42B,45B,52B ''intric'':30B ''leather'':47B ''nordic'':1A,3B,9B,31B ''protect'':14B ''qualiti'':15B ''quicksilv'':44B,69B ''silver'':26B ''silver-gray'':25B ''smith'':59B ''steel'':51B ''strip'':48B ''sturdi'':20B ''tempered/improved'':66B ''use'':68B ''visual'':17B ''weather'':22B ''workbench'':72B', 'blacksmith', 'Nordic Carved Helmet is a basic Nordic carved helmet with great protection quality. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mixwater_mill', 'Mixwater Mill is a modest lumber mill located along the White River in Eastmarch, southwest of Windhelm and southeast of Gallows Rock. The mill is owned and operated by Gilfre, who has lived and worked there alone since her five employees left to join the ongoing civil war.', '''alon'':39B ''along'':11B ''civil'':49B ''eastmarch'':16B ''employe'':43B ''five'':42B ''gallow'':23B ''gilfr'':32B ''join'':46B ''left'':44B ''live'':35B ''locat'':10B ''lumber'':8B ''mill'':2A,4B,9B,26B ''mixwat'':1A,3B ''modest'':7B ''ongo'':48B ''oper'':30B ''own'':28B ''river'':14B ''rock'':24B ''sinc'':40B ''southeast'':21B ''southwest'':17B ''war'':50B ''white'':13B ''windhelm'':19B ''work'':37B', 'eastmarch', 'Mixwater Mill is a modest lumber mill located along the White River in Eastmarch. You do not know who runs the mill.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steepfall_burrow', 'Steepfall Burrow is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge and east of Northwatch Keep in Haafingar. It is inhabited by trolls and wolves.', '''bridg'':13B ''burrow'':2A,4B ''cave'':8B ''dragon'':12B ''east'':15B ''haafingar'':20B ''inhabit'':23B ''keep'':18B ''locat'':9B ''northwatch'':17B ''northwest'':10B ''small'':7B ''steepfal'':1A,3B ''troll'':25B ''wolv'':27B', 'haafingar', 'Steepfall Burrow is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hillgrunds_tomb', 'Hillgrund''s Tomb is a small Nordic burial site nestled southwest of Windhelm and south-southeast of Valtheim Towers, hidden within the rugged wilderness of Skyrim. The tomb''s shadowy corridors are inhabited by draugr, ancient guardians who rise to defend their sanctum from intruders. ', '''ancient'':39B ''burial'':10B ''corridor'':34B ''defend'':44B ''draugr'':38B ''guardian'':40B ''hidden'':23B ''hillgrund'':1A,3B ''inhabit'':36B ''intrud'':48B ''nestl'':12B ''nordic'':9B ''rise'':42B ''rug'':26B ''sanctum'':46B ''shadowi'':33B ''site'':11B ''skyrim'':29B ''small'':8B ''south'':18B ''south-southeast'':17B ''southeast'':19B ''southwest'':13B ''tomb'':2A,5B,31B ''tower'':22B ''valtheim'':21B ''wilder'':27B ''windhelm'':15B ''within'':24B', 'whiterun', 'Hillgrund''s Tomb is a small Nordic burial site nestled southwest of Windhelm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('liar''s_retreat', 'Liar''s Retreat is a small cave and underground cellar located northwest of Broken Tower Redoubt and northeast of Karthwasten in the Reach. The entrance is marked by a cairn, making it easier to spot amidst the rugged terrain. The cave is occupied by bandits.', '''amidst'':39B ''bandit'':48B ''broken'':17B ''cairn'':33B ''cave'':10B,44B ''cellar'':13B ''easier'':36B ''entranc'':28B ''karthwasten'':23B ''liar'':1A,4B ''locat'':14B ''make'':34B ''mark'':30B ''northeast'':21B ''northwest'':15B ''occupi'':46B ''reach'':26B ''redoubt'':19B ''retreat'':3A,6B ''rug'':41B ''small'':9B ''spot'':38B ''terrain'':42B ''tower'':18B ''underground'':12B', 'reach', 'Liar''s Retreat is a small cave and underground cellar located northeast of Karthwasten in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('solstheim', 'Solstheim is a large island located in the Sea of Ghosts, to the north of Tamriel, with a history that stretches back to the ancient Snow Elves, the first inhabitants of the region. They built grand settlements on Solstheim that outlasted their mainland holdings, leaving a lasting mark on the island. Though the island has been home to various races over the centuries, it has traditionally been dominated by Nordic influence. In 4E 16, Solstheim officially became part of Morrowind.

The island’s history took a tragic turn during the Red Year of 4E 5, when the eruption of Red Mountain devastated the southern half of Solstheim. Fort Frostmoth was destroyed, leaving the Imperial garrison in disarray and killing General Carius. Raven Rock, a settlement on the island, quickly took over the remnants of the garrison and was fortified by elite members of the Redoran Guard. In the aftermath of the eruption, the ash from Red Mountain transformed the southern part of the island into vast ashlands. To protect Raven Rock from the encroaching ash, Brara Morvayn designed and oversaw the construction of a great stone wall known as the Bulwark, funded by the East Empire Company.

In 4E 16, as part of a political compromise, Skyrim ceded control of Solstheim to Morrowind. While this act appeared to be a compassionate gesture toward the Dunmer, it was driven by political motives. Skyrim sought to avoid a conflict with Morrowind, which had long claimed the island, and by relinquishing control, it preserved its image as a savior to the Dunmer. As a result, many Dunmer refugees, including members of the minor House Sathil, began flocking to the island. The East Empire Company was forced to hand over control of Raven Rock to House Redoran, and by 4E 48, Solstheim was no longer considered part of the Empire.', '''16'':75B,200B ''48'':297B ''4e'':74B,94B,199B,296B ''5'':95B ''act'':216B ''aftermath'':149B ''ancient'':26B ''appear'':217B ''ash'':154B,175B ''ashland'':167B ''avoid'':235B ''back'':23B ''becam'':78B ''began'':273B ''brara'':176B ''built'':36B ''bulwark'':191B ''carius'':121B ''cede'':208B ''centuri'':64B ''claim'':243B ''compani'':197B,281B ''compassion'':221B ''compromis'':206B ''conflict'':237B ''consid'':302B ''construct'':182B ''control'':209B,249B,287B ''design'':178B ''destroy'':111B ''devast'':102B ''disarray'':117B ''domin'':69B ''driven'':228B ''dunmer'':225B,259B,264B ''east'':195B,279B ''elit'':141B ''elv'':28B ''empir'':196B,280B,306B ''encroach'':174B ''erupt'':98B,152B ''first'':30B ''flock'':274B ''forc'':283B ''fort'':108B ''fortifi'':139B ''frostmoth'':109B ''fund'':192B ''garrison'':115B,136B ''general'':120B ''gestur'':222B ''ghost'':12B ''grand'':37B ''great'':185B ''guard'':146B ''half'':105B ''hand'':285B ''histori'':20B,84B ''hold'':45B ''home'':58B ''hous'':271B,292B ''imag'':253B ''imperi'':114B ''includ'':266B ''influenc'':72B ''inhabit'':31B ''island'':6B,52B,55B,128B,164B,245B,277B ''island’'':83B ''kill'':119B ''known'':188B ''larg'':5B ''last'':48B ''leav'':46B,112B ''locat'':7B ''long'':242B ''longer'':301B ''mainland'':44B ''mani'':263B ''mark'':49B ''member'':142B,267B ''minor'':270B ''morrowind'':81B,213B,239B ''morvayn'':177B ''motiv'':231B ''mountain'':101B,157B ''nordic'':71B ''north'':15B ''offici'':77B ''outlast'':42B ''oversaw'':180B ''part'':79B,161B,202B,303B ''polit'':205B,230B ''preserv'':251B ''protect'':169B ''quick'':129B ''race'':61B ''raven'':122B,170B,289B ''red'':91B,100B,156B ''redoran'':145B,293B ''refuge'':265B ''region'':34B ''relinquish'':248B ''remnant'':133B ''result'':262B ''rock'':123B,171B,290B ''sathil'':272B ''savior'':256B ''sea'':10B ''settlement'':38B,125B ''skyrim'':207B,232B ''snow'':27B ''solstheim'':1A,2B,40B,76B,107B,211B,298B ''sought'':233B ''southern'':104B,160B ''stone'':186B ''stretch'':22B ''tamriel'':17B ''though'':53B ''took'':85B,130B ''toward'':223B ''tradit'':67B ''tragic'':87B ''transform'':158B ''turn'':88B ''various'':60B ''vast'':166B ''wall'':187B ''year'':92B', 'solstheim, noble, scholar', 'Solstheim is a large island located in the Sea of Ghosts, to the north of Tamriel, with a history that stretches back to the ancient Snow Elves, the first inhabitants of the region. They built grand settlements on Solstheim that outlasted their mainland holdings, leaving a lasting mark on the island. Though the island has been home to various races over the centuries, it has traditionally been dominated by Nordic influence. In 4E 16, Solstheim officially became part of Morrowind. The island’s history took a tragic turn during the Red Year of 4E 5, when the eruption of Red Mountain devastated the southern half of Solstheim. You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nordic_shield', 'Nordic Shield is a basic Nordic shield with great protection quality. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. To craft it: 1 quicksilver ingot, 1 leather strip, and 4 steel ingots at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using quicksilver at a workbench. It can be tempered/improved by using quicksilver at a workbench.', '''1'':38B,41B ''4'':45B ''adept'':53B ''ancient'':33B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':50B ''craft'':36B,56B ''craftsmanship'':34B ''design'':16B ''engrav'':30B ''evok'':32B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':51B ''gray'':25B ''great'':11B ''ingot'':40B,47B ''intric'':28B ''leather'':42B ''nordic'':1A,3B,8B,29B ''protect'':12B ''qualiti'':13B ''quicksilv'':39B,64B,74B ''shield'':2A,4B,9B ''silver'':24B ''silver-gray'':23B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':46B ''strip'':43B ''sturdi'':18B ''tempered/improved'':61B,71B ''use'':63B,73B ''visual'':15B ''weather'':20B ''workbench'':67B,77B', 'blacksmith', 'Nordic Shield is a basic Nordic shield with great protection quality. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('iron_armor', 'Iron Armor is a basic iron chest piece with basic protection quality. Its visual design is crude and basic, with a dark, weathered appearance and simple, utilitarian shapes. To craft it: 5 iron ingots and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Novice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''3'':38B ''5'':34B ''appear'':26B ''armor'':2A,4B ''basic'':7B,12B,21B ''blacksmith'':43B ''chest'':9B ''craft'':32B,49B ''crude'':19B ''dark'':24B ''design'':17B ''forg'':44B ''ingot'':36B ''iron'':1A,3B,8B,35B,57B ''leather'':39B ''novic'':46B ''piec'':10B ''protect'':13B ''qualiti'':14B ''shape'':30B ''simpl'':28B ''smith'':47B ''strip'':40B ''tempered/improved'':54B ''use'':56B ''utilitarian'':29B ''visual'':16B ''weather'':25B ''workbench'':60B', 'blacksmith', 'Iron Armor is a basic iron chest piece with basic protection quality. Its visual design is crude and basic, with a dark, weathered appearance and simple, utilitarian shapes. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('iron_shield', 'Iron Shield is a basic iron shield with basic protection quality. Its visual design is crude and basic, with a dark, weathered appearance and simple, utilitarian shapes. To craft it: 4 iron ingots and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. A Novice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''1'':37B ''4'':33B ''appear'':25B ''basic'':7B,11B,20B ''blacksmith'':42B ''craft'':31B,48B ''crude'':18B ''dark'':23B ''design'':16B ''forg'':43B ''ingot'':35B ''iron'':1A,3B,8B,34B,56B ''leather'':38B ''novic'':45B ''protect'':12B ''qualiti'':13B ''shape'':29B ''shield'':2A,4B,9B ''simpl'':27B ''smith'':46B ''strip'':39B ''tempered/improved'':53B ''use'':55B ''utilitarian'':28B ''visual'':15B ''weather'':24B ''workbench'':59B', 'blacksmith', 'Iron Shield is a basic iron shield with basic protection quality. Its visual design is crude and basic, with a dark, weathered appearance and simple, utilitarian shapes. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nordic_mace', 'Nordic Mace is a blunt Nordic weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. To craft it: 1 quicksilver ingot, 1 leather strip, and 1 steel ingot at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using quicksilver at a workbench.', '''1'':38B,41B,45B ''adept'':53B ''ancient'':33B ''blacksmith'':50B ''blunt'':7B ''craft'':36B,56B ''craftsmanship'':34B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''engrav'':30B ''evok'':32B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':51B ''good'':12B ''gray'':25B ''ingot'':40B,47B ''intric'':28B ''leather'':42B ''mace'':2A,4B ''nordic'':1A,3B,8B,29B ''quicksilv'':39B,64B ''silver'':24B ''silver-gray'':23B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':46B ''strip'':43B ''sturdi'':18B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''weather'':20B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Nordic Mace is a blunt Nordic weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('death_of_a_wanderer', '
The Death of a Wanderer, written by Anonymous, is a tale of an Argonian who meets a tragic end after venturing into a Draugr crypt. The story is told through the eyes of a companion, who recounts the final moments of the Argonian''s life as he reflects on his failed attempt to use a mysterious claw he had found in an ancient crypt. The claw, believed to be a key for opening sealing doors in crypts, holds an important revelation about the Draugr: the symbols on the doors were not just locks, but a mechanism to ensure that only the living could enter, while the Draugr were trapped inside.

The themes of the story revolve around the dangers of seeking forbidden knowledge, the wisdom gained through hardship, and the ironies of life and death. The Argonian''s struggle with the Draugr highlights the conflict between mortal ambition and the inevitability of death. His final insights, including the realization that the crypt doors were meant to keep the Draugr in, provide a somber reflection on the cost of discovery and the meaning of survival. The book is a single, standalone tale that offers a glimpse into the life and untold stories of an adventurous Argonian who, despite his survival instincts, ultimately succumbs to the dangers he sought to conquer.', '''adventur'':208B ''ambit'':152B ''ancient'':67B ''anonym'':12B ''argonian'':18B,47B,141B,209B ''around'':121B ''attempt'':56B ''believ'':71B ''book'':190B ''claw'':61B,70B ''companion'':39B ''conflict'':149B ''conquer'':223B ''cost'':181B ''could'':107B ''crypt'':29B,68B,81B,166B ''danger'':123B,219B ''death'':1A,6B,139B,157B ''despit'':211B ''discoveri'':183B ''door'':79B,93B,167B ''draugr'':28B,88B,111B,146B,173B ''end'':23B ''ensur'':102B ''enter'':108B ''eye'':36B ''fail'':55B ''final'':43B,159B ''forbidden'':126B ''found'':64B ''gain'':130B ''glimps'':199B ''hardship'':132B ''highlight'':147B ''hold'':82B ''import'':84B ''includ'':161B ''inevit'':155B ''insid'':114B ''insight'':160B ''instinct'':214B ''ironi'':135B ''keep'':171B ''key'':75B ''knowledg'':127B ''life'':49B,137B,202B ''live'':106B ''lock'':97B ''mean'':186B ''meant'':169B ''mechan'':100B ''meet'':20B ''moment'':44B ''mortal'':151B ''mysteri'':60B ''offer'':197B ''open'':77B ''provid'':175B ''realiz'':163B ''recount'':41B ''reflect'':52B,178B ''revel'':85B ''revolv'':120B ''seal'':78B ''seek'':125B ''singl'':193B ''somber'':177B ''sought'':221B ''standalon'':194B ''stori'':31B,119B,205B ''struggl'':143B ''succumb'':216B ''surviv'':188B,213B ''symbol'':90B ''tale'':15B,195B ''theme'':116B ''told'':33B ''tragic'':22B ''trap'':113B ''ultim'':215B ''untold'':204B ''use'':58B ''ventur'':25B ''wander'':4A,9B ''wisdom'':129B ''written'':10B', 'scholar', '
The Death of a Wanderer, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, is a tragic tale of an Argonian''s ill-fated exploration of a Draugr crypt. Themes of forbidden knowledge, the inevitability of death, and the ironies of life and survival are central, as the Argonian learns the crypt''s deadly secrets too late, reflecting on the cost of discovery.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('jazbay_grapes', 'Jazbay Grapes are harvested from vines growing on rocky outcroppings in Eastmarch''s volcanic tundra, and are used both in alchemy and for baking Jazbay Crostata. Alchemy effects: Weakness to Magic, Fortify Magicka, Regenerate Magicka, and Ravage Health.', '''alchemi'':23B,29B ''bake'':26B ''crostata'':28B ''eastmarch'':14B ''effect'':30B ''fortifi'':34B ''grape'':2A,4B ''grow'':9B ''harvest'':6B ''health'':40B ''jazbay'':1A,3B,27B ''magic'':33B ''magicka'':35B,37B ''outcrop'':12B ''ravag'':39B ''regener'':36B ''rocki'':11B ''tundra'':17B ''use'':20B ''vine'':8B ''volcan'':16B ''weak'':31B', 'alchemist', 'Jazbay Grapes are harvested from vines growing on rocky outcroppings in Eastmarch''s volcanic tundra, and are used both in alchemy and for baking Jazbay Crostata.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_the_healer', 'This potion strengthens restoration magic, enhancing the effectiveness of healing and protective spells. Slightly enhances restoration magic, with higher tiers greatly increasing the potency of healing and protection spells. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':45B ''draught'':55B ''effect'':12B ''elixir'':58B ''enhanc'':10B,19B ''found'':38B ''great'':25B ''heal'':14B,30B ''healer'':4A ''higher'':23B ''increas'':26B ''loot'':41B ''magic'':9B,21B ''philter'':56B ''potenc'':28B ''potion'':1A,6B,35B,54B ''protect'':16B,32B ''purchas'':43B ''random'':40B ''restor'':8B,20B ''sever'':48B ''slight'':18B ''spell'':17B,33B ''strengthen'':7B ''strongest'':53B ''tier'':24B,49B ''weakest'':51B', 'priest, alchemist, mage, scholar, collegeofwinterhold', 'The Potion of the Healer enhances restoration magic, improving healing and protection spells. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_regeneration', 'This potion accelerates natural healing, allowing wounds to close and vitality to return at an enhanced rate. Slightly boosts health regeneration, with stronger potions significantly accelerating natural recovery. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, solution, philter, and elixir.', '''acceler'':6B,29B ''alchemist'':43B ''allow'':9B ''boost'':22B ''close'':12B ''draught'':53B ''elixir'':57B ''enhanc'':19B ''found'':36B ''heal'':8B ''health'':23B ''loot'':39B ''natur'':7B,30B ''philter'':55B ''potion'':1A,5B,27B,33B,52B ''purchas'':41B ''random'':38B ''rate'':20B ''recoveri'':31B ''regener'':3A,24B ''return'':16B ''sever'':46B ''signific'':28B ''slight'':21B ''solut'':54B ''stronger'':26B ''strongest'':51B ''tier'':47B ''vital'':14B ''weakest'':49B ''wound'':10B', 'alchemist, priest, mage, companions, traveler', 'The Potion of Regeneration accelerates natural healing, restoring health over time. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('oblivion_crisis', 'The Oblivion Crisis, also known as the Great Anguish, was a catastrophic conflict between the Daedric hordes of Mehrunes Dagon and the people of Tamriel, beginning in the year 3E 433. The crisis was ignited by the assassination of Emperor Uriel Septim VII and his heirs, leading to the opening of Oblivion Gates across the continent, through which Daedra emerged in overwhelming numbers. These gates were facilitated by the Mythic Dawn, a fanatical cult devoted to Mehrunes Dagon, resulting in widespread devastation throughout various provinces. Key regions such as Skyrim faced brutal sieges, while Kvatch in Cyrodiil was completely destroyed. The Argonians of Black Marsh, called upon by the Hist, mounted a successful counter-offensive against the Daedra, forcing them to close their gates in that region.

Despite the turmoil, the Empire struggled to maintain order, with significant forces withdrawn from provinces like Morrowind, leaving Cyrodiil largely defenseless. Amidst this chaos, Martin Septim, the last heir of the Septim bloodline, emerged as a pivotal figure. He joined forces with a hero of destiny to confront the Daedric threat. In a climactic sacrifice, Martin transformed into an Avatar of Akatosh, utilizing the power of the Amulet of Kings to banish Mehrunes Dagon back to Oblivion, thus ending the crisis and marking the conclusion of the Third Era.', '''3e'':32B ''433'':33B ''across'':56B ''akatosh'':192B ''also'':6B ''amidst'':152B ''amulet'':198B ''anguish'':11B ''argonian'':104B ''assassin'':40B ''avatar'':190B ''back'':205B ''banish'':202B ''begin'':28B ''black'':106B ''bloodlin'':163B ''brutal'':94B ''call'':108B ''catastroph'':14B ''chao'':154B ''climact'':184B ''close'':125B ''complet'':101B ''conclus'':215B ''conflict'':15B ''confront'':178B ''contin'':58B ''counter'':117B ''counter-offens'':116B ''crisi'':2A,5B,35B,211B ''cult'':76B ''cyrodiil'':99B,149B ''daedra'':61B,121B ''daedric'':18B,180B ''dagon'':22B,80B,204B ''dawn'':73B ''defenseless'':151B ''despit'':131B ''destini'':176B ''destroy'':102B ''devast'':84B ''devot'':77B ''emerg'':62B,164B ''emperor'':42B ''empir'':135B ''end'':209B ''era'':219B ''face'':93B ''facilit'':69B ''fanat'':75B ''figur'':168B ''forc'':122B,142B,171B ''gate'':55B,67B,127B ''great'':10B ''heir'':48B,159B ''hero'':174B ''hist'':112B ''hord'':19B ''ignit'':37B ''join'':170B ''key'':88B ''king'':200B ''known'':7B ''kvatch'':97B ''larg'':150B ''last'':158B ''lead'':49B ''leav'':148B ''like'':146B ''maintain'':138B ''mark'':213B ''marsh'':107B ''martin'':155B,186B ''mehrun'':21B,79B,203B ''morrowind'':147B ''mount'':113B ''mythic'':72B ''number'':65B ''oblivion'':1A,4B,54B,207B ''offens'':118B ''open'':52B ''order'':139B ''overwhelm'':64B ''peopl'':25B ''pivot'':167B ''power'':195B ''provinc'':87B,145B ''region'':89B,130B ''result'':81B ''sacrific'':185B ''septim'':44B,156B,162B ''sieg'':95B ''signific'':141B ''skyrim'':92B ''struggl'':136B ''success'':115B ''tamriel'':27B ''third'':218B ''threat'':181B ''throughout'':85B ''thus'':208B ''transform'':187B ''turmoil'':133B ''upon'':109B ''uriel'':43B ''util'':193B ''various'':86B ''vii'':45B ''widespread'':83B ''withdrawn'':143B ''year'':31B', 'scholar, daedra, daedric', '
The Oblivion Crisis, or Great Anguish, began in 3E 433 when the assassination of Emperor Uriel Septim VII and his heirs enabled the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon to unleash his forces on Tamriel through Oblivion Gates. Facilitated by the Mythic Dawn cult, the Daedra wrought devastation, destroying cities like Kvatch and besieging regions such as Skyrim. In Black Marsh, the Argonians, guided by the Hist, successfully repelled the Daedric hordes. Amid the chaos, Martin Septim, the last of the Septim bloodline, sacrificed himself by becoming the Avatar of Akatosh, using the Amulet of Kings to banish Mehrunes Dagon and end the crisis, concluding the Third Era.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thalmor_embassy', 'The Thalmor Embassy is a heavily guarded diplomatic compound located northwest of Solitude, in Haafingar. It serves as the headquarters for the Aldmeri Dominion''s operations in Skyrim and is a focal point for Thalmor activity in the province. 

The embassy is led by Elenwen, the Thalmor ambassador, who is known for hosting extravagant parties attended by Skyrim''s most influential figures. The building is a center for the Thalmor''s political maneuvering in Skyrim, and it is here that you infiltrate the compound using a forged invitation as part of the main quest. The embassy is situated in a remote area, east of Ironback Hideout, making it a secretive and well-protected location.', '''activ'':38B ''aldmeri'':25B ''ambassador'':50B ''area'':104B ''attend'':58B ''build'':66B ''center'':69B ''compound'':11B,86B ''diplomat'':10B ''dominion'':26B ''east'':105B ''elenwen'':47B ''embassi'':2A,5B,43B,98B ''extravag'':56B ''figur'':64B ''focal'':34B ''forg'':89B ''guard'':9B ''haafingar'':17B ''headquart'':22B ''heavili'':8B ''hideout'':108B ''host'':55B ''infiltr'':84B ''influenti'':63B ''invit'':90B ''ironback'':107B ''known'':53B ''led'':45B ''locat'':12B,117B ''main'':95B ''make'':109B ''maneuv'':75B ''northwest'':13B ''oper'':28B ''part'':92B ''parti'':57B ''point'':35B ''polit'':74B ''protect'':116B ''provinc'':41B ''quest'':96B ''remot'':103B ''secret'':112B ''serv'':19B ''situat'':100B ''skyrim'':30B,60B,77B ''solitud'':15B ''thalmor'':1A,4B,37B,49B,72B ''use'':87B ''well'':115B ''well-protect'':114B', 'haafingar, thalmor, legion', 'The Thalmor Embassy is a heavily guarded diplomatic compound located northwest of Solitude, in Haafingar. It serves as the headquarters for the Aldmeri Dominion''s operations in Skyrim and is a focal point for Thalmor activity in the province. You do not know who runs the embassy.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('giant_toe', 'Giant''s Toes are dropped by giants and are known for their powerful alchemical effects. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina, Fortify Health, Fortify Carry Weight, and Damage Stamina Regen.', '''alchem'':16B ''alchemi'':18B ''carri'':25B ''damag'':20B,28B ''drop'':7B ''effect'':17B,19B ''fortifi'':22B,24B ''giant'':1A,3B,9B ''health'':23B ''known'':12B ''power'':15B ''regen'':30B ''stamina'':21B,29B ''toe'':2A,5B ''weight'':26B', 'alchemist', 'Giant''s Toes are dropped by giants and are known for their powerful alchemical effects. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('volskygge', 'Volskygge is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located west of Solitude and southeast of Pinefrost Tower in Haafingar. The ruin is home to bandits.

The site is marked by the remnants of ancient Nordic architecture, and its crumbling halls and towers make it a haunting place to visit.', '''ancient'':35B ''architectur'':37B ''bandit'':26B ''crumbl'':40B ''haafingar'':20B ''hall'':41B ''haunt'':47B ''home'':24B ''locat'':10B ''make'':44B ''mark'':30B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''nordic'':8B,36B ''pinefrost'':17B ''place'':48B ''remnant'':33B ''ruin'':9B,22B ''site'':28B ''size'':7B ''solitud'':13B ''southeast'':15B ''tower'':18B,43B ''visit'':50B ''volskygg'':1A,2B ''west'':11B', 'haafingar', 'Volskygge is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located west of Solitude in Haafingar..
