INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('argonian_ale', 'Argonian Ale is a rare and potent drink, said to invigorate the body at the cost of slowing its recovery. It is sought after by certain individuals and is a point of pride among Argonians.', '''ale'':2A,4B ''among'':36B ''argonian'':1A,3B,37B ''bodi'':15B ''certain'':28B ''cost'':18B ''drink'':10B ''individu'':29B ''invigor'':13B ''point'':33B ''potent'':9B ''pride'':35B ''rare'':7B ''recoveri'':22B ''said'':11B ''slow'':20B ''sought'':25B', 'argonian, brenuin', 'You have only heard vague references to Argonian Ale but know nothing specific about it.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rorikstead', 'Rorikstead is a small farming town in western Whiterun Hold, located west of Swindler''s Den and east-southeast of Bleakwind Bluff. The town is named after Rorik, a noble who resides in the local "manor" and plays a central role in its community. Despite its living namesake, Rorikstead’s name and origins appear much older, being referenced in the Merethic or First Era text Holdings of Jarl Gjalund as "Rorik''s Steading" and in the Second Era text Atlas of Dragons. It is also immortalized in the bard''s song Ragnar the Red, which describes it as "ole Rorikstead," hinting at the existence of an ancient settlement that preceded the current town.


Frostfruit Inn, owned by Mralki, is located here. Known for its abundant crop fields, Rorikstead boasts a reputation for bountiful harvests, with residents proudly claiming they have not suffered a bad season in years. ', '''abund'':126B ''also'':86B ''ancient'':108B ''appear'':55B ''atlas'':81B ''bad'':145B ''bard'':90B ''bleakwind'':23B ''bluff'':24B ''boast'':130B ''bounti'':134B ''central'':42B ''claim'':139B ''communiti'':46B ''crop'':127B ''current'':113B ''den'':17B ''describ'':97B ''despit'':47B ''dragon'':83B ''east'':20B ''east-southeast'':19B ''era'':65B,79B ''exist'':105B ''farm'':6B ''field'':128B ''first'':64B ''frostfruit'':115B ''gjalund'':70B ''harvest'':135B ''hint'':102B ''hold'':11B,67B ''immort'':87B ''inn'':116B ''jarl'':69B ''known'':123B ''live'':49B ''local'':37B ''locat'':12B,121B ''manor'':38B ''mereth'':62B ''mralki'':119B ''much'':56B ''name'':28B,52B ''namesak'':50B ''nobl'':32B ''older'':57B ''ole'':100B ''origin'':54B ''own'':117B ''play'':40B ''preced'':111B ''proud'':138B ''ragnar'':93B ''red'':95B ''referenc'':59B ''reput'':132B ''resid'':34B,137B ''role'':43B ''rorik'':30B,72B ''rorikstead'':1A,2B,101B,129B ''rorikstead’'':51B ''season'':146B ''second'':78B ''settlement'':109B ''small'':5B ''song'':92B ''southeast'':21B ''stead'':74B ''suffer'':143B ''swindler'':15B ''text'':66B,80B ''town'':7B,26B,114B ''west'':13B ''western'':9B ''whiterun'':10B ''year'':148B', 'whiterun', 'Rorikstead is a small farming town in western Whiterun Hold, located west of Swindler''s Den and east-southeast of Bleakwind Bluff. Frostfruit Inn is situtated here,  but you do not know who owns it.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_gauntlets', 'Steel Gauntlets are a pair of steel gauntlets with good protection quality. Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished silver-gray finish and minimal ornamentation focused on practicality. To craft it: 2 steel ingots, 1 iron ingot, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Apprentice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''1'':41B,45B ''2'':38B ''apprentic'':53B ''blacksmith'':50B ''craft'':36B,56B ''design'':17B ''finish'':28B ''focus'':32B ''forg'':51B ''function'':21B ''gauntlet'':2A,4B,10B ''good'':12B ''gray'':27B ''ingot'':40B,43B ''iron'':42B ''leather'':46B ''minim'':30B ''ornament'':31B ''pair'':7B ''polish'':24B ''practic'':34B ''protect'':13B ''qualiti'':14B ''silver'':26B ''silver-gray'':25B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':1A,3B,9B,39B,64B ''straightforward'':19B ''strip'':47B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':16B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel Gauntlets are a pair of steel gauntlets with good protection quality. Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished silver-gray finish and minimal ornamentation focused on practicality. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
