You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_war_axe', 'Steel War Axe is a sturdy steel weapon which deals average damage.Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished silver-gray finish and minimal ornamentation focused on practicality.  To craft it: 2 steel ingots, 2 iron ingots, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''1'':45B ''2'':38B,41B ''adept'':53B ''averag'':14B ''axe'':3A,6B ''blacksmith'':50B ''craft'':36B,56B ''damage.its'':15B ''deal'':13B ''design'':17B ''finish'':28B ''focus'':32B ''forg'':51B ''function'':21B ''gray'':27B ''ingot'':40B,43B ''iron'':42B ''leather'':46B ''minim'':30B ''ornament'':31B ''polish'':24B ''practic'':34B ''silver'':26B ''silver-gray'':25B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':1A,4B,10B,39B,64B ''straightforward'':19B ''strip'':47B ''sturdi'':9B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':16B ''war'':2A,5B ''weapon'':11B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel War Axe is a sturdy steel weapon which deals average damage.Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished silver-gray finish and minimal ornamentation focused on practicality.  You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_battleaxe', 'Steel Battleaxe is a heavy steel weapon which deals average damage. Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished silver-gray finish and minimal ornamentation focused on practicality. To craft it: 4 steel ingots, 1 iron ingot, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''1'':40B ''2'':44B ''4'':37B ''adept'':52B ''averag'':12B ''battleax'':2A,4B ''blacksmith'':49B ''craft'':35B,55B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''finish'':27B ''focus'':31B ''forg'':50B ''function'':20B ''gray'':26B ''heavi'':7B ''ingot'':39B,42B ''iron'':41B ''leather'':45B ''minim'':29B ''ornament'':30B ''polish'':23B ''practic'':33B ''silver'':25B ''silver-gray'':24B ''smith'':53B ''steel'':1A,3B,8B,38B,63B ''straightforward'':18B ''strip'':46B ''tempered/improved'':60B ''use'':62B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':66B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel Battleaxe is a heavy steel weapon which deals average damage. Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished silver-gray finish and minimal ornamentation focused on practicality. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brain_rot', 'Brain Rot is a disease contracted from zombies and hagravens, causing a gradual loss of strength and magicka. As the disease progresses, it severely weakens the victim’s magical abilities and overall physical condition. If left untreated, the disease can lead to debilitating effects, leaving the afflicted unable to effectively use their magicka and becoming significantly weaker.', '''abil'':31B ''afflict'':48B ''becom'':56B ''brain'':1A,3B ''caus'':13B ''condit'':35B ''contract'':8B ''debilit'':44B ''diseas'':7B,23B,40B ''effect'':45B,51B ''gradual'':15B ''hagraven'':12B ''lead'':42B ''leav'':46B ''left'':37B ''loss'':16B ''magic'':30B ''magicka'':20B,54B ''overal'':33B ''physic'':34B ''progress'':24B ''rot'':2A,4B ''sever'':26B ''signific'':57B ''strength'':18B ''unabl'':49B ''untreat'':38B ''use'':52B ''victim’'':29B ''weaken'':27B ''weaker'':58B ''zombi'':10B', 'alchemist', 'Brain Rot is a disease contracted from zombies and hagravens, causing a gradual loss of strength and magicka. As the disease progresses, it severely weakens the victim’s magical abilities and overall physical condition. You do not know much else about this disease, but an alchemist would.magicka and becoming significantly weaker.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stalhrim_boots', 'Stalhrim Boots have fantastic protection quality. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding. To craft it: 4 stalhrim, 1 quicksilver ingot, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using stalhrim at a workbench.', '''1'':31B ''2'':35B ''4'':29B ''appear'':22B ''blacksmith'':40B ''blue'':19B ''boot'':2A,4B ''cold'':23B ''craft'':27B,46B ''crystallin'':15B ''design'':11B ''expert'':43B ''fantast'':6B ''forg'':41B ''frosti'':18B ''ici'':13B ''ingot'':33B ''leather'':36B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''quicksilv'':32B ''sheen'':20B ''smith'':44B ''stalhrim'':1A,3B,30B,54B ''strip'':37B ''tempered/improved'':51B ''unyield'':25B ''use'':53B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':57B', 'blacksmith', 'Stalhrim Boots have fantastic protection quality. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stalhrim_war_axe', 'Stalhrim War Axe is a sturdy stalhrim weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding. To craft it: 2 stalhrim and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using stalhrim at a workbench.', '''2'':36B,39B ''appear'':29B ''axe'':3A,6B ''blacksmith'':44B ''blue'':26B ''cold'':30B ''craft'':34B,50B ''crystallin'':22B ''damag'':15B ''deal'':13B ''design'':18B ''expert'':47B ''fantast'':14B ''forg'':45B ''frosti'':25B ''ici'':20B ''leather'':40B ''sheen'':27B ''smith'':48B ''stalhrim'':1A,4B,10B,37B,58B ''strip'':41B ''sturdi'':9B ''tempered/improved'':55B ''unyield'':32B ''use'':57B ''visual'':17B ''war'':2A,5B ''weapon'':11B ''workbench'':61B', 'blacksmith', 'Stalhrim War Axe is a sturdy stalhrim weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sheogorath', '
Sheogorath is the Daedric Prince of Madness, chaos, and creativity, known for his unpredictable and often cruel sense of humor. He rules the Shivering Isles, a plane of Oblivion divided into Mania and Dementia, reflecting the dual aspects of madness. Sheogorath is notorious for his bizarre, sadistic, and whimsical behavior, often treating mortals and even other Daedric Princes as his playthings. His appearance is usually that of a well-dressed, eccentric man wielding a cane, which contrasts sharply with his unpredictable and dangerous nature. Legends tell that Sheogorath was once Jyggalag, the Daedric Prince of Order, but was cursed by the other Daedric Princes to embody the chaos he once despised. This curse led to the recurring Greymarch, during which Jyggalag would briefly reclaim his form before reverting back to Sheogorath.

Sheogorath is revered and feared in many cultures, especially among the Khajiit, who call him the Skooma Cat, and the Dunmer, who regard him as one of the Four Corners of the House of Troubles. His influence is marked by a fondness for driving mortals into madness, either through direct interaction or by creating chaotic circumstances that lead to mental unraveling. He delights in playing cruel pranks, manipulating the minds of his followers, and challenging them with seemingly impossible tasks. Sheogorath’s iconic artifacts include the Wabbajack, a staff that can unpredictably transform its targets, and the Fork of Horripilation, a mundane-looking but cursed utensil he uses to torment mortals for his amusement.', '''among'':143B ''amus'':247B ''appear'':64B ''artifact'':216B ''aspect'':39B ''back'':131B ''behavior'':51B ''bizarr'':47B ''briefli'':125B ''call'':147B ''cane'':77B ''cat'':151B ''challeng'':208B ''chao'':9B,110B ''chaotic'':188B ''circumst'':189B ''contrast'':79B ''corner'':163B ''creat'':187B ''creativ'':11B ''cruel'':18B,199B ''cultur'':141B ''curs'':101B,115B,238B ''daedric'':5B,58B,95B,105B ''danger'':85B ''delight'':196B ''dementia'':35B ''despis'':113B ''direct'':183B ''divid'':31B ''dress'':72B ''drive'':177B ''dual'':38B ''dunmer'':154B ''eccentr'':73B ''either'':181B ''embodi'':108B ''especi'':142B ''even'':56B ''fear'':138B ''follow'':206B ''fond'':175B ''fork'':230B ''form'':128B ''four'':162B ''greymarch'':120B ''horripil'':232B ''hous'':166B ''humor'':21B ''icon'':215B ''imposs'':212B ''includ'':217B ''influenc'':170B ''interact'':184B ''isl'':26B ''jyggalag'':93B,123B ''khajiit'':145B ''known'':12B ''lead'':191B ''led'':116B ''legend'':87B ''look'':236B ''mad'':8B,41B,180B ''man'':74B ''mani'':140B ''mania'':33B ''manipul'':201B ''mark'':172B ''mental'':193B ''mind'':203B ''mortal'':54B,178B,244B ''mundan'':235B ''mundane-look'':234B ''natur'':86B ''notori'':44B ''oblivion'':30B ''often'':17B,52B ''one'':159B ''order'':98B ''plane'':28B ''play'':198B ''playth'':62B ''prank'':200B ''princ'':6B,59B,96B,106B ''reclaim'':126B ''recur'':119B ''reflect'':36B ''regard'':156B ''rever'':136B ''revert'':130B ''rule'':23B ''sadist'':48B ''seem'':211B ''sens'':19B ''sharpli'':80B ''sheogorath'':1A,2B,42B,90B,133B,134B ''sheogorath’'':214B ''shiver'':25B ''skooma'':150B ''staff'':221B ''target'':227B ''task'':213B ''tell'':88B ''torment'':243B ''transform'':225B ''treat'':53B ''troubl'':168B ''unpredict'':15B,83B,224B ''unravel'':194B ''use'':241B ''usual'':66B ''utensil'':239B ''wabbajack'':219B ''well'':71B ''well-dress'':70B ''whimsic'':50B ''wield'':75B ''would'':124B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
Sheogorath, the Daedric Prince of Madness, chaos, and creativity, rules the Shivering Isles, a realm divided into Mania and Dementia. Known for his unpredictable and cruel sense of humor, Sheogorath often treats mortals and even other Daedric Princes as playthings. Once Jyggalag, the Daedric Prince of Order, he was cursed to embody chaos, leading to the recurring Greymarch. Revered and feared across Tamriel, especially by the Khajiit and Dunmer, Sheogorath drives mortals to madness through his pranks and chaotic influence. His notable artifacts include the Wabbajack, a staff that unpredictably transforms targets, and the Fork of Horripilation, a cursed utensil used for torment.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_armor', 'Dwarven Armor is a basic dwarven chest piece with good protection quality. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. To craft it: 3 dwarven metal ingots, 1 iron ingot, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dwarvern ingot at a workbench.', '''1'':39B ''3'':35B,43B ''adept'':51B ''angular'':19B ''armor'':2A,4B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':48B ''bronz'':26B ''chest'':9B ''craft'':33B,54B ''design'':17B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,8B,36B ''dwarvern'':62B ''finish'':27B ''forg'':49B ''golden'':25B ''golden-bronz'':24B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':38B,41B,63B ''intric'':29B ''iron'':40B ''leather'':44B ''mechan'':30B ''metal'':37B ''ornat'':21B ''pattern'':31B ''piec'':10B ''protect'':13B ''qualiti'':14B ''smith'':52B ''strip'':45B ''tempered/improved'':59B ''use'':61B ''visual'':16B ''workbench'':66B', 'blacksmith', 'Dwarven Armor is a basic dwarven chest piece with good protection quality. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonplate_helmet', 'Dragonplate Helmet has brilliant protection quality .Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance.To craft it: 2 dragon scales, 1 dragon bone, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dragonbone at a workbench.', '''1'':30B ''2'':27B,34B ''appearance.to'':24B ''blacksmith'':39B ''bone'':19B,32B ''brilliant'':6B ''craft'':16B,25B,45B ''design'':11B ''dragon'':18B,28B,31B ''dragonbon'':53B ''dragonpl'':1A,3B ''forg'':40B ''helmet'':2A,4B ''jag'':15B ''leather'':35B ''master'':42B ''organ'':23B ''pale'':13B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''rough'':22B ''scale'':29B ''smith'':43B ''strip'':36B ''tempered/improved'':50B ''use'':52B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':56B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragonplate Helmet has brilliant protection quality. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sun_damage', 'These magical effects are offensive Destruction abilities that deal radiant damage specifically to undead, particularly vampires. This effect is only available as a spell, making it a potent weapon for combating unholy forces.', '''abil'':9B ''avail'':23B ''combat'':33B ''damag'':2A,13B ''deal'':11B ''destruct'':8B ''effect'':5B,20B ''forc'':35B ''magic'':4B ''make'':27B ''offens'':7B ''particular'':17B ''potent'':30B ''radiant'':12B ''specif'':14B ''spell'':26B ''sun'':1A ''undead'':16B ''unholi'':34B ''vampir'':18B ''weapon'':31B', 'mage', 'This spell harms undead creatures like vampires with radiant light, making it very effective. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedric_armor', 'Daedric Armor has Godly protection quality. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. To craft it: 1 Daedra heart, 5 ebony ingots, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using ebony at a workbench.', '''1'':33B ''3'':40B ''5'':36B ''accent'':24B ''armor'':2A,4B ''aura'':29B ''blacksmith'':45B ''craft'':31B,51B ''daedra'':34B ''daedric'':1A,3B ''dark'':13B ''design'':11B ''eboni'':37B,59B ''edg'':19B ''exud'':26B ''forg'':46B ''glow'':22B ''god'':6B ''heart'':35B ''ingot'':38B ''jag'':18B ''leather'':41B ''master'':48B ''menac'':15B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''red'':23B ''sharp'':17B ''sinist'':28B ''smith'':49B ''strip'':42B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''use'':58B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Daedric Armor has Godly protection quality. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('serpents_bluff_redoubt', 'Serpent''s Bluff Redoubt is a Forsworn camp and ancient ruin located atop a steep incline southwest of Rorikstead and east of the Old Hroldan Inn. The redoubt serves as a fortified refuge for the Forsworn and their hagraven matriarch, with a camp sprawling across the lower levels and a ruin hidden farther uphill.', '''across'':48B ''ancient'':13B ''atop'':16B ''bluff'':2A,6B ''camp'':11B,46B ''east'':24B ''farther'':56B ''forsworn'':10B,39B ''fortifi'':35B ''hagraven'':42B ''hidden'':55B ''hroldan'':28B ''inclin'':19B ''inn'':29B ''level'':51B ''locat'':15B ''lower'':50B ''matriarch'':43B ''old'':27B ''redoubt'':3A,7B,31B ''refug'':36B ''rorikstead'':22B ''ruin'':14B,54B ''serpent'':1A,4B ''serv'':32B ''southwest'':20B ''sprawl'':47B ''steep'':18B ''uphil'':57B', 'whiterun, forsworn', 'Serpent''s Bluff Redoubt is a Forsworn camp and ancient ruin located atop a steep incline southwest of Rorikstead.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('whitewatch_tower', 'Whitewatch Tower is a modest fortification located north-northeast of Whiterun and south of Loreius Farm, overlooking the plains of Whiterun Hold. The tower serves as a strategic outpost.

The structure consists of an intact eastern watchtower connected by an archway to the ruins of a western tower.', '''archway'':44B ''connect'':41B ''consist'':35B ''eastern'':39B ''farm'':19B ''fortif'':8B ''hold'':25B ''intact'':38B ''locat'':9B ''loreius'':18B ''modest'':7B ''north'':11B ''north-northeast'':10B ''northeast'':12B ''outpost'':32B ''overlook'':20B ''plain'':22B ''ruin'':47B ''serv'':28B ''south'':16B ''strateg'':31B ''structur'':34B ''tower'':2A,4B,27B,51B ''watchtow'':40B ''western'':50B ''whiterun'':14B,24B ''whitewatch'':1A,3B', 'whiterun', 'Whitewatch Tower is a modest fortification located north-northeast of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vampire_dust', 'Vampire Dust is a purpleish powder alchemical ingredient dropped by vampires, prized for its magical and restorative properties. Alchemy effects: Invisibility, Restore Magicka, Regenerate Health, and Cure Disease.', '''alchem'':9B ''alchemi'':21B ''cure'':29B ''diseas'':30B ''drop'':11B ''dust'':2A,4B ''effect'':22B ''health'':27B ''ingredi'':10B ''invis'':23B ''magic'':17B ''magicka'':25B ''powder'':8B ''prize'':14B ''properti'':20B ''purpleish'':7B ''regener'':26B ''restor'':19B,24B ''vampir'':1A,3B,13B', 'alchemist', 'Vampire Dust is a purpleish powder alchemical ingredient dropped by vampires, prized for its magical and restorative properties.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('throat_of_the_world', 'The Throat of the World, known as Monahven ("Mother Wind") in the language of dragons, is the highest mountain in all of Tamriel, dominating the landscape of Skyrim. Towering above the northern province, it was once rivaled only by Red Mountain before the latter''s catastrophic eruption in the Fourth Era. The mountain is home to the revered settlement of High Hrothgar, perched near its summit, where the Greybeards dwell in silence, dedicating their lives to the mastery of the Thu’um. The ascent to High Hrothgar is marked by the legendary "7,000 steps," a path rich with Nordic lore, including tales of King Wulfharth rebuilding the 418th step.

The Throat of the World holds profound significance for the Nords, often symbolizing their homeland as a whole. Also referred to as Snow Throat or Throat Mountain, it is one of the mystical Towers, ancient anchors of power in Tamriel. Prophecy links it to the destiny of the Dragonborn, foretelling a time when the "Snow Tower" will lie "sundered, kingless, bleeding," reflecting Skyrim’s turbulent history and uncertain future. This sacred peak stands as a testament to the power and mystery that define the land of the Nords.', '''000'':97B ''418th'':112B ''7'':96B ''also'':132B ''anchor'':149B ''ancient'':148B ''ascent'':87B ''bleed'':174B ''catastroph'':50B ''dedic'':77B ''defin'':195B ''destini'':159B ''domin'':28B ''dragon'':19B ''dragonborn'':162B ''dwell'':74B ''era'':55B ''erupt'':51B ''foretel'':163B ''fourth'':54B ''futur'':181B ''greybeard'':73B ''high'':65B,89B ''highest'':22B ''histori'':178B ''hold'':119B ''home'':59B ''homeland'':128B ''hrothgar'':66B,90B ''includ'':105B ''king'':108B ''kingless'':173B ''known'':10B ''land'':197B ''landscap'':30B ''languag'':17B ''latter'':48B ''legendari'':95B ''lie'':171B ''link'':155B ''live'':79B ''lore'':104B ''mark'':92B ''masteri'':82B ''monahven'':12B ''mother'':13B ''mountain'':23B,45B,57B,140B ''mysteri'':193B ''mystic'':146B ''near'':68B ''nord'':124B,200B ''nordic'':103B ''northern'':36B ''often'':125B ''one'':143B ''path'':100B ''peak'':184B ''perch'':67B ''power'':151B,191B ''profound'':120B ''propheci'':154B ''provinc'':37B ''rebuild'':110B ''red'':44B ''refer'':133B ''reflect'':175B ''rever'':62B ''rich'':101B ''rival'':41B ''sacr'':183B ''settlement'':63B ''signific'':121B ''silenc'':76B ''skyrim'':32B ''skyrim’'':176B ''snow'':136B,168B ''stand'':185B ''step'':98B,113B ''summit'':70B ''sunder'':172B ''symbol'':126B ''tale'':106B ''tamriel'':27B,153B ''testament'':188B ''throat'':1A,6B,115B,137B,139B ''thu’um'':85B ''time'':165B ''tower'':33B,147B,169B ''turbul'':177B ''uncertain'':180B ''whole'':131B ''wind'':14B ''world'':4A,9B,118B ''wulfharth'':109B', 'whiterun, dragon, scholar, nord', 'The Throat of the World, known as Monahven ("Mother Wind") in the language of dragons, is the highest mountain in all of Tamriel, dominating the landscape of Skyrim. Towering above the northern province, it was once rivaled only by Red Mountain before the latter''s catastrophic eruption in the Fourth Era. The mountain is home to the revered settlement of High Hrothgar, perched near its summit, where the Greybeards dwell in silence, dedicating their lives to the mastery of the Thu’um. The ascent to High Hrothgar is marked by the legendary "7,000 steps," a path rich with Nordic lore, including tales of King Wulfharth rebuilding the 418th step.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedric_helmet', 'Daedric Helmet has Godly protection quality. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. To craft it: 1 Daedra heart, 3 ebony ingots, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using ebony at a workbench.', '''1'':33B ''2'':40B ''3'':36B ''accent'':24B ''aura'':29B ''blacksmith'':45B ''craft'':31B,51B ''daedra'':34B ''daedric'':1A,3B ''dark'':13B ''design'':11B ''eboni'':37B,59B ''edg'':19B ''exud'':26B ''forg'':46B ''glow'':22B ''god'':6B ''heart'':35B ''helmet'':2A,4B ''ingot'':38B ''jag'':18B ''leather'':41B ''master'':48B ''menac'':15B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''red'':23B ''sharp'':17B ''sinist'':28B ''smith'':49B ''strip'':42B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''use'':58B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Daedric Helmet has Godly protection quality. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arkngthamz_puzzle', 'You will see four small blue orbs set in paddle-like extensions on a metal pole. The orbs will spin around the pole when activated.
Solution: Activating the orbs on the paddles will activate the resonator. When several kinetic resonators are combined into a tonal lock, the resonators must be activated in the correct order to solve the puzzle and open the corresponding gate.', '''activ'':28B,30B,37B,54B ''arkngthamz'':1A ''around'':24B ''blue'':8B ''combin'':45B ''correct'':57B ''correspond'':66B ''extens'':15B ''four'':6B ''gate'':67B ''kinet'':42B ''like'':14B ''lock'':49B ''metal'':18B ''must'':52B ''open'':64B ''orb'':9B,21B,32B ''order'':58B ''paddl'':13B,35B ''paddle-lik'':12B ''pole'':19B,26B ''puzzl'':2A,62B ''reson'':39B,43B,51B ''see'':5B ''set'':10B ''sever'':41B ''small'':7B ''solut'':29B ''solv'':60B ''spin'':23B ''tonal'':48B', 'puzzle', 'You have no idea what this puzzle is or how to solze it.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bone_break_fever', '
Bone Break Fever is a disease contracted from rats and bears, causing a loss of strength and stamina. It initially drains your stamina and progresses to more severe stages, draining up to even more stamina at its most crippling. If left untreated, the disease worsens, significantly reducing stamina and hindering the victim''s physical capabilities.', '''bear'':14B ''bone'':1A,4B ''break'':2A,5B ''capabl'':58B ''caus'':15B ''contract'':10B ''crippl'':42B ''diseas'':9B,47B ''drain'':24B,33B ''even'':36B ''fever'':3A,6B ''hinder'':53B ''initi'':23B ''left'':44B ''loss'':17B ''physic'':57B ''progress'':28B ''rat'':12B ''reduc'':50B ''sever'':31B ''signific'':49B ''stage'':32B ''stamina'':21B,26B,38B,51B ''strength'':19B ''untreat'':45B ''victim'':55B ''worsen'':48B', 'alchemist', '
Bone Break Fever is a disease contracted from rats and bears, causing a loss of strength and stamina. It initially drains your stamina and progresses to more severe stages, draining up to even more stamina at its most crippling. You do not know much else about this disease, but an alchemist would.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_white_phial', 'The White Phial is an alchemical shop located on the north side of Windhelm''s market district. It is owned by Nurelion, who named the shop after the legendary artifact he has spent many years searching for. When Nurelion is unavailable, his assistant, Quintus Navale, handles the shop duties. The White Phial itself is a legendary item, crafted from the magically infused snow that fell on the Throat of the World. It is said to have the ability to replenish any fluid placed inside of it, adding to its mystique and Nurelion''s obsession with finding it.', '''abil'':81B ''ad'':90B ''alchem'':9B ''artifact'':33B ''assist'':46B ''craft'':61B ''district'':20B ''duti'':52B ''fell'':68B ''find'':99B ''fluid'':85B ''handl'':49B ''infus'':65B ''insid'':87B ''item'':60B ''legendari'':32B,59B ''locat'':11B ''magic'':64B ''mani'':37B ''market'':19B ''mystiqu'':93B ''name'':27B ''naval'':48B ''north'':14B ''nurelion'':25B,42B,95B ''obsess'':97B ''own'':23B ''phial'':3A,6B,55B ''place'':86B ''quintus'':47B ''replenish'':83B ''said'':77B ''search'':39B ''shop'':10B,29B,51B ''side'':15B ''snow'':66B ''spent'':36B ''throat'':71B ''unavail'':44B ''white'':2A,5B,54B ''windhelm'':17B ''world'':74B ''year'':38B', 'eastmarch, alchemist', 'The White Phial is an alchemical shop located on the north side of Windhelm''s market district. The White Phial itself is a legendary item, crafted from the magically infused snow that fell on the Throat of the World. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('void_salts', 'Void Salts are blackish powder dropped by storm atronachs and are known for their potent magical properties. Alchemy effects: Weakness to Shock, Resist Magic, Damage Health, and Fortify Magicka.', '''alchemi'':20B ''atronach'':11B ''blackish'':6B ''damag'':27B ''drop'':8B ''effect'':21B ''fortifi'':30B ''health'':28B ''known'':14B ''magic'':18B,26B ''magicka'':31B ''potent'':17B ''powder'':7B ''properti'':19B ''resist'':25B ''salt'':2A,4B ''shock'':24B ''storm'':10B ''void'':1A,3B ''weak'':22B', 'alchemist', 'Void Salts are blackish powder dropped by storm atronachs and are known for their potent magical properties.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('an_accounting_of_the_scrolls', 'An Accounting of the Scrolls, written by Quintus Nerevelus, Former Imperial Librarian, is a reflective exploration of the mysteries surrounding the Elder Scrolls and the author''s personal journey into the Cult of the Ancestor Moth. The book begins with Nerevelus''s attempt to catalog the Scrolls to prevent theft or loss, only to confront their unquantifiable nature. His efforts reveal contradictions and anomalies, culminating in a moment where the number of Scrolls in a repository seemingly changes before his eyes. This experience leads him to abandon his skepticism and join the Cult to seek deeper understanding.

Thematically, the book delves into the limits of human comprehension, the allure of forbidden knowledge, and the transition from intellectual curiosity to spiritual surrender. This standalone work portrays the Elder Scrolls as enigmatic artifacts that defy conventional logic, underscoring their connection to fate, prophecy, and metaphysical truths beyond mortal grasp.', '''abandon'':92B ''account'':2A,7B ''allur'':114B ''ancestor'':40B ''anomali'':69B ''artifact'':136B ''attempt'':48B ''author'':31B ''begin'':44B ''beyond'':150B ''book'':43B,105B ''catalog'':50B ''chang'':83B ''comprehens'':112B ''confront'':60B ''connect'':143B ''contradict'':67B ''convent'':139B ''culmin'':70B ''cult'':37B,98B ''curios'':123B ''deeper'':101B ''defi'':138B ''delv'':106B ''effort'':65B ''elder'':27B,132B ''enigmat'':135B ''experi'':88B ''explor'':21B ''eye'':86B ''fate'':145B ''forbidden'':116B ''former'':15B ''grasp'':152B ''human'':111B ''imperi'':16B ''intellectu'':122B ''join'':96B ''journey'':34B ''knowledg'':117B ''lead'':89B ''librarian'':17B ''limit'':109B ''logic'':140B ''loss'':57B ''metaphys'':148B ''moment'':73B ''mortal'':151B ''moth'':41B ''mysteri'':24B ''natur'':63B ''nerevelus'':14B,46B ''number'':76B ''person'':33B ''portray'':130B ''prevent'':54B ''propheci'':146B ''quintus'':13B ''reflect'':20B ''repositori'':81B ''reveal'':66B ''scroll'':5A,10B,28B,52B,78B,133B ''seek'':100B ''seem'':82B ''skeptic'':94B ''spiritu'':125B ''standalon'':128B ''surrend'':126B ''surround'':25B ''theft'':55B ''themat'':103B ''transit'':120B ''truth'':149B ''underscor'':141B ''understand'':102B ''unquantifi'':62B ''work'':129B ''written'':11B', 'scholar', 'An Accounting of the Scrolls, written by Quintus Nerevelus, Former Imperial Librarian, explores the mysteries of the Elder Scrolls through the author''s attempts to catalog them, only to encounter their unquantifiable and paradoxical nature. The book reflects on the limits of human understanding, the allure of forbidden knowledge, and the shift from intellectual curiosity to spiritual surrender, portraying the Scrolls as enigmatic artifacts tied to fate and metaphysical truths beyond mortal comprehension.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nordic_arrow', 'Nordic Arrow  is an arrow that deals great damage. 
Its visual design is sturdy and intricate, with a silver-gray shaft, a sharp, engraved arrowhead, and dark, well-crafted fletching.  It can be crafted by an expert smith at a forge. 1 quicksilver ingot, 1 steel ingot, 1 firewood = 24 arrows.', '''1'':46B,49B,52B ''24'':54B ''arrow'':2A,4B,7B,55B ''arrowhead'':28B ''craft'':33B,38B ''damag'':11B ''dark'':30B ''deal'':9B ''design'':14B ''engrav'':27B ''expert'':41B ''firewood'':53B ''fletch'':34B ''forg'':45B ''gray'':23B ''great'':10B ''ingot'':48B,51B ''intric'':18B ''nordic'':1A,3B ''quicksilv'':47B ''shaft'':24B ''sharp'':26B ''silver'':22B ''silver-gray'':21B ''smith'':42B ''steel'':50B ''sturdi'':16B ''visual'':13B ''well'':32B ''well-craft'':31B', 'blacksmith', 'Nordic Arrow  is an arrow that deals great damage. 
Its visual design is sturdy and intricate, with a silver-gray shaft, a sharp, engraved arrowhead, and dark, well-crafted fletching.  You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('house_of_clan_shatter-shield', 'The House of Clan Shatter-Shield is a large residence on the western wall of Windhelm, located opposite Viola Giordano''s House and next door to Hjerim, which was formerly owned by their daughter Friga Shatter-Shield. The house is home to Torbjorn Shatter-Shield, his wife Tova, and their daughter Nilsine. The family is in mourning over the tragic loss of Friga, who was murdered.', '''clan'':3A,10B ''daughter'':41B,60B ''door'':32B ''famili'':63B ''former'':37B ''friga'':42B,72B ''giordano'':27B ''hjerim'':34B ''home'':49B ''hous'':1A,8B,29B,47B ''larg'':16B ''locat'':24B ''loss'':70B ''mourn'':66B ''murder'':75B ''next'':31B ''nilsin'':61B ''opposit'':25B ''own'':38B ''resid'':17B ''shatter'':5A,12B,44B,53B ''shatter-shield'':4A,11B,43B,52B ''shield'':6A,13B,45B,54B ''torbjorn'':51B ''tova'':57B ''tragic'':69B ''viola'':26B ''wall'':21B ''western'':20B ''wife'':56B ''windhelm'':23B', 'eastmarch', 'The House of Clan Shatter-Shield is a large residence on the western wall of Windhelm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('imp_gall', 'Imp Gall, a yellowish gall originating from Cyrodiil, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Damage Health, Weakness to Fire, Fortify Barter, and Cure Poison.', '''alchemi'':21B ''barter'':29B ''caravan'':20B ''cure'':31B ''cyrodiil'':10B ''damag'':23B ''effect'':22B ''fire'':27B ''fortifi'':28B ''gall'':2A,4B,7B ''health'':24B ''imp'':1A,3B ''ingredi'':13B ''khajiit'':19B ''origin'':8B ''poison'':32B ''purchas'':17B ''weak'':25B ''yellowish'':6B', 'alchemist', 'Imp Gall, a yellowish gall originating from Cyrodiil, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_greatsword', 'Dwarven Greatsword is a two-handed dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. To craft it: 2 dwarven metal ingots, 2 steel ingots, 2 iron ingots, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dwarvern ingot at a workbench.', '''2'':36B,40B,43B ''3'':47B ''adept'':55B ''angular'':20B ''blacksmith'':52B ''bronz'':27B ''craft'':34B,58B ''damag'':15B ''deal'':13B ''design'':18B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,10B,37B ''dwarvern'':66B ''finish'':28B ''forg'':53B ''golden'':26B ''golden-bronz'':25B ''good'':14B ''greatsword'':2A,4B ''hand'':9B ''ingot'':39B,42B,45B,67B ''intric'':30B ''iron'':44B ''leather'':48B ''mechan'':31B ''metal'':38B ''ornat'':22B ''pattern'':32B ''smith'':56B ''steel'':41B ''strip'':49B ''tempered/improved'':63B ''two'':8B ''two-hand'':7B ''use'':65B ''visual'':17B ''weapon'':11B ''workbench'':70B', 'blacksmith', 'Dwarven Greatsword is a two-handed dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('half-moon_mill', 'Half-Moon Mill is a location on the southwest shore of Lake Ilinalta in Falkreath Hold, situated west of The Lady Stone and east of Hunter''s Rest. Accessible via the road leading north from Falkreath toward Rorikstead, it serves as a lumber mill supplying both Helgen and Falkreath.

Operated by Hert and Hern, the mill consists of a wood mill and a butcher shack on the east side of a salmon-filled stream, with a wooden bridge connecting to their cabin on the west. There are rumors of people going missing around the mill.', '''access'':34B ''around'':99B ''bridg'':84B ''butcher'':69B ''cabin'':88B ''connect'':85B ''consist'':62B ''east'':29B,73B ''falkreath'':20B,41B,54B ''fill'':79B ''go'':97B ''half'':2A,6B ''half-moon'':1A,5B ''helgen'':52B ''hern'':59B ''hert'':57B ''hold'':21B ''hunter'':31B ''ilinalta'':18B ''ladi'':26B ''lake'':17B ''lead'':38B ''locat'':11B ''lumber'':48B ''mill'':4A,8B,49B,61B,66B,101B ''miss'':98B ''moon'':3A,7B ''north'':39B ''oper'':55B ''peopl'':96B ''rest'':33B ''road'':37B ''rorikstead'':43B ''rumor'':94B ''salmon'':78B ''salmon-fil'':77B ''serv'':45B ''shack'':70B ''shore'':15B ''side'':74B ''situat'':22B ''southwest'':14B ''stone'':27B ''stream'':80B ''suppli'':50B ''toward'':42B ''via'':35B ''west'':23B,91B ''wood'':65B ''wooden'':83B', 'falkreath', 'Half-Moon Mill is a location on the southwest shore of Lake Ilinalta in Falkreath Hold. You do not know who operates the mill.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('anise''s_cabin', 'Anise''s Cabin is a small shack located west-southwest of Riverwood in Falkreath Hold, near the Guardian Stones to the south and Bleak Falls Barrow to the north. The cabin lies close to your escape route from Helgen, making it an early point of interest for travelers.

The sole occupant, Anise, is an elderly Nord woman who is rumored to be a witch.', '''anis'':1A,4B,56B ''barrow'':30B ''bleak'':28B ''cabin'':3A,6B,35B ''close'':37B ''earli'':47B ''elder'':59B ''escap'':40B ''falkreath'':18B ''fall'':29B ''guardian'':22B ''helgen'':43B ''hold'':19B ''interest'':50B ''lie'':36B ''locat'':11B ''make'':44B ''near'':20B ''nord'':60B ''north'':33B ''occup'':55B ''point'':48B ''riverwood'':16B ''rout'':41B ''rumor'':64B ''shack'':10B ''small'':9B ''sole'':54B ''south'':26B ''southwest'':14B ''stone'':23B ''travel'':52B ''west'':13B ''west-southwest'':12B ''witch'':68B ''woman'':61B', 'falkreath', 'Anise''s Cabin is a small shack located west-southwest of Riverwood in Falkreath Hold, to the south and Bleak Falls Barrow. You do not know anything about who Ansie is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_arrow', 'Steel Arrow  is an arrow that deals standard damage. 
Its visual design is simple and practical, with a polished metal shaft, a sharp steel arrowhead, and plain feathered fletching.It can be crafted by an adept smith at a forge. 1 steel ingot, 1 firewood = 24 arrows.', '''1'':42B,45B ''24'':47B ''adept'':37B ''arrow'':2A,4B,7B,48B ''arrowhead'':27B ''craft'':34B ''damag'':11B ''deal'':9B ''design'':14B ''feather'':30B ''firewood'':46B ''fletching.it'':31B ''forg'':41B ''ingot'':44B ''metal'':22B ''plain'':29B ''polish'':21B ''practic'':18B ''shaft'':23B ''sharp'':25B ''simpl'':16B ''smith'':38B ''standard'':10B ''steel'':1A,3B,26B,43B ''visual'':13B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel Arrow  is an arrow that deals standard damage. 
Its visual design is simple and practical, with a polished metal shaft, a sharp steel arrowhead, and plain feathered fletching.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('second_treaty_of_stros_mkai', 'The Second Treaty of Stros M''Kai, signed in 4E 180, marked a significant turning point in the relationship between the Aldmeri Dominion and the Redguards of Hammerfell. This treaty concluded a decade-long conflict that arose from the Dominion''s attempts to conquer Hammerfell, which had reached a stalemate. As part of the treaty''s conditions, the Aldmeri Dominion was required to withdraw all military forces from the region, solidifying Hammerfell''s status as an independent nation, albeit a diminished one.

The treaty''s aftermath left lingering tensions between Hammerfell and the Empire. Many Redguards viewed Emperor Titus Mede II''s earlier acceptance of the White-Gold Concordat, which had concluded the Great War, as a betrayal. This agreement had required the cession of significant territory in Hammerfell to the Dominion and ultimately led to the Empire renouncing Hammerfell as a province when it protested the treaty''s terms. In response to these events, a clandestine organization known as the Remnants was formed in Hammerfell, tasked with ensuring that the Aldmeri Dominion adhered to the treaty and investigating any potential violations.', '''180'':16B ''4e'':15B ''accept'':110B ''adher'':181B ''aftermath'':92B ''agreement'':127B ''albeit'':85B ''aldmeri'':27B,65B,179B ''aros'':43B ''attempt'':48B ''betray'':125B ''cession'':131B ''clandestin'':164B ''conclud'':36B,119B ''concordat'':116B ''condit'':63B ''conflict'':41B ''conquer'':50B ''decad'':39B ''decade-long'':38B ''diminish'':87B ''dominion'':28B,46B,66B,139B,180B ''earlier'':109B ''emperor'':104B ''empir'':100B,145B ''ensur'':176B ''event'':162B ''forc'':73B ''form'':171B ''gold'':115B ''great'':121B ''hammerfel'':33B,51B,78B,97B,136B,147B,173B ''ii'':107B ''independ'':83B ''investig'':186B ''kai'':12B ''known'':166B ''led'':142B ''left'':93B ''linger'':94B ''long'':40B ''m'':11B ''mani'':101B ''mark'':17B ''mede'':106B ''militari'':72B ''mkai'':5A ''nation'':84B ''one'':88B ''organ'':165B ''part'':58B ''point'':21B ''potenti'':188B ''protest'':153B ''provinc'':150B ''reach'':54B ''redguard'':31B,102B ''region'':76B ''relationship'':24B ''remnant'':169B ''renounc'':146B ''requir'':68B,129B ''respons'':159B ''second'':1A,7B ''sign'':13B ''signific'':19B,133B ''solidifi'':77B ''stalem'':56B ''status'':80B ''stros'':4A,10B ''task'':174B ''tension'':95B ''term'':157B ''territori'':134B ''titus'':105B ''treati'':2A,8B,35B,61B,90B,155B,184B ''turn'':20B ''ultim'':141B ''view'':103B ''violat'':189B ''war'':122B ''white'':114B ''white-gold'':113B ''withdraw'':70B', 'redguard, scholar, noble', 'The Second Treaty of Stros M''Kai, signed in 4E 180, ended a decade-long conflict between the Aldmeri Dominion and the Redguards of Hammerfell. The treaty required the Dominion to withdraw its forces, confirming Hammerfell''s independence but leaving the nation weakened. The treaty followed tensions sparked by Emperor Titus Mede II''s acceptance of the White-Gold Concordat, which ceded Hammerfell territory to the Dominion. Hammerfell''s protest against these terms led to its renouncement as an Imperial province. In the aftermath, the clandestine group known as the Remnants formed to monitor Dominion compliance and address potential treaty violations.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vigil_of_stendarr', 'The Vigil of Stendarr is a devout order of holy warriors dedicated to the eradication of Daedra, vampires, werewolves, witches, and other so-called "abominations" in the name of the god Stendarr, the Divine of Mercy. Vigilants of Stendarr are often found patrolling the roads of Skyrim in their quest to rid the land of these creatures. They offer healing services, including curing diseases, to those they encounter on their travels. The order''s main base in Skyrim is the Hall of the Vigilant, located south of Dawnstar, though they also maintain a presence at Stendarr''s Beacon in The Rift.', '''abomin'':29B ''also'':95B ''base'':80B ''beacon'':102B ''call'':28B ''creatur'':61B ''cure'':67B ''daedra'':20B ''dawnstar'':92B ''dedic'':15B ''devout'':10B ''diseas'':68B ''divin'':38B ''encount'':72B ''erad'':18B ''found'':46B ''god'':35B ''hall'':85B ''heal'':64B ''holi'':13B ''includ'':66B ''land'':58B ''locat'':89B ''main'':79B ''maintain'':96B ''merci'':40B ''name'':32B ''offer'':63B ''often'':45B ''order'':11B,77B ''patrol'':47B ''presenc'':98B ''quest'':54B ''rid'':56B ''rift'':105B ''road'':49B ''servic'':65B ''skyrim'':51B,82B ''so-cal'':26B ''south'':90B ''stendarr'':3A,7B,36B,43B,100B ''though'':93B ''travel'':75B ''vampir'':21B ''vigil'':1A,5B,41B,88B ''warrior'':14B ''werewolv'':22B ''witch'':23B', 'dawnguard, priest, daedric, daedra, noble', '
The Vigil of Stendarr is a holy order dedicated to eradicating Daedra, vampires, werewolves, witches, and other "abominations" in the name of Stendarr, the Divine of Mercy. Vigilants patrol Skyrim''s roads, offering healing services and curing diseases. Their main base, the Hall of the Vigilant, is south of Dawnstar, with an additional presence at Stendarr''s Beacon in The Rift.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_bow', 'Dwarven Bow is a ranged dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. To craft it: 2 dwarven metal ingots and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dwarvern ingot at a workbench.', '''1'':39B ''2'':34B ''adept'':47B ''angular'':18B ''blacksmith'':44B ''bow'':2A,4B ''bronz'':25B ''craft'':32B,50B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,8B,35B ''dwarvern'':58B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':45B ''golden'':24B ''golden-bronz'':23B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':37B,59B ''intric'':28B ''leather'':40B ''mechan'':29B ''metal'':36B ''ornat'':20B ''pattern'':30B ''rang'':7B ''smith'':48B ''strip'':41B ''tempered/improved'':55B ''use'':57B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Dwarven Bow is a ranged dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_plate_gauntlets', 'Steel Plate Gauntlets are a pair of steel plate gauntlets with good protection quality. Its visual design is robust and practical, with polished steel surfaces and reinforced plates that emphasize durability and function. To craft it: 1 steel ingot, 1 corundum ingot, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''1'':40B,43B ''2'':47B ''adept'':55B ''blacksmith'':52B ''corundum'':44B ''craft'':38B,58B ''design'':20B ''durabl'':34B ''emphas'':33B ''forg'':53B ''function'':36B ''gauntlet'':3A,6B,13B ''good'':15B ''ingot'':42B,45B ''leather'':48B ''pair'':9B ''plate'':2A,5B,12B,31B ''polish'':26B ''practic'':24B ''protect'':16B ''qualiti'':17B ''reinforc'':30B ''robust'':22B ''smith'':56B ''steel'':1A,4B,11B,27B,41B,66B ''strip'':49B ''surfac'':28B ''tempered/improved'':63B ''use'':65B ''visual'':19B ''workbench'':69B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel Plate Gauntlets are a pair of steel plate gauntlets with good protection quality. Its visual design is robust and practical, with polished steel surfaces and reinforced plates that emphasize durability and function. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('blister_pod_cap', 'Blister Pod Cap is an ingredient originating from the Shivering Isles, and can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Restore Magicka , Fortify Magicka, Night Eye, and Invisibility.', '''alchemi'':22B ''blister'':1A,4B ''cap'':3A,6B ''caravan'':21B ''effect'':23B ''eye'':29B ''fortifi'':26B ''ingredi'':9B ''invis'':31B ''isl'':14B ''khajiit'':20B ''magicka'':25B,27B ''night'':28B ''origin'':10B ''pod'':2A,5B ''purchas'':18B ''restor'':24B ''shiver'':13B', 'alchemist', 'Blister Pod Cap is an ingredient originating from the Shivering Isles, and can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
