You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortified_combat_healing', 'These magical effects are restorative Restoration enchantments that enhance the caster;s ability to regenerate health during combat. This effect is only available on enchanted items, providing warriors with sustained recovery in prolonged battles.', '''abil'':16B ''avail'':26B ''battl'':37B ''caster'':14B ''combat'':2A,21B ''effect'':6B,23B ''enchant'':10B,28B ''enhanc'':12B ''fortifi'':1A ''heal'':3A ''health'':19B ''item'':29B ''magic'':5B ''prolong'':36B ''provid'':30B ''recoveri'':34B ''regener'':18B ''restor'':8B,9B ''sustain'':33B ''warrior'':31B', 'mage', 'This enchantment helps you heal faster during fights, keeping you alive longer. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_plate_helmet', 'Steel Plate Helmet is a basic steel plate helmet with good protection quality. Its visual design is robust and practical, with polished steel surfaces and reinforced plates that emphasize durability and function. To craft it: 2 steel ingots, 1 corundum ingot, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''1'':42B,46B ''2'':39B ''adept'':54B ''basic'':9B ''blacksmith'':51B ''corundum'':43B ''craft'':37B,57B ''design'':19B ''durabl'':33B ''emphas'':32B ''forg'':52B ''function'':35B ''good'':14B ''helmet'':3A,6B,12B ''ingot'':41B,44B ''leather'':47B ''plate'':2A,5B,11B,30B ''polish'':25B ''practic'':23B ''protect'':15B ''qualiti'':16B ''reinforc'':29B ''robust'':21B ''smith'':55B ''steel'':1A,4B,10B,26B,40B,65B ''strip'':48B ''surfac'':27B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''use'':64B ''visual'':18B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel Plate Helmet is a basic steel plate helmet with good protection quality. Its visual design is robust and practical, with polished steel surfaces and reinforced plates that emphasize durability and function.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('banded_iron_shield', 'Hide Shield is a basic hide shield with little protection quality. Its visual design is rugged and reinforced, combining dark, weathered metal with additional banded plates for extra protection. To craft it: 4 iron ingot, and 1 corrundum ingots and 1 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Novice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''1'':40B,44B ''4'':36B ''addit'':27B ''band'':1A,28B ''basic'':8B ''blacksmith'':49B ''combin'':22B ''corrundum'':41B ''craft'':34B,55B ''dark'':23B ''design'':17B ''extra'':31B ''forg'':50B ''hide'':4B,9B ''ingot'':38B,42B ''iron'':2A,37B,63B ''leather'':45B ''littl'':12B ''metal'':25B ''novic'':52B ''plate'':29B ''protect'':13B,32B ''qualiti'':14B ''reinforc'':21B ''rug'':19B ''shield'':3A,5B,10B ''smith'':53B ''strip'':46B ''tempered/improved'':60B ''use'':62B ''visual'':16B ''weather'':24B ''workbench'':66B', 'blacksmith', 'Hide Shield is a basic hide shield with little protection quality. Its visual design is rugged and reinforced, combining dark, weathered metal with additional banded plates for extra protection. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nordic_sword', 'Nordic Sword is a basic Nordic weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. To craft it: 1 quicksilver ingot, 2 leather strips, and 1 steel ingot at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using quicksilver at a workbench.', '''1'':38B,45B ''2'':41B ''adept'':53B ''ancient'':33B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':50B ''craft'':36B,56B ''craftsmanship'':34B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''engrav'':30B ''evok'':32B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':51B ''good'':12B ''gray'':25B ''ingot'':40B,47B ''intric'':28B ''leather'':42B ''nordic'':1A,3B,8B,29B ''quicksilv'':39B,64B ''silver'':24B ''silver-gray'':23B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':46B ''strip'':43B ''sturdi'':18B ''sword'':2A,4B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''weather'':20B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Nordic Sword is a basic Nordic weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bound_dagger', 'Bound Dagger is a Conjuration spell that summons a magical dagger made of Daedric energy, which functions as a temporary weapon. It requires a Novice skill level to cast.', '''bound'':1A,3B ''cast'':31B ''conjur'':7B ''daedric'':16B ''dagger'':2A,4B,13B ''energi'':17B ''function'':19B ''level'':29B ''made'':14B ''magic'':12B ''novic'':27B ''requir'':25B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':8B ''summon'':10B ''temporari'':22B ''weapon'':23B', 'mage', '
Bound Dagger is a spell that summons a magical dagger made of Daedric energy, giving the caster a temporary weapon to use in combat. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('coda_flower', 'Coda Flower is a bright blue flower that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans originating from Vvardenfell.. Alchemy effects: Damage Health, Lingering Damage Stamina, Ravage Magicka, and Fortify Carry Weight.', '''..'':20B ''alchemi'':21B ''blue'':8B ''bright'':7B ''caravan'':16B ''carri'':32B ''coda'':1A,3B ''damag'':23B,26B ''effect'':22B ''flower'':2A,4B,9B ''fortifi'':31B ''health'':24B ''khajiit'':15B ''linger'':25B ''magicka'':29B ''origin'':17B ''purchas'':13B ''ravag'':28B ''stamina'':27B ''vvardenfel'':19B ''weight'':33B', 'alchemist', 'Coda Flower is a bright blue flower that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans originating from Vvardenfell.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hrodulf''s_house', 'Hrodulf''s House is an abandoned shack located southwest of Fort Frostmoth and southeast of Kolbjorn Barrow on Solstheim.', '''abandon'':9B ''barrow'':20B ''fort'':14B ''frostmoth'':15B ''hous'':3A,6B ''hrodulf'':1A,4B ''kolbjorn'':19B ''locat'':11B ''shack'':10B ''solstheim'':22B ''southeast'':17B ''southwest'':12B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('amren''s_house', 'Amren''s House is a modest residence located in the Wind District of Whiterun, nestled beside Uthgerd''s House and directly across from the House of Clan Battle-Born. This cozy home serves as the dwelling of Amren, a Redguard warrior, his wife Saffir, and their spirited daughter Braith.', '''across'':25B ''amren'':1A,4B,42B ''battl'':32B ''battle-born'':31B ''besid'':19B ''born'':33B ''braith'':53B ''clan'':30B ''cozi'':35B ''daughter'':52B ''direct'':24B ''district'':15B ''dwell'':40B ''home'':36B ''hous'':3A,6B,22B,28B ''locat'':11B ''modest'':9B ''nestl'':18B ''redguard'':44B ''resid'':10B ''saffir'':48B ''serv'':37B ''spirit'':51B ''uthgerd'':20B ''warrior'':45B ''whiterun'':17B ''wife'':47B ''wind'':14B', 'whiterun', 'Amren''s House is a modest residence located in the Wind District of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedric_greatsword', 'Daedric Greatsword is a two-handed Daedric weapon which deals Godly damage. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. To craft it: 1 Daedra heart, 5 ebony ingots, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using ebony at a workbench.', '''1'':40B ''3'':47B ''5'':43B ''accent'':31B ''aura'':36B ''blacksmith'':52B ''craft'':38B,58B ''daedra'':41B ''daedric'':1A,3B,10B ''damag'':15B ''dark'':20B ''deal'':13B ''design'':18B ''eboni'':44B,66B ''edg'':26B ''exud'':33B ''forg'':53B ''glow'':29B ''god'':14B ''greatsword'':2A,4B ''hand'':9B ''heart'':42B ''ingot'':45B ''jag'':25B ''leather'':48B ''master'':55B ''menac'':22B ''red'':30B ''sharp'':24B ''sinist'':35B ''smith'':56B ''strip'':49B ''tempered/improved'':63B ''two'':8B ''two-hand'':7B ''use'':65B ''visual'':17B ''weapon'':11B ''workbench'':69B', 'blacksmith', 'Daedric Greatsword is a two-handed Daedric weapon which deals Godly damage. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('khajiit', 'The Khajiit are a feline race native to the province of Elsweyr, known for their agility, intelligence, and distinctive cat-like appearance. They are skilled in acrobatics, stealth, and make excellent thieves, but they are also capable warriors and traders. Although Khajiit are rarely mages, their unique physical traits, such as fur, tails, and digitigrade walking, set them apart from both men and mer. These differences have led to their classification as one of Tamriel''s "beast races," alongside Argonians and Imga. The Khajiit are known for their love of moon sugar, an integral part of their culture and economy, which is often refined into the addictive substance skooma.

Khajiit society is structured around clans and their relationship with the phases of Nirn''s moons, Masser and Secunda, which influence their physiology and determine their form upon birth. The Khajiit exhibit a wide variety of shapes, from bipedal, human-like figures to quadrupedal, more animalistic forms. Their homeland of Elsweyr is a land of deserts and jungles, where they have developed a rich cultural heritage with distinct architecture, art, and traditions. Despite facing racial prejudice across Tamriel, Khajiit are proud of their heritage and the unique contributions they bring to Tamrielic society.', '''acrobat'':29B ''across'':189B ''addict'':109B ''agil'':17B ''alongsid'':81B ''also'':38B ''although'':43B ''animalist'':158B ''apart'':61B ''appear'':24B ''architectur'':181B ''argonian'':82B ''around'':116B ''art'':182B ''beast'':79B ''biped'':150B ''birth'':140B ''bring'':202B ''capabl'':39B ''cat'':22B ''cat-lik'':21B ''clan'':117B ''classif'':73B ''contribut'':200B ''cultur'':100B,177B ''desert'':168B ''despit'':185B ''determin'':136B ''develop'':174B ''differ'':68B ''digitigrad'':57B ''distinct'':20B,180B ''economi'':102B ''elsweyr'':13B,163B ''excel'':33B ''exhibit'':143B ''face'':186B ''felin'':6B ''figur'':154B ''form'':138B,159B ''fur'':54B ''heritag'':178B,196B ''homeland'':161B ''human'':152B ''human-lik'':151B ''imga'':84B ''influenc'':132B ''integr'':96B ''intellig'':18B ''jungl'':170B ''khajiit'':1A,3B,44B,86B,112B,142B,191B ''known'':14B,88B ''land'':166B ''led'':70B ''like'':23B,153B ''love'':91B ''mage'':47B ''make'':32B ''masser'':128B ''men'':64B ''mer'':66B ''moon'':93B,127B ''nativ'':8B ''nirn'':125B ''often'':105B ''one'':75B ''part'':97B ''phase'':123B ''physic'':50B ''physiolog'':134B ''prejudic'':188B ''proud'':193B ''provinc'':11B ''quadruped'':156B ''race'':7B,80B ''racial'':187B ''rare'':46B ''refin'':106B ''relationship'':120B ''rich'':176B ''secunda'':130B ''set'':59B ''shape'':148B ''skill'':27B ''skooma'':111B ''societi'':113B,205B ''stealth'':30B ''structur'':115B ''substanc'':110B ''sugar'':94B ''tail'':55B ''tamriel'':77B,190B,204B ''thiev'':34B ''trader'':42B ''tradit'':184B ''trait'':51B ''uniqu'':49B,199B ''upon'':139B ''varieti'':146B ''walk'':58B ''warrior'':40B ''wide'':145B', 'khajiit, scholar', '
The Khajiit are a feline race from Elsweyr, known for their agility, stealth, and distinctive cat-like traits such as fur, tails, and digitigrade walking. Skilled as thieves, warriors, and traders, they are tied to the moons Masser and Secunda, which influence their form at birth. Their culture revolves around moon sugar, central to their economy and traditions, though its refinement into skooma has caused controversy. Despite facing prejudice, the Khajiit take pride in their rich heritage, vibrant arts, and unique contributions to Tamrielic society.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cornberry', 'Comberry, a red berry originating from Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina, Spell Absorption, Restore Magicka, and Fortify Destruction.', '''absorpt'':24B ''alchemi'':19B ''berri'':5B ''caravan'':18B ''comberri'':2B ''cornberri'':1A ''damag'':21B ''destruct'':29B ''effect'':20B ''fortifi'':28B ''ingredi'':11B ''khajiit'':17B ''magicka'':26B ''origin'':6B ''purchas'':15B ''red'':4B ''restor'':25B ''spell'':23B ''stamina'':22B ''vvardenfel'':8B', 'alchemist', 'Comberry, a red berry originating from Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonbone', 'Dragon items are high-quality armor and weapons made from dragon parts, including light Dragonscale Armor and heavy Dragonplate Armor. These can be crafted with the Dragon Armor perk, which requires a master Blacksmith .', '''armor'':8B,18B,22B,30B ''blacksmith'':36B ''craft'':26B ''dragon'':2B,13B,29B ''dragonbon'':1A ''dragonpl'':21B ''dragonscal'':17B ''heavi'':20B ''high'':6B ''high-qual'':5B ''includ'':15B ''item'':3B ''light'':16B ''made'':11B ''master'':35B ''part'':14B ''perk'':31B ''qualiti'':7B ''requir'':33B ''weapon'':10B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragon Bone is used to craft powerful dragon armor and weapons from only the most masterful blacksmiths.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedric_warhammer', 'Daedric Warhammer is a massive Daedric weapon which deals Godly damage. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. To craft it: 1 Daedra heart, 5 ebony ingots, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using ebony at a workbench.', '''1'':38B ''3'':45B ''5'':41B ''accent'':29B ''aura'':34B ''blacksmith'':50B ''craft'':36B,56B ''daedra'':39B ''daedric'':1A,3B,8B ''damag'':13B ''dark'':18B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''eboni'':42B,64B ''edg'':24B ''exud'':31B ''forg'':51B ''glow'':27B ''god'':12B ''heart'':40B ''ingot'':43B ''jag'':23B ''leather'':46B ''massiv'':7B ''master'':53B ''menac'':20B ''red'':28B ''sharp'':22B ''sinist'':33B ''smith'':54B ''strip'':47B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''warhamm'':2A,4B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Daedric Warhammer is a massive Daedric weapon which deals Godly damage. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fury', 'Fury is an Illusion spell that causes a target to become enraged, making them attack anything in their path, including allies. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''alli'':22B ''anyth'':17B ''apprentic'':26B ''attack'':16B ''becom'':12B ''cast'':30B ''caus'':8B ''enrag'':13B ''furi'':1A,2B ''illus'':5B ''includ'':21B ''level'':28B ''make'':14B ''path'':20B ''requir'':24B ''skill'':27B ''spell'':6B ''target'':10B', 'mage', 'Fury is a spell that causes a target to become enraged, making them attack anything in their path, including allies. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thalmor', 'The Thalmor are the ruling government of the Third Aldmeri Dominion, a political and military alliance between the Altmer (High Elves) and Bosmer (Wood Elves). They promote a supremacist ideology, seeking to establish Mer (Elves) as racially superior to Men and to extend their control across Tamriel. By 4E 201, the Thalmor have a significant presence in Skyrim, where they enforce the White-Gold Concordat, a peace treaty signed after the Great War between the Empire and the Aldmeri Dominion. One of the treaty''s key provisions is the banning of Talos worship, a point of great contention between the Thalmor and many Nords.

In Skyrim, the Thalmor operate from their embassy in Haafingar, north of Solitude, and use Northwatch Keep as a detention center for political prisoners. Thalmor Justiciars, who act as enforcers of their policies, can often be seen traveling Skyrim''s roads, sometimes escorting prisoners. While they may not initially show hostility, questioning them about Talos or other sensitive topics can provoke aggressive responses. The Thalmor''s activities and their enforcement of the ban on Talos worship have fueled resentment among Skyrim''s populace, particularly among Stormcloak rebels who oppose both the Empire and the Dominion.', '''201'':51B ''4e'':50B ''across'':47B ''act'':134B ''activ'':173B ''aggress'':168B ''aldmeri'':11B,81B ''allianc'':17B ''altmer'':20B ''among'':186B,191B ''ban'':92B,179B ''bosmer'':24B ''center'':127B ''concordat'':67B ''content'':100B ''control'':46B ''detent'':126B ''dominion'':12B,82B,201B ''elv'':22B,26B,36B ''embassi'':114B ''empir'':78B,198B ''enforc'':62B,136B,176B ''escort'':149B ''establish'':34B ''extend'':44B ''fuel'':184B ''gold'':66B ''govern'':7B ''great'':74B,99B ''haafingar'':116B ''high'':21B ''hostil'':157B ''ideolog'':31B ''initi'':155B ''justiciar'':132B ''keep'':123B ''key'':88B ''mani'':105B ''may'':153B ''men'':41B ''mer'':35B ''militari'':16B ''nord'':106B ''north'':117B ''northwatch'':122B ''often'':141B ''one'':83B ''oper'':111B ''oppos'':195B ''particular'':190B ''peac'':69B ''point'':97B ''polici'':139B ''polit'':14B,129B ''populac'':189B ''presenc'':57B ''prison'':130B,150B ''promot'':28B ''provis'':89B ''provok'':167B ''question'':158B ''racial'':38B ''rebel'':193B ''resent'':185B ''respons'':169B ''road'':147B ''rule'':6B ''seek'':32B ''seen'':143B ''sensit'':164B ''show'':156B ''sign'':71B ''signific'':56B ''skyrim'':59B,108B,145B,187B ''solitud'':119B ''sometim'':148B ''stormcloak'':192B ''superior'':39B ''supremacist'':30B ''talo'':94B,161B,181B ''tamriel'':48B ''thalmor'':1A,3B,53B,103B,110B,131B,171B ''third'':10B ''topic'':165B ''travel'':144B ''treati'':70B,86B ''use'':121B ''war'':75B ''white'':65B ''white-gold'':64B ''wood'':25B ''worship'':95B,182B', 'thalmor, highelf, woodelf, redguard, noble', '
The Thalmor are the ruling government of the Third Aldmeri Dominion, an alliance of Altmer and Bosmer promoting elven supremacy and seeking dominance over Tamriel. By 4E 201, they enforce the White-Gold Concordat in Skyrim, including the controversial ban on Talos worship, sparking resentment among Nords, especially Stormcloak rebels. Operating from their embassy near Solitude and using Northwatch Keep as a detention center, Thalmor Justiciars patrol Skyrim''s roads, enforcing their policies and suppressing dissent.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stalhrim_battleaxe', 'Stalhrim Battleaxe is a heavy stalhrim weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding. To craft it: 5 stalhrim and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it.
 It can be tempered/improved by using stalhrim at a workbench.', '''2'':37B ''5'':34B ''appear'':27B ''battleax'':2A,4B ''blacksmith'':42B ''blue'':24B ''cold'':28B ''craft'':32B,48B ''crystallin'':20B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''expert'':45B ''fantast'':12B ''forg'':43B ''frosti'':23B ''heavi'':7B ''ici'':18B ''leather'':38B ''sheen'':25B ''smith'':46B ''stalhrim'':1A,3B,8B,35B,56B ''strip'':39B ''tempered/improved'':53B ''unyield'':30B ''use'':55B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':59B', 'blacksmith', 'Stalhrim Battleaxe is a heavy stalhrim weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_drunken_huntsman', 'The Drunken Huntsman is a lively tavern and hunting supply store located in Whiterun, directly across the street from Breezehome. A favorite among hunters and adventurers, the establishment combines the warmth of a traditional tavern with the practicality of a well-stocked supply shop.

Owned and managed by Elrindir, the Drunken Huntsman offers a range of goods, including weapons, armor, food, and various miscellaneous items, catering to both seasoned travelers and local patrons. Open daily from 8 a.m. to 8 p.m.', '''8'':81B,84B ''a.m'':82B ''across'':19B ''adventur'':29B ''among'':26B ''armor'':64B ''breezehom'':23B ''cater'':70B ''combin'':32B ''daili'':79B ''direct'':18B ''drunken'':2A,5B,55B ''elrindir'':53B ''establish'':31B ''favorit'':25B ''food'':65B ''good'':61B ''hunt'':12B ''hunter'':27B ''huntsman'':3A,6B,56B ''includ'':62B ''item'':69B ''live'':9B ''local'':76B ''locat'':15B ''manag'':51B ''miscellan'':68B ''offer'':57B ''open'':78B ''own'':49B ''p.m'':85B ''patron'':77B ''practic'':41B ''rang'':59B ''season'':73B ''shop'':48B ''stock'':46B ''store'':14B ''street'':21B ''suppli'':13B,47B ''tavern'':10B,38B ''tradit'':37B ''travel'':74B ''various'':67B ''warmth'':34B ''weapon'':63B ''well'':45B ''well-stock'':44B ''whiterun'':17B', 'whiterun', 'The Drunken Huntsman is a lively tavern and hunting supply store located in Whiterun. You do not know who owns it.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('luna_moth_wing', 'Luna Moth Wings can be acquired by catching luna moths, which only come out at night but are easily spotted due to their glowing wings. Alchemy effects: Damage Magicka, Fortify Light Armor, Regenerate Health, and Invisibility.', '''acquir'':9B ''alchemi'':29B ''armor'':35B ''catch'':11B ''come'':16B ''damag'':31B ''due'':24B ''easili'':22B ''effect'':30B ''fortifi'':33B ''glow'':27B ''health'':37B ''invis'':39B ''light'':34B ''luna'':1A,4B,12B ''magicka'':32B ''moth'':2A,5B,13B ''night'':19B ''regener'':36B ''spot'':23B ''wing'':3A,6B,28B', 'alchemist', 'Luna Moth Wings can be acquired by catching luna moths, which only come out at night but are easily spotted due to their glowing wings. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ancestor_glade', 'The Ancestor Glade is a small, serene glade located east-southeast of Falkreath and northwest of Bloodlet Throne in Falkreath Hold. Situated within a cavern, it consists of a single zone, Ancestor Glade, and is one of the few such locations in Tamriel, as well as the only one in Skyrim.

The glade is home to swarms of ancestor moths and the rare yellow mountain flowers.', '''ancestor'':1A,4B,35B,62B ''bloodlet'':20B ''cavern'':28B ''consist'':30B ''east'':13B ''east-southeast'':12B ''falkreath'':16B,23B ''flower'':69B ''glade'':2A,5B,10B,36B,56B ''hold'':24B ''home'':58B ''locat'':11B,44B ''moth'':63B ''mountain'':68B ''northwest'':18B ''one'':39B,52B ''rare'':66B ''seren'':9B ''singl'':33B ''situat'':25B ''skyrim'':54B ''small'':8B ''southeast'':14B ''swarm'':60B ''tamriel'':46B ''throne'':21B ''well'':48B ''within'':26B ''yellow'':67B ''zone'':34B', 'dawnguard, vampire, volkihar, scholar', 'The Ancestor Glade is a small, serene glade located somewhere in the South of Skyrim, but you do not know where.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'falkreath', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gildergreen', 'The Gildergreen is a sacred tree located in the city of Whiterun, revered by worshippers of Kynareth and central to the city''s Temple of Kynareth. Planted during the early days of Whiterun''s settlement, the Gildergreen is said to have grown from a cutting or seedling of the ancient Eldergleam, one of the oldest living trees in Tamriel. The tree''s holiness is reflected in its name, which echoes that of its revered ancestor, and in the many pilgrims who have journeyed to Whiterun to hear the goddess’s wind whisper through its branches.

In 4E 201, the Gildergreen was struck by lightning, leaving it severely burned and lifeless. This tragedy deeply saddened its worshippers, causing pilgrimages to cease. ', '''201'':98B ''4e'':97B ''ancestor'':76B ''ancient'':51B ''branch'':95B ''burn'':108B ''caus'':117B ''ceas'':120B ''central'':20B ''citi'':11B,23B ''cut'':46B ''day'':32B ''deepli'':113B ''earli'':31B ''echo'':71B ''eldergleam'':52B ''gildergreen'':1A,3B,38B,100B ''goddess’'':90B ''grown'':43B ''hear'':88B ''holi'':64B ''journey'':84B ''kynareth'':18B,27B ''leav'':105B ''lifeless'':110B ''lightn'':104B ''live'':57B ''locat'':8B ''mani'':80B ''name'':69B ''oldest'':56B ''one'':53B ''pilgrim'':81B ''pilgrimag'':118B ''plant'':28B ''reflect'':66B ''rever'':14B,75B ''sacr'':6B ''sadden'':114B ''said'':40B ''seedl'':48B ''settlement'':36B ''sever'':107B ''struck'':102B ''tamriel'':60B ''templ'':25B ''tragedi'':112B ''tree'':7B,58B,62B ''whisper'':92B ''whiterun'':13B,34B,86B ''wind'':91B ''worshipp'':16B,116B', 'whiterun, priest', 'The Gildergreen is a sacred tree located in the city of Whiterun, revered by worshippers of Kynareth and central to the city''s Temple of Kynareth. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('merryfair_farm', 'Merryfair Farm is a modest, struggling farm located northwest of Riften, just west of Riften Stables on the north shore of Lake Honrich. Owned and operated by Dravin Llanith and his wife Synda, the couple make a meager living growing wheat, cabbages, and gourds, with a single cow providing milk. Dravin can often be seen milling wheat for their bread.

There are rumours that the farm has recently been burglarized with a valuable bow being stolen.', '''bow'':76B ''bread'':62B ''burglar'':72B ''cabbag'':44B ''coupl'':37B ''cow'':50B ''dravin'':30B,53B ''farm'':2A,4B,9B,68B ''gourd'':46B ''grow'':42B ''honrich'':25B ''lake'':24B ''live'':41B ''llanith'':31B ''locat'':10B ''make'':38B ''meager'':40B ''merryfair'':1A,3B ''milk'':52B ''mill'':58B ''modest'':7B ''north'':21B ''northwest'':11B ''often'':55B ''oper'':28B ''own'':26B ''provid'':51B ''recent'':70B ''riften'':13B,17B ''rumour'':65B ''seen'':57B ''shore'':22B ''singl'':49B ''stabl'':18B ''stolen'':78B ''struggl'':8B ''synda'':35B ''valuabl'':75B ''west'':15B ''wheat'':43B,59B ''wife'':34B', 'rift', 'Merryfair Farm is a modest, struggling farm located northwest of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('aetherium_forge', 'The Aetherium Forge is an ancient Dwemer forge located southeast of Ivarstead and east of the Rift Imperial Camp in the Rift. It is rumoured that the mighty forge can be used to craft Aetherium items, powerful Dwemer Relics. 

Aetherium is a rare, blue, luminescent crystal found exclusively in Dwemer city ruins, originally discovered by Dwemer miners in the vast underground expanse of Blackreach. ', '''aetherium'':1A,4B,37B,42B ''ancient'':8B ''blackreach'':66B ''blue'':46B ''camp'':21B ''citi'':53B ''craft'':36B ''crystal'':48B ''discov'':56B ''dwemer'':9B,40B,52B,58B ''east'':16B ''exclus'':50B ''expans'':64B ''forg'':2A,5B,10B,31B ''found'':49B ''imperi'':20B ''item'':38B ''ivarstead'':14B ''locat'':11B ''luminesc'':47B ''mighti'':30B ''miner'':59B ''origin'':55B ''power'':39B ''rare'':45B ''relic'':41B ''rift'':19B,24B ''ruin'':54B ''rumour'':27B ''southeast'':12B ''underground'':63B ''use'':34B ''vast'':62B', 'katriah', 'The Aetherium Forge is a rumor of an ancient Dwemer forge that is hidden somewhere in the Rift. But you do not know where.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'rift', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('carlotta_valentia''s_house', 'Carlotta Valentia''s House is a modest residence located in the Wind District of Whiterun. Nestled next door to the House of Clan Battle-Born and directly across from Amren''s House, it serves as the home of Carlotta Valentia and her young daughter, Mila.', '''across'':33B ''amren'':35B ''battl'':29B ''battle-born'':28B ''born'':30B ''carlotta'':1A,5B,44B ''clan'':27B ''daughter'':49B ''direct'':32B ''district'':17B ''door'':22B ''home'':42B ''hous'':4A,8B,25B,37B ''locat'':13B ''mila'':50B ''modest'':11B ''nestl'':20B ''next'':21B ''resid'':12B ''serv'':39B ''valentia'':2A,6B,45B ''whiterun'':19B ''wind'':16B ''young'':48B', 'whiterun', 'Carlotta Valentia''s House is a modest residence located in the Wind District of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fort_dawnguard', 'Fort Dawnguard is a large, ancient fort located southeast of Riften near Stendarr''s Beacon, serving as the headquarters for the Dawnguard, an order of vampire hunters dedicated to protecting Skyrim from the Volkihar clan. The fort is hidden in the eastern Rift and can only be accessed through Dayspring Canyon.

Built in the Second Era by the Jarl of Riften to contain his son, who had contracted vampirism, the fort was guarded by the mercenary band that became the Dawnguard. Over time, the threat of vampires faded, and the fort fell into disuse. Isran now leads efforts to rebuild the Dawnguard and combat the rising vampire menace, restoring the fort to its former purpose as a bastion against darkness.', '''access'':50B ''ancient'':8B ''band'':79B ''bastion'':120B ''beacon'':17B ''becam'':81B ''built'':54B ''canyon'':53B ''clan'':37B ''combat'':106B ''contain'':65B ''contract'':70B ''dark'':122B ''dawnguard'':2A,4B,24B,83B,104B ''dayspr'':52B ''dedic'':30B ''disus'':96B ''eastern'':44B ''effort'':100B ''era'':58B ''fade'':90B ''fell'':94B ''former'':116B ''fort'':1A,3B,9B,39B,73B,93B,113B ''guard'':75B ''headquart'':21B ''hidden'':41B ''hunter'':29B ''isran'':97B ''jarl'':61B ''larg'':7B ''lead'':99B ''locat'':10B ''menac'':110B ''mercenari'':78B ''near'':14B ''order'':26B ''protect'':32B ''purpos'':117B ''rebuild'':102B ''restor'':111B ''rift'':45B ''riften'':13B,63B ''rise'':108B ''second'':57B ''serv'':18B ''skyrim'':33B ''son'':67B ''southeast'':11B ''stendarr'':15B ''threat'':87B ''time'':85B ''vampir'':28B,71B,89B,109B ''volkihar'':36B', 'rift, dawnguard, vampire, volkihar', 'Fort Dawnguard is a large, ancient fort located southeast of Riften near Stendarr''s Beacon, serving as the headquarters for the Dawnguard, an order of vampire hunters dedicated to protecting Skyrim from the Volkihar clan.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('goldenglow_estate', 'Goldenglow Estate is a secluded honey farm located west of Riften in the Rift, southeast of Faldar''s Tooth. Situated on three small islands in Lake Honrich and connected by footbridges, the estate consists of a house, an apiary, docks, and the Goldenglow Estate Sewer. Guarded by hostile mercenaries and infested with skeevers, the property is owned by Aringoth.', '''apiari'':41B ''aringoth'':61B ''connect'':31B ''consist'':36B ''dock'':42B ''estat'':2A,4B,35B,46B ''faldar'':19B ''farm'':9B ''footbridg'':33B ''goldenglow'':1A,3B,45B ''guard'':48B ''honey'':8B ''honrich'':29B ''hostil'':50B ''hous'':39B ''infest'':53B ''island'':26B ''lake'':28B ''locat'':10B ''mercenari'':51B ''own'':59B ''properti'':57B ''rift'':16B ''riften'':13B ''seclud'':7B ''sewer'':47B ''situat'':22B ''skeever'':55B ''small'':25B ''southeast'':17B ''three'':24B ''tooth'':21B ''west'':11B', 'rift, noble', 'Goldenglow Estate is a secluded honey farm located west of Riften in the Rift.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('honorhall_orphanage', 'Honorhall Orphanage is located in the southern part of Riften and consists of a single interior zone. It serves as a home for four orphans under the strict and widely disliked care of its headmistress, Grelod the Kind, who is actually known to be an awful person. Constance Michel, Grelod''s timid assistant, also resides in the orphanage and provides a more nurturing presence for the children.', '''actual'':43B ''also'':56B ''assist'':55B ''aw'':48B ''care'':34B ''children'':69B ''consist'':14B ''constanc'':50B ''dislik'':33B ''four'':26B ''grelod'':38B,52B ''headmistress'':37B ''home'':24B ''honorhal'':1A,3B ''interior'':18B ''kind'':40B ''known'':44B ''locat'':6B ''michel'':51B ''nurtur'':65B ''orphan'':27B ''orphanag'':2A,4B,60B ''part'':10B ''person'':49B ''presenc'':66B ''provid'':62B ''resid'':57B ''riften'':12B ''serv'':21B ''singl'':17B ''southern'':9B ''strict'':30B ''timid'':54B ''wide'':32B ''zone'':19B', 'rift, darkbrotherhood', 'Honorhall Orphanage is located in the southern part of Riften and consists of a single interior zone.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ivarstead', 'Ivarstead is a small milling town at the western edge of the Rift, nestled at the base of the Throat of the World near the path to High Hrothgar. Located on the shores of Lake Geir, the town is powered by a fork of the Darkwater River, which drives Temba Wide-Arm''s sawmill. The settlement consists of five buildings, including Vilemyr Inn, run by Wilhelm, and the haunted Shroud Hearth Barrow looming to the east.

Once a stop for travelers and pilgrims, Ivarstead has fallen into decline due to the barrow''s haunting, causing many residents to leave for Riften or consider moving away. Notable locations include Fellstar Farm, Klimmek''s house, and Narfi''s ruined home across the river. Despite its struggles, Ivarstead remains an essential waypoint for those making the pilgrimage up the "7,000 Steps" to High Hrothgar.', '''000'':140B ''7'':139B ''across'':121B ''arm'':54B ''away'':107B ''barrow'':74B,94B ''base'':18B ''build'':62B ''caus'':97B ''consid'':105B ''consist'':59B ''darkwat'':47B ''declin'':90B ''despit'':124B ''drive'':50B ''due'':91B ''east'':78B ''edg'':11B ''essenti'':130B ''fallen'':88B ''farm'':112B ''fellstar'':111B ''five'':61B ''fork'':44B ''geir'':37B ''haunt'':71B,96B ''hearth'':73B ''high'':29B,143B ''home'':120B ''hous'':115B ''hrothgar'':30B,144B ''includ'':63B,110B ''inn'':65B ''ivarstead'':1A,2B,86B,127B ''klimmek'':113B ''lake'':36B ''leav'':101B ''locat'':31B,109B ''loom'':75B ''make'':134B ''mani'':98B ''mill'':6B ''move'':106B ''narfi'':117B ''near'':25B ''nestl'':15B ''notabl'':108B ''path'':27B ''pilgrim'':85B ''pilgrimag'':136B ''power'':41B ''remain'':128B ''resid'':99B ''rift'':14B ''riften'':103B ''river'':48B,123B ''ruin'':119B ''run'':66B ''sawmil'':56B ''settlement'':58B ''shore'':34B ''shroud'':72B ''small'':5B ''step'':141B ''stop'':81B ''struggl'':126B ''temba'':51B ''throat'':21B ''town'':7B,39B ''travel'':83B ''vilemyr'':64B ''waypoint'':131B ''western'':10B ''wide'':53B ''wide-arm'':52B ''wilhelm'':68B ''world'':24B', 'rift', 'Ivarstead is a small milling town at the western edge of the Rift, nestled at the base of the Throat of the World near the path to High Hrothgar. It is essential waypoint for those making the pilgrimage up the "7,000 Steps" to High Hrothgar.', '', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bend_will', 'Bend Will is a Shout that allows you to bend the very stones to your will, and as it grows stronger, animals, people, and even dragons are compelled to obey your commands. The three words of power in this Shout are Gol (Earth), which gives you control over the land itself; Hah (Mind), which influences the minds of others; and Dov (Dragon), which allows you to command even dragons to do your bidding.', '''allow'':8B,65B ''anim'':23B ''bend'':1A,2B,11B ''bid'':74B ''command'':33B,68B ''compel'':29B ''control'':48B ''dov'':62B ''dragon'':27B,63B,70B ''earth'':44B ''even'':26B,69B ''give'':46B ''gol'':43B ''grow'':21B ''hah'':53B ''influenc'':56B ''land'':51B ''mind'':54B,58B ''obey'':31B ''other'':60B ''peopl'':24B ''power'':38B ''shout'':6B,41B ''stone'':14B ''stronger'':22B ''three'':35B ''word'':36B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lake_geir', 'Lake Geir is a picturesque lake located in the western part of the Rift, with the village of Ivarstead situated along its shores. At the center of the lake lies an island that is home to Geirmund''s Hall, a Nordic ruin steeped in history and intrigue. Geographically, the lake is fed by the Treva River and drained by the Darkwater River, forming a key part of the region''s waterway network.', '''along'':23B ''center'':28B ''darkwat'':63B ''drain'':60B ''fed'':54B ''form'':65B ''geir'':2A,4B ''geirmund'':39B ''geograph'':50B ''hall'':41B ''histori'':47B ''home'':37B ''intrigu'':49B ''island'':34B ''ivarstead'':21B ''key'':67B ''lake'':1A,3B,8B,31B,52B ''lie'':32B ''locat'':9B ''network'':74B ''nordic'':43B ''part'':13B,68B ''picturesqu'':7B ''region'':71B ''rift'':16B ''river'':58B,64B ''ruin'':44B ''shore'':25B ''situat'':22B ''steep'':45B ''treva'':57B ''villag'':19B ''waterway'':73B ''western'':12B', 'rift', 'Lake Geir is a picturesque lake located in the western part of the Rift, with the village of Ivarstead situated along its shores. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lake_honrich', 'Lake Honrich is a sprawling lake in the eastern Rift, located immediately southwest of Riften. Known as Lake Honnith during the First Era, it is a prominent natural feature of the region. The lake is drained by the Treva River and is home to Goldenglow Estate, which occupies a cluster of islands at its center.

Popular among fishermen from across Skyrim, Lake Honrich provides ample opportunities for fishing and is supported by a fishery located on Riften''s eastern shores. ', '''across'':62B ''among'':59B ''ampl'':67B ''center'':57B ''cluster'':52B ''drain'':38B ''eastern'':11B,81B ''era'':25B ''estat'':48B ''featur'':31B ''first'':24B ''fish'':70B ''fisheri'':76B ''fishermen'':60B ''goldenglow'':47B ''home'':45B ''honnith'':21B ''honrich'':2A,4B,65B ''immedi'':14B ''island'':54B ''known'':18B ''lake'':1A,3B,8B,20B,36B,64B ''locat'':13B,77B ''natur'':30B ''occupi'':50B ''opportun'':68B ''popular'':58B ''promin'':29B ''provid'':66B ''region'':34B ''rift'':12B ''riften'':17B,79B ''river'':42B ''shore'':82B ''skyrim'':63B ''southwest'':15B ''sprawl'':7B ''support'':73B ''treva'':41B', 'rift', 'Lake Honrich is a sprawling lake in the eastern Rift, located immediately southwest of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('largashbur', 'Largashbur is an accursed Orc stronghold in the southeast of Skyrim, located west-southwest of Riften in the Rift. Besieged by giants, the stronghold contains two zones: Largashbur Longhouse and Largashbur Cellar. Unlike other Orc strongholds, Largashbur lacks a mine and has sent two of its workers to assist Narzulbur, which has a mine but is short on labor. 

The stronghold features a makeshift altar to Malacath, adorned with Orcish armor and weapons. It is rumoured that the god Malacath is not pleased with this tribe and have cursed it.', '''accurs'':5B ''adorn'':70B ''altar'':67B ''armor'':73B ''assist'':51B ''besieg'':22B ''cellar'':34B ''contain'':27B ''curs'':91B ''featur'':64B ''giant'':24B ''god'':81B ''labor'':61B ''lack'':40B ''largashbur'':1A,2B,30B,33B,39B ''locat'':13B ''longhous'':31B ''makeshift'':66B ''malacath'':69B,82B ''mine'':42B,56B ''narzulbur'':52B ''orc'':6B,37B ''orcish'':72B ''pleas'':85B ''rift'':21B ''riften'':18B ''rumour'':78B ''sent'':45B ''short'':59B ''skyrim'':12B ''southeast'':10B ''southwest'':16B ''stronghold'':7B,26B,38B,63B ''tribe'':88B ''two'':28B,46B ''unlik'':35B ''weapon'':75B ''west'':15B ''west-southwest'':14B ''worker'':49B ''zone'':29B', 'rift, orc', 'Largashbur is an accursed Orc stronghold in the southeast of Skyrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pinepeak_cavern', 'Pinepeak Cavern is a small cave north of Ivarstead, situated on the shore opposite the town across the Treva River. To find it, follow the road north from Ivarstead, cross the river as if heading to the "7,000 Steps," and turn north at the start of the climb. There are rumours that some local hunters have headed to this cave, but have not returned.', '''000'':41B ''7'':40B ''across'':19B ''cave'':8B,63B ''cavern'':2A,4B ''climb'':51B ''cross'':32B ''find'':24B ''follow'':26B ''head'':37B,60B ''hunter'':58B ''ivarstead'':11B,31B ''local'':57B ''north'':9B,29B,45B ''opposit'':16B ''pinepeak'':1A,3B ''return'':67B ''river'':22B,34B ''road'':28B ''rumour'':54B ''shore'':15B ''situat'':12B ''small'':7B ''start'':48B ''step'':42B ''town'':18B ''treva'':21B ''turn'':44B', 'rift', 'Pinepeak Cavern is a small cave north of Ivarstead.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('redbelly_mine', 'Redbelly Mine is a small ebony mine located in the village of Shor''s Stone in the Rift. The mine, which serves as the lifeblood of the settlement, initially becomes infested with frostbite spiders.  It consists of a single zone and is a valuable resource for ebony ore.

The mine gets its name from the eerie red mist that flows through it, with a sulfurous smell reminiscent of the volcanic tundra. ', '''becom'':32B ''consist'':38B ''eboni'':8B,49B ''eeri'':58B ''flow'':62B ''frostbit'':35B ''get'':53B ''infest'':33B ''initi'':31B ''lifeblood'':27B ''locat'':10B ''mine'':2A,4B,9B,22B,52B ''mist'':60B ''name'':55B ''ore'':50B ''red'':59B ''redbelli'':1A,3B ''reminisc'':69B ''resourc'':47B ''rift'':20B ''serv'':24B ''settlement'':30B ''shor'':15B ''singl'':41B ''small'':7B ''smell'':68B ''spider'':36B ''stone'':17B ''sulfur'':67B ''tundra'':73B ''valuabl'':46B ''villag'':13B ''volcan'':72B ''zone'':42B', 'rift', 'Redbelly Mine is a small ebony mine located in the village of Shor''s Stone in the Rift.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stendarr''s_beacon', 'Stendarr''s Beacon is a small tower southeast of Riften and south of Black-Briar Lodge in the Rift. The path to the beacon branches off the main road southeast of Riften, opposite the path leading to Black-Briar Lodge. It passes by the route to Broken Helm Hollow and winds south, then east, before climbing north to the beacon.

Outside the tower, the resident Vigilants of Stendarr have set up a makeshift camp.', '''beacon'':3A,6B,28B,65B ''black'':18B,43B ''black-briar'':17B,42B ''branch'':29B ''briar'':19B,44B ''broken'':52B ''camp'':79B ''climb'':61B ''east'':59B ''helm'':53B ''hollow'':54B ''lead'':40B ''lodg'':20B,45B ''main'':32B ''makeshift'':78B ''north'':62B ''opposit'':37B ''outsid'':66B ''pass'':47B ''path'':25B,39B ''resid'':70B ''rift'':23B ''riften'':13B,36B ''road'':33B ''rout'':50B ''set'':75B ''small'':9B ''south'':15B,57B ''southeast'':11B,34B ''stendarr'':1A,4B,73B ''tower'':10B,68B ''vigil'':71B ''wind'':56B', 'rift, dawnguard, vampire, volkihar', 'Stendarr''s Beacon is a small tower southeast of Riften and south of Black-Briar Lodge in the Rift.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('windhelm', 'Windhelm is a major city in northeastern Skyrim, located near the Dunmeth Pass to Morrowind and serving as the capital of Eastmarch. Situated near the northern coast, the city experiences extreme cold and frequent blizzards. Windhelm is ruled by Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak, the leader of the Stormcloak Rebellion, who resides in the Palace of the Kings. Known for its open defiance of the Imperial ban on Talos worship, Windhelm features a prominent Temple of Talos. However, the city is also infamous for its anti-foreigner sentiment, particularly toward its sizable population of Dark Elves, who live in the cramped Gray Quarter, and Argonians, who are confined to the docks outside the city walls.

The city''s layout reflects its rich history. The Stone Quarter houses the marketplace, where traders like Aval Atheron and Niranye run stalls selling goods. Valunstrad, or "Avenue of Valor," contains the oldest parts of Windhelm, including the palace and notable residences like Hjerim. Candlehearth Hall serves as a hub for travelers, providing food, drink, and lodging. Windhelm''s proximity to Morrowind has made it a refuge for Dunmer displaced by the eruption of Red Mountain, though they face suspicion and neglect from the local Nords. Despite this, figures like Brunwulf Free-Winter advocate for the rights of the Dunmer and Argonians, challenging the city''s entrenched prejudices.', '''advoc'':210B ''also'':81B ''anti'':86B ''anti-foreign'':85B ''argonian'':105B,218B ''atheron'':134B ''aval'':133B ''avenu'':143B ''ban'':66B ''blizzard'':36B ''brunwulf'':206B ''candlehearth'':160B ''capit'':21B ''challeng'':219B ''citi'':6B,30B,79B,114B,117B,221B ''coast'':28B ''cold'':33B ''confin'':108B ''contain'':146B ''cramp'':101B ''dark'':95B ''defianc'':62B ''despit'':202B ''displac'':185B ''dock'':111B ''drink'':170B ''dunmer'':184B,216B ''dunmeth'':13B ''eastmarch'':23B ''elv'':96B ''entrench'':223B ''erupt'':188B ''experi'':31B ''extrem'':32B ''face'':194B ''featur'':71B ''figur'':204B ''food'':169B ''foreign'':87B ''free'':208B ''free-wint'':207B ''frequent'':35B ''good'':140B ''gray'':102B ''hall'':161B ''histori'':123B ''hjerim'':159B ''hous'':127B ''howev'':77B ''hub'':165B ''imperi'':65B ''includ'':152B ''infam'':82B ''jarl'':41B ''king'':57B ''known'':58B ''layout'':119B ''leader'':45B ''like'':132B,158B,205B ''live'':98B ''local'':200B ''locat'':10B ''lodg'':172B ''made'':179B ''major'':5B ''marketplac'':129B ''morrowind'':16B,177B ''mountain'':191B ''near'':11B,25B ''neglect'':197B ''nirany'':136B ''nord'':201B ''northeastern'':8B ''northern'':27B ''notabl'':156B ''oldest'':148B ''open'':61B ''outsid'':112B ''palac'':54B,154B ''part'':149B ''particular'':89B ''pass'':14B ''popul'':93B ''prejudic'':224B ''promin'':73B ''provid'':168B ''proxim'':175B ''quarter'':103B,126B ''rebellion'':49B ''red'':190B ''reflect'':120B ''refug'':182B ''resid'':51B,157B ''rich'':122B ''right'':213B ''rule'':39B ''run'':137B ''sell'':139B ''sentiment'':88B ''serv'':18B,162B ''situat'':24B ''sizabl'':92B ''skyrim'':9B ''stall'':138B ''stone'':125B ''stormcloak'':43B,48B ''suspicion'':195B ''talo'':68B,76B ''templ'':74B ''though'':192B ''toward'':90B ''trader'':131B ''travel'':167B ''ulfric'':42B ''valor'':145B ''valunstrad'':141B ''wall'':115B ''windhelm'':1A,2B,37B,70B,151B,173B ''winter'':209B ''worship'':69B', 'eastmarch, noble, scholar', '
Windhelm is a major city in northeastern Skyrim, serving as the capital of Eastmarch and located near the Dunmeth Pass to Morrowind. The city experiences extreme cold and frequent blizzards, and is ruled by Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak, leader of the Stormcloak Rebellion. Known for defying the Imperial ban on Talos worship, Windhelm houses a prominent Temple of Talos. However, the city has a history of anti-foreigner sentiment, with Dark Elves living in the cramped Gray Quarter and Argonians confined to the docks outside the city. You do not know who runs the shops or who lives in the area.', '', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mora_tapinella', 'Mora Tapinella is a fungus found growing on tree stumps and fallen trees in forested regions across Skyrim, although it is less common in the Rift, where the scaly pholiota dominates. Alchemy effects: Restore Magicka, Lingering Damage Health, Regenerate Stamina, and Fortify Illusion.', '''across'':19B ''alchemi'':34B ''although'':21B ''common'':25B ''damag'':39B ''domin'':33B ''effect'':35B ''fallen'':14B ''forest'':17B ''fortifi'':44B ''found'':8B ''fungus'':7B ''grow'':9B ''health'':40B ''illus'':45B ''less'':24B ''linger'':38B ''magicka'':37B ''mora'':1A,3B ''pholiota'':32B ''regener'':41B ''region'':18B ''restor'':36B ''rift'':28B ''scali'':31B ''skyrim'':20B ''stamina'':42B ''stump'':12B ''tapinella'':2A,4B ''tree'':11B,15B', 'alchemist', 'Mora Tapinella is a fungus found growing on tree stumps and fallen trees in forested regions across Skyrim, although it is less common in the Rift, where the scaly pholiota dominates. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('temple_of_mara', 'The Temple of Mara is a sacred temple in Riften dedicated to Mara, the Aedric goddess of love, compassion, and understanding. It serves as a spiritual center for worshippers of Mara and those seeking her blessings, including marriage rites.

The temple is home to three Priests of Mara: Briehl, Dinya Balu, and Maramal. Alessandra, a Priestess of Arkay who tends to Riften''s Hall of the Dead, also resides here. As a beacon of Mara''s teachings, the temple is a place of solace and guidance for Riften''s residents and travelers alike.', '''aedric'':18B ''alessandra'':57B ''alik'':96B ''also'':71B ''arkay'':61B ''balu'':54B ''beacon'':76B ''bless'':39B ''briehl'':52B ''center'':30B ''compass'':22B ''dead'':70B ''dedic'':14B ''dinya'':53B ''goddess'':19B ''guidanc'':89B ''hall'':67B ''home'':46B ''includ'':40B ''love'':21B ''mara'':3A,7B,16B,34B,51B,78B ''maram'':56B ''marriag'':41B ''place'':85B ''priest'':49B ''priestess'':59B ''resid'':72B,93B ''riften'':13B,65B,91B ''rite'':42B ''sacr'':10B ''seek'':37B ''serv'':26B ''solac'':87B ''spiritu'':29B ''teach'':80B ''templ'':1A,5B,11B,44B,82B ''tend'':63B ''three'':48B ''travel'':95B ''understand'':24B ''worshipp'':32B', 'rift, priest', 'The Temple of Mara is a sacred temple in Riften dedicated to Mara, the Aedric goddess of love, compassion, and understanding.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_bee_and_barb', 'The Bee and Barb is a lively inn located in the heart of Riften, next to the bustling marketplace. Owned and operated by Keerava, with her husband Talen-Jei, an Argonian bartender, the inn is a popular gathering spot for both locals and travelers.

Marcurio, a mercenary for hire, can often be found sitting in the southwest corner of the inn, relaxing on a wooden bench. ', '''argonian'':36B ''barb'':4A,8B ''bartend'':37B ''bee'':2A,6B ''bench'':71B ''bustl'':22B ''corner'':63B ''found'':58B ''gather'':43B ''heart'':16B ''hire'':54B ''husband'':31B ''inn'':12B,39B,66B ''jei'':34B ''keerava'':28B ''live'':11B ''local'':47B ''locat'':13B ''marcurio'':50B ''marketplac'':23B ''mercenari'':52B ''next'':19B ''often'':56B ''oper'':26B ''own'':24B ''popular'':42B ''relax'':67B ''riften'':18B ''sit'':59B ''southwest'':62B ''spot'':44B ''talen'':33B ''talen-jei'':32B ''travel'':49B ''wooden'':70B', 'rift, traveler, innkeeper', 'The Bee and Barb is a lively inn located in the heart of Riften. You do not know who owns the inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_pawned_prawn', 'The Pawned Prawn is a general goods store located in the heart of Riften, next door to Black-Briar Meadery and to the west of The Bee and Barb. Owned and operated by Bersi Honey-Hand, the store offers a variety of items for sale, ranging from goods and supplies to more unusual wares.', '''barb'':33B ''bee'':31B ''bersi'':38B ''black'':22B ''black-briar'':21B ''briar'':23B ''door'':19B ''general'':9B ''good'':10B,53B ''hand'':41B ''heart'':15B ''honey'':40B ''honey-hand'':39B ''item'':48B ''locat'':12B ''meaderi'':24B ''next'':18B ''offer'':44B ''oper'':36B ''own'':34B ''pawn'':2A,5B ''prawn'':3A,6B ''rang'':51B ''riften'':17B ''sale'':50B ''store'':11B,43B ''suppli'':55B ''unusu'':58B ''varieti'':46B ''ware'':59B ''west'':28B', 'rift', 'The Pawned Prawn is a general goods store located in the heart of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('embershard_mine', 'Embershard Mine is a location southwest of Riverwood in Falkreath Hold, nestled north of Helgen. This small iron mine is occupied by bandits and consists of a single zone, Embershard Mine.', '''bandit'':25B ''consist'':27B ''embershard'':1A,3B,32B ''falkreath'':12B ''helgen'':17B ''hold'':13B ''iron'':20B ''locat'':7B ''mine'':2A,4B,21B,33B ''nestl'':14B ''north'':15B ''occupi'':23B ''riverwood'':10B ''singl'':30B ''small'':19B ''southwest'':8B ''zone'':31B', 'falkreath', 'Embershard Mine is a location southwest of Riverwood in Falkreath Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_ragged_flagon', 'The Ragged Flagon is a tavern located within the Thieves Guild''s headquarters in Riften, situated in the city''s old sewer network. It can be accessed through the Ratway, though after joining the Thieves Guild, quicker access is available through a secret entrance behind the Hall of the Dead, leading directly into the Ragged Flagon - Cistern.

The tavern is run by Vekel the Man, though Dirge, the bouncer, takes over bartender duties if anything happens to Vekel. Tonilia, the Thieves Guild''s first fence, is always present at the bar.', '''access'':30B,41B ''alway'':90B ''anyth'':78B ''avail'':43B ''bar'':94B ''bartend'':75B ''behind'':48B ''bouncer'':72B ''cistern'':60B ''citi'':22B ''dead'':53B ''direct'':55B ''dirg'':70B ''duti'':76B ''entranc'':47B ''fenc'':88B ''first'':87B ''flagon'':3A,6B,59B ''guild'':14B,39B,85B ''hall'':50B ''happen'':79B ''headquart'':16B ''join'':36B ''lead'':54B ''locat'':10B ''man'':68B ''network'':26B ''old'':24B ''present'':91B ''quicker'':40B ''rag'':2A,5B,58B ''ratway'':33B ''riften'':18B ''run'':64B ''secret'':46B ''sewer'':25B ''situat'':19B ''take'':73B ''tavern'':9B,62B ''thiev'':13B,38B,84B ''though'':34B,69B ''tonilia'':82B ''vekel'':66B,81B ''within'':11B', 'thievesguild', 'The Ragged Flagon is a tavern located within the Thieves Guild''s headquarters in Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'rift', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('purple_mountain_flower', 'Purple Mountain Flower is harvested from the purple-flowered variety of mountain flower, commonly found in Skyrim''s mountainous regions. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Fortify Sneak, Lingering Damage Magicka, and Resist Frost.', '''alchemi'':25B ''common'':18B ''damag'':32B ''effect'':26B ''flower'':3A,6B,13B,17B ''fortifi'':29B ''found'':19B ''frost'':36B ''harvest'':8B ''linger'':31B ''magicka'':33B ''mountain'':2A,5B,16B,23B ''purpl'':1A,4B,12B ''purple-flow'':11B ''region'':24B ''resist'':35B ''restor'':27B ''skyrim'':21B ''sneak'':30B ''stamina'':28B ''varieti'':14B', 'alchemist', 'Purple Mountain Flower is harvested from the purple-flowered variety of mountain flower, commonly found in Skyrim''s mountainous regions. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('green_butterfly_wing', 'Green Butterfly Wing can be harvested by catching Green Butterflies in a far-off, unknown land. Alchemy effects: Restore Magicka, Fear, Slow, and Invisibility.', '''alchemi'':21B ''butterfli'':2A,5B,13B ''catch'':11B ''effect'':22B ''far'':17B ''far-off'':16B ''fear'':25B ''green'':1A,4B,12B ''harvest'':9B ''invis'':28B ''land'':20B ''magicka'':24B ''restor'':23B ''slow'':26B ''unknown'':19B ''wing'':3A,6B', 'alchemist', 'Green Butterfly Wing can be harvested by catching Green Butterflies in a far-off, unknown land. 
