INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ancient_nord_boots', 'Ancient Nord Boots have good protection quality. Their visual design is sturdy and weathered, featuring thick leather and reinforced metal plates built to endure harsh conditions. Can only be crafted at the Skyforge, 4 steel ingots, 2 iron ingots, 2 leather, 3 leather strips. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''2'':40B,43B ''3'':45B ''4'':37B ''ancient'':1A,4B ''boot'':3A,6B ''built'':25B ''condit'':29B ''craft'':33B ''design'':13B ''endur'':27B ''featur'':18B ''good'':8B ''harsh'':28B ''ingot'':39B,42B ''iron'':41B,54B ''leather'':20B,44B,46B ''metal'':23B ''nord'':2A,5B ''plate'':24B ''protect'':9B ''qualiti'':10B ''reinforc'':22B ''skyforg'':36B ''steel'':38B ''strip'':47B ''sturdi'':15B ''tempered/improved'':51B ''thick'':19B ''use'':53B ''visual'':12B ''weather'':17B ''workbench'':57B', 'blacksmith', 'Ancient Nord Boots have good protection quality. Their visual design is sturdy and weathered, featuring thick leather and reinforced metal plates built to endure harsh conditions. Can only be crafted at the Skyforge, 4 steel ingots, 2 iron ingots, 2 leather, 3 leather strips. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_rift', 'The Rift is a hold in southeast Skyrim, with its capital in Riften,  aligned with the Stormcloaks. Nestled on a vast plateau bordered by the Jerall and Velothi Mountains, the Rift connects Skyrim to Morrowind and Cyrodiil and is renowned for its vibrant autumnal forests, aspen trees, and rich alchemical resources like mountain flowers, scaly pholiota, and canis root.', '''alchem'':52B ''align'':16B ''aspen'':48B ''autumn'':46B ''border'':25B ''cani'':60B ''capit'':13B ''connect'':34B ''cyrodiil'':39B ''flower'':56B ''forest'':47B ''hold'':7B ''jeral'':28B ''like'':54B ''morrowind'':37B ''mountain'':31B,55B ''nestl'':20B ''pholiota'':58B ''plateau'':24B ''renown'':42B ''resourc'':53B ''rich'':51B ''rift'':2A,4B,33B ''riften'':15B ''root'':61B ''scali'':57B ''skyrim'':10B,35B ''southeast'':9B ''stormcloak'':19B ''tree'':49B ''vast'':23B ''velothi'':30B ''vibrant'':45B', 'rift, noble, scholar', 'The Rift is a hold in southeast Skyrim, with its capital in Riften,  aligned with the Stormcloaks. Nestled on a vast plateau bordered by the Jerall and Velothi Mountains, the Rift connects Skyrim to Morrowind and Cyrodiil and is renowned for its vibrant autumnal forests, aspen trees, and rich alchemical resources like mountain flowers, scaly pholiota, and canis root.', '', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_shadow_stone', 'The Shadow Stone is one of Skyrim''s thirteen Standing Stones, located south of Riften, east of Snow-Shod Farm, and near Nightingale Hall in the Rift. Activating the stone grants the unique ability to become invisible instantly once per day, providing a quick escape or stealth advantage in critical situations.', '''abil'':38B ''activ'':32B ''advantag'':52B ''becom'':40B ''critic'':54B ''day'':45B ''east'':19B ''escap'':49B ''farm'':24B ''grant'':35B ''hall'':28B ''instant'':42B ''invis'':41B ''locat'':15B ''near'':26B ''nightingal'':27B ''one'':8B ''per'':44B ''provid'':46B ''quick'':48B ''rift'':31B ''riften'':18B ''shadow'':2A,5B ''shod'':23B ''situat'':55B ''skyrim'':10B ''snow'':22B ''snow-shod'':21B ''south'':16B ''stand'':13B ''stealth'':51B ''stone'':3A,6B,14B,34B ''thirteen'':12B ''uniqu'':37B', 'rift, scholar, traveler', 'The Shadow Stone is one of Skyrim''s thirteen Standing Stones, located south of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elven_helmet', 'Elven Helmet has good protection quality. Its visual design is elegant and golden, with smooth curves and intricate patterns that reflect refined craftsmanship. To craft it: 2 refined moonstone, 1 iron ingot, 1 leather, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using moonstone at a workbench.', '''1'':32B,35B,38B ''2'':29B ''adept'':46B,52B ''blacksmith'':43B ''craft'':27B,49B,55B ''craftsmanship'':25B ''curv'':18B ''design'':11B ''eleg'':13B ''elven'':1A,3B ''forg'':44B ''golden'':15B ''good'':6B ''helmet'':2A,4B ''ingot'':34B ''intric'':20B ''iron'':33B ''it.it'':56B ''leather'':36B,39B ''moonston'':31B,62B ''pattern'':21B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''refin'':24B,30B ''reflect'':23B ''smith'':47B,53B ''smooth'':17B ''strip'':40B ''tempered/improved'':59B ''use'':61B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':65B', 'blacksmith', 'Elven Helmet has good protection quality. Its visual design is elegant and golden, with smooth curves and intricate patterns that reflect refined craftsmanship. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('scalon_fin', 'Scalon Fin, a large grey fish fin originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Waterbreathing, Damage Health, Lingering Damage Magicka, and Damage Magicka Regen.', '''alchemi'':25B ''caravan'':24B ''damag'':28B,31B,34B ''effect'':26B ''fin'':2A,4B,9B ''fish'':8B ''grey'':7B ''health'':29B ''ingredi'':17B ''isl'':14B ''khajiit'':23B ''larg'':6B ''linger'':30B ''magicka'':32B,35B ''origin'':10B ''purchas'':21B ''regen'':36B ''scalon'':1A,3B ''shiver'':13B ''waterbreath'':27B', 'alchemist', 'Scalon Fin, a large grey fish fin originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
