INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ahzidal''s_descent', '
Ahzidal''s Descent, written by Halund Greycloak, tells the tragic tale of Ahzidal, a gifted enchanter whose relentless pursuit of knowledge and vengeance led to his downfall. Born in Saarthal, Ahzidal left his home to study under elven masters, only to return years later to find his city in ruins, destroyed by the elves. Consumed by grief and anger, he vowed revenge and devoted himself to mastering the magical arts, learning from the Dwemer, Ayleids, Falmer, and others. His skills proved instrumental in helping Ysgramor and the Companions reclaim Saarthal, fulfilling his oath of vengeance against the elves. However, his insatiable hunger for power drove him further, delving into forbidden knowledge of Dragon Priests and the realms of Oblivion, which ultimately consumed him.

Thematically, the story warns against the dangers of obsession and the cost of unchecked ambition. Ahzidal’s descent serves as a cautionary tale about losing oneself in the pursuit of perfection and vengeance. The legend, intertwined with historical and mythical elements, underscores the thin line between genius and madness. Though part of a single text, the account carries universal lessons, resonating with the recurring Skyrim theme of power’s corrupting influence.', '''account'':182B ''ahzid'':1A,4B,16B,34B ''ahzidal’'':142B ''ambit'':141B ''anger'':62B ''art'':73B ''ayleid'':78B ''born'':31B ''carri'':183B ''cautionari'':147B ''citi'':51B ''companion'':91B ''consum'':58B,125B ''corrupt'':194B ''cost'':138B ''danger'':133B ''delv'':111B ''descent'':3A,6B,143B ''destroy'':54B ''devot'':67B ''downfal'':30B ''dragon'':116B ''drove'':108B ''dwemer'':77B ''element'':166B ''elv'':57B,101B ''elven'':41B ''enchant'':19B ''falmer'':79B ''find'':49B ''forbidden'':113B ''fulfil'':94B ''genius'':172B ''gift'':18B ''greycloak'':10B ''grief'':60B ''halund'':9B ''help'':87B ''histor'':163B ''home'':37B ''howev'':102B ''hunger'':105B ''influenc'':195B ''insati'':104B ''instrument'':85B ''intertwin'':161B ''knowledg'':24B,114B ''later'':47B ''learn'':74B ''led'':27B ''left'':35B ''legend'':160B ''lesson'':185B ''line'':170B ''lose'':150B ''mad'':174B ''magic'':72B ''master'':42B,70B ''mythic'':165B ''oath'':96B ''oblivion'':122B ''obsess'':135B ''oneself'':151B ''other'':81B ''part'':176B ''perfect'':156B ''power'':107B ''power’'':193B ''priest'':117B ''prove'':84B ''pursuit'':22B,154B ''realm'':120B ''reclaim'':92B ''recur'':189B ''relentless'':21B ''reson'':186B ''return'':45B ''reveng'':65B ''ruin'':53B ''saarthal'':33B,93B ''serv'':144B ''singl'':179B ''skill'':83B ''skyrim'':190B ''stori'':129B ''studi'':39B ''tale'':14B,148B ''tell'':11B ''text'':180B ''themat'':127B ''theme'':191B ''thin'':169B ''though'':175B ''tragic'':13B ''ultim'':124B ''uncheck'':140B ''underscor'':16