INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_buying_game', '
The Buying Game, written by Adabael Timsar-Dadisun, provides practical advice on the art of bargaining, a common and expected practice across Tamriel. Emphasizing both strategy and etiquette, the book highlights the importance of politeness, cultural awareness, and the subtleties of negotiation. From initiating pleasantries with shopkeepers to gauging regional specialties and prejudices, it offers insights into navigating trade effectively. The author underscores the importance of recognizing different types of merchants and being prepared for their quirks, such as rural shopkeepers’ resourcefulness or city merchants’ shrewdness.

Themes of cultural nuance, adaptability, and strategic thinking permeate the text. The book also cautions against hesitation, advising readers to seize opportunities for valuable purchases rather than risking regret. By treating trade as a "game" where both buyer and seller can benefit, the guide promotes a balanced and rewarding approach to commerce in Tamriel.', '''across'':26B ''adabael'':9B ''adapt'':95B ''advic'':15B ''advis'':108B ''also'':104B ''approach'':140B ''art'':18B ''author'':66B ''awar'':41B ''balanc'':137B ''bargain'':20B ''benefit'':132B ''book'':34B,103B ''buy'':2A,5B ''buyer'':128B ''caution'':105B ''citi'':88B ''commerc'':142B ''common'':22B ''cultur'':40B,93B ''dadisun'':12B ''differ'':72B ''effect'':64B ''emphas'':28B ''etiquett'':32B ''expect'':24B ''game'':3A,6B,125B ''gaug'':53B ''guid'':134B ''hesit'':107B ''highlight'':35B ''import'':37B,69B ''initi'':48B ''insight'':60B ''merchant'':75B ''merchants’'':89B ''navig'':62B ''negoti'':46B ''nuanc'':94B ''offer'':59B ''opportun'':112B ''permeat'':99B ''pleasantri'':49B ''polit'':39B ''practic'':14B,25B ''prejudic'':57B ''prepar'':78B ''promot'':135B ''provid'':13B ''purchas'':115B ''quirk'':81B ''rather'':116B ''reader'':109B ''recogn'':71B ''region'':54B ''regret'':119B ''resourc'':86B ''reward'':139B ''risk'':118B ''rural'':84B ''seiz'':111B ''seller'':130B ''shopkeep'':51B ''shopkeepers’'':85B ''shrewd'':90B ''specialti'':55B ''strateg'':97B ''strategi'':30B ''subtleti'':44B ''tamriel'':27B,144B ''text'':101B ''theme'':91B ''think'':98B ''timsar'':11B ''timsar-dadisun'':10B ''trade'':63B,122B ''treat'':121B ''type'':73B ''underscor'':67B ''valuabl'':114B ''written'':7B', 'scholar', 'The Buying Game, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, provides practical advice on bargaining, emphasizing strategy, cultural awareness, and etiquette in negotiations. Themes of adaptability, cultural nuance, and strategic thinking highlight the importance of recognizing different merchant types and seizing opportunities in Tamrielic commerce.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_book_of_daedra', 'The Book of Daedra, written by an unknown author, offers a concise yet insightful overview of the Daedric Princes, detailing their spheres of influence and nature. The text serves as a reference for scholars and worshippers alike, highlighting the unique roles of each Prince, from Azura''s dominion over twilight to Sheogorath''s chaotic madness, and Mehrunes Dagon''s focus on destruction and revolution. It explores the motivations and attributes of these powerful entities, emphasizing their complex relationships with mortals and their realms in Oblivion.

Key themes include power, knowledge, chaos, and morality, as each Prince embodies distinct aspects of existence, often reflecting human ambition, fears, and desires. The book also discusses legendary Daedric artifacts, such as Scourge, a weapon blessed by Malacath to combat Daedra but cursed to banish any Daedra who attempts to wield it. This single-volume tome stands as both a theological and practical guide, underscoring the enigmatic and often perilous nature of Daedric interactions with the mortal world.', '''alik'':41B ''also'':115B ''ambit'':109B ''artifact'':119B ''aspect'':103B ''attempt'':138B ''attribut'':74B ''author'':13B ''azura'':50B ''banish'':134B ''bless'':125B ''book'':2A,6B,114B ''chao'':95B ''chaotic'':58B ''combat'':129B ''complex'':81B ''concis'':16B ''curs'':132B ''daedra'':4A,8B,130B,136B ''daedric'':22B,118B,163B ''dagon'':62B ''desir'':112B ''destruct'':66B ''detail'':24B ''discuss'':116B ''distinct'':102B ''dominion'':52B ''embodi'':101B ''emphas'':79B ''enigmat'':157B ''entiti'':78B ''exist'':105B ''explor'':70B ''fear'':110B ''focus'':64B ''guid'':154B ''highlight'':42B ''human'':108B ''includ'':92B ''influenc'':28B ''insight'':18B ''interact'':164B ''key'':90B ''knowledg'':94B ''legendari'':117B ''mad'':59B ''malacath'':127B ''mehrun'':61B ''moral'':97B ''mortal'':84B,167B ''motiv'':72B ''natur'':30B,161B ''oblivion'':89B ''offer'':14B ''often'':106B,159B ''overview'':19B ''peril'':160B ''power'':77B,93B ''practic'':153B ''princ'':23B,48B,100B ''realm'':87B ''refer'':36B ''reflect'':107B ''relationship'':82B ''revolut'':68B ''role'':45B ''scholar'':38B ''scourg'':122B ''serv'':33B ''sheogorath'':56B ''singl'':144B ''single-volum'':143B ''sphere'':26B ''stand'':147B ''text'':32B ''theme'':91B ''theolog'':151B ''tome'':146B ''twilight'':54B ''underscor'':155B ''uniqu'':44B ''unknown'':12B ''volum'':145B ''weapon'':124B ''wield'':140B ''world'':168B ''worshipp'':40B ''written'':9B ''yet'':17B', 'scholar', 'The Book of Daedra, you do not kn