INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('breathing_water', 'Breathing Water, written by Haliel Myrm, is a story blending magic, ambition, and fatal irony. It follows Tharien Winloth, a smuggler seeking the power to breathe underwater. He apprentices himself to the eccentric sorceress Seryne Relas, who teaches him the School of Alteration''s lessons on breaking reality to achieve the impossible. Through practice and understanding, Tharien masters the spell of water breathing and sets off to retrieve treasure from the sunken ship Morodrung. Despite his magical skill, his obsession with the treasure blinds him to the spell''s limitations, and he tragically drowns, clutching two unused potions of water breathing.

Themes of the book include the pursuit of power, the dangers of overconfidence, and the impermanence of human defiance against nature. The narrative underscores the importance of understanding the boundaries of magic and life, emphasizing that desire alone cannot override reality. This standalone work is a cautionary tale for those who wield magic, highlighting the balance between ambition and prudence.', '''achiev'':52B ''alon'':141B ''alter'':45B ''ambit'':14B,161B ''apprentic'':31B ''balanc'':159B ''blend'':12B ''blind'':86B ''book'':107B ''boundari'':133B ''break'':49B ''breath'':1A,3B,28B,65B,103B ''cannot'':142B ''cautionari'':150B ''clutch'':97B ''danger'':114B ''defianc'':122B ''desir'':140B ''despit'':77B ''drown'':96B ''eccentr'':35B ''emphas'':138B ''fatal'':16B ''follow'':19B ''haliel'':7B ''highlight'':157B ''human'':121B ''imperman'':119B ''import'':129B ''imposs'':54B ''includ'':108B ''ironi'':17B ''lesson'':47B ''life'':137B ''limit'':92B ''magic'':13B,79B,135B,156B ''master'':60B ''morodrung'':76B ''myrm'':8B ''narrat'':126B ''natur'':124B ''obsess'':82B ''overconfid'':116B ''overrid'':143B ''potion'':100B ''power'':26B,112B ''practic'':56B ''prudenc'':163B ''pursuit'':110B ''realiti'':50B,144B ''rela'':38B ''retriev'':70B ''school'':43B ''seek'':24B ''seryn'':37B ''set'':67B ''ship'':75B ''skill'':80B ''smuggler'':23B ''sorceress'':36B ''spell'':62B,90B ''standalon'':146B ''stori'':11B ''sunken'':74B ''tale'':151B ''teach'':40B ''tharien'':20B,59B ''theme'':104B ''tragic'':95B ''treasur'':71B,85B ''two'':98B ''underscor'':127B ''understand'':58B,131B ''underwat'':29B ''unus'':99B ''water'':2A,4B,64B,102B ''wield'':155B ''winloth'':21B ''work'':147B ''written'':5B', 'scholar', 'Breathing Water, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, tells the story of Tharien Winloth, a smuggler who seeks the power to breathe underwater, only to tragically drown due to his obsession with treasure and overconfidence in his magical abilities. The book explores themes of the pursuit of power, the dangers of overconfidence, and the importance of understanding the limitations of magic and life.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arcadia''s_cauldron', 'Arcadia''s Cauldron is a bustling alchemy shop located in Whiterun''s market district, serving as a hub for those seeking potions, ingredients, and expertise in the art of alchemy. The shop is owned and operated by Arcadia, a skilled apothecary and trainer in alchemy, who also resides within the premises. Open daily from 8 a.m. to 8 p.m.', '''8'':58B,61B ''a.m'':59B ''alchemi'':10B,33B,48B ''also'':50B ''apothecari'':44B ''arcadia'':1A,4B,41B ''art'':31B ''bustl'':9B ''cauldron'':3A,6B ''daili'':56B ''district'':17B ''expertis'':28B ''hub'':21B ''ingredi'':26B ''locat'':12B ''market'':16B ''open'':55B ''oper'':39B ''own'':37B ''p.m'':62B ''potion'':25B ''premis'':54B ''resid'':51B ''seek'':24B ''serv'':18B ''shop'':11B,35B ''skill'':43B ''trainer'':46B ''whiterun'':14B ''within'':52B', 'whiterun', 'Arcadia''s Cauldron is a bustling alchemy shop located in Whiterun''s market district.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brief_history_of_the_empire', '
A Brief History of the Empire, written by Stronach k''Thojj III, Imperial Historian, is a four-volume series chronicling the rise and reign of the Septim Dynasty. Beginning with Tiber Septim’s conquest of Tamriel and the establishment of the Third Era, the books explore the subsequent rulers, political struggles, and pivotal events that shaped the Empire. From the glory of Tiber’s rule to the War of the Red Diamond and the turmoil of assassinations, rebellions, and betrayals, the series provides a detailed account of the Empire’s fluctuating fortunes. Themes of power, unity, ambition, and the consequences of governance underlie the narrative, emphasizing the challenges of maintaining a vast empire.

The series concludes with the reign of Uriel Septim VII, detailing his imprisonment by the treacherous Battlemage Jagar Tharn and his subsequent liberation. Uriel VII’s efforts to restore Tamriel to its former glory reflect the ongoing struggle to uphold the vision of the Septim legacy. This comprehensive history offers a rich perspective on the political and cultural evolution of the Empire, blending triumph and tragedy in its portrayal of one of Tamriel’s most iconic dynasties.', '''account'':90B ''ambit'':100B ''assassin'':81B ''battlemag'':133B ''begin'':35B ''betray'':84B ''blend'':178B ''book'':50B ''brief'':1A,7B ''challeng'':111B ''chronicl'':26B ''comprehens'':163B ''conclud'':119B ''conquest'':39B ''consequ'':103B ''cultur'':173B ''detail'':89B,127B ''diamond'':76B ''dynasti'':34B,191B ''effort'':142B ''emphas'':109B ''empir'':5A,11B,63B,116B,177B ''empire’'':93B ''era'':48B ''establish'':44B ''event'':59B ''evolut'':174B ''explor'':51B ''fluctuat'':94B ''former'':148B ''fortun'':95B ''four'':23B ''four-volum'':22B ''glori'':66B,149B ''govern'':105B ''histori'':2A,8B,164B ''historian'':19B ''icon'':190B ''iii'':17B ''imperi'':18B ''imprison'':129B ''jagar'':134B ''k'':15B ''legaci'':161B ''liber'':139B ''maintain'':113B ''narrat'':108B ''offer'':165B ''one'':186B ''ongo'':152B ''perspect'':168B ''pivot'':58B ''polit'':55B,171B ''portray'':184B ''power'':98B ''provid'':87B ''rebellion'':82B ''red'':75B ''reflect'':150B ''reign'':30B,122B ''restor'':144B ''rich'':167B ''rise'':28B ''rule'':69B ''ruler'':54B ''septim'':33B,125B,160B ''septim’'':38B ''seri'':25B,86B,118B ''shape'':61B ''stronach'':14B ''struggl'':56B,153B ''subsequ'':53B,138B ''tamriel'':41B,145B ''tamriel’'':188B ''tharn'':135B ''theme'':96B ''third'':47B ''thojj'':16B ''tiber'':37B ''tiber’'':68B ''tragedi'':181B ''treacher'':132B ''triumph'':179B ''turmoil'':79B ''underli'':106B ''uniti'':99B ''uphold'':155B ''uriel'':124B,140B ''vast'':115B ''vii'':126B ''vii’'':141B ''vision'':157B ''volum'':24B ''war'':72B ''written'':12B', 'scholar', '
A Brief History of the Empire, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, chronicles the rise and reign of the Septim Dynasty, from Tiber Septim’s conquest of Tamriel to the reign of Uriel Septim VII. The book explores themes of power, unity, ambition, and the challenges of governance, highlighting the political struggles and fluctuating fortunes of the Empire throughout its history.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('leather_bracers', 'Leather Bracers are a pair of leather bracers with basic protection quality. Its visual design is simple and flexible, with dark, weathered leather panels stitched together for mobility and basic protection. To craft it: 1 leather and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge.  A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''1'':37B ''2'':40B ''basic'':12B,32B ''blacksmith'':45B ''bracer'':2A,4B,10B ''craft'':35B,51B ''dark'':23B ''design'':17B ''flexibl'':21B ''forg'':46B ''leather'':1A,3B,9B,25B,38B,41B,59B ''mobil'':30B ''novic'':48B ''pair'':7B ''panel'':26B ''protect'':13B,33B ''qualiti'':14B ''simpl'':19B ''smith'':49B ''stitch'':27B ''strip'':42B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''togeth'':28B ''use'':58B ''visual'':16B ''weather'':24B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Leather Bracers are a pair of leather bracers with basic protection quality. Its visual design is simple and flexible, with dark, weathered leather panels stitched together for mobility and basic protection. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skyborn_altar', 'Skyborn Altar is a mountaintop dragon lair located east-southeast of Morthal and south of Stonehills in Hjaalmarch. The path to the altar can be accessed from the south by traveling between Silent Moons Camp and Dustman''s Cairn, with a dirt path marked by two stone bird heads flanking the base of stone steps leading up the mountain.', '''access'':29B ''altar'':2A,4B,26B ''base'':55B ''bird'':51B ''cairn'':42B ''camp'':38B ''dirt'':45B ''dragon'':8B ''dustman'':40B ''east'':12B ''east-southeast'':11B ''flank'':53B ''head'':52B ''hjaalmarch'':21B ''lair'':9B ''lead'':59B ''locat'':10B ''mark'':47B ''moon'':37B ''morthal'':15B ''mountain'':62B ''mountaintop'':7B ''path'':23B,46B ''silent'':36B ''skyborn'':1A,3B ''south'':17B,32B ''southeast'':13B ''step'':58B ''stone'':50B,57B ''stonehil'':19B ''travel'':34B ''two'':49B', 'hjaalmarch, dragon', 'Skyborn Altar is a mountaintop dragon lair located east-southeast of Morthal and in Hjaalmarch. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('jorgen_and_lami''s_house', 'Jorgen and Lami''s House is a modest, one-room cottage located on the outskirts of Morthal, across from the town''s lumber mill. The house is home to Jorgen, a Nord lumberjack, and his wife Lami, who runs the Thaumaturgist''s Hut in Morthal as the town''s apothecary.', '''across'':24B ''apothecari'':56B ''cottag'':17B ''home'':34B ''hous'':5A,10B,32B ''hut'':49B ''jorgen'':1A,6B,36B ''lami'':3A,8B,43B ''locat'':18B ''lumber'':29B ''lumberjack'':39B ''mill'':30B ''modest'':13B ''morthal'':23B,51B ''nord'':38B ''one'':15B ''one-room'':14B ''outskirt'':21B ''room'':16B ''run'':45B ''thaumaturgist'':47B ''town'':27B,54B ''wife'':42B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Jorgen and Lami''s House is located in Morthal. You do not know the occupents of the house.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('effects_of_the_elder_scrolls', '
Effects of the Elder Scrolls, written by Justinius Poluhnius, is a scholarly examination of the profound and often dangerous effects that the Elder Scrolls have on their readers. Poluhnius categorizes these effects into four distinct groups, depending on the reader''s level of knowledge and mental fortitude. The first group, The Naifs, consists of those who lack sufficient understanding to interpret the scrolls, leaving them unaffected but also unable to glean any knowledge. The second group, The Unguarded Intellects, experiences the greatest danger, suffering total blindness upon reading, though they gain a fragment of forbidden knowledge. The third group, Mediated Understanding, includes the trained initiates of the Cult of the Ancestor Moth, who, through years of mental discipline, can read the scrolls with minimal blindness and gain tempered insights. Finally, Illuminated Understanding describes the advanced monks who experience progressive blindness but gain an increasingly profound comprehension of the scrolls'' revelations, culminating in a final, irreversible reading.

The theme of the book revolves around the perils and mysteries of seeking forbidden knowledge and the costs associated with understanding the Elder Scrolls. It highlights the discipline required to safely access such knowledge and the toll it takes on both the mind and body. The text serves as both a cautionary tale and a scholarly guide for those seeking to engage with the scrolls, offering insights into their powerful effects and the philosophy behind the Cult of the Ancestor Moth''s teachings.', '''access'':193B ''advanc'':140B ''also'':73B ''ancestor'':116B,241B ''around'':168B ''associ'':180B ''behind'':236B ''blind'':91B,130B,145B ''bodi'':206B ''book'':166B ''categor'':35B ''cautionari'':213B ''comprehens'':151B ''consist'':58B ''cost'':179B ''culmin'':156B ''cult'':113B,238B ''danger'':24B,88B ''depend'':42B ''describ'':138B ''disciplin'':123B,189B ''distinct'':40B ''effect'':1A,6B,25B,37B,232B ''elder'':4A,9B,28B,184B ''engag'':223B ''examin'':18B ''experi'':85B,143B ''final'':135B,159B ''first'':54B ''forbidden'':100B,175B ''fortitud'':52B ''four'':39B ''fragment'':98B ''gain'':96B,132B,147B ''glean'':76B ''greatest'':87B ''group'':41B,55B,81B,104B ''guid'':218B ''highlight'':187B ''illumin'':136B ''includ'':107B ''increas'':149B ''initi'':110B ''insight'':134B,228B ''intellect'':84B ''interpret'':66B ''irrevers'':160B ''justinius'':13B ''knowledg'':49B,78B,101B,176B,195B ''lack'':62B ''leav'':69B ''level'':47B ''mediat'':105B ''mental'':51B,122B ''mind'':204B ''minim'':129B ''monk'':141B ''moth'':117B,242B ''mysteri'':172B ''naif'':57B ''offer'':227B ''often'':23B ''peril'':170B ''philosophi'':235B ''poluhnius'':14B,34B ''power'':231B ''profound'':21B,150B ''progress'':144B ''read'':93B,125B,161B ''reader'':33B,45B ''requir'':190B ''revel'':155B ''revolv'':167B ''safe'':192B ''scholar'':17B,217B ''scroll'':5A,10B,29B,68B,127B,154B,185B,226B ''second'':80B ''seek'':174B,221B ''serv'':209B ''suffer'':89B ''suffici'':63B ''take'':200B ''tale'':214B ''teach''