INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mid_vur_shaan', 'Battle Fury is a Shout that enchants the weapons of your nearby allies, allowing them to attack faster. The three words of power in this Shout are Mid (Loyal), which strengthens the bond of your allies, Vur (Valor), which imbues them with courage and power, and Shaan (Inspire), which increases their speed and effectiveness in combat.', '''alli'':16B,39B ''allow'':17B ''attack'':20B ''battl'':4B ''bond'':36B ''combat'':59B ''courag'':46B ''effect'':57B ''enchant'':10B ''faster'':21B ''furi'':5B ''imbu'':43B ''increas'':53B ''inspir'':51B ''loyal'':32B ''mid'':1A,31B ''nearbi'':15B ''power'':26B,48B ''shaan'':3A,50B ''shout'':8B,29B ''speed'':55B ''strengthen'':34B ''three'':23B ''valor'':41B ''vur'':2A,40B ''weapon'':12B ''word'':24B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_city_of_stone', 'The City of Stone: A Sellsword''s Guide to Markarth, written by Amanda Alleia, is a practical guide for mercenaries navigating the rugged and politically charged environment of Markarth. The city, with its vertical architecture and harsh geography, is known for its lucrative but dangerous work, primarily dealing with the Forsworn, a group frequently targeted for bounty hunting. Alleia offers a detailed account of the city’s layout, key locations such as Cidhna Mine and the Temple of Dibella, and the political dynamics at play, notably the powerful Silver-Blood family. Her advice includes maintaining a low profile, avoiding trouble with the distrustful locals, and seeking employment with the city’s wealthier patrons in Dryside.

Themes of survival, opportunism, and the harsh realities of life as a mercenary are prevalent in this guide. It highlights the tensions within Markarth, from its deeply ingrained class divisions to its dangerous criminal elements. Alleia’s no-nonsense approach provides valuable insight into making a living in the unforgiving city, though she cautions readers to avoid unnecessary conflicts and to keep their focus on earning gold. This guide is part of a series that provides practical advice for sellswords across Skyrim.', '''account'':67B ''across'':199B ''advic'':97B,196B ''alleia'':18B,63B ''alleia’'':154B ''amanda'':17B ''approach'':158B ''architectur'':39B ''avoid'':103B,175B ''blood'':94B ''bounti'':61B ''caution'':172B ''charg'':30B ''cidhna'':76B ''citi'':2A,6B,35B,169B ''city’'':70B,114B ''class'':147B ''conflict'':177B ''crimin'':152B ''danger'':49B,151B ''deal'':52B ''deepli'':145B ''detail'':66B ''dibella'':82B ''distrust'':107B ''divis'':148B ''drysid'':118B ''dynam'':86B ''earn'':184B ''element'':153B ''employ'':111B ''environ'':31B ''famili'':95B ''focus'':182B ''forsworn'':55B ''frequent'':58B ''geographi'':42B ''gold'':185B ''group'':57B ''guid'':12B,22B,136B,187B ''harsh'':41B,125B ''highlight'':138B ''hunt'':62B ''includ'':98B ''ingrain'':146B ''insight'':161B ''keep'':180B ''key'':72B ''known'':44B ''layout'':71B ''life'':128B ''live'':165B ''local'':108B ''locat'':73B ''low'':101B ''lucrat'':47B ''maintain'':99B ''make'':163B ''markarth'':14B,33B,142B ''mercenari'':24B,131B ''mine'':77B ''navig'':25B ''no-nonsens'':155B ''nonsens'':157B ''notabl'':89B ''offer'':64B ''opportun'':122B ''part'':189B ''patron'':116B ''play'':88B ''polit'':29B,85B ''power'':91B ''practic'':21B,195B ''preval'':133B ''primarili'':51B ''profil'':102B ''provid'':159B,194B ''reader'':173B ''realiti'':126B ''rug'':27B ''seek'':110B ''sellsword'':10B,198B ''seri'':192B ''silver'':93B ''silver-blood'':92B ''skyrim'':200B ''stone'':4A,8B ''surviv'':121B ''target'':59B ''templ''