INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonbone_arrow', 'Dragonbone Arrow is an arrow that deals Godly damage. Its visual design is pale and jagged, with a sturdy wooden shaft, sharp dragon bone tip, and dark feather fletching.. It can be crafted by a master smith at a forge. 1 Dragonbone, 1 firewood = 24 arrows.', '''..'':32B ''1'':44B,46B ''24'':48B ''arrow'':2A,4B,7B,49B ''bone'':26B ''craft'':36B ''damag'':11B ''dark'':29B ''deal'':9B ''design'':14B ''dragon'':25B ''dragonbon'':1A,3B,45B ''feather'':30B ''firewood'':47B ''fletch'':31B ''forg'':43B ''god'':10B ''jag'':18B ''master'':39B ''pale'':16B ''shaft'':23B ''sharp'':24B ''smith'':40B ''sturdi'':21B ''tip'':27B ''visual'':13B ''wooden'':22B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragonbone Arrow is an arrow that deals Godly damage. Its visual design is pale and jagged, with a sturdy wooden shaft, sharp dragon bone tip, and dark feather fletching. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('riften_jail', 'Riften Jail is located beneath Mistveil Keep, serving as the city''s detention facility. Accessible via an entrance to the right of the main doors to Mistveil Keep, the jail is a secure area where criminals and wrongdoers are held.', '''access'':17B ''area'':36B ''beneath'':7B ''citi'':13B ''crimin'':38B ''detent'':15B ''door'':27B ''entranc'':20B ''facil'':16B ''held'':42B ''jail'':2A,4B,32B ''keep'':9B,30B ''locat'':6B ''main'':26B ''mistveil'':8B,29B ''riften'':1A,3B ''right'':23B ''secur'':35B ''serv'':10B ''via'':18B ''wrongdoer'':40B', 'rift', 'Riften Jail is located beneath Mistveil Keep.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nerevar_at_red_mountain', 'Nerevar at Red Mountain, written by the Tribunal Temple, is a scholarly retelling of the events surrounding the Battle of Red Mountain and the tragic aftermath involving Nerevar, Dagoth Ur, and the Tribunal. The text details the conflict between the Chimer, led by Nerevar, and the Dwemer, led by Dumac Dwarf-Orc, culminating in the discovery of the Heart of Lorkhan. Nerevar, guided by Azura, seeks to destroy the Heart''s corrupting power, but the Tribunal, led by Almalexia, Sotha Sil, and Vivec, covet the Heart''s power for themselves, leading to Nerevar''s murder by his own generals. Azura curses the Tribunal for their betrayal, transforming the Chimer into the ashen-skinned Dunmer, and condemns them to live with their guilt.

The story explores themes of betrayal, greed, and the corrupting influence of power. It examines the tragic fall of Nerevar, the noble king, and the rise of the Tribunal as gods, whose ascension is tainted by their dark deeds. The book also reflects on the consequences of forsaking old ways and the eternal mark of their actions, as seen in the physical transformation of the Dunmer. The text is part of a larger body of work, the Apographa, consisting of hidden writings that challenge Temple doctrine and offer a more nuanced view of Morrowind''s history.', '''action'':185B ''aftermath'':30B ''almalexia'':84B ''also'':170B ''apographa'':206B ''ascens'':161B ''ashen'':118B ''ashen-skin'':117B ''azura'':70B,105B ''battl'':23B ''betray'':111B,134B ''bodi'':202B ''book'':169B ''challeng'':212B ''chimer'':45B,114B ''condemn'':122B ''conflict'':42B ''consequ'':174B ''consist'':207B ''corrupt'':77B,138B ''covet'':89B ''culmin'':58B ''curs'':106B ''dagoth'':33B ''dark'':166B ''deed'':167B ''destroy'':73B ''detail'':40B ''discoveri'':61B ''doctrin'':214B ''dumac'':54B ''dunmer'':120B,194B ''dwarf'':56B ''dwarf-orc'':55B ''dwemer'':51B ''etern'':181B ''event'':20B ''examin'':143B ''explor'':131B ''fall'':146B ''forsak'':176B ''general'':104B ''god'':159B ''greed'':135B ''guid'':68B ''guilt'':128B ''heart'':64B,75B,91B ''hidden'':209B ''histori'':224B ''influenc'':139B ''involv'':31B ''king'':151B ''larger'':201B ''lead'':96B ''led'':46B,52B,82B ''live'':125B ''lorkhan'':66B ''mark'':182B ''morrowind'':222B ''mountain'':4A,8B,26B ''murder'':100B ''nerevar'':1A,5B,32B,48B,67B,98B,148B ''nobl'':150B ''nuanc'':219B ''offer'':216B ''old'':177B ''orc'':57B ''part'':198B ''physic'':190B ''power'':78B,93B,141B ''red'':3A,7B,25B ''reflect'':171B ''retel'':17B ''rise'':154B ''scholar'':16B ''seek'':71B ''seen'':187B ''sil'':86B ''skin'':119B ''sotha'':85B ''stori'':130B ''surround'':21B ''taint'':163B ''templ'':13B,213B ''text'':39B,196B ''theme'':132B ''tragic'':29B,145B ''transform'':11