INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('magnus', 'Magnus, the God of Magic and the Great Architect, is a revered figure among many cultures in Tamriel, known as the creator of the schematics for Mundus. During the Dawn Era, he collaborated with other et''Ada to forge the mortal plane, but upon realizing the great sacrifice required, he abandoned the project. His departure from Mundus tore a hole into Aetherius, forming the sun, which is also referred to as Magnus. The stars, believed to be fragments of his being or tears in the sky made by his followers, the Magna Ge, illuminate the night as remnants of his retreat. Magnus’s legacy is steeped in mysticism, as he is credited with creating powerful artifacts like the Staff of Magnus and the Eye of Magnus, each holding immense arcane power capable of influencing the balance of the magical world.

Worship of Magnus varies across Tamriel. The Altmer and Bretons revere him as the God of Sight and Insight, while the Khajiit call him Magrus, the Cat''s Eye, integrating his mythos into their lunar cycles. The Ayleids dedicated temples to his name, celebrating his association with light and divine order. Legends suggest Magnus influences powerful mages, lending them his energy, though his contributions to Mundus are viewed with skepticism by the Imperials, who question the dual nature of his gift. Despite his detachment from Nirn, Magnus remains a symbol of the enigmatic power of magic, with his artifacts and celestial presence serving as constant reminders of the god who shaped the mystical fabric of the world.', '''abandon'':52B ''across'':145B ''ada'':38B ''aetherius'':63B ''also'':69B ''altmer'':148B ''among'':15B ''arcan'':130B ''architect'':10B ''artifact'':116B,239B ''associ'':186B ''ayleid'':178B ''balanc'':136B ''believ'':76B ''breton'':150B ''call'':163B ''capabl'':132B ''cat'':167B ''celebr'':184B ''celesti'':241B ''collabor'':34B ''constant'':245B ''contribut'':204B ''creat'':114B ''creator'':23B ''credit'':112B ''cultur'':17B ''cycl'':176B ''dawn'':31B ''dedic'':179B ''departur'':56B ''despit'':222B ''detach'':224B ''divin'':190B ''dual'':217B ''energi'':201B ''enigmat'':233B ''era'':32B ''et'':37B ''eye'':124B,169B ''fabric'':254B ''figur'':14B ''follow'':91B ''forg'':40B ''form'':64B ''fragment'':79B ''ge'':94B ''gift'':221B ''god'':4B,155B,249B ''great'':9B,48B ''hold'':128B ''hole'':61B ''illumin'':95B ''immens'':129B ''imperi'':213B ''influenc'':134B,195B ''insight'':159B ''integr'':170B ''khajiit'':162B ''known'':20B ''legaci'':104B ''legend'':192B ''lend'':198B ''light'':188B ''like'':117B ''lunar'':175B ''made'':88B ''mage'':197B ''magic'':6B,139B,236B ''magna'':93B ''magnus'':1A,2B,73B,121B,126B,143B,194B,227B ''magnus’'':103B ''magrus'':165B ''mani'':16B ''mortal'':42B ''mundus'':28B,58B,206B ''mystic'':108B,253B ''mytho'':172B ''name'':183B 