INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glass_war_axe', 'Glass War Axe is a sturdy glass weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is sleek and translucent, with sharp edges and a greenish hue resembling polished malachite. To craft it: 1 refined malachite, 1 refined moonstone, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using moonstone at a workbench.', '''1'':36B,39B ''2'':43B ''adept'':57B ''axe'':3A,6B ''blacksmith'':48B ''craft'':34B,54B,60B ''damag'':15B ''deal'':13B ''design'':18B ''edg'':25B ''expert'':51B ''fantast'':14B ''forg'':49B ''glass'':1A,4B,10B ''greenish'':28B ''hue'':29B ''it.it'':61B ''leather'':44B ''malachit'':32B,38B ''moonston'':41B,67B ''polish'':31B ''refin'':37B,40B ''resembl'':30B ''sharp'':24B ''sleek'':20B ''smith'':52B,58B ''strip'':45B ''sturdi'':9B ''tempered/improved'':64B ''transluc'':22B ''use'':66B ''visual'':17B ''war'':2A,5B ''weapon'':11B ''workbench'':70B', 'blacksmith', 'Glass War Axe is a sturdy glass weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is sleek and translucent, with sharp edges and a greenish hue resembling polished malachite. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('three_thieves', 'Three Thieves, written by Anonymous, follows the story of three thieves in Morrowind as they plan and execute a heist on the Cobblers Guildhall. The book highlights the personalities of the thieves—Lledos, the experienced mastermind with a penchant for precision and technique; Imalyn, the impulsive and somewhat reckless thief; and Galsiah, the calm and strategic planner. Together, they navigate the dangerous world of theft in Tel Aruhn, discussing the finer points of assassination, stealth, and the art of robbery. Their plan unfolds smoothly, and they successfully steal the gold, leaving behind a trail of corpses.

The themes of the book center around betrayal, trust, and the complexities of the criminal underworld. The story not only focuses on the heist itself but also explores the dynamics between the three thieves, particularly the subtle undercurrents of manipulation and self-interest that ultimately lead to Lledos''s betrayal. As Lledos escapes with the gold, the tension builds to a chilling conclusion when Galsiah exacts her revenge on him for his treachery. Three Thieves offers a dark, cynical look at the lives of criminals and the consequences of their actions, blending crime, camaraderie, and treachery in a tight, suspenseful narrative.', '''action'':189B ''also'':124B ''anonym'':7B ''around'':104B ''art'':79B ''aruhn'':69B ''assassin'':75B ''behind'':93B ''betray'':105B,148B ''blend'':190B ''book'':28B,102B ''build'':157B ''calm'':55B ''camaraderi'':192B ''center'':103B ''chill'':160B ''cobbler'':25B ''complex'':109B ''conclus'':161B ''consequ'':186B ''corps'':97B ''crime'':191B ''crimin'':112B,183B ''cynic'':177B ''danger'':63B ''dark'':176B ''discuss'':70B ''dynam'':127B ''escap'':151B ''exact'':164B ''execut'':20B ''experienc'':36B ''explor'':125B ''finer'':72B ''focus'':118B ''follow'':8B ''galsiah'':53B,163B ''gold'':91B,154B ''guildhal'':26B ''heist'':22B,121B ''highlight'':29B ''imalyn'':45B ''impuls'':47B ''interest'':141B ''lead'':144B ''leav'':92B ''live'':181B ''lledo'':146B,150B ''look'':178B ''manipul'':137B ''mastermind'':37B ''morrowind'':15B ''narrat'':199B ''navig'':61B ''offer'':174B ''particular'':132B ''penchant'':40B ''person'':31B ''plan'':18B,83B ''planner'':58B ''point'':73B ''precis'':42B ''reckless'':50B ''reveng'':166B ''robberi'':81B ''self'':140B ''self-interest'':139B ''smooth'':85B ''somewhat'':49B ''steal'':89B ''stealth'':76B ''stori'':10B,115B ''strateg'':57B ''subtl'':134B ''success'':88B ''suspens'':198B ''techniqu'':44B ''tel'':68B ''tension'':156B ''theft'':66B ''theme'':99B ''thief'':51B ''thiev'':2A,4B,13B,131B,173B ''thieves—