INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bloodthirst', 'Bloodthirst is a legendary Akaviri longsword, crafted in the style of Dawnfang and Duskfang, with a design that evokes unease through its beast-like blade and blood-infused jewel. Renowned for its unquenchable thirst for blood, the sword enhances its wielder''s strength and speed. After a convoluted history involving betrayal, necromancy, and failed plots.', '''akaviri'':6B ''beast'':25B ''beast-lik'':24B ''betray'':54B ''blade'':27B ''blood'':30B,39B ''blood-infus'':29B ''bloodthirst'':1A,2B ''convolut'':51B ''craft'':8B ''dawnfang'':13B ''design'':18B ''duskfang'':15B ''enhanc'':42B ''evok'':20B ''fail'':57B ''histori'':52B ''infus'':31B ''involv'':53B ''jewel'':32B ''legendari'':5B ''like'':26B ''longsword'':7B ''necrom'':55B ''plot'':58B ''renown'':33B ''speed'':48B ''strength'':46B ''style'':11B ''sword'':41B ''thirst'':37B ''uneas'':21B ''unquench'':36B ''wielder'':44B', 'scholar', 'Bloodthirst is a legendary Akaviri longsword with a beast-like design and blood-infused jewel, known for enhancing the wielder''s strength and speed. Its history is marked by betrayal, necromancy, and failed schemes.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('flight_from_the_thalmor', 'Flight from the Thalmor, written by Hadrik Oaken-Heart, is a harrowing first-person account of a Nord skald''s defiance against the Thalmor and his subsequent flight for survival. The story begins with Hadrik''s bold decision to sing of Talos, the revered god of Skyrim, in defiance of the Thalmor''s ban on Talos worship, a law enforced by their Justiciars. His actions, which initially seemed like a simple act of defiance, lead to his capture and imprisonment by the Thalmor, where he faces the grim prospect of never leaving the secret detention camp alive. After an arduous escape, he spends the next nine days in constant flight, pursued relentlessly by the Aldmeri Dominion.

The themes of the book center on resistance, pride, and the harsh realities of living under oppressive rule. Hadrik’s struggle symbolizes the broader Nordic resistance to the Thalmor’s authoritarian control over Skyrim, reflecting the tension between personal conviction and the threat of overwhelming power. The book is a single volume, offering a raw and emotional narrative of one man''s fight for freedom in a world where the cost of defiance may be death.', '''account'':21B ''act'':78B ''action'':71B ''aldmeri'':121B ''aliv'':103B ''arduous'':106B ''authoritarian'':151B ''ban'':60B ''begin'':39B ''bold'':43B ''book'':127B,168B ''broader'':145B ''camp'':102B ''captur'':84B ''center'':128B ''constant'':115B ''control'':152B ''convict'':160B ''cost'':191B ''day'':113B ''death'':196B ''decis'':44B ''defianc'':27B,55B,80B,193B ''detent'':101B ''dominion'':122B ''emot'':177B ''enforc'':66B ''escap'':107B ''face'':92B ''fight'':183B ''first'':19B ''first-person'':18B ''flight'':1A,5B,34B,116B ''freedom'':185B ''god'':51B ''grim'':94B ''hadrik'':11B,41B ''hadrik’'':141B ''harrow'':17B ''harsh'':134B ''heart'':14B ''imprison'':86B ''initi'':73B ''justiciar'':69B ''law'':65B ''lead'':81B ''leav'':98B ''like'':75B ''live'':137B ''man'':181B ''may'':194B ''narrat'':178B ''never'':97B ''next'':111B ''nine'':112B ''nord'':24B ''nordic'':146B ''oaken'':13B ''oaken-heart'':12B ''offer'':173B ''one'':180B ''oppress'':139B ''overwhelm'':165B ''person'':20B,159B ''power'':166B ''pride'':131B ''prospect'':95B ''pursu'':117B ''raw'':175B ''realiti'':135B ''reflect'':155B ''relentless'':118B ''resist'':130B,147B ''rever'':50B ''rule'':140B ''secret'':100B ''seem'':74B ''simpl'':77B ''sing'':46B ''singl'':171B ''skald'':25B ''skyrim'':53B,154B ''spend'':109B ''stori'':38B ''struggl'':142B ''subsequ'':33B ''surviv'':36B ''symbol'':143B ''talo'':48B,62B ''tension'':157B ''thalmor'':4A,8B,30B,58B,89B ''thalmor’'':150B ''theme'':124B ''threat'':163B ''volum'':172B ''world'':188B ''worship'':63B ''written'':9B', 'scholar', '
