INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chaos_damage', 'These magical effects are offensive Destruction enchantments that deal randomized elemental damage—fire, frost, or shock—on each strike. This effect can be applied through custom enchanting and is also found on enchanted items, offering versatility in combat.', '''also'':30B ''appli'':24B ''chao'':1A ''combat'':38B ''custom'':26B ''damag'':2A ''damage—fir'':14B ''deal'':11B ''destruct'':8B ''effect'':5B,21B ''element'':13B ''enchant'':9B,27B,33B ''found'':31B ''frost'':15B ''item'':34B ''magic'':4B ''offens'':7B ''offer'':35B ''random'':12B ''shock—on'':17B ''strike'':19B ''versatil'':36B', 'mage', 'This enchantment randomly deals fire, frost, or shock damage, making it unpredictable in battle. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wispmother', 'Wispmothers, sometimes referred to as wispfathers, are mystical entities believed to be ghosts, wraiths, or nature spirits, commonly found in the wilds of Tamriel. These beings can communicate and often refer to the wisps that accompany them as their children. Legends from Black Marsh suggest that while a wispmother can be killed, its essence must be sealed to prevent it from resurrecting. In Valenwood, a rarer variant is known as the Amronal.', '''accompani'':37B ''amron'':73B ''be'':27B ''believ'':11B ''black'':44B ''children'':41B ''common'':19B ''communic'':29B ''entiti'':10B ''essenc'':55B ''found'':20B ''ghost'':14B ''kill'':53B ''known'':70B ''legend'':42B ''marsh'':45B ''must'':56B ''mystic'':9B ''natur'':17B ''often'':31B ''prevent'':60B ''rarer'':67B ''refer'':4B,32B ''resurrect'':63B ''seal'':58B ''sometim'':3B ''spirit'':18B ''suggest'':46B ''tamriel'':25B ''valenwood'':65B ''variant'':68B ''wild'':23B ''wisp'':35B ''wispfath'':7B ''wispmoth'':1A,2B,50B ''wraith'':15B', 'scholar, mage', '
Wispmothers are mystical entities, often believed to be ghosts or nature spirits, found in the wilds of Tamriel. They are accompanied by wisps, which they refer to as their children.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragon_priest', 'Dragon Priests are powerful undead beings that were once the devoted servants of the ancient dragons in Skyrim. Revered for their formidable magical abilities, these priests commanded legions of warriors in the name of their dragon deities. Today, they reside in ornate coffins within prominent dragon worship sites, and if disturbed, they will rise with great force to confront intruders.', '''abil'':26B ''ancient'':17B ''be'':8B ''coffin'':45B ''command'':29B ''confront'':61B ''deiti'':39B ''devot'':13B ''disturb'':53B ''dragon'':1A,3B,18B,38B,48B ''forc'':59B ''formid'':24B ''great'':58B ''intrud'':62B ''legion'':30B ''magic'':25B ''name'':35B ''ornat'':44B ''power'':6B ''priest'':2A,4B,28B ''promin'':47B ''resid'':42B ''rever'':21B ''rise'':56B ''servant'':14B ''site'':50B ''skyrim'':20B ''today'':40B ''undead'':7B ''warrior'':32B ''within'':46B ''worship'':49B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Dragon Priests are powerful undead beings who once served ancient dragons in Skyrim. They are thought to rest in ornate coffins at dragon worship sites, rising to confront intruders if disturbed.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orc_stronghold', '
Orc strongholds are fortified settlements primarily inhabited by Orcs, also known as Orsimer. These strongholds are typically located in remote, harsh regions such as Skyrim, Hammerfell, and Orsinium (the Orc homeland). They are often isolated from the rest of Tamrielic society, with the Orcs living a clan-based, warrior culture. The strongholds are often led by a chief, and Orcs are known for their crafting, particularly their skill in blacksmithing and the forging of weapons and armor. Though Orcs were once ostracized by other races, especially after the sacking of Orsinium, many Orcs now live in these strongholds, maintaining a fierce independence. Some strongholds have formed alliances with other factions, while others remain neutral or wary of outsiders. The Orcs’ traditional way of life is rooted in honor, strength, and self-reliance, making their strongholds key centers of Orcish identity.






', '''allianc'':110B ''also'':12B ''armor'':80B ''base'':51B ''blacksmith'':73B ''center'':141B ''chief'':61B ''clan'':50B ''clan-bas'':49B ''craft'':68B ''cultur'':53B ''especi'':89B ''faction'':113B ''fierc'':104B ''forg'':76B ''form'':109B ''fortifi'':6B ''hammerfel'':28B ''harsh'':23B ''homeland'':33B ''honor'':131B ''ident'':144B ''independ'':105B ''inhabit'':9B ''isol'':37B ''key'':140B ''known'':13B,65B ''led'':58B ''life'':127B ''live'':47B,98B ''locat'':20B ''maintain'':102B ''make'':137B ''mani'':95B ''neutral'':117B ''often'':36B,57B ''orc'':1A,3B,11B,32B,46B,63B,82B,96B ''orcish'':143B ''orcs’'':123B ''orsim'':15B ''orsinium'':30B,94B ''ostrac'':85B ''other'':115B ''outsid'':121B ''particular'':69B ''primarili'':8B ''race'':88B ''region'':24B ''relianc'':136B ''remain'':116B ''remot'':22B ''rest'':40B ''root'':129B ''sack'':92B ''self'':135B ''self-reli'':134B ''settlement'':7B ''skill'':71B ''skyrim'':27B ''societi'':43B ''strength'':132B ''stronghold'':2A,4B,17B,55B,101B,107B,139B ''tamriel'':42B ''though'':81B ''tradit'':124B ''typic'':19B ''wari'':119B ''warrior'':52B ''way'':125B ''weapon'':78B', 'orc, scholar', 'Orc strongholds are fortified settlements primarily inhabited by Orcs, also known as Orsimer. These strongholds are typically located in remote, harsh regions such as Skyrim, Hammerfell, and Orsinium (the Orc homeland). They are often isolated from the rest of Tamrielic society, with the Orcs living a clan-based, warrior culture. The strongholds are often led by a chief, and Orcs are known for their crafting, particularly their skill in blacksmithing and the forging of weapons and arm', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('draugr', 'Draugr are the mummified remains of ancient Nords, found primarily in the cold, tomb-laden landscapes of Skyrim and Solstheim. These undead creatures were preserved before their reanimation, which has helped them retain much of their physical integrity, allowing their muscles and ligaments to resist decay. This preservation has resulted in a diverse range of combat styles among draugr, reflecting the varied skills they possessed in life.', '''allow'':41B ''among'':60B ''ancient'':8B ''cold'':14B ''combat'':58B ''creatur'':25B ''decay'':48B ''divers'':55B ''draugr'':1A,2B,61B ''found'':10B ''help'':33B ''integr'':40B ''laden'':17B ''landscap'':18B ''life'':69B ''ligament'':45B ''much'':36B ''mummifi'':5B ''muscl'':43B ''nord'':9B ''physic'':39B ''possess'':67B ''preserv'':27B,50B ''primarili'':11B ''rang'':56B ''reanim'':30B ''reflect'':62B ''remain'':6B ''resist'':47B ''result'':52B ''retain'':35B ''skill'':65B ''skyrim'':20B ''solstheim'':22B ''style'':59B ''tomb'':16B ''tomb-laden'':15B ''undead'':24B ''vari'':64B', 'nord, scholar', 'Draugr are the mummified remains of ancient Nords. They are believed to reanimate and attack any intruders to their ancient burial sites.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pygmy_sunfish', 'Pygmy Sunfish are rare small black and blue fish found near Heartwood Mill, west of Riften. It is rumored it can only be caught with an alikri fishing rod while wearing a Lucky Fishing Hat. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Restore Stamina, Lingering Damage Magicka, Damage Magicka Regen and Fortify Restoration.', '''alikri'':29B ''black'':8B ''blue'':10B ''caught'':26B ''damag'':54B,56B ''effect'':48B ''fish'':11B,30B,36B ''fortifi'':60B ''found'':12B ''hat'':37B ''heartwood'':14B ''ingredi'':42B ''linger'':53B ''lucki'':35B ''magicka'':55B,57B ''make'':45B ''mill'':15B ''near'':13B ''offer'':47B ''potion'':44B ''pygmi'':1A,3B ''rare'':6B ''regen'':58B ''restor'':51B,61B ''riften'':18B ''rod'':31B ''rumor'':21B ''small'':7B ''stamina'':52B ''sunfish'':2A,4B ''use'':39B ''wear'':33B ''west'':16B', 'fisher', 'Pygmy Sunfish are rare small black and blue fish found  You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_persuasion', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration enchantments that enhance the caster;s ability to influence others in dialogue, increasing the likelihood of success in persuasion, intimidation, or bargaining. This effect is only available on enchanted gear, making it a rare boon for charismatic adventurers.', '''abil'':17B ''adventur'':48B ''avail'':37B ''bargain'':32B ''boon'':45B ''caster'':15B ''charismat'':47B ''dialogu'':22B ''effect'':5B,34B ''enchant'':11B,39B ''enhanc'':13B ''focus'':9B ''fortifi'':1A ''gear'':40B ''increas'':23B ''influenc'':19B ''intimid'':30B ''likelihood'':25B ''magic'':4B ''make'':41B ''other'':20B ''persuas'':2A,29B ''rare'':44B ''restor'':10B ''success'':27B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B', 'mage', 'This enchantment improves your ability to persuade or intimidate others in conversations. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('horker', 'Horkers are sea animals resembling walruses, commonly found in packs near rivers and icy shores in northern Skyrim. They are slow and easy to avoid on land but become faster and harder to outrun in water. If provoked, horkers will become hostile. Looting their bodies may yield horker meat, tusks, and occasionally small amounts of gold or gems.', '''amount'':55B ''anim'':5B ''avoid'':26B ''becom'':30B,42B ''bodi'':46B ''common'':8B ''easi'':24B ''faster'':31B ''found'':9B ''gem'':59B ''gold'':57B ''harder'':33B ''horker'':1A,2B,40B,49B ''hostil'':43B ''ici'':15B ''land'':28B ''loot'':44B ''may'':47B ''meat'':50B ''near'':12B ''northern'':18B ''occasion'':53B ''outrun'':35B ''pack'':11B ''provok'':39B ''resembl'':6B ''river'':13B ''sea'':4B ''shore'':16B ''skyrim'':19B ''slow'':22B ''small'':54B ''tusk'':51B ''walrus'':7B ''water'':37B ''yield'':48B', 'hunter', 'Horkers are sea animals resembling walruses, commonly found in packs near rivers and icy shores in northern Skyrim. They are slow and easy to avoid on land but become faster and harder to outrun in water.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mammoth', '
Mammoths are massive creatures found in the tundra of Skyrim, often seen alongside giants or traveling under their protection. They have long tusks, with tame mammoths having engraved tusks, while wild ones have plain tusks. Mammoths will defend themselves if attacked, with the herding giant rushing to protect them, but will turn passive if the giant is killed. They avoid water and can get stuck behind obstacles, making them easier to evade or attack from a distance.', '''alongsid'':14B ''attack'':42B,75B ''avoid'':61B ''behind'':67B ''creatur'':5B ''defend'':39B ''distanc'':78B ''easier'':71B ''engrav'':29B ''evad'':73B ''found'':6B ''get'':65B ''giant'':15B,46B,57B ''herd'':45B ''kill'':59B ''long'':23B ''make'':69B ''mammoth'':1A,2B,27B,37B ''massiv'':4B ''obstacl'':68B ''often'':12B ''one'':33B ''passiv'':54B ''plain'':35B ''protect'':20B,49B ''rush'':47B ''seen'':13B ''skyrim'':11B ''stuck'':66B ''tame'':26B ''travel'':17B ''tundra'':9B ''turn'':53B ''tusk'':24B,30B,36B ''water'':62B ''wild'':32B', 'hunter', 'Mammoths are massive creatures  with long tusks found in the tundra of Skyrim, often seen alongside giants or traveling under their protection. ', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('battle-born_farm', 'Battle-Born Farm is a productive homestead located just east of Whiterun and north of Chillfurrow Farm, nestled in the rolling fields of Whiterun Hold. Owned by the influential Battle-Born clan, the farm is tended by Alfhild and Gwendolyn, who diligently manage its fertile fields and livestock.

The farm boasts expansive fields planted with leeks, gourds, and wheat, along with a penned cow and free-roaming chickens. ', '''alfhild'':44B ''along'':66B ''battl'':2A,6B,36B ''battle-born'':1A,5B,35B ''boast'':57B ''born'':3A,7B,37B ''chicken'':75B ''chillfurrow'':21B ''clan'':38B ''cow'':70B ''dilig'':48B ''east'':15B ''expans'':58B ''farm'':4A,8B,22B,40B,56B ''fertil'':51B ''field'':27B,52B,59B ''free'':73B ''free-roam'':72B ''gourd'':63B ''gwendolyn'':46B ''hold'':30B ''homestead'':12B ''influenti'':34B ''leek'':62B ''livestock'':54B ''locat'':13B ''manag'':49B ''nestl'':23B ''north'':19B ''own'':31B ''pen'':69B ''plant'':60B ''product'':11B ''roam'':74B ''roll'':26B ''tend'':42B ''wheat'':65B ''whiterun'':17B,29B', 'whiterun', 'Battle-Born Farm is a productive homestead located just east of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('conjure_familiar', 'Conjure Familiar is a Conjuration spell that summons a spectral wolf to fight alongside the caster for a limited time. It requires a Novice skill level to cast.', '''alongsid'':16B ''cast'':30B ''caster'':18B ''conjur'':1A,3B,7B ''familiar'':2A,4B ''fight'':15B ''level'':28B ''limit'':21B ''novic'':26B ''requir'':24B ''skill'':27B ''spectral'':12B ''spell'':8B ''summon'':10B ''time'':22B ''wolf'':13B', 'mage', 'Conjure Familiar is a spell that summons a spectral wolf to fight by the caster''s side for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('whiterun_stormcloak_camp', 'The Whiterun Stormcloak Camp is a rugged military encampment in Whiterun Hold, located south of the Ritual Stone and east of White River Watch. Commanded by Hjornskar Head-Smasher, the camp serves as a strategic outpost for the Stormcloak rebellion during their efforts to wrest control of Whiterun from Imperial forces.', '''camp'':3A,7B,35B ''command'':28B ''control'':50B ''east'':23B ''effort'':47B ''encamp'':12B ''forc'':55B ''head'':32B ''head-smash'':31B ''hjornskar'':30B ''hold'':15B ''imperi'':54B ''locat'':16B ''militari'':11B ''outpost'':40B ''rebellion'':44B ''ritual'':20B ''river'':26B ''rug'':10B ''serv'':36B ''smasher'':33B ''south'':17B ''stone'':21B ''stormcloak'':2A,6B,43B ''strateg'':39B ''watch'':27B ''white'':25B ''whiterun'':1A,5B,14B,52B ''wrest'':49B', 'whiterun, stormcloak', 'The Whiterun Stormcloak Camp is a rugged military encampment in  the eastern part of Whiterun Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_wild_elves', 'The Wild Elves, written by Kier-Jo Chorvak, provides an overview of the Ayleids, often called the Wild Elves, who have remained secluded from the mainstream cultures of Tamriel. While the other Elven races—the Altmer, Bosmer, and Dunmer—have integrated into society, the Ayleids continue to follow their ancient customs, living far from civilization. They speak a variation of Old Cyrodilic and maintain a dark and reserved demeanor that contrasts with the more familiar Elven cultures. Although outsiders view them with suspicion, scholars like Tjurhane Fyrre offer a different perspective, suggesting that the Ayleids have a vibrant and multifaceted culture.

The book explores themes of cultural isolation, fear of the unknown, and the complexity of ancient traditions. The Ayleids'' refusal to assimilate into Tamrielic society has led to their enigmatic status, with little documented history to illuminate their ways. Their mysterious nature, combined with their elusive presence in history, has kept them one of the most enigmatic peoples of Tamriel. Chorvak''s work underscores how the Ayleids'' reluctance to engage with the outside world has preserved their culture, but also left them shrouded in myth and legend. The book is a single volume and serves as a brief yet intriguing introduction to a largely forgotten race of elves.', '''also'':183B ''although'':80B ''altmer'':39B ''ancient'':52B,119B ''assimil'':125B ''ayleid'':18B,47B,97B,122B,170B ''book'':105B,192B ''bosmer'':40B ''brief'':201B ''call'':20B ''chorvak'':12B,164B ''civil'':57B ''combin'':146B ''complex'':117B ''continu'':48B ''contrast'':73B ''cultur'':31B,79B,103B,109B,181B ''custom'':53B ''cyrodil'':64B ''dark'':68B ''demeanor'':71B ''differ'':92B ''document'':137B ''dunmer—hav'':42B ''elus'':149B ''elv'':3A,6B,23B,211B ''elven'':37B,78B ''engag'':173B ''enigmat'':133B,160B ''explor'':106B ''familiar'':77B ''far'':55B ''fear'':111B ''follow'':50B ''forgotten'':208B ''fyrr'':89B ''histori'':138B,152B ''illumin'':140B ''integr'':43B ''intrigu'':203B ''introduct'':204B ''isol'':110B ''jo'':11B ''kept'':154B ''kier'':10B ''kier-jo'':9B ''larg'':207B ''led'':130B ''left'':184B ''legend'':190B ''like'':87B ''littl'':136B ''live'':54B ''mainstream'':30B ''maintain'':66B ''multifacet'':102B ''mysteri'':144B ''myth'':188B ''natur'':145B ''offer'':90B ''often'':19B ''old'':63B ''one'':156B ''outsid'':81B,176B ''overview'':15B ''peopl'':161B ''perspect'':93B ''presenc'':150B ''preserv'':179B ''provid'':13B ''race'':209B ''races—th'':38B ''refus'':123B ''reluct'':171B ''remain'':26B ''reserv'':70B ''scholar'':86B ''seclud'':27B ''serv'':198B ''shroud'':186B ''singl'':195B ''societi'':45B,128B ''speak'':59B ''status'':134B ''suggest'':94B ''suspicion'':85B ''tamriel'':33B,127B,163B ''theme'':107B ''tjurhan'':88B ''tradit'':120B ''underscor'':167B ''unknown'':114B ''variat'':61B ''vibrant'':100B ''view'':82B ''volum'':196B ''way'':142B ''wild'':2A,5B,22B ''work'':166B ''world'':177B ''written'':7B ''yet'':202B', 'scholar', '
The Wild Elves, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, examines the enigmatic Ayleids, focusing on themes of cultural isolation, ancient traditions, and the fear of the unknown. The book highlights how their seclusion preserves their unique customs while keeping their history and ways shrouded in mystery and myth.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pelagia_farm', 'Pelagia Farm is a large and thriving homestead located south of Whiterun Stables and west of Honningbrew Meadery in the fertile plains of Whiterun Hold. Owned by Severio Pelagia, the farm is a bustling agricultural hub, managed by his workers Nimriel and Gloth, who live on-site while Severio resides in Whiterun.

The farm is characterized by its sprawling fields of vegetables, enclosed by stone walls and fences, where Severio often works alongside his laborers during the day. A grain mill stands to the east of the farmhouse, and the property includes various outbuildings and storage sheds. To the west, a penned cow grazes peacefully, while chickens nest near the farmhouse entrance.', '''agricultur'':37B ''alongsid'':76B ''bustl'':36B ''character'':59B ''chicken'':110B ''cow'':106B ''day'':81B ''east'':88B ''enclos'':66B ''entranc'':115B ''farm'':2A,4B,33B,57B ''farmhous'':91B,114B ''fenc'':71B ''fertil'':23B ''field'':63B ''gloth'':45B ''grain'':83B ''graze'':107B ''hold'':27B ''homestead'':10B ''honningbrew'':19B ''hub'':38B ''includ'':95B ''labor'':78B ''larg'':7B ''live'':47B ''locat'':11B ''manag'':39B ''meaderi'':20B ''mill'':84B ''near'':112B ''nest'':111B ''nimriel'':43B ''often'':74B ''on-sit'':48B ''outbuild'':97B ''own'':28B ''peac'':108B ''pelagia'':1A,3B,31B ''pen'':105B ''plain'':24B ''properti'':94B ''resid'':53B ''severio'':30B,52B,73B ''shed'':100B ''site'':50B ''south'':12B ''sprawl'':62B ''stabl'':15B ''stand'':85B ''stone'':68B ''storag'':99B ''thrive'':9B ''various'':96B ''veget'':65B ''wall'':69B ''west'':17B,103B ''whiterun'':14B,26B,55B ''work'':75B ''worker'':42B', 'whiterun', 'Pelagia Farm is a large and thriving homestead located south of Whiterun Stables.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('guldun_rock', 'Guldun Rock is a secluded giant camp located east of Whiterun and south of Valtheim Towers, nestled along the road that traces the White River toward Fort Amol. A marked path, distinguished by a stone cairn surrounded by tundra cotton and vibrant mountain flowers, leads to the camp, winding up to a plateau where the giants dwell.

The camp is home to a few giants who guard their territory amid scattered mammoth cheese bowls, bones, and skulls. Painted stones and frost mirriam bundles decorate the area, giving it an air of primal ritual. The campfire, set atop a ruined stone structure near the entrance to Guldun Rock Cave, offers a commanding view of the surrounding plains to the north. ', '''air'':92B ''along'':20B ''amid'':72B ''amol'':30B ''area'':88B ''atop'':99B ''bone'':77B ''bowl'':76B ''bundl'':85B ''cairn'':38B ''camp'':9B,50B,61B ''campfir'':97B ''cave'':110B ''chees'':75B ''command'':113B ''cotton'':42B ''decor'':86B ''distinguish'':34B ''dwell'':59B ''east'':11B ''entranc'':106B ''flower'':46B ''fort'':29B ''frost'':83B ''giant'':8B,58B,67B ''give'':89B ''guard'':69B ''guldun'':1A,3B,108B ''home'':63B ''lead'':47B ''locat'':10B ''mammoth'':74B ''mark'':32B ''mirriam'':84B ''mountain'':45B ''near'':104B ''nestl'':19B ''north'':121B ''offer'':111B ''paint'':80B ''path'':33B ''plain'':118B ''plateau'':55B ''primal'':94B ''ritual'':95B ''river'':27B ''road'':22B ''rock'':2A,4B,109B ''ruin'':101B ''scatter'':73B ''seclud'':7B ''set'':98B ''skull'':79B ''south'':15B ''stone'':37B,81B,102B ''structur'':103B ''surround'':39B,117B ''territori'':71B ''toward'':28B ''tower'':18B ''trace'':24B ''tundra'':41B ''valtheim'':17B ''vibrant'':44B ''view'':114B ''white'':26B ''whiterun'':13B ''wind'':51B', 'whiterun', 'Guldun Rock is a secluded giant camp located east of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('high_hrothgar', 'High Hrothgar is a secluded settlement perched roughly halfway up the Throat of the World, southeast of Whiterun. As a major landmark, it serves as the home of the Greybeards, the reclusive masters of the Thu''um, or The Voice. Revered as a place of spiritual significance, High Hrothgar is steeped in ancient tradition and shrouded in an air of solemnity.

Reaching High Hrothgar requires traversing the legendary "7,000 Steps" from Ivarstead, a treacherous ascent fraught with challenges. Along the way, travelers may encounter hostile creatures such as frost trolls, snow bears, and ice wraiths.', '''000'':72B ''7'':71B ''air'':61B ''along'':82B ''ancient'':55B ''ascent'':78B ''bear'':95B ''challeng'':81B ''creatur'':89B ''encount'':87B ''fraught'':79B ''frost'':92B ''greybeard'':32B ''halfway'':11B ''high'':1A,3B,50B,65B ''home'':29B ''hostil'':88B ''hrothgar'':2A,4B,51B,66B ''ice'':97B ''ivarstead'':75B ''landmark'':24B ''legendari'':70B ''major'':23B ''master'':35B ''may'':86B ''perch'':9B ''place'':46B ''reach'':64B ''reclus'':34B ''requir'':67B ''rever'':43B ''rough'':10B ''seclud'':7B ''serv'':26B ''settlement'':8B ''shroud'':58B ''signific'':49B ''snow'':94B ''solemn'':63B ''southeast'':18B ''spiritu'':48B ''steep'':53B ''step'':73B ''throat'':14B ''thu'':38B ''tradit'':56B ''travel'':85B ''travers'':68B ''treacher'':77B ''troll'':93B ''um'':39B ''voic'':42B ''way'':84B ''whiterun'':20B ''world'':17B ''wraith'':98B', 'whiterun, dragon, scholar', 'High Hrothgar is a secluded settlement perched roughly halfway up the Throat of the World, southeast of Whiterun. As a major landmark, it serves as the home of the Greybeards, the reclusive masters of the Thu''um, or The Voice. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frenzy_rune', 'Frenzy Rune is an Illusion spell that places a magical rune on the ground, causing any enemy that steps on it to become enraged and attack nearby creatures or people. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':36B ''attack'':28B ''becom'':25B ''cast'':40B ''caus'':17B ''creatur'':30B ''enemi'':19B ''enrag'':26B ''frenzi'':1A,3B ''ground'':16B ''illus'':7B ''level'':38B ''magic'':12B ''nearbi'':29B ''peopl'':32B ''place'':10B ''requir'':34B ''rune'':2A,4B,13B ''skill'':37B ''spell'':8B ''step'':21B', 'mage', 'Frenzy Rune is a spell that places a magical rune on the ground, causing any enemy that steps on it to become enraged and attack nearby creatures or people. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('valtheim_towers', 'Valtheim Towers is a pair of ancient Nordic towers located east of Whiterun and west of Darkshade, perched along the White River in Whiterun Hold. Once a defensive structure, the towers are now in ruins and have been taken over by bandits who use the location to control passage along the river and extort tolls from travelers.

The two towers are linked by a precarious bridge spanning the river, and their commanding position provides a clear view of the surrounding area. Despite their dilapidated state, the bandits have fortified the towers and made them a base of operations, making this once-proud structure a dangerous place for unwary adventurers.', '''adventur'':112B ''along'':21B,52B ''ancient'':9B ''area'':83B ''bandit'':44B,89B ''base'':98B ''bridg'':68B ''clear'':78B ''command'':74B ''control'':50B ''danger'':108B ''darkshad'':19B ''defens'':30B ''despit'':84B ''dilapid'':86B ''east'':13B ''extort'':56B ''fortifi'':91B ''hold'':27B ''link'':64B ''locat'':12B,48B ''made'':95B ''make'':101B ''nordic'':10B ''once-proud'':103B ''oper'':100B ''pair'':7B ''passag'':51B ''perch'':20B ''place'':109B ''posit'':75B ''precari'':67B ''proud'':105B ''provid'':76B ''river'':24B,54B,71B ''ruin'':37B ''span'':69B ''state'':87B ''structur'':31B,106B ''surround'':82B ''taken'':41B ''toll'':57B ''tower'':2A,4B,11B,33B,62B,93B ''travel'':59B ''two'':61B ''unwari'':111B ''use'':46B ''valtheim'':1A,3B ''view'':79B ''west'':17B ''white'':23B ''whiterun'':15B,26B', 'whiterun', 'Valtheim Towers is a pair of ancient Nordic towers located east of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('charwich-koniinge_letters', 'Charwich-Koniinge Letters, written by Charwich and Koniinge, is a four-volume collection of letters chronicling the perilous search for the Daedric artifact Azura''s Star. The correspondence reveals a tale of intrigue, deception, and betrayal as the two adventurers, Charwich and Koniinge, navigate a web of lies, Daedric forces, and deadly encounters. Their journey spans High Rock, Morrowind, and beyond, as they pursue Hadwaf Neithwyr, a conjurer who first summoned Azura to obtain the Star. Themes of trust, ambition, and the corrupting influence of power drive the narrative, ultimately culminating in Charwich''s betrayal and Koniinge''s vengeful quest.

The series reveals the dark consequences of greed and ambition. While Charwich manipulates Koniinge with fabricated stories of his death and a fictional Daedric adversary, Koniinge unravels the truth and exacts his revenge. The letters highlight the lengths individuals will go to attain power and the deadly price of betrayal, leaving a trail of destruction and lost lives in their wake. The story emphasizes the dangers of meddling with Daedric artifacts and the fragile nature of trust in a world rife with treachery.', '''adventur'':46B ''adversari'':131B ''ambit'':86B,116B ''artifact'':29B,177B ''attain'':149B ''azura'':30B,78B ''betray'':42B,101B,156B ''beyond'':67B ''charwich'':2A,6B,11B,47B,99B,118B ''charwich-koniing'':1A,5B ''chronicl'':22B ''collect'':19B ''conjur'':74B ''consequ'':112B ''correspond'':34B ''corrupt'':89B ''culmin'':97B ''daedric'':28B,55B,130B,176B ''danger'':172B ''dark'':111B ''dead'':58B,153B ''death'':126B ''decept'':40B ''destruct'':161B ''drive'':93B ''emphas'':170B ''encount'':59B ''exact'':137B ''fabric'':122B ''fiction'':129B ''first'':76B ''forc'':56B ''four'':17B ''four-volum'':16B ''fragil'':180B ''go'':147B ''greed'':114B ''hadwaf'':71B ''high'':63B ''highlight'':142B ''individu'':145B ''influenc'':90B ''intrigu'':39B ''journey'':61B ''koniing'':3A,7B,13B,49B,103B,120B,132B ''leav'':157B ''length'':144B ''letter'':4A,8B,21B,141B ''lie'':54B ''live'':164B ''lost'':163B ''manipul'':119B ''meddl'':174B ''morrowind'':65B ''narrat'':95B ''natur'':181B ''navig'':50B ''neithwyr'':72B ''obtain'':80B ''peril'':24B ''power'':92B,150B ''price'':154B ''pursu'':70B ''quest'':106B ''reveal'':35B,109B ''reveng'':139B ''rife'':187B ''rock'':64B ''search'':25B ''seri'':108B ''span'':62B ''star'':32B,82B ''stori'':123B,169B ''summon'':77B ''tale'':37B ''theme'':83B ''trail'':159B ''treacheri'':189B ''trust'':85B,183B ''truth'':135B ''two'':45B ''ultim'':96B ''unravel'':133B ''veng'':105B ''volum'':18B ''wake'':167B ''web'':52B ''world'':186B ''written'':9B', 'scholar', 'Charwich-Koniinge Letters, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, follows the dangerous pursuit of the Daedric artifact Azura''s Star, revealing a tale of betrayal, manipulation, and deadly encounters. Themes of ambition, trust, the corrupting influence of power, and the consequences of greed are central, illustrating the destructive cost of meddling with Daedric artifacts and the fragility of trust.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('north_skybound_watch', 'Skybound Watch Pass is a small, ancient Nordic ruin located northeast of Helgen and west of Orphan Rock, straddling the border of Falkreath Hold. The pass connects two distinct entrances: South Skybound Watch, marked by a Nordic tower south of Riverwood, and North Skybound Watch, represented as a Nordic ruin southeast of the town. These entrances form a hidden pathway through the mountain, offering a secluded and perilous route.

The ruins are inhabited by bandits making it a dangerous place for travelers', '''ancient'':10B ''bandit'':78B ''border'':24B ''connect'':30B ''danger'':82B ''distinct'':32B ''entranc'':33B,59B ''falkreath'':26B ''form'':60B ''helgen'':16B ''hidden'':62B ''hold'':27B ''inhabit'':76B ''locat'':13B ''make'':79B ''mark'':37B ''mountain'':66B ''nordic'':11B,40B,52B ''north'':1A,46B ''northeast'':14B ''offer'':67B ''orphan'':20B ''pass'':6B,29B ''pathway'':63B ''peril'':71B ''place'':83B ''repres'':49B ''riverwood'':44B ''rock'':21B ''rout'':72B ''ruin'':12B,53B,74B ''seclud'':69B ''skybound'':2A,4B,35B,47B ''small'':9B ''south'':34B,42B ''southeast'':54B ''straddl'':22B ''tower'':41B ''town'':57B ''travel'':85B ''two'':31B ''watch'':3A,5B,36B,48B ''west'':18B', 'whiterun, legion, stormcloak', 'Skybound Watch Pass is a small, ancient Nordic ruin located northeast of Helgen.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('swindlers_den', 'Swindler''s Den is a small, secluded cave located east of Rorikstead and south of Rannveig''s Fast, nestled within the arid foothills of Whiterun Hold. The cave serves as a hideout for bandits, who have established a makeshift base within its winding passages.', '''arid'':24B ''bandit'':36B ''base'':42B ''cave'':10B,30B ''den'':2A,5B ''east'':12B ''establish'':39B ''fast'':20B ''foothil'':25B ''hideout'':34B ''hold'':28B ''locat'':11B ''makeshift'':41B ''nestl'':21B ''passag'':46B ''rannveig'':18B ''rorikstead'':14B ''seclud'':9B ''serv'':31B ''small'':8B ''south'':16B ''swindler'':1A,3B ''whiterun'':27B ''wind'':45B ''within'':22B,43B', 'whiterun', 'Swindler''s Den is a small, secluded cave located east of Rorikstead.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('aversion_to_magic', 'A general-purpose tool, this poison heightens the target''s vulnerability to all magic, making them susceptible to spells. Stronger poisons amplify this vulnerability. These poisons can be found in random loot, purchased from apothecaries, or crafted using alchemy. Tiers: weak, standard, potent, virulent, deadly.', '''alchemi'':43B ''amplifi'':26B ''apothecari'':39B ''avers'':1A ''craft'':41B ''dead'':49B ''found'':33B ''general'':6B ''general-purpos'':5B ''heighten'':11B ''loot'':36B ''magic'':3A,18B ''make'':19B ''poison'':10B,25B,30B ''potent'':47B ''purchas'':37B ''purpos'':7B ''random'':35B ''spell'':23B ''standard'':46B ''stronger'':24B ''suscept'':21B ''target'':13B ''tier'':44B ''tool'':8B ''use'':42B ''virul'':48B ''vulner'':15B,28B ''weak'':45B', 'alchemist, mage, scholar, psijic, collegeofwinterhold, daedric', 'This poison increases a target''s vulnerability to all forms of magic. You do not know the full effects or details of this poison. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_sphere', 'Dwarven Spheres, also referred to as Centurion Spheres or Dwarven Centurions, are formidable automatons crafted by the Dwemer, known for their agility and combat strength. These constructs typically patrol ancient ruins in a spherical form, remaining dormant until they detect intruders. Upon encountering an opponent, they emerge from their protective shells to engage in combat.', '''agil'':24B ''also'':5B ''ancient'':32B ''automaton'':16B ''centurion'':9B,13B ''combat'':26B,57B ''construct'':29B ''craft'':17B ''detect'':42B ''dormant'':39B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,12B ''dwemer'':20B ''emerg'':49B ''encount'':45B ''engag'':55B ''form'':37B ''formid'':15B ''intrud'':43B ''known'':21B ''oppon'':47B ''patrol'':31B ''protect'':52B ''refer'':6B ''remain'':38B ''ruin'':33B ''shell'':53B ''sphere'':2A,4B,10B ''spheric'':36B ''strength'':27B ''typic'':30B ''upon'':44B', 'dwemer', '
Dwarven Spheres are powerful automatons created by the Dwemer, that will attack anyone foolish enough to enter a dwemer ruin.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('graywinter_watch', 'Graywinter Watch is a small, shadowy cave located east of Whiterun and south of Shimmermist Cave, nestled beneath the Ritual Stone''s rocky foundation overlooking the White River. A dirt path along the western side of the Ritual Stone leads directly to the cave, making it easily accessible from the nearby road. 

It is rumoured the cave is home to trolls.', '''access'':50B ''along'':34B ''beneath'':20B ''cave'':9B,18B,46B,59B ''direct'':43B ''dirt'':32B ''easili'':49B ''east'':11B ''foundat'':26B ''graywint'':1A,3B ''home'':61B ''lead'':42B ''locat'':10B ''make'':47B ''nearbi'':53B ''nestl'':19B ''overlook'':27B ''path'':33B ''ritual'':22B,40B ''river'':30B ''road'':54B ''rocki'':25B ''rumour'':57B ''shadowi'':8B ''shimmermist'':17B ''side'':37B ''small'':7B ''south'':15B ''stone'':23B,41B ''troll'':63B ''watch'':2A,4B ''western'':36B ''white'':29B ''whiterun'':13B', 'whiterun', 'Graywinter Watch is a small, shadowy cave located east of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ritual_stone', 'The Ritual Stone is one of Skyrim''s thirteen enigmatic Standing Stones, located east of Whiterun by the roadside, perched on a rocky outcrop overlooking the entrance to Graywinter Watch. This ancient monument is marked by its circle of candles and commands a commanding view of the surrounding landscape.

The stone grants a powerful and unique blessing to those who activate it, enabling them to reanimate nearby corpses to fight as allies for a limited time. The raised bodies remain intact after the power''s effects wear off, and there is no limit to how many corpses can be reanimated.

The path leading to the stone winds upward through squared-off arches, reflecting the artistry and mysticism of the Nords who revered these ancient relics. The Ritual Stone''s eerie aura and potent magic serve as a testament to the mysterious forces that shape Skyrim''s untamed lands.', '''activ'':63B ''alli'':74B ''ancient'':34B,127B ''arch'':115B ''artistri'':118B ''aura'':134B ''bless'':59B ''bodi'':81B ''candl'':42B ''circl'':40B ''command'':44B,46B ''corps'':70B,99B ''east'':16B ''eeri'':133B ''effect'':88B ''enabl'':65B ''enigmat'':12B ''entranc'':29B ''fight'':72B ''forc'':145B ''grant'':54B ''graywint'':31B ''intact'':83B ''land'':151B ''landscap'':51B ''lead'':105B ''limit'':77B,95B ''locat'':15B ''magic'':137B ''mani'':98B ''mark'':37B ''monument'':35B ''mysteri'':144B ''mystic'':120B ''nearbi'':69B ''nord'':123B ''one'':7B ''outcrop'':26B ''overlook'':27B ''path'':104B ''perch'':22B ''potent'':136B ''power'':56B,86B ''rais'':80B ''reanim'':68B,102B ''reflect'':116B ''relic'':128B ''remain'':82B ''rever'':125B ''ritual'':1A,4B,130B ''roadsid'':21B ''rocki'':25B ''serv'':138B ''shape'':147B ''skyrim'':9B,148B ''squar'':113B ''squared-off'':112B ''stand'':13B ''stone'':2A,5B,14B,53B,108B,131B ''surround'':50B ''testament'':141B ''thirteen'':11B ''time'':78B ''uniqu'':58B ''untam'':150B ''upward'':110B ''view'':47B ''watch'':32B ''wear'':89B ''whiterun'':18B ''wind'':109B', 'whiterun, scholar, traveler', 'The Ritual Stone is one of Skyrim''s thirteen enigmatic Standing Stones, located east of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('house_gray-mane', 'House Gray-Mane is the ancestral home of Clan Gray-Mane, one of Whiterun''s most prominent and traditional families. Situated in the Wind District, the house stands directly opposite the sacred Gildergreen tree, at the top of the stairs leading up from the bustling marketplace.

The home reflects the clan''s storied history and deep-rooted Nordic pride, serving as a gathering place for its members amidst the political tensions of Whiterun. As staunch supporters of the Stormcloak rebellion and advocates for Nordic independence, the Gray-Manes are known for their unwavering values and rivalry with the Imperial-aligned Clan Battle-Born. ', '''advoc'':89B ''align'':109B ''amidst'':75B ''ancestr'':11B ''battl'':112B ''battle-born'':111B ''born'':113B ''bustl'':51B ''clan'':14B,57B,110B ''deep'':63B ''deep-root'':62B ''direct'':35B ''district'':31B ''famili'':26B ''gather'':70B ''gildergreen'':39B ''gray'':3A,7B,16B,95B ''gray-man'':2A,6B,15B,94B ''histori'':60B ''home'':12B,54B ''hous'':1A,5B,33B ''imperi'':108B ''imperial-align'':107B ''independ'':92B ''known'':98B ''lead'':47B ''mane'':4A,8B,17B,96B ''marketplac'':52B ''member'':74B ''nordic'':65B,91B ''one'':18B ''opposit'':36B ''place'':71B ''polit'':77B ''pride'':66B ''promin'':23B ''rebellion'':87B ''reflect'':55B ''rivalri'':104B ''root'':64B ''sacr'':38B ''serv'':67B ''situat'':27B ''stair'':46B ''stand'':34B ''staunch'':82B ''stori'':59B ''stormcloak'':86B ''support'':83B ''tension'':78B ''top'':43B ''tradit'':25B ''tree'':40B ''unwav'':101B ''valu'':102B ''whiterun'':20B,80B ''wind'':30B', 'whiterun, noble', 'House Gray-Mane is the ancestral home of Clan Gray-Mane, one of Whiterun''s most prominent and traditional families. Situated in the Wind District.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('flame_thrall', 'Flame Thrall is a Conjuration spell that permanently summons a Flame Atronach to fight for the caster until it is defeated. It requires a Master skill level to cast.', '''atronach'':14B ''cast'':31B ''caster'':19B ''conjur'':7B ''defeat'':23B ''fight'':16B ''flame'':1A,3B,13B ''level'':29B ''master'':27B ''perman'':10B ''requir'':25B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':8B ''summon'':11B ''thrall'':2A,4B', 'mage', '
