INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('before_the_ages_of_Man', '
Before the Ages of Man, written by Aicantar of Shimerene, is the first volume in the Timeline Series and chronicles the mythical and historical events of the Dawn and Merethic Eras, the ages before recorded history. The Dawn Era, characterized by the formation of the cosmos and the actions of gods, ends with the creation of the mortal plane and the departure of divine powers after Lorkhan’s heart was cast to form the Red Mountain. The Merethic Era, or “Era of the Elves,” follows, marked by the arrival of the Aldmeri to Tamriel, the construction of landmarks like the Adamantine and White-Gold Towers, and the cultural rise of the Chimer and Dwemer. It also recounts the migration of humans from Atmora and their clashes with Elves, such as the Night of Tears and Ysgramor’s return with his Five Hundred Companions.

Themes include the interplay between divine intervention and mortal agency, the rise and decline of civilizations, and the cultural conflicts that shaped Tamriel’s history. Through its detailed recounting of mythical events, migrations, and the foundations of historical institutions, the book highlights how myth and history intertwine in Tamrielic tradition.', '''action'':54B ''adamantin'':106B ''age'':3A,8B,38B ''agenc'':158B ''aicantar'':13B ''aldmeri'':97B ''also'':122B ''arriv'':94B ''atmora'':129B ''book'':188B ''cast'':75B ''character'':45B ''chimer'':118B ''chronicl'':25B ''civil'':164B ''clash'':132B ''companion'':148B ''conflict'':168B ''construct'':101B ''cosmos'':51B ''creation'':60B ''cultur'':114B,167B ''dawn'':33B,43B ''declin'':162B ''departur'':67B ''detail'':175B ''divin'':69B,154B ''dwemer'':120B ''elv'':88B,134B ''end'':57B ''era'':36B,44B,83B ''event'':30B,179B ''first'':18B ''five'':146B ''follow'':90B ''form'':77B ''format'':48B ''foundat'':183B ''god'':56B ''gold'':110B ''heart'':73B ''highlight'':189B ''histor'':29B,185B ''histori'':41B,172B,193B ''human'':127B ''hundr'':147B ''includ'':150B ''institut'':186B ''interplay'':152B ''intertwin'':194B ''intervent'':155B ''landmark'':103B ''like'':104B ''lorkhan’'':72B ''man'':5A,10B ''mark'':91B ''mereth'':35B,82B ''migrat'':125B,180B ''mortal'':63B,157B ''mountain'':80B ''myth'':191B ''mythic'':27B,178B ''night'':138B ''plane'':64B ''power'':70B ''record'':40B ''recount'':123B,176B ''red'':79B ''return'':143B ''rise'':115B,160B ''seri'':23B ''shape'':170B ''shimeren'':15B ''tamriel'':99B,196B ''tamriel’'':171B ''tear'':140B ''theme'':149B ''timelin'':22B ''tower'':111B ''tradit'':197B ''volum'':19B ''white'':109B ''white-gold'':108B ''written'':11B ''ysgramor’'':142B ''“era'':85B ''”'':89B', 'scholar', '
Before the Ages of Man, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, explores the mythical and historical events of the Dawn and Merethic Eras, focusing on the creation of the cosmos, the rise of the Aldmeri, and the cultural conflicts that shaped Tamriel. Thematically, the book examines divine intervention, the rise and fall of civilizations, and the blending of myth and history in Tamrielic tradition.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('house_of_clan_battle-born', 'The House of Clan Battle-Born is the residence of the influential Battle-Born family, situated in the Wind District of Whiterun. Nestled beside the Hall of the Dead, the home is a prominent landmark in the city, standing directly across from the house of their rivals, Clan Gray-Mane.

The Battle-Borns are staunch supporters of the Empire and the Imperial Legion, embodying loyalty to tradition and order. Their home reflects their status and role in Whiterun’s political and social landscape. As one of the city’s leading families, the House of Clan Battle-Born serves as both a symbol of their allegiance to the Empire and a focal point in the ongoing feud with the fiercely independent Gray-Manes.', '''across'':49B ''allegi'':114B ''battl'':5A,12B,21B,62B,105B ''battle-born'':4A,11B,20B,61B,104B ''besid'':32B ''born'':6A,13B,22B,63B,106B ''citi'':46B ''city’'':97B ''clan'':3A,10B,56B,103B ''dead'':37B ''direct'':48B ''district'':28B ''embodi'':74B ''empir'':69B,117B ''famili'':23B,99B ''feud'':125B ''fierc'':128B ''focal'':120B ''gray'':58B,131B ''gray-man'':57B,130B ''hall'':34B ''home'':39B,81B ''hous'':1A,8B,52B,101B ''imperi'':72B ''independ'':129B ''influenti'':19B ''landmark'':43B ''landscap'':92B ''lead'':98B ''legion'':73B ''loyalti'':75B ''mane'':59B,132B ''nestl'':31B ''one'':94B ''ongo'':124B ''order'':79B ''point'':121B ''polit'':89B ''promin'':42B ''reflect'':82B ''resid'':16B ''rival'':55B ''role'':86B ''serv'':107B ''situat'':24B ''social'':91B ''stand'':47B ''status'':84B ''staunch'':65B ''support'':66B ''symbol'':111B ''tradit'':77B ''whiterun'':30B ''whiterun’'':88B ''wind'':27B', 'whiterun, noble', 'The House of Clan Battle-Born is the residence of the influential Battle-Born family, situated in the Wind District of Whiterun. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('jorrvaskr', 'Jorrvaskr is the legendary mead hall and headquarters of the Companions, situated atop the steps leading from Whiterun''s central plaza. It is the oldest structure in Whiterun, predating the city itself, and was established around the revered Skyforge. Over centuries, Whiterun grew around this sacred site, cementing Jorrvaskr''s role as a cornerstone of Nordic heritage.

The building, crafted from the overturned hull of a longship, reflects its deep ties to Atmoran tradition. Jorrvaskr was originally the ship of Ysgramor’s fleet, carried across the land by its crew and repurposed as a shelter when Jeek of the River founded the Great City. This connection to Ysgramor and the Five Hundred Companions imbues the hall with immense historical and cultural significance.', '''across'':85B ''around'':37B,45B ''atmoran'':74B ''atop'':14B ''build'':60B ''carri'':84B ''cement'':49B ''central'':21B ''centuri'':42B ''citi'':32B,104B ''companion'':12B,113B ''connect'':106B ''cornerston'':55B ''craft'':61B ''crew'':90B ''cultur'':121B ''deep'':71B ''establish'':36B ''five'':111B ''fleet'':83B ''found'':101B ''great'':103B ''grew'':44B ''hall'':7B,116B ''headquart'':9B ''heritag'':58B ''histor'':119B ''hull'':65B ''hundr'':112B ''imbu'':114B ''immens'':118B ''jeek'':97B ''jorrvaskr'':1A,2B,50B,76B ''land'':87B ''lead'':17B ''legendari'':5B ''longship'':68B ''mead'':6B ''nordic'':57B ''oldest'':26B ''origin'':78B ''overturn'':64B ''plaza'':22B ''predat'':30B ''reflect'':69B ''repurpos'':92B ''rever'':39B ''river'':100B ''role'':52B ''sacr'':47B ''shelter'':95B ''ship'':80B ''signific'':122B ''site'':48B ''situat'':13B ''skyforg'':40B ''step'':16B ''structur'':27B ''tie'':72B ''tradit'':75B ''whiterun'':19B,29B,43B ''ysgramor'':108B ''ysgramor’'':82B', 'whiterun, companions', 'Jorrvaskr is the legendary mead hall and headquarters of the Companions, situated atop the steps leading from Whiterun''s central plaza. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
