INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('forsworn_armor', 'Forsworn Armor has basic protection quality. Its visual design is rough and tribal, made of fur, leather, and bone, with a primitive and rugged appearance. It can not be crafted.', '''appear'':27B ''armor'':2A,4B ''basic'':6B ''bone'':21B ''craft'':32B ''design'':11B ''forsworn'':1A,3B ''fur'':18B ''leather'':19B ''made'':16B ''primit'':24B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''rough'':13B ''rug'':26B ''tribal'':15B ''visual'':10B', 'blacksmith', 'Forsworn Armor has basic protection quality. Its visual design is rough and tribal, made of fur, leather, and bone, with a primitive and rugged appearance. It can not be crafted.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bleakfalls_tower', 'Bleak Falls Tower is a tall, imposing structure located atop the hill above Riverwood. The tower might be described as a crumbling, ancient ruin, possibly linked to the same mysterious history that surrounds Bleak Falls Barrow. Some  speculate that the tower was once part of a larger complex, possibly related to old Nordic rituals or military defenses, though few would know its exact purpose.
Some might believe the tower is haunted or tied to dark forces that are linked to the barrow''s ancient curse. Some believe that this is a story circulated by bandits who have made it their hideout, in order to keep people away.', '''ancient'':25B,86B ''atop'':12B ''away'':109B ''bandit'':97B ''barrow'':38B,84B ''believ'':69B,89B ''bleak'':3B,36B ''bleakfal'':1A ''circul'':95B ''complex'':50B ''crumbl'':24B ''curs'':87B ''dark'':77B ''defens'':59B ''describ'':21B ''exact'':65B ''fall'':4B,37B ''forc'':78B ''haunt'':73B ''hideout'':103B ''hill'':14B ''histori'':33B ''impos'':9B ''keep'':107B ''know'':63B ''larger'':49B ''link'':28B,81B ''locat'':11B ''made'':100B ''might'':19B,68B ''militari'':58B ''mysteri'':32B ''nordic'':55B ''old'':54B ''order'':105B ''part'':46B ''peopl'':108B ''possibl'':27B,51B ''purpos'':66B ''relat'':52B ''ritual'':56B ''riverwood'':16B ''ruin'':26B ''specul'':40B ''stori'':94B ''structur'':10B ''surround'':35B ''tall'':8B ''though'':60B ''tie'':75B ''tower'':2A,5B,18B,43B,71B ''would'':62B', 'whiterun', 'Bleak Falls Tower is a tall, imposing structure located atop the hill above Riverwood. The tower might be described as a crumbling, ancient ruin, possibly linked to the same mysterious history that surrounds Bleak Falls Barrow.  You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', '');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frostfruit_inn', 'Frostfruit Inn is a modest, welcoming establishment in Rorikstead, a quiet farming village located in the western part of Whiterun Hold. The inn is located at the edge of the village, near the main road that connects to Whiterun and Hjaalmarch. This makes it a common stop for merchants, adventurers, and anyone passing through the area. It''s a small but vital part of Rorikstead''s hospitality, offering food, drink, and a warm bed. It is run by Mralki and his sone Erik.', '''adventur'':52B ''anyon'':54B ''area'':58B ''bed'':76B ''common'':48B ''connect'':39B ''drink'':72B ''edg'':30B ''erik'':85B ''establish'':9B ''farm'':14B ''food'':71B ''frostfruit'':1A,3B ''hjaalmarch'':43B ''hold'':23B ''hospit'':69B ''inn'':2A,4B,25B ''locat'':16B,27B ''main'':36B ''make'':45B ''merchant'':51B ''modest'':7B ''mralki'':81B ''near'':34B ''offer'':70B ''part'':20B,65B ''pass'':55B ''quiet'':13B ''road'':37B ''rorikstead'':11B,67B ''run'':79B ''small'':62B ''sone'':84B ''stop'':49B ''villag'':15B,33B ''vital'':64B ''warm'':75B ''welcom'':8B ''western'':19B ''whiterun'':22B,41B', 'whiterun, hjaalmarch', 'Frostfruit Inn is a modest, welcoming establishment in Rorikstead You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', '');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('black-briar_meadery', 'Black-Briar Meadery is a bar and brewery located in the western part of Riften in the Rift. Owned by the influential Maven Black-Briar, the meadery serves as a cornerstone of her business empire. While Maven oversees the operation, day-to-day tasks are handled by her employees. 

Ungrien acts as the barkeeper and greets most visitors, while Indaryn, the brewmaster, oversees the production of the renowned Black-Briar Mead. Other employees, including Romlyn Dreth, Niluva Hlaalu, and Asgeir Snow-Shod, perform various duties around the establishment.', '''act'':58B ''around'':95B ''asgeir'':88B ''bar'':11B ''barkeep'':61B ''black'':2A,6B,30B,77B ''black-briar'':1A,5B,29B,76B ''breweri'':13B ''brewmast'':69B ''briar'':3A,7B,31B,78B ''busi'':40B ''cornerston'':37B ''day'':48B,50B ''day-to-day'':47B ''dreth'':84B ''duti'':94B ''empir'':41B ''employe'':56B,81B ''establish'':97B ''greet'':63B ''handl'':53B ''hlaalu'':86B ''includ'':82B ''indaryn'':67B ''influenti'':27B ''locat'':14B ''maven'':28B,43B ''mead'':79B ''meaderi'':4A,8B,33B ''niluva'':85B ''oper'':46B ''overse'':44B,70B ''own'':24B ''part'':18B ''perform'':92B ''product'':72B ''renown'':75B ''rift'':23B ''riften'':20B ''romlyn'':83B ''serv'':34B ''shod'':91B ''snow'':90B ''snow-shod'':89B ''task'':51B ''ungrien'':57B ''various'':93B ''visitor'':65B ''western'':17B', 'rift, noble', 'Black-Briar Meadery is a bar and brewery located in the western part of Riften in the Rift. Owned by the influential Maven Black-Briar, the meadery serves as a cornerstone of her business empire.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('darklight_tower', 'Darklight Tower is a medium-sized, dilapidated fort located southwest of Riften and east-southeast of Largashbur in the Rift. The path to the tower, south of the road between Riften and Ivarstead. There are rumours that witches have taken over the tower.', '''darklight'':1A,3B ''dilapid'':10B ''east'':18B ''east-southeast'':17B ''fort'':11B ''ivarstead'':37B ''largashbur'':21B ''locat'':12B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''path'':26B ''rift'':24B ''riften'':15B,35B ''road'':33B ''rumour'':40B ''size'':9B ''south'':30B ''southeast'':19B ''southwest'':13B ''taken'':44B ''tower'':2A,4B,29B,47B ''witch'':42B', 'rift', 'Darklight Tower is a medium-sized, dilapidated fort located southwest of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('history_of_raven_rock', 'History of Raven Rock, written by Lyrin Telleno, provides a detailed account of the development and history of the mining town of Raven Rock on Solstheim, focusing on its transformation from an East Empire Company colony to a thriving Dunmer settlement. The book is divided into three volumes, each covering significant events and challenges faced by the town over the centuries. The first volume covers the town''s founding in 3E 427, the initial imperial settlement, and the eruption of Red Mountain in 4E 5, which caused widespread destruction but ultimately solidified Raven Rock''s resilience. The second volume details the construction of protective structures like the Bulwark, the transition of control to House Redoran, and the prosperity that followed under the leadership of Brara Morvayn. The third volume chronicles the challenges Raven Rock faced during the Fourth Era, including internal strife from House Hlaalu, the depletion of the ebony mine, and the ongoing efforts to maintain order and security under Lleril Morvayn’s rule.

The themes of the book include perseverance, leadership, and the struggle for autonomy in the face of external pressures. Telleno highlights the dynamic relationship between the Dunmer and the imperial settlers, as well as the influence of political rivalries, such as between Houses Redoran and Hlaalu, on the town’s fate. The work is a testament to the spirit of the people of Raven Rock, their resilience through disasters, and their ability to adapt as their main resource dwindles.', '''3e'':75B ''427'':76B ''4e'':88B ''5'':89B ''abil'':239B ''account'':16B ''adapt'':241B ''autonomi'':181B ''book'':47B,173B ''brara'':129B ''bulwark'':112B ''caus'':91B ''centuri'':65B ''challeng'':58B,136B ''chronicl'':134B ''coloni'':40B ''compani'':39B ''construct'':106B ''control'':116B ''cover'':54B,69B ''deplet'':151B ''destruct'':93B ''detail'':15B,104B ''develop'':19B ''disast'':236B ''divid'':49B ''dunmer'':44B,195B ''dwindl'':246B ''dynam'':191B ''east'':37B ''eboni'':154B ''effort'':159B ''empir'':38B ''era'':143B ''erupt'':83B ''event'':56B ''extern'':186B ''face'':59B,139B,184B ''fate'':218B ''first'':67B ''focus'':31B ''follow'':124B ''found'':73B ''fourth'':142B ''highlight'':189B ''histori'':1A,5B,21B ''hlaalu'':149B,214B ''hous'':118B,148B,211B ''imperi'':79B,198B ''includ'':144B,174B ''influenc'':204B ''initi'':78B ''intern'':145B ''leadership'':127B,176B ''like'':110B ''lleril'':166B ''lyrin'':11B ''main'':244B ''maintain'':161B ''mine'':24B,155B ''morvayn'':130B ''morvayn’'':167B ''mountain'':86B ''ongo'':158B ''order'':162B ''peopl'':229B ''persever'':175B ''polit'':206B ''pressur'':187B ''prosper'':122B ''protect'':108B ''provid'':13B ''raven'':3A,7B,27B,97B,137B,231B ''red'':85B ''redoran'':119B,212B ''relationship'':192B ''resili'':100B,234B ''resourc'':245B ''rivalri'':207B ''rock'':4A,8B,28B,98B,138B,232B ''rule'':168B ''second'':102B ''secur'':164B ''settlement'':45B,80B ''settler'':199B ''signific'':55B ''solidifi'':96B ''solstheim'':30B ''spirit'':226B ''s