History of Raven Rock, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, chronicles the transformation of Raven Rock from an imperial colony to a thriving Dunmer settlement, highlighting themes of perseverance, leadership, and the struggle for autonomy. The book explores the challenges faced by the town, including external pressures, internal rivalries, and the resilience of its people.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('darkwater_pass', 'Darkwater Pass is a small cave located south-southwest of Darkwater Crossing and northeast of Nilheim, home to Falmer. The cave, situated near a large waterfall along the Darkwater River, has a foreboding entrance marked by a statue.

To find the cave, cross the bridge southwest of Darkwater Crossing, follow the road northwest toward Fort Amol, and look for a rock-marked path on your left before the next bridge. At the fork, take the left path (southeast) to reach the cave.', '''along'':30B ''amol'':59B ''bridg'':48B,74B ''cave'':8B,24B,45B,86B ''cross'':15B,46B,52B ''darkwat'':1A,3B,14B,32B,51B ''entranc'':37B ''falmer'':22B ''find'':43B ''follow'':53B ''forebod'':36B ''fork'':77B ''fort'':58B ''home'':20B ''larg'':28B ''left'':70B,80B ''locat'':9B ''look'':61B ''mark'':38B,66B ''near'':26B ''next'':73B ''nilheim'':19B ''northeast'':17B ''northwest'':56B ''pass'':2A,4B ''path'':67B,81B ''reach'':84B ''river'':33B ''road'':55B ''rock'':65B ''rock-mark'':64B ''situat'':25B ''small'':7B ''south'':11B ''south-southwest'':10B ''southeast'':82B ''southwest'':12B,49B ''statu'':41B ''take'':78B ''toward'':57B ''waterfal'':29B', 'rift', 'Darkwater Pass is a small cave located south-southwest of Darkwater Crossing.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mistveil_keep', 'Mistveil Keep is a grand castle located at the southern end of Riften, its stone walls standing in stark contrast to the city''s wooden buildings and walkways. Serving as an extra layer of protection during times of conflict, the keep is the seat of power for the Rift. Mistveil Keep is home to Jarl Laila Law-Giver and her sons, Harrald and Saerlund. The steward, Anuriel, and the eccentric court wizard, Wylandriah, also reside here, assisting in the governance of the hold.', '''also'':77B ''anuriel'':70B ''assist'':80B ''build'':28B ''castl'':8B ''citi'':25B ''conflict'':41B ''contrast'':22B ''court'':74B ''eccentr'':73B ''end'':13B ''extra'':34B ''giver'':61B ''govern'':83B ''grand'':7B ''harrald'':65B ''hold'':86B ''home'':55B ''jarl'':57B ''keep'':2A,4B,43B,53B ''laila'':58B ''law'':60B ''law-giv'':59B ''layer'':35B ''locat'':9B ''mistveil'':1A,3B,52B ''power'':48B ''protect'':37B ''resid'':78B ''rift'':51B ''riften'':15B ''saerlund'':67B ''seat'':46B ''serv'':31B ''son'':64B ''southern'':12B ''stand'':19B ''stark'':21B ''steward'':69B ''stone'':17B ''time'':39B ''walkway'':30B ''wall'':18B ''wizard'':75B ''wooden'':27B ''wylandriah'':76B', 'rift, noble', 'Mistveil Keep is a grand castle located at the southern end of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nightingale_hall', 'Nightingale Hall is the secret home of the Nightingales, located directly south of Riften near the Shadow Stone. The entrance is accessed via a steep, narrow path illuminated by ceiling fissures and adorned with Nightingale sigil banners. Inside, the hall opens into a grand cavern with a waterfall and a rushing stream, crossed by a wooden bridge leading to the living quarters.', '''access'':24B ''adorn'':35B ''banner'':39B ''bridg'':59B ''cavern'':47B ''ceil'':32B ''cross'':55B ''direct'':13B ''entranc'':22B ''fissur'':33B ''grand'':46B ''hall'':2A,4B,42B ''home'':8B ''illumin'':30B ''insid'':40B ''lead'':60B ''live'':63B ''locat'':12B ''narrow'':28B ''near'':17B ''nightingal'':1A,3B,11B,37B ''open'':43B ''path'':29B ''quarter'':64B ''riften'':16B ''rush'':53B ''secret'':7B ''shadow'':19B ''sigil'':38B ''south'':14B ''steep'':27B ''stone'':20B ''stream'':54B ''via'':25B ''waterfal'':50B ''wooden'':58B', 'karliah', 'Nightingale Hall is the secret home of the Nightingales, located somewhere in Riften but you do not know where. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath, rift', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nilheim', 'Nilheim is a small, ruined Nordic tower located east-northeast of Ivarstead and northwest of Sarethi Farm in the Rift. It is known that the local Guard have taken control of this area, however they can barely be seen patroling outside the location.', '''area'':35B ''bare'':39B ''control'':32B ''east'':11B ''east-northeast'':10B ''farm'':19B ''guard'':29B ''howev'':36B ''ivarstead'':14B ''known'':25B ''local'':28B ''locat'':9B,45B ''nilheim'':1A,2B ''nordic'':7B ''northeast'':12B ''northwest'':16B ''outsid'':43B ''patrol'':42B ''rift'':22B ''ruin'':6B ''sarethi'':18B ''seen'':41B ''small'':5B ''taken'':31B ''tower'':8B', 'rift', 'Nilheim is a small, ruined Nordic tower located east-northeast of Ivarstead.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('iron_claw', 'Combination: Dragon—Hawk—Wolf', '''claw'':2A ''combin'':3B ''dragon—hawk—wolf'':4B ''iron'':1A', 'puzzle', 'You have no idea what the claw is or how to solze its puzzle.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('northwind_mine', 'Northwind Mine is a small iron mine located northwest of Shor''s Stone and southeast of Mistwatch in the Rift. Inhabited by skeletons, the mine consists of a single zone and offers adventurers an opportunity to collect iron ore while facing minimal resistance.

To reach the mine, follow the path north from Shor''s Stone, passing Shor''s Watchtower on the right. A set of steps on the left leads up to the mine entrance.', '''adventur'':35B ''collect'':39B ''consist'':28B ''entranc'':77B ''face'':43B ''follow'':50B ''inhabit'':23B ''iron'':8B,40B ''lead'':72B ''left'':71B ''locat'':10B ''mine'':2A,4B,9B,27B,49B,76B ''minim'':44B ''mistwatch'':19B ''north'':53B ''northwest'':11B ''northwind'':1A,3B ''offer'':34B ''opportun'':37B ''ore'':41B ''pass'':58B ''path'':52B ''reach'':47B ''resist'':45B ''rift'':22B ''right'':64B ''set'':66B ''shor'':13B,55B,59B ''singl'':31B ''skeleton'':25B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':17B ''step'':68B ''stone'':15B,57B ''watchtow'':61B ''zone'':32B', 'rift', 'Northwind Mine is a small iron mine located northwest of Shor''s Stone.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rift', 'The Rift is a hold in southeast Skyrim, with its capital in Riften,  aligned with the Stormcloaks. Nestled on a vast plateau bordered by the Jerall and Velothi Mountains, the Rift connects Skyrim to Morrowind and Cyrodiil and is renowned for its vibrant autumnal forests, aspen trees, and rich alchemical resources like mountain flowers, scaly pholiota, and canis root.', '''alchem'':51B ''align'':15B ''aspen'':47B ''autumn'':45B ''border'':24B ''cani'':59B ''capit'':12B ''connect'':33B ''cyrodiil'':38B ''flower'':55B ''forest'':46B ''hold'':6B ''jeral'':27B ''like'':53B ''morrowind'':36B ''mountain'':30B,54B ''nestl'':19B ''pholiota'':57B ''plateau'':23B ''renown'':41B ''resourc'':52B ''rich'':50B ''rift'':1A,3B,32B ''riften'':14B ''root'':60B ''scali'':56B ''skyrim'':9B,34B ''southeast'':8B ''stormcloak'':18B ''tree'':48B ''vast'':22B ''velothi'':29B ''vibrant'':44B', 'rift, noble, scholar', 'The Rift is a hold in southeast Skyrim, with its capital in Riften,  aligned with the Stormcloaks. Nestled on a vast plateau bordered by the Jerall and Velothi Mountains, the Rift connects Skyrim to Morrowind and Cyrodiil and is renowned for its vibrant autumnal forests, aspen trees, and rich alchemical resources like mountain flowers, scaly pholiota, and canis root.', '', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('abacean_longfish', 'Abacean Longfish are a long grey ship that can be caught with your hands around Skyrim. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Weakness to Frost, Fortify Sneak, Weakness to Poison and Fortify Restoration.', '''abacean'':1A,3B ''around'':17B ''caught'':13B ''effect'':29B ''fortifi'':35B,41B ''frost'':34B ''grey'':8B ''hand'':16B ''ingredi'':23B ''long'':7B ''longfish'':2A,4B ''make'':26B ''offer'':28B ''poison'':39B ''potion'':25B ''restor'':42B ''ship'':9B ''skyrim'':18B ''sneak'':36B ''use'':20B ''weak'':32B,37B', 'fisher', 'Abacean Longfish are a long greyfish that can be caught with your hands around Skyrim. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rift_imperial_camp', 'The Rift Imperial Camp is an Imperial military outpost in the Rift, situated south of Ivarstead and west of the Ruins of Bthalft. Typically commanded by Legate Fasendi. It serves as a strategic base for the Imperial Legion''s operations in the region.', '''base'':37B ''bthalft'':26B ''camp'':3A,7B ''command'':28B ''fasendi'':31B ''imperi'':2A,6B,10B,40B ''ivarstead'':19B ''legat'':30B ''legion'':41B ''militari'':11B ''oper'':43B ''outpost'':12B ''region'':46B ''rift'':1A,5B,15B ''ruin'':24B ''serv'':33B ''situat'':16B ''south'':17B ''strateg'':36B ''typic'':27B ''west'':21B', 'rift, legion', 'The Rift Imperial Camp is an Imperial military outpost in the Rift, situated south of Ivarstead.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ruins_of_rkund', 'The Ruins of Rkund are a small, eerie Dwarven ruin nestled in the mountains southwest of Riften and southeast of Darklight Tower in the Rift. The ruins, accessible by passing through the Darklight Tower and continuing southeast, are sparsely scattered with broken pillars and collapsed structures. ', '''access'':31B ''broken'':45B ''collaps'':48B ''continu'':39B ''darklight'':24B,36B ''dwarven'':12B ''eeri'':11B ''mountain'':17B ''nestl'':14B ''pass'':33B ''pillar'':46B ''rift'':28B ''riften'':20B ''rkund'':3A,7B ''ruin'':1A,5B,13B,30B ''scatter'':43B ''small'':10B ''southeast'':22B,40B ''southwest'':18B ''spars'':42B ''structur'':49B ''tower'':25B,37B', 'rift', 'The Ruins of Rkund are a small, eerie Dwarven ruin nestled in the mountains southwest of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('restore_health_to_undead', 'These magical effects are restorative Restoration spells that uniquely restore vitality to undead creatures, sustaining their unnatural existence. This effect is only available as a spell, reflecting the darker uses of Restoration magic.', '''avail'':27B ''creatur'':18B ''darker'':33B ''effect'':7B,24B ''exist'':22B ''health'':2A ''magic'':6B,37B ''reflect'':31B ''restor'':1A,9B,10B,14B,36B ''spell'':11B,30B ''sustain'':19B ''undead'':4A,17B ''uniqu'':13B ''unnatur'':21B ''use'':34B ''vital'':15B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic restores health to undead creatures, keeping them alive and able to fight. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('palace_of_the_kings', 'The Palace of the Kings is a grand castle located at the far end of the Valunstrad district in Windhelm, serving as the residence of Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak and the headquarters of the Stormcloak movement. The palace is a symbol of the city''s ancient history, as Windhelm was one of the first human settlements in Tamriel and the capital of Ysgramor''s first empire. It remains one of the last surviving structures from that era.', '''ancient'':49B ''capit'':64B ''castl'':13B ''citi'':47B ''district'':22B ''empir'':69B ''end'':18B ''era'':80B ''far'':17B ''first'':57B,68B ''grand'':12B ''headquart'':35B ''histori'':50B ''human'':58B ''jarl'':30B ''king'':4A,9B ''last'':75B ''locat'':14B ''movement'':39B ''one'':54B,72B ''palac'':1A,6B,41B ''remain'':71B ''resid'':28B ''serv'':25B ''settlement'':59B ''stormcloak'':32B,38B ''structur'':77B ''surviv'':76B ''symbol'':44B ''tamriel'':61B ''ulfric'':31B ''valunstrad'':21B ''windhelm'':24B,52B ''ysgramor'':66B', 'eastmarch, noble', 'The Palace of the Kings is a grand castle located at the far end of the Valunstrad district in Windhelm. It serves as the residence of Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak and the headquarters of the Stormcloak movement. As a symbol of Windhelm''s ancient history, the palace stands as one of the last surviving structures from Ysgramor''s first empire, making it a significant reminder of the city''s early role in Tamriel''s history.', '', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('deathbell', 'Deathbell is a large purple flower found in swampy regions like Hjaalmarch, known for its potent poison effects and darker folklore surrounding its growth. Alchemy effects: Damage Health, Ravage Stamina, Slow, and Weakness to Poison.', '''alchemi'':26B ''damag'':28B ''darker'':21B ''deathbel'':1A,2B ''effect'':19B,27B ''flower'':7B ''folklor'':22B ''found'':8B ''growth'':25B ''health'':29B ''hjaalmarch'':13B ''known'':14B ''larg'':5B ''like'':12B ''poison'':18B,36B ''potent'':17B ''purpl'':6B ''ravag'':30B ''region'':11B ''slow'':32B ''stamina'':31B ''surround'':23B ''swampi'':10B ''weak'':34B', 'alchemist', 'Deathbell is a large purple flower found in swampy regions like Hjaalmarch, known for its potent poison effects and darker folklore surrounding its growth.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('kynesgrove', 'Kynesgrove is a small settlement located south of Windhelm and west of Narzulbur in Eastmarch. Originally intended as a lumber mill by Ganna and Gemma Uriel, the settlement shifted to mining malachite after the grove''s trees were found to be sacred to Kyne. The Uriels now work in Steamscorch Mine, often arguing about their lost life in Cyrodiil. Kjeld manages the settlement and buys malachite ore, while Dravynea the Stoneweaver ensures the mine''s safety using potions crafted from frost salts. The Braidwood Inn, run by Iddra, serves as the central gathering spot for residents and travelers.

The settlement consists of the Braidwood Inn, Steamscorch Mine, and a miner''s camp. There is also a dragon mound to the east of it.', '''also'':116B ''argu'':54B ''braidwood'':85B,105B ''buy'':66B ''camp'':113B ''central'':93B ''consist'':102B ''craft'':80B ''cyrodiil'':60B ''dragon'':118B ''dravynea'':70B ''east'':122B ''eastmarch'':16B ''ensur'':73B ''found'':40B ''frost'':82B ''ganna'':24B ''gather'':94B ''gemma'':26B ''grove'':36B ''iddra'':89B ''inn'':86B,106B ''intend'':18B ''kjeld'':61B ''kyne'':45B ''kynesgrov'':1A,2B ''life'':58B ''locat'':7B ''lost'':57B ''lumber'':21B ''malachit'':33B,67B ''manag'':62B ''mill'':22B ''mine'':32B,52B,75B,108B ''miner'':111B ''mound'':119B ''narzulbur'':14B ''often'':53B ''ore'':68B ''origin'':17B ''potion'':79B ''resid'':97B ''run'':87B ''sacr'':43B ''safeti'':77B ''salt'':83B ''serv'':90B ''settlement'':6B,29B,64B,101B ''shift'':30B ''small'':5B ''south'':8B ''spot'':95B ''steamscorch'':51B,107B ''stoneweav'':72B ''travel'':99B ''tree'':38B ''uriel'':27B,47B ''use'':78B ''west'':12B ''windhelm'':10B ''work'':49B', 'eastmarch', 'Kynesgrove is a small settlement located south of Windhelm and west of Narzulbur in Eastmarch. Originally intended as a lumber mill by Ganna and Gemma Uriel, the settlement shifted to mining malachite after the grove''s trees were found to be sacred to Kyne. You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pale_stormcloak_camp', 'Pale Stormcloak Camp is a Stormcloak military encampment located in The Pale, southeast of Bronze Water Cave on the southern shore of Lake Yorgrim. The camp serves as a strategic base for Stormcloak forces in the region, supporting their efforts in the ongoing civil war.', '''base'':34B ''bronz'':18B ''camp'':3A,6B,29B ''cave'':20B ''civil'':47B ''effort'':43B ''encamp'':11B ''forc'':37B ''lake'':26B ''locat'':12B ''militari'':10B ''ongo'':46B ''pale'':1A,4B,15B ''region'':40B ''serv'':30B ''shore'':24B ''southeast'':16B ''southern'':23B ''stormcloak'':2A,5B,9B,36B ''strateg'':33B ''support'':41B ''war'':48B ''water'':19B ''yorgrim'':27B', 'pale, stormcloak', 'Pale Stormcloak Camp is a Stormcloak military encampment located in The Pale on the southern shore of Lake Yorgrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hlaalu_farm', 'Hlaalu Farm is a small agricultural property located east of Windhelm, northeast of Windhelm Stables, and west of Hollyfrost Farm in Eastmarch. Owned by Belyn Hlaalu, a Dunmer who resides in Windhelm, the farm is managed and worked by Adisla, a Nord woman who lives in the single-room farmhouse on the property.', '''adisla'':42B ''agricultur'':8B ''belyn'':27B ''dunmer'':30B ''east'':11B ''eastmarch'':24B ''farm'':2A,4B,22B,36B ''farmhous'':53B ''hlaalu'':1A,3B,28B ''hollyfrost'':21B ''live'':47B ''locat'':10B ''manag'':38B ''nord'':44B ''northeast'':14B ''own'':25B ''properti'':9B,56B ''resid'':32B ''room'':52B ''singl'':51B ''single-room'':50B ''small'':7B ''stabl'':17B ''west'':19B ''windhelm'':13B,16B,34B ''woman'':45B ''work'':40B', 'eastmarch', 'Hlaalu Farm is a small agricultural property located east of Windhelm. You do not know who runs the farm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hollyfrost_farm', 'Hollyfrost Farm is a large agricultural property located east of Windhelm, east of Hlaalu Farm, and northeast of Windhelm Stables in Eastmarch. The farm is owned by Torsten Cruel-Sea but is primarily worked by Tulvur, who resides on the property along with his two loyal dogs, Tiber and Ysgramor.', '''agricultur'':8B ''along'':45B ''cruel'':32B ''cruel-sea'':31B ''dog'':50B ''east'':11B,14B ''eastmarch'':24B ''farm'':2A,4B,17B,26B ''hlaalu'':16B ''hollyfrost'':1A,3B ''larg'':7B ''locat'':10B ''loyal'':49B ''northeast'':19B ''own'':28B ''primarili'':36B ''properti'':9B,44B ''resid'':41B ''sea'':33B ''stabl'':22B ''tiber'':51B ''torsten'':30B ''tulvur'':39B ''two'':48B ''windhelm'':13B,21B ''work'':37B ''ysgramor'':53B', 'eastmarch', 'Hollyfrost Farm is a large agricultural property located east of Windhelm. You do not know who runs the farm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragon_wars', 'The Dragon War was a pivotal conflict in the Merethic Era, marking a violent upheaval between dragons and the human population of Skyrim. When Ysgramor and his people arrived in Tamriel, they brought with them a faith that worshipped animals, including the dragon, which held a central role as a god-king figure. Grand temples were constructed to honor the dragons, and dragon priests were granted power in exchange for ruling humanity on their behalf. However, this balance of power shifted as the dragon priests grew tyrannical, enslaving the population and demanding absolute obedience. When rebellion broke out, the dragons retaliated with devastating force, sparking the Dragon War.

Initially, humanity suffered immense losses, but the tide shifted when certain dragons sided with men. It is said that from these traitorous dragons, men learned powerful magics, possibly with the intervention of Akatosh, allowing them to combat their former overlords. Over time, the dragon priests were overthrown, and dragons were hunted to near extinction. The remnants of the dragon cult preserved their belief in the dragons'' eventual return, entombing fallen dragons in dragon mounds and maintaining their faith. The war not only shaped Skyrim''s ancient history but left a legacy evident in its ruins, myths, and the fearsome reputation of dragons.', '''absolut'':96B ''akatosh'':144B ''allow'':145B ''ancient'':197B ''anim'':42B ''arriv'':31B ''balanc'':81B ''behalf'':78B ''belief'':174B ''broke'':100B ''brought'':35B ''central'':49B ''certain'':122B ''combat'':148B ''conflict'':9B ''construct'':60B ''cult'':171B ''demand'':95B ''devast'':106B ''dragon'':1A,4B,19B,45B,64B,66B,87B,103B,110B,123B,134B,155B,160B,170B,177B,182B,184B,213B ''enslav'':91B ''entomb'':180B ''era'':13B ''eventu'':178B ''evid'':203B ''exchang'':72B ''extinct'':165B ''faith'':39B,189B ''fallen'':181B ''fearsom'':210B ''figur'':56B ''forc'':107B ''former'':150B ''god'':54B ''god-k'':53B ''grand'':57B ''grant'':69B ''grew'':89B ''held'':47B ''histori'':198B ''honor'':62B ''howev'':79B ''human'':22B,75B,113B ''hunt'':162B ''immens'':115B ''includ'':43B ''initi'':112B ''intervent'':142B ''king'':55B ''learn'':136B ''left'':200B ''legaci'':202B ''loss'':116B ''magic'':138B ''maintain'':187B ''mark'':14B ''men'':126B,135B ''mereth'':12B ''mound'':185B ''myth'':207B ''near'':164B ''obedi'':97B ''overlord'':151B ''overthrown'':158B ''peopl'':30B ''pivot'':8B ''popul'':23B,93B ''possibl'':139B ''power'':70B,83B,137B ''preserv'':172B ''priest'':67B,88B,156B ''rebellion'':99B ''remnant'':167B ''reput'':211B ''retali'':104B ''return'':179B ''role'':50B ''ruin'':206B ''rule'':74B ''said'':129B ''shape'':194B ''shift'':84B,120B ''side'':124B ''skyrim'':25B,195B ''spark'':108B ''suffer'':114B ''tamriel'':33B ''templ'':58B ''tide'':119B ''time'':153B ''traitor'':133B ''tyrann'':90B ''upheav'':17B ''violent'':16B ''war'':2A,5B,111B,191B ''worship'':41B ''ysgramor'':27B', 'scholar, dragon, miraakcult', '
The Dragon War was a significant conflict in the Merethic Era, sparked by a violent uprising between dragons and humans in Skyrim. The Nords, led by Ysgramor, brought a faith that revered dragons as god-kings, with dragon priests ruling humanity. Over time, the priests became tyrannical, enslaving the population, which led to a rebellion. The dragons retaliated, but the tide turned when some dragons allied with humans, teaching them powerful magics, possibly with Akatosh''s influence. The dragon priests were overthrown, and dragons were nearly hunted to extinction. The remnants of the dragon cult preserved their faith in the dragons'' return, entombing dragons in mounds. The war''s legacy is seen in Skyrim''s ruins, myths, and the fearsome reputation of dragons.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('saviors_hide', 'Savior''s Hide, also known as Hircine''s Hide or the Scourge of the Oathbreaker, is a Daedric artifact associated primarily with the Daedric Prince Hircine. It was originally part of a full set of armor, but over time, the term has come to refer only to the cuirass, as the rest of the set has not been seen since the Third Era. The cuirass is known for granting the wearer resistance to magic, making it a prized item for those facing powerful sorcerers or hostile enchantments.

There are multiple origins for the Hide. One popular version claims Hircine himself gifted the Hide to the first mortal to escape his Hunting Grounds, who then fashioned it into armor. Another tale suggests that Hircine sewed the armor from the hide of a werewolf. A lesser-known tradition credits Malacath, though this version mistakenly claims the Hide made its wearer vulnerable to magic. Despite these differences, all stories agree that the Hide offers protection against the blows of oathbreakers and the Spear of Bitter Mercy.', '''agre'':160B ''also'':6B ''anoth'':121B ''armor'':38B,120B,128B ''artifact'':21B ''associ'':22B ''bitter'':175B ''blow'':168B ''claim'':100B,146B ''come'':45B ''credit'':140B ''cuirass'':51B,67B ''daedric'':20B,26B ''despit'':155B ''differ'':157B ''enchant'':89B ''era'':65B ''escap'':111B ''face'':84B ''fashion'':117B ''first'':108B ''full'':35B ''gift'':103B ''grant'':71B ''ground'':114B ''hide'':2A,5B,11B,96B,105B,131B,148B,163B ''hircin'':9B,28B,101B,125B ''hostil'':88B ''hunt'':113B ''item'':81B ''known'':7B,69B,138B ''lesser'':137B ''lesser-known'':136B ''made'':149B ''magic'':76B,154B ''make'':77B ''malacath'':141B ''merci'':176B ''mistaken'':145B ''mortal'':109B ''multipl'':92B ''oathbreak'':17B,170B ''offer'':164B ''one'':97B ''origin'':31B,93B ''part'':32B ''popular'':98B ''power'':85B ''primarili'':23B ''princ'':27B ''prize'':80B ''protect'':165B ''refer'':47B ''resist'':74B ''rest'':54B ''savior'':1A,3B ''scourg'':14B ''seen'':61B ''set'':36B,57B ''sew'':126B ''sinc'':62B ''sorcer'':86B ''spear'':173B ''stori'':159B ''suggest'':123B ''tale'':122B ''term'':43B ''third'':64B ''though'':142B ''time'':41B ''tradit'':139B ''version'':99B,144B ''vulner'':152B ''wearer'':73B,151B ''werewolf'':134B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar, werewolf, hunter', 'Savior''s Hide, is a Daedric artifact linked to Hircine. It is a cuirass that is thought to protect against powerful sorcerers and enchantments. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stonehills', 'Stonehills is a small mining settlement located east of Morthal and west of Dimhollow Crypt in Hjaalmarch. It serves as the encampment for workers at Rockwallow Mine, which is owned by Thane Bryling of Solitude. The mine is managed by Sorli the Builder and her husband, Pactur, who live in a house near the mine with their son, Sirgar.', '''bryle'':34B ''builder'':44B ''crypt'':16B ''dimhollow'':15B ''east'':9B ''encamp'':23B ''hjaalmarch'':18B ''hous'':53B ''husband'':47B ''live'':50B ''locat'':8B ''manag'':40B ''mine'':6B,28B,38B,56B ''morthal'':11B ''near'':54B ''own'':31B ''pactur'':48B ''rockwallow'':27B ''serv'':20B ''settlement'':7B ''sirgar'':60B ''small'':5B ''solitud'':36B ''son'':59B ''sor'':42B ''stonehil'':1A,2B ''thane'':33B ''west'':13B ''worker'':25B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Stonehills is a small mining settlement located east of Morthal.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_atronach_stone', 'The Atronach Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones found across Skyrim, located south of Bonestrewn Crest and east-northeast of Darkwater Crossing in the southernmost part of Eastmarch''s hot springs. The stone is positioned atop a mound surrounded by roiling volcanic pools, with other angular stones jutting around it, creating a striking and mystical setting.

Activating the Atronach Stone grants a passive power that increases magicka by a decent amount and provides good spell absorption, but at the cost of a 50% reduction in magicka regeneration.', '''50'':89B ''absorpt'':82B ''across'':15B ''activ'':63B ''amount'':77B ''angular'':52B ''around'':55B ''atop'':42B ''atronach'':2A,5B,65B ''bonestrewn'':20B ''cost'':86B ''creat'':57B ''crest'':21B ''cross'':28B ''darkwat'':27B ''decent'':76B ''east'':24B ''east-northeast'':23B ''eastmarch'':34B ''found'':14B ''good'':80B ''grant'':67B ''hot'':36B ''increas'':72B ''jut'':54B ''locat'':17B ''magicka'':73B,92B ''mound'':44B ''mystic'':61B ''northeast'':25B ''one'':8B ''part'':32B ''passiv'':69B ''pool'':49B ''posit'':41B ''power'':70B ''provid'':79B ''reduct'':90B ''regener'':93B ''roil'':47B ''set'':62B ''skyrim'':16B ''south'':18B ''southernmost'':31B ''spell'':81B ''spring'':37B ''stand'':12B ''stone'':3A,6B,13B,39B,53B,66B ''strike'':59B ''surround'':45B ''thirteen'':11B ''volcan'':48B', 'eastmarch, scholar, traveler', 'The Atronach Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones found across Skyrim, located east-northeast of Darkwater Crossing in the southernmost part of Eastmarch''s hot springs. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fireball', 'Fireball is a Destruction spell that hurls an explosive ball of fire at a target, dealing damage in an area of effect upon impact. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':29B ''area'':21B ''ball'':11B ''cast'':33B ''damag'':18B ''deal'':17B ''destruct'':5B ''effect'':23B ''explos'':10B ''fire'':13B ''firebal'':1A,2B ''hurl'':8B ''impact'':25B ''level'':31B ''requir'':27B ''skill'':30B ''spell'':6B ''target'':16B ''upon'':24B', 'mage', 'Fireball is a spell that hurls a fiery ball at a target, causing an explosion that deals damage in an area around it. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('blood_horkers', 'The Blood Horkers are a notorious group of pirates operating in the Sea of Ghosts under the command of a battlemage named Haldyn. Known for their ruthless raids along the northern coastline of Tamriel, they have exploited the chaos of the Civil War in Skyrim to intensify their attacks without fear of reprisal from the major factions. The group has a secret stronghold, Japhet''s Folly, where Haldyn employs powerful magic to shroud the island in fog, ensuring its location remains hidden.', '''along'':31B ''attack'':51B ''battlemag'':23B ''blood'':1A,4B ''chao'':41B ''civil'':44B ''coastlin'':34B ''command'':20B ''employ'':71B ''ensur'':80B ''exploit'':39B ''faction'':59B ''fear'':53B ''fog'':79B ''folli'':68B ''ghost'':17B ''group'':9B,61B ''haldyn'':25B,70B ''hidden'':84B ''horker'':2A,5B ''intensifi'':49B ''island'':77B ''japhet'':66B ''known'':26B ''locat'':82B ''magic'':73B ''major'':58B ''name'':24B ''northern'':33B ''notori'':8B ''oper'':12B ''pirat'':11B ''power'':72B ''raid'':30B ''remain'':83B ''repris'':55B ''ruthless'':29B ''sea'':15B ''secret'':64B ''shroud'':75B ''skyrim'':47B ''stronghold'':65B ''tamriel'':36B ''war'':45B ''without'':52B', 'eastmarch, sailor, thief', 'The Blood Horkers are a ruthless pirate group led by the battlemage Haldyn, operating in the Sea of Ghosts. Exploiting Skyrim''s Civil War, they conduct raids along Tamriel''s northern coast. ', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('healing_hands', 'Healing Hands is a Restoration spell that allows the caster to heal a target by touching them, restoring health over a short period. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''allow'':10B ''apprentic'':29B ''cast'':33B ''caster'':12B ''hand'':2A,4B ''heal'':1A,3B,14B ''health'':21B ''level'':31B ''period'':25B ''requir'':27B ''restor'':7B,20B ''short'':24B ''skill'':30B ''spell'':8B ''target'':16B ''touch'':18B', 'mage', 'Healing Hands is a spell that allows the caster to heal a target by touching them, restoring health over a short period. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('candlehearth_hall', 'Candlehearth Hall is a prominent tavern located in the heart of Windhelm. It has a rich history, with the building originally serving as the home of Vundheim, a great warrior from the early Fourth Era. Upon Vundheim''s death in 4E 38, his son Deroct honored his memory by lighting a candle above the hearth, a tradition that continues to this day, giving the tavern its name.

The hall has become a popular gathering place for Windhelm''s citizens, offering drinks, hearty meals, and performances from bards. Elda Early-Dawn is the tavern''s owner, with Nils serving as the cook.', '''38'':44B ''4e'':43B ''bard'':89B ''becom'':73B ''build'':22B ''candl'':54B ''candlehearth'':1A,3B ''citizen'':81B ''continu'':61B ''cook'':104B ''dawn'':93B ''day'':64B ''death'':41B ''deroct'':47B ''drink'':83B ''earli'':35B,92B ''early-dawn'':91B ''elda'':90B ''era'':37B ''fourth'':36B ''gather'':76B ''give'':65B ''great'':31B ''hall'':2A,4B,71B ''heart'':12B ''hearth'':57B ''hearti'':84B ''histori'':19B ''home'':27B ''honor'':48B ''light'':52B ''locat'':9B ''meal'':85B ''memori'':50B ''name'':69B ''nil'':100B ''offer'':82B ''origin'':23B ''owner'':98B ''perform'':87B ''place'':77B ''popular'':75B ''promin'':7B ''rich'':18B ''serv'':24B,101B ''son'':46B ''tavern'':8B,67B,96B ''tradit'':59B ''upon'':38B ''vundheim'':29B,39B ''warrior'':32B ''windhelm'':14B,79B', 'eastmarch, innkeeper, traveler', 'Candlehearth Hall is a prominent tavern located in the heart of Windhelm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nord', 'Nords, also known as the Children of the Sky, are a race of tall, fair-haired humans from the province of Skyrim, renowned for their resistance to cold and magical frost. Known as fierce and powerful warriors, Nords excel in all forms of combat, often serving as soldiers, mercenaries, or adventurers across Tamriel. Their culture is deeply martial, and their history is filled with tales of conquests and warfare, dating back to their migration from the northern land of Atmora. Though once famed for their seafaring prowess, the Nords have since established their homeland of Skyrim, where they are fiercely protective of their traditions and independence.

Nordic society is built around a strong sense of honor, loyalty, and ancestor worship. Their religion, known as the Old Ways, venerates a pantheon of gods, including Kyne, the goddess of the sky, and Shor, the god of the underworld. Nords also revere the Thu’um, the power of the Voice, a mystical force used by legendary warriors known as Tongues. Nords have a distinct architectural style, marked by wooden longhouses and fortresses, and their funerary customs emphasize ancestor worship, with burial sites treated as sacred places. Their cultural heritage and warrior spirit define much of their identity, making them one of Tamriel’s most formidable and respected peoples.', '''across'':54B ''adventur'':53B ''also'':3B,150B ''ancestor'':121B,186B ''architectur'':173B ''around'':113B ''atmora'':82B ''back'':73B ''built'':112B ''burial'':189B ''children'':7B ''cold'':30B ''combat'':46B ''conquest'':69B ''cultur'':57B,196B ''custom'':184B ''date'':72B ''deepli'':59B ''defin'':201B ''distinct'':172B ''emphas'':185B ''establish'':94B ''excel'':41B ''fair'':17B ''fair-hair'':16B ''fame'':85B ''fierc'':36B,102B ''fill'':65B ''forc'':161B ''form'':44B ''formid'':212B ''fortress'':180B ''frost'':33B ''funerari'':183B ''god'':134B,145B ''goddess'':138B ''hair'':18B ''heritag'':197B ''histori'':63B ''homeland'':96B ''honor'':118B ''human'':19B ''ident'':205B ''includ'':135B ''independ'':108B ''known'':4B,34B,125B,166B ''kyne'':136B ''land'':80B ''legendari'':164B ''longhous'':178B ''loyalti'':119B ''magic'':32B ''make'':206B ''mark'':175B ''martial'':60B ''mercenari'':51B ''migrat'':76B ''much'':202B ''mystic'':160B ''nord'':1A,2B,40B,91B,149B,169B ''nordic'':109B ''northern'':79B ''often'':47B ''old'':128B ''one'':208B ''pantheon'':132B ''peopl'':215B ''place'':194B ''power'':38B,155B ''protect'':103B ''provinc'':22B ''prowess'':89B ''race'':13B ''religion'':124B ''renown'':25B ''resist'':28B ''respect'':214B ''rever'':151B ''sacr'':193B ''seafar'':88B ''sens'':116B ''serv'':48B ''shor'':143B ''sinc'':93B ''site'':190B ''sky'':10B,141B ''skyrim'':24B,98B ''societi'':110B ''soldier'':50B ''spirit'':200B ''strong'':115B ''style'':174B ''tale'':67B ''tall'':15B ''tamriel'':55B ''tamriel’'':210B ''though'':83B ''thu’um'':153B ''tongu'':168B ''tradit'':106B ''treat'':191B ''underworld'':148B ''use'':162B ''vener'':130B ''voic'':158B ''warfar'':71B ''warrior'':39B,165B,199B ''way'':129B ''wooden'':177B ''worship'':122B,187B', 'nord, dragon, scholar', '
Nords, or the Children of the Sky, are tall, fair-haired humans from Skyrim, known for their resistance to cold and frost magic. Renowned as fierce warriors, they excel in combat and value honor, loyalty, and independence. Their culture, rooted in ancestor worship and the Old Ways, venerates gods like Kyne and Shor and honors the mystical Thu’um, or Voice. With a rich history of warfare and a distinct architectural style of wooden longhouses, Nords remain a proud and formidable people, deeply connected to their traditions and homeland.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sunderstone_gorge', 'Sunderstone Gorge is a small cave located north-northwest of Falkreath and east of Bilegulch Mine in Falkreath Hold. It is rumored that warlocks have taken over the area.', '''area'':32B ''bilegulch'':18B ''cave'':8B ''east'':16B ''falkreath'':14B,21B ''gorg'':2A,4B ''hold'':22B ''locat'':9B ''mine'':19B ''north'':11B ''north-northwest'':10B ''northwest'':12B ''rumor'':25B ''small'':7B ''sunderston'':1A,3B ''taken'':29B ''warlock'':27B', 'falkreath', 'Sunderstone Gorge is a small cave located north-northwest of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glenmoril_coven', 'Glenmoril Coven is a small, foreboding cave located northwest of Falkreath and south of Bilegulch Mine in Falkreath Hold. The cave is home to hags or Glenmoril Witches and consists of a single zone, Glenmoril Cave.

The approach to the cave is ominous, with dead plant life and mutilated shrines lining the path that begins north of an unmarked ruined tower. As the path ascends through several switchbacks, travelers will encounter eerie hagraven symbols, bone totems, and severed heads mounted on stakes. ', '''approach'':40B ''ascend'':67B ''begin'':57B ''bilegulch'':17B ''bone'':77B ''cave'':9B,23B,38B,43B ''consist'':32B ''coven'':2A,4B ''dead'':47B ''eeri'':74B ''encount'':73B ''falkreath'':13B,20B ''forebod'':8B ''glenmoril'':1A,3B,29B,37B ''hag'':27B ''hagraven'':75B ''head'':81B ''hold'':21B ''home'':25B ''life'':49B ''line'':53B ''locat'':10B ''mine'':18B ''mount'':82B ''mutil'':51B ''north'':58B ''northwest'':11B ''omin'':45B ''path'':55B,66B ''plant'':48B ''ruin'':62B ''sever'':69B,80B ''shrine'':52B ''singl'':35B ''small'':7B ''south'':15B ''stake'':84B ''switchback'':70B ''symbol'':76B ''totem'':78B ''tower'':63B ''travel'':71B ''unmark'':61B ''witch'':30B ''zone'':36B', 'falkreath, witch', 'Glenmoril Coven is a small, foreboding cave located northwest of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. TYou do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dead_man''s_drink', 'Dead Man''s Drink is an inn located near the center of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold, opposite Gray Pine Goods and adjacent to Corpselight Farm. Owned by Valga Vinicia, it serves as a hub for travelers and locals alike.

The inn features Narri as a waitress, often found outside leaning against the porch fence, and Delacourt as the resident bard, providing entertainment to patrons. With a warm, rustic atmosphere, Dead Man''s Drink offers a single interior zone and is a welcoming stop for adventurers exploring the region.', '''adjac'':26B ''adventur'':89B ''alik'':43B ''atmospher'':73B ''bard'':64B ''center'':15B ''corpselight'':28B ''dead'':1A,5B,74B ''delacourt'':60B ''drink'':4A,8B,77B ''entertain'':66B ''explor'':90B ''falkreath'':17B,19B ''farm'':29B ''featur'':46B ''fenc'':58B ''found'':52B ''good'':24B ''gray'':22B ''hold'':20B ''hub'':38B ''inn'':11B,45B ''interior'':81B ''lean'':54B ''local'':42B ''locat'':12B ''man'':2A,6B,75B ''narri'':47B ''near'':13B ''offer'':78B ''often'':51B ''opposit'':21B ''outsid'':53B ''own'':30B ''patron'':68B ''pine'':23B ''porch'':57B ''provid'':65B ''region'':92B ''resid'':63B ''rustic'':72B ''serv'':35B ''singl'':80B ''stop'':87B ''travel'':40B ''valga'':32B ''vinicia'':33B ''waitress'':50B ''warm'':71B ''welcom'':86B ''zone'':82B', 'falkreath, innkeeper, traveler', 'Dead Man''s Drink is an inn located near the center of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. You do not know who runs the inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('viola_giordano''s_house', 'Viola Giordano''s House is a large, two-story Nordic-style residence located in Windhelm''s Valunstrad district. It is positioned in one of the city''s better neighborhoods, directly opposite the house of Clan Shatter-Shield and to the north of the graveyard and Hall of the Dead. Viola Giordano is the sole occupant of the house, though she is rarely seen there, spending little time in her home.', '''better'':34B ''citi'':32B ''clan'':41B ''dead'':56B ''direct'':36B ''district'':24B ''giordano'':2A,6B,58B ''graveyard'':51B ''hall'':53B ''home'':77B ''hous'':4A,8B,39B,65B ''larg'':11B ''littl'':73B ''locat'':19B ''neighborhood'':35B ''nordic'':16B ''nordic-styl'':15B ''north'':48B ''occup'':62B ''one'':29B ''opposit'':37B ''posit'':27B ''rare'':69B ''resid'':18B ''seen'':70B ''shatter'':43B ''shatter-shield'':42B ''shield'':44B ''sole'':61B ''spend'':72B ''stori'':14B ''style'':17B ''though'':66B ''time'':74B ''two'':13B ''two-stori'':12B ''valunstrad'':23B ''viola'':1A,5B,57B ''windhelm'':21B', 'eastmarch', 'Viola Giordano''s House is a large, two-story Nordic-style residence located in Windhelm''s Valunstrad district.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lost_tongue_overlook', 'Lost Tongue Overlook is a dragon lair located south of Riften and east-southeast of Crystaldrift Cave. The path to the lair begins just past Snow-Shod Farm and winds south, passing a dragon mound and climbing several flights of stairs marked by piles of rocks.', '''begin'':27B ''cave'':21B ''climb'':42B ''crystaldrift'':20B ''dragon'':9B,39B ''east'':17B ''east-southeast'':16B ''farm'':33B ''flight'':44B ''lair'':10B,26B ''locat'':11B ''lost'':1A,4B ''mark'':47B ''mound'':40B ''overlook'':3A,6B ''pass'':37B ''past'':29B ''path'':23B ''pile'':49B ''riften'':14B ''rock'':51B ''sever'':43B ''shod'':32B ''snow'':31B ''snow-shod'':30B ''south'':12B,36B ''southeast'':18B ''stair'':46B ''tongu'':2A,5B ''wind'':35B', 'rift, dragon', 'Lost Tongue Overlook is a dragon lair located south of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_plate_armor', 'Steel Plate Armor is a basic steel plate chest piece with good protection quality. Its visual design is robust and practical, with polished steel surfaces and reinforced plates that emphasize durability and function. To craft it: 3 steel ingots, 1 corundum ingot, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''1'':43B ''3'':40B,47B ''adept'':55B ''armor'':3A,6B ''basic'':9B ''blacksmith'':52B ''chest'':12B ''corundum'':44B ''craft'':38B,58B ''design'':20B ''durabl'':34B ''emphas'':33B ''forg'':53B ''function'':36B ''good'':15B ''ingot'':42B,45B ''leather'':48B ''piec'':13B ''plate'':2A,5B,11B,31B ''polish'':26B ''practic'':24B ''protect'':16B ''qualiti'':17B ''reinforc'':30B ''robust'':22B ''smith'':56B ''steel'':1A,4B,10B,27B,41B,66B ''strip'':49B ''surfac'':28B ''tempered/improved'':63B ''use'':65B ''visual'':19B ''workbench'':69B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel Plate Armor is a basic steel plate chest piece with good protection quality. Its visual design is robust and practical, with polished steel surfaces and reinforced plates that emphasize durability and function. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('conjure_seeker', 'Conjure Seeker is a Conjuration spell that summons a Seeker from Apocrypha to fight for the caster for a limited time. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''apocrypha'':14B ''cast'':31B ''caster'':19B ''conjur'':1A,3B,7B ''expert'':27B ''fight'':16B ''level'':29B ''limit'':22B ''requir'':25B ''seeker'':2A,4B,12B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':8B ''summon'':10B ''time'':23B', 'mage', '
Conjure Seeker is a spell that summons a Seeker from Apocrypha to fight alongside the caster for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('morthal', 'Morthal is a small city in northern Skyrim and the capital of Hjaalmarch, located on the southern edge of the Drajkmyr marsh. Initially aligned with the Empire, Jarl Idgrod Ravencrone’s mystical and reclusive nature has led to perceptions of her as an ineffective ruler. She often speaks of sensing larger forces at play, which has distanced her from her citizens, many of whom worry about the war bringing outsiders and prefer their isolated way of life.

The city is a humble settlement with little economic or strategic value, supported only by a small lumber mill, an apothecary (Thaumaturgist''s Hut), and an inn (Moorside Inn). Morthal’s surroundings are often shrouded in thick fog, with twisted trees and glowing torches creating a haunting atmosphere. The swampy lands are rich in deathbells, swamp fungal pods, and giant lichen, but are also dangerous at night, with creatures such as trolls and occasionally chaurus lurking nearby.', '''align'':25B ''also'':140B ''apothecari'':98B ''atmospher'':124B ''bring'':69B ''capit'':12B ''chaurus'':151B ''citi'':6B,79B ''citizen'':61B ''creat'':121B ''creatur'':145B ''danger'':141B ''deathbel'':131B ''distanc'':57B ''drajkmyr'':22B ''econom'':86B ''edg'':19B ''empir'':28B ''fog'':114B ''forc'':52B ''fungal'':133B ''giant'':136B ''glow'':119B ''haunt'':123B ''hjaalmarch'':14B ''humbl'':82B ''hut'':101B ''idgrod'':30B ''ineffect'':44B ''initi'':24B ''inn'':104B,106B ''isol'':74B ''jarl'':29B ''land'':127B ''larger'':51B ''led'':37B ''lichen'':137B ''life'':77B ''littl'':85B ''locat'':15B ''lumber'':95B ''lurk'':152B ''mani'':62B ''marsh'':23B ''mill'':96B ''moorsid'':105B ''morthal'':1A,2B ''morthal’'':107B ''mystic'':32B ''natur'':35B ''nearbi'':153B ''night'':143B ''northern'':8B ''occasion'':150B ''often'':47B,110B ''outsid'':70B ''percept'':39B ''play'':54B ''pod'':134B ''prefer'':72B ''ravencrone’'':31B ''reclus'':34B ''rich'':129B ''ruler'':45B ''sens'':50B ''settlement'':83B ''shroud'':111B ''skyrim'':9B ''small'':5B,94B ''southern'':18B ''speak'':48B ''strateg'':88B ''support'':90B ''surround'':108B ''swamp'':132B ''swampi'':126B ''thaumaturgist'':99B ''thick'':113B ''torch'':120B ''tree'':117B ''troll'':148B ''twist'':116B ''valu'':89B ''war'':68B ''way'':75B ''worri'':65B', 'hjaalmarch, noble, scholar', 'Morthal is a small city in northern Skyrim and the capital of Hjaalmarch, located on the southern edge of the Drajkmyr marsh. Initially aligned with the Empire, Jarl Idgrod Ravencrone’s mystical and reclusive nature has led to perceptions of her as an ineffective ruler. 

The city is a humble settlement with little economic or strategic value, supported only by a small lumber mill, an apothecary (Thaumaturgist''s Hut), and an inn (Moorside Inn). Morthal’s surroundings are often shrouded in thick fog, with twisted trees and glowing torches creating a haunting atmosphere. The swampy lands are rich in deathbells, swamp fungal pods, and giant lichen, but are also dangerous at night, with creatures such as trolls and occasionally chaurus lurking nearby.', '', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falkreath_watchtower', 'Falkreath Watchtower is a small, ruined tower located north of Falkreath and northeast of Roadside Ruins in Falkreath Hold. It is rumoured to be inhabited by a lone necromancer and accessed via a dirt path branching south from the road along the southern shore of Lake Ilinalta, marked by a pile of rocks.', '''access'':33B ''along'':43B ''branch'':38B ''dirt'':36B ''falkreath'':1A,3B,13B,20B ''hold'':21B ''ilinalta'':49B ''inhabit'':27B ''lake'':48B ''locat'':10B ''lone'':30B ''mark'':50B ''necromanc'':31B ''north'':11B ''northeast'':15B ''path'':37B ''pile'':53B ''road'':42B ''roadsid'':17B ''rock'':55B ''ruin'':8B,18B ''rumour'':24B ''shore'':46B ''small'':7B ''south'':39B ''southern'':45B ''tower'':9B ''via'':34B ''watchtow'':2A,4B', 'falkreath', 'Falkreath Watchtower is a small, ruined tower located north of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_lord_stone', 'The Lord Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located east of Morthal and northeast of the Shrine of Mehrunes Dagon in Hjaalmarch. When activated, the Lord Stone grants a moderate boost to your armor rating and  a decent amount of magic resistance, making it easier to reach the armor and magic resistance caps. While it offers less defense than the Atronach Stone, it has no associated penalty, making it a more balanced defensive option.

The stone itself is perched atop a stone base, flanked by the remains of large arches. To reach the Lord Stone, follow the path that leads past the Shrine of Mehrunes Dagon, which begins to the west of the Hall of the Vigilant. The route is marked by several piles of rocks, some with remnants of banners flapping in the wind. After passing Dimhollow Crypt, ascend a flight of stone steps leading up to the shrine, then turn northeast to find the Lord Stone atop a nearby hill.', '''across'':15B ''activ'':32B ''amount'':47B ''arch'':98B ''armor'':42B,57B ''ascend'':148B ''associ'':74B ''atop'':88B,167B ''atronach'':69B ''balanc'':80B ''banner'':139B ''base'':91B ''begin'':116B ''boost'':39B ''cap'':61B ''crypt'':147B ''dagon'':28B,114B ''decent'':46B ''defens'':66B,81B ''dimhollow'':146B ''easier'':53B ''east'':18B ''find'':163B ''flank'':92B ''flap'':140B ''flight'':150B ''follow'':104B ''grant'':36B ''hall'':122B ''hill'':170B ''hjaalmarch'':30B ''larg'':97B ''lead'':108B,154B ''less'':65B ''locat'':17B ''lord'':2A,5B,34B,102B,165B ''magic'':49B,59B ''make'':51B,76B ''mark'':129B ''mehrun'':27B,113B ''moder'':38B ''morthal'':20B ''nearbi'':169B ''northeast'':22B,161B ''offer'':64B ''one'':8B ''option'':82B ''pass'':145B ''past'':109B ''path'':106B ''penalti'':75B ''perch'':87B ''pile'':132B ''rate'':43B ''reach'':55B,100B ''remain'':95B ''remnant'':137B ''resist'':50B,60B ''rock'':134B ''rout'':127B ''scatter'':14B ''sever'':131B ''shrine'':25B,111B,158B ''skyrim'':16B ''stand'':12B ''step'':153B ''stone'':3A,6B,13B,35B,70B,84B,90B,103B,152B,166B ''thirteen'':11B ''turn'':160B ''vigil'':125B ''west'':119B ''wind'':143B', 'hjaalmarch, scholar, traveler', 'The Lord Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located east of Morthal in Hjaalmarch. When activated, the Lord Stone grants a moderate boost to your armor rating and  a decent amount of magic resistance, making it easier to reach the armor and magic resistance caps. While it offers less defense than the Atronach Stone, it has no associated penalty, making it a more balanced defensive option.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ironback_hideout', 'Ironback Hideout is a dilapidated house located to the northwest of Solitude, a short distance east of The Steed Stone in Haafingar. The structure is in ruins, with no roof, windows, or doors, and has been taken over by a group of bandits, including a bandit chief.

The hideout can be accessed by following the road towards the Thalmor Embassy, turning west once you are east of the house.', '''access'':54B ''bandit'':45B,48B ''chief'':49B ''dilapid'':7B ''distanc'':17B ''door'':35B ''east'':18B,68B ''embassi'':62B ''follow'':56B ''group'':43B ''haafingar'':24B ''hideout'':2A,4B,51B ''hous'':8B,71B ''includ'':46B ''ironback'':1A,3B ''locat'':9B ''northwest'':12B ''road'':58B ''roof'':32B ''ruin'':29B ''short'':16B ''solitud'':14B ''steed'':21B ''stone'':22B ''structur'':26B ''taken'':39B ''thalmor'':61B ''toward'':59B ''turn'':63B ''west'':64B ''window'':33B', 'haafingar', 'Ironback Hideout is a dilapidated house located to the northwest of Solitude in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('solitude', 'Solitude is a major city located on the northwest coast of Skyrim, serving as the capital of both Haafingar and the entire province. Built atop a natural arch over the Sea of Ghosts, it is the largest city in Skyrim and the seat of the province''s High King. The city is ruled by Jarl Elisif the Fair, widow of the late High King Torygg, and her throne resides in the Blue Palace.

Solitude is home to many important buildings and institutions, including the headquarters of the Imperial Legion in Skyrim, the East Empire Company Warehouse, and the Bards College. The Thalmor Embassy is located nearby, adding to the city’s political significance. Notable locations within Solitude include the Bards College, Bits and Pieces shop, Blue Palace, Castle Dour, the Fletcher, the Temple of the Divines, and the Winking Skeever inn.', '''ad'':108B ''arch'':29B ''atop'':26B ''bard'':100B,120B ''bit'':122B ''blue'':73B,126B ''build'':81B ''built'':25B ''capit'':17B ''castl'':128B ''citi'':6B,39B,52B ''city’'':111B ''coast'':11B ''colleg'':101B,121B ''compani'':96B ''divin'':136B ''dour'':129B ''east'':94B ''elisif'':57B ''embassi'':104B ''empir'':95B ''entir'':23B ''fair'':59B ''fletcher'':131B ''ghost'':34B ''haafingar'':20B ''headquart'':86B ''high'':49B,64B ''home'':77B ''imperi'':89B ''import'':80B ''includ'':84B,118B ''inn'':141B ''institut'':83B ''jarl'':56B ''king'':50B,65B ''largest'':38B ''late'':63B ''legion'':90B ''locat'':7B,106B,115B ''major'':5B ''mani'':79B ''natur'':28B ''nearbi'':107B ''northwest'':10B ''notabl'':114B ''palac'':74B,127B ''piec'':124B ''polit'':112B ''provinc'':24B,47B ''resid'':70B ''rule'':54B ''sea'':32B ''seat'':44B ''serv'':14B ''shop'':125B ''signific'':113B ''skeever'':140B ''skyrim'':13B,41B,92B ''solitud'':1A,2B,75B,117B ''templ'':133B ''thalmor'':103B ''throne'':69B ''torygg'':66B ''warehous'':97B ''widow'':60B ''wink'':139B ''within'':116B', 'haafingar, noble, scholar', 'Solitude is a major city located on the northwest coast of Skyrim, serving as the capital of both Haafingar and the entire province. Built atop a natural arch over the Sea of Ghosts, it is the largest city in Skyrim and the seat of the province''s High King. The city is ruled by Jarl Elisif the Fair, widow of the late High King Torygg, and her throne resides in the Blue Palace.', '', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('charred_skeever_hide', 'Charred Skeever Hides can be collected from charred skeevers, often found after a battle or fire. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Cure Disease, Resist Poison, and Restore Health.', '''alchemi'':20B ''battl'':17B ''char'':1A,4B,11B ''collect'':9B ''cure'':24B ''diseas'':25B ''effect'':21B ''fire'':19B ''found'':14B ''health'':30B ''hide'':3A,6B ''often'':13B ''poison'':27B ''resist'':26B ''restor'':22B,29B ''skeever'':2A,5B,12B ''stamina'':23B', 'alchemist', 'Charred Skeever Hides can be collected from charred skeevers, often found after a battle or fire.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sotha_sil', 'Sotha Sil, also known as Seht, was the wizard-mystic god of the Dunmer and one of the most enigmatic figures of the Tribunal. Revered by his followers for his wisdom and magical prowess, he held many titles, including the Mainspring Ever-Wound, the Father of Mysteries, and the Clockwork King of the Three in One. Unlike his counterparts, Sotha Sil did not consider himself a god but allowed Vivec and Almalexia to embrace their divine identities. He famously rejected the notion of free will, dedicating himself to the creation of his greatest invention, the Clockwork City, where his Clockwork Apostles resided and pursued a vision for a new Nirn.

Sotha Sil''s legacy extended beyond his mechanical creations. He negotiated the Coldharbour Compact with eight Daedric Princes, believed to limit their direct involvement in mortal affairs, although this agreement was not always upheld. His craftsmanship yielded numerous artifacts and advanced metallic prosthetics, which could replace lost limbs, reflecting his belief that "the truth of clockwork is for all." However, his followers took great care to protect his inventions from misuse. With the advent of the New Temple in the Fourth Era, Sotha Sil, along with the other members of the Tribunal, was reclassified as a saint, while the worship of the Good Daedra was restored as central to Dunmeri faith.', '''advanc'':155B ''advent'':188B ''affair'':141B ''agreement'':144B ''allow'':73B ''almalexia'':76B ''along'':199B ''also'':5B ''although'':142B ''alway'':147B ''apostl'':105B ''artifact'':153B ''belief'':165B ''believ'':133B ''beyond'':120B ''care'':179B ''central'':222B ''citi'':101B ''clockwork'':54B,100B,104B,170B ''coldharbour'':127B ''compact'':128B ''consid'':68B ''could'':159B ''counterpart'':63B ''craftsmanship'':150B ''creation'':94B,123B ''daedra'':218B ''daedric'':131B ''dedic'':90B ''direct'':137B ''divin'':80B ''dunmer'':17B ''dunmeri'':224B ''eight'':130B ''embrac'':78B ''enigmat'':23B ''era'':196B ''ever'':46B ''ever-wound'':45B ''extend'':119B ''faith'':225B ''famous'':83B ''father'':49B ''figur'':24B ''follow'':31B,176B ''fourth'':195B ''free'':88B ''god'':14B,71B ''good'':217B ''great'':178B ''greatest'':97B ''held'':39B ''howev'':174B ''ident'':81B ''includ'':42B ''invent'':98B,183B ''involv'':138B ''king'':55B ''known'':6B ''legaci'':118B ''limb'':162B ''limit'':135B ''lost'':161B ''magic'':36B ''mainspr'':44B ''mani'':40B ''mechan'':122B ''member'':203B ''metal'':156B ''misus'':185B ''mortal'':140B ''mysteri'':51B ''mystic'':13B ''negoti'':125B ''new'':113B,191B ''nirn'':114B ''notion'':86B ''numer'':152B ''one'':19B,60B ''princ'':132B ''prosthet'':157B ''protect'':181B ''prowess'':37B ''pursu'':108B ''reclassifi'':208B ''reflect'':163B ''reject'':84B ''replac'':160B ''resid'':106B ''restor'':220B ''rever'':28B ''saint'':211B ''seht'':8B ''sil'':2A,4B,65B,116B,198B ''sotha'':1A,3B,64B,115B,197B ''templ'':192B ''three'':58B ''titl'':41B ''took'':177B ''tribun'':27B,206B ''truth'':168B ''unlik'':61B ''upheld'':148B ''vision'':110B ''vivec'':74B ''wisdom'':34B ''wizard'':12B ''wizard-myst'':11B ''worship'':214B ''wound'':47B ''yield'':151B', 'darkelf, daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Sotha Sil, also known as Seht, was the wizard-mystic god of the Dunmer and one of the Tribunal''s most enigmatic figures. Revered for his magical prowess and wisdom, he did not consider himself a god like Vivec and Almalexia. Instead, he focused on creating the Clockwork City and believed in a vision for a new Nirn. Sotha Sil also negotiated the Coldharbour Compact with the Daedric Princes, although this was not always respected. His craftsmanship led to the creation of many artifacts and prosthetics. In the Fourth Era, he and the Tribunal were reclassified as saints, and the worship of the Good Daedra was restored in Dunmeri faith.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('east_empire_company_warehouse', 'The East Empire Company Warehouse is located on the Solitude docks, immediately southeast of the city. It serves as the headquarters and main storage facility for the East Empire Company in Skyrim. The entrance to the warehouse is typically locked, and entering without permission will result in trespassing charges. A Solitude guard can often be found patrolling outside, while the warehouse''s interior is staffed by Dockworkers, the Dockmaster, and Snorreid, along with three patrolling Solitude guards.
', '''along'':76B ''charg'':53B ''citi'':20B ''compani'':3A,8B,34B ''dock'':15B ''dockmast'':73B ''dockwork'':71B ''east'':1A,6B,32B ''empir'':2A,7B,33B ''enter'':46B ''entranc'':38B ''facil'':29B ''found'':60B ''guard'':56B,81B ''headquart'':25B ''immedi'':16B ''interior'':67B ''locat'':11B ''lock'':44B ''main'':27B ''often'':58B ''outsid'':62B ''patrol'':61B,79B ''permiss'':48B ''result'':50B ''serv'':22B ''skyrim'':36B ''snorreid'':75B ''solitud'':14B,55B,80B ''southeast'':17B ''staf'':69B ''storag'':28B ''three'':78B ''trespass'':52B ''typic'':43B ''warehous'':4A,9B,41B,65B ''without'':47B', 'haafingar, legion', 'The East Empire Company Warehouse is located on the Solitude docks, immediately southeast of the city. It serves as the headquarters and main storage facility for the East Empire Company in Skyrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orphan_rock', 'Orphan Rock is a wooded valley featuring a central rock plateau, located northeast of Helgen and south of North Skybound Watch in Falkreath Hold. The area is inhabited by witches or hags led by a hagraven, making it a dangerous location for unwary travelers.

There are rumors of a powerful dagger, Nettlebane, being held at this location.', '''area'':28B ''central'':11B ''dagger'':53B ''danger'':42B ''falkreath'':25B ''featur'':9B ''hag'':34B ''hagraven'':38B ''held'':56B ''helgen'':17B ''hold'':26B ''inhabit'':30B ''led'':35B ''locat'':14B,43B,59B ''make'':39B ''nettleban'':54B ''north'':21B ''northeast'':15B ''orphan'':1A,3B ''plateau'':13B ''power'':52B ''rock'':2A,4B,12B ''rumor'':49B ''skybound'':22B ''south'':19B ''travel'':46B ''unwari'':45B ''valley'':8B ''watch'':23B ''witch'':32B ''wood'':7B', 'falkreath', 'Orphan Rock is a wooded valley featuring a central rock plateau, located northeast of Helgen in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('conjure_ash_spawn', 'Conjure Ash Spawn is a Conjuration spell that summons an Ash Spawn to fight alongside the caster for a limited time. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':28B ''alongsid'':18B ''ash'':2A,5B,14B ''cast'':32B ''caster'':20B ''conjur'':1A,4B,9B ''fight'':17B ''level'':30B ''limit'':23B ''requir'':26B ''skill'':29B ''spawn'':3A,6B,15B ''spell'':10B ''summon'':12B ''time'':24B', 'mage', 'Conjure Ash Spawn is a spell that summons an Ash Spawn, a fiery creature, to fight by the caster''s side for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('spectral_arrow', 'Spectral Arrow is a Conjuration spell that summons a magical arrow to strike a target, dealing damage and staggering them. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':26B ''arrow'':2A,4B,13B ''cast'':30B ''conjur'':7B ''damag'':19B ''deal'':18B ''level'':28B ''magic'':12B ''requir'':24B ''skill'':27B ''spectral'':1A,3B ''spell'':8B ''stagger'':21B ''strike'':15B ''summon'':10B ''target'':17B', 'mage', 'Spectral Arrow is a spell that summons a magical arrow to strike a target, dealing damage and staggering them. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('widow''s_watch_ruins', 'Widow''s Watch Ruins is a small, weathered tower located west-northwest of Solitude and northeast of Fort Hraggstad in Haafingar. The tower stands as a forgotten remnant of Skyrim''s past, surrounded by the rugged terrain of the region, There are rumors of a witch living in the area.', '''area'':55B ''forgotten'':32B ''fort'':23B ''haafingar'':26B ''hraggstad'':24B ''live'':52B ''locat'':14B ''northeast'':21B ''northwest'':17B ''past'':37B ''region'':45B ''remnant'':33B ''rug'':41B ''ruin'':4A,8B ''rumor'':48B ''skyrim'':35B ''small'':11B ''solitud'':19B ''stand'':29B ''surround'':38B ''terrain'':42B ''tower'':13B,28B ''watch'':3A,7B ''weather'':12B ''west'':16B ''west-northwest'':15B ''widow'':1A,5B ''witch'':51B', 'haafingar', 'Widow''s Watch Ruins is a small, weathered tower located west-northwest of Solitude in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('moldering_ruins', 'Moldering Ruins is a hidden and foreboding site west of Rorikstead and east of Soljund''s Sinkhole, shrouded in mystery amidst the rugged landscapes of Whiterun Hold. 

It is rumoured that vampires and the undead take residence here in a hidden cave.', '''amidst'':23B ''cave'':44B ''east'':15B ''forebod'':9B ''hidden'':7B,43B ''hold'':29B ''landscap'':26B ''molder'':1A,3B ''mysteri'':22B ''resid'':39B ''rorikstead'':13B ''rug'':25B ''ruin'':2A,4B ''rumour'':32B ''shroud'':20B ''sinkhol'':19B ''site'':10B ''soljund'':17B ''take'':38B ''undead'':37B ''vampir'':34B ''west'':11B ''whiterun'':28B', 'whiterun', 'Moldering Ruins is a hidden and foreboding site west of Rorikstead.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('kilkreath_ruins', 'Kilkreath Ruins is a large, ancient temple located west of Solitude and southeast of Wolfskull Cave in Haafingar. The ruins are home to corrupted shades, spectral enemies who haunt the temple''s dilapidated halls. There are rumors that a necromancer has taken over the ruins, causing the shades to appear. ', '''ancient'':8B ''appear'':52B ''caus'':48B ''cave'':18B ''corrupt'':26B ''dilapid'':35B ''enemi'':29B ''haafingar'':20B ''hall'':36B ''haunt'':31B ''home'':24B ''kilkreath'':1A,3B ''larg'':7B ''locat'':10B ''necromanc'':42B ''ruin'':2A,4B,22B,47B ''rumor'':39B ''shade'':27B,50B ''solitud'':13B ''southeast'':15B ''spectral'':28B ''taken'':44B ''templ'':9B,33B ''west'':11B ''wolfskul'':17B', 'haafingar, daedra, daedric', 'Kilkreath Ruins is a large, ancient temple located west of Solitude in Haafingar.  You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('statue_to_meridia', 'The Statue to Meridia is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince of Life and Light, Meridia. Located west of Solitude and east of Clearpine Pond in Haafingar, the statue stands as a beacon of Meridia''s influence in Skyrim. It is rumored that the Beacon of Meridia is missing from this location, hidden somewhere in Skyrim.', '''beacon'':37B,49B ''clearpin'':28B ''daedric'':14B ''dedic'':11B ''east'':26B ''haafingar'':31B ''hidden'':57B ''influenc'':41B ''life'':17B ''light'':19B ''locat'':21B,56B ''meridia'':3A,7B,20B,39B,51B ''miss'':53B ''pond'':29B ''princ'':15B ''rumor'':46B ''shrine'':10B ''skyrim'':43B,60B ''solitud'':24B ''somewher'':58B ''stand'':34B ''statu'':1A,5B,33B ''west'':22B', 'haafingar, daedra, daedric', 'The Statue to Meridia is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince of Life and Light, Meridia. Located west of Solitude in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('beitild''s_house', '
Beitild''s House is the residence of Beitild, a Nord miner and the owner of Iron-Breaker Mine, located in Dawnstar.  Beitild is known for her strong personality and her position as a key figure in Dawnstar''s economy, with the mine being one of the town''s primary sources of income.', '''beitild'':1A,4B,11B,26B ''breaker'':21B ''dawnstar'':25B,41B ''economi'':43B ''figur'':39B ''hous'':3A,6B ''incom'':56B ''iron'':20B ''iron-break'':19B ''key'':38B ''known'':28B ''locat'':23B ''mine'':22B,46B ''miner'':14B ''nord'':13B ''one'':48B ''owner'':17B ''person'':32B ''posit'':35B ''primari'':53B ''resid'':9B ''sourc'':54B ''strong'':31B ''town'':51B', 'pale', 'Beitild''s House is the residence of Beitild, located in Dawnstar. You do not know who Betilid is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lost_echo_cave', 'Lost Echo Cave is a small cave located west of Solitude in Falkreath Hold, south of Steepfall Burrow. The cave is situated along the road that runs west of Fort Hraggstad, near the point where it turns south. The entrance is marked by piles of stones leading up to stone steps, and, unusually for a cave, the entrance is a wooden door adorned with lit candles on either side, with a statue positioned to the right. Rumors of Falmer have been seen coming out the cave late at night.', '''adorn'':66B ''along'':26B ''burrow'':21B ''candl'':69B ''cave'':3A,6B,10B,23B,59B,89B ''come'':86B ''door'':65B ''echo'':2A,5B ''either'':71B ''entranc'':43B,61B ''falkreath'':16B ''falmer'':82B ''fort'':33B ''hold'':17B ''hraggstad'':34B ''late'':90B ''lead'':50B ''lit'':68B ''locat'':11B ''lost'':1A,4B ''mark'':45B ''near'':35B ''night'':92B ''pile'':47B ''point'':37B ''posit'':76B ''right'':79B ''road'':28B ''rumor'':80B ''run'':30B ''seen'':85B ''side'':72B ''situat'':25B ''small'':9B ''solitud'':14B ''south'':18B,41B ''statu'':75B ''steepfal'':20B ''step'':54B ''stone'':49B,53B ''turn'':40B ''unusu'':56B ''west'':12B,31B ''wooden'':64B', 'haafingar', 'Lost Echo Cave is a small cave located west of Solitude in Haafingar Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brinewater_grotto', 'Brinewater Grotto is a small cave located north of Solitude, on the coast near the path that leads to Solitude Lighthouse. As you approach the lighthouse, the path splits, with a branch leading northwest toward a small jetty where a rowboat is moored. At the end of this path, a lantern hangs from a post, marking the entrance to the cave. Bandits occupy the grotto.', '''approach'':26B ''bandit'':64B ''branch'':34B ''brinewat'':1A,3B ''cave'':8B,63B ''coast'':15B ''end'':48B ''entranc'':60B ''grotto'':2A,4B,67B ''hang'':54B ''jetti'':40B ''lantern'':53B ''lead'':20B,35B ''lighthous'':23B,28B ''locat'':9B ''mark'':58B ''moor'':45B ''near'':16B ''north'':10B ''northwest'':36B ''occupi'':65B ''path'':18B,30B,51B ''post'':57B ''rowboat'':43B ''small'':7B,39B ''solitud'':12B,22B ''split'':31B ''toward'':37B', 'haafingar', 'Brinewater Grotto is a small cave located north of Solitude, on the coast near the path that leads to Solitude Lighthouse. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bleakwind_basin', 'Bleakwind Basin is a giants camp located west of Whiterun and north of the Western Watchtower, set against the wide, open plains of Whiterun Hold. The camp is home to a small group of giants and their mammoths, who roam peacefully amidst the sparse vegetation and scattered boulders characteristic of the region.

Marked by a large central fire pit and the towering figures of its inhabitants, Bleakwind Basin serves as a tranquil yet imposing presence in the Hold. ', '''amidst'':44B ''basin'':2A,4B,70B ''bleakwind'':1A,3B,69B ''boulder'':50B ''camp'':8B,29B ''central'':59B ''characterist'':51B ''figur'':65B ''fire'':60B ''giant'':7B,37B ''group'':35B ''hold'':27B,80B ''home'':31B ''impos'':76B ''inhabit'':68B ''larg'':58B ''locat'':9B ''mammoth'':40B ''mark'':55B ''north'':14B ''open'':23B ''peac'':43B ''pit'':61B ''plain'':24B ''presenc'':77B ''region'':54B ''roam'':42B ''scatter'':49B ''serv'':71B ''set'':19B ''small'':34B ''spars'':46B ''tower'':64B ''tranquil'':74B ''veget'':47B ''watchtow'':18B ''west'':10B ''western'':17B ''whiterun'':12B,26B ''wide'':22B ''yet'':75B', 'whiterun', 'Bleakwind Basin is a giants camp located west of Whiterun. The camp is home to a small group of giants and their mammoths.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rimerock_burrow', 'Rimerock Burrow is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge and south of Northwatch Keep in Haafingar. To reach the cave, follow a rough path that leads over a wooden bridge spanning a crevice in the cliff wall just before the entrance. The path branches off from the larger road near Pinefrost Tower, marked by a pile of rocks, though the fork can be easily missed. It is rumored that a powerful Conjuer, who has angered a Daedric God, resides in this location.', '''anger'':79B ''branch'':48B ''bridg'':13B,34B ''burrow'':2A,4B ''cave'':8B,24B ''cliff'':40B ''conjuer'':76B ''crevic'':37B ''daedric'':81B ''dragon'':12B ''easili'':68B ''entranc'':45B ''follow'':25B ''fork'':65B ''god'':82B ''haafingar'':20B ''keep'':18B ''larger'':52B ''lead'':30B ''locat'':9B,86B ''mark'':57B ''miss'':69B ''near'':54B ''northwatch'':17B ''northwest'':10B ''path'':28B,47B ''pile'':60B ''pinefrost'':55B ''power'':75B ''reach'':22B ''resid'':83B ''rimerock'':1A,3B ''road'':53B ''rock'':62B ''rough'':27B ''rumor'':72B ''small'':7B ''south'':15B ''span'':35B ''though'':63B ''tower'':56B ''wall'':41B ''wooden'':33B', 'haafingar', 'Rimerock Burrow is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('forgotten_vale', 'The Forgotten Vale is an isolated region located in northwestern Skyrim, once inhabited by the Snow Elves, who worshipped the god Auri-El. This secluded area is only accessible after navigating both Darkfall Cave and Darkfall Passage, and it provides access to eight distinct locations: Darkfall Grotto, Darkfall Passage, Forgotten Vale Cave, Forgotten Vale Forest, Forgotten Vale Overlook, the Glacial Crevice, the Inner Sanctum, and Sharpslope Cave.

Now, the Forgotten Vale is home to the corrupted Falmer, once the Snow Elves, along with a variety of dangerous creatures such as frost giants. The Snow Elves once built a temple dedicated to Auri-El, which can be found in the Inner Sanctum', '''access'':32B,44B ''along'':85B ''area'':29B ''auri'':25B,106B ''auri-el'':24B,105B ''built'':100B ''cave'':37B,55B,70B ''corrupt'':79B ''creatur'':91B ''crevic'':64B ''danger'':90B ''darkfal'':36B,39B,49B,51B ''dedic'':103B ''distinct'':47B ''eight'':46B ''el'':26B,107B ''elv'':19B,84B,98B ''falmer'':80B ''forest'':58B ''forgotten'':1A,4B,53B,56B,59B,73B ''found'':111B ''frost'':94B ''giant'':95B ''glacial'':63B ''god'':23B ''grotto'':50B ''home'':76B ''inhabit'':15B ''inner'':66B,114B ''isol'':8B ''locat'':10B,48B ''navig'':34B ''northwestern'':12B ''overlook'':61B ''passag'':40B,52B ''provid'':43B ''region'':9B ''sanctum'':67B,115B ''seclud'':28B ''sharpslop'':69B ''skyrim'':13B ''snow'':18B,83B,97B ''templ'':102B ''vale'':2A,5B,54B,57B,60B,74B ''varieti'':88B ''worship'':21B', 'snowelf', 'The Forgotten Vale is an isolated region located in northwestern Skyrim, once inhabited by the Snow Elves, who worshipped the god Auri-El. It is hidden somwhere in Haafingar Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'dawnguard, volkihar', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('angeline''s_aromatics', 'Angeline''s Aromatics is the alchemy shop in Solitude, located as the second building on the left after passing through Solitude''s main gate, just past The Winking Skeever. The shop is owned by Angeline Morrard, who specializes in selling potions, food, ingredients, and books.', '''alchemi'':9B ''angelin'':1A,4B,38B ''aromat'':3A,6B ''book'':48B ''build'':17B ''food'':45B ''gate'':27B ''ingredi'':46B ''left'':20B ''locat'':13B ''main'':26B ''morrard'':39B ''own'':36B ''pass'':22B ''past'':29B ''potion'':44B ''second'':16B ''sell'':43B ''shop'':10B,34B ''skeever'':32B ''solitud'':12B,24B ''special'':41B ''wink'':31B', 'haafingar', 'Angeline''s Aromatics is the alchemy shop in Solitude.  You do not know.who owns it.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fletcher', 'The Castle Fletcher is a store in Solitude that specializes in selling bows, arrows, and other ranged weapons. It is located on the outside of the walls of the Castle Dour courtyard, next to the Solitude Blacksmith.

The store is run by Fihada, who offers a variety of bows and arrows for purchase, as well as buying them from customers. The shop caters to archers and adventurers in need of quality ranged weapons.', '''adventur'':68B ''archer'':66B ''arrow'':15B,52B ''blacksmith'':38B ''bow'':14B,50B ''buy'':58B ''castl'':3B,31B ''cater'':64B ''courtyard'':33B ''custom'':61B ''dour'':32B ''fihada'':44B ''fletcher'':1A,4B ''locat'':22B ''need'':70B ''next'':34B ''offer'':46B ''outsid'':25B ''purchas'':54B ''qualiti'':72B ''rang'':18B,73B ''run'':42B ''sell'':13B ''shop'':63B ''solitud'':9B,37B ''special'':11B ''store'':7B,40B ''varieti'':48B ''wall'':28B ''weapon'':19B,74B ''well'':56B', 'haafingar', 'The Castle Fletcher is a store in Solitude that specializes in selling bows, arrows, and other ranged weapons. You do not know who runs the store.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('calixto''s_house_of_curiosities', 'Calixto''s House of Curiosities serves as both the home and museum of Calixto Corrium, showcasing an eclectic collection of oddities and curious artifacts.

The house is located on the east side of Windhelm, just before entering the Gray Quarter. Visitors can explore its single interior zone, where Calixto enthusiastically shares stories about his intriguing items.', '''artifact'':29B ''calixto'':1A,6B,19B,54B ''collect'':24B ''corrium'':20B ''curios'':5A,10B ''curious'':28B ''east'':36B ''eclect'':23B ''enter'':42B ''enthusiast'':55B ''explor'':48B ''gray'':44B ''home'':15B ''hous'':3A,8B,31B ''interior'':51B ''intrigu'':60B ''item'':61B ''locat'':33B ''museum'':17B ''odditi'':26B ''quarter'':45B ''serv'':11B ''share'':56B ''showcas'':21B ''side'':37B ''singl'':50B ''stori'':57B ''visitor'':46B ''windhelm'':39B ''zone'':52B', 'eastmarch', 'Calixto''s House of Curiosities serves as both the home and museum of Calixto Corrium, showcasing an eclectic collection of oddities and curious artifacts.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bryling''s_house', 'Bryling''s House is a small residence in Solitude, home to Bryling, a Thane of Solitude. The house is located just outside the Blue Palace on the left-hand side, next door to the Bards College.

Bryling spends most of her time at the Blue Palace. Irnskar Ironhand, a Nord warrior, serves as Bryling''s personal protector and also resides in Solitude, ensuring her safety while she holds her position as Thane.', '''also'':63B ''bard'':39B ''blue'':27B,49B ''bryle'':1A,4B,15B,41B,58B ''colleg'':40B ''door'':36B ''ensur'':67B ''hand'':33B ''hold'':72B ''home'':13B ''hous'':3A,6B,21B ''irnskar'':51B ''ironhand'':52B ''left'':32B ''left-hand'':31B ''locat'':23B ''next'':35B ''nord'':54B ''outsid'':25B ''palac'':28B,50B ''person'':60B ''posit'':74B ''protector'':61B ''resid'':10B,64B ''safeti'':69B ''serv'':56B ''side'':34B ''small'':9B ''solitud'':12B,19B,66B ''spend'':42B ''thane'':17B,76B ''time'':46B ''warrior'':55B', 'haafingar', 'Bryling''s House is a small residence in Solitude, home to Bryling, a Thane of Solitude.  You do not know much about Bryling apart from the fact he is the Thane of Solitude.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fur_shoes', 'Fur Shoes have basic protection quality. Their visual design is simple and functional, made of tanned leather and fur for warmth. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''adept'':25B ''basic'':6B ''craft'':28B ''design'':11B ''function'':15B ''fur'':1A,3B,21B ''it.it'':29B ''leather'':19B,35B ''made'':16B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''shoe'':2A,4B ''simpl'':13B ''smith'':26B ''tan'':18B ''tempered/improved'':32B ''use'':34B ''visual'':10B ''warmth'':23B ''workbench'':38B', 'blacksmith', 'Fur Shoes have basic protection quality. Their visual design is simple and functional, made of tanned leather and fur for warmth. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('castle_dour', 'Castle Dour is a large fortress located in Solitude, serving as the headquarters of the Imperial Legion and the residence of the Emperor in Skyrim. The fortress is a significant military and political landmark in the city.

The exterior of Castle Dour is separated from the rest of Solitude by high stone walls, with two main gateways providing access. One gateway is on the southwest side, leading to the Wells District of Solitude, while the other is on the southeast side, granting access to the Avenues District and the Blue Palace. The castle is a vital hub for the Imperial presence in Skyrim, overseeing military operations and strategic affairs within the region.', '''access'':61B,85B ''affair'':111B ''avenu'':88B ''blue'':92B ''castl'':1A,3B,43B,95B ''citi'':39B ''district'':73B,89B ''dour'':2A,4B,44B ''emperor'':25B ''exterior'':41B ''fortress'':8B,29B ''gateway'':59B,63B ''grant'':84B ''headquart'':15B ''high'':53B ''hub'':99B ''imperi'':18B,102B ''landmark'':36B ''larg'':7B ''lead'':69B ''legion'':19B ''locat'':9B ''main'':58B ''militari'':33B,107B ''one'':62B ''oper'':108B ''overse'':106B ''palac'':93B ''polit'':35B ''presenc'':103B ''provid'':60B ''region'':114B ''resid'':22B ''rest'':49B ''separ'':46B ''serv'':12B ''side'':68B,83B ''signific'':32B ''skyrim'':27B,105B ''solitud'':11B,51B,75B ''southeast'':82B ''southwest'':67B ''stone'':54B ''strateg'':110B ''two'':57B ''vital'':98B ''wall'':55B ''well'':72B ''within'':112B', 'haafingar, noble, legion, stormcloak', 'Castle Dour is a large fortress located in Solitude, serving as the headquarters of the Imperial Legion and the residence of the Emperor in Skyrim. The fortress is a significant military and political landmark in the city.
You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('evette_san''s_house', 'Evette San''s House is the home of Evette and Octieve San in Solitude. It is located beside Addvar''s House, opposite the bottom door of Proudspire Manor.

Evette San is a Nord food vendor who operates both a house and a market stall in Solitude, selling her wares to residents and travelers alike. Her husband, Octieve San, is an elderly Breton who resides in Solitude, often found in The Winking Skeever, enjoying the local tavern atmosphere. Their home is a modest but well-located residence in the heart of Solitude''s bustling distri', '''addvar'':23B ''alik'':58B ''atmospher'':81B ''besid'':22B ''bottom'':28B ''breton'':66B ''bustl'':98B ''distri'':99B ''door'':29B ''elder'':65B ''enjoy'':77B ''evett'':1A,5B,13B,33B ''food'':38B ''found'':72B ''heart'':94B ''home'':11B,83B ''hous'':4A,8B,25B,44B ''husband'':60B ''local'':79B ''locat'':21B,90B ''manor'':32B ''market'':47B ''modest'':86B ''nord'':37B ''octiev'':15B,61B ''often'':71B ''oper'':41B ''opposit'':26B ''proudspir'':31B ''resid'':55B,68B,91B ''san'':2A,6B,16B,34B,62B ''sell'':51B ''skeever'':76B ''solitud'':18B,50B,70B,96B ''stall'':48B ''tavern'':80B ''travel'':57B ''vendor'':39B ''ware'':53B ''well'':89B ''well-loc'':88B ''wink'':75B', 'haafingar', 'Evette San''s House is the home of Evette San in Solitude. You do not know anything else about Evette.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pearlfish', 'Pearlfish are large pearly coloured fish found in temperate lakes and streams when it is raining. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Restore Stamina, Resist Frost, Fortify Smithing, Fortify One-handed.', '''colour'':6B ''effect'':28B ''fish'':7B ''fortifi'':35B,37B ''found'':8B ''frost'':34B ''hand'':40B ''ingredi'':22B ''lake'':11B ''larg'':4B ''make'':25B ''offer'':27B ''one'':39B ''one-hand'':38B ''pear'':5B ''pearlfish'':1A,2B ''potion'':24B ''rain'':17B ''resist'':33B ''restor'':31B ''smith'':36B ''stamina'':32B ''stream'':13B ''temper'':10B ''use'':19B', 'fisher', 'Pearlfish are large pearly coloured fish. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thalmor_headquarters', 'Thalmor Headquarters is a building located within the walls of Castle Dour in Solitude, Haafingar. The entrance is accessed via a long straight flight of stairs that lead up from the courtyard in Castle Dour.

Despite its name, the building is notably devoid of Thalmor personnel or anyone else, giving it an eerie, abandoned feel. It seems to have been left suddenly, adding an air of mystery surrounding its purpose and the circumstances of its abandonment. The empty headquarters stands in stark contrast to the bustling political and military presence elsewhere in Castle Dour.', '''abandon'':56B,78B ''access'':21B ''ad'':65B ''air'':67B ''anyon'':50B ''build'':7B,42B ''bustl'':88B ''castl'':13B,36B,95B ''circumst'':75B ''contrast'':85B ''courtyard'':34B ''despit'':38B ''devoid'':45B ''dour'':14B,37B,96B ''eeri'':55B ''els'':51B ''elsewher'':93B ''empti'':80B ''entranc'':19B ''feel'':57B ''flight'':26B ''give'':52B ''haafingar'':17B ''headquart'':2A,4B,81B ''lead'':30B ''left'':63B ''locat'':8B ''long'':24B ''militari'':91B ''mysteri'':69B ''name'':40B ''notabl'':44B ''personnel'':48B ''polit'':89B ''presenc'':92B ''purpos'':72B ''seem'':59B ''solitud'':16B ''stair'':28B ''stand'':82B ''stark'':84B ''straight'':25B ''sudden'':64B ''surround'':70B ''thalmor'':1A,3B,47B ''via'':22B ''wall'':11B ''within'':9B', 'haafingar, thalmor, legion', 'Thalmor Headquarters is a building located within the walls of Castle Dour in Solitude, Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('haelga''s_bunkhouse', 'Haelga''s Bunkhouse is a boarding house located in Riften, operated by Haelga. It serves as a residence for several of Riften''s citizens, providing a place to stay for those seeking shelter in the city. The bunkhouse is the first building on the right when entering Riften through the main northern gate.', '''board'':9B ''build'':45B ''bunkhous'':3A,6B,41B ''citi'':39B ''citizen'':27B ''enter'':50B ''first'':44B ''gate'':56B ''haelga'':1A,4B,16B ''hous'':10B ''locat'':11B ''main'':54B ''northern'':55B ''oper'':14B ''place'':30B ''provid'':28B ''resid'':21B ''riften'':13B,25B,51B ''right'':48B ''seek'':35B ''serv'':18B ''sever'':23B ''shelter'':36B ''stay'':32B', 'rift', 'Haelga''s Bunkhouse is a boarding house located in Riften, operated by Haelga.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_pale', 'The Pale is a hold in northern Skyrim, with its capital in Dawnstar. It is aligned with the Stormcloaks. 

The Pale is a sparsely populated region, known for its harsh, snow-covered terrain and limited safe havens for travelers. The unforgiving landscape is largely unsuitable for farming, though the far southern edges, where the mountains give way to more hospitable terrain, offer better conditions. The hold''s largest lake, Lake Yorgrim, lies to the south, feeding the River Yorgrim. One of three entrances to Blackreach can be found in Raldbthar, a Dwarven ruin located south of the lake.

Despite its challenging climate, the Pale is rich in natural resources. Snowberries thrive in the snowy environment, while sturdy blue and purple mountain flowers can be found in the region. Along the coastline, Nordic barnacles, clams, and spiky grass are abundant. The hold''s wildlife includes giants, sabre cats, wolves, ice wraiths, trolls, and frostbite spiders, making it a rugged and dangerous region. Brina Merilis serves as the Jarl of the Pale, overseeing the hold from Dawnstar.', '''abund'':142B ''align'':18B ''along'':132B ''barnacl'':136B ''better'':66B ''blackreach'':88B ''blue'':121B ''brina'':165B ''capit'':13B ''cat'':150B ''challeng'':104B ''clam'':137B ''climat'':105B ''coastlin'':134B ''condit'':67B ''cover'':35B ''danger'':163B ''dawnstar'':15B,178B ''despit'':102B ''dwarven'':95B ''edg'':55B ''entranc'':86B ''environ'':118B ''far'':53B ''farm'':50B ''feed'':79B ''flower'':125B ''found'':91B,128B ''frostbit'':156B ''giant'':148B ''give'':59B ''grass'':140B ''harsh'':32B ''haven'':40B ''hold'':7B,69B,144B,176B ''hospit'':63B ''ice'':152B ''includ'':147B ''jarl'':170B ''known'':29B ''lake'':72B,73B,101B ''landscap'':45B ''larg'':47B ''largest'':71B ''lie'':75B ''limit'':38B ''locat'':97B ''make'':158B ''merili'':166B ''mountain'':58B,124B ''natur'':111B ''nordic'':135B ''northern'':9B ''offer'':65B ''one'':83B ''overse'':174B ''pale'':2A,4B,23B,107B,173B ''popul'':27B ''purpl'':123B ''raldbthar'':93B ''region'':28B,131B,164B ''resourc'':112B ''rich'':109B ''river'':81B ''rug'':161B ''ruin'':96B ''sabr'':149B ''safe'':39B ''serv'':167B ''skyrim'':10B ''snow'':34B ''snow-cov'':33B ''snowberri'':113B ''snowi'':117B ''south'':78B,98B ''southern'':54B ''spars'':26B ''spider'':157B ''spiki'':139B ''stormcloak'':21B ''sturdi'':120B ''terrain'':36B,64B ''though'':51B ''three'':85B ''thrive'':114B ''travel'':42B ''troll'':154B ''unforgiv'':44B ''unsuit'':48B ''way'':60B ''wildlif'':146B ''wolv'':151B ''wraith'':153B ''yorgrim'':74B,82B', 'pale, scholar, noble', 'The Pale is a hold in northern Skyrim, with its capital in Dawnstar. It is aligned with the Stormcloaks. 

The Pale is a sparsely populated region, known for its harsh, snow-covered terrain and limited safe havens for travelers. The unforgiving landscape is largely unsuitable for farming, though the far southern edges, where the mountains give way to more hospitable terrain, offer better conditions. The hold''s largest lake, Lake Yorgrim, lies to the south, feeding the River Yorgrim. One of three entrances to Blackreach can be found in Raldbthar, a Dwarven ruin located south of the lake.', '', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hall_of_the_vigilant', 'The Hall of the Vigilant is a secluded lodge located south-southwest of Dawnstar and northwest of Fort Dunstad in The Pale. It serves as the headquarters for the Vigilants of Stendarr, a group dedicated to hunting Daedra and other malevolent forces in Skyrim.

The lodge is led by Keeper Carcette, who provides expert training in Restoration magic to those seeking to improve their healing abilities. The Hall of the Vigilant is a refuge for the Vigilants, offering a safe haven for their mission to protect Skyrim from supernatural threats.', '''abil'':71B ''carcett'':56B ''daedra'':43B ''dawnstar'':19B ''dedic'':40B ''dunstad'':24B ''expert'':59B ''forc'':47B ''fort'':23B ''group'':39B ''hall'':1A,6B,73B ''haven'':86B ''headquart'':32B ''heal'':70B ''hunt'':42B ''improv'':68B ''keeper'':55B ''led'':53B ''locat'':14B ''lodg'':13B,51B ''magic'':63B ''malevol'':46B ''mission'':89B ''northwest'':21B ''offer'':83B ''pale'':27B ''protect'':91B ''provid'':58B ''refug'':79B ''restor'':62B ''safe'':85B ''seclud'':12B ''seek'':66B ''serv'':29B ''skyrim'':49B,92B ''south'':16B ''south-southwest'':15B ''southwest'':17B ''stendarr'':37B ''supernatur'':94B ''threat'':95B ''train'':60B ''vigil'':4A,9B,35B,76B,82B', 'pale, dawnguard, volkihar', 'The Hall of the Vigilant is a secluded lodge located south-southwest of Dawnstar in The Pale. It serves as the headquarters for the Vigilants of Stendarr, a group dedicated to hunting Daedra and other malevolent forces in Skyrim. You do not know who is in charge of the hall/You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pale_imperial_camp', 'Pale Imperial Camp is an Imperial military encampment located in The Pale, west of Dawnstar and northwest of Mzinchaleft. It serves as a strategic base for the Imperial Legion during their efforts in the Skyrim civil war.

The camp is typically under the command of Legate Constantius Tituleius.', '''base'':28B ''camp'':3A,6B,42B ''civil'':39B ''command'':47B ''constantius'':50B ''dawnstar'':18B ''effort'':35B ''encamp'':11B ''imperi'':2A,5B,9B,31B ''legat'':49B ''legion'':32B ''locat'':12B ''militari'':10B ''mzinchaleft'':22B ''northwest'':20B ''pale'':1A,4B,15B ''serv'':24B ''skyrim'':38B ''strateg'':27B ''tituleius'':51B ''typic'':44B ''war'':40B ''west'':16B', 'pale, legion', 'Pale Imperial Camp is an Imperial military encampment located in The Pale, west of Dawnstar.

You do not know who is in charge of the camp/You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('harmony', 'Harmony is an Illusion spell that pacifies all nearby creatures and people, making them stop fighting and become neutral toward the caster. It requires a Master skill level to cast.', '''becom'':19B ''cast'':31B ''caster'':23B ''creatur'':11B ''fight'':17B ''harmoni'':1A,2B ''illus'':5B ''level'':29B ''make'':14B ''master'':27B ''nearbi'':10B ''neutral'':20B ''pacifi'':8B ''peopl'':13B ''requir'':25B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':6B ''stop'':16B ''toward'':21B', 'mage', '
Harmony is a spell that pacifies all nearby creatures and people, making them stop fighting and become neutral toward the caster. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('red_road_pass', 'Red Road Pass is a giant camp located south-southwest of Dawnstar and north of the Hall of the Vigilant in The Pale. The camp is inhabited by giants and features the typical elements of a giant encampment, such as mammoth bones and a cooking fire.', '''bone'':46B ''camp'':10B,29B ''cook'':49B ''dawnstar'':16B ''element'':38B ''encamp'':42B ''featur'':35B ''fire'':50B ''giant'':9B,33B,41B ''hall'':21B ''inhabit'':31B ''locat'':11B ''mammoth'':45B ''north'':18B ''pale'':27B ''pass'':3A,6B ''red'':1A,4B ''road'':2A,5B ''south'':13B ''south-southwest'':12B ''southwest'':14B ''typic'':37B ''vigil'':24B', 'pale', 'Red Road Pass is a giant camp located south-southwest of Dawnstar and north of the Hall of the Vigilant in The Pale. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('northwatch_keep', 'Northwatch Keep is a small fort located northwest of Dragon Bridge and north of Rimerock Burrow in Haafingar. The fort is occupied by the Thalmor and serves as a prison, off-limits to anyone not authorized by the Thalmor.', '''anyon'':37B ''author'':39B ''bridg'':13B ''burrow'':18B ''dragon'':12B ''fort'':8B,22B ''haafingar'':20B ''keep'':2A,4B ''limit'':35B ''locat'':9B ''north'':15B ''northwatch'':1A,3B ''northwest'':10B ''occupi'':24B ''off-limit'':33B ''prison'':32B ''rimerock'':17B ''serv'':29B ''small'':7B ''thalmor'':27B,42B', 'haafingar, thalmor', 'Northwatch Keep is a small fort located northwest of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rustleif''s_house', 'Rustleif''s House is a smithy located near the shoreline of Dawnstar, facing the bay. It serves as both the home and workshop of Rustleif, a renowned weaponsmith known for crafting arms and armor for the jarl''s men. His skill and reputation make him an important figure in the town''s economy and defense.

Rustleif is assisted by his Redguard wife, Seren, who is pregnant and plays an active role in the business. Both Rustleif and Seren offer merchant services, providing weapons, armor, and crafting supplies to adventurers and locals alike. ', '''activ'':73B ''adventur'':92B ''alik'':95B ''arm'':35B ''armor'':37B,87B ''assist'':61B ''bay'':18B ''busi'':77B ''craft'':34B,89B ''dawnstar'':15B ''defens'':58B ''economi'':56B ''face'':16B ''figur'':51B ''home'':24B ''hous'':3A,6B ''import'':50B ''jarl'':40B ''known'':32B ''local'':94B ''locat'':10B ''make'':47B ''men'':42B ''merchant'':83B ''near'':11B ''offer'':82B ''play'':71B ''pregnant'':69B ''provid'':85B ''redguard'':64B ''renown'':30B ''reput'':46B ''role'':74B ''rustleif'':1A,4B,28B,59B,79B ''seren'':66B,81B ''serv'':20B ''servic'':84B ''shorelin'':13B ''skill'':44B ''smithi'':9B ''suppli'':90B ''town'':54B ''weapon'':86B ''weaponsmith'':31B ''wife'':65B ''workshop'':26B', 'pale', 'Rustleif''s House is a building located in Dawnstar. You do not know who Rustleif is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nightcaller_temple', 'Nightcaller Temple is a small fort perched on a clifftop overlooking Dawnstar, located east of the town in The Pale. Known to some locals as the Tower of Dawn, the temple is a ruin within a ruin—originally a military fort, it was later abandoned and eventually occupied by worshippers of the Daedric Prince Vaermina.

The temple''s history is marked by a violent conflict. When the Daedric devotees began using the Skull of Corruption, its dark influence caused terrible nightmares among a nearby Orc war party. The Orcs attacked the temple, determined to destroy the artifact. In a desperate bid to protect the Skull, the worshippers released the Miasma, a gas that put everyone within the temple into a deep sleep, leaving the structure abandoned once more.', '''abandon'':46B,127B ''among'':83B ''artifact'':98B ''attack'':91B ''began'':71B ''bid'':102B ''caus'':80B ''clifftop'':12B ''conflict'':66B ''corrupt'':76B ''daedric'':54B,69B ''dark'':78B ''dawn'':31B ''dawnstar'':14B ''deep'':122B ''desper'':101B ''destroy'':96B ''determin'':94B ''devote'':70B ''east'':16B ''eventu'':48B ''everyon'':116B ''fort'':8B,42B ''gas'':113B ''histori'':60B ''influenc'':79B ''known'':23B ''later'':45B ''leav'':124B ''local'':26B ''locat'':15B ''mark'':62B ''miasma'':111B ''militari'':41B ''nearbi'':85B ''nightcal'':1A,3B ''nightmar'':82B ''occupi'':49B ''orc'':86B,90B ''overlook'':13B ''pale'':22B ''parti'':88B ''perch'':9B ''princ'':55B ''protect'':104B ''put'':115B ''releas'':109B ''ruin'':36B ''ruin—origin'':39B ''skull'':74B,106B ''sleep'':123B ''small'':7B ''structur'':126B ''templ'':2A,4B,33B,58B,93B,119B ''terribl'':81B ''tower'':29B ''town'':19B ''use'':72B ''vaermina'':56B ''violent'':65B ''war'':87B ''within'':37B,117B ''worshipp'':51B,108B', 'daedra, daedric, erandur', 'Nightcaller Temple is a small fort perched on a clifftop overlooking Dawnstar, located east of the town in The Pale.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'pale', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('high_gate_ruins', 'High Gate Ruins is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located west of Dawnstar and east of the Wreck of the Icerunner in The Pale. The ruins are inhabited by draugr.', '''dawnstar'':17B ''draugr'':34B ''east'':19B ''gate'':2A,5B ''high'':1A,4B ''icerunn'':25B ''inhabit'':32B ''locat'':14B ''medium'':10B ''medium-s'':9B ''nordic'':12B ''pale'':28B ''ruin'':3A,6B,13B,30B ''size'':11B ''west'':15B ''wreck'':22B', 'pale', 'High Gate Ruins is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located west of Dawnstar in The Pale. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fellglow_keep', 'Fellglow Keep is a medium-sized, crumbling fortress located east-northeast of Whiterun and northwest of Valtheim Towers, nestled amidst the rugged terrain of Whiterun Hold. It is rumoured that the keep has been overtaken by warlocks who conduct dark rituals within its walls.', '''amidst'':24B ''conduct'':43B ''crumbl'':10B ''dark'':44B ''east'':14B ''east-northeast'':13B ''fellglow'':1A,3B ''fortress'':11B ''hold'':30B ''keep'':2A,4B,36B ''locat'':12B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''nestl'':23B ''northeast'':15B ''northwest'':19B ''overtaken'':39B ''ritual'':45B ''rug'':26B ''rumour'':33B ''size'':9B ''terrain'':27B ''tower'':22B ''valtheim'':21B ''wall'':48B ''warlock'':41B ''whiterun'':17B,29B ''within'':46B', 'whiterun, legion, stormcloak', 'Fellglow Keep is a medium-sized, crumbling fortress located east-northeast of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('satakal', 'Satakal, the Worldskin, is the Yokudan god of creation, destruction, and the endless cycles of existence. Known as the First Serpent, Satakal embodies the fusion of Anu and Padomay, symbolizing both chaos and order. In Yokudan mythology, Satakal devours entire worlds, shedding its skin to birth new ones, a process that has occurred countless times. This eternal cycle inspired the birth of spirits like Ruptga, the first to learn how to survive these transitions, who later formed the Yokudan pantheon. Satakal''s cycles echo the Redguard understanding of mortality and the longing for the Far Shores, the ultimate spiritual haven they believe lies beyond the reach of mortal life.

Worship of Satakal is prevalent among Redguard nomads of the Alik''r Desert, where the deity is revered as both destroyer and creator. Rituals dedicated to Satakal often involve symbolic "shedding of skin," and its devotees weave the serpent into their maps and lives as a reminder of the god''s dominion over all. Some groups, such as the Pyre Watch and Hunding’s sword-singers, interpret Satakal''s influence as a call to cast aside fixed destinies in pursuit of transcendence. Satakal’s worship is deeply rooted in Redguard culture, influencing not only their spiritual practices but also their myths, oaths, and settlements, such as the city of Satakalaam. Despite Satakal''s profound role in their heritage, his followers have often clashed with more modern Imperial beliefs, reflecting the tension between the god''s timeless cycles and the structured order of the Eight Divines.', '''alik'':121B ''also'':208B ''among'':116B ''anu'':28B ''asid'':186B ''belief'':237B ''believ'':103B ''beyond'':105B ''birth'':47B,62B ''call'':183B ''cast'':185B ''chao'':33B ''citi'':217B ''clash'':232B ''countless'':55B ''creation'':10B ''creator'':133B ''cultur'':200B ''cycl'':15B,59B,84B,246B ''dedic'':135B ''deepli'':196B ''deiti'':126B ''desert'':123B ''despit'':220B ''destini'':188B ''destroy'':131B ''destruct'':11B ''devote'':146B ''devour'':40B ''divin'':254B ''dominion'':162B ''echo'':85B ''eight'':253B ''embodi'':24B ''endless'':14B ''entir'':41B ''etern'':58B ''exist'':17B ''far'':96B ''first'':21B,68B ''fix'':187B ''follow'':229B ''form'':78B ''fusion'':26B ''god'':8B,160B,243B ''group'':166B ''haven'':101B ''heritag'':227B ''hunding’'':173B ''imperi'':236B ''influenc'':180B,201B ''inspir'':60B ''interpret'':177B ''involv'':139B ''known'':18B ''later'':77B ''learn'':70B ''lie'':104B ''life'':110B ''like'':65B ''live'':154B ''long'':93B ''map'':152B ''modern'':235B ''mortal'':90B,109B ''myth'':210B ''mytholog'':38B ''new'':48B ''nomad'':118B ''oath'':211B ''occur'':54B ''often'':138B,231B ''one'':49B ''order'':35B,250B ''padomay'':30B ''pantheon'':81B ''practic'':206B ''preval'':115B ''process'':51B ''profound'':223B ''pursuit'':190B ''pyre'':170B ''r'':122B ''reach'':107B ''redguard'':87B,117B,199B ''reflect'':238B ''remind'':157B ''rever'':128B ''ritual'':134B ''role'':224B ''root'':197B ''ruptga'':66B ''satak'':1A,2B,23B,39B,82B,113B,137B,178B,221B ''satakalaam'':219B ''satakal’'':193B ''serpent'':22B,149B ''settlement'':213B ''shed'':43B,141B ''shore'':97B ''singer'':176B ''skin'':45B,143B ''spirit'':64B ''spiritu'':100B,205B ''structur'':249B ''surviv'':73B ''sword'':175B ''sword-sing'':174B ''symbol'':31B,140B ''tension'':240B ''time'':56B ''timeless'':245B ''transcend'':192B ''transit'':75B ''ultim'':99B ''understand'':88B ''watch'':171B ''weav'':147B ''world'':42B ''worldskin'':4B ''worship'':111B,194B ''yokudan'':7B,37B,80B', 'redguard, scholar', 'Satakal, the Worldskin, is the Yokudan god of creation, destruction, and the eternal cycles of existence. Known as the First Serpent, Satakal represents the fusion of Anu and Padomay, symbolizing both chaos and order. In Yokudan mythology, Satakal devours worlds, shedding its skin to give birth to new ones. Worshiped by Redguard nomads in the Alik''r Desert, Satakal''s followers practice rituals of "shedding skin" as a symbol of transcendence. His influence extends to the city of Satakalaam and traditions like those of the Pyre Watch and Hunding’s sword-singers. Despite its profound impact on Redguard culture, Satakal’s worship often conflicts with Imperial beliefs, reflecting the tension between eternal cycles and structured order.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('loreius_farm', 'Loreius Farm is a small farm located in The Pale, north of Whitewatch Tower and south of Blizzard Rest. The farm is home to Vantus Loreius and his wife, Curwe.', '''blizzard'':20B ''curw'':32B ''farm'':2A,4B,8B,23B ''home'':25B ''locat'':9B ''loreius'':1A,3B,28B ''north'':13B ''pale'':12B ''rest'':21B ''small'':7B ''south'':18B ''tower'':16B ''vantus'':27B ''whitewatch'':15B ''wife'':31B', 'pale', 'Loreius Farm is a small farm located in The Pale, north of Whitewatch Tower. You do not know who Loreius is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('irkngthand', 'Irkngthand is a large Dwarven ruin located west of Windhelm and northwest of Raldbthar in The Pale. The ruin is initially occupied by bandits.

The entrance to Irkngthand can be reached by following a dirt path south from Nightgate Inn. When the path diverges, take the eastern route, as the southwest branch leads to Tumble Arch Pass. Alternatively, the entrance can be accessed by descending the mountain from the south and navigating a series of wooden bridges leading up to the ruin.', '''access'':64B ''altern'':59B ''arch'':57B ''bandit'':25B ''branch'':53B ''bridg'':78B ''descend'':66B ''dirt'':36B ''diverg'':45B ''dwarven'':6B ''eastern'':48B ''entranc'':27B,61B ''follow'':34B ''initi'':22B ''inn'':41B ''irkngthand'':1A,2B,29B ''larg'':5B ''lead'':54B,79B ''locat'':8B ''mountain'':68B ''navig'':73B ''nightgat'':40B ''northwest'':13B ''occupi'':23B ''pale'':18B ''pass'':58B ''path'':37B,44B ''raldbthar'':15B ''reach'':32B ''rout'':49B ''ruin'':7B,20B,83B ''seri'':75B ''south'':38B,71B ''southwest'':52B ''take'':46B ''tumbl'':56B ''west'':9B ''windhelm'':11B ''wooden'':77B', 'pale, dwemer', 'Irkngthand is a large Dwarven ruin located west of Windhelm in The Pale.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sanuarach_mine', 'Sanuarach Mine is a small silver mine located in northern Karthwasten in the Reach. It is occupied by Silver-Blood mercenaries attempting to take control of the mine.

The mine, along with the settlement of Karthwasten and its other mine, Fenn''s Gulch Mine, is owned by Ainethach, one of the few non-Nord landowners in the Reach', '''ainethach'':51B ''along'':34B ''attempt'':25B ''blood'':23B ''control'':28B ''fenn'':44B ''gulch'':46B ''karthwasten'':13B,39B ''landown'':59B ''locat'':10B ''mercenari'':24B ''mine'':2A,4B,9B,31B,33B,43B,47B ''non'':57B ''non-nord'':56B ''nord'':58B ''northern'':12B ''occupi'':19B ''one'':52B ''own'':49B ''reach'':16B,62B ''sanuarach'':1A,3B ''settlement'':37B ''silver'':8B,22B ''silver-blood'':21B ''small'':7B ''take'':27B', 'reach', 'Sanuarach Mine is a small silver mine located in northern Karthwasten in the Reach. You do not know anyone at the mine.
You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('silus_vesuius''s_house', 'Silus Vesuius''s House is a residence in Dawnstar that doubles as a museum dedicated to the Mythic Dawn, a secretive cult infamous for worshipping the Daedric Prince of Destruction, Mehrunes Dagon. The Mythic Dawn, led by Mankar Camoran, orchestrated the assassination of Emperor Uriel Septim VII and his heirs in 3E 433, a plot that triggered the Oblivion Crisis and the end of the Third Era.

Silus''s museum preserves artifacts and history from this dark chapter of Tamriel''s past, offering visitors a chance to learn about the Mythic Dawn''s deeds and their catastrophic legacy. It is a controversial location due to the subject matter. ', '''3e'':56B ''433'':57B ''artifact'':76B ''assassin'':46B ''camoran'':43B ''catastroph'':101B ''chanc'':90B ''chapter'':82B ''controversi'':106B ''crisi'':64B ''cult'':26B ''daedric'':31B ''dagon'':36B ''dark'':81B ''dawn'':23B,39B,96B ''dawnstar'':13B ''dedic'':19B ''deed'':98B ''destruct'':34B ''doubl'':15B ''due'':108B ''emperor'':48B ''end'':67B ''era'':71B ''heir'':54B ''histori'':78B ''hous'':4A,8B ''infam'':27B ''learn'':92B ''led'':40B ''legaci'':102B ''locat'':107B ''mankar'':42B ''matter'':112B ''mehrun'':35B ''museum'':18B,74B ''mythic'':22B,38B,95B ''oblivion'':63B ''offer'':87B ''orchestr'':44B ''past'':86B ''plot'':59B ''preserv'':75B ''princ'':32B ''resid'':11B ''secret'':25B ''septim'':50B ''silus'':1A,5B,72B ''subject'':111B ''tamriel'':84B ''third'':70B ''trigger'':61B ''uriel'':49B ''vesuius'':2A,6B ''vii'':51B ''visitor'':88B ''worship'':29B', 'pale', 'Silus Vesuius''s House is a residence in Dawnstar that doubles as a museum dedicated to the Mythic Dawn, a secretive cult infamous for worshipping the Daedric Prince of Destruction, Mehrunes Dagon. The Mythic Dawn, led by Mankar Camoran, orchestrated the assassination of Emperor Uriel Septim VII and his heirs in 3E 433, a plot that triggered the Oblivion Crisis and the end of the Third Era.

Silus''s museum preserves artifacts and history from this dark chapter of Tamriel''s past, offering visitors a chance to learn about the Mythic Dawn''s deeds and their catastrophic legacy. It is a controversial location due to the subject matter. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_white_hall', 'The White Hall is a prominent two-story structure located on a hillside overlooking Dawnstar. Positioned next to the Dawnstar Barracks, it serves as the seat of power for the Jarl of the Pale and their court. The hall is home to Jarl Skald, the ruler of the Pale, along with key members of his court, including Madena, the court wizard; Jod, the housecarl; Frorkmar Banner-Torn, the military advisor; and Bulfrek, the servant. The White Hall is central to the governance of the Pale, reflecting both its importance and the modest nature of its northern setting.', '''advisor'':75B ''along'':54B ''banner'':71B ''banner-torn'':70B ''barrack'':25B ''bulfrek'':77B ''central'':84B ''court'':41B,60B,64B ''dawnstar'':19B,24B ''frorkmar'':69B ''govern'':87B ''hall'':3A,6B,43B,82B ''hillsid'':17B ''home'':45B ''housecarl'':68B ''import'':94B ''includ'':61B ''jarl'':35B,47B ''jod'':66B ''key'':56B ''locat'':14B ''madena'':62B ''member'':57B ''militari'':74B ''modest'':97B ''natur'':98B ''next'':21B ''northern'':101B ''overlook'':18B ''pale'':38B,53B,90B ''posit'':20B ''power'':32B ''promin'':9B ''reflect'':91B ''ruler'':50B ''seat'':30B ''serv'':27B ''servant'':79B ''set'':102B ''skald'':48B ''stori'':12B ''structur'':13B ''torn'':72B ''two'':11B ''two-stori'':10B ''white'':2A,5B,81B ''wizard'':65B', 'pale, noble', 'The White Hall is a prominent structure in Dawnstar. It serves as the seat of power for the Jarl of the Pale and their court. The hall is home to Jarl Skald, the ruler of the Pale. You do now know anyone else who works here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('karthspire_camp', 'Karthspire is a large Forsworn camp and cave located east of Markarth and northwest of Old Hroldan Inn in the Reach. The Karthspire, and serves as a significant base for the Forsworn. Situated in a strikingly rugged landscape, Karthspire features both open camp areas and natural cave passages, blending Forsworn structures with the surrounding terrain. It is rumored that some hidden temple is somewhere in the mountainside of Karthspire.', '''area'':46B ''base'':31B ''blend'':51B ''camp'':2A,8B,45B ''cave'':10B,49B ''east'':12B ''featur'':42B ''forsworn'':7B,34B,52B ''hidden'':63B ''hroldan'':19B ''inn'':20B ''karthspir'':1A,3B,25B,41B,71B ''landscap'':40B ''larg'':6B ''locat'':11B ''markarth'':14B ''mountainsid'':69B ''natur'':48B ''northwest'':16B ''old'':18B ''open'':44B ''passag'':50B ''reach'':23B ''rug'':39B ''rumor'':60B ''serv'':27B ''signific'':30B ''situat'':35B ''somewher'':66B ''strike'':38B ''structur'':53B ''surround'':56B ''templ'':64B ''terrain'':57B', 'reach', 'Karthspire is a large Forsworn camp and cave located east of Markarth in the Reach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bleakwind_bluff', 'Bleakwind Bluff is a small, ruined Nordic tower located northwest of Rorikstead in the Reach. Perched on an outcrop of rock, it is inhabited by hagravens and Forsworn, making it a dangerous site for unwary travelers.

The tower is accessed via a winding path marked by a pile of rocks on the north side of the main route connecting Old Hroldan Inn with Rorikstead. The path loops around a large rock, doubles back on itself, and ascends several flights of stairs that circle the outcrop, eventually leading to the tower.', '''access'':42B ''around'':70B ''ascend'':79B ''back'':75B ''bleakwind'':1A,3B ''bluff'':2A,4B ''circl'':85B ''connect'':61B ''danger'':34B ''doubl'':74B ''eventu'':88B ''flight'':81B ''forsworn'':30B ''hagraven'':28B ''hroldan'':63B ''inhabit'':26B ''inn'':64B ''larg'':72B ''lead'':89B ''locat'':11B ''loop'':69B ''main'':59B ''make'':31B ''mark'':47B ''nordic'':9B ''north'':55B ''northwest'':12B ''old'':62B ''outcrop'':21B,87B ''path'':46B,68B ''perch'':18B ''pile'':50B ''reach'':17B ''rock'':23B,52B,73B ''rorikstead'':14B,66B ''rout'':60B ''ruin'':8B ''sever'':80B ''side'':56B ''site'':35B ''small'':7B ''stair'':83B ''tower'':10B,40B,92B ''travel'':38B ''unwari'':37B ''via'':43B ''wind'':45B', 'reach', 'Bleakwind Bluff is a small, ruined Nordic tower located northwest of Rorikstead in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_reach', 'The Reach is a mountainous hold in western Skyrim, with its capital, Markarth, nestled in the southwestern corner of the region. It is aligned with the Imperial Legion. The hold is dominated by the rugged Druadach Mountains, while its eastern edge, stretching from Broken Tower Redoubt to Fort Sungard, is characterized by hilly terrain. The Karth River originates in the southern mountains, carving the dramatic Karth River Canyon as it flows through the hold.

Markarth, a former Dwemer city, rises from the living rock of the Druadach Mountains, reflecting the ancient ingenuity of its creators. The Reach is also home to smaller settlements such as Karthwasten and Old Hroldan, as well as the  Orc stronghold Dushnikh Yal in the southern steppes. The region is populated by the native Reachmen, who form the majority in many settlements, and the Forsworn, a militant faction that fiercely guards their independence, attacking outsiders on sight.

Flora in the Reach includes juniper berry bushes, hanging moss, mora tapinella, and scattered mountain flowers, with greater concentrations in the northeast. Its fauna is equally rugged, with bears, sabre cats, and other predators roaming its hills and valleys.', '''align'':26B ''also'':101B ''ancient'':93B ''attack'':150B ''bear'':182B ''berri'':160B ''broken'':46B ''bush'':161B ''canyon'':70B ''capit'':14B ''carv'':65B ''cat'':184B ''character'':53B ''citi'':81B ''concentr'':172B ''corner'':20B ''creator'':97B ''domin'':34B ''dramat'':67B ''druadach'':38B,89B ''dushnikh'':118B ''dwemer'':80B ''eastern'':42B ''edg'':43B ''equal'':179B ''faction'':144B ''fauna'':177B ''fierc'':146B ''flora'':154B ''flow'':73B ''flower'':169B ''form'':133B ''former'':79B ''forsworn'':141B ''fort'':50B ''greater'':171B ''guard'':147B ''hang'':162B ''hill'':190B ''hilli'':55B ''hold'':8B,32B,76B ''home'':102B ''hroldan'':111B ''imperi'':29B ''includ'':158B ''independ'':149B ''ingenu'':94B ''junip'':159B ''karth'':58B,68B ''karthwasten'':108B ''legion'':30B ''live'':85B ''major'':135B ''mani'':137B ''markarth'':15B,77B ''milit'':143B ''mora'':164B ''moss'':163B ''mountain'':7B,39B,64B,90B,168B ''nativ'':130B ''nestl'':16B ''northeast'':175B ''old'':110B ''orc'':116B ''origin'':60B ''outsid'':151B ''popul'':127B ''predat'':187B ''reach'':2A,4B,99B,157B ''reachmen'':131B ''redoubt'':48B ''reflect'':91B ''region'':23B,125B ''rise'':82B ''river'':59B,69B ''roam'':188B ''rock'':86B ''rug'':37B,180B ''sabr'':183B ''scatter'':167B ''settlement'':105B,138B ''sight'':153B ''skyrim'':11B ''smaller'':104B ''southern'':63B,122B ''southwestern'':19B ''stepp'':123B ''stretch'':44B ''stronghold'':117B ''sungard'':51B ''tapinella'':165B ''terrain'':56B ''tower'':47B ''valley'':192B ''well'':113B ''western'':10B ''yal'':119B', 'reach, noble, scholar', 'The Reach is a mountainous hold in western Skyrim, with its capital, Markarth, nestled in the southwestern corner of the region. It is aligned with the I