The current Jarl is Igmund. You do not know anyone else or lives here.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sanguine', 'Sanguine is the Daedric Prince of revelry, debauchery, and hedonistic indulgence. Known as the Lord of Revelry, Sanguine embodies excess in all forms, encouraging the pursuit of pleasure, lust, and wild abandon. He is commonly depicted as a portly, crimson-skinned figure with a mischievous grin, often holding a bottle or surrounded by indulgences. His sphere encompasses not only drunken revelry and wild orgies but also the darker aspects of human desire, such as perversion and excess. Sanguine''s influence is most evident in the Myriad Realms of Revelry, small chaotic realms dedicated to endless pleasure, where mortals often become trapped, lured by indulgence.

Despite his carefree demeanor, Sanguine''s worship can have dangerous consequences. His followers, ranging from party-goers to secret cults, revel in excess, sometimes to the point of destruction or death. Celebrations in his name can be found across Tamriel, from Khajiiti midnight rites to Imperial festivals, where indulgence in drink, dance, and flesh is seen as acts of devotion. His most famous artifact, the Sanguine Rose, allows its wielder to summon a Daedra to cause havoc. Though Sanguine appears less malicious compared to other Daedric Princes, his power lies in seduction and indulgence, tempting mortals to abandon restraint for a life of dangerous pleasure.', '''abandon'':33B,205B ''across'':146B ''act'':165B ''allow'':175B ''also'':68B ''appear'':187B ''artifact'':171B ''aspect'':71B ''becom'':102B ''bottl'':52B ''carefre'':109B ''caus'':183B ''celebr'':139B ''chaotic'':93B ''common'':36B ''compar'':190B ''consequ'':117B ''crimson'':42B ''crimson-skin'':41B ''cult'':127B ''daedra'':181B ''daedric'':5B,193B ''danc'':159B ''danger'':116B,211B ''darker'':70B ''death'':138B ''debaucheri'':9B ''dedic'':95B ''demeanor'':110B ''depict'':37B ''desir'':74B ''despit'':107B ''destruct'':136B ''devot'':167B ''drink'':158B ''drunken'':62B ''embodi'':20B ''encompass'':59B ''encourag'':25B ''endless'':97B ''evid'':85B ''excess'':21B,79B,130B ''famous'':170B ''festiv'':154B ''figur'':44B ''flesh'':161B ''follow'':119B ''form'':24B ''found'':145B ''goer'':124B ''grin'':48B ''havoc'':184B ''hedonist'':11B ''hold'':50B ''human'':73B ''imperi'':153B ''indulg'':12B,56B,106B,156B,201B ''influenc'':82B ''khajiiti'':149B ''known'':13B ''less'':188B ''lie'':197B ''life'':209B ''lord'':16B ''lure'':104B ''lust'':30B ''malici'':189B ''midnight'':150B ''mischiev'':47B ''mortal'':100B,203B ''myriad'':88B ''name'':142B ''often'':49B,101B ''orgi'':66B ''parti'':123B ''party-go'':122B ''pervers'':77B ''pleasur'':29B,98B,212B ''point'':134B ''port'':40B ''power'':196B ''princ'':6B,194B ''pursuit'':27B ''rang'':120B ''realm'':89B,94B ''restraint'':206B ''revel'':128B ''revelri'':8B,18B,63B,91B ''rite'':151B ''rose'':174B ''sanguin'':1A,2B,19B,80B,111B,173B,186B ''secret'':126B ''seduct'':199B ''seen'':163B ''skin'':43B ''small'':92B ''sometim'':131B ''sphere'':58B ''summon'':179B ''surround'':54B ''tamriel'':147B ''tempt'':202B ''though'':185B ''trap'':103B ''wielder'':177B ''wild'':32B,65B ''worship'':113B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
Sanguine, the Daedric Prince of revelry and indulgence, embodies excess, pleasure, and wild abandon. Known as the Lord of Revelry, he encourages mortals to pursue hedonistic desires, from drunken celebrations to darker perversions. Depicted as a crimson, portly figure with a mischievous grin, Sanguine rules the Myriad Realms of Revelry, chaotic planes dedicated to endless pleasure that often trap mortals. While his carefree nature may seem less malicious, his influence leads followers to dangerous extremes. Celebrations in his honor, found across Tamriel, range from lively festivals to secretive, hedonistic cults. His notable artifact, the Sanguine Rose, summons Daedra to spread chaos, reflecting his power to seduce mortals into abandoning restraint for destructive indulgence.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('karthwasten', 'Karthwasten is a small mining town located in the Reach, east of the Shrine to Peryite and north of Blind Cliff Cave. The town is notable for being one of the few mining settlements in the Reach not owned by a Nord, with Ainethach, a Reachman, holding ownership of both surrounding silver mines: Sanuarach Mine and Fenn''s Gulch Mine.

The town consists of three buildings: Karthwasten Hall, where Ainethach resides; Enmon''s house, home to Enmon, his wife Mena, and daughter Fjotra; and the miner''s barracks, housing Belchimac, Lash gra-Dushnikh, and Ragnar. Amenities include a tanning rack near Karthwasten Hall and a grindstone on the deck of the miner’s barracks.

Sanuarach Mine, the main silver mine, is located north of Karthwasten Hall, with a smelter and silver ore nearby. Fenn’s Gulch Mine lies at the town’s northwestern edge and also features a smelter, along with silver ingots and ore near its entrance. ', '''ainethach'':45B,71B ''along'':149B ''also'':145B ''amen'':98B ''barrack'':89B,115B ''belchimac'':91B ''blind'':21B ''build'':67B ''cave'':23B ''cliff'':22B ''consist'':64B ''daughter'':83B ''deck'':111B ''dushnikh'':95B ''east'':12B ''edg'':143B ''enmon'':73B,78B ''entranc'':157B ''featur'':146B ''fenn'':58B ''fenn’'':135B ''fjotra'':84B ''gra'':94B ''gra-dushnikh'':93B ''grindston'':108B ''gulch'':60B,136B ''hall'':69B,105B,127B ''hold'':48B ''home'':76B ''hous'':75B,90B ''includ'':99B ''ingot'':152B ''karthwasten'':1A,2B,68B,104B,126B ''lash'':92B ''lie'':138B ''locat'':8B,123B ''main'':119B ''mena'':81B ''mine'':6B,34B,54B,56B,61B,117B,121B,137B ''miner'':87B ''miner’'':114B ''near'':103B,155B ''nearbi'':134B ''nord'':43B ''north'':19B,124B ''northwestern'':142B ''notabl'':27B ''one'':30B ''ore'':133B,154B ''own'':40B ''ownership'':49B ''peryit'':17B ''rack'':102B ''ragnar'':97B ''reach'':11B,38B ''reachman'':47B ''resid'':72B ''sanuarach'':55B,116B ''settlement'':35B ''shrine'':15B ''silver'':53B,120B,132B,151B ''small'':5B ''smelter'':130B,148B ''surround'':52B ''tan'':101B ''three'':66B ''town'':7B,25B,63B ''town’'':141B ''wife'':80B', 'reach', 'Karthwasten is a small mining town located in the center of the Reach. You do not know anyone who works here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_red_year', 'The Red Year, written by Melis Ravel, is a two-volume account detailing the catastrophic eruption of Red Mountain in Morrowind and its aftermath, as told through the personal stories of survivors. The narrative captures the harrowing experiences of the Dunmer people, from the destruction of cities like Tear and Vivec City to the struggles faced by those in Mournhold. Themes of survival, community, and resilience are central to the work, as the survivors recount how they coped with the loss of life, the physical devastation, and the psychological toll of the disaster. Despite the tragedy, the Dunmer exhibit unwavering courage and solidarity, helping one another in the face of the calamity.

Volume I introduces the accounts of individuals who experienced the immediate chaos of the eruption, while Volume II shifts focus to the long-term impacts, including recovery efforts and the emotional aftermath. The contrast between the physical destruction and the emotional resilience of the people highlights the theme of overcoming adversity. Through interviews and first-hand stories, Ravel paints a vivid picture of the Red Year, making it a powerful testament to the strength of the Dunmer people in the face of unimaginable loss.', '''account'':16B,121B ''advers'':168B ''aftermath'':28B,149B ''anoth'':110B ''calam'':116B ''captur'':39B ''catastroph'':19B ''central'':72B ''chao'':128B ''citi'':51B,56B ''communiti'':68B ''contrast'':151B ''cope'':82B ''courag'':105B ''despit'':98B ''destruct'':49B,155B ''detail'':17B ''devast'':90B ''disast'':97B ''dunmer'':45B,102B,195B ''effort'':145B ''emot'':148B,158B ''erupt'':20B,131B ''exhibit'':103B ''experi'':42B ''experienc'':125B ''face'':60B,113B,199B ''first'':173B ''first-hand'':172B ''focus'':136B ''hand'':174B ''harrow'':41B ''help'':108B ''highlight'':163B ''ii'':134B ''immedi'':127B ''impact'':142B ''includ'':143B ''individu'':123B ''interview'':170B ''introduc'':119B ''life'':87B ''like'':52B ''long'':140B ''long-term'':139B ''loss'':85B,202B ''make'':185B ''meli'':9B ''morrowind'':25B ''mountain'':23B ''mournhold'':64B ''narrat'':38B ''one'':109B ''overcom'':167B ''paint'':177B ''peopl'':46B,162B,196B ''person'':33B ''physic'':89B,154B ''pictur'':180B ''power'':188B ''psycholog'':93B ''ravel'':10B,176B ''recount'':79B ''recoveri'':144B ''red'':2A,5B,22B,183B ''resili'':70B,159B ''shift'':135B ''solidar'':107B ''stori'':34B,175B ''strength'':192B ''struggl'':59B ''surviv'':67B ''survivor'':36B,78B ''tear'':53B ''term'':141B ''testament'':189B ''theme'':65B,165B ''told'':30B ''toll'':94B ''tragedi'':100B ''two'':14B ''two-volum'':13B ''unimagin'':201B ''unwav'':104B ''vivec'':55B ''vivid'':179B ''volum'':15B,117B,133B ''work'':75B ''written'':7B ''year'':3A,6B,184B', 'scholar', 'The Red Year, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, chronicles the devastating eruption of Red Mountain and its aftermath through the personal stories of survivors. Themes of survival, community, resilience, and the emotional toll of catastrophe are central, emphasizing the strength and solidarity of the Dunmer people in the face of unimaginable loss.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cradle_stone_tower', '
Cradle Stone Tower is a small, ruined Nordic tower located west of Bard''s Leap Summit and east of Valthume in the Reach. The tower is home to a hagraven, making it a perilous destination for adventurers exploring the region.

To reach the tower, scale the Forsworn-filled hills at Lost Valley Redoubt, cross the waterfall at Bard''s Leap Summit, and follow the trail up the western hill. ', '''adventur'':40B ''bard'':16B,62B ''cradl'':1A,4B ''cross'':58B ''destin'':38B ''east'':21B ''explor'':41B ''fill'':52B ''follow'':67B ''forsworn'':51B ''forsworn-fil'':50B ''hagraven'':33B ''hill'':53B,73B ''home'':30B ''leap'':18B,64B ''locat'':13B ''lost'':55B ''make'':34B ''nordic'':11B ''peril'':37B ''reach'':26B,45B ''redoubt'':57B ''region'':43B ''ruin'':10B ''scale'':48B ''small'':9B ''stone'':2A,5B ''summit'':19B,65B ''tower'':3A,6B,12B,28B,47B ''trail'':69B ''valley'':56B ''valthum'':23B ''waterfal'':60B ''west'':14B ''western'':72B', 'reach', '
Cradle Stone Tower is a small, ruined Nordic tower located west of Bard''s Leap Summit in the Reach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('repel_undead', 'Repel Undead is a Restoration spell that forces undead creatures to flee in terror, effectively neutralizing them for a short period. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':27B ''cast'':31B ''creatur'':12B ''effect'':17B ''flee'':14B ''forc'':10B ''level'':29B ''neutral'':18B ''period'':23B ''repel'':1A,3B ''requir'':25B ''restor'':7B ''short'':22B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':8B ''terror'':16B ''undead'':2A,4B,11B', 'mage', 'Repel Undead is a spell that forces undead creatures to flee in terror, effectively neutralizing them for a short period. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('auriels_bow', 'Auriel''s Bow, also known as Auri-El''s Bow, is a revered artifact associated with the elven god Auriel. It manifests as a modest elven moonstone bow but is recognized as one of the most formidable weapons in all of Tamriel. The bow draws its immense power from Aetherius, channeling energy through the sun, allowing it to transform ordinary arrows into devastating projectiles.', '''aetherius'':53B ''allow'':59B ''also'':6B ''arrow'':64B ''artifact'':17B ''associ'':18B ''auri'':10B ''auri-el'':9B ''auriel'':1A,3B,23B ''bow'':2A,5B,13B,31B,47B ''channel'':54B ''devast'':66B ''draw'':48B ''el'':11B ''elven'':21B,29B ''energi'':55B ''formid'':40B ''god'':22B ''immens'':50B ''known'':7B ''manifest'':25B ''modest'':28B ''moonston'':30B ''one'':36B ''ordinari'':63B ''power'':51B ''projectil'':67B ''recogn'':34B ''rever'':16B ''sun'':58B ''tamriel'':45B ''transform'':62B ''weapon'':41B', 'dawnguard, vampire, snowelf, scholar, priest', 'Auriel''s Bow is a powerful artifact of the elven god Auriel, drawing energy from Aetherius to transform ordinary arrows into devastating projectiles. It is revered as one of Tamriel''s most formidable weapons.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chitin_armor', 'Chitin Armor is a basic chitin chest piece with good protection quality. Its visual design is organic and jagged, with dark, shell-like plates and a rough, natural texture. To craft it: 2 leather, 1 iron ingot and 5 chitin at a blacksmith forge.  An Adept smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using chitin at a workbench.', '''1'':38B ''2'':36B ''5'':42B ''adept'':49B ''armor'':2A,4B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':46B ''chest'':9B ''chitin'':1A,3B,8B,43B,60B ''craft'':34B,52B ''dark'':23B ''design'':17B ''forg'':47B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':40B ''iron'':39B ''jag'':21B ''leather'':37B ''like'':26B ''natur'':31B ''organ'':19B ''piec'':10B ''plate'':27B ''protect'':13B ''qualiti'':14B ''rough'':30B ''shell'':25B ''shell-lik'':24B ''smith'':50B ''tempered/improved'':57B ''textur'':32B ''use'':59B ''visual'':16B ''workbench'':63B', 'blacksmith', 'Chitin Armor is a basic chitin chest piece with good protection quality. Its visual design is organic and jagged, with dark, shell-like plates and a rough, natural texture. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hag_rock_redoubt', 'Hag Rock Redoubt is a small Nordic ruin located south of Markarth in the Reach. This multi-tiered structure is built into the mountainside and features multiple entrances and exits across different levels, creating a maze-like layout.

As you approach the site, a Nordic tower greets you at the base, with a path leading south past the tower, flanked by tall stone arches high above. The Forsworn occupy the redoubt, making it a dangerous location for travelers. ', '''across'':35B ''approach'':46B ''arch'':69B ''base'':56B ''built'':25B ''creat'':38B ''danger'':80B ''differ'':36B ''entranc'':32B ''exit'':34B ''featur'':30B ''flank'':65B ''forsworn'':73B ''greet'':52B ''hag'':1A,4B ''high'':70B ''layout'':43B ''lead'':60B ''level'':37B ''like'':42B ''locat'':12B,81B ''make'':77B ''markarth'':15B ''maze'':41B ''maze-lik'':40B ''mountainsid'':28B ''multi'':21B ''multi-ti'':20B ''multipl'':31B ''nordic'':10B,50B ''occupi'':74B ''past'':62B ''path'':59B ''reach'':18B ''redoubt'':3A,6B,76B ''rock'':2A,5B ''ruin'':11B ''site'':48B ''small'':9B ''south'':13B,61B ''stone'':68B ''structur'':23B ''tall'':67B ''tier'':22B ''tower'':51B,64B ''travel'':83B', 'reach, witch', 'Hag Rock Redoubt is a small Nordic ruin located south of Markarth in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('zenithar', 'Zenithar, the God of Work and Commerce, is one of the Divines, revered for his association with labor, trade, wealth, and honest enterprise. Known as the Provider of Ease, Zenithar embodies the virtues of hard work, integrity, and prosperity through peaceful means. His priests teach that wealth and success are achieved not through war or theft but by diligent work and fair trade. Often symbolized by a blacksmith''s anvil, Zenithar''s influence extends across Cyrodiil, High Rock, and beyond, with close ties to Kynareth due to the natural resources required for craftsmanship.

Worship of Zenithar is prevalent in cities with strong mercantile traditions, such as Leyawiin and Kambria, and his temples, known as Resolutions, are dedicated to fostering honest labor and prosperity. His devotees may offer prayers using special prayer beads for good fortune in business and negotiations. Zenithar is also linked to the Bosmeri god Z''en, showing his widespread influence across different cultures. Artifacts such as the Mace of the Crusader, which burns enemies with holy flames, and the Golden Anvil, blessed by Zenithar himself, are symbols of his divine favor. Zenithar''s planet, seen in the skies of Mundus, represents his presence in both the material and spiritual realms, embodying his role as a god of work and reward.', '''achiev'':52B ''across'':76B,155B ''also'':143B ''anvil'':71B,175B ''artifact'':158B ''associ'':17B ''bead'':133B ''beyond'':81B ''blacksmith'':69B ''bless'':176B ''bosmeri'':147B ''burn'':167B ''busi'':138B ''citi'':101B ''close'':83B ''commerc'':8B ''craftsmanship'':94B ''crusad'':165B ''cultur'':157B ''cyrodiil'':77B ''dedic'':118B ''devote'':126B ''differ'':156B ''dilig'':60B ''divin'':13B,184B ''due'':87B ''eas'':30B ''embodi'':32B,205B ''en'':150B ''enemi'':168B ''enterpris'':24B ''extend'':75B ''fair'':63B ''favor'':185B ''flame'':171B ''fortun'':136B ''foster'':120B ''god'':4B,148B,210B ''golden'':174B ''good'':135B ''hard'':36B ''high'':78B ''holi'':170B ''honest'':23B,121B ''influenc'':74B,154B ''integr'':38B ''kambria'':110B ''known'':25B,114B ''kynareth'':86B ''labor'':19B,122B ''leyawiin'':108B ''link'':144B ''mace'':162B ''materi'':201B ''may'':127B ''mean'':43B ''mercantil'':104B ''mundus'':194B ''natur'':90B ''negoti'':140B ''offer'':128B ''often'':65B ''one'':10B ''peac'':42B ''planet'':188B ''prayer'':129B,132B ''presenc'':197B ''preval'':99B ''priest'':45B ''prosper'':40B,124B ''provid'':28B ''realm'':204B ''repres'':195B ''requir'':92B ''resolut'':116B ''resourc'':91B ''rever'':14B ''reward'':214B ''rock'':79B ''role'':207B ''seen'':189B ''show'':151B ''sky'':192B ''special'':131B ''spiritu'':203B ''strong'':103B ''success'':50B ''symbol'':66B,181B ''teach'':46B ''templ'':113B ''theft'':57B ''tie'':84B ''trade'':20B,64B ''tradit'':105B ''use'':130B ''virtu'':34B ''war'':55B ''wealth'':21B,48B ''widespread'':153B ''work'':6B,37B,61B,212B ''worship'':95B ''z'':149B ''zenithar'':1A,2B,31B,72B,97B,141B,178B,186B', 'priest, scholar', 'Zenithar, the God of Work and Commerce, is a Divine associated with labor, trade, and honest enterprise. He represents virtues like hard work, integrity, and prosperity achieved through peaceful means. Symbolized by a blacksmith’s anvil, Zenithar is worshipped across Tamriel, especially in regions with strong mercantile traditions like Leyawiin and Kambria. His temples, known as Resolutions, promote honest labor and success, while prayer beads and artifacts like the Mace of the Crusader and the Golden Anvil symbolize his blessings. Zenithar''s influence spans various cultures, connecting to deities like the Bosmeri Z''en, embodying his role as the provider of reward through diligence.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nchuand-zel', 'Nchuand-Zel is a large Dwarven ruin located within Understone Keep in the city of Markarth, in the Reach. This ancient Dwarven castle, carved deep into the mountain, forms the cavernous interior of the keep and is currently being excavated under the supervision of Calcelmo, Markarth’s court wizard and a renowned Dwemer scholar.

Accessible through Understone Keep, Nchuand-Ze.', '''access'':58B ''ancient'':25B ''calcelmo'':49B ''carv'':28B ''castl'':27B ''cavern'':35B ''citi'':18B ''court'':51B ''current'':42B ''deep'':29B ''dwarven'':10B,26B ''dwemer'':56B ''excav'':44B ''form'':33B ''interior'':36B ''keep'':15B,39B,61B ''larg'':9B ''locat'':12B ''markarth'':20B ''markarth’'':50B ''mountain'':32B ''nchuand'':2A,5B,63B ''nchuand-z'':62B ''nchuand-zel'':1A,4B ''reach'':23B ''renown'':55B ''ruin'':11B ''scholar'':57B ''supervis'':47B ''underston'':14B,60B ''within'':13B ''wizard'':52B ''ze'':64B ''zel'':3A,6B', 'reach, dwemer', 'Nchuand-Zel is a large Dwarven ruin located within Understone Keep in the city of Markarth, in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('volsung', 'Volsung is one of the eight high-ranking dragon priests in Skyrim. He was an aloof Dragon priest who did nothing of note during the Dragon war.', '''aloof'':18B ''dragon'':11B,19B,28B ''eight'':7B ''high'':9B ''high-rank'':8B ''note'':25B ''noth'':23B ''one'':4B ''priest'':12B,20B ''rank'':10B ''skyrim'':14B ''volsung'':1A,2B ''war'':29B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Volsung must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shrine_to_peryite', 'The Shrine to Peryite is a secluded shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince Peryite, located northeast of Markarth and west of Karthwasten in the Reach. To reach the shrine from Markarth, travelers should take the path north of Salvius Farm and follow the right fork near Ragnvald, as there is no direct route from Karthwasten.

The shrine is a place of worship for Peryite’s, the Daedric Prince of Pestilence, followers,.', '''daedric'':15B,69B ''dedic'':12B ''direct'':55B ''farm'':43B ''follow'':45B,73B ''fork'':48B ''karthwasten'':25B,58B ''locat'':18B ''markarth'':21B,34B ''near'':49B ''north'':40B ''northeast'':19B ''path'':39B ''peryit'':3A,7B,17B ''peryite’'':67B ''pestil'':72B ''place'':63B ''princ'':16B,70B ''ragnvald'':50B ''reach'':28B,30B ''right'':47B ''rout'':56B ''salvius'':42B ''seclud'':10B ''shrine'':1A,5B,11B,32B,60B ''take'':37B ''travel'':35B ''west'':23B ''worship'':65B', 'reach, daedra, daedric', 'The Shrine to Peryite is a secluded shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince Peryite, located northeast of Markarth and west of Karthwasten in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wuuthrad', 'Wuuthrad, known as "Storm''s Tears" in the Atmoran language, is a legendary battleaxe forged from the ebony tears of Ysgramor, the founder of the First Empire of the Nords. The axe was created during a pivotal moment in Nord history, specifically during the Night of Tears, when Ysgramor and his son, Yngol, fled to Atmora after witnessing the destruction of Saarthal, the first human city in Skyrim. Overcome with grief, Ysgramor''s tears transformed into pure ebony, which Yngol, renowned as the greatest blacksmith of the Atmorans, collected and used to forge the axe aboard their ship.', '''aboard'':97B ''atmora'':57B ''atmoran'':10B,89B ''axe'':33B,96B ''battleax'':15B ''blacksmith'':86B ''citi'':67B ''collect'':90B ''creat'':35B ''destruct'':61B ''eboni'':19B,79B ''empir'':28B ''first'':27B,65B ''fled'':55B ''forg'':16B,94B ''founder'':24B ''greatest'':85B ''grief'':72B ''histori'':42B ''human'':66B ''known'':3B ''languag'':11B ''legendari'':14B ''moment'':39B ''night'':46B ''nord'':31B,41B ''overcom'':70B ''pivot'':38B ''pure'':78B ''renown'':82B ''saarthal'':63B ''ship'':99B ''skyrim'':69B ''son'':53B ''specif'':43B ''storm'':5B ''tear'':7B,20B,48B,75B ''transform'':76B ''use'':92B ''wit'':59B ''wuuthrad'':1A,2B ''yngol'':54B,81B ''ysgramor'':22B,50B,73B', 'companions, scholar', '
Wuuthrad is a legendary battleaxe forged from Ysgramor''s ebony tears, created during the Nord''s Night of Tears as a symbol of grief and vengeance after the fall of Saarthal.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fort_frostmoth', 'Fort Frostmoth is a small Imperial fort located south of Highpoint Tower and northeast of Hrodulf''s House on Solstheim. Once a bastion of Imperial presence on the island, the fort has since been overrun by ash spawn, hostile creatures tied to Solstheim''s volatile volcanic environment.', '''ash'':39B ''bastion'':25B ''creatur'':42B ''environ'':49B ''fort'':1A,3B,9B,33B ''frostmoth'':2A,4B ''highpoint'':13B ''hostil'':41B ''hous'':20B ''hrodulf'':18B ''imperi'':8B,27B ''island'':31B ''locat'':10B ''northeast'':16B ''overrun'':37B ''presenc'':28B ''sinc'':35B ''small'':7B ''solstheim'':22B,45B ''south'':11B ''spawn'':40B ''tie'':43B ''tower'':14B ''volatil'':47B ''volcan'':48B', 'solstheim, legion', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('reachwind_eyrie', 'Reachwind Eyrie is a small Dwarven tower located east-southeast of Markarth, perched atop a large cliff overlooking the Karth River. It is surrounded by some of Skyrim''s greener lands, providing a stunning view of the valley below.

Despite standing for thousands of years, the tower is remarkably well-preserved.', '''atop'':17B ''cliff'':20B ''despit'':43B ''dwarven'':8B ''east'':12B ''east-southeast'':11B ''eyri'':2A,4B ''greener'':33B ''karth'':23B ''land'':34B ''larg'':19B ''locat'':10B ''markarth'':15B ''overlook'':21B ''perch'':16B ''preserv'':55B ''provid'':35B ''reachwind'':1A,3B ''remark'':52B ''river'':24B ''skyrim'':31B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':13B ''stand'':44B ''stun'':37B ''surround'':27B ''thousand'':46B ''tower'':9B,50B ''valley'':41B ''view'':38B ''well'':54B ''well-preserv'':53B ''year'':48B', 'reach', 'Reachwind Eyrie is a small Dwarven tower located east-southeast of Markarth, perched atop a large cliff overlooking the Karth River.

You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sky_haven_temple', 'Sky Haven Temple is a large, mountaintop fort located east of Markarth in the Reach, accessible through the Karthspire cave. Once a major temple and outpost for the Blades, it has long been abandoned and is now under Forsworn control. Despite its abandonment, Sky Haven Temple remains a key historical site due to its role as the Blades'' primary base in Skyrim and its connection to Alduin''s Wall, a pictorial repository of ancient Akaviri dragonlore.

The temple''s history stretches back thousands of years, and although its last use by the Blades is unknown, the structure has remained remarkably well-preserved. Upon reclaiming the temple, Delphine, acting as the Blades'' Grandmaster, aims to rebuild the organization and use it as a hidden base of operations. The temple houses Alduin''s Wall, which details the Dragon Cult''s reign and a prophecy concerning Alduin''s return.', '''abandon'':37B,46B ''access'':19B ''act'':112B ''aim'':117B ''akaviri'':78B ''alduin'':70B,134B,148B ''although'':90B ''ancient'':77B ''back'':85B ''base'':63B,128B ''blade'':32B,61B,96B,115B ''cave'':23B ''concern'':147B ''connect'':68B ''control'':43B ''cult'':141B ''delphin'':111B ''despit'':44B ''detail'':138B ''dragon'':140B ''dragonlor'':79B ''due'':55B ''east'':13B ''forsworn'':42B ''fort'':11B ''grandmast'':116B ''haven'':2A,5B,48B ''hidden'':127B ''histor'':53B ''histori'':83B ''hous'':133B ''karthspir'':22B ''key'':52B ''larg'':9B ''last'':92B ''locat'':12B ''long'':35B ''major'':26B ''markarth'':15B ''mountaintop'':10B ''oper'':130B ''organ'':121B ''outpost'':29B ''pictori'':74B ''preserv'':106B ''primari'':62B ''propheci'':146B ''reach'':18B ''rebuild'':119B ''reclaim'':108B ''reign'':143B ''remain'':50B,102B ''remark'':103B ''repositori'':75B ''return'':150B ''role'':58B ''site'':54B ''sky'':1A,4B,47B ''skyrim'':65B ''stretch'':84B ''structur'':100B ''templ'':3A,6B,27B,49B,81B,110B,132B ''thousand'':86B ''unknown'':98B ''upon'':107B ''use'':93B,123B ''wall'':72B,136B ''well'':105B ''well-preserv'':104B ''year'':88B', 'reach, scholar, traveler', 'Sky Haven Temple is a large, mountaintop fort located somewhere east of Markarth in the Reach.  It is rumored to be an old base to the Imperial Blades, the imperials secret agents. However its exact location has been lost to time.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('snowberries', 'Snowberries are red berries harvested from the snowberry plant, commonly found near the snowline in Skyrim. Alchemy effects: Resist Fire, Fortify Enchanting, Resist Frost, and Resist Shock.', '''alchemi'':18B ''berri'':5B ''common'':11B ''effect'':19B ''enchant'':23B ''fire'':21B ''fortifi'':22B ''found'':12B ''frost'':25B ''harvest'':6B ''near'':13B ''plant'':10B ''red'':4B ''resist'':20B,24B,27B ''shock'':28B ''skyrim'':17B ''snowberri'':1A,2B,9B ''snowlin'':15B', 'alchemist', 'Snowberries are red berries harvested from the snowberry plant, commonly found near the snowline in Skyrim.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steamcrag_camp', 'Steamcrag Camp is a giant camp located south of Windhelm and east of Bonestrewn Crest in Eastmarch. The camp is a typical giant settlement, featuring a large bonfire, mammoth bones, and other signs of giant activity. Surrounded by the sulfurous pools characteristic of the region, it is a notable landmark in Eastmarch''s volcanic landscape.', '''activ'':38B ''bone'':32B ''bonestrewn'':16B ''bonfir'':30B ''camp'':2A,4B,8B,21B ''characterist'':44B ''crest'':17B ''east'':14B ''eastmarch'':19B,54B ''featur'':27B ''giant'':7B,25B,37B ''landmark'':52B ''landscap'':57B ''larg'':29B ''locat'':9B ''mammoth'':31B ''notabl'':51B ''pool'':43B ''region'':47B ''settlement'':26B ''sign'':35B ''south'':10B ''steamcrag'':1A,3B ''sulfur'':42B ''surround'':39B ''typic'':24B ''volcan'':56B ''windhelm'':12B', 'eastmarch', 'Steamcrag Camp is a giant camp located south of Windhelm in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('amongst_the_draugr', 'Amongst the Draugr, written by Bernadette Bantien of the College of Winterhold, explores the enigmatic nature of the draugr, their behaviors, and their ties to the ancient dragon cults. After months of cautious observation, Bantien discovers that the draugr exhibit complex, ritualistic behaviors centered around the worship of dragon priests. These undead warriors perform daily acts of homage and even transfer life energy to sustain their masters for eternity. Bantien theorizes that the draugr were originally buried as living humans, and over the centuries, their physical forms deteriorated into the grotesque undead creatures known today.

Themes of religious devotion, the preservation of life force, and the interplay between life and undeath dominate the text. The work also emphasizes the intersection of scholarly curiosity and personal peril, as Bantien aims to uncover deeper truths about the draugr and their connection to Skyrim’s ancient history. This singular book captures a blend of academic inquiry and eerie folklore.', '''academ'':154B ''act'':59B ''aim'':132B ''also'':120B ''amongst'':1A,4B ''ancient'':30B,145B ''around'':48B ''bantien'':10B,38B,73B,131B ''behavior'':24B,46B ''bernadett'':9B ''blend'':152B ''book'':149B ''buri'':80B ''captur'':150B ''cautious'':36B ''center'':47B ''centuri'':87B ''colleg'':13B ''complex'':44B ''connect'':142B ''creatur'':96B ''cult'':32B ''curios'':126B ''daili'':58B ''deeper'':135B ''deterior'':91B ''devot'':102B ''discov'':39B ''domin'':115B ''dragon'':31B,52B ''draugr'':3A,6B,22B,42B,77B,139B ''eeri'':157B ''emphas'':121B ''energi'':66B ''enigmat'':18B ''etern'':72B ''even'':63B ''exhibit'':43B ''explor'':16B ''folklor'':158B ''forc'':107B ''form'':90B ''grotesqu'':94B ''histori'':146B ''homag'':61B ''human'':83B ''inquiri'':155B ''interplay'':110B ''intersect'':123B ''known'':97B ''life'':65B,106B,112B ''live'':82B ''master'':70B ''month'':34B ''natur'':19B ''observ'':37B ''origin'':79B ''perform'':57B ''peril'':129B ''person'':128B ''physic'':89B ''preserv'':104B ''priest'':53B ''religi'':101B ''ritualist'':45B ''scholar'':125B ''singular'':148B ''skyrim’'':144B ''sustain'':68B ''text'':117B ''theme'':99B ''theoriz'':74B ''tie'':27B ''today'':98B ''transfer'':64B ''truth'':136B ''uncov'':134B ''undead'':55B,95B ''undeath'':114B ''warrior'':56B ''winterhold'':15B ''work'':119B ''worship'':50B ''written'':7B', 'scholar', '
Amongst the Draugr, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, delves into the mysterious behaviors of draugr and their connections to ancient dragon cults. The book explores themes of religious devotion, the preservation of life force, and the boundary between life and undeath, while highlighting the risks of scholarly curiosity in uncovering such ancient and eerie truths.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('old_hroldan_inn', 'Old Hroldan Inn is a remote and historic inn located in the Reach, east of Markarth and southwest of Rorikstead. The inn is notable for its connection to Tiber Septim, who once stayed there, adding to its mystique and significance. It is run by Eydis, a widow who manages the inn with the help of her young son, Skuli. Eydis mentions that her husband is fighting in the war, but there is ambiguity surrounding which side he fights for, adding an element of mystery to their story.

Leontius Salvius, a regular at the inn, spends his days working on various menial tasks outside.', '''ad'':38B,83B ''ambigu'':76B ''connect'':30B ''day'':100B ''east'':17B ''element'':85B ''eydi'':48B,63B ''fight'':69B,81B ''help'':57B ''histor'':11B ''hroldan'':2A,5B ''husband'':67B ''inn'':3A,6B,12B,25B,54B,97B ''leontius'':91B ''locat'':13B ''manag'':52B ''markarth'':19B ''menial'':104B ''mention'':64B ''mysteri'':87B ''mystiqu'':41B ''notabl'':27B ''old'':1A,4B ''outsid'':106B ''reach'':16B ''regular'':94B ''remot'':9B ''rorikstead'':23B ''run'':46B ''salvius'':92B ''septim'':33B ''side'':79B ''signific'':43B ''skuli'':62B ''son'':61B ''southwest'':21B ''spend'':98B ''stay'':36B ''stori'':90B ''surround'':77B ''task'':105B ''tiber'':32B ''various'':103B ''war'':72B ''widow'':50B ''work'':101B ''young'':60B', 'reach, innkeeper, traveler', 'Old Hroldan Inn is a remote and historic inn located in the Reach, east of Markarth and southwest of Rorikstead.  You do not know who works here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dushnikh_yal', 'Dushnikh Yal is a prosperous Orc stronghold located in the southwest of Skyrim, southeast of Markarth. The stronghold thrives due to its combination of resource production and trade. The hunters, Arob and her son Nagrub, supply Hogni Red-Arm with meat for sale in Markarth''s marketplace, while Dushnikh Mine, an orichalcum mine with seven ore veins, contributes to the stronghold''s wealth.

Like many Orc strongholds, Dushnikh Yal is surrounded by a wooden palisade with lookout platforms positioned at regular intervals along the walls. A raised walkway runs along the inside of the wall, providing a clear view of the compound. The longhouse sits at the center of the stronghold, with various other structures and activities arranged around it. There are two gates for entry: one to the east and one to the west. ', '''activ'':120B ''along'':86B,93B ''arm'':42B ''arob'':33B ''around'':122B ''arrang'':121B ''center'':111B ''clear'':101B ''combin'':25B ''compound'':105B ''contribut'':61B ''due'':22B ''dushnikh'':1A,3B,52B,71B ''east'':133B ''entri'':129B ''gate'':127B ''hogni'':39B ''hunter'':32B ''insid'':95B ''interv'':85B ''like'':67B ''locat'':10B ''longhous'':107B ''lookout'':80B ''mani'':68B ''markarth'':18B,48B ''marketplac'':50B ''meat'':44B ''mine'':53B,56B ''nagrub'':37B ''one'':130B,135B ''orc'':8B,69B ''ore'':59B ''orichalcum'':55B ''palisad'':78B ''platform'':81B ''posit'':82B ''product'':28B ''prosper'':7B ''provid'':99B ''rais'':90B ''red'':41B ''red-arm'':40B ''regular'':84B ''resourc'':27B ''run'':92B ''sale'':46B ''seven'':58B ''sit'':108B ''skyrim'':15B ''son'':36B ''southeast'':16B ''southwest'':13B ''stronghold'':9B,20B,64B,70B,114B ''structur'':118B ''suppli'':38B ''surround'':74B ''thrive'':21B ''trade'':30B ''two'':126B ''various'':116B ''vein'':60B ''view'':102B ''walkway'':91B ''wall'':88B,98B ''wealth'':66B ''west'':138B ''wooden'':77B ''yal'':2A,4B,72B', 'reach, orc', 'Dushnikh Yal is a prosperous Orc stronghold located in the southwest of Skyrim, southeast of Markarth. You do not know anyone at the fort.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('treasury_house', 'The Treasury House is a location at the northern end of the first terrace in Markarth, overlooking the city and the surrounding Reach. This vital financial institution serves as the lifeblood of the region''s economy, offering support and services to landowners, particularly the influential Silver-Blood family. The Treasury House is where miners, farmers, and day-laborers receive their wages, making it essential to the daily functioning of the Reach.

Rhiada runs the front desk, overseeing the flow of gold and coin, while the treasury itself is secured behind an expert-locked gate. Nana Ildene and Donnel maintain order and cleanliness in the building, with Nana having worked there for over twenty years. ', '''behind'':94B ''blood'':50B ''build'':110B ''citi'':21B ''cleanli'':107B ''coin'':87B ''daili'':71B ''day'':61B ''day-labor'':60B ''desk'':80B ''donnel'':103B ''economi'':38B ''end'':12B ''essenti'':68B ''expert'':97B ''expert-lock'':96B ''famili'':51B ''farmer'':58B ''financi'':28B ''first'':15B ''flow'':83B ''front'':79B ''function'':72B ''gate'':99B ''gold'':85B ''hous'':2A,5B,54B ''ilden'':101B ''influenti'':47B ''institut'':29B ''labor'':62B ''landown'':44B ''lifeblood'':33B ''locat'':8B ''lock'':98B ''maintain'':104B ''make'':66B ''markarth'':18B ''miner'':57B ''nana'':100B,112B ''northern'':11B ''offer'':39B ''order'':105B ''overlook'':19B ''overse'':81B ''particular'':45B ''reach'':25B,75B ''receiv'':63B ''region'':36B ''rhiada'':76B ''run'':77B ''secur'':93B ''serv'':30B ''servic'':42B ''silver'':49B ''silver-blood'':48B ''support'':40B ''surround'':24B ''terrac'':16B ''treasuri'':1A,4B,53B,90B ''twenti'':118B ''vital'':27B ''wage'':65B ''work'':114B ''year'':119B', 'reach', 'The Treasury House is a location at the northern end of the first terrace in Markarth, overlooking the city and the surrounding Reach.  You do not know who works here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cragwallow_slope', 'Cragwallow Slope is a medium-sized cave located southeast of Windhelm and south of Narzulbur in Eastmarch.  There are rumours that conjuers have taken over the cage.', '''cage'':30B ''cave'':10B ''conjuer'':25B ''cragwallow'':1A,3B ''eastmarch'':20B ''locat'':11B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''narzulbur'':18B ''rumour'':23B ''size'':9B ''slope'':2A,4B ''south'':16B ''southeast'':12B ''taken'':27B ''windhelm'':14B', 'eastmarch', 'Cragwallow Slope is a medium-sized cave located southeast of Windhelm in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hall_of_attainment', 'The Hall of Attainment is the primary sleeping quarters for students at the College of Winterhold, housing many of the College''s aspiring mages. Alongside the Hall of Countenance, it is one of the two main dormitory halls at the College. The hall provides living spaces for students who are further along in their magical training.

On the ground floor, students such as Brelyna Maryon, J''zargo, and Onmund can be found, alongside Tolfdir, the master trainer of Alteration. The upper floor is home to several notable figures, including Arniel Gane, a mysterious mage with his own secrets, Enthir, a general goods vendor and fence, and Mirabelle Ervine, the College’s Master-Wizard. Nirya, another resident, is also found on the upper floor.', '''along'':55B ''alongsid'':28B,76B ''also'':121B ''alter'':82B ''anoth'':118B ''arniel'':93B ''aspir'':26B ''attain'':3A,7B ''brelyna'':67B ''colleg'':17B,24B,44B ''college’'':113B ''counten'':32B ''dormitori'':40B ''enthir'':102B ''ervin'':111B ''fenc'':108B ''figur'':91B ''floor'':63B,85B,126B ''found'':75B,122B ''gane'':94B ''general'':104B ''good'':105B ''ground'':62B ''hall'':1A,5B,30B,41B,46B ''home'':87B ''hous'':20B ''includ'':92B ''j'':69B ''live'':48B ''mage'':27B,97B ''magic'':58B ''main'':39B ''mani'':21B ''maryon'':68B ''master'':79B,115B ''master-wizard'':114B ''mirabell'':110B ''mysteri'':96B ''nirya'':117B ''notabl'':90B ''one'':35B ''onmund'':72B ''primari'':10B ''provid'':47B ''quarter'':12B ''resid'':119B ''secret'':101B ''sever'':89B ''sleep'':11B ''space'':49B ''student'':14B,51B,64B ''tolfdir'':77B ''train'':59B ''trainer'':80B ''two'':38B ''upper'':84B,125B ''vendor'':106B ''winterhold'':19B ''wizard'':116B ''zargo'':70B', 'collegeofwinterhold', 'The Hall of Attainment is one of the areas in the College. You do not know anything else about the area.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'winterhold', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_midden', 'The Midden is a medium-sized dungeon located beneath the College of Winterhold, housing both the Atronach Forge and the mysterious Augur of Dunlain, a former mage of the College. The dungeon is a place of arcane secrets, filled with ancient magic and hidden knowledge.

There are three entrances to the Midden: a trapdoor located in the northern corner of the College courtyard, another at the base of the stairwell in the Hall of Countenance, and a hidden cave in the northern face of the rocky outcropping where the College is situated.  The Augur of Dunlain, a spectral figure, resides in the depths of the Midden.', '''ancient'':44B ''anoth'':67B ''arcan'':40B ''atronach'':20B ''augur'':25B,97B ''base'':70B ''beneath'':12B ''cave'':82B ''colleg'':14B,33B,65B,93B ''corner'':62B ''counten'':78B ''courtyard'':66B ''depth'':106B ''dungeon'':10B,35B ''dunlain'':27B,99B ''entranc'':52B ''face'':86B ''figur'':102B ''fill'':42B ''forg'':21B ''former'':29B ''hall'':76B ''hidden'':47B,81B ''hous'':17B ''knowledg'':48B ''locat'':11B,58B ''mage'':30B ''magic'':45B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''midden'':2A,4B,55B,109B ''mysteri'':24B ''northern'':61B,85B ''outcrop'':90B ''place'':38B ''resid'':103B ''rocki'':89B ''secret'':41B ''situat'':95B ''size'':9B ''spectral'':101B ''stairwel'':73B ''three'':51B ''trapdoor'':57B ''winterhold'':16B', 'collegeofwinterhold', 'The Midden is rumored to be a hidden cave under the College of Winterhold. You do not know anything else about the area.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'winterhold', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('spell_absorption', 'These magical effects are defensive Destruction abilities that absorb incoming spells and convert their energy into magicka for the caster. This effect is rare and not available through standard enchanting or potions, making it a highly coveted ability for mages.', '''abil'':9B,40B ''absorb'':11B ''absorpt'':2A ''avail'':29B ''caster'':22B ''convert'':15B ''covet'':39B ''defens'':7B ''destruct'':8B ''effect'':5B,24B ''enchant'':32B ''energi'':17B ''high'':38B ''incom'':12B ''mage'':42B ''magic'':4B ''magicka'':19B ''make'':35B ''potion'':34B ''rare'':26B ''spell'':1A,13B ''standard'':31B', 'mage', 'This rare magic absorbs incoming spells, turning them into magicka for the user. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('driftshade_refuge', 'Driftshade Refuge is a medium-sized fort located southeast of Dawnstar and southwest of Frostflow Lighthouse in the Winterhold region. The fort, now largely dilapidated and nearly lost beneath heavy snowdrifts, serves as the base of operations for the Silver Hand, a notorious group of werewolf hunters. Its remote location in the mountains, along with its near-erasure from local memory, makes it an ideal hideout for the group’s clandestine activities.

Once a much larger and more imposing structure, Driftshade Refuge still bears the remnants of its former grandeur, with broken walls scattered a short distance from the only remaining intact building.', '''activ'':75B ''along'':57B ''base'':38B ''bear'':87B ''beneath'':32B ''broken'':95B ''build'':106B ''clandestin'':74B ''dawnstar'':14B ''dilapid'':28B ''distanc'':100B ''driftshad'':1A,3B,84B ''erasur'':62B ''former'':92B ''fort'':10B,25B ''frostflow'':18B ''grandeur'':93B ''group'':47B ''group’'':73B ''hand'':44B ''heavi'':33B ''hideout'':70B ''hunter'':50B ''ideal'':69B ''impos'':82B ''intact'':105B ''larg'':27B ''larger'':79B ''lighthous'':19B ''local'':64B ''locat'':11B,53B ''lost'':31B ''make'':66B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''memori'':65B ''mountain'':56B ''much'':78B ''near'':30B,61B ''near-erasur'':60B ''notori'':46B ''oper'':40B ''refug'':2A,4B,85B ''region'':23B ''remain'':104B ''remnant'':89B ''remot'':52B ''scatter'':97B ''serv'':35B ''short'':99B ''silver'':43B ''size'':9B ''snowdrift'':34B ''southeast'':12B ''southwest'':16B ''still'':86B ''structur'':83B ''wall'':96B ''werewolf'':49B ''winterhold'':22B', 'winterhold, legion, stormcloak', 'Driftshade Refuge is a medium-sized fort located southeast of Dawnstar in the Winterhold region. The fort, now largely dilapidated and nearly lost beneath heavy snowdrifts.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('snowpoint_beacon', 'Snowpoint Beacon is a small tower located southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and east of Fort Fellhammer. The tower is perched on a rocky outcrop, and its main path approaches from the north, where stone steps lead up to a doorway. The tower has been taken over by bandits, who use it as a base of operations, making it a dangerous location for travelers.

The tower itself, though small, is strategically placed, offering a commanding view of the surrounding area.', '''approach'':34B ''area'':84B ''bandit'':53B ''base'':59B ''beacon'':2A,4B ''command'':79B ''danger'':65B ''doorway'':45B ''east'':18B ''fellhamm'':21B ''fort'':20B ''lead'':41B ''locat'':9B,66B ''main'':32B ''make'':62B ''north'':37B ''offer'':77B ''oper'':61B ''outcrop'':29B ''path'':33B ''perch'':25B ''place'':76B ''region'':16B ''rocki'':28B ''small'':7B,73B ''snowpoint'':1A,3B ''southwest'':10B ''step'':40B ''stone'':39B ''strateg'':75B ''surround'':83B ''taken'':50B ''though'':72B ''tower'':8B,23B,47B,70B ''travel'':68B ''use'':55B ''view'':80B ''winterhold'':12B,15B', 'winterhold', 'Snowpoint Beacon is a small tower located southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ironbind_barrow', 'Ironbind Barrow is a small Nordic ruin located southwest of Winterhold, north of Nightgate Inn. This ancient tomb is home to draugr, the undead guardians of Nordic burial sites, and serves as the resting place for the powerful Warlord Gathrik. The ruin is largely forgotten, hidden in the wilderness and surrounded by the harsh environment of Skyrim’s northern reaches.

The tomb itself contains the remains of Warlord Gathrik, a once-great warrior, whose spirit still lingers to protect the barrow from intruders.', '''ancient'':19B ''barrow'':2A,4B,83B ''burial'':30B ''contain'':65B ''draugr'':24B ''environ'':57B ''forgotten'':47B ''gathrik'':42B,70B ''great'':74B ''guardian'':27B ''harsh'':56B ''hidden'':48B ''home'':22B ''inn'':17B ''intrud'':85B ''ironbind'':1A,3B ''larg'':46B ''linger'':79B ''locat'':10B ''nightgat'':16B ''nordic'':8B,29B ''north'':14B ''northern'':60B ''once-great'':72B ''place'':37B ''power'':40B ''protect'':81B ''reach'':61B ''remain'':67B ''rest'':36B ''ruin'':9B,44B ''serv'':33B ''site'':31B ''skyrim’'':59B ''small'':7B ''southwest'':11B ''spirit'':77B ''still'':78B ''surround'':53B ''tomb'':20B,63B ''undead'':26B ''warlord'':41B,69B ''warrior'':75B ''whose'':76B ''wilder'':51B ''winterhold'':13B', 'winterhold', 'Ironbind Barrow is a small Nordic ruin located southwest of Winterhold, north of Nightgate Inn. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sightless_pit', 'Sightless Pit is a medium-sized cave located south-southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and south-southeast of Saarthal. The cave is inhabited by Falmer, the blind and hostile subterranean elves, who make their homes in dark and forsaken places like this one.', '''blind'':34B ''cave'':10B,28B ''dark'':44B ''elv'':38B ''falmer'':32B ''forsaken'':46B ''home'':42B ''hostil'':36B ''inhabit'':30B ''like'':48B ''locat'':11B ''make'':40B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''one'':50B ''pit'':2A,4B ''place'':47B ''region'':20B ''saarthal'':26B ''sightless'':1A,3B ''size'':9B ''south'':13B,23B ''south-southeast'':22B ''south-southwest'':12B ''southeast'':24B ''southwest'':14B ''subterranean'':37B ''winterhold'':16B,19B', 'winterhold', 'Sightless Pit is a medium-sized cave located south-southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ramshackle_trading_post', 'The Ramshackle Trading Post is an old, weathered shack located south of Kagrumez and west-northwest of Ashfallow Citadel on Solstheim. Despite its dilapidated appearance, the trading post serves as an unconventional merchant spot, operated by Falas Selvayn, a Dark Elf trader with an unusual schedule.

Falas can be found at the trading post only between the hours of midnight and 5 a.m., offering goods to adventurers who stumble upon this remote location during the night. ', '''5'':66B ''a.m'':67B ''adventur'':71B ''appear'':29B ''ashfallow'':22B ''citadel'':23B ''dark'':44B ''despit'':26B ''dilapid'':28B ''elf'':45B ''fala'':41B,51B ''found'':54B ''good'':69B ''hour'':62B ''kagrumez'':16B ''locat'':13B,77B ''merchant'':37B ''midnight'':64B ''night'':80B ''northwest'':20B ''offer'':68B ''old'':10B ''oper'':39B ''post'':3A,7B,32B,58B ''ramshackl'':1A,5B ''remot'':76B ''schedul'':50B ''selvayn'':42B ''serv'':33B ''shack'':12B ''solstheim'':25B ''south'':14B ''spot'':38B ''stumbl'':73B ''trade'':2A,6B,31B,57B ''trader'':46B ''unconvent'':36B ''unusu'':49B ''upon'':74B ''weather'':11B ''west'':19B ''west-northwest'':18B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ysgramor''s_tomb', 'Ysgramor''s Tomb is a small Nordic ruin located northwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and east of Pilgrim''s Trench. The tomb is the final resting place of Ysgramor, a legendary figure known as Ysgramor the Invader, or "the harbinger of us all." Ysgramor was an Atmoran who fled civil war in Atmora and arrived in Tamriel long before recorded history. He is often regarded as the first human ruler and king of Skyrim, playing a foundational role in the region''s history.

The tomb is a place of great significance, tied to the origins of Skyrim and the early history of the Nords. As a revered figure, Ysgramor''s legacy lives on, and his tomb is a site of both reverence and mystery.', '''arriv'':60B ''atmora'':58B ''atmoran'':52B ''civil'':55B ''earli'':105B ''east'':21B ''figur'':37B,113B ''final'':30B ''first'':73B ''fled'':54B ''foundat'':82B ''great'':95B ''harbing'':45B ''histori'':66B,88B,106B ''human'':74B ''invad'':42B ''king'':77B ''known'':38B ''legaci'':116B ''legendari'':36B ''live'':117B ''locat'':12B ''long'':63B ''mysteri'':129B ''nord'':109B ''nordic'':10B ''northwest'':13B ''often'':69B ''origin'':100B ''pilgrim'':23B ''place'':32B,93B ''play'':80B ''record'':65B ''regard'':70B ''region'':19B,86B ''rest'':31B ''rever'':112B,127B ''role'':83B ''ruin'':11B ''ruler'':75B ''signific'':96B ''site'':124B ''skyrim'':79B,102B ''small'':9B ''tamriel'':62B ''tie'':97B ''tomb'':3A,6B,27B,90B,121B ''trench'':25B ''us'':47B ''war'':56B ''winterhold'':15B,18B ''ysgramor'':1A,4B,34B,40B,49B,114B', 'companions', 'Ysgramor''s Tomb is a small Nordic ruin located northwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region. The tomb is the final resting place of Ysgramor, a legendary figure known as Ysgramor the Invader, or "the harbinger of us all." Ysgramor was an Atmoran who fled civil war in Atmora and arrived in Tamriel long before recorded history. He is often regarded as the first human ruler and king of Skyrim, playing a foundational role in the region''s history.
You do not know anything else about this area.', 'pale', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wood_elf', 'The Bosmer, commonly known as Wood Elves, are the native Elven people of Valenwood, a forested region in southwestern Tamriel. Unlike their Altmeri cousins, the Bosmer embrace a simpler, more natural lifestyle, living in harmony with their forested environment. Agile and nimble, they are renowned for their skill as archers and scouts, often regarded as the best bowmen in Tamriel. Many Bosmer are also adept at stealth and possess the unique ability to command animals or blend seamlessly into the forest. Despite their wild and free-spirited nature, they are also known for their quick wit and often succeed in scholarly or mercantile pursuits.

Bosmer society is shaped by the Green Pact, a unique belief system that prohibits harming Valenwood’s plant life, leading many Bosmer to live as strict carnivores, even practicing ritual cannibalism in accordance with their religious customs. Though less politically influential than other Elven races, the Bosmer are prolific and have spread across Tamriel, living two to three times as long as humans. Despite being perceived by some as unruly or naive, their deep connection to the wilderness and survival skills make them a formidable people.', '''abil'':74B ''accord'':139B ''across'':159B ''adept'':67B ''agil'':42B ''also'':66B,94B ''altmeri'':25B ''anim'':77B ''archer'':52B ''belief'':118B ''best'':59B ''blend'':79B ''bosmer'':4B,28B,64B,108B,128B,153B ''bowmen'':60B ''cannib'':137B ''carnivor'':133B ''command'':76B ''common'':5B ''connect'':181B ''cousin'':26B ''custom'':143B ''deep'':180B ''despit'':84B,170B ''elf'':2A ''elv'':9B ''elven'':13B,150B ''embrac'':29B ''environ'':41B ''even'':134B ''forest'':18B,40B,83B ''formid'':191B ''free'':89B ''free-spirit'':88B ''green'':114B ''harm'':122B ''harmoni'':37B ''human'':169B ''influenti'':147B ''known'':6B,95B ''lead'':126B ''less'':145B ''life'':125B ''lifestyl'':34B ''live'':35B,130B,161B ''long'':167B ''make'':188B ''mani'':63B,127B ''mercantil'':106B ''naiv'':178B ''nativ'':12B ''natur'':33B,91B ''nimbl'':44B ''often'':55B,101B ''pact'':115B ''peopl'':14B,192B ''perceiv'':172B ''plant'':124B ''polit'':146B ''possess'':71B ''practic'':135B ''prohibit'':121B ''prolif'':155B ''pursuit'':107B ''quick'':98B ''race'':151B ''regard'':56B ''region'':19B ''religi'':142B ''renown'':47B ''ritual'':136B ''scholar'':104B ''scout'':54B ''seamless'':80B ''shape'':111B ''simpler'':31B ''skill'':50B,187B ''societi'':109B ''southwestern'':21B ''spirit'':90B ''spread'':158B ''stealth'':69B ''strict'':132B ''succeed'':102B ''surviv'':186B ''system'':119B ''tamriel'':22B,62B,160B ''though'':144B ''three'':164B ''time'':165B ''two'':162B ''uniqu'':73B,117B ''unlik'':23B ''unruli'':176B ''valenwood'':16B ''valenwood’'':123B ''wild'':86B ''wilder'':184B ''wit'':99B ''wood'':1A,8B', 'woodelf, scholar', 'The Bosmer, or Wood Elves, are the native Elves of Valenwood, known for their harmony with nature and exceptional archery and scouting skills. Agile and stealthy, they can command animals and blend into forests. Their society is shaped by the Green Pact, a belief forbidding harm to Valenwood''s plants, making them strict carnivores and ritualistic cannibals. While less politically influential than other Elves, their wit, survival skills, and deep connection to the wilderness make them a resilient and unique people.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tel_mithryn', 'Tel Mithryn is a Telvanni tower settlement located east of Fort Frostmoth on the island of Solstheim. This unique settlement is home to Master Wizard Neloth of House Telvanni, a prominent and eccentric figure with a reputation for both brilliance and controversy. Tel Mithryn consists of four large mushroom structures grown from special fungal spores brought from Morrowind at the beginning of the Fourth Era. These structures include the main tower, the apothecary, the kitchen, and the steward''s house.

Access to each building is provided by long, organic ramps that lead to round wooden doors, blending seamlessly with the settlement’s distinctive fungal architecture. Surrounding the structures, various flora, such as bleeding crown, fly amanita fungi, and scathecraw, thrive near the ramps, adding to the natural ambiance of the area. Behind the kitchen lies a heart stone deposit with a conveniently placed pickaxe, and additional deposits can be found on the cliffs near the southeastern coast.', '''access'':83B ''ad'':125B ''addit'':147B ''amanita'':117B ''ambianc'':129B ''apothecari'':75B ''architectur'':106B ''area'':132B ''begin'':63B ''behind'':133B ''bleed'':114B ''blend'':99B ''brillianc'':42B ''brought'':58B ''build'':86B ''cliff'':154B ''coast'':158B ''consist'':47B ''controversi'':44B ''conveni'':143B ''crown'':115B ''deposit'':140B,148B ''distinct'':104B ''door'':98B ''east'':11B ''eccentr'':35B ''era'':67B ''figur'':36B ''fli'':116B ''flora'':111B ''fort'':13B ''found'':151B ''four'':49B ''fourth'':66B ''frostmoth'':14B ''fungal'':56B,105B ''fungi'':118B ''grown'':53B ''heart'':138B ''home'':24B ''hous'':30B,82B ''includ'':70B ''island'':17B ''kitchen'':77B,135B ''larg'':50B ''lead'':94B ''lie'':136B ''locat'':10B ''long'':90B ''main'':72B ''master'':26B ''mithryn'':2A,4B,46B ''morrowind'':60B ''mushroom'':51B ''natur'':128B ''near'':122B,155B ''neloth'':28B ''organ'':91B ''pickax'':145B ''place'':144B ''promin'':33B ''provid'':88B ''ramp'':92B,124B ''reput'':39B ''round'':96B ''scathecraw'':120B ''seamless'':100B ''settlement'':9B,22B ''settlement’'':103B ''solstheim'':19B ''southeastern'':157B ''special'':55B ''spore'':57B ''steward'':80B ''stone'':139B ''structur'':52B,69B,109B ''surround'':107B ''tel'':1A,3B,45B ''telvanni'':7B,31B ''thrive'':121B ''tower'':8B,73B ''uniqu'':21B ''various'':110B ''wizard'':27B ''wooden'':97B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shrine_of_azura', 'The Shrine of Azura is a massive sacred site dedicated to Azura, the Daedric Prince of Dawn and Dusk. It is located south of Winterhold, perched atop the summit of a tall mountain. The path leading to the shrine is found not far south of Whistling Mine, where it rises sharply to the west. To reach the shrine, travelers must head southeast along the path from Winterhold, heading in the direction of Windhelm. On clear days one can enjoy sweeping views from the summit, with expansive vistas stretching in all directions.

The shrine itself is situated atop a stone fort-like structure, believed to have been built by the Dunmer, who revere Azura. A massive statue of Azura dominates the site, with an altar positioned in front of it. Aranea Ienith, a devout worshiper of Azura, spends her time at the altar, offering prayers when she is not following you. To the right of the altar, a small camp lies below on a lower level.', '''along'':66B ''altar'':128B,146B,160B ''aranea'':134B ''atop'':30B,100B ''azura'':3A,7B,15B,117B,122B,140B ''believ'':107B ''built'':111B ''camp'':163B ''clear'':78B ''daedric'':17B ''dawn'':20B ''day'':79B ''dedic'':13B ''devout'':137B ''direct'':74B,94B ''domin'':123B ''dunmer'':114B ''dusk'':22B ''enjoy'':82B ''expans'':89B ''far'':46B ''follow'':153B ''fort'':104B ''fort-lik'':103B ''found'':44B ''front'':131B ''head'':64B,71B ''ienith'':135B ''lead'':39B ''level'':169B ''lie'':164B ''like'':105B ''locat'':25B ''lower'':168B ''massiv'':10B,119B ''mine'':50B ''mountain'':36B ''must'':63B ''offer'':147B ''one'':80B ''path'':38B,68B ''perch'':29B ''posit'':129B ''prayer'':148B ''princ'':18B ''reach'':59B ''rever'':116B ''right'':157B ''rise'':53B ''sacr'':11B ''sharpli'':54B ''shrine'':1A,5B,42B,61B,96B ''site'':12B,125B ''situat'':99B ''small'':162B ''south'':26B,47B ''southeast'':65B ''spend'':141B ''statu'':120B ''stone'':102B ''stretch'':91B ''structur'':106B ''summit'':32B,87B ''sweep'':83B ''tall'':35B ''time'':143B ''travel'':62B ''view'':84B ''vista'':90B ''west'':57B ''whistl'':49B ''windhelm'':76B ''winterhold'':28B,70B ''worship'':138B', 'winterhold, daedra, daedric', 'The Shrine of Azura is a massive sacred site dedicated to Azura, the Daedric Prince of Dawn and Dusk. It is located south of Winterhold, perched atop the summit of a tall mountain.

A massive statue of Azura dominates the site that can be seen from almost anywhere in Skyrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('yngvild', 'Yngvild is a medium-sized cave located east-northeast of Dawnstar, in the Winterhold region, and south-southeast of Hela''s Folly. The cave is home to draugr, the undead guardians that protect ancient Nordic tombs, making it a perilous site for adventurers.
', '''adventur'':47B ''ancient'':38B ''cave'':8B,28B ''dawnstar'':14B ''draugr'':32B ''east'':11B ''east-northeast'':10B ''folli'':26B ''guardian'':35B ''hela'':24B ''home'':30B ''locat'':9B ''make'':41B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''nordic'':39B ''northeast'':12B ''peril'':44B ''protect'':37B ''region'':18B ''site'':45B ''size'':7B ''south'':21B ''south-southeast'':20B ''southeast'':22B ''tomb'':40B ''undead'':34B ''winterhold'':17B ''yngvild'':1A,2B', 'winterhold', 'Yngvild is a medium-sized cave located east-northeast of Dawnstar, in the Winterhold region.
You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('septimus_signus''s_outpost', 'Septimus Signus''s Outpost is a small cave located north of the College of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and northeast of Ysgramor''s Tomb. This remote and secluded outpost serves as the residence of Septimus Signus, a reclusive and eccentric scholar of the Dwemer and their ancient knowledge.

The outpost consists of a single zone, known as Septimus Signus''s Outpost, where the scholar conducts his studies on the enigmatic Dwemer and their lost artifacts.', '''ancient'':52B ''artifact'':80B ''cave'':12B ''colleg'':17B ''conduct'':70B ''consist'':56B ''dwemer'':49B,76B ''eccentr'':45B ''enigmat'':75B ''knowledg'':53B ''known'':61B ''locat'':13B ''lost'':79B ''north'':14B ''northeast'':25B ''outpost'':4A,8B,34B,55B,66B ''reclus'':43B ''region'':23B ''remot'':31B ''resid'':38B ''scholar'':46B,69B ''seclud'':33B ''septimus'':1A,5B,40B,63B ''serv'':35B ''signus'':2A,6B,41B,64B ''singl'':59B ''small'':11B ''studi'':72B ''tomb'':29B ''winterhold'':19B,22B ''ysgramor'':27B ''zone'':60B', 'collegeofwinterhold', 'Septimus Signus''s Outpost is a small cave located somewhere north of the College of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region. It is rumored that Septimus is some crazy Imperial scholar who is looking for some weird artifact in the cave. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'winterhold', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stillborn_cave', 'Stillborn Cave is a small cave located north-northwest of Windhelm, across the mountains from the city in the Winterhold region. The cave is inhabited by falmer, the twisted, blind, subterranean elves, making it a dangerous location for anyone who ventures inside. 

The entrance to the cave leads into an ice tunnel that stretches southward, with the path soon turning west. As the tunnel continues, an ice melt runoff creates a rapid stream flowing from east to west, cutting through the cave.', '''across'':15B ''anyon'':42B ''blind'':33B ''cave'':2A,4B,8B,26B,50B,85B ''citi'':20B ''continu'':68B ''creat'':73B ''cut'':82B ''danger'':39B ''east'':79B ''elv'':35B ''entranc'':47B ''falmer'':30B ''flow'':77B ''ice'':54B,70B ''inhabit'':28B ''insid'':45B ''lead'':51B ''locat'':9B,40B ''make'':36B ''melt'':71B ''mountain'':17B ''north'':11B ''north-northwest'':10B ''northwest'':12B ''path'':61B ''rapid'':75B ''region'':24B ''runoff'':72B ''small'':7B ''soon'':62B ''southward'':58B ''stillborn'':1A,3B ''stream'':76B ''stretch'':57B ''subterranean'':34B ''tunnel'':55B,67B ''turn'':63B ''twist'':32B ''ventur'':44B ''west'':64B,81B ''windhelm'':14B ''winterhold'':23B', 'winterhold', 'Stillborn Cave is a small cave located north-northwest of Windhelm, across the mountains from the city in the Winterhold region. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chrysamere', 'Chrysamere, also known as the Chrysamere Blade or the Sword of Heroes, is an ancient adamantium claymore renowned for its extraordinary combination of offensive power and defensive capabilities. Forged in the late Merethic Era by the Breton swordsmith Asterie Bedel, Chrysamere embodies a unique blend of techniques from both human and elven craftsmanship. Its design features a distinctive "mage''s knot," symbolizing its deep connection to the early cultural roots of Breton society and the influence of their Elven ancestors.', '''adamantium'':17B ''also'':3B ''ancestor'':81B ''ancient'':16B ''asteri'':40B ''bedel'':41B ''blade'':8B ''blend'':46B ''breton'':38B,73B ''capabl'':29B ''chrysamer'':1A,2B,7B,42B ''claymor'':18B ''combin'':23B ''connect'':66B ''craftsmanship'':54B ''cultur'':70B ''deep'':65B ''defens'':28B ''design'':56B ''distinct'':59B ''earli'':69B ''elven'':53B,80B ''embodi'':43B ''era'':35B ''extraordinari'':22B ''featur'':57B ''forg'':30B ''hero'':13B ''human'':51B ''influenc'':77B ''knot'':62B ''known'':4B ''late'':33B ''mage'':60B ''mereth'':34B ''offens'':25B ''power'':26B ''renown'':19B ''root'':71B ''societi'':74B ''sword'':11B ''swordsmith'':39B ''symbol'':63B ''techniqu'':48B ''uniqu'':45B', 'breton, highelf, scholar', '
Chrysamere is an ancient adamantium claymore, blending human and elven craftsmanship, celebrated for its immense offensive power and defensive capabilities. Known as the Sword of Heroes, it symbolizes Breton cultural heritage.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedra_silk', 'Daedra Silk, originating from the planes of Oblivion, is a whiteish silk used in alchemy. It can be purchased from Khajiit caravans Alchemy effects: Lingering Damage Stamina, Paralysis, Night Eye, and Invisibility.', '''alchemi'':17B,25B ''caravan'':24B ''daedra'':1A,3B ''damag'':28B ''effect'':26B ''eye'':32B ''invis'':34B ''khajiit'':23B ''linger'':27B ''night'':31B ''oblivion'':10B ''origin'':5B ''paralysi'':30B ''plane'':8B ''purchas'':21B ''silk'':2A,4B,14B ''stamina'':29B ''use'':15B ''whiteish'':13B', 'alchemist', 'Daedra Silk, originating from the planes of Oblivion, is a whiteish silk used in alchemy. It can be purchased from Khajiit caravans 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sparks', 'Sparks is a Destruction spell that discharges a stream of electrical energy, dealing shock damage to health and magicka. It requires a Novice skill level to cast.', '''cast'':28B ''damag'':16B ''deal'':14B ''destruct'':5B ''discharg'':8B ''electr'':12B ''energi'':13B ''health'':18B ''level'':26B ''magicka'':20B ''novic'':24B ''requir'':22B ''shock'':15B ''skill'':25B ''spark'':1A,2B ''spell'':6B ''stream'':10B', 'mage', 'Sparks is a spell that releases a stream of electrical energy, damaging both the health and magicka of enemies. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_the_defender', 'Favored by warriors and shield-bearers, this potion reinforces defensive techniques, allowing for greater resistance against incoming strikes. Improves blocking techniques slightly, increasing protection with higher-grade potions. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':46B ''allow'':17B ''bearer'':11B ''block'':25B ''defend'':4A ''defens'':15B ''draught'':56B ''elixir'':59B ''favor'':5B ''found'':39B ''grade'':33B ''greater'':19B ''higher'':32B ''higher-grad'':31B ''improv'':24B ''incom'':22B ''increas'':28B ''loot'':42B ''philter'':57B ''potion'':1A,13B,34B,36B,55B ''protect'':29B ''purchas'':44B ''random'':41B ''reinforc'':14B ''resist'':20B ''sever'':49B ''shield'':10B ''shield-bear'':9B ''slight'':27B ''strike'':23B ''strongest'':54B ''techniqu'':16B,26B ''tier'':50B ''warrior'':7B ''weakest'':52B', 'warrior, alchemist, companions, guard', 'The Potion of the Defender reinforces defensive techniques, helping to block attacks more effectively. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('incident_at_necrom', 'Incident in Necrom, written by Jonquilla Bothe, is a suspenseful tale about a group of adventurers tasked with cleansing a haunted cemetery near the city of Necrom. The story follows Phlaxith, the leader of the group, as he assembles a team consisting of Nitrah, a skilled swordswoman, Osmic, a burglar, and Massitha, a sorceress specializing in illusion magic. The group sets out to eliminate a vampire infestation in the graveyard and encounters deadly foes, with Massitha''s unique abilities playing a crucial role in their survival. As the group navigates the crypts, they face overwhelming odds, but ultimately, Massitha''s powers help them defeat the vampires, only for a final, shocking twist.

The book explores themes of betrayal, the unexpected nature of allies, and the dangers of underestimating the power of illusion magic. Massitha’s development from an unsure illusionist into a vital force in the battle highlights the versatility and unpredictability of magic. The play concludes with an ironic twist, as Massitha, thought to be the victim, turns the tables on her treacherous companions. The story is self-contained within a single volume, blending action with deception and dark magic.', '''abil'':82B ''action'':189B ''adventur'':19B ''alli'':126B ''assembl'':42B ''battl'':149B ''betray'':121B ''blend'':188B ''book'':117B ''both'':10B ''burglar'':53B ''cemeteri'':25B ''citi'':28B ''cleans'':22B ''companion'':177B ''conclud'':159B ''consist'':45B ''contain'':183B ''crucial'':85B ''crypt'':95B ''danger'':129B ''dark'':193B ''dead'':76B ''decept'':191B ''defeat'':107B ''develop'':138B ''elimin'':67B ''encount'':75B ''explor'':118B ''face'':97B ''final'':113B ''foe'':77B ''follow'':33B ''forc'':146B ''graveyard'':73B ''group'':17B,39B,63B,92B ''haunt'':24B ''help'':105B ''highlight'':150B ''illus'':60B,135B ''illusionist'':142B ''incid'':1A,4B ''infest'':70B ''iron'':162B ''jonquilla'':9B ''leader'':36B ''magic'':61B,136B,156B,194B ''massitha'':55B,79B,102B,165B ''massitha’'':137B ''natur'':124B ''navig'':93B ''near'':26B ''necrom'':3A,6B,30B ''nitrah'':47B ''odd'':99B ''osmic'':51B ''overwhelm'':98B ''phlaxith'':34B ''play'':83B,158B ''power'':104B,133B ''role'':86B ''self'':182B ''self-contain'':181B ''set'':64B ''shock'':114B ''singl'':186B ''skill'':49B ''sorceress'':57B ''special'':58B ''stori'':32B,179B ''surviv'':89B ''suspens'':13B ''swordswoman'':50B ''tabl'':173B ''tale'':14B ''task'':20B ''team'':44B ''theme'':119B ''thought'':166B ''treacher'':176B ''turn'':171B ''twist'':115B,163B ''ultim'':101B ''underestim'':131B ''unexpect'':123B ''uniqu'':81B ''unpredict'':154B ''unsur'':141B ''vampir'':69B,109B ''versatil'':152B ''victim'':170B ''vital'':145B ''volum'':187B ''within'':184B ''written'':7B', 'scholar', 'Incident in Necrom, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, is a suspenseful tale of a group of adventurers battling a vampire infestation in a haunted cemetery, where betrayal and dark magic play key roles. The themes focus on deception, the power of illusion magic, and the unexpected nature of allies, with a twist highlighting Massitha''s growth and her ultimate role in the group’s survival.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wreck_of_the_winter_war', 'The Wreck of the Winter War is a shipwreck located east-southeast of Snow Veil Sanctum and far northeast of Windhelm, in the Winterhold region. The wreck lies along the rugged and icy coastline, a remnant of a tragic event lost to time. The area is remote, with few travelers daring to approach the wreck due to its harsh environment and the treacherous terrain surrounding it. Situated between Yngol Barrow to the southwest and Snow Veil Sanctum to the northwest, the wreck serves as a mysterious and eerie landmark in the region.', '''along'':35B ''approach'':59B ''area'':51B ''barrow'':76B ''coastlin'':40B ''dare'':57B ''due'':62B ''east'':17B ''east-southeast'':16B ''eeri'':94B ''environ'':66B ''event'':46B ''far'':24B ''harsh'':65B ''ici'':39B ''landmark'':95B ''lie'':34B ''locat'':15B ''lost'':47B ''mysteri'':92B ''northeast'':25B ''northwest'':86B ''region'':31B,98B ''remnant'':42B ''remot'':53B ''rug'':37B ''sanctum'':22B,83B ''serv'':89B ''shipwreck'':14B ''situat'':73B ''snow'':20B,81B ''southeast'':18B ''southwest'':79B ''surround'':71B ''terrain'':70B ''time'':49B ''tragic'':45B ''travel'':56B ''treacher'':69B ''veil'':21B,82B ''war'':5A,11B ''windhelm'':27B ''winter'':4A,10B ''winterhold'':30B ''wreck'':1A,7B,33B,61B,88B ''yngol'':75B', 'winterhold, sailor', 'The Wreck of the Winter War is a shipwreck located far northeast of Windhelm, in the Winterhold region. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tiid_klo_ul', 'Slow Time is a Shout that commands time itself to obey, causing the world around you to stand still while you move at normal speed. The three words of power in this Shout are Tiid (Time), which controls the flow of time; Klo (Sand), which symbolizes the slow passage of time, like grains of sand slipping away; and Ul (Eternity), which extends the effect, allowing time to remain frozen for a longer duration.', '''allow'':68B ''around'':18B ''away'':60B ''caus'':15B ''command'':10B ''control'':41B ''durat'':76B ''effect'':67B ''etern'':63B ''extend'':65B ''flow'':43B ''frozen'':72B ''grain'':56B ''klo'':2A,46B ''like'':55B ''longer'':75B ''move'':25B ''normal'':27B ''obey'':14B ''passag'':52B ''power'':33B ''remain'':71B ''sand'':47B,58B ''shout'':8B,36B ''slip'':59B ''slow'':4B,51B ''speed'':28B ''stand'':21B ''still'':22B ''symbol'':49B ''three'':30B ''tiid'':1A,38B ''time'':5B,11B,39B,45B,54B,69B ''ul'':3A,62B ''word'':31B ''world'':17B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_serpent_stone', 'The Serpent Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located directly east of the College of Winterhold and northeast of the Wreck of The Pride of Tel Vos, on a small island.

When activated, the Serpent Stone grants the player the ability to use a ranged attack that paralyzes a target for a few seconds while dealing damage. The effect is powerful and useful, particularly for disabling enemies from a distance. ', '''abil'':49B ''across'':15B ''activ'':41B ''attack'':54B ''colleg'':22B ''damag'':65B ''deal'':64B ''direct'':18B ''disabl'':74B ''distanc'':78B ''east'':19B ''effect'':67B ''enemi'':75B ''grant'':45B ''island'':39B ''locat'':17B ''northeast'':26B ''one'':8B ''paralyz'':56B ''particular'':72B ''player'':47B ''power'':69B ''pride'':32B ''rang'':53B ''scatter'':14B ''second'':62B ''serpent'':2A,5B,43B ''skyrim'':16B ''small'':38B ''stand'':12B ''stone'':3A,6B,13B,44B ''target'':58B ''tel'':34B ''thirteen'':11B ''use'':51B,71B ''vos'':35B ''winterhold'':24B ''wreck'':29B', 'winterhold, scholar, traveler', '"The Serpent Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located directly east of the College of Winterhold.

When activated, the Serpent Stone grants the player the ability to use a ranged attack that paralyzes a target for a few seconds while dealing damage. The effect is powerful and useful, particularly for disabling enemies from a distance. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('imperial_city', 'The Imperial City, also known as Cyrodiil City, is the cultural and political heart of Tamriel, located on City Isle in the center of Lake Rumare. Dominated by the iconic White-Gold Tower, the city serves as the capital of Cyrodiil and the Tamrielic Empire. Its origins trace back to the Merethic Era, when the Aldmer constructed the White-Gold Tower as a temple, marking the beginnings of Ayleid civilization in the region. Over centuries, the city became the seat of power for various empires, from Alessia''s rebellion to the rise of the Reman and Septim Dynasties. Despite its grandeur, the city has endured numerous challenges, including sieges, invasions, and disasters such as the Oblivion Crisis and the Great War.

The city is divided into several districts, each with distinct roles and architectural styles. Key areas include the Market District, a hub of commerce; the Arboretum, home to statues of the Divines; and the Temple District, housing the Temple of the One. The Arena District hosts the Imperial Arena, famous for its bloody spectacles, while the Waterfront District serves as a harbor and residential area for the city''s poorer residents. Beneath the city lies an extensive network of sewers and Ayleid ruins, often used as hideouts by outlaws and secretive organizations like the Thieves Guild. Throughout history, the city has been a focal point of Tamrielic events, from the Alessian Slave Rebellion to the Planemeld, showcasing its enduring significance as the center of Tamrielic culture and governance.', '''aldmer'':59B ''alessia'':91B ''alessian'':236B ''also'':6B ''arboretum'':151B ''architectur'':138B ''area'':141B,190B ''arena'':169B,174B ''ayleid'':73B,207B ''back'':52B ''becam'':82B ''begin'':71B ''beneath'':197B ''bloodi'':178B ''capit'':42B ''center'':25B,248B ''centuri'':79B ''challeng'':111B ''citi'':2A,5B,10B,21B,38B,81B,107B,127B,193B,199B,225B ''civil'':74B ''commerc'':149B ''construct'':60B ''crisi'':121B ''cultur'':13B,251B ''cyrodiil'':9B,44B ''despit'':103B ''disast'':116B ''distinct'':135B ''district'':132B,145B,161B,170B,183B ''divid'':129B ''divin'':157B ''domin'':29B ''dynasti'':102B ''empir'':48B,89B ''endur'':109B,244B ''era'':56B ''event'':233B ''extens'':202B ''famous'':175B ''focal'':229B ''gold'':35B,64B ''govern'':253B ''grandeur'':105B ''great'':124B ''guild'':221B ''harbor'':187B ''heart'':16B ''hideout'':212B ''histori'':223B ''home'':152B ''host'':171B ''hous'':162B ''hub'':147B ''icon'':32B ''imperi'':1A,4B,173B ''includ'':112B,142B ''invas'':114B ''isl'':22B ''key'':140B ''known'':7B ''lake'':27B ''lie'':200B ''like'':218B ''locat'':19B ''mark'':69B ''market'':144B ''mereth'':55B ''network'':203B ''numer'':110B ''oblivion'':120B ''often'':209B ''one'':167B ''organ'':217B ''origin'':50B ''outlaw'':214B ''planemeld'':241B ''point'':230B ''polit'':15B ''poorer'':195B ''power'':86B ''rebellion'':93B,238B ''region'':77B ''reman'':99B ''resid'':196B ''residenti'':189B ''rise'':96B ''role'':136B ''ruin'':208B ''rumar'':28B ''seat'':84B ''secret'':216B ''septim'':101B ''serv'':39B,184B ''sever'':131B ''sewer'':205B ''showcas'':242B ''sieg'':113B ''signific'':245B ''slave'':237B ''spectacl'':179B ''statu'':154B ''style'':139B ''tamriel'':18B,47B,232B,250B ''templ'':68B,160B,164B ''thiev'':220B ''throughout'':222B ''tower'':36B,65B ''trace'':51B ''use'':210B ''various'':88B ''war'':125B ''waterfront'':182B ''white'':34B,63B ''white-gold'':33B,62B', 'scholar, imperial, noble', 'The Imperial City, located on City Isle in Lake Rumare, is the political and cultural heart of Tamriel and serves as the capital of Cyrodiil and the Tamrielic Empire. Founded by the Aldmer in the Merethic Era, the city is home to the iconic White-Gold Tower and has witnessed numerous historical events, from the Alessian Slave Rebellion to the Oblivion Crisis and the Great War. The city is divided into several districts, including the Market District, the Temple District, and the Arena District. Beneath the city lies an extensive network of sewers and Ayleid ruins, often used by outlaws and secret organizations like the Thieves Guild. The Imperial City remains central to Tamriel''s history, culture, and governance.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('camora_tong', 'The Camonna Tong is a notorious Dunmer criminal syndicate rooted in Morrowind, infamous for its opposition to foreign influence and its ruthless criminal activities. As one of Tamriel''s oldest criminal organizations, the Tong has operated since at least the Second Era, engaging in smuggling, extortion, slavery, and murder, often targeting outlanders to protect what they see as Dunmeri sovereignty. Members of the Tong take pride in their dark history, promoting a vision of Morrowind where outsiders are either enslaved or expelled. Despite their xenophobic ideology, the Tong occasionally collaborates with foreigners when profit outweighs prejudice. Throughout its history, the Camonna Tong has clashed with abolitionist groups, Great Houses, and rival factions like the Dark Brotherhood and Thieves Guild while maintaining its power in Morrowind’s criminal underworld.

By the Third Era, the Camonna Tong wielded significant influence through its alliance with House Hlaalu, operating openly in towns like Balmora, Hla Oad, and Vivec City. Under Orvas Dren, the Tong became intertwined with House Hlaalu''s leadership, controlling councilors and influencing major decisions while secretly allying with the Sixth House during the Nerevarine prophecy. The Tong’s collaboration with corrupt Fighters Guild leaders further extended its reach, using the guild to eliminate competitors like the Imperial Thieves Guild. However, its dominance waned as the Nerevarine dismantled its power base, and its future after the Oblivion Crisis, Red Year, and Argonian Invasion remains uncertain. With the decline of House Hlaalu and the devastation of Morrowind, the Camonna Tong likely faced significant challenges, though its enduring legacy as a symbol of xenophobia and criminal enterprise in Dunmeri society remains indelible.', '''abolitionist'':108B ''activ'':26B ''alli'':177B ''allianc'':142B ''argonian'':230B ''balmora'':151B ''base'':219B ''becam'':162B ''brotherhood'':118B ''camonna'':4B,103B,135B,246B ''camora'':1A ''challeng'':251B ''citi'':156B ''clash'':106B ''collabor'':92B,188B ''competitor'':203B ''control'':169B ''corrupt'':190B ''councilor'':170B ''crimin'':10B,25B,33B,128B,262B ''crisi'':226B ''dark'':71B,117B ''decis'':174B ''declin'':236B ''despit'':85B ''devast'':242B ''dismantl'':216B ''domin'':211B ''dren'':159B ''dunmer'':9B ''dunmeri'':61B,265B ''either'':81B ''elimin'':202B ''endur'':254B ''engag'':45B ''enslav'':82B ''enterpris'':263B ''era'':44B,133B ''expel'':84B ''extend'':195B ''extort'':48B ''face'':249B ''faction'':114B ''fighter'':191B ''foreign'':20B,94B ''futur'':222B ''great'':110B ''group'':109B ''guild'':121B,192B,200B,208B ''histori'':72B,101B ''hla'':152B ''hlaalu'':145B,166B,239B ''hous'':111B,144B,165B,181B,238B ''howev'':209B ''ideolog'':88B ''imperi'':206B ''indel'':268B ''infam'':15B ''influenc'':21B,139B,172B ''inter