INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cragslane_cavern', 'Cragslane Cavern is a small cave located north of Shor''s Stone and west of Ansilvund in Eastmarch. It is situated just off the road between Riften and Windhelm, making it accessible to travelers in the region. The cavern is occupied by bandits and pit wolves and serves as a base for illicit skooma operations and brutal animal blood sports.', '''access'':34B ''anim'':60B ''ansilvund'':18B ''bandit'':45B ''base'':53B ''blood'':61B ''brutal'':59B ''cave'':8B ''cavern'':2A,4B,41B ''cragslan'':1A,3B ''eastmarch'':20B ''illicit'':55B ''locat'':9B ''make'':32B ''north'':10B ''occupi'':43B ''oper'':57B ''pit'':47B ''region'':39B ''riften'':29B ''road'':27B ''serv'':50B ''shor'':12B ''situat'':23B ''skooma'':56B ''small'':7B ''sport'':62B ''stone'':14B ''travel'':36B ''west'':16B ''windhelm'':31B ''wolv'':48B', 'eastmarch', 'Cragslane Cavern is a small cave located north of Shor''s Stone in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frostflow_lighthouse', 'Frostflow Lighthouse is a lighthouse located west of Winterhold, on the northern coast of Skyrim. It sits on a headland, offering a commanding view of the coastline between Dawnstar and Winterhold. The lighthouse is home to a Redguard family who recently purchased it, you do not know their names. However they have not been seen from in weeks.', '''coast'':15B ''coastlin'':29B ''command'':25B ''dawnstar'':31B ''famili'':41B ''frostflow'':1A,3B ''headland'':22B ''home'':37B ''howev'':52B ''know'':49B ''lighthous'':2A,4B,7B,35B ''locat'':8B ''name'':51B ''northern'':14B ''offer'':23B ''purchas'':44B ''recent'':43B ''redguard'':40B ''seen'':57B ''sit'':19B ''skyrim'':17B ''view'':26B ''week'':60B ''west'':9B ''winterhold'':11B,33B', 'winterhold', 'Frostflow Lighthouse is a lighthouse located west of Winterhold, on the northern coast of Skyrim. The lighthouse is home to a Redguard family who recently purchased it, you do not know their names. However they have not been seen from in weeks.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ancestors_and_the_dunmer', '
Ancestors and the Dunmer, written by an anonymous scholar, is a guide for outsiders seeking to understand the ancestor veneration and spirit magic practiced by the Dunmer of Morrowind. The text explores the sacred bond between the Dunmer and their ancestors, maintained through rituals at family shrines called Waiting Doors and fortified by ghost fences constructed from ancestral remains. These practices emphasize the importance of familial duty and the spiritual protection ancestors provide to their descendants. However, spirits bound against their will may become "mad ghosts," used as guardians or manipulated for rituals. The book highlights how the Dunmer view Oblivion as interconnected with the mortal world, unlike the dualistic perspective of humans, and how foreign views often misinterpret ancestor worship as necromancy.

Thematically, the book delves into reverence, familial loyalty, and the clash of cultural perceptions, particularly regarding necromancy, which the Dunmer abhor outside their sacred traditions. The text also touches on the Empire’s policy of tolerance and the adaptation of ancestral practices in the wake of changes like the construction of the Great Ghostfence. This singular work offers insight into the spiritual foundations of Dunmer society and their intricate relationship with death and memory.', '''abhor'':148B ''adapt'':165B ''also'':155B ''ancestor'':1A,5B,23B,45B,76B,124B ''ancestr'':62B,167B ''anonym'':12B ''becom'':88B ''bond'':39B ''book'':99B,130B ''bound'':83B ''call'':52B ''chang'':173B ''clash'':138B ''construct'':60B,176B ''cultur'':140B ''death'':198B ''delv'':131B ''descend'':80B ''door'':54B ''dualist'':114B ''dunmer'':4A,8B,31B,42B,103B,147B,191B ''duti'':71B ''emphas'':66B ''empire’'':159B ''explor'':36B ''famili'':50B,70B,134B ''fenc'':59B ''foreign'':120B ''fortifi'':56B ''foundat'':189B ''ghost'':58B,90B ''ghostfenc'':180B ''great'':179B ''guardian'':93B ''guid'':16B ''highlight'':100B ''howev'':81B ''human'':117B ''import'':68B ''insight'':185B ''interconnect'':107B ''intric'':195B ''like'':174B ''loyalti'':135B ''mad'':89B ''magic'':27B ''maintain'':46B ''manipul'':95B ''may'':87B ''memori'':200B ''misinterpret'':123B ''morrowind'':33B ''mortal'':110B ''necrom'':127B,144B ''oblivion'':105B ''offer'':184B ''often'':122B ''outsid'':18B,149B ''particular'':142B ''percept'':141B ''perspect'':115B ''polici'':160B ''practic'':28B,65B,168B ''protect'':75B ''provid'':77B ''regard'':143B ''relationship'':196B ''remain'':63B ''rever'':133B ''ritual'':48B,97B ''sacr'':38B,151B ''scholar'':13B ''seek'':19B ''shrine'':51B ''singular'':182B ''societi'':192B ''spirit'':26B,82B ''spiritu'':74B,188B ''text'':35B,154B ''themat'':128B ''toler'':162B ''touch'':156B ''tradit'':152B ''understand'':21B ''unlik'':112B ''use'':91B ''vener'':24B ''view'':104B,121B ''wait'':53B ''wake'':171B ''work'':183B ''world'':111B ''worship'':125B ''written'':9B', 'scholar', '
Ancestors and the Dunmer, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, explores the Dunmer''s practices of ancestor veneration, spirit magic, and the sacred bond with their ancestors. Thematically, it examines reverence, familial loyalty, and the clash of cultural perceptions, especially regarding the misinterpretation of ancestor worship as necromancy, while highlighting the Dunmer''s unique spiritual relationship with death and Oblivion.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stalhrim', '
Stalhrim is a rare, enchanted ice found only on the island of Solstheim. It has a rich history, initially used in ancient Nordic burial rituals to encase the deceased as a form of protection, and later as a crafting material for weapons, armor, clothing, and jewelry. Stalhrim armor can be made in light or heavy variants and is known for its impressive protection. It also enhances frost enchantments, making them more powerful.

Described as a rigid, blue-white crystalline metal, stalhrim is as hard as iron and nearly indestructible by conventional means. The only way to mine it is with an ancient Nordic pickaxe, crafted with superior skill. In addition to its use in armor and crafting, raw stalhrim can be used in alchemy to induce paralysis and inflict frost damage. Working with stalhrim is similar to ebony smithing and requires the expertise of a skilled blacksmith.', '''addit'':112B ''alchemi'':126B ''also'':66B ''ancient'':23B,104B ''armor'':44B,49B,117B ''blacksmith'':149B ''blue'':79B ''blue-whit'':78B ''burial'':25B ''cloth'':45B ''convent'':93B ''craft'':40B,107B,119B ''crystallin'':81B ''damag'':133B ''deceas'':30B ''describ'':74B ''eboni'':140B ''encas'':28B ''enchant'':6B,69B ''enhanc'':67B ''expertis'':145B ''form'':33B ''found'':8B ''frost'':68B,132B ''hard'':86B ''heavi'':56B ''histori'':19B ''ice'':7B ''impress'':63B ''indestruct'':91B ''induc'':128B ''inflict'':131B ''initi'':20B ''iron'':88B ''island'':12B ''jewelri'':47B ''known'':60B ''later'':37B ''light'':54B ''made'':52B ''make'':70B ''materi'':41B ''mean'':94B ''metal'':82B ''mine'':99B ''near'':90B ''nordic'':24B,105B ''paralysi'':129B ''pickax'':106B ''power'':73B ''protect'':35B,64B ''rare'':5B ''raw'':120B ''requir'':143B ''rich'':18B ''rigid'':77B ''ritual'':26B ''similar'':138B ''skill'':110B,148B ''smith'':141B ''solstheim'':14B ''stalhrim'':1A,2B,48B,83B,121B,136B ''superior'':109B ''use'':21B,115B,124B ''variant'':57B ''way'':97B ''weapon'':43B ''white'':80B ''work'':134B', 'blacksmith, skaal', 'Stalhrim is a rare, enchanted ice found only on the island of Solstheim. It has a rich history, initially used in ancient Nordic burial rituals to encase the deceased as a form of protection, and later as a crafting material for weapons, armor, clothing, and jewelry. Stalhrim armor can be made in light or heavy variants and is known for its impressive protection. It also enhances frost enchantments, making them more powerful.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_frozen_hearth', 'The Frozen Hearth is a cozy inn located in the heart of Winterhold, one of the few inhabited buildings left in the city. Situated directly across the street from the Jarl''s Longhouse, it serves as a central gathering point for the remaining residents of Winterhold, offering a warm respite from the harsh northern climate.

The inn is run by Dagur, a Nord innkeeper, alongside his wife Haran, who operates a food stall in the town. Together, they manage The Frozen Hearth, providing food, drink, and shelter to the people of Winterhold. Their daughter, Eirid, also resides in the inn, with her parents working together to maintain the establishment and serve the few souls left in the dwindling city.', '''across'':29B ''alongsid'':68B ''also'':99B ''build'':22B ''central'':41B ''citi'':26B,122B ''climat'':58B ''cozi'':9B ''dagur'':64B ''daughter'':97B ''direct'':28B ''drink'':88B ''dwindl'':121B ''eirid'':98B ''establish'':112B ''food'':75B,87B ''frozen'':2A,5B,84B ''gather'':42B ''haran'':71B ''harsh'':56B ''heart'':14B ''hearth'':3A,6B,85B ''inhabit'':21B ''inn'':10B,60B,103B ''innkeep'':67B ''jarl'':34B ''left'':23B,118B ''locat'':11B ''longhous'':36B ''maintain'':110B ''manag'':82B ''nord'':66B ''northern'':57B ''offer'':50B ''one'':17B ''oper'':73B ''parent'':106B ''peopl'':93B ''point'':43B ''provid'':86B ''remain'':46B ''resid'':47B,100B ''respit'':53B ''run'':62B ''serv'':38B,114B ''shelter'':90B ''situat'':27B ''soul'':117B ''stall'':76B ''street'':31B ''togeth'':80B,108B ''town'':79B ''warm'':52B ''wife'':70B ''winterhold'':16B,49B,95B ''work'':107B', 'winterhold, innkeeper, traveler', 'The Frozen Hearth is a cozy inn located in the heart of Winterhold, one of the few inhabited buildings left in the city. You do not know who runs the Inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('raven_rock', 'Raven Rock is a city located on the southwest coast of Solstheim, serving as the first settlement encountered in the Dragonborn expansion. Once a thriving East Empire Company mining outpost, it has since become a House Redoran colony. The depletion of its ebony mine has left Raven Rock a shadow of its former prosperity, now a largely forgotten settlement struggling to endure amidst the ash-laden environment caused by the nearby Red Mountain.

The city features a single thoroughfare running from the entrance through the Bulwark in the east to the Earth Stone in the west, following the curve of a small adjacent bay. The Bulwark, a sturdy defensive wall, houses both the city’s jail and the Redoran guards'' garrison, providing protection against the encroaching ash. A curved wooden boardwalk lines the bay, complete with a short pier and a longer pier to the east, where the Northern Maiden is docked, offering transport between Solstheim and Windhelm in Skyrim.

Raven Rock''s central marketplace, located near the city''s well north of the bay, is home to its shops and services. The Temple of Raven Rock is situated near the Bulwark to the east, providing spiritual guidance to the community. Scattered throughout the city are various crafting stations, including smelters, tanning racks, a forge, an alchemy lab, and more, located near key sites such as Alor House, Glover Mallory''s House, Ienth Farm, and Raven Rock Mine. ', '''adjac'':106B ''alchemi'':219B ''alor'':229B ''amidst'':65B ''ash'':68B,129B ''ash-laden'':67B ''bay'':107B,136B,177B ''becom'':36B ''boardwalk'':133B ''bulwark'':89B,109B,194B ''caus'':71B ''central'':166B ''citi'':7B,78B,171B,207B ''city’'':117B ''coast'':12B ''coloni'':40B ''communiti'':203B ''compani'':30B ''complet'':137B ''craft'':210B ''curv'':102B,131B ''defens'':112B ''deplet'':42B ''dock'':154B ''dragonborn'':23B ''earth'':95B ''east'':28B,92B,148B,197B ''eboni'':45B ''empir'':29B ''encount'':20B ''encroach'':128B ''endur'':64B ''entranc'':86B ''environ'':70B ''expans'':24B ''farm'':236B ''featur'':79B ''first'':18B ''follow'':100B ''forg'':217B ''forgotten'':60B ''former'':55B ''garrison'':123B ''glover'':231B ''guard'':122B ''guidanc'':200B ''home'':179B ''hous'':38B,114B,230B,234B ''ienth'':235B ''includ'':212B ''jail'':118B ''key'':225B ''lab'':220B ''laden'':69B ''larg'':59B ''left'':48B ''line'':134B ''locat'':8B,168B,223B ''longer'':144B ''maiden'':152B ''mallori'':232B ''marketplac'':167B ''mine'':31B,46B,240B ''mountain'':76B ''near'':169B,192B,224B ''nearbi'':74B ''north'':174B ''northern'':151B ''offer'':155B ''outpost'':32B ''pier'':141B,145B ''prosper'':56B ''protect'':125B ''provid'':124B,198B ''rack'':215B ''raven'':1A,3B,49B,163B,188B,238B ''red'':75B ''redoran'':39B,121B ''rock'':2A,4B,50B,164B,189B,239B ''run'':83B ''scatter'':204B ''serv'':15B ''servic'':184B ''settlement'':19B,61B ''shadow'':52B ''shop'':182B ''short'':140B ''sinc'':35B ''singl'':81B ''site'':226B ''situat'':191B ''skyrim'':162B ''small'':105B ''smelter'':213B ''solstheim'':14B,158B ''southwest'':11B ''spiritu'':199B ''station'':211B ''stone'':96B ''struggl'':62B ''sturdi'':111B ''tan'':214B ''templ'':186B ''thoroughfar'':82B ''thrive'':27B ''throughout'':205B ''transport'':156B ''various'':209B ''wall'':113B ''well'':173B ''west'':99B ''windhelm'':160B ''wooden'':132B', 'solstheim, noble, scholar', 'Raven Rock is a city located on the southwest coast of Solstheim, serving as the first settlement encountered in the Dragonborn expansion. Once a thriving East Empire Company mining outpost, it has since become a House Redoran colony. You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skaal_village', 'Skaal Village is a small, secluded settlement located in the northeastern region of Solstheim, along the Felsaad Coast, just north of Lake Fjalding and east of the Isild River. It is home to the Skaal, a unique offshoot tribe of Nords who live in harmony with nature as part of their worship of the All-Maker. The Skaal lead a simple, self-sufficient life in the frozen north, relying on hunting, minor agriculture, and their knowledge of crafting stalhrim, a rare and ancient material.

The village consists of eight buildings arranged in a circle around a central well, reflecting the communal nature of Skaal society. The Skaal believe Solstheim was originally part of Skyrim, transformed into an island during a climactic battle between Dragon Cult loyalists and rebels. The Skaal trace their lineage back to the loyalist faction and have preserved their history through oral tradition. This narrative is supported by archaeological evidence, including multiple Dragon Cult ruins and carvings uncovered in the Fourth Era. ', '''agricultur'':77B ''all-mak'':57B ''along'':17B ''ancient'':87B ''archaeolog'':156B ''around'':99B ''arrang'':95B ''back'':138B ''battl'':126B ''believ'':112B ''build'':94B ''carv'':164B ''central'':101B ''circl'':98B ''climact'':125B ''coast'':20B ''communal'':105B ''consist'':91B ''craft'':82B ''cult'':129B,161B ''dragon'':128B,160B ''east'':27B ''eight'':93B ''era'':169B ''evid'':157B ''faction'':142B ''felsaad'':19B ''fjald'':25B ''fourth'':168B ''frozen'':71B ''harmoni'':47B ''histori'':147B ''home'':34B ''hunt'':75B ''includ'':158B ''isild'':30B ''island'':122B ''knowledg'':80B ''lake'':24B ''lead'':62B ''life'':68B ''lineag'':137B ''live'':45B ''locat'':10B ''loyalist'':130B,141B ''maker'':59B ''materi'':88B ''minor'':76B ''multipl'':159B ''narrat'':152B ''natur'':49B,106B ''nord'':43B ''north'':22B,72B ''northeastern'':13B ''offshoot'':40B ''oral'':149B ''origin'':115B ''part'':51B,116B ''preserv'':145B ''rare'':85B ''rebel'':132B ''reflect'':103B ''region'':14B ''reli'':73B ''river'':31B ''ruin'':162B ''seclud'':8B ''self'':66B ''self-suffici'':65B ''settlement'':9B ''simpl'':64B ''skaal'':1A,3B,37B,61B,108B,111B,134B ''skyrim'':118B ''small'':7B ''societi'':109B ''solstheim'':16B,113B ''stalhrim'':83B ''suffici'':67B ''support'':154B ''trace'':135B ''tradit'':150B ''transform'':119B ''tribe'':41B ''uncov'':165B ''uniqu'':39B ''villag'':2A,4B,90B ''well'':102B ''worship'':54B', 'skaal. scholar, miraakcult', 'Skaal Village is a small, secluded settlement located in the northeastern region of Solstheim. It is home to the Skaal, Nordic people who worship animal gods.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'solstheim', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('castle_karstaag_caverns', 'Castle Karstaag Caverns is a medium-sized cave located on the north coast of Solstheim, southeast of Castle Karstaag Ruins. The cave serves as a refuge for bristlebacks and rieklings, who have made the area their domain. Its remote and rugged setting adds to its mystique and danger.

The entrance to the caverns lies above a tall waterfall that cascades into an inlet by the sea. The path leading to the entrance descends from the west-southwest, following a stream that feeds the waterfall. ', '''add'':47B ''area'':39B ''bristleback'':32B ''cascad'':64B ''castl'':1A,4B,22B ''cave'':12B,26B ''cavern'':3A,6B,57B ''coast'':17B ''danger'':52B ''descend'':77B ''domain'':41B ''entranc'':54B,76B ''feed'':87B ''follow'':83B ''inlet'':67B ''karstaag'':2A,5B,23B ''lead'':73B ''lie'':58B ''locat'':13B ''made'':37B ''medium'':10B ''medium-s'':9B ''mystiqu'':50B ''north'':16B ''path'':72B ''refug'':30B ''remot'':43B ''riekl'':34B ''rug'':45B ''ruin'':24B ''sea'':70B ''serv'':27B ''set'':46B ''size'':11B ''solstheim'':19B ''southeast'':20B ''southwest'':82B ''stream'':85B ''tall'':61B ''waterfal'':62B,89B ''west'':81B ''west-southwest'':80B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('temple_of_miraak', 'The Temple of Miraak is a foreboding Nordic temple located west of Thirsk Mead Hall and north of Kagrumez, perched high on the rocky landscape of Solstheim. The temple is a place of dark power, housing cultists devoted to the mysterious and malevolent Miraak, as well as the restless draugr who serve as its ancient guardians. The temple is a place of chilling atmosphere, where the echoes of forgotten rituals still linger in the air.

The main approach to the temple is from the west, where travelers must climb wide flights of stairs, past the bleached bones of fallen dragons, a grim reminder of Miraak’s ancient dominion over both men and beasts. As you ascend, you pass beneath a pair of large stone arches, their surfaces marred by time but still imposing. The arches are flanked by construction scaffolding, hinting at ongoing efforts to maintain the temple, yet the dark energy within remains undisturbed. The Temple of Miraak stands as a monumental testament to Solstheim’s forgotten past, a place of both allure and danger for those daring enough to venture within.', '''air'':78B ''allur'':175B ''ancient'':58B,109B ''approach'':81B ''arch'':127B,137B ''ascend'':118B ''atmospher'':67B ''beast'':115B ''beneath'':121B ''bleach'':99B ''bone'':100B ''chill'':66B ''climb'':92B ''construct'':141B ''cultist'':40B ''danger'':177B ''dare'':180B ''dark'':37B,153B ''devot'':41B ''dominion'':110B ''dragon'':103B ''draugr'':53B ''echo'':70B ''effort'':146B ''energi'':154B ''enough'':181B ''fallen'':102B ''flank'':139B ''flight'':94B ''forebod'':10B ''forgotten'':72B,169B ''grim'':105B ''guardian'':59B ''hall'':18B ''high'':24B ''hint'':143B ''hous'':39B ''impos'':135B ''kagrumez'':22B ''landscap'':28B ''larg'':125B ''linger'':75B ''locat'':13B ''main'':80B ''maintain'':148B ''malevol'':46B ''mar'':130B ''mead'':17B ''men'':113B ''miraak'':3A,7B,47B,161B ''miraak’'':108B ''monument'':165B ''must'':91B ''mysteri'':44B ''nordic'':11B ''north'':20B ''ongo'':145B ''pair'':123B ''pass'':120B ''past'':97B,170B ''perch'':23B ''place'':35B,64B,172B ''power'':38B ''remain'':156B ''remind'':106B ''restless'':52B ''ritual'':73B ''rocki'':27B ''scaffold'':142B ''serv'':55B ''solstheim'':30B ''solstheim’'':168B ''stair'':96B ''stand'':162B ''still'':74B,134B ''stone'':126B ''surfac'':129B ''templ'':1A,5B,12B,32B,61B,84B,150B,159B ''testament'':166B ''thirsk'':16B ''time'':132B ''travel'':90B ''undisturb'':157B ''ventur'':183B 