INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mzulft', 'Mzulft is a large Dwarven ruin located south-southeast of Windhelm and north-northwest of Stony Creek Cave in Eastmarch. There are rumours of imperial mages entering the ruins recently. ', '''cave'':21B ''creek'':20B ''dwarven'':6B ''eastmarch'':23B ''enter'':30B ''imperi'':28B ''larg'':5B ''locat'':8B ''mage'':29B ''mzulft'':1A,2B ''north'':16B ''north-northwest'':15B ''northwest'':17B ''recent'':33B ''ruin'':7B,32B ''rumour'':26B ''south'':10B ''south-southeast'':9B ''southeast'':11B ''stoni'':19B ''windhelm'':13B', 'eastmarch, dwemer', 'Mzulft is a large Dwarven ruin located south-southeast of Windhelm in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('south_skybound_watch', 'Skybound Watch Pass is a small Nordic tower and ruin located northeast of Helgen and west of Orphan Rock in Falkreath Hold.', '''falkreath'':24B ''helgen'':17B ''hold'':25B ''locat'':14B ''nordic'':10B ''northeast'':15B ''orphan'':21B ''pass'':6B ''rock'':22B ''ruin'':13B ''skybound'':2A,4B ''small'':9B ''south'':1A ''tower'':11B ''watch'':3A,5B ''west'':19B', 'falkreath', 'Skybound Watch Pass is a small Nordic tower and ruin located northeast of Helgen in Falkreath Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('16_accords_of_madness', 'In 16 Accords of Madness, written by Shalidor recounts vivid tales of Sheogorath''s chaotic encounters with other Daedric Princes, highlighting his unparalleled cunning and penchant for disorder. One such tale details a contest between Sheogorath and Hircine, where each was to groom a beast for battle. While Hircine bred a monstrous Daedroth imbued with lycanthropy, Sheogorath introduced a tiny, colorful bird. Despite its size, the bird''s antics drove the Daedroth into a self-destructive frenzy, humiliating Hircine. Another account describes a wager between Sheogorath and Vaermina, testing their influence over a mortal bard, Darius Shano. Vaermina subjected the bard to horrific dreams that fueled his notoriety, while Sheogorath withdrew her presence, letting bitterness and madness consume him. Ultimately, Sheogorath claimed Darius''s soul, demonstrating the intricate interplay of madness and creation.

In another tale, Sheogorath''s manipulations involve the Orc champion Emmeg Gro-Kayra, who receives a cursed blade, Neb-Crescen, from a mysterious figure. The blade drives Emmeg to commit an unspeakable act, killing another Orc in a frenzied state. This crime draws Malacath, who, seeking vengeance, unknowingly slays his own son. Sheogorath appears to claim the fallen champion''s severed head and weapon, leaving Malacath in despair. These stories exemplify Sheogorath''s talent for sowing chaos, exposing the vulnerabilities of even the mightiest beings, and illustrating the destructive yet oddly creative nature of his madness.', '''16'':1A,6B ''accord'':2A,7B ''account'':86B ''act'':173B ''anoth'':85B,140B,175B ''antic'':73B ''appear'':194B ''bard'':100B,106B ''battl'':51B ''be'':225B ''beast'':49B ''bird'':66B,71B ''bitter'':120B ''blade'':157B,166B ''bred'':54B ''champion'':148B,199B ''chao'':217B ''chaotic'':19B ''claim'':127B,196B ''color'':65B ''commit'':170B ''consum'':123B ''contest'':38B ''creation'':138B ''creativ'':232B ''crescen'':160B ''crime'':182B ''cun'':28B ''curs'':156B ''daedric'':23B ''daedroth'':57B,76B ''darius'':101B,128B ''demonstr'':131B ''describ'':87B ''despair'':208B ''despit'':67B ''destruct'':81B,229B ''detail'':36B ''disord'':32B ''draw'':183B ''dream'':109B ''drive'':167B ''drove'':74B ''emmeg'':149B,168B ''encount'':20B ''even'':222B ''exemplifi'':211B ''expos'':218B ''fallen'':198B ''figur'':164B ''frenzi'':82B,179B ''fuel'':111B ''gro'':151B ''gro-kayra'':150B ''groom'':47B ''head'':202B ''highlight'':25B ''hircin'':42B,53B,84B ''horrif'':108B ''humili'':83B ''illustr'':227B ''imbu'':58B ''influenc'':96B ''interplay'':134B ''intric'':133B ''introduc'':62B ''involv'':145B ''kayra'':152B ''kill'':174B ''leav'':205B ''let'':119B ''lycanthropi'':60B ''mad'':4A,9B,122B,136B,236B ''malacath'':184B,206B ''manipul'':144B ''mightiest'':224B ''monstrous'':56B ''mortal'':99B ''mysteri'':163B ''natur'':233B ''neb'':159B ''neb-crescen'':158B ''not