INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('morag_tong', 'The Morag Tong, or "Foresters Guild" in Dark Elvish, is an ancient guild of assassins based in Morrowind, operating under the patronage of the Daedric Prince Mephala. Founded in the First Era, the Morag Tong gained prominence as a means to settle disputes within Morrowind''s Great Houses, preventing open warfare through sanctioned killings known as Honorable Writs of Execution. These writs allowed assassins to carry out legal executions with complete immunity, cementing their role in Dunmeri politics. Despite their lawful standing in Morrowind, their methods and allegiance to Mephala stirred controversy. Some legends suggest the guild originally worshipped Sithis and even influenced the formation of the Dark Brotherhood, a splinter group that rose to prominence outside of Morrowind. Over centuries, the Morag Tong oscillated between shadowy obscurity and political power, adapting to the changing tides of history.

The guild''s practices reflect Mephala''s principles of subtlety and precision, with their assassins employing shortblades, light armor, and archery as their tools of choice. Their deadly arsenal is meticulously crafted, blending functionality with intimidating designs that evoke chitinous creatures. The Morag Tong''s influence waned during periods of upheaval, such as after the assassination of the Akaviri Potentate Versidue-Shaie, but they resurfaced in times of need, maintaining their ancient role as arbiters of Dunmeri vendettas. Despite their decline after the Red Year, the Morag Tong remains active, taking contracts on Solstheim and mainland Morrowind, and often clashing with their sworn enemies, the Dark Brotherhood. Bound by their strict code and enduring reverence for Mephala, the Morag Tong continues to embody the dark yet lawful traditions of Morrowind’s political and spiritual heritage.', '''activ'':231B ''adapt'':134B ''akaviri'':199B ''allegi'':90B ''allow'':65B ''ancient'':14B,213B ''arbit'':216B ''archeri'':161B ''armor'':159B ''arsenal'':169B ''assassin'':17B,66B,155B,196B ''base'':18B ''blend'':173B ''bound'':249B ''brotherhood'':111B,248B ''carri'':68B ''cement'':75B ''centuri'':123B ''chang'':137B ''chitin'':180B ''choic'':166B ''clash'':241B ''code'':253B ''complet'':73B ''continu'':262B ''contract'':233B ''controversi'':94B ''craft'':172B ''creatur'':181B ''daedric'':27B ''dark'':10B,110B,247B,266B ''dead'':168B ''declin'':222B ''design'':177B ''despit'':81B,220B ''disput'':45B ''dunmeri'':79B,218B ''elvish'':11B ''embodi'':264B ''employ'':156B ''endur'':255B ''enemi'':245B ''era'':34B ''even'':104B ''evok'':179B ''execut'':62B,71B ''first'':33B ''forest'':7B ''format'':107B ''found'':30B ''function'':174B ''gain'':38B ''great'':49B ''group'':114B ''guild'':8B,15B,99B,142B ''heritag'':275B ''histori'':140B ''honor'':59B ''hous'':50B ''immun'':74B ''influenc'':105B,186B ''intimid'':176B ''kill'':56B ''known'':57B ''law'':83B,268B ''legal'':70B ''legend'':96B ''light'':158B ''mainland'':237B ''maintain'':211B ''mean'':42B ''mephala'':29B,92B,146B,258B ''method'':88B ''meticul'':171B ''morag'':1A,4B,36B,125B,183B,228B,260B ''morrowind'':20B,47B,86B,121B,238B ''morrowind’'':271B ''need'':210B ''obscur'':130B ''often'':240B ''open'':52B ''oper'':21B ''origin'':100B ''oscil'':127B ''outsid'':119B ''patronag'':24B ''period'':189B ''polit'':80B,132B,272B ''potent'':200B ''power'':133B ''practic'':144B ''precis'':152B ''prevent'':51B ''princ'':28B ''principl'':148B ''promin'':39B,118B ''red'':225B ''reflect'':145B ''remain'':230B ''resurfac'':206B ''rever'':256B ''role'':77B,214B ''rose'':116B ''sanction'':55B ''settl'':44B ''shadowi'':129B ''shaie'':203B ''shortblad'':157B ''sithi'':102B ''solstheim'':235B ''spiritu'':274B ''splinter'':113B ''stand'':84B ''stir'':93B ''strict'':252B ''subtleti'':150B ''suggest'':97B ''sworn'':244B ''take'':232B ''tide'':138B ''time'':208B ''tong'':2A,5B,37B,126B,184B,229B,261B ''tool'':164B ''tradit'':269B ''upheav'':191B ''vendetta'':219B ''versidu'':202B ''versidue-shai'':201B ''wane'':187B ''warfar'':53B ''within'':46B ''worship'':101B ''writ'':60B,64B ''year'':226B ''yet'':267B', 'darkelf, scholar', '
The Morag Tong, an ancient assassin guild in Morrowind, operates under the patronage of Mephala, settling Great House disputes through sanctioned Honorable Writs of Execution, granting legal immunity to its assassins. Founded in the First Era, the guild is known for its precision, subtlety, and use of shortblades and chitinous-themed weaponry, reflecting Mephala''s influence. Though their power declined after events like the Red Year, they remain active in Solstheim and Morrowind, often clashing with the Dark Brotherhood, a splinter group linked to their Sithis-worshipping origins. The Morag Tong continues to embody Morrowind''s dark yet lawful traditions.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('torval', '
Torval, one of Elsweyr''s eight major cities, is nestled within the lush jungles of the Tenmar Forest, serving as the spiritual and political heart of the Khajiit. Historically a center of worship for the Mane, the revered leader of the Khajiit, Torval''s cultural and religious significance dates back to its origins as one of the sixteen ancient Khajiiti kingdoms. Its layout features grand timber palaces surrounded by symmetrical moon-sugarcane gardens, where the Mane meditates and governs. The city is renowned for its rare ochre pigment, southern wines, and temples like the famed Temple of Two-Moons Dance, a hub for hand-to-hand combat training that attracts students from across Tamriel.

Throughout its history, Torval has endured various challenges, from the dissolution of the sixteen kingdoms following the Thrassian Plague to its involvement in conflicts such as the Five Year War and the Slaughter of Torval. In the Second Era, under the leadership of Mane Akkhuz-ri and his Speaker, Lord Gharesh-ri, Torval played a pivotal role in forming the Aldmeri Dominion during the Knahaten Flu crisis. By the Third Era, the city saw rebellion, cultural vibrancy, and significant events such as Emperor Pelagius III''s legendary asylum ball. Despite its turbulent history, Torval remains a symbol of Khajiiti resilience and tradition, blending ancient customs with its enduring political and spiritual importance.', '''across'':117B ''akkhuz'':164B ''akkhuz-ri'':163B ''aldmeri'':181B ''ancient'':60B,224B ''asylum'':208B ''attract'':114B ''back'':51B ''ball'':209B ''blend'':223B ''center'':32B ''challeng'':126B ''citi'':9B,83B,193B ''combat'':111B ''conflict'':142B ''crisi'':187B ''cultur'':46B,196B ''custom'':225B ''danc'':103B ''date'':50B ''despit'':210B ''dissolut'':129B ''dominion'':182B ''eight'':7B ''elsweyr'':5B ''emperor'':203B ''endur'':124B,228B ''era'':157B,191B ''event'':200B ''fame'':97B ''featur'':65B ''five'':146B ''flu'':186B ''follow'':134B ''forest'':19B ''form'':179B ''garden'':75B ''gharesh'':171B ''gharesh-ri'':170B ''govern'':81B ''grand'':66B ''hand'':108B,110B ''hand-to-hand'':107B ''heart'':26B ''histor'':30B ''histori'':121B,213B ''hub'':105B ''iii'':205B ''import'':232B ''involv'':140B ''jungl'':15B ''khajiit'':29B,43B ''khajiiti'':61B,219B ''kingdom'':62B,133B ''knahaten'':185B ''layout'':64B ''leader'':40B ''leadership'':160B ''legendari'':207B ''like'':95B ''lord'':169B ''lush'':14B ''major'':8B ''mane'':37B,78B,162B ''medit'':79B ''moon'':73B,102B ''moon-sugarcan'':72B ''nestl'':11B ''ochr'':89B ''one'':3B,56B ''origin'':54B ''palac'':68B ''pelagius'':204B ''pigment'':90B ''pivot'':176B ''plagu'':137B ''play'':174B ''polit'':25B,229B ''rare'':88B ''rebellion'':195B ''religi'':48B ''remain'':215B ''renown'':85B ''resili'':220B ''rever'':39B ''ri'':165B,172B ''role'':177B ''saw'':194B ''second'':156B ''serv'':20B ''signific'':49B,199B ''sixteen'':59B,132B ''slaughter'':151B ''southern'':91B ''speaker'':168B ''spiritu'':23B,231B ''student'':115B ''sugarcan'':74B ''surround'':69B ''symbol'':217B ''symmetr'':71B ''tamriel'':118B ''templ'':94B,98B ''tenmar'':18B ''third'':190B ''thrassian'':136B ''throughout'':119B ''timber'':67B ''torval'':1A,2B,44B,122B,153B,173B,214B ''tradit'':222B ''train'':112B ''turbul'':212B ''two'':101B ''two-moon'':100B ''various'':125B ''vibranc'':197B ''war'':148B ''wine'':92B ''within'':12B ''worship'':34B ''year'':147B', 'scholar, khajiit', '
Torval, one of Elsweyr''s major cities, is located in the Tenmar Forest and serves as the spiritual and political center for the Khajiit. Known for its significance as a religious hub for the Mane, Torval features grand palaces and moon-sugarcane gardens, along with the Temple of Two-Moons Dance, a renowned combat training site. Over its history, the city has faced challenges like the dissolution of the ancient Khajiiti kingdoms, involvement in the Five Year War, and the Slaughter of Torval. Despite these events, Torval remains a symbol of Khajiiti resilience, blending tradition with political and spiritual importance.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hydnum_azure_giant_spore', 'Hydnum Azure Giant Spore, a blue-purple sphere plant originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Resist Frost, Fortify Health, and Regenerate Health.', '''alchemi'':30B ''azur'':2A,6B ''blue'':11B ''blue-purpl'':10B ''caravan'':29B ''effect'':31B ''fortifi'':34B ''frost'':33B ''giant'':3A,7B ''health'':35B,38B ''hydnum'':1A,5B ''ingredi'':22B ''isl'':19B ''khajiit'':28B ''origin'':15B ''plant'':14B ''purchas'':26B ''purpl'':12B ''regener'':37B ''resist'':32B ''shiver'':18B ''sphere'':13B ''spore'':4A,8B', 'alchemist', 'Hydnum Azure Giant Spore, a blue-purple sphere plant originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
