You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vittoria_vici', 'Vittoria Vici is an influential Imperial from Solitude, cousin to Emperor Titus Mede II, and oversees the East Empire Company''s holdings in the city. Engaged to Stormcloak Asgeir Snow-Shod, their upcoming wedding is seen as a symbolic end to the civil war. However, the event attracts the attention of the Dark Brotherhood, who plan to use it to restore their reputation.', '''asgeir'':31B ''attent'':53B ''attract'':51B ''brotherhood'':57B ''citi'':27B ''civil'':46B ''compani'':22B ''cousin'':11B ''dark'':56B ''east'':20B ''emperor'':13B ''empir'':21B ''end'':43B ''engag'':28B ''event'':50B ''hold'':24B ''howev'':48B ''ii'':16B ''imperi'':8B ''influenti'':7B ''mede'':15B ''overse'':18B ''plan'':59B ''reput'':66B ''restor'':64B ''seen'':39B ''shod'':34B ''snow'':33B ''snow-shod'':32B ''solitud'':10B ''stormcloak'':30B ''symbol'':42B ''titus'':14B ''upcom'':36B ''use'':61B ''vici'':2A,4B ''vittoria'':1A,3B ''war'':47B ''wed'':37B', 'noble, darkbrotherhood', 'Vittoria Vici is an influential Imperial from Solitude, cousin to Emperor Titus Mede II, and oversees the East Empire Company''s holdings in the city. She is having a wedding in Solitude at somepoint.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lok_vah_koor', 'Clear Skies is a Shout that causes Skyrim itself to yield before the Thu''um, clearing away fog and inclement weather. The three words of power in this Shout are Lok (Sky), which calls upon the power of the heavens; Vah (Spring), which ushers in clear, refreshing weather; and Koor (Summer), which brings warm, clear skies to the land.', '''away'':20B ''bring'':56B ''call'':37B ''caus'':10B ''clear'':4B,19B,49B,58B ''fog'':21B ''heaven'':43B ''inclement'':23B ''koor'':3A,53B ''land'':62B ''lok'':1A,34B ''power'':29B,40B ''refresh'':50B ''shout'':8B,32B ''sky'':5B,35B,59B ''skyrim'':11B ''spring'':45B ''summer'':54B ''three'':26B ''thu'':17B ''um'':18B ''upon'':38B ''usher'':47B ''vah'':2A,44B ''warm'':57B ''weather'':24B,51B ''word'':27B ''yield'':14B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('physicalities_of_werewolves', 'Experimentation in the Physicalities of the Werewolf, written by Reman Crex, is a morbid and scientific examination of the physical changes that occur in werewolves during their transformations. The author, with no personal vendetta against werewolves, delves into the anatomy and biology of these creatures, conducting gruesome experiments on live subjects in an attempt to better understand the nature of their physical changes. The experiments observe subjects in both their human and werewolf forms, noting the physical changes in proportions, muscle structure, and the effects on internal organs. Crex''s focus is solely on the physiological aspects, deliberately ignoring the origins, causes, and potential cures for lycanthropy.

The book explores themes of obsession with the unnatural, scientific curiosity, and the moral implications of experimenting on living creatures. Through his clinical and detached observations, Crex reveals the disturbing and often painful transformations that werewolves undergo, highlighting the inhuman nature of the affliction. The experiments, which ultimately result in the death of the subjects, emphasize the brutality of Crex''s approach. The work is a single volume, presenting an unsettling look at the physical aspects of lycanthropy from a purely anatomical perspective.', '''afflict'':154B ''anatom'':192B ''anatomi'':43B ''approach'':172B ''aspect'':100B,186B ''attempt'':57B ''author'':33B ''better'':59B ''biolog'':45B ''book'':112B ''brutal'':168B ''caus'':105B ''chang'':24B,66B,81B ''clinic'':133B ''conduct'':49B ''creatur'':48B,130B ''crex'':14B,92B,137B,170B ''cure'':108B ''curios'':121B ''death'':162B ''deliber'':101B ''delv'':40B ''detach'':135B ''disturb'':140B ''effect'':88B ''emphas'':166B ''examin'':20B ''experi'':51B,68B,127B,156B ''experiment'':4B ''explor'':113B ''focus'':94B ''form'':77B ''gruesom'':50B ''highlight'':148B ''human'':74B ''ignor'':102B ''implic'':125B ''inhuman'':150B ''intern'':90B ''live'':53B,129B ''look'':182B ''lycanthropi'':110B,188B ''moral'':124B ''morbid'':17B ''muscl'':84B ''natur'':62B,151B ''note'':78B ''observ'':69B,136B ''obsess'':116B ''occur'':26B ''often'':142B ''organ'':91B ''origin'':104B ''pain'':143B ''person'':36B ''perspect'':193B ''physic'':1A,7B,23B,65B,80B,185B ''physiolog'':99B ''potenti'':107B ''present'':179B ''proport'':83B ''pure'':191B ''reman'':13B ''result'':159B ''reveal'':138B ''scientif'':19B,120B ''singl'':177B ''sole'':96B ''structur'':85B ''subject'':54B,70B,165B ''theme'':114B ''transform'':31B,144B ''ultim'':158B ''undergo'':147B ''understand'':60B ''unnatur'':119B ''unsettl'':181B ''vendetta'':37B ''volum'':178B ''werewolf'':10B,76B ''werewolv'':3A,28B,39B,146B ''work'':174B ''written'':11B', 'scholar', '
