INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedric_mace', 'Daedric Mace is a blunt Daedric weapon which deals Godly damage. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. To craft it: 1 Daedra heart, 3 ebony ingots, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using ebony at a workbench.', '''1'':38B,45B ''3'':41B ''accent'':29B ''aura'':34B ''blacksmith'':50B ''blunt'':7B ''craft'':36B,56B ''daedra'':39B ''daedric'':1A,3B,8B ''damag'':13B ''dark'':18B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''eboni'':42B,64B ''edg'':24B ''exud'':31B ''forg'':51B ''glow'':27B ''god'':12B ''heart'':40B ''ingot'':43B ''jag'':23B ''leather'':46B ''mace'':2A,4B ''master'':53B ''menac'':20B ''red'':28B ''sharp'':22B ''sinist'':33B ''smith'':54B ''strip'':47B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Daedric Mace is a blunt Daedric weapon which deals Godly damage. Its visual design is dark and menacing, with sharp, jagged edges and a glowing red accent that exudes a sinister aura. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frostmoon_crag', 'Frostmoon Crag is a small, secluded camp located under a rock overhang south of Mount Moesring and northeast of the Abandoned Lodge on Solstheim. The camp is inhabited by werewolves, who have created a sanctuary away from the rest of the island''s inhabitants.', '''abandon'':23B ''away'':38B ''camp'':9B,28B ''crag'':2A,4B ''creat'':35B ''frostmoon'':1A,3B ''inhabit'':30B,46B ''island'':44B ''locat'':10B ''lodg'':24B ''moesr'':18B ''mount'':17B ''northeast'':20B ''overhang'':14B ''rest'':41B ''rock'':13B ''sanctuari'':37B ''seclud'':8B ''small'':7B ''solstheim'':26B ''south'':15B ''werewolv'':32B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bard''s_leap_summit', 'Bard''s Leap Summit is a wooden plank situated at the very top of Lost Valley Redoubt in the Reach, roughly halfway between Markarth and Falkreath. Reaching the summit requires battling through Forsworn who occupy the ruins and ascending to the highest point of the structure.

At the summit, a narrow walkway extends over the edge of a waterfall, offering a dramatic and scenic view. Legend has it that leaping from the plank and surviving the fall can lead to great reawrds.', '''ascend'':43B ''bard'':1A,5B ''battl'':35B ''dramat'':66B ''edg'':60B ''extend'':57B ''falkreath'':30B ''fall'':81B ''forsworn'':37B ''great'':85B ''halfway'':26B ''highest'':46B ''lead'':83B ''leap'':3A,7B,74B ''legend'':70B ''lost'':19B ''markarth'':28B ''narrow'':55B ''occupi'':39B ''offer'':64B ''plank'':12B,77B ''point'':47B ''reach'':24B,31B ''reawrd'':86B ''redoubt'':21B ''requir'':34B ''rough'':25B ''ruin'':41B ''scenic'':68B ''situat'':13B ''structur'':50B ''summit'':4A,8B,33B,53B ''surviv'':79B ''top'':17B ''valley'':20B ''view'':69B ''walkway'':56B ''waterfal'':63B ''wooden'':11B', 'reach, bard', 'Bard''s Leap Summit is a wooden plank situated at the very top of Lost Valley Redoubt in the Reach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wheat', 'Wheat is commonly grown in farms around Skyrim and is used for various alchemical and culinary purposes. Alchemy effects: Restore Health, Fortify Health, Damage Stamina Regen, and Lingering Damage Magicka.', '''alchem'':15B ''alchemi'':19B ''around'':8B ''common'':4B ''culinari'':17B ''damag'':25B,30B ''effect'':20B ''farm'':7B ''fortifi'':23B ''grown'':5B ''health'':22B,24B ''linger'':29B ''magicka'':31B ''purpos'':18B ''regen'':27B ''restor'':21B ''skyrim'':9B ''stamina'':26B ''use'':12B ''various'':14B ''wheat'':1A,2B', 'alchemist', 'Wheat is commonly grown in farms around Skyrim and is used for various alchemical and culinary purposes. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('greenpact', 'The Green Pact is a strict code followed by the Bosmer of Valenwood, focused on preserving the forest, known as "the Green." It prohibits harming plants, eating plant-based foods, and mandates that enemies be consumed, typically within three days of their death. Bosmer who adhere to the Pact are fiercely protective of Valenwood and will attack anyone who threatens it. However, the Pact allows for some exceptions, such as eating dairy, honey, and insects. The Pact also involves a unique form of magic that enables Bosmer to shape their settlements within the forest using ritualistic practices, and the Wild Hunt, a transformative ritual allowing the Bosmer to shift into powerful beasts, is a key feature of their culture.

In return for their protection of Valenwood, the Bosmer are granted patronage from Y''ffre, the god of the Green. The Pact is enforced by the Spinners of Y''ffre, spiritual leaders who hold great influence. The Bosmer are known for their devotion to the Pact, even when it involves great personal sacrifice, such as allowing loved ones to die rather than break the rules. The Green Pact has led to conflicts with outsiders and tensions with other races, particularly over the felling of trees. Despite their fierce reputation, the Bosmer are highly intelligent and hospitable to those who respect their beliefs. Breaking the Pact is considered a severe crime, often punishable by sacrifice to the Green itself.', '''adher'':48B ''allow'':67B,107B,177B ''also'':80B ''anyon'':60B ''attack'':59B ''base'':31B ''beast'':114B ''belief'':223B ''bosmer'':12B,46B,89B,109B,130B,159B,212B ''break'':184B,224B ''code'':8B ''conflict'':193B ''consid'':228B ''consum'':38B ''crime'':231B ''cultur'':121B ''dairi'':74B ''day'':42B ''death'':45B ''despit'':207B ''devot'':164B ''die'':181B ''eat'':28B,73B ''enabl'':88B ''enemi'':36B ''enforc'':145B ''even'':168B ''except'':70B ''featur'':118B ''fell'':204B ''ffre'':136B,151B ''fierc'':53B,209B ''focus'':15B ''follow'':9B ''food'':32B ''forest'':19B,96B ''form'':84B ''god'':138B ''grant'':132B ''great'':156B,172B ''green'':3B,23B,141B,188B,238B ''greenpact'':1A ''harm'':26B ''high'':214B ''hold'':155B ''honey'':75B ''hospit'':217B ''howev'':64B ''hunt'':103B ''influenc'':157B ''insect'':77B ''intellig'':215B ''involv'':81B,171B ''key'':117B ''known'':20B,161B ''leader'':153B ''led'':191B ''love'':178B ''magic'':86B ''mandat'':34B ''often'':232B ''one'':179B ''outsid'':195B ''pact'':4B,51B,66B,79B,143B,167B,189B,226B ''particular'':201B ''patronag'':133B ''person'':173B ''plant'':27B,30B ''plant-bas'':29B ''power'':113B ''practic'':99B ''preserv'':17B ''prohibit'':25B ''protect'':54B,126B ''punish'':233B ''race'':200B ''rather'':182B ''reput'':210B ''respect'':221B ''return'':123B ''ritual'':106B ''ritualist'':98B ''rule'':186B ''sacrific'':174B,235B ''settlement'':93B ''sever'':230B ''shape'':91B ''shift'':111B ''spinner'':148B ''spiritu'':152B ''strict'':7B ''tension'':197B ''threaten'':62B ''three'':41B ''transform'':105B ''tree'':206B ''typic'':39B ''uniqu'':83B ''use'':97B ''valenwood'':14B,56B,128B ''wild'':102B ''within'':40B,94B ''y'':135B,150B', 'woodelf, scholar', '
The Green Pact is a strict code followed by the Bosmer of Valenwood, focused on protecting the forest and prohibiting the harming of plants or eating plant-based foods. Bosmer are required to consume the flesh of enemies and are fiercely protective of Valenwood, with exceptions for certain foods like dairy and insects. The Pact also grants Bosmer magical abilities to shape settlements and perform the Wild Hunt, a ritual that transforms them into powerful beasts. The Bosmer are deeply devoted to the Pact, with violations often punishable by sacrifice to the Green.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stalhrim_light_boots', 'Stalhrim Light Boots are a pair of stalhrim boots with fantastic protection quality. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding. To craft it: 3 stalhrim, 1 steel ingot, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using stalhrim at a workbench.', '''1'':39B ''2'':43B ''3'':37B ''appear'':30B ''blacksmith'':48B ''blue'':27B ''boot'':3A,6B,12B ''cold'':31B ''craft'':35B,54B ''crystallin'':23B ''design'':19B ''expert'':51B ''fantast'':14B ''forg'':49B ''frosti'':26B ''ici'':21B ''ingot'':41B ''leather'':44B ''light'':2A,5B ''pair'':9B ''protect'':15B ''qualiti'':16B ''sheen'':28B ''smith'':52B ''stalhrim'':1A,4B,11B,38B,62B ''steel'':40B ''strip'':45B ''tempered/improved'':59B ''unyield'':33B ''use'':61B ''visual'':18B ''workbench'':65B', 'blacksmith', 'Stalhrim Light Boots are a pair of stalhrim boots with fantastic protection quality. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nordic_boots', 'Nordic Carved Boots are a pair of Nordic carved boots with great protection quality. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. To craft it: 1 ebony ingot, 1 quicksilver ingot, 2 leather strips, and 4 steel ingots at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using quicksilver at a workbench.', '''1'':41B,44B ''2'':47B ''4'':51B ''adept'':59B ''ancient'':36B ''blacksmith'':56B ''boot'':2A,5B,12B ''carv'':4B,11B ''craft'':39B,62B ''craftsmanship'':37B ''design'':19B ''eboni'':42B ''engrav'':33B ''evok'':35B ''finish'':29B ''forg'':57B ''gray'':28B ''great'':14B ''ingot'':43B,46B,53B ''intric'':31B ''leather'':48B ''nordic'':1A,3B,10B,32B ''pair'':8B ''protect'':15B ''qualiti'':16B ''quicksilv'':45B,70B ''silver'':27B ''silver-gray'':26B ''smith'':60B ''steel'':52B ''strip'':49B ''sturdi'':21B ''tempered/improved'':67B ''use'':69B ''visual'':18B ''weather'':23B ''workbench'':73B', 'blacksmith', 'Nordic Carved Boots are a pair of Nordic carved boots with great protection quality. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_larceny', 'The Potion of Larceny makes lockpicking and pickpocketing easier for a brief time. It is crafted in tiers ranging from potion to prime elixir, offering increasing effectiveness. Rumors suggest it may have something to do with Glover Mallory in Raven Rock, though nothing is confirmed.', '''brief'':15B ''confirm'':48B ''craft'':19B ''easier'':12B ''effect'':30B ''elixir'':27B ''glover'':40B ''increas'':29B ''larceni'':3A,7B ''lockpick'':9B ''make'':8B ''mallori'':41B ''may'':34B ''noth'':46B ''offer'':28B ''pickpocket'':11B ''potion'':1A,5B,24B ''prime'':26B ''rang'':22B ''raven'':43B ''rock'':44B ''rumor'':31B ''someth'':36B ''suggest'':32B ''though'':45B ''tier'':21B ''time'':16B', 'thievesguild', 'You don''t know anything about this, but it sounds like something the Thieves Guild might find useful by the sound of it.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_holds_of_skyrim', 'The Holds of Skyrim: A Field Officer''s Guide, written by Imperial Legion Officers, is an official guide detailing the geography and strategic importance of the nine holds of Skyrim. The guide offers insights on each hold''s terrain, inhabitants, and potential significance in the ongoing civil conflict, focusing on the military concerns of the Empire. The holds range from the strategically important to the practically irrelevant. Key holds like Eastmarch, Haafingar, and the Reach are highlighted for their direct importance in the war, while others like Hjaalmarch and Winterhold are noted for their limited strategic value but still necessary to monitor. The guide emphasizes the difficulty of maintaining control in the hostile climate of Skyrim, with specific warnings about local threats such as the Stormcloaks, the Forsworn, and criminal organizations like the Thieves'' Guild.

The overarching theme is the Empire''s continued struggle to maintain order and dominance in a province rife with rebellion, harsh terrain, and resource scarcity. The guide provides crucial information for military officers tasked with securing Skyrim, focusing on the challenges of each hold while acknowledging the unpredictable nature of local governance and resistance. It serves as both a practical military resource and a reflection on the complexities of ruling a volatile province.', '''acknowledg'':185B ''challeng'':180B ''civil'':51B ''climat'':118B ''complex'':207B ''concern'':57B ''conflict'':52B ''continu'':147B ''control'':114B ''crimin'':134B ''crucial'':168B ''detail'':23B ''difficulti'':111B ''direct'':84B ''domin'':153B ''eastmarch'':75B ''emphas'':109B ''empir'':60B,145B ''field'':10B ''focus'':53B,177B ''forsworn'':132B ''geographi'':25B ''govern'':191B ''guid'':13B,22B,36B,108B,166B ''guild'':139B ''haafingar'':76B ''harsh'':160B ''highlight'':81B ''hjaalmarch'':92B ''hold'':2A,6B,32B,41B,62B,73B,183B ''hostil'':117B ''imperi'':16B ''import'':28B,67B,85B ''inform'':169B ''inhabit'':44B ''insight'':38B ''irrelev'':71B ''key'':72B ''legion'':17B ''like'':74B,91B,136B ''limit'':99B ''local'':125B,190B ''maintain'':113B,150B ''militari'':56B,171B,200B ''monitor'':106B ''natur'':188B ''necessari'':104B ''nine'':31B ''note'':96B ''offer'':37B ''offic'':11B,18B,172B ''offici'':21B ''ongo'':50B ''order'':151B ''organ'':135B ''other'':90B ''overarch'':141B ''potenti'':46B ''practic'':70B,199B ''provid'':167B ''provinc'':156B,212B ''rang'':63B ''reach'':79B ''rebellion'':159B ''reflect'':204B ''resist'':193B ''resourc'':163B,201B ''rife'':157B ''rule'':209B ''scarciti'':164B ''secur'':175B ''serv'':195B ''signific'':47B ''skyrim'':4A,8B,34B,120B,176B ''specif'':122B ''still'':103B ''stormcloak'':130B ''strateg'':27B,66B,100B ''struggl'':148B ''task'':173B ''terrain'':43B,161B ''theme'':142B ''thiev'':138B ''threat'':126B ''unpredict'':187B ''valu'':101B ''vola