INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('belyn_hlaalu''s_house', 'Belyn Hlaalu''s House is a modest dwelling located in the Gray Quarter of Windhelm, positioned as the first house on the left when entering the district from Candlehearth Hall.

The house is the residence of Belyn Hlaalu, the owner of Hlaalu Farm, who lives there alone. ', '''alon'':51B ''belyn'':1A,5B,41B ''candlehearth'':33B ''district'':31B ''dwell'':12B ''enter'':29B ''farm'':47B ''first'':23B ''gray'':16B ''hall'':34B ''hlaalu'':2A,6B,42B,46B ''hous'':4A,8B,24B,36B ''left'':27B ''live'':49B ''locat'':13B ''modest'':11B ''owner'':44B ''posit'':20B ''quarter'':17B ''resid'':39B ''windhelm'':19B', 'eastmarch', 'Belyn Hlaalu''s House is a modest dwelling located in the Gray Quarter of Windhelm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_cabin_in_the_woods', 'The Cabin in the Woods, Volume II, as Told By Mogen Son of Molag, recounts the harrowing tale of a soldier’s journey through a haunted forest. After encountering eerie sobbing on his first night, the soldier faces a ghostly woman wielding an axe, who appears at his campfire and later in an abandoned cabin where he seeks refuge. The story builds tension as the soldier confronts his fear, ultimately defeating the ghost with a scroll of firebolt. Though he escapes the forest, the tale closes on an ominous note, with the sound of sobbing echoing behind him.

Themes of perseverance, courage in the face of supernatural terror, and the lingering nature of fear permeate the story. The tale captures the atmosphere of isolation, suspense, and the chilling realization that some forces cannot be entirely escaped. It is a standalone narrative and part of a larger tradition of eerie folklore within Skyrim’s world.', '''abandon'':58B ''appear'':50B ''atmospher'':126B ''axe'':48B ''behind'':101B ''build'':66B ''cabin'':2A,7B,59B ''campfir'':53B ''cannot'':137B ''captur'':124B ''chill'':132B ''close'':90B ''confront'':71B ''courag'':106B ''defeat'':75B ''echo'':100B ''eeri'':34B,153B ''encount'':33B ''entir'':139B ''escap'':85B,140B ''face'':42B,109B ''fear'':73B,118B ''firebolt'':82B ''first'':38B ''folklor'':154B ''forc'':136B ''forest'':31B,87B ''ghost'':44B,77B ''harrow'':22B ''haunt'':30B ''ii'':12B ''isol'':128B ''journey'':27B ''larger'':150B ''later'':55B ''linger'':115B ''mogen'':16B ''molag'':19B ''narrat'':145B ''natur'':116B ''night'':39B ''note'':94B ''omin'':93B ''part'':147B ''permeat'':119B ''persever'':105B ''realiz'':133B ''recount'':20B ''refug'':63B ''scroll'':80B ''seek'':62B ''skyrim’'':156B ''sob'':35B,99B ''soldier'':41B,70B ''soldier’'':26B ''son'':17B ''sound'':97B ''standalon'':144B ''stori'':65B,121B ''supernatur'':111B ''suspens'':129B ''tale'':23B,89B,123B ''tension'':67B ''terror'':112B ''theme'':103B ''though'':83B ''told'':14B ''tradit'':151B ''ultim'':74B ''volum'':11B ''wield'':46B ''within'':155B ''woman'':45B ''wood'':5A,10B ''world'':157B', 'scholar', 'The Cabin in the Woods, Volume II, as Told By Mogen Son of Molag, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, recounts a soldier''s encounter with a ghostly woman in a haunted forest, showcasing his courage and perseverance as he confronts supernatural terror. Themes of fear, isolation, and the haunting realization that some forces linger beyond escape are central to the story.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('movarth''s_lair', 'Movarth''s Lair is a small cave located north-northeast of Morthal and southwest of Ustengrav in Hjaalmarch. The lair is home to vampires led by Movarth Piquine and consists of a single zone.

A winding path connects the cave to Morthal, making it accessible for adventurers investigating the vampire menace in the region. ', '''access'':49B ''adventur'':51B ''cave'':10B,44B ''connect'':42B ''consist'':34B ''hjaalmarch'':22B ''home'':26B ''investig'':52B ''lair'':3A,6B,24B ''led'':29B ''locat'':11B ''make'':47B ''menac'':55B ''morthal'':16B,46B ''movarth'':1A,4B,31B ''north'':13B ''north-northeast'':12B ''northeast'':14B ''path'':41B ''piquin'':32B ''region'':58B ''singl'':37B ''small'':9B ''southwest'':18B ''ustengrav'':20B ''vampir'':28B,54B ''wind'':40B ''zone'':38B', 'hjaalmarch, vampire', 'Movarth''s Lair is a small cave located north-northeast of Morthal.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glass_dagger', 'Glass Dagger is a light glass weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is sleek and translucent, with sharp edges and a greenish hue resembling polished malachite. To craft it: 1 refined malachite, 1 refined moonstone, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using moonstone at a workbench.', '''1'':34B,37B,41B ''adept'':55B ''blacksmith'':46B ''craft'':32B,52B,58B ''dagger'':2A,4B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''edg'':23B ''expert'':49B ''fantast'':12B ''forg'':47B ''glass'':1A,3B,8B ''greenish'':26B ''hue'':27B ''it.it'':59B ''leather'':42B ''light'':7B ''malachit'':30B,36B ''moonston'':39B,65B ''polish'':29B ''refin'':35B,38B ''resembl'':28B ''sharp'':22B ''sleek'':18B ''smith'':50B,56B ''strip'':43B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''transluc'':20B ''use'':64B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Glass Dagger is a light glass weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is sleek and translucent, with sharp edges and a greenish hue resembling polished malachite. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
