INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('crown_of_barenziah', 'The Crown of Barenziah is a legendary coronation artifact crafted for Queen Barenziah during her ascension to the throne of Mournhold in the early Third Era, under the reign of Emperor Tiber Septim. This golden crown features a striking winged motif adorned with twenty-four ornate jewels, known as the Stones of Barenziah, set across its wings and a central gem on its temple. However, the crown’s grandeur was short-lived as it was stolen shortly after the coronation. The thief pried the stones from the crown, scattering them across Skyrim. The crown itself remained in Morrowind for much of its history, while the Thieves Guild of Skyrim sought to recover its scattered stones for centuries.', '''across'':59B,95B ''adorn'':45B ''artifact'':12B ''ascens'':19B ''barenziah'':3A,7B,16B,57B ''central'':64B ''centuri'':121B ''coron'':11B,84B ''craft'':13B ''crown'':1A,5B,39B,92B,98B ''crown’'':71B ''earli'':27B ''emperor'':34B ''era'':29B ''featur'':40B ''four'':49B ''gem'':65B ''golden'':38B ''grandeur'':72B ''guild'':111B ''histori'':107B ''howev'':69B ''jewel'':51B ''known'':52B ''legendari'':10B ''live'':76B ''morrowind'':102B ''motif'':44B ''mournhold'':24B ''much'':104B ''ornat'':50B ''pri'':87B ''queen'':15B ''recov'':116B ''reign'':32B ''remain'':100B ''scatter'':93B,118B ''septim'':36B ''set'':58B ''short'':75B,81B ''short-liv'':74B ''skyrim'':96B,113B ''sought'':114B ''stolen'':80B ''stone'':55B,89B,119B ''strike'':42B ''templ'':68B ''thief'':86B ''thiev'':110B ''third'':28B ''throne'':22B ''tiber'':35B ''twenti'':48B ''twenty-four'':47B ''wing'':43B,61B', 'scholar', 'The Crown of Barenziah is a legendary artifact created for Queen Barenziah''s coronation in the early Third Era. The golden crown, adorned with twenty-four jewels known as the Stones of Barenziah, was stolen after the coronation, and its jewels were scattered across Skyrim. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fort_snowhawk', 'Fort Snowhawk is a medium-sized fort located west of Morthal and south of The Apprentice Stone in Hjaalmarch. It has been taken over by necromancers.', '''apprentic'':19B ''fort'':1A,3B,10B ''hjaalmarch'':22B ''locat'':11B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''morthal'':14B ''necromanc'':29B ''size'':9B ''snowhawk'':2A,4B ''south'':16B ''stone'':20B ''taken'':26B ''west'':12B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Fort Snowhawk is a medium-sized fort located west of Morthal.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frostbite', 'Frostbite is a Destruction spell that projects a continuous stream of frost, dealing frost damage to health and stamina. It requires a Novice skill level to cast.', '''cast'':28B ''continu'':10B ''damag'':16B ''deal'':14B ''destruct'':5B ''frost'':13B,15B ''frostbit'':1A,2B ''health'':18B ''level'':26B ''novic'':24B ''project'':8B ''requir'':22B ''skill'':25B ''spell'':6B ''stamina'':20B ''stream'':11B', 'mage', 'Frostbite is a spell that releases a continuous stream of frost, freezing enemies and draining their health and stamina. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonsreach', 'Dragonsreach is a prominent location in the Cloud District of Whiterun, a central city in Skyrim. Situated atop three flights of stairs beginning at the Gildergreen tree, this iconic palace serves as the residence of the Jarl of Whiterun Hold, the seat of the hold’s political power, and the location of its jail. Overlooking the city and with the Throat of the World as its backdrop, Dragonsreach is divided into four main sections: the main hall, the Jarl’s Quarters, the Great Porch, and the dungeon.

The palace is steeped in history and legend, having been built around the remnants of a dragon trap purportedly used by Olaf One-Eye. Its interior is a hub of activity, centered around the Jarl’s throne, where courtiers and family members move about amidst ornate furnishings, grand feasts, and a roaring hearth. The court wizard’s laboratory and the Jarl’s personal quarters further enhance the palace''s grandeur, with treasures and artifacts scattered throughout.

Dragonsreach’s dungeon serves as Whiterun''s jail, featuring several cells, evidence storage, and an escape tunnel leading to the Guard Barracks. The Great Porch, once a dragon’s prison, now serves as a multipurpose area for guard training and hosting quests pivotal to Skyrim’s Civil War and main storyline. As a symbol of both Whiterun’s authority and its role in Skyrim’s tumultuous history, Dragonsreach stands as a monument to power, strategy, and lore.', '''activ'':118B ''amidst'':131B ''area'':194B ''around'':98B,120B ''artifact'':158B ''atop'':19B ''author'':215B ''backdrop'':67B ''barrack'':181B ''begin'':24B ''built'':97B ''cell'':170B ''center'':119B ''central'':14B ''citi'':15B,57B ''civil'':204B ''cloud'':9B ''court'':141B ''courtier'':125B ''district'':10B ''divid'':70B ''dragon'':103B ''dragonsreach'':1A,2B,68B,223B ''dragonsreach’'':161B ''dragon’'':187B ''dungeon'':86B,162B ''enhanc'':150B ''escap'':175B ''evid'':171B ''eye'':111B ''famili'':127B ''feast'':135B ''featur'':168B ''flight'':21B ''four'':72B ''furnish'':133B ''gildergreen'':27B ''grand'':134B ''grandeur'':154B ''great'':82B,183B ''guard'':180B,196B ''hall'':77B ''hearth'':139B ''histori'':92B,222B ''hold'':41B ''hold’'':46B ''host'':199B ''hub'':116B ''icon'':30B ''interior'':113B ''jail'':54B,167B ''jarl'':38B ''jarl’'':79B,122B,146B ''laboratori'':143B ''lead'':177B ''legend'':94B ''locat'':6B,51B ''lore'':232B ''main'':73B,76B,207B ''member'':128B ''monument'':227B ''move'':129B ''multipurpos'':193B ''olaf'':108B ''one'':110B ''one-ey'':109B ''ornat'':132B ''overlook'':55B ''palac'':31B,88B,152B ''person'':147B ''pivot'':201B ''polit'':47B ''porch'':83B,184B ''power'':48B,229B ''prison'':188B ''promin'':5B ''purport'':105B ''quarter'':80B,148B ''quest'':200B ''remnant'':100B ''resid'':35B ''roar'':138B ''role'':218B ''scatter'':159B ''seat'':43B ''section'':74B ''serv'':32B,163B,190B ''sever'':169B ''situat'':18B ''skyrim'':17B ''skyrim’'':203B,220B ''stair'':23B ''stand'':224B ''steep'':90B ''storag'':172B ''storylin'':208B ''strategi'':230B ''symbol'':211B ''three'':20B ''throat'':61B ''throne'':123B ''throughout'':160B ''train'':197B ''trap'':104B ''treasur'':156B ''tree'':28B ''tumultu'':221B ''tunnel'':176B ''use'':106B ''war'':205B ''whiterun'':12B,40B,165B ''whiterun’'':214B ''wizard’'':142B ''world'':64B', 'whiterun, noble, scholar', '
Dragonsreach, perched in the Cloud District of Whiterun, is the grand palace of the Jarl and the heart of Whiterun Hold’s political power. Dragonsreach is not just a residence but a historic landmark, said to be built around a dragon trap used by Olaf One-Eye. ', '', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_arcturian_heresy', '
The Arcturian Heresy, written by The Underking, Ysmir Kingmaker, explores the early history of Tiber Septim and his rise as the first Emperor of Tamriel, presenting a controversial narrative that questions the accepted myths of the Empire. The text chronicles the Underking’s involvement with Tiber Septim, from aiding his military campaigns to enabling the unification of Tamriel through the construction of the Numidium. However, betrayal and manipulation underpin their relationship, culminating in the Underking’s death, Zurin Arctus’s treachery, and the ultimate ascension of Tiber Septim as Talos Stormcrown. Themes of divine ambition, mortal frailty, and the rewriting of history for political gain permeate the narrative, emphasizing the complexities of leadership and power.

This singular volume combines myth and history, casting doubt on official accounts of Tiber Septim’s reign, including his origins, military conquests, and the true nature of the Numidium. It delves into the interplay between mortals and gods, loyalty and betrayal, and the enduring enigma of Talos, whose legend remains central to the identity of the Empire.', '''accept'':36B ''account'':127B ''aid'':51B ''ambit'':95B ''arcturian'':2A,5B ''arctus’'':80B ''ascens'':85B ''betray'':68B,155B ''campaign'':54B ''cast'':123B ''central'':165B ''chronicl'':43B ''combin'':119B ''complex'':111B ''conquest'':136B ''construct'':63B ''controversi'':31B ''culmin'':74B ''death'':78B ''delv'':145B ''divin'':94B ''doubt'':124B ''earli'':15B ''emperor'':26B ''emphas'':109B ''empir'':40B,171B ''enabl'':56B ''endur'':158B ''enigma'':159B ''explor'':13B ''first'':25B ''frailti'':97B ''gain'':105B ''god'':152B ''heresi'':3A,6B ''histori'':16B,102B,122B ''howev'':67B ''ident'':168B ''includ'':132B ''interplay'':148B ''involv'':46B ''kingmak'':12B ''leadership'':113B ''legend'':163B ''loyalti'':153B ''manipul'':70B ''militari'':53B,135B ''mortal'':96B,150B ''myth'':37B,120B ''narrat'':32B,108B ''natur'':140B ''numidium'':66B,143B ''offici'':126B ''origin'':134B ''permeat'':106B ''polit'':104B ''power'':115B ''present'':29B ''question'':34B ''reign'':131B ''relationship'':73B ''remain'':164B ''rewrit'':100B ''rise'':22B ''septim'':19B,49B,88B ''septim’'':130B ''singular'':117B ''stormcrown'':91B ''talo'':90B,161B ''tamriel'':28B,60B ''text'':42B ''theme'':92B ''tiber'':18B,48B,87B,129B ''treacheri'':81B ''true'':139B ''ultim'':84B ''underk'':10B ''underking’'':45B,77B ''underpin'':71B ''unif'':58B ''volum'':118B ''whose'':162B ''written'':7B ''ysmir'':11B ''zurin'':79B', 'scholar', ' The Arcturian Heresy, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, challenges the official narratives of Tiber Septim''s rise to power and explores his complex relationship with the Underking. Thematically, the book delves into divine ambition, mortal frailty, betrayal, and the manipulation of history for political purposes, casting doubt on the myths surrounding Tiber Septim’s reign.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('unrelenting_force', 'Unrelenting Force is a Shout that uses raw power to push aside anything or anyone in your path. The three words of power in this Shout are Fus (Force), which unleashes the power of your voice; Ro (Balance), which knocks back enemies and objects; and Dah (Push), which sends your target flying, clearing your way.', '''anyon'':17B ''anyth'':15B ''asid'':14B ''back'':43B ''balanc'':40B ''clear'':55B ''dah'':48B ''enemi'':44B ''fli'':54B ''forc'':2A,4B,31B ''fus'':30B ''knock'':42B ''object'':46B ''path'':20B ''power'':11B,25B,35B ''push'':13B,49B ''raw'':10B ''ro'':39B ''send'':51B ''shout'':7B,28B ''target'':53B ''three'':22B ''unleash'':33B ''unrel'':1A,3B ''use'':9B ''voic'':38B ''way'':57B ''word'':23B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
