Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. To craft it: 1 netch leather, 1 iron ingots, 8 bonemold at a blacksmith forge. An Apprentice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using bonemeal at a workbench.', '''1'':39B,42B ''8'':45B ''apprentic'':52B ''basic'':7B,11B ''bind'':31B ''blacksmith'':49B ''bone'':25B ''bone-lik'':24B ''bonem'':63B ''bonemold'':1A,3B,8B,46B ''craft'':37B,55B ''dark'':30B ''design'':16B ''forg'':50B ''helmet'':9B ''ingot'':44B ''iron'':43B ''leather'':41B ''like'':26B ''netch'':40B ''organ'':20B ''protect'':12B ''qualiti'':13B ''reinforc'':28B ''rough'':18B ''shape'':35B ''shield'':2A,4B ''smith'':53B ''tan'':23B ''tempered/improved'':60B ''textur'':27B ''use'':62B ''utilitarian'':34B ''visual'':15B ''workbench'':66B', 'blacksmith', 'Bonemold Shield is a basic bonemold helmet with basic protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('corrundum', 'Corundum is a valuable metal used primarily for creating stronger alloys in the crafting of weapons and armor. When mixed with iron, it produces steel, a widely utilized material known for its durability. The most common alloy consists of equal parts of iron and corundum, while smaller amounts can enhance the strength of lower-quality alloys, such as those used in banded iron armor. Additionally, by incorporating extra corundum into steel, blacksmiths can forge advanced armors, including scaled and steel plate varieties.', '''addit'':67B ''advanc'':77B ''alloy'':12B,38B,58B ''amount'':49B ''armor'':19B,66B,78B ''band'':64B ''blacksmith'':74B ''common'':37B ''consist'':39B ''corrundum'':1A ''corundum'':2B,46B,71B ''craft'':15B ''creat'':10B ''durabl'':34B ''enhanc'':51B ''equal'':41B ''extra'':70B ''forg'':76B ''includ'':79B ''incorpor'':69B ''iron'':23B,44B,65B ''known'':31B ''lower'':56B ''lower-qu'':55B ''materi'':30B ''metal'':6B ''mix'':21B ''part'':42B ''plate'':83B ''primarili'':8B ''produc'':25B ''qualiti'':57B ''scale'':80B ''smaller'':48B ''steel'':26B,73B,82B ''strength'':53B ''stronger'':11B ''use'':7B,62B ''util'':29B ''valuabl'':5B ''varieti'':84B ''weapon'':17B ''wide'':28B', 'blacksmith', 'Corundum is a valuable metal used primarily for creating stronger alloys in the crafting of weapons and armor. ', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('whirlwind_cloak', 'These magical effects are offensive Destruction spells that surround the caster with a vortex of wind, repelling enemies and creating a protective barrier. This effect is only available as a spell, making it a defensive tool for combat-focused mages.', '''avail'':30B ''barrier'':25B ''caster'':13B ''cloak'':2A ''combat'':41B ''combat-focus'':40B ''creat'':22B ''defens'':37B ''destruct'':8B ''effect'':5B,27B ''enemi'':20B ''focus'':42B ''mage'':43B ''magic'':4B ''make'':34B ''offens'':7B ''protect'':24B ''repel'':19B ''spell'':9B,33B ''surround'':11B ''tool'':38B ''vortex'':16B ''whirlwind'':1A ''wind'':18B', 'mage', 'This spell surrounds the caster with wind, pushing enemies away and keeping them at a distance. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('void_essence', 'Void Essence, a light red crystal originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Restore Health, Fortify Health, Fortify Stamina, and Regenerate Health.', '''alchemi'':24B ''caravan'':23B ''crystal'':8B ''effect'':25B ''essenc'':2A,4B ''fortifi'':28B,30B ''health'':27B,29B,34B ''ingredi'':16B ''isl'':13B ''khajiit'':22B ''light'':6B ''origin'':9B ''purchas'':20B ''red'':7B ''regener'':33B ''restor'':26B ''shiver'':12B ''stamina'':31B ''void'':1A,3B', 'alchemist', 'Void Essence, a light red crystal originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_dagger', 'Dwarven Dagger is a light dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. To craft it: 1 dwarven metal ingot, 1 steel ingot, 1 iron ingot, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dwarvern ingot at a workbench.', '''1'':34B,38B,41B,45B ''adept'':53B ''angular'':18B ''blacksmith'':50B ''bronz'':25B ''craft'':32B,56B ''dagger'':2A,4B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,8B,35B ''dwarvern'':64B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':51B ''golden'':24B ''golden-bronz'':23B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':37B,40B,43B,65B ''intric'':28B ''iron'':42B ''leather'':46B ''light'':7B ''mechan'':29B ''metal'':36B ''ornat'':20B ''pattern'':30B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':39B ''strip'':47B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Dwarven Dagger is a light dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elven_gilded_armor', 'Elven Gilded Armor has good protection quality. Its visual design is elegant and golden, with smooth curves and intricate patterns that reflect refined craftsmanship. To craft it: 4 refined moonstone, 1 quicksilver ingot, 1 iron ingot, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using moonstone at a workbench.', '''1'':34B,37B ''3'':41B ''4'':31B ''adept'':49B ''armor'':3A,6B ''blacksmith'':46B ''craft'':29B,52B ''craftsmanship'':27B ''curv'':20B ''design'':13B ''eleg'':15B ''elven'':1A,4B ''forg'':47B ''gild'':2A,5B ''golden'':17B ''good'':8B ''ingot'':36B,39B ''intric'':22B ''iron'':38B ''it.it'':53B ''leather'':42B ''moonston'':33B,59B ''pattern'':23B ''protect'':9B ''qualiti'':10B ''quicksilv'':35B ''refin'':26B,32B ''reflect'':25B ''smith'':50B ''smooth'':19B ''strip'':43B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''use'':58B ''visual'':12B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Elven Gilded Armor has good protection quality. Its visual design is elegant and golden, with smooth curves and intricate patterns that reflect refined craftsmanship. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('scaled_bracers', 'Scaled Bracers are a pair of scaled bracers with good protection quality. 
Its visual design is sleek and layered, resembling overlapping metallic scales with a polished, reflective surface. To craft it: 1 leather, 1 steel ingots, and 1 corrundum ingots and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge.. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using corrundum at a workbench.', '''..'':51B ''1'':34B,36B,40B ''2'':44B ''adept'':53B ''blacksmith'':49B ''bracer'':2A,4B,10B ''corrundum'':41B,64B ''craft'':32B,56B ''design'':17B ''forg'':50B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':38B,42B ''layer'':21B ''leather'':35B,45B ''metal'':24B ''overlap'':23B ''pair'':7B ''polish'':28B ''protect'':13B ''qualiti'':14B ''reflect'':29B ''resembl'':22B ''scale'':1A,3B,9B,25B ''sleek'':19B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':37B ''strip'':46B ''surfac'':30B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':16B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Scaled Bracers are a pair of scaled bracers with good protection quality. 
Its visual design is sleek and layered, resembling overlapping metallic scales with a polished, reflective surface. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('resist_magic', 'These magical effects are defensive Restoration abilities that reduce damage taken from all forms of magic, offering broad protection against hostile spells. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted items. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Resist Magic effect: Bleeding Crown, Hagraven Claw, Nirnroot, Tundra Cotton', '''abil'':9B ''also'':42B ''appli'':44B ''avail'':28B ''bleed'':71B ''brew'':36B ''broad'':20B ''claw'':74B ''combin'':49B ''cotton'':77B ''craft'':32B ''creat'':63B ''crown'':72B ''custom'':38B ''damag'':12B ''defens'':7B ''effect'':5B,26B,61B,70B ''enchant'':46B ''follow'':55B ''form'':16B ''general'':48B ''hagraven'':73B ''hostil'':23B ''ingredi'':56B ''item'':47B ''least'':51B ''magic'':2A,4B,18B,69B ''nirnroot'':75B ''offer'':19B ''potion'':33B,39B,65B ''pre'':31B ''pre-craft'':30B ''protect'':21B ''provid'':57B ''reduc'':11B ''resist'':1A,68B ''restor'':8B ''share'':59B ''spell'':24B ''taken'':13B ''tundra'':76B ''two'':52B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic protects you from magical attacks, making spells hurt less. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chance''s_folly', '
Chance''s Folly, written by Zylmoc Golge, tells the cautionary tale of Minevah Iolos, a skilled thief known as "Chance," whose ambition and betrayal lead to her demise. The story follows her partnership with Ulstyr Moresby, a seemingly mad Breton warrior, as they explore the Heran Ancestral Tomb in search of treasure. While Chance relies on her lockpicking prowess and cunning, Ulstyr’s cryptic ramblings and combat skills prove vital to their survival. However, as they delve deeper into the tomb, Chance grows suspicious of Ulstyr’s enigmatic knowledge, ultimately plotting to betray him once the treasure is found.

Themes of greed, mistrust, and divine intervention are central to the narrative. Chance''s overconfidence and disregard for her partner’s peculiar insights lead her to activate a trap that seals her inside the treasure room, leaving her to perish. Ulstyr returns two months later, fulfilling his eerie prophecy of "two months and back" to claim the gold. The tale underscores the folly of deceit and the unpredictable influence of the Daedric Prince Sheogorath, whose presence looms over the story’s events.', '''activ'':126B ''ambit'':25B ''ancestr'':50B ''back'':153B ''betray'':27B,94B ''breton'':43B ''cautionari'':13B ''central'':109B ''chanc'':1A,4B,23B,57B,84B,113B ''claim'':155B ''combat'':69B ''cryptic'':66B ''cun'':64B ''daedric'':171B ''deceit'':164B ''deeper'':80B ''delv'':79B ''demis'':31B ''disregard'':117B ''divin'':106B ''eeri'':147B ''enigmat'':89B ''event'':180B ''explor'':47B ''folli'':3A,6B,162B ''follow'':34B ''found'':100B ''fulfil'':145B ''gold'':157B ''golg'':10B ''greed'':103B ''grow'':85B ''heran'':49B ''howev'':76B ''influenc'':168B ''insid'':132B ''insight'':122B ''intervent'':107B ''iolo'':17B ''knowledg'':90B ''known'':21B ''later'':144B ''lead'':28B,123B ''leav'':136B ''lockpick'':61B ''loom'':176B ''mad'':42B ''minevah'':16B ''mistrust'':104B ''month'':143B,151B ''moresbi'':39B ''narrat'':112B ''overconfid'':115B ''partnership'':36B ''partner’'':120B ''peculiar'':121B ''perish'':139B ''plot'':92B ''presenc'':175B ''princ'':172B ''propheci'':148B ''prove'':71B ''prowess'':62B ''rambl'':67B ''reli'':58B ''return'':141B ''room'':135B ''seal'':130B ''search'':53B ''seem'':41B ''sheogorath'':173B ''skill'':19B,70B ''stori'':33B ''story’'':179B ''surviv'':75B ''suspici'':86B ''tale'':14B,159B ''tell'':11B ''theme'':101B ''thief'':20B ''tomb'':51B,83B ''trap'':128B ''treasur'':55B,98B,134B ''two'':142B,150B ''ulstyr'':38B,140B ''ulstyr’'':65B,88B ''ultim'':91B ''underscor'':160B ''unpredict'':167B ''vital'':72B ''warrior'':44B ''whose'':24B,174B ''written'':7B ''zylmoc'':9B', 'scholar', 'Chance''s Folly, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, tells the tale of Minevah Iolos, a thief whose greed and betrayal lead to her tragic end. Themes of greed, mistrust, divine intervention, and the consequences of deceit are explored, highlighting the unpredictable influence of Sheogorath and the folly of overconfidence.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('boots_of_the_crusader', '
The Boots of the Crusader, also known as the Boots of Kynareth, are a sacred artifact created by Kynareth, granting the wearer harmony with nature, preventing attacks from forest creatures. After Sir Juncan''s death while seeking the boots, a pilgrim visited the Shrine of Kynareth and was guided to the Grove of Trials, where they faced the Forest Guardian. By showing reverence for nature and refusing to fight, the pilgrim earned access to the grotto where the boots were hidden. ', '''access'':77B ''also'':10B ''artifact'':20B ''attack'':31B ''boot'':1A,6B,14B,43B,83B ''creat'':21B ''creatur'':34B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''death'':39B ''earn'':76B ''face'':61B ''fight'':73B ''forest'':33B,63B ''grant'':24B ''grotto'':80B ''grove'':56B ''guardian'':64B ''guid'':53B ''harmoni'':27B ''hidden'':85B ''juncan'':37B ''known'':11B ''kynareth'':16B,23B,50B ''natur'':29B,69B ''pilgrim'':45B,75B ''prevent'':30B ''refus'':71B ''rever'':67B ''sacr'':19B ''seek'':41B ''show'':66B ''shrine'':48B ''sir'':36B ''trial'':58B ''visit'':46B ''wearer'':26B', 'imperial, scholar', 'The Boots of the Crusader, created by Kynareth, grant harmony with nature and prevent attacks from forest creatures. They were recovered by a pilgrim who earned them by showing reverence for nature in the Grove of Trials.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('summon_arniel''s_shade', 'Summon Arniel''s Shade is a Conjuration spell that summons the shade of Arniel Gane to fight alongside the caster for a limited time. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''alongsid'':22B ''arniel'':2A,6B,18B ''cast'':36B ''caster'':24B ''conjur'':11B ''expert'':32B ''fight'':21B ''gane'':19B ''level'':34B ''limit'':27B ''requir'':30B ''shade'':4A,8B,16B ''skill'':33B ''spell'':12B ''summon'':1A,5B,14B ''time'':28B', 'mage', 'Summon Arniel''s Shade is a spell that summons the shade of Arniel Gane to fight alongside the caster for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arkay', 'Arkay, also known as the Lord of the Wheel of Life, is the Divine associated with the cycle of birth and death, and the god of funerals, burial rites, and seasons. As a member of the Divines, Arkay ensures the natural order of life and death is maintained, and his priests play a critical role in preventing necromancy by bestowing Arkay''s Law on the deceased. This divine protection ensures that the dead cannot be raised as undead. Necromancers see Arkay as their greatest foe, as his followers are dedicated to stopping the profane manipulation of mortal souls.

Arkay’s worship is widespread across Tamriel, from the Bretons, who believe he was once a mortal granted godhood by Mara, to the Nords, where he has replaced the older figure of Orkey. Redguards see him as a guide of souls through life and death, while Bosmer invoke him in matters concerning the Green Pact. Temples dedicated to Arkay, such as the Great Chapel of Arkay in Cyrodiil, perform sacred rites and house relics such as the Sword of the Crusader, a holy artifact. His followers, known as Arkayns, uphold his teachings by maintaining the balance of life and death, fiercely opposing necromancy and ensuring the proper passage of souls into the afterlife.', '''across'':104B ''afterlif'':211B ''also'':3B ''arkay'':1A,2B,39B,62B,82B,157B,164B ''arkayn'':187B ''arkay’'':100B ''artifact'':182B ''associ'':16B ''balanc'':194B ''believ'':110B ''bestow'':61B ''birth'':21B ''bosmer'':145B ''breton'':108B ''burial'':29B ''cannot'':75B ''chapel'':162B ''concern'':150B ''critic'':55B ''crusad'':179B ''cycl'':19B ''cyrodiil'':166B ''dead'':74B ''death'':23B,47B,143B,198B ''deceas'':67B ''dedic'':91B,155B ''divin'':15B,38B,69B ''ensur'':40B,71B,203B ''fierc'':199B ''figur'':129B ''foe'':86B ''follow'':89B,184B ''funer'':28B ''god'':26B ''godhood'':117B ''grant'':116B ''great'':161B ''greatest'':85B ''green'':152B ''guid'':137B ''holi'':181B ''hous'':171B ''invok'':146B ''known'':4B,185B ''law'':64B ''life'':12B,45B,141B,196B ''lord'':7B ''maintain'':49B,192B ''manipul'':96B ''mara'':119B ''matter'':149B ''member'':35B ''mortal'':98B,115B ''natur'':42B ''necrom'':59B,201B ''necromanc'':80B ''nord'':122B ''older'':128B ''oppos'':200B ''order'':43B ''orkey'':131B ''pact'':153B ''passag'':206B ''perform'':167B ''play'':53B ''prevent'':58B ''priest'':52B ''profan'':95B ''proper'':205B ''protect'':70B ''rais'':77B ''redguard'':132B ''relic'':172B ''replac'':126B ''rite'':30B,169B ''role'':56B ''sacr'':168B ''season'':32B ''see'':81B,133B ''soul'':99B,139B,208B ''stop'':93B ''sword'':176B ''tamriel'':105B ''teach'':190B ''templ'':154B ''undead'':79B ''uphold'':188B ''wheel'':10B ''widespread'':103B ''worship'':101B', 'priest, scholar', '
Arkay, the Divine of birth, death, and the seasons, governs the natural cycle of life and death. Known as the Lord of the Wheel of Life, he is revered for his role in funerals, burial rites, and preventing necromancy through Arkay''s Law, which protects the dead from being raised as undead. Worship of Arkay is widespread, with cultures like the Bretons believing he was once mortal, the Nords replacing Orkey with him, and the Redguards viewing him as a soul guide. Temples dedicated to Arkay, such as the Great Chapel in Cyrodiil, uphold his teachings, perform sacred rites, and house relics like the Sword of the Crusader, while his followers fiercely oppose necromancy and safeguard the passage of souls.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('eternal_champion', 'The Eternal Champion, reputedly known as Talin, emerged as a pivotal hero in Tamriel''s history during the late Third Era. Born in 3E 370, he is best remembered for his critical role in ending the Imperial Simulacrum in 3E 399. The Eternal Champion successfully gathered the fragments of the Staff of Chaos, a powerful artifact, which enabled him to confront and defeat the impostor emperor, Jagar Tharn. His quest culminated in the rescue of the true emperor, Uriel Septim VII, alongside General Talin Warhaft, who had been imprisoned in a realm of Tharn''s choosing for a decade. This heroic act not only restored the rightful leadership of the Empire but also ended Tharn''s deceptive reign.', '''370'':27B ''399'':43B ''3e'':26B,42B ''act'':104B ''alongsid'':84B ''also'':115B ''artifact'':58B ''best'':30B ''born'':24B ''champion'':2A,5B,46B ''chao'':55B ''choos'':98B ''confront'':63B ''critic'':34B ''culmin'':73B ''decad'':101B ''decept'':119B ''defeat'':65B ''emerg'':10B ''emperor'':68B,80B ''empir'':113B ''enabl'':60B ''end'':37B,116B ''era'':23B ''etern'':1A,4B,45B ''fragment'':50B ''gather'':48B ''general'':85B ''hero'':14B ''heroic'':103B ''histori'':18B ''imperi'':39B ''impostor'':67B ''imprison'':91B ''jagar'':69B ''known'':7B ''late'':21B ''leadership'':110B ''pivot'':13B ''power'':57B ''quest'':72B ''realm'':94B ''reign'':120B ''rememb'':31B ''reput'':6B ''rescu'':76B ''restor'':107B ''right'':109B ''role'':35B ''septim'':82B ''simulacrum'':40B ''staff'':53B ''success'':47B ''talin'':9B,86B ''tamriel'':16B ''tharn'':70B,96B,117B ''third'':22B ''true'':79B ''uriel'':81B ''vii'':83B ''warhaft'':87B', 'scholar', 'The Eternal Champion, reputedly known as Talin, played a pivotal role in ending the Imperial Simulacrum in 3E 399. Born in 3E 370, he is remembered for gathering the fragments of the Staff of Chaos, allowing him to defeat the impostor emperor, Jagar Tharn. His quest led to the rescue of the true emperor, Uriel Septim VII, and General Talin Warhaft, who had been imprisoned for a decade. This act restored the rightful leadership of the Empire and ended Tharn''s reign.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('addvar''s_house', 'Addvar''s House is a small residence located in the residential district of Solitude, right next to Evette San''s House. It is the home of Addvar, the town''s fishmonger, along with his wife Greta and their daughter Svari. ', '''addvar'':1A,4B,30B ''along'':35B ''daughter'':42B ''district'':15B ''evett'':21B ''fishmong'':34B ''greta'':39B ''home'':28B ''hous'':3A,6B,24B ''locat'':11B ''next'':19B ''resid'':10B ''residenti'':14B ''right'':18B ''san'':22B ''small'':9B ''solitud'':17B ''svari'':43B ''town'':32B ''wife'':38B', 'haafingar', 'Addvar''s House is a small residence located in the residential district of Solitude. You do not know Addvar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('angarvunde', 'Angarvunde is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located west of Riften and south of Treva''s Watch in the Rift. The ruin is inhabited by draugr.', '''angarvund'':1A,2B ''draugr'':28B ''inhabit'':26B ''locat'':10B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''nordic'':8B ''rift'':22B ''riften'':13B ''ruin'':9B,24B ''size'':7B ''south'':15B ''treva'':17B ''watch'':19B ''west'':11B', 'rift', 'Angarvunde is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located west of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_pickpocket', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration abilities that improve the caster;s skill in stealing from others, reducing the chance of detection while pickpocketing. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted gear. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Fortify Pickpocket effect: Blue Dartwing, Nordic Barnacle, Orange Dartwing, Slaughterfish Egg, Spadefish', '''abil'':11B ''also'':46B ''appli'':48B ''avail'':32B ''barnacl'':78B ''blue'':75B ''brew'':40B ''caster'':15B ''chanc'':24B ''combin'':53B ''craft'':36B ''creat'':67B ''custom'':42B ''dartw'':76B,80B ''detect'':26B ''effect'':5B,30B,65B,74B ''egg'':82B ''enchant'':50B ''focus'':9B ''follow'':59B ''fortifi'':1A,72B ''gear'':51B ''general'':52B ''improv'':13B ''ingredi'':60B ''least'':55B ''magic'':4B ''nordic'':77B ''orang'':79B ''other'':21B ''pickpocket'':2A,28B,73B ''potion'':37B,43B,69B ''pre'':35B ''pre-craft'':34B ''provid'':61B ''reduc'':22B ''restor'':10B ''share'':63B ''skill'':17B ''slaughterfish'':81B ''spadefish'':83B ''steal'':19B ''two'':56B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic makes it easier to pick pockets without being noticed. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('haafingar', 'Haafingar is a location at the northwestern edge of Skyrim, home to the provincial capital, Solitude. The hold serves as the center of Imperial rule in Skyrim.

Haafingar is defined by a large ridge that stretches across the hold, with pine forests and meadows covering the southern slopes down to the Karth River. The northern areas are colder, with mountains and a frozen coastline. Solitude itself is perched on a massive natural archway over the mouth of the Karth River. The region''s coastline is rich in resources like nordic barnacles and clams, while the land supports plants like canis root and spiky grass. Near Solitude, you can enjoy fishing by the Solitude Sawmill, where dragonflies hover over the water. The hold is home to various flora, including nightshade, mora tapinella, and thistles, while the snow-covered Druadach Mountains only allow snowberries and scattered mountain flowers to grow. Jarl Elisif the Fair governs the region.', '''across'':38B ''allow'':143B ''archway'':74B ''area'':57B ''barnacl'':92B ''cani'':101B ''capit'':16B ''center'':23B ''clam'':94B ''coastlin'':65B,85B ''colder'':59B ''cover'':46B,139B ''defin'':31B ''dragonfli'':117B ''druadach'':140B ''edg'':9B ''elisif'':152B ''enjoy'':110B ''fair'':154B ''fish'':111B ''flora'':128B ''flower'':148B ''forest'':43B ''frozen'':64B ''govern'':155B ''grass'':105B ''grow'':150B ''haafingar'':1A,2B,29B ''hold'':19B,40B,123B ''home'':12B,125B ''hover'':118B ''imperi'':25B ''includ'':129B ''jarl'':151B ''karth'':53B,80B ''land'':97B ''larg'':34B ''like'':90B,100B ''locat'':5B ''massiv'':72B ''meadow'':45B ''mora'':131B ''mountain'':61B,141B,147B ''mouth'':77B ''natur'':73B ''near'':106B ''nightshad'':130B ''nordic'':91B ''northern'':56B ''northwestern'':8B ''perch'':69B ''pine'':42B ''plant'':99B ''provinci'':15B ''region'':83B,157B ''resourc'':89B ''rich'':87B ''ridg'':35B ''river'':54B,81B ''root'':102B ''rule'':26B ''sawmil'':115B ''scatter'':146B ''serv'':20B ''skyrim'':11B,28B ''slope'':49B ''snow'':138B ''snow-cov'':137B ''snowberri'':144B ''solitud'':17B,66B,107B,114B ''southern'':48B ''spiki'':104B ''stretch'':37B ''support'':98B ''tapinella'':132B ''thistl'':134B ''various'':127B ''water'':121B', 'haafingar, noble, scholar', 'Haafingar is a location at the northwestern edge of Skyrim, home to the provincial capital, Solitude. The hold serves as the center of Imperial rule in Skyrim.

Haafingar is defined by a large ridge that stretches across the hold, with pine forests and meadows covering the southern slopes down to the Karth River. Jarl Elisif the Fair governs the region.', '', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wreck_of_the_icerunner', 'The Wreck of the Icerunner is a location east of Solitude, where an Imperial ship has run aground. The ship was originally transporting passengers and cargo between Skyrim and Cyrodiil, there are rumors that a noteable imperial scholar, who you do not know the name of, was looking for a rare unkown artifact in Skyrim.', '''aground'':22B ''artifact'':57B ''cargo'':30B ''cyrodiil'':34B ''east'':13B ''icerunn'':4A,9B ''imperi'':18B,41B ''know'':47B ''locat'':12B ''look'':52B ''name'':49B ''noteabl'':40B ''origin'':26B ''passeng'':28B ''rare'':55B ''rumor'':37B ''run'':21B ''scholar'':42B ''ship'':19B,24B ''skyrim'':32B,59B ''solitud'':15B ''transport'':27B ''unkown'':56B ''wreck'':1A,6B', 'hjaalmarch, sailor', 'The Wreck of the Icerunner is a location east of Solitude, where an Imperial ship has run aground. The ship was originally transporting passengers and cargo between Skyrim and Cyrodiil, there are rumors that a noteable imperial scholar, who you do not know the name of, was looking for a rare unkown artifact in Skyrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fort_neugrad', 'Fort Neugrad is a medium-sized fort located east of Falkreath and southeast of Helgen in Falkreath Hold. It is occupied by bandits', '''bandit'':26B ''east'':12B ''falkreath'':14B,20B ''fort'':1A,3B,10B ''helgen'':18B ''hold'':21B ''locat'':11B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''neugrad'':2A,4B ''occupi'':24B ''size'':9B ''southeast'':16B', 'falkreath', 'Fort Neugrad is a medium-sized fort located east of Falkreath.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('kraldar''s_house', 'Kraldar''s House is located in Winterhold, situated as the last building on the left before the bridge leading to the College of Winterhold. The house serves as the residence of Kraldar, a local figure, and his manservant, Thonjolf.', '''bridg'':21B ''build'':15B ''colleg'':25B ''figur'':38B ''hous'':3A,6B,29B ''kraldar'':1A,4B,35B ''last'':14B ''lead'':22B ''left'':18B ''local'':37B ''locat'':8B ''manserv'':41B ''resid'':33B ''serv'':30B ''situat'':11B ''thonjolf'':42B ''winterhold'':10B,27B', 'winterhold', 'Kraldar''s House is located in Winterhold. You dot know who Kraldar is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('helm_of_the_crusader', 'The Helm of the Crusader, created by Dibella, grants the wearer serene beauty, enhances bartering abilities, and improves skills in Illusion magic. After Pelinal Whitestrake''s death, his followers enshrined the helm in the halls of Vanua, which later became submerged under Lake Rumare. In 3E 153, Sir Amiel perished in the haunted ruins while seeking the helm to restore his order’s honor. Centuries later, a pilgrim, guided by a vision of Whitestrake, discovered Sir Amiel’s remains and reclaimed the helm.', '''153'':51B ''3e'':50B ''abil'':20B ''amiel'':53B ''amiel’'':80B ''barter'':19B ''beauti'':17B ''becam'':44B ''centuri'':68B ''creat'':10B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''death'':31B ''dibella'':12B ''discov'':78B ''enhanc'':18B ''enshrin'':34B ''follow'':33B ''grant'':13B ''guid'':72B ''hall'':39B ''haunt'':57B ''helm'':1A,6B,36B,62B,85B ''honor'':67B ''illus'':25B ''improv'':22B ''lake'':47B ''later'':43B,69B ''magic'':26B ''order’'':66B ''pelin'':28B ''perish'':54B ''pilgrim'':71B ''reclaim'':83B ''remain'':81B ''restor'':64B ''ruin'':58B ''rumar'':48B ''seek'':60B ''seren'':16B ''sir'':52B,79B ''skill'':23B ''submerg'':45B ''vanua'':41B ''vision'':75B ''wearer'':15B ''whitestrak'':29B,77B', 'imperial, scholar', '
The Helm of the Crusader, created by Dibella, enhances beauty, bartering, and Illusion skills. It was enshrined in Vanua after Pelinal Whitestrake''s death and reclaimed centuries later by a pilgrim guided by a vision.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('improved_bonemold_boots', 'Improved Bonemold Boots are a basic bonemold pair of boots with good protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. To craft it: 1 netch leather, 1 iron ingot, 6 bonemold, 1 netch jelly, 1 stalhrim, and 1 void salts at a blacksmith forge. An Apprentice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using bonemeal at a workbench.', '''1'':43B,46B,51B,54B,57B ''6'':49B ''apprentic'':65B ''basic'':9B ''bind'':35B ''blacksmith'':62B ''bone'':29B ''bone-lik'':28B ''bonem'':76B ''bonemold'':2A,5B,10B,50B ''boot'':3A,6B,13B ''craft'':41B,68B ''dark'':34B ''design'':20B ''forg'':63B ''good'':15B ''improv'':1A,4B ''ingot'':48B ''iron'':47B ''jelli'':53B ''leather'':45B ''like'':30B ''netch'':44B,52B ''organ'':24B ''pair'':11B ''protect'':16B ''qualiti'':17B ''reinforc'':32B ''rough'':22B ''salt'':59B ''shape'':39B ''smith'':66B ''stalhrim'':55B ''tan'':27B ''tempered/improved'':73B ''textur'':31B ''use'':75B ''utilitarian'':38B ''visual'':19B ''void'':58B ''workbench'':79B', 'blacksmith', 'Improved Bonemold Boots are a basic bonemold pair of boots with good protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
