Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. To craft it: 1 netch leather, 1 iron ingot, 4 bonemold, 1 netch jelly, 1 stalhrim, and 1 void salts at a blacksmith forge. An Apprentice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using bonemeal at a workbench.', '''1'':43B,46B,51B,54B,57B ''4'':49B ''apprentic'':65B ''basic'':9B ''bind'':35B ''blacksmith'':62B ''bone'':29B ''bone-lik'':28B ''bonem'':76B ''bonemold'':2A,5B,10B,50B ''craft'':41B,68B ''dark'':34B ''design'':20B ''forg'':63B ''gauntlet'':3A,6B,13B ''good'':15B ''improv'':1A,4B ''ingot'':48B ''iron'':47B ''jelli'':53B ''leather'':45B ''like'':30B ''netch'':44B,52B ''organ'':24B ''pair'':11B ''protect'':16B ''qualiti'':17B ''reinforc'':32B ''rough'':22B ''salt'':59B ''shape'':39B ''smith'':66B ''stalhrim'':55B ''tan'':27B ''tempered/improved'':73B ''textur'':31B ''use'':75B ''utilitarian'':38B ''visual'':19B ''void'':58B ''workbench'':79B', 'blacksmith', 'Improved Bonemold Gauntlets are a basic bonemold pair of gauntlets with good protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orichalcum', 'Orichalcum, also known as orichalc, is a gray-green metal renowned for its use in crafting weapons and armor, particularly by the Orcs, who are celebrated for their orichalcum equipment. The metal is typically melded with iron at low temperatures to maintain its strength and prevent brittleness. Orcish armor, which is often crafted with superior skill, is characterized as medium to heavy in weight, while orichalcum weapons are less common and can vary in quality.', '''also'':3B ''armor'':21B,51B ''brittl'':49B ''celebr'':28B ''character'':60B ''common'':72B ''craft'':18B,55B ''equip'':32B ''gray'':10B ''gray-green'':9B ''green'':11B ''heavi'':64B ''iron'':39B ''known'':4B ''less'':71B ''low'':41B ''maintain'':44B ''medium'':62B ''meld'':37B ''metal'':12B,34B ''often'':54B ''orc'':25B ''orcish'':50B ''orichalc'':6B ''orichalcum'':1A,2B,31B,68B ''particular'':22B ''prevent'':48B ''qualiti'':77B ''renown'':13B ''skill'':58B ''strength'':46B ''superior'':57B ''temperatur'':42B ''typic'':36B ''use'':16B ''vari'':75B ''weapon'':19B,69B ''weight'':66B', 'blacksmith, orc', 'Orichalcum, also known as orichalc, is a gray-green metal renowned for its use in crafting weapons and armor, particularly by the Orcs, who are celebrated for their orichalcum equipment.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hide_boots', 'Hide Boots are are a pair of hide boots with little protection quality.
Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides bound together with crude stitching.  To craft it: 2 leather and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge.  A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''2'':37B,40B ''anim'':27B ''blacksmith'':45B ''boot'':2A,4B,11B ''bound'':29B ''craft'':35B,51B ''crude'':32B ''design'':18B ''forg'':46B ''hide'':1A,3B,10B,28B ''leather'':38B,41B,59B ''light'':25B ''littl'':13B ''made'':23B ''novic'':48B ''pair'':8B ''primit'':22B ''protect'':14B ''qualiti'':15B ''rough'':20B ''smith'':49B ''stitch'':33B ''strip'':42B ''tan'':26B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''togeth'':30B ''use'':58B ''visual'':17B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Hide Boots are are a pair of hide boots with little protection quality.
Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides bound together with crude stitching.  You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('swamp_fungal_pod', 'Swamp Fungal Pod are a white brownish fungus found in the marshes of Hjaalmarch. Alchemy effects: Resist Shock, Lingering Damage Magicka, Paralysis, and Restore Health.', '''alchemi'':18B ''brownish'':10B ''damag'':23B ''effect'':19B ''found'':12B ''fungal'':2A,5B ''fungus'':11B ''health'':28B ''hjaalmarch'':17B ''linger'':22B ''magicka'':24B ''marsh'':15B ''paralysi'':25B ''pod'':3A,6B ''resist'':20B ''restor'':27B ''shock'':21B ''swamp'':1A,4B ''white'':9B', 'alchemist', 'Swamp Fungal Pod are a white brownish fungus found in the marshes of Hjaalmarch. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('black_marsh', '
Black Marsh, also called Argonia by the Mer, is a dense and treacherous swampland in southeastern Tamriel, home to the Argonians and the sapient Hist trees. The Argonians, who organize into tribes rather than a unified nation, thrive in this tropical and hostile environment filled with poisonous plants and dangerous predators. Foreign attempts at colonization and agriculture have largely failed due to the land''s resilience against outside interference.

In addition to Argonians, Black Marsh has been home to various other sapient races, including the now-extinct Kothringi and Lilmothiit, who were wiped out by the Knahaten Flu. The region also hosts unique creatures like the serpent-bodied Lamias and the fox-like Lilmothiit, adding to its rich and mysterious cultural and ecological diversity. Black Marsh remains one of the most enigmatic provinces of Tamriel, resisting full integration into the Cyrodiilic Empire.', '''ad'':120B ''addit'':73B ''agricultur'':59B ''also'':5B,104B ''argonia'':7B ''argonian'':23B,30B,75B ''attempt'':55B ''black'':1A,3B,76B,130B ''bodi'':112B ''call'':6B ''colon'':57B ''creatur'':107B ''cultur'':126B ''cyrodiil'':146B ''danger'':52B ''dens'':13B ''divers'':129B ''due'':63B ''ecolog'':128B ''empir'':147B ''enigmat'':137B ''environ'':46B ''extinct'':90B ''fail'':62B ''fill'':47B ''flu'':101B ''foreign'':54B ''fox'':117B ''fox-lik'':116B ''full'':142B ''hist'':27B ''home'':20B,80B ''host'':105B ''hostil'':45B ''includ'':86B ''integr'':143B ''interfer'':71B ''knahaten'':100B ''kothringi'':91B ''lamia'':113B ''land'':66B ''larg'':61B ''like'':108B,118B ''lilmothiit'':93B,119B ''marsh'':2A,4B,77B,131B ''mer'':10B ''mysteri'':125B ''nation'':39B ''now-extinct'':88B ''one'':133B ''organ'':32B ''outsid'':70B ''plant'':50B ''poison'':49B ''predat'':53B ''provinc'':138B ''race'':85B ''rather'':35B ''region'':103B ''remain'':132B ''resili'':68B ''resist'':141B ''rich'':123B ''sapient'':26B,84B ''serpent'':111B ''serpent-bodi'':110B ''southeastern'':18B ''swampland'':16B ''tamriel'':19B,140B ''thrive'':40B ''treacher'':15B ''tree'':28B ''tribe'':34B ''tropic'':43B ''unifi'':38B ''uniqu'':106B ''various'':82B ''wipe'':96B', 'scholar, argonian', '
Black Marsh, or Argonia, is a dense, dangerous swampland in southeastern Tamriel, inhabited by the Argonians and the sapient Hist trees. The Argonians live in tribes and thrive in the hostile environment filled with poisonous plants and dangerous animals. Foreign attempts at colonization have failed due to the land''s resilience. The region also hosted extinct races like the Kothringi and Lilmothiit, and unique creatures like Lamias. Despite its rich cultural and ecological diversity, Black Marsh remains enigmatic and resistant to full integration into the Cyrodiilic Empire.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ashfallow_citadel', 'Ashfallow Citadel is a small, abandoned Imperial fort located east of Highpoint Tower and northwest of the Sun Stone on Solstheim. The fort, once a symbol of Imperial authority, has fallen into disrepair and is now used as a base of operations by the Morag Tong, a secretive and deadly assassins'' guild with ties to Morrowind.', '''abandon'':8B ''ashfallow'':1A,3B ''assassin'':53B ''author'':31B ''base'':42B ''citadel'':2A,4B ''dead'':52B ''disrepair'':35B ''east'':12B ''fallen'':33B ''fort'':10B,25B ''guild'':54B ''highpoint'':14B ''imperi'':9B,30B ''locat'':11B ''morag'':47B ''morrowind'':58B ''northwest'':17B ''oper'':44B ''secret'':50B ''small'':7B ''solstheim'':23B ''stone'':21B ''sun'':20B ''symbol'':28B ''tie'':56B ''tong'':48B ''tower'':15B ''use'':39B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('labyrinthian', 'Labyrinthian is a vast and ancient Nordic ruin located southeast of Morthal, situated in a mountain pass that connects Hjaalmarch and Whiterun Hold. Once the great city of Bromjunaar, the capital of the Dragon Cult, Labyrinthian was built during the Merethic Era as a temple to the dragons who ruled Skyrim at the time. Over centuries, the city grew into a thriving hub of power for the cult, where the highest-ranking Dragon Priests convened to govern. Following the defeat of the Dragon Cult during the Dragon War, Bromjunaar fell into ruin, leaving behind the eerie remnants of its past, including the famed Labyrinth.', '''ancient'':7B ''behind'':96B ''bromjunaar'':30B,91B ''built'':39B ''capit'':32B ''centuri'':57B ''citi'':28B,59B ''connect'':20B ''conven'':77B ''cult'':36B,69B,86B ''defeat'':82B ''dragon'':35B,49B,75B,85B,89B ''eeri'':98B ''era'':43B ''fame'':105B ''fell'':92B ''follow'':80B ''govern'':79B ''great'':27B ''grew'':60B ''highest'':73B ''highest-rank'':72B ''hjaalmarch'':21B ''hold'':24B ''hub'':64B ''includ'':103B ''labyrinth'':106B ''labyrinthian'':1A,2B,37B ''leav'':95B ''locat'':10B ''mereth'':42B ''morthal'':13B ''mountain'':17B ''nordic'':8B ''pass'':18B ''past'':102B ''power'':66B ''priest'':76B ''rank'':74B ''remnant'':99B ''ruin'':9B,94B ''rule'':51B ''situat'':14B ''skyrim'':52B ''southeast'':11B ''templ'':46B ''thrive'':63B ''time'':55B ''vast'':5B ''war'':90B ''whiterun'':23B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Labyrinthian is a vast and ancient Nordic ruin located southeast of Morthal, situated in a mountain pass that connects Hjaalmarch and Whiterun Hold. It used to be a mighty city a long time ago under the rule of the Dragon cult.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonbone_warhammer', 'Dragonbone Warhammer is a massive Dragonbone weapon which deals brilliant damage. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. To craft it: 3 dragon bones, 2 ebony ingots, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it.', '''2'':36B ''3'':33B,40B ''appear'':29B ''blacksmith'':45B ''bone'':24B,35B ''brilliant'':12B ''craft'':21B,31B,51B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''dragon'':23B,34B ''dragonbon'':1A,3B,8B ''eboni'':37B ''forg'':46B ''ingot'':38B ''jag'':20B ''leather'':41B ''massiv'':7B ''master'':48B ''organ'':28B ''pale'':18B ''rough'':27B ''smith'':49B ''strip'':42B ''visual'':15B ''warhamm'':2A,4B ''weapon'':9B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragonbone Warhammer is a massive Dragonbone weapon which deals brilliant damage. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glass_bow', 'Glass Bow is a ranged glass weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is sleek and translucent, with sharp edges and a greenish hue resembling polished malachite.To craft it: 2 refined malachite, 1 refined moonstone, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using moonstone at a workbench.', '''1'':36B ''2'':33B,40B ''adept'':54B ''blacksmith'':45B ''bow'':2A,4B ''craft'':31B,51B,57B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''edg'':23B ''expert'':48B ''fantast'':12B ''forg'':46B ''glass'':1A,3B,8B ''greenish'':26B ''hue'':27B ''it.it'':58B ''leather'':41B ''malachit'':35B ''malachite.to'':30B ''moonston'':38B,64B ''polish'':29B ''rang'':7B ''refin'':34B,37B ''resembl'':28B ''sharp'':22B ''sleek'':18B ''smith'':49B,55B ''strip'':42B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''transluc'':20B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Glass Bow is a ranged glass weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is sleek and translucent, with sharp edges and a greenish hue resembling polished malachite. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwemer_museum', 'The Dwemer Museum is located in Understone Keep, in Markath in the Reach Hold. It holds various artifacts belonging to the Dwemer.', '''artifact'':20B ''belong'':21B ''dwemer'':1A,4B,24B ''hold'':16B,18B ''keep'':10B ''locat'':7B ''markath'':12B ''museum'':2A,5B ''reach'':15B ''underston'':9B ''various'':19B', 'reach, dwemer', 'The Dwemer Museum is located in Understone Keep, in Markath in the Reach Hold. It holds various artifacts belonging to the Dwemer.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonscale_armor', 'Dragonscale Armor has brilliant protection quality. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. To craft it: 4 dragon scales, 2 iron ingots, 1 leather, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dragonbone at a workbench.', '''1'':34B ''2'':31B ''3'':37B ''4'':28B ''appear'':24B ''armor'':2A,4B ''blacksmith'':42B ''bone'':19B ''brilliant'':6B ''craft'':16B,26B,48B ''design'':11B ''dragon'':18B,29B ''dragonbon'':56B ''dragonscal'':1A,3B ''forg'':43B ''ingot'':33B ''iron'':32B ''jag'':15B ''leather'':35B,38B ''master'':45B ''organ'':23B ''pale'':13B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''rough'':22B ''scale'':30B ''smith'':46B ''strip'':39B ''tempered/improved'':53B ''use'':55B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':59B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragonscale Armor has brilliant protection quality. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
