INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pinemoon_cave', 'Pinemoon Cave is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge and east of Volskygge in Haafingar. The cave is inhabited by vampires, making it a dangerous place for anyone who ventures inside.

Its secluded location, nestled between Dragon Bridge and Volskygge, adds to the mystery and menace of the cave. Adventurers who explore Pinemoon Cave can expect to face off against the vampire inhabitants and uncover the dark secrets hidden within its depths.', '''add'':45B ''adventur'':54B ''anyon'':32B ''bridg'':13B,42B ''cave'':2A,4B,8B,21B,53B,58B ''danger'':29B ''dark'':71B ''depth'':76B ''dragon'':12B,41B ''east'':15B ''expect'':60B ''explor'':56B ''face'':62B ''haafingar'':19B ''hidden'':73B ''inhabit'':23B,67B ''insid'':35B ''locat'':9B,38B ''make'':26B ''menac'':50B ''mysteri'':48B ''nestl'':39B ''northwest'':10B ''pinemoon'':1A,3B,57B ''place'':30B ''seclud'':37B ''secret'':72B ''small'':7B ''uncov'':69B ''vampir'':25B,66B ''ventur'':34B ''volskygg'':17B,44B ''within'':74B', 'haafingar', 'Pinemoon Cave is a small cave located northwest of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elgrim''s_elixirs', 'Elgrim''s Elixirs is a damp alchemist''s shop situated on the lower level of Riften, next to the canal that runs through the city''s center. Owned and operated by Elgrim and his wife, Hafjorg, the shop specializes in alchemical supplies and potions. It is conveniently located opposite the entrance to Beggar''s Row and near the northern watergate leading to Lake Honrich.', '''alchem'':44B ''alchemist'':10B ''beggar'':56B ''canal'':23B ''center'':30B ''citi'':28B ''conveni'':50B ''damp'':9B ''elgrim'':1A,4B,35B ''elixir'':3A,6B ''entranc'':54B ''hafjorg'':39B ''honrich'':67B ''lake'':66B ''lead'':64B ''level'':17B ''locat'':51B ''lower'':16B ''near'':60B ''next'':20B ''northern'':62B ''oper'':33B ''opposit'':52B ''own'':31B ''potion'':47B ''riften'':19B ''row'':58B ''run'':25B ''shop'':12B,41B ''situat'':13B ''special'':42B ''suppli'':45B ''waterg'':63B ''wife'':38B', 'rift', 'Elgrim''s Elixirs is a damp alchemist''s shop situated in Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bits_and_pieces', 'Bits and Pieces is the general goods store in Solitude, run by Sayma, a Redguard merchant. The store is located next door to Radiant Raiment, on the corner by the market square. It is the second building on the right as you enter Solitude from the main gate.

Sayma is married to Beirand, and together they have a son named Kayd, a Redguard child. Bits and Pieces offers a variety of general goods, catering to the needs of Solitude''s residents and travelers passing through the city. The store plays an important role in the local economy, providing various items to those in need.', '''beirand'':56B ''bit'':1A,4B,68B ''build'':40B ''cater'':77B ''child'':67B ''citi'':90B ''corner'':31B ''door'':25B ''economi'':100B ''enter'':46B ''gate'':51B ''general'':9B,75B ''good'':10B,76B ''import'':95B ''item'':103B ''kayd'':64B ''local'':99B ''locat'':23B ''main'':50B ''market'':34B ''marri'':54B ''merchant'':19B ''name'':63B ''need'':80B,107B ''next'':24B ''offer'':71B ''pass'':87B ''piec'':3A,6B,70B ''play'':93B ''provid'':101B ''radiant'':27B ''raiment'':28B ''redguard'':18B,66B ''resid'':84B ''right'':43B ''role'':96B ''run'':14B ''sayma'':16B,52B ''second'':39B ''solitud'':13B,47B,82B ''son'':62B ''squar'':35B ''store'':11B,21B,92B ''togeth'':58B ''travel'':86B ''varieti'':73B ''various'':102B', 'haafingar', 'Bits and Pieces is the general goods store in Solitude. You do not know who owns it.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_lover_stone', 'The Lover Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located east of Markarth and north of Kolskeggr Mine in the Reach. To access the stone, approach from the west, as the eastern side is obstructed by a steep cliff.

Activating the Lover Stone grants the ability to improve all skills by a marginal amount.', '''abil'':53B ''access'':30B ''across'':15B ''activ'':47B ''amount'':61B ''approach'':33B ''cliff'':46B ''east'':18B ''eastern'':39B ''grant'':51B ''improv'':55B ''kolskeggr'':24B ''locat'':17B ''lover'':2A,5B,49B ''margin'':60B ''markarth'':20B ''mine'':25B ''north'':22B ''obstruct'':42B ''one'':8B ''reach'':28B ''scatter'':14B ''side'':40B ''skill'':57B ''skyrim'':16B ''stand'':12B ''steep'':45B ''stone'':3A,6B,13B,32B,50B ''thirteen'':11B ''west'':36B', 'reach, scholar, traveler', 'The Lover Stone is one of the thirteen Standing Stones scattered across Skyrim, located east of Markarth in the Reach. 

Activating the Lover Stone grants the ability to improve all skills by a marginal amount.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elixir_of_resist_magic', 'The Elixir of Resist Magic provides temporary protection against magic, reducing the damage taken from spells. It is a rare potion and not tied to any specific location or vendor. It is likely an advanced creation known to skilled alchemists and scholars studying defensive magic.', '''advanc'':39B ''alchemist'':44B ''creation'':40B ''damag'':17B ''defens'':48B ''elixir'':1A,6B ''known'':41B ''like'':37B ''locat'':32B ''magic'':4A,9B,14B,49B ''potion'':25B ''protect'':12B ''provid'':10B ''rare'':24B ''reduc'':15B ''resist'':3A,8B ''scholar'':46B ''skill'':43B ''specif'':31B ''spell'':20B ''studi'':47B ''taken'':18B ''temporari'':11B ''tie'':28B ''vendor'':34B', 'alchemist', 'You have heard of potions that protect against magic, but nothing about this specific elixir. Maybe an alchemist might though.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glover_mallory''s_house', '
Glover Mallory''s House is a modest yet well-kept home located in Raven Rock, belonging to Glover Mallory, a skilled Breton blacksmith. The house serves as both his personal residence and a place where he hones his craft, forging weapons and armor for the people of Raven Rock. Glover is known for his expertise in blacksmithing, and his work is highly regarded by both locals and travelers alike, offering both practicality and a sense of pride to the town''s defenses.', '''alik'':74B ''armor'':48B ''belong'':21B ''blacksmith'':28B,62B ''breton'':27B ''craft'':44B ''defens'':87B ''expertis'':60B ''forg'':45B ''glover'':1A,5B,23B,55B ''high'':67B ''home'':16B ''hone'':42B ''hous'':4A,8B,30B ''kept'':15B ''known'':57B ''local'':71B ''locat'':17B ''mallori'':2A,6B,24B ''modest'':11B ''offer'':75B ''peopl'':51B ''person'':35B ''place'':39B ''practic'':77B ''pride'':82B ''raven'':19B,53B ''regard'':68B ''resid'':36B ''rock'':20B,54B ''sens'':80B ''serv'':31B ''skill'':26B ''town'':85B ''travel'':73B ''weapon'':46B ''well'':14B ''well-kept'':13B ''work'':65B ''yet'':12B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('adamantine_tower', 'The Adamantine Tower, also known as the Balfiera Tower, Direnni Tower, or Ada-mantia, is an ancient and towering structure located at the highest point of the Isle of Balfiera in the Iliac Bay. Renowned as the oldest known structure in Tamriel, its construction is estimated to date back to around ME 2500. The tower has served various purposes over the centuries, including as a fortress, prison, and palace for the Direnni Hegemony. Despite numerous modifications to its exterior, the tower''s central cylindrical core of metal remains untouched, rumored to extend deep into the ground, with its depths still largely unexplored.', '''2500'':56B ''ada'':16B ''ada-mantia'':15B ''adamantin'':1A,4B ''also'':6B ''ancient'':20B ''around'':54B ''back'':52B ''balfiera'':10B,33B ''bay'':37B ''central'':86B ''centuri'':65B ''construct'':47B ''core'':88B ''cylindr'':87B ''date'':51B ''deep'':96B ''depth'':102B ''despit'':77B ''direnni'':12B,75B ''estim'':49B ''extend'':95B ''exterior'':82B ''fortress'':69B ''ground'':99B ''hegemoni'':76B ''highest'':27B ''iliac'':36B ''includ'':66B ''isl'':31B ''known'':7B,42B ''larg'':104B ''locat'':24B ''mantia'':17B ''metal'':90B ''modif'':79B ''numer'':78B ''oldest'':41B ''palac'':72B ''point'':28B ''prison'':70B ''purpos'':62B ''remain'':91B ''renown'':38B ''rumor'':93B ''serv'':60B ''still'':103B ''structur'':23B,43B ''tamriel'':45B ''tower'':2A,5B,11B,13B,22B,58B,84B ''unexplor'':105B ''untouch'':92B ''various'':61B', 'scholard, daedra, breton', '
The Adamantine Tower, located on the Isle of Balfiera in the Iliac Bay, is the oldest known structure in Tamriel, dating back to around ME 2500. It has served as a fortress, prison, and palace, with its central metal core remaining largely unexplored despite numerous modifications over the centuries.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('improved_bonemold_helmet', 'Improved Bonemold Helmet is a basic bonemold helmet with good protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. To craft it: 1 netch leather, 1 iron ingot, 6 bonemold, 1 netch jelly, 1 stalhrim, and 1 void salts at a blacksmith forge. An Apprentice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using bonemeal at a workbench.', '''1'':41B,44B,49B,52B,55B ''6'':47B ''apprentic'':63B ''basic'':9B ''bind'':33B ''blacksmith'':60B ''bone'':27B ''bone-lik'':26B ''bonem'':74B ''bonemold'':2A,5B,10B,48B ''craft'':39B,66B ''dark'':32B ''design'':18B ''forg'':61B ''good'':13B ''helmet'':3A,6B,11B ''improv'':1A,4B ''ingot'':46B ''iron'':45B ''jelli'':51B ''leather'':43B ''like'':28B ''netch'':42B,50B ''organ'':22B ''protect'':14B ''qualiti'':15B ''reinforc'':30B ''rough'':20B ''salt'':57B ''shape'':37B ''smith'':64B ''stalhrim'':53B ''tan'':25B ''tempered/improved'':71B ''textur'':29B ''use'':73B ''utilitarian'':36B ''visual'':17B ''void'':56B ''workbench'':77B', 'blacksmith', 'Improved Bonemold Helmet is a basic bonemold helmet with good protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('revenant', 'Revenant is a Conjuration spell that reanimates a more powerful dead body to fight for the caster for a limited time. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':26B ''bodi'':13B ''cast'':30B ''caster'':18B ''conjur'':5B ''dead'':12B ''fight'':15B ''level'':28B ''limit'':21B ''power'':11B ''reanim'':8B ''requir'':24B ''reven'':1A,2B ''skill'':27B ''spell'':6B ''time'':22B', 'mage', '
Revenant is a spell that reanimates a more powerful dead body, bringing it back to life to fight for the caster for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonplate_shield', 'Dragonplate Shield has brilliant protection quality. 
Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. To craft it: 3 dragon scales, 1 dragon bone, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dragonbone at a workbench.', '''1'':31B,35B ''3'':28B ''appear'':24B ''blacksmith'':40B ''bone'':19B,33B ''brilliant'':6B ''craft'':16B,26B,46B ''design'':11B ''dragon'':18B,29B,32B ''dragonbon'':54B ''dragonpl'':1A,3B ''forg'':41B ''jag'':15B ''leather'':36B ''master'':43B ''organ'':23B ''pale'':13B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''rough'':22B ''scale'':30B ''shield'':2A,4B ''smith'':44B ''strip'':37B ''tempered/improved'':51B ''use'':53B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':57B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragonplate Shield has brilliant protection quality. 
Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would..', '', '', 'equipment');
