INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('edla''s_house', 'Edla''s House is a warm, inviting home located on the north side of Skaal Village, nestled between Wulf Wild-Blood''s House to the southwest and Morwen''s House to the east. This residence is the home of Edla and her son Nikulas, who live a modest but fulfilling life in the village.', '''blood'':25B ''east'':37B ''edla'':1A,4B,44B ''fulfil'':54B ''home'':11B,42B ''hous'':3A,6B,27B,34B ''invit'':10B ''life'':55B ''live'':50B ''locat'':12B ''modest'':52B ''morwen'':32B ''nestl'':20B ''nikula'':48B ''north'':15B ''resid'':39B ''side'':16B ''skaal'':18B ''son'':47B ''southwest'':30B ''villag'':19B,58B ''warm'':9B ''wild'':24B ''wild-blood'':23B ''wulf'':22B', 'skaal', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('romlyn_dreth''s_house', 'Romlyn Dreth''s House is a modest dwelling located in the lower part of Riften, adjacent to the canal that flows through the city. The house is situated near the stairs leading down to the canal from the area in front of Honorhall Orphanage.', '''adjac'':20B ''area'':43B ''canal'':23B,40B ''citi'':28B ''dreth'':2A,6B ''dwell'':12B ''flow'':25B ''front'':45B ''honorhal'':47B ''hous'':4A,8B,30B ''lead'':36B ''locat'':13B ''lower'':16B ''modest'':11B ''near'':33B ''orphanag'':48B ''part'':17B ''riften'':19B ''romlyn'':1A,5B ''situat'':32B ''stair'':35B', 'rift', 'Romlyn Dreth''s House is a dwelling located in the lower part of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glass_warhammer', 'Glass Warhammer is a massive glass weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is sleek and translucent, with sharp edges and a greenish hue resembling polished malachite. To craft it: 3 refined malachite, 2 refined moonstone, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using moonstone at a workbench.', '''2'':37B ''3'':34B,41B ''adept'':55B ''blacksmith'':46B ''craft'':32B,52B,58B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''edg'':23B ''expert'':49B ''fantast'':12B ''forg'':47B ''glass'':1A,3B,8B ''greenish'':26B ''hue'':27B ''it.it'':59B ''leather'':42B ''malachit'':30B,36B ''massiv'':7B ''moonston'':39B,65B ''polish'':29B ''refin'':35B,38B ''resembl'':28B ''sharp'':22B ''sleek'':18B ''smith'':50B,56B ''strip'':43B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''transluc'':20B ''use'':64B ''visual'':15B ''warhamm'':2A,4B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Glass Warhammer is a massive glass weapon which deals fantastic damage. Its visual design is sleek and translucent, with sharp edges and a greenish hue resembling polished malachite. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('baan_dar', 'Baan Dar, known as the Bandit God, the Pariah, or the Man of a Thousand Faces, is a trickster spirit worshipped primarily by the Khajiit of Elsweyr, but also influential in places like Valenwood. He embodies the cleverness and desperate genius of the Khajiit, helping them outplay their oppressors and outwit others. His domain, the Five Fingers Dance, symbolizes his ability to shape lives and lands for the better, often through unconventional means. His name is widely used, particularly by thieves and criminals who take on the persona of Baan Dar to mask their identity or seek inspiration. To the Khajiit, Baan Dar represents defiance against oppression, while to other races, such as the Bretons, he is associated with sneaky thieves and living legends.

Baan Dar’s influence extends beyond his Khajiiti followers. In Valenwood, he is viewed as a god of archery, while to the Bretons, he is known as the Bandit and revered by the Thieves Guild in the Iliac Bay. His name is even used by the Baandari Pedlars, a traveling merchant tribe. In addition, Baan Dar is commemorated by the Khajiit and Bosmer at the ruins of Thormar, where they participate in the "Boast," a festival of pranks between the two races. Despite the varying interpretations of his nature across cultures, Baan Dar remains a symbol of defiance, resourcefulness, and the clever trickster spirit that shapes the world around him.', '''abil'':63B ''across'':215B ''addit'':179B ''also'':31B ''archeri'':144B ''around'':234B ''associ'':120B ''baan'':1A,3B,92B,104B,127B,180B,217B ''baandari'':172B ''bandit'':8B,154B ''bay'':164B ''better'':71B ''beyond'':131B ''boast'':199B ''bosmer'':188B ''breton'':117B,148B ''clever'':40B,227B ''commemor'':183B ''crimin'':85B ''cultur'':216B ''danc'':60B ''dar'':2A,4B,93B,105B,181B,218B ''dar’'':128B ''defianc'':107B,223B ''desper'':42B ''despit'':208B ''domain'':56B ''elsweyr'':29B ''embodi'':38B ''even'':168B ''extend'':130B ''face'':18B ''festiv'':201B ''finger'':59B ''five'':58B ''follow'':134B ''genius'':43B ''god'':9B,142B ''guild'':160B ''help'':47B ''ident'':97B ''iliac'':163B ''influenc'':129B ''influenti'':32B ''inspir'':100B ''interpret'':211B ''khajiit'':27B,46B,103B,186B ''khajiiti'':133B ''known'':5B,151B ''land'':68B ''legend'':126B ''like'':35B ''live'':66B,125B ''man'':14B ''mask'':95B ''mean'':75B ''merchant'':176B ''name'':77B,166B ''natur'':214B ''often'':72B ''oppress'':109B ''oppressor'':51B ''other'':54B ''outplay'':49B ''outwit'':53B ''pariah'':11B ''particip'':196B ''particular'':81B ''pedlar'':173B ''persona'':90B ''place'':34B ''prank'':203B ''primarili'':24B ''race'':113B,207B ''remain'':219B ''repres'':106B ''resourc'':224B ''rever'':156B ''ruin'':191B ''seek'':99B ''shape'':65B,231B ''sneaki'':122B ''spirit'':22B,229B ''symbol'':61B,221B ''take'':87B ''thiev'':83B,123B,159B ''thormar'':193B ''thousand'':17B ''travel'':175B ''tribe'':177B ''trickster'':21B,228B ''two'':206B ''unconvent'':74B ''use'':80B,169B ''valenwood'':36B,136B ''vari'':210B ''view'':139B ''wide'':79B ''world'':233B ''worship'':23B', 'woodelf, khajiit, scholar', '
Baan Dar, the Bandit God or Man of a Thousand Faces, is a trickster spirit worshipped by the Khajiit of Elsweyr and influential in Valenwood. He embodies cleverness and defiance, helping the Khajiit outwit their oppressors. His domain, the Five Fingers Dance, symbolizes his power to shape lives and lands through unconventional means. ', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pacify', 'These magical effects are offensive Illusion spells that calm hostile targets within range, neutralizing aggression and preventing them from attacking. This effect is available as a spell and is also found on enchanted items, making it ideal for resolving conflicts peacefully.', '''aggress'':16B ''also'':31B ''attack'':21B ''avail'':25B ''calm'':10B ''conflict'':41B ''effect'':4B,23B ''enchant'':34B ''found'':32B ''hostil'':11B ''ideal'':38B ''illus'':7B ''item'':35B ''magic'':3B ''make'':36B ''neutral'':15B ''offens'':6B ''pacifi'':1A ''peac'':42B ''prevent'':18B ''rang'':14B ''resolv'':40B ''spell'':8B,28B ''target'':12B ''within'':13B', 'mage', 'This spell calms angry enemies, making them stop fighting for a while. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gray_pine_goods', 'Gray Pine Goods is a small general goods store located near the center of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. It is situated opposite Dead Man''s Drink and adjacent to Lod''s House.

The store is run by Solaf, with his brother Bolund also residing there. Gray Pine Goods provides a variety of essential items, making it a convenient stop for adventurers and townsfolk in need of supplies.', '''adjac'':31B ''adventur'':64B ''also'':46B ''bolund'':45B ''brother'':44B ''center'':16B ''conveni'':61B ''dead'':26B ''drink'':29B ''essenti'':56B ''falkreath'':18B,20B ''general'':10B ''good'':3A,6B,11B,51B ''gray'':1A,4B,49B ''hold'':21B ''hous'':35B ''item'':57B ''locat'':13B ''lod'':33B ''make'':58B ''man'':27B ''near'':14B ''need'':68B ''opposit'':25B ''pine'':2A,5B,50B ''provid'':52B ''resid'':47B ''run'':39B ''situat'':24B ''small'':9B ''solaf'':41B ''stop'':62B ''store'':12B,37B ''suppli'':70B ''townsfolk'':66B ''varieti'':54B', 'falkreath', 'Gray Pine Goods is a small general goods store in Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. You do not know who runs the store.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hjaalmarch', 'Hjaalmarch is a hold in northern Skyrim, with its capital in Morthal, located east of Solitude and south of the Pale. Despite its proximity to Skyrim''s capital, Hjaalmarch is remote and isolated, dominated by a vast, fog-shrouded swamp in the north and bordered by snowy mountains in the south. The ancient ruins of Labyrinthian block potential trade routes to Whiterun Hold, adding to its seclusion.  It is ruled by Jarl Idgrod Ravencrone.

Hjaalmarch’s salt marshes, stretching from Fort Snowhawk in the west to Ustengrav in the east, are rich in flora, including deathbell, swamp fungal pods, and giant lichen, as well as rare blue mountain flowers around Morthal. The swamps are teeming with dangerous creatures like frostbite spiders, trolls, and even chaurus, while mudcrabs, fish, and dragonflies populate the waterways. The southern regions are snowy and mountainous, with bears, sabre cats, and deer roaming the rugged terrain. A single paved road connects Dragon Bridge in the west to Morthal.', '''ad'':66B ''ancient'':55B ''around'':111B ''bear'':143B ''block'':59B ''blue'':108B ''border'':47B ''bridg'':158B ''capit'':11B,29B ''cat'':145B ''chaurus'':126B ''connect'':156B ''creatur'':119B ''danger'':118B ''deathbel'':97B ''deer'':147B ''despit'':23B ''domin'':35B ''dragon'':157B ''dragonfli'':131B ''east'':15B,91B ''even'':125B ''fish'':129B ''flora'':95B ''flower'':110B ''fog'':40B ''fog-shroud'':39B ''fort'':82B ''frostbit'':121B ''fungal'':99B ''giant'':102B ''hjaalmarch'':1A,2B,30B ''hjaalmarch’'':77B ''hold'':5B,65B ''idgrod'':75B ''includ'':96B ''isol'':34B ''jarl'':74B ''labyrinthian'':58B ''lichen'':103B ''like'':120B ''locat'':14B ''marsh'':79B ''morthal'':13B,112B,163B ''mountain'':50B,109B,141B ''mudcrab'':128B ''north'':45B ''northern'':7B ''pale'':22B ''pave'':154B ''pod'':100B ''popul'':132B ''potenti'':60B ''proxim'':25B ''rare'':107B ''ravencron'':76B ''region'':137B ''remot'':32B ''rich'':93B ''road'':155B ''roam'':148B ''rout'':62B ''rug'':150B ''ruin'':56B ''rule'':72B ''sabr'':144B ''salt'':78B ''seclus'':69B ''shroud'':41B ''singl'':153B ''skyrim'':8B,27B ''snowhawk'':83B ''snowi'':49B,139B ''solitud'':17B ''south'':19B,53B ''southern'':136B ''spider'':122B ''stretch'':80B ''swamp'':42B,98B,114B ''teem'':116B ''terrain'':151B ''trade'':61B ''troll'':123B ''ustengrav'':88B ''vast'':38B ''waterway'':134B ''well'':105B ''west'':86B,161B ''whiterun'':64B', 'hjaalmarch, noble, scholar', 'Hjaalmarch is a hold in northern Skyrim, with its capital in Morthal, located east of Solitude and south of the Pale. Despite its proximity to Skyrim''s capital, Hjaalmarch is remote and isolated, dominated by a vast, fog-shrouded swamp in the north and bordered by snowy mountains in the south. The ancient ruins of Labyrinthian block potential trade routes to Whiterun Hold, adding to its seclusion.  It is ruled by Jarl Idgrod Ravencrone.

Hjaalmarch’s salt marshes, stretching from Fort Snowhawk in the west to Ustengrav in the east, are rich in flora.', '', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wabbajack', 'The Wabbajack is a Daedric artifact created by Sheogorath, the Daedric Prince of Madness. This distinctive staff, often adorned with engravings of angry, gaping faces, embodies the unpredictable and chaotic nature of its creator. The Wabbajack possesses the power to transform its target into a completely random creature, making it a double-edged sword in combat. While it can convert a formidable foe into a harmless animal, it may just as easily turn a weak opponent into a fearsome monster. The staff can also cause various effects, such as damage, healing, petrification, or even instant death.', '''adorn'':20B ''also'':86B ''angri'':24B ''anim'':69B ''artifact'':7B ''caus'':87B ''chaotic'':31B ''combat'':58B ''complet'':47B ''convert'':62B ''creat'':8B ''creator'':35B ''creatur'':49B ''daedric'':6B,12B ''damag'':92B ''death'':98B ''distinct'':17B ''doubl'':54B ''double-edg'':53B ''easili'':74B ''edg'':55B ''effect'':89B ''embodi'':27B ''engrav'':22B ''even'':96B ''face'':26B ''fearsom'':81B ''foe'':65B ''formid'':64B ''gape'':25B ''harmless'':68B ''heal'':93B ''instant'':97B ''mad'':15B ''make'':50B ''may'':71B ''monster'':82B ''natur'':32B ''often'':19B ''oppon'':78B ''petrif'':94B ''possess'':38B ''power'':40B ''princ'':13B ''random'':48B ''sheogorath'':10B ''staff'':18B,84B ''sword'':56B ''target'':44B ''transform'':42B ''turn'':75B ''unpredict'':29B ''various'':88B ''wabbajack'':1A,3B,37B ''weak'':77B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
The Wabbajack is a chaotic Daedric artifact of Sheogorath, it is thought to be capable of transforming targets into random creatures but may be unpredicatble due the madness of its creator.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedra_heart', 'Daedra Hearts are collected from slain Dremora and are not only used in alchemy but also in crafting Daedric armor and weapons at both standard and Atronach forges. Alchemy effects: Restore Health, Damage Stamina Regen, Damage Magicka, and Fear.', '''alchemi'':16B,31B ''also'':18B ''armor'':22B ''atronach'':29B ''collect'':6B ''craft'':20B ''daedra'':1A,3B ''daedric'':21B ''damag'':35B,38B ''dremora'':9B ''effect'':32B ''fear'':41B ''forg'':30B ''health'':34B ''heart'':2A,4B ''magicka'':39B ''regen'':37B ''restor'':33B ''slain'':8B ''stamina'':36B ''standard'':27B ''use'':14B ''weapon'':24B', 'alchemist', 'Daedra Hearts are collected from slain Dremora and are not only used in alchemy but also in crafting Daedric armor and weapons at both standard and Atronach forges.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hall_of_countenance', '
The Hall of Countenance serves as the primary living and sleeping quarters for many of the higher-ranked mages at the College of Winterhold. Located within this hall are the personal cubicles and beds of notable mages, including Drevis Neloren, the master trainer of Illusion, and Faralda, the master trainer of Destruction. Along with the Hall of Attainment, it is one of the two main sleeping areas for students and faculty at the College.

The hall contains several notable features: a trapdoor leading to the Midden, the underground area housing some of the College''s deepest secrets, as well as an arcane enchanter and an alchemy lab on the upper floor. Drevis Neloren’s bedroom on the lower floor also holds an alchemy lab, allowing for easy access to alchemical experimentation. The upper floor is home to Colette Marence, a Restoration expert, and Sergius Turrianus, an expert in Enchanting, both of whom also provide their respective magical training to students.', '''access'':131B ''alchem'':133B ''alchemi'':110B,126B ''allow'':128B ''along'':57B ''also'':123B,156B ''arcan'':106B ''area'':71B,93B ''attain'':62B ''bed'':38B ''bedroom'':118B ''colett'':141B ''colleg'':26B,78B,98B ''contain'':81B ''counten'':3A,7B ''cubicl'':36B ''deepest'':100B ''destruct'':56B ''drevi'':43B,116B ''easi'':130B ''enchant'':107B,152B ''experiment'':134B ''expert'':145B,150B ''faculti'':75B ''faralda'':51B ''featur'':84B ''floor'':115B,122B,137B ''hall'':1A,5B,32B,60B,80B ''higher'':21B ''higher-rank'':20B ''hold'':124B ''home'':139B ''hous'':94B ''illus'':49B ''includ'':42B ''lab'':111B,127B ''lead'':87B ''live'':12B ''locat'':29B ''lower'':121B ''mage'':23B,41B ''magic'':160B ''main'':69B ''mani'':17B ''marenc'':142B ''master'':46B,53B ''midden'':90B ''neloren'':44B ''neloren’'':117B ''notabl'':40B,83B ''one'':65B ''person'':35B ''primari'':11B ''provid'':157B ''quarter'':15B ''rank'':22B ''respect'':159B ''restor'':144B ''secret'':101B ''sergius'':147B ''serv'':8B ''sever'':82B ''sleep'':14B,70B ''student'':73B,163B ''train'':161B ''trainer'':47B,54B ''trapdoor'':86B ''turrianus'':148B ''two'':68B ''underground'':92B ''upper'':114B,136B ''well'':103B ''winterhold'':28B ''within'':30B', 'collegeofwinterhold', 'The Hall of Countenance is one of the areas in the College. You do not know anything else. about the area.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'winterhold', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('erikur''s_house', 'Erikur''s House is a large mansion located just northwest of the Blue Palace in Solitude. It is the last building on the right before the Blue Palace, across from the Bards College and Bryling''s House. The mansion is the residence of Erikur, a Nord warrior and Thane of Solitude, who oversees local businesses and engages in trade, notably importing low-quality elven weapons from Black Marsh to sell at inflated prices to the Imperial army.

The house is also home to Gisli, a Nord ranger and Erikur''s sister, who is known for being discouraged and disillusioned, in contrast to her arrogant brother. Additionally, the mansion houses Melaran, a High Elf mage, who likely brings his magical expertise to the household. The mansion''s central location and notable inhabitants make it a significant location in Solitude''s upper social circle.', '''across'':32B ''addit'':110B ''also'':85B ''armi'':81B ''arrog'':108B ''bard'':35B ''black'':71B ''blue'':16B,30B ''bring'':121B ''brother'':109B ''bryle'':38B ''build'':24B ''busi'':58B ''central'':131B ''circl'':146B ''colleg'':36B ''contrast'':105B ''discourag'':101B ''disillus'':103B ''elf'':117B ''elven'':68B ''engag'':60B ''erikur'':1A,4B,47B,93B ''expertis'':124B ''gisli'':88B ''high'':116B ''home'':86B ''hous'':3A,6B,40B,83B,113B ''household'':127B ''imperi'':80B ''import'':64B ''inflat'':76B ''inhabit'':135B ''known'':98B ''larg'':9B ''last'':23B ''like'':120B ''local'':57B ''locat'':11B,132B,140B ''low'':66B ''low-qual'':65B ''mage'':118B ''magic'':123B ''make'':136B ''mansion'':10B,42B,112B,129B ''marsh'':72B ''melaran'':114B ''nord'':49B,90B ''northwest'':13B ''notabl'':63B,134B ''overse'':56B ''palac'':17B,31B ''price'':77B ''qualiti'':67B ''ranger'':91B ''resid'':45B ''right'':27B ''sell'':74B ''signific'':139B ''sister'':95B ''social'':145B ''solitud'':19B,54B,142B ''thane'':52B ''trade'':62B ''upper'':144B ''warrior'':50B ''weapon'':69B', 'haafingar', 'Erikur''s House is a large mansion located just northwest of the Blue Palace in Solitude. You do not know about Erikur.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lost_valley_redoubt', 'Lost Valley Redoubt is a massive Nordic ruin located a short distance west of Bilegulch Mine, southeast of Markarth, and northwest of Falkreath in the Reach. The site is inhabited by Forsworn and hagravens, presenting a formidable challenge for adventurers.

The pathway from the river ascends through several open terraces, each guarded by Forsworn sentries. The sprawling layout and numerous foes make it a location that requires preparation and endurance.', '''adventur'':43B ''ascend'':49B ''bilegulch'':18B ''challeng'':41B ''distanc'':15B ''endur'':73B ''falkreath'':26B ''foe'':64B ''formid'':40B ''forsworn'':35B,57B ''guard'':55B ''hagraven'':37B ''inhabit'':33B ''layout'':61B ''locat'':12B,68B ''lost'':1A,4B ''make'':65B ''markarth'':22B ''massiv'':9B ''mine'':19B ''nordic'':10B ''northwest'':24B ''numer'':63B ''open'':52B ''pathway'':45B ''prepar'':71B ''present'':38B ''reach'':29B ''redoubt'':3A,6B ''requir'':70B ''river'':48B ''ruin'':11B ''sentri'':58B ''sever'':51B ''short'':14B ''site'':31B ''southeast'':20B ''sprawl'':60B ''terrac'':53B ''valley'':2A,5B ''west'':16B', 'reach', 'Lost Valley Redoubt is a massive Nordic ruin located southeast of Markarth, and northwest of Falkreath in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('freeze', 'Freeze is an Alteration spell that encases a target in ice, immobilizing them for a brief duration. It requires a Novice skill level to cast.', '''alter'':5B ''brief'':17B ''cast'':26B ''durat'':18B ''encas'':8B ''freez'':1A,2B ''ice'':12B ''immobil'':13B ''level'':24B ''novic'':22B ''requir'':20B ''skill'':23B ''spell'':6B ''target'':10B', 'mage', '
Freeze is a spell that encases a target in ice, temporarily immobilizing them. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fort_kastav', 'Fort Kastav is a medium-sized fort located south of Winterhold, situated in a mountain pass that spans almost the entire width of the pass, leaving just enough room for the Whiterun-Winterhold road to pass through. The fort’s impressive exterior takes full advantage of the natural features of the mountain, featuring numerous lookout platforms and an extensive ramp system for easy access to its high walls.

Once occupied by warlocks, the fort is now overrun by skeletons who patrol its walls and grounds. These undead guardians make the fort a dangerous place for any who dare approach.', '''access'':67B ''advantag'':48B ''almost'':22B ''approach'':102B ''danger'':96B ''dare'':101B ''easi'':66B ''enough'':31B ''entir'':24B ''extens'':62B ''exterior'':45B ''featur'':52B,56B ''fort'':1A,3B,10B,77B,94B ''fort’'':43B ''full'':47B ''ground'':88B ''guardian'':91B ''high'':70B ''impress'':44B ''kastav'':2A,4B ''leav'':29B ''locat'':11B ''lookout'':58B ''make'':92B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''mountain'':18B,55B ''natur'':51B ''numer'':57B ''occupi'':73B ''overrun'':80B ''pass'':19B,28B,40B ''patrol'':84B ''place'':97B ''platform'':59B ''ramp'':63B ''road'':38B ''room'':32B ''situat'':15B ''size'':9B ''skeleton'':82B ''south'':12B ''span'':21B ''system'':64B ''take'':46B ''undead'':90B ''wall'':71B,86B ''warlock'':75B ''whiterun'':36B ''whiterun-winterhold'':35B ''width'':25B ''winterhold'':14B,37B', 'winterhold, legion, stormcloak', 'Fort Kastav is a medium-sized fort located south of Winterhold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('absorb_health', 'These magical effects are offensive Destruction enchantments that drain health from the target and transfer it to the wielder. This effect can be applied through custom enchanting and is also found on enchanted weapons, combining offense and self-healing.', '''absorb'':1A ''also'':32B ''appli'':26B ''combin'':37B ''custom'':28B ''destruct'':8B ''drain'':11B ''effect'':5B,23B ''enchant'':9B,29B,35B ''found'':33B ''heal'':42B ''health'':2A,12B ''magic'':4B ''offens'':7B,38B ''self'':41B ''self-heal'':40B ''target'':15B ''transfer'':17B ''weapon'':36B ''wielder'':21B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic drains health from an enemy and gives it to the person using the enchantment. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('teleport_pet', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Alteration spells that instantly summon the caster;s bonded animal companion or summoned creature to their side. This effect is only available as a spell, ensuring that loyal companions remain close during travel or combat, even when separated by great distances.', '''alter'':10B ''anim'':19B ''avail'':31B ''bond'':18B ''caster'':16B ''close'':40B ''combat'':44B ''companion'':20B,38B ''creatur'':23B ''distanc'':50B ''effect'':5B,28B ''ensur'':35B ''even'':45B ''focus'':9B ''great'':49B ''instant'':13B ''loyal'':37B ''magic'':4B ''pet'':2A ''remain'':39B ''separ'':47B ''side'':26B ''spell'':11B,34B ''summon'':14B,22B ''teleport'':1A ''travel'':42B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B', 'mage', 'This spell brings your pet or summoned creature back to your side instantly. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nordic_dagger', 'Nordic Dagger is a light Nordic weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. To craft it: 1 quicksilver ingot, 1 leather strip, and 1 steel ingot at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using quicksilver at a workbench.', '''1'':38B,41B,45B ''adept'':53B ''ancient'':33B ''blacksmith'':50B ''craft'':36B,56B ''craftsmanship'':34B ''dagger'':2A,4B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''engrav'':30B ''evok'':32B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':51B ''good'':12B ''gray'':25B ''ingot'':40B,47B ''intric'':28B ''leather'':42B ''light'':7B ''nordic'':1A,3B,8B,29B ''quicksilv'':39B,64B ''silver'':24B ''silver-gray'':23B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':46B ''strip'':43B ''sturdi'':18B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''weather'':20B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Nordic Dagger is a light Nordic weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('knights_of_the_nine', 'The Knights of the Nine was a knightly order founded in 3E 111 by Sir Amiel Lannus, a hero of the War of the Isle, with the aim of recovering the lost Relics of Pelinal Whitestrake, the Divine Crusader. Initially celebrated for their victories, including the recovery of the Cuirass, Gauntlets, Greaves, and Sword, the order became the most prestigious in Cyrodiil after the arrival of the noble Berich Vlindrel. However, their success led to personal pride and internal conflict. In 3E 121, the order fractured during the War of the Red Diamond when Sir Berich stole relics, leading to a deadly confrontation with Sir Caius. Many knights left to join the war, and the order gradually dissolved, with only a few knights continuing quests for the remaining relics.

The order''s decline continued with individual knights meeting tragic fates. Sir Ralvas failed to claim the Mace of the Crusader, while Sir Juncan died shortly after discovering the Boots'' location. Sir Torolf and Sir Gregory perished in the War, and Sir Henrik hid the Shield of the Crusader before dying in defense of it. Sir Casimir''s arrogance led to his downfall when he killed a beggar in the Chapel of Stendarr, resulting in a curse and his eventual death. By 3E 131, the Knights of the Nine were officially disbanded, and Sir Berich became a political figure with resentment towards the order. In 3E 153, Sir Amiel embarked on a final quest but never returned. In 3E 433, the Hero of Kvatch restored the Knights by recovering the Relics and slaying Umaril the Unfeathered, regaining the order’s lost honor.', '''111'':17B ''121'':87B ''131'':217B ''153'':240B ''3e'':16B,86B,216B,239B,252B ''433'':253B ''aim'':32B ''amiel'':20B,242B ''arriv'':69B ''arrog'':192B ''becam'':61B,229B ''beggar'':201B ''berich'':73B,100B,228B ''boot'':163B ''caius'':110B ''casimir'':190B ''celebr'':45B ''chapel'':204B ''claim'':149B ''conflict'':84B ''confront'':107B ''continu'':128B,138B ''crusad'':43B,154B,182B ''cuirass'':54B ''curs'':210B ''cyrodiil'':66B ''dead'':106B ''death'':214B ''declin'':137B ''defens'':186B ''diamond'':97B ''die'':158B,184B ''disband'':225B ''discov'':161B ''dissolv'':122B ''divin'':42B ''downfal'':196B ''embark'':243B ''eventu'':213B ''fail'':147B ''fate'':144B ''figur'':232B ''final'':246B ''found'':14B ''fractur'':90B ''gauntlet'':55B ''gradual'':121B ''greav'':56B ''gregori'':169B ''henrik'':176B ''hero'':23B,255B ''hid'':177B ''honor'':274B ''howev'':75B ''includ'':49B ''individu'':140B ''initi'':44B ''intern'':83B ''isl'':29B ''join'':115B ''juncan'':157B ''kill'':199B ''knight'':1A,6B,12B,112B,127B,141B,219B,260B ''kvatch'':257B ''lannus'':21B ''lead'':103B ''led'':78B,193B ''left'':113B ''locat'':164B ''lost'':36B,273B ''mace'':151B ''mani'':111B ''meet'':142B ''never'':249B ''nine'':4A,9B,222B ''nobl'':72B ''offici'':224B ''order'':13B,60B,89B,120B,135B,237B ''order’'':272B ''pelin'':39B ''perish'':170B ''person'':80B ''polit'':231B ''prestigi'':64B ''pride'':81B ''quest'':129B,247B ''ralva'':146B ''recov'':34B,262B ''recoveri'':51B ''red'':96B ''regain'':270B ''relic'':37B,102B,133B,264B ''remain'':132B ''resent'':234B ''restor'':258B ''result'':207B ''return'':250B ''shield'':179B ''short'':159B ''sir'':19B,99B,109B,145B,156B,165B,168B,175B,189B,227B,241B ''slay'':266B ''stendarr'':206B ''stole'':101B ''success'':77B ''sword'':58B ''torolf'':166B ''toward'':235B ''tragic'':143B ''umaril'':267B ''unfeath'':269B ''victori'':48B ''vlindrel'':74B ''war'':26B,93B,117B,173B ''whitestrak'':40B', 'imperial, scholar', '', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bonemold_boots', 'Bonemold Boots are a pair of bonemold boots with basic protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. To craft it: 1 netch leather, 1 iron ingots, 6 bonemold ingot at a blacksmith forge. An Apprentice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using bonemeal at a workbench.', '''1'':40B,43B ''6'':46B ''apprentic'':54B ''basic'':12B ''bind'':32B ''blacksmith'':51B ''bone'':26B ''bone-lik'':25B ''bonem'':65B ''bonemold'':1A,3B,9B,47B ''boot'':2A,4B,10B ''craft'':38B,57B ''dark'':31B ''design'':17B ''forg'':52B ''ingot'':45B,48B ''iron'':44B ''leather'':42B ''like'':27B ''netch'':41B ''organ'':21B ''pair'':7B ''protect'':13B ''qualiti'':14B ''reinforc'':29B ''rough'':19B ''shape'':36B ''smith'':55B ''tan'':24B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''textur'':28B ''use'':64B ''utilitarian'':35B ''visual'':16B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Bonemold Boots are a pair of bonemold boots with basic protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_the_berserker', 'This potion empowers warriors who wield two-handed weapons, increasing their strength for devastating blows. Slightly increases two-handed weapon damage, with higher-tier potions greatly amplifying the strength of each strike. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':51B ''amplifi'':34B ''berserk'':4A ''blow'':20B ''damag'':27B ''devast'':19B ''draught'':61B ''elixir'':64B ''empow'':7B ''found'':44B ''great'':33B ''hand'':13B,25B ''higher'':30B ''higher-ti'':29B ''increas'':15B,22B ''loot'':47B ''philter'':62B ''potion'':1A,6B,32B,41B,60B ''purchas'':49B ''random'':46B ''sever'':54B ''slight'':21B ''strength'':17B,36B ''strike'':39B ''strongest'':59B ''tier'':31B,55B ''two'':12B,24B ''two-hand'':11B,23B ''warrior'':8B ''weakest'':57B ''weapon'':14B,26B ''wield'':10B', 'warrior, alchemist, companions, guard', 'The Potion of the Berserker boosts the strength of two-handed weapon strikes. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rannveig''s_fast', '
Rannveig''s Fast is a small Nordic ruin located east-northeast of Rorikstead and south of Cold Rock Pass in Whiterun Hold. The ruin is shrouded in mystery.', '''cold'':21B ''east'':14B ''east-northeast'':13B ''fast'':3A,6B ''hold'':26B ''locat'':12B ''mysteri'':32B ''nordic'':10B ''northeast'':15B ''pass'':23B ''rannveig'':1A,4B ''rock'':22B ''rorikstead'':17B ''ruin'':11B,28B ''shroud'':30B ''small'':9B ''south'':19B ''whiterun'':25B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Rannveig''s Fast is a small Nordic ruin located east-northeast of Rorikstead in Whiterun Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('colovia', 'Colovia, also known as the Colovian West or Old Colovia, constitutes the western half of the province of Cyrodiil. Renowned for its strong-willed and industrious inhabitants, Colovia has a rich martial tradition, with many citizens serving in the Imperial Legion. The region is characterized by its rugged landscapes, which include hilly terrains along the Gold Road, dense forests in the Great Forest, and expansive grasslands within the Imperial Reserve, a well-known area for hunting.

The Colovians are known for their self-sufficiency and craftsmanship, particularly in timber, which is highly sought after for construction and weaponry. While most Colovians reside in major cities such as Anvil, Chorrol, Kvatch, and Skingrad, the nobility often inhabit private estates near the Gold Coast. Despite shifts in territorial borders over the eras, Colovia remains a vital part of Cyrodiil, blending a fierce frontier spirit with a deep appreciation for their agricultural and natural resources.', '''agricultur'':153B ''along'':56B ''also'':3B ''anvil'':112B ''appreci'':150B ''area'':77B ''blend'':142B ''border'':131B ''character'':47B ''chorrol'':113B ''citi'':109B ''citizen'':38B ''coast'':126B ''colovia'':1A,2B,11B,30B,135B ''colovian'':7B,81B,105B ''constitut'':12B ''construct'':100B ''craftsmanship'':90B ''cyrodiil'':20B,141B ''deep'':149B ''dens'':60B ''despit'':127B ''era'':134B ''estat'':122B ''expans'':67B ''fierc'':144B ''forest'':61B,65B ''frontier'':145B ''gold'':58B,125B ''grassland'':68B ''great'':64B ''half'':15B ''high'':96B ''hilli'':54B ''hunt'':79B ''imperi'':42B,71B ''includ'':53B ''industri'':28B ''inhabit'':29B,120B ''known'':4B,76B,83B ''kvatch'':114B ''landscap'':51B ''legion'':43B ''major'':108B ''mani'':37B ''martial'':34B ''natur'':155B ''near'':123B ''nobil'':118B ''often'':119B ''old'':10B ''part'':139B ''particular'':91B ''privat'':121B ''provinc'':18B ''region'':45B ''remain'':136B ''renown'':21B ''reserv'':72B ''resid'':106B ''resourc'':156B ''rich'':33B ''road'':59B ''rug'':50B ''self'':87B ''self-suffici'':86B ''serv'':39B ''shift'':128B ''skingrad'':116B ''sought'':97B ''spirit'':146B ''strong'':25B ''strong-wil'':24B ''suffici'':88B ''terrain'':55B ''territori'':130B ''timber'':93B ''tradit'':35B ''vital'':138B ''weaponri'':102B ''well'':75B ''well-known'':74B ''west'':8B ''western'':14B ''will'':26B ''within'':69B', 'scholar, imperial', '
Colovia, or Old Colovia, is the western half of Cyrodiil, known for its strong-willed inhabitants and rich martial tradition. The region is characterized by rugged landscapes, including hilly terrains, dense forests, and expansive grasslands. Colovians are self-sufficient and skilled in craftsmanship, especially in timber used for construction and weaponry. Major cities like Anvil, Chorrol, Kvatch, and Skingrad are home to most Colovians, while the nobility live near the Gold Coast. Despite historical shifts in borders, Colovia remains a vital region in Cyrodiil, blending frontier spirit with a deep respect for agricultural and natural resources.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('haafingar_stormcloak_camp', 'Haafingar Stormcloak Camp is a Stormcloak military encampment located northeast of Dragon Bridge and south of the Statue to Meridia in Haafingar. This camp serves as a base for Stormcloak forces operating in the region during the civil war.', '''base'':31B ''bridg'':16B ''camp'':3A,6B,27B ''civil'':41B ''dragon'':15B ''encamp'':11B ''forc'':34B ''haafingar'':1A,4B,25B ''locat'':12B ''meridia'':23B ''militari'':10B ''northeast'':13B ''oper'':35B ''region'':38B ''serv'':28B ''south'':18B ''statu'':21B ''stormcloak'':2A,5B,9B,33B ''war'':42B', 'haafingar, stormcloak', 'Haafingar Stormcloak Camp is a Stormcloak military encampment located northeast of Dragon Bridge in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ebony_greatsword', 'Ebony Greatsword is a two-handed ebony weapon which deals fantastic damage. 
Its visual design is sleek and black, with smooth, angular lines and silver accents that give it a refined yet intimidating appearance. To craft it: 5 ebony ingots and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using ebony at a workbench.', '''3'':45B ''5'':41B ''accent'':29B ''angular'':25B ''appear'':37B ''black'':22B ''blacksmith'':50B ''craft'':39B,56B ''damag'':15B ''deal'':13B ''design'':18B ''eboni'':1A,3B,10B,42B,64B ''expert'':53B ''fantast'':14B ''forg'':51B ''give'':31B ''greatsword'':2A,4B ''hand'':9B ''ingot'':43B ''intimid'':36B ''leather'':46B ''line'':26B ''refin'':34B ''silver'':28B ''sleek'':20B ''smith'':54B ''smooth'':24B ''strip'':47B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''two'':8B ''two-hand'':7B ''use'':63B ''visual'':17B ''weapon'':11B ''workbench'':67B ''yet'':35B', 'blacksmith', 'Ebony Greatsword is a two-handed ebony weapon which deals fantastic damage. 
Its visual design is sleek and black, with smooth, angular lines and silver accents that give it a refined yet intimidating appearance. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stamina_poison', 'Favored by warriors, this poison saps the target''s stamina, reducing their ability to perform power attacks or block effectively. Higher tiers drain more stamina, debilitating melee combatants. These poisons can be found in random loot, purchased from apothecaries, or crafted using alchemy. Tiers: weak, standard, potent, virulent, deadly.', '''abil'':15B ''alchemi'':45B ''apothecari'':41B ''attack'':19B ''block'':21B ''combat'':30B ''craft'':43B ''dead'':51B ''debilit'':28B ''drain'':25B ''effect'':22B ''favor'':3B ''found'':35B ''higher'':23B ''loot'':38B ''mele'':29B ''perform'':17B ''poison'':2A,7B,32B ''potent'':49B ''power'':18B ''purchas'':39B ''random'':37B ''reduc'':13B ''sap'':8B ''stamina'':1A,12B,27B ''standard'':48B ''target'':10B ''tier'':24B,46B ''use'':44B ''virul'':50B ''warrior'':5B ''weak'':47B', 'warrior, alchemist, thief, hunter, companions, darkbrotherhood', 'This poison drains stamina, reducing the effectiveness of melee attacks. You do not know the full effects or details of this poison. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fear_poison', 'A tool for controlling the battlefield, this poison causes creatures and people to flee in fear, giving you time to regroup. Stronger variants affect higher-level targets. These poisons can be found in random loot, purchased from apothecaries, or crafted using alchemy. Tiers: weak, standard, potent, virulent, deadly.', '''affect'':26B ''alchemi'':45B ''apothecari'':41B ''battlefield'':8B ''caus'':11B ''control'':6B ''craft'':43B ''creatur'':12B ''dead'':51B ''fear'':1A,18B ''flee'':16B ''found'':35B ''give'':19B ''higher'':28B ''higher-level'':27B ''level'':29B ''loot'':38B ''peopl'':14B ''poison'':2A,10B,32B ''potent'':49B ''purchas'':39B ''random'':37B ''regroup'':23B ''standard'':48B ''stronger'':24B ''target'':30B ''tier'':46B ''time'':21B ''tool'':4B ''use'':44B ''variant'':25B ''virul'':50B ''weak'':47B', 'alchemist, thief, mage, bard, scholar, darkbrotherhood, witch', 'This poison causes fear in enemies, making them flee temporarily. You do not know the full effects or details of this poison. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('conjurers_potion', 'This potion empowers conjuration magic, extending the duration of summoned allies or bound weapons. It is a staple for necromancers and battle mages alike. Extends conjuration spell durations slightly, with higher tiers providing more substantial enhancements for summoning magic. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':53B ''alik'':26B ''alli'':13B ''battl'':24B ''bound'':15B ''conjur'':1A,6B,28B ''draught'':63B ''durat'':10B,30B ''elixir'':66B ''empow'':5B ''enhanc'':38B ''extend'':8B,27B ''found'':46B ''higher'':33B ''loot'':49B ''mage'':25B ''magic'':7B,41B ''necromanc'':22B ''philter'':64B ''potion'':2A,4B,43B,62B ''provid'':35B ''purchas'':51B ''random'':48B ''sever'':56B ''slight'':31B ''spell'':29B ''stapl'':20B ''strongest'':61B ''substanti'':37B ''summon'':12B,40B ''tier'':34B,57B ''weakest'':59B ''weapon'':16B', 'mage, alchemist, scholar, collegeofwinterhold, psijic, witch', 'The Conjurer''s Potion extends the duration of summoned allies or bound weapons. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('abandoned_lodge', 'The Abandoned Lodge is a small, secluded shack located north-northeast of Raven Rock on Solstheim. ', '''abandon'':1A,4B ''locat'':11B ''lodg'':2A,5B ''north'':13B ''north-northeast'':12B ''northeast'':14B ''raven'':16B ''rock'':17B ''seclud'':9B ''shack'':10B ''small'':8B ''solstheim'':19B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tolvald''s_cave', 'Tolvald''s Cave is a large cavern complex located in the Velothi Mountains, northeast of Shor''s Stone and south-southeast of Ansilvund in the Rift. Rumours of Falmer have been seen coming out the cave late at night.', '''ansilvund'':27B ''cave'':3A,6B,40B ''cavern'':10B ''come'':37B ''complex'':11B ''falmer'':33B ''larg'':9B ''late'':41B ''locat'':12B ''mountain'':16B ''night'':43B ''northeast'':17B ''rift'':30B ''rumour'':31B ''seen'':36B ''shor'':19B ''south'':24B ''south-southeast'':23B ''southeast'':25B ''stone'':21B ''tolvald'':1A,4B ''velothi'':15B', 'rift', 'Tolvald''s Cave is a large cavern complex located in the Velothi Mountains, northeast of Shor''s Stone.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fly_amanita', 'Fly Amanita is a red capped mushroom commonly found in caves, known for its fiery and strengthening properties. Alchemy effects: Resist Fire, Fortify Two-handed, Frenzy, and Regenerate Stamina.', '''alchemi'':21B ''amanita'':2A,4B ''cap'':8B ''cave'':13B ''common'':10B ''effect'':22B ''fieri'':17B ''fire'':24B ''fli'':1A,3B ''fortifi'':25B ''found'':11B ''frenzi'':29B ''hand'':28B ''known'':14B ''mushroom'':9B ''properti'':20B ''red'':7B ''regener'':31B ''resist'':23B ''stamina'':32B ''strengthen'':19B ''two'':27B ''two-hand'':26B', 'alchemist', 'Fly Amanita is a red capped mushroom commonly found in caves, known for its fiery and strengthening properties. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gleamblossom', 'Gleamblossom are purple and light blue plants, that look like an upside down bell, is harvested from the flower of the same name, known for its potent magical effects. Alchemy effects: Resist Magic, Fear, Regenerate Health, and Paralysis.', '''alchemi'':31B ''bell'':15B ''blue'':7B ''effect'':30B,32B ''fear'':35B ''flower'':20B ''gleamblossom'':1A,2B ''harvest'':17B ''health'':37B ''known'':25B ''light'':6B ''like'':11B ''look'':10B ''magic'':29B,34B ''name'':24B ''paralysi'':39B ''plant'':8B ''potent'':28B ''purpl'':4B ''regener'':36B ''resist'':33B ''upsid'':13B', 'alchemist', 'Gleamblossom are purple and light blue plants, that look like an upside down bell, is harvested from the flower of the same name, known for its potent magical effects. 
