INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gloomreach', 'Gloomreach is a medium-sized cave located southeast of Old Hroldan Inn in the Reach. The cave is inhabited by Falmer.', '''cave'':8B,19B ''falmer'':23B ''gloomreach'':1A,2B ''hroldan'':13B ''inhabit'':21B ''inn'':14B ''locat'':9B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''old'':12B ''reach'':17B ''size'':7B ''southeast'':10B', 'reach', 'Gloomreach is a medium-sized cave located southeast of Old Hroldan Inn in the Reach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('olaf_and_the_dragon', 'Olaf and the Dragon, written by Adonato Leotelli, explores the legendary tale of Olaf One-Eye, a hero who defeated the dragon Numinex in an epic battle for Skyrim''s future. The dragon, a terrifying force that had ravaged Skyrim, was eventually confronted by Olaf, a warrior who would later become the High King of Skyrim. The legend tells of Olaf''s battle against Numinex atop Mount Athor, where the two engage in a brutal shouting contest that shatters the land. Ultimately, Olaf triumphs, capturing the dragon and bringing him to Whiterun, where the beast is imprisoned in a place that would become known as Dragonsreach. Olaf''s victory solidifies his leadership, ending a bitter war of succession among Skyrim''s holds.

Themes of heroism, power, and the distortion of history are prevalent throughout the work. Leotelli presents Olaf''s victory as a symbol of Nordic strength and unity, though he acknowledges doubts surrounding the legend''s authenticity. Alternative versions of the story suggest that Numinex was already weak due to age, and that Olaf and his men may have fabricated the tale for personal gain. The account also references a rebellious bard, Svaknir, who challenged Olaf''s version, adding an intriguing layer of historical ambiguity. The book raises important questions about how history is remembered and the ways in which legends are shaped by those in power.', '''account'':193B ''acknowledg'':157B ''ad'':205B ''adonato'':11B ''age'':177B ''alreadi'':173B ''also'':194B ''altern'':164B ''ambigu'':211B ''among'':124B ''athor'':73B ''atop'':71B ''authent'':163B ''bard'':198B ''battl'':32B,68B ''beast'':100B ''becom'':56B,108B ''bitter'':120B ''book'':213B ''bring'':94B ''brutal'':80B ''captur'':90B ''challeng'':201B ''confront'':48B ''contest'':82B ''defeat'':25B ''distort'':134B ''doubt'':158B ''dragon'':4A,8B,27B,38B,92B ''dragonsreach'':111B ''due'':175B ''end'':118B ''engag'':77B ''epic'':31B ''eventu'':47B ''explor'':13B ''eye'':21B ''fabric'':186B ''forc'':41B ''futur'':36B ''gain'':191B ''hero'':23B ''heroism'':130B ''high'':58B ''histor'':210B ''histori'':136B,219B ''hold'':127B ''import'':215B ''imprison'':102B ''intrigu'':207B ''king'':59B ''known'':109B ''land'':86B ''later'':55B ''layer'':208B ''leadership'':117B ''legend'':63B,161B,227B ''legendari'':15B ''leotelli'':12B,142B ''may'':184B ''men'':183B ''mount'':72B ''nordic'':151B ''numinex'':28B,70B,171B ''olaf'':1A,5B,18B,50B,66B,88B,112B,144B,180B,202B ''one'':20B ''one-ey'':19B ''person'':190B ''place'':105B ''power'':131B,233B ''present'':143B ''preval'':138B ''question'':216B ''rais'':214B ''ravag'':44B ''rebelli'':197B ''refer'':195B ''rememb'':221B ''shape'':229B ''shatter'':84B ''shout'':81B ''skyrim'':34B,45B,61B,125B ''solidifi'':115B ''stori'':168B ''strength'':152B ''success'':123B ''suggest'':169B ''surround'':159B ''svaknir'':199B ''symbol'':149B ''tale'':16B,188B ''tell'':64B ''terrifi'':40B ''theme'':128B ''though'':155B ''throughout'':139B ''triumph'':89B ''two'':76B ''ultim'':87B ''uniti'':154B ''version'':165B,204B ''victori'':114B,146B ''war'':121B ''warrior'':52B ''way'':224B ''weak'':174B ''whiterun'':97B ''work'':141B ''would'':54B,107B ''written'':9B', 'scholar', 'Olaf and the Dragon, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, recounts the legendary battle between Olaf One-Eye and the dragon Numinex, exploring themes of heroism, power, and the distortion of history. The book delves into how legends are shaped by those in power, questioning the authenticity of the story while reflecting on Nordic strength and unity.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('beehive_husk', 'Beehive Husk is a versatile ingredient known for its ability to enhance defense and magical abilities. Alchemy effects: Resist Poison, Fortify Light Armor, Fortify Sneak, and Fortify Destruction.', '''abil'':12B,18B ''alchemi'':19B ''armor'':25B ''beehiv'':1A,3B ''defens'':15B ''destruct'':30B ''effect'':20B ''enhanc'':14B ''fortifi'':23B,26B,29B ''husk'':2A,4B ''ingredi'':8B ''known'':9B ''light'':24B ''magic'':17B ''poison'':22B ''resist'':21B ''sneak'':27B ''versatil'':7B', 'alchemist', 'Beehive Husk is a versatile ingredient known for its ability to enhance defense and magical abilities.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ragnar_the_red', 'Verses for Ragnar the Red song:
There once was a hero named Ragnar the Red, who came riding to Whiterun from ole Rorikstead!
And the braggart did swagger and brandish his blade, as he told of bold battles and gold he had made!
But then he went quiet, did Ragnar the Red, when he met the shieldmaiden Matilda who said...
Oh, you talk and you lie and you drink all our mead! Now I think it''s high time that you lie down and bleed!
And so then came the clashing and slashing of steel, as the brave lass Matilda charged in full of zeal!
And the braggart named Ragnar was boastful no moooooree... when his ugly red head rolled around on the floor!', '''around'':124B ''battl'':41B ''blade'':35B ''bleed'':88B ''boast'':115B ''bold'':40B ''braggart'':29B,111B ''brandish'':33B ''brave'':101B ''came'':20B,92B ''charg'':104B ''clash'':94B ''drink'':72B ''floor'':127B ''full'':106B ''gold'':43B ''head'':122B ''hero'':14B ''high'':81B ''lass'':102B ''lie'':69B,85B ''made'':46B ''matilda'':61B,103B ''mead'':75B ''met'':58B ''mooooore'':117B ''name'':15B,112B ''oh'':64B ''ole'':25B ''quiet'':51B ''ragnar'':1A,6B,16B,53B,113B ''red'':3A,8B,18B,55B,121B ''ride'':21B ''roll'':123B ''rorikstead'':26B ''said'':63B ''shieldmaiden'':60B ''slash'':96B ''song'':9B ''steel'':98B ''swagger'':31B ''talk'':66B ''think'':78B ''time'':82B ''told'':38B ''ugli'':120B ''vers'':4B ''went'':50B ''whiterun'':23B ''zeal'':108B', 'bard, scholar', '
The song tells the story of Ragnar the Red, a boastful hero who brags about his battles and wealth, only to be confronted and defeated by the shieldmaiden Matilda, who silences him with a swift and fatal blow. You don''t know the lyrics by heart.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('command_daedra', 'Command Daedra is a Conjuration spell that forces a summoned or hostile Daedra to fight for the caster for a limited time. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''cast'':32B ''caster'':20B ''command'':1A,3B ''conjur'':7B ''daedra'':2A,4B,15B ''expert'':28B ''fight'':17B ''forc'':10B ''hostil'':14B ''level'':30B ''limit'':23B ''requir'':26B ''skill'':29B ''spell'':8B ''summon'':12B ''time'':24B', 'mage', '
Command Daedra is a spell that forces a summoned or hostile Daedra to fight for the caster for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('jagar_tharn', 'Jagar Tharn was the Imperial Battlemage of Tamriel who ascended to the throne as Emperor following a nefarious scheme. He secretly imprisoned Emperor Uriel Septim VII in Oblivion and utilized Illusion magic to impersonate him for a decade, ruling from 3E 389 to 3E 399 during a tumultuous period known as the Imperial Simulacrum. While Tharn held the reins of power over the war-torn Empire, the specifics of his ambitions and achievements during this time remain largely unclear. His actions significantly impacted the political landscape of Tamriel, but the true extent of his goals and motivations has been lost to history.', '''389'':44B ''399'':47B ''3e'':43B,46B ''achiev'':76B ''action'':84B ''ambit'':74B ''ascend'':12B ''battlemag'':8B ''decad'':40B ''emperor'':17B,25B ''empir'':69B ''extent'':95B ''follow'':18B ''goal'':98B ''held'':59B ''histori'':105B ''illus'':33B ''impact'':86B ''imperi'':7B,55B ''imperson'':36B ''imprison'':24B ''jagar'':1A,3B ''known'':52B ''landscap'':89B ''larg'':81B ''lost'':103B ''magic'':34B ''motiv'':100B ''nefari'':20B ''oblivion'':30B ''period'':51B ''polit'':88B ''power'':63B ''rein'':61B ''remain'':80B ''rule'':41B ''scheme'':21B ''secret'':23B ''septim'':27B ''signific'':85B ''simulacrum'':56B ''specif'':71B ''tamriel'':10B,91B ''tharn'':2A,4B,58B ''throne'':15B ''time'':79B ''torn'':68B ''true'':94B ''tumultu'':50B ''unclear'':82B ''uriel'':26B ''util'':32B ''vii'':28B ''war'':67B ''war-torn'':66B', 'imperial, scholar', 'Jagar Tharn was the Imperial Battlemage who ascended to the throne through deception, secretly imprisoning Emperor Uriel Septim VII in Oblivion and using Illusion magic to impersonate him. He ruled as Emperor from 3E 389 to 3E 399 during the Imperial Simulacrum, a period of political turmoil. Although Tharn held power, the details of his ambitions and achievements remain largely unclear, and his actions significantly influenced the political landscape of Tamriel. The full extent of his goals and motivations has been lost to history.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('saint_jiub', 'Saint Jiub, also known as Jiub the Magnificent and Eradicator of the Winged Menace, is a revered figure in the Tribunal Temple and the New Temple. Originally a Dunmer assassin with a troubled past marked by addiction and crime, Jiub sought redemption after being imprisoned for his deeds. He famously dedicated himself to eradicating the cliff racers that plagued Vvardenfell, achieving this feat after years of effort. His actions earned him sainthood from Vivec, who admired his virtue, and he became celebrated as a hero throughout Morrowind.

In 3E 433, during the onset of the Oblivion Crisis, Jiub was in Kvatch working on an extensive autobiography when the city was attacked. He was trapped in the Soul Cairn by a Dremora, leading to a long existence in that realm. His spirit remained unaware of his death until he encountered the Last Dragonborn in 4E 201, who assisted him in compiling his memoirs. Jiub''s story serves as a testament to his transformation from a fallen assassin to a saint, embodying themes of redemption and legacy in Tamriel.', '''201'':147B ''3e'':91B ''433'':92B ''4e'':146B ''achiev'':63B ''action'':71B ''addict'':39B ''admir'':78B ''also'':5B ''assassin'':32B,168B ''assist'':149B ''attack'':113B ''autobiographi'':108B ''becam'':83B ''cairn'':120B ''celebr'':84B ''citi'':111B ''cliff'':58B ''compil'':152B ''crime'':41B ''crisi'':99B ''death'':138B ''dedic'':53B ''deed'':50B ''dragonborn'':144B ''dremora'':123B ''dunmer'':31B ''earn'':72B ''effort'':69B ''embodi'':172B ''encount'':141B ''erad'':12B,56B ''exist'':128B ''extens'':107B ''fallen'':167B ''famous'':52B ''feat'':65B ''figur'':20B ''hero'':87B ''imprison'':47B ''jiub'':2A,4B,8B,42B,100B,155B ''known'':6B ''kvatch'':103B ''last'':143B ''lead'':124B ''legaci'':177B ''long'':127B ''magnific'':10B ''mark'':37B ''memoir'':154B ''menac'':16B ''morrowind'':89B ''new'':27B ''oblivion'':98B ''onset'':95B ''origin'':29B ''past'':36B ''plagu'':61B ''racer'':59B ''realm'':131B ''redempt'':44B,175B ''remain'':134B ''rever'':19B ''saint'':1A,3B,171B ''sainthood'':74B ''serv'':158B ''sought'':43B ''soul'':119B ''spirit'':133B ''stori'':157B ''tamriel'':179B ''templ'':24B,28B ''testament'':161B ''theme'':173B ''throughout'':88B ''transform'':164B ''trap'':116B ''tribun'':23B ''troubl'':35B ''unawar'':135B ''virtu'':80B ''vivec'':76B ''vvardenfel'':62B ''wing'':15B ''work'':104B ''year'':67B', 'darkelf, daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Saint Jiub, also known as Jiub the Magnificent and Eradicator of the Winged Menace, is a revered figure in both the Tribunal Temple and the New Temple. Once a Dunmer assassin with a troubled past, he sought redemption by eradicating the cliff racers of Vvardenfell, a feat that earned him sainthood from Vivec. In 3E 433, during the Oblivion Crisis, Jiub was trapped in the Soul Cairn, unaware of his death, until he encountered the Last Dragonborn in 4E 201. Jiub’s transformation from a fallen assassin to a saint embodies themes of redemption and legacy.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rueful_axe', 'The Rueful Axe is a Daedric artifact forged by Clavicus Vile, the Prince of bargains and twisted desires, as the result of a grim pact. This massive iron-like battleaxe, adorned with engravings of werewolves but crafted from ebony, carries a powerful enchantment that saps the strength of those it strikes and is particularly effective against beasts. The axe is a testament to Clavicus Vile''s propensity for granting wishes in ways that bring misery, as its creation embodies the consequences of dark bargains.', '''adorn'':34B ''artifact'':9B ''axe'':2A,5B,62B ''bargain'':17B,87B ''battleax'':33B ''beast'':60B ''bring'':77B ''carri'':43B ''clavicus'':12B,67B ''consequ'':84B ''craft'':40B ''creation'':81B ''daedric'':8B ''dark'':86B ''desir'':20B ''eboni'':42B ''effect'':58B ''embodi'':82B ''enchant'':46B ''engrav'':36B ''forg'':10B ''grant'':72B ''grim'':26B ''iron'':31B ''iron-lik'':30B ''like'':32B ''massiv'':29B ''miseri'':78B ''pact'':27B ''particular'':57B ''power'':45B ''princ'':15B ''propens'':70B ''result'':23B ''rueful'':1A,4B ''sap'':48B ''strength'':50B ''strike'':54B ''testament'':65B ''twist'':19B ''vile'':13B,68B ''way'':75B ''werewolv'':38B ''wish'':73B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
The Rueful Axe is a Daedric artifact created by Clavicus Vile,thought ot be enchanted .', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mace_of_molag_bal', 'The Mace of Molag Bal, also known as the Vampire''s Mace, is a Daedric artifact associated with Molag Bal, the Daedric Prince of Domination and Enslavement. This powerful weapon is enchanted to drain the stamina and magicka of its victims, transferring their energy to its wielder. It is also capable of sapping an enemy''s strength and even trapping their soul, making it a fearsome weapon against wizards and other formidable foes. The mace is often described as a symbol of Molag Bal''s power and cruelty, embodying his desire to dominate and enslave.

The origins of the Mace can be traced back to when Molag Bal tricked an Orcish blacksmith into forging it while enslaving him in Coldharbour, the Daedric Prince''s plane of Oblivion. The mace is frequently granted to mortals deemed worthy by Molag Bal, who relishes the trail of death and destruction it leaves in its wake. Worshippers of Molag Bal refer to the weapon as the Master''s Mace and often invoke it in their prayers and oaths.', '''also'':10B,54B ''artifact'':20B ''associ'':21B ''back'':108B ''bal'':4A,9B,24B,88B,112B,143B,160B ''blacksmith'':116B ''capabl'':55B ''coldharbour'':124B ''cruelti'':92B ''daedric'':19B,26B,126B ''death'':149B ''deem'':139B ''describ'':82B ''desir'':95B ''destruct'':151B ''domin'':29B,97B ''drain'':38B ''embodi'':93B ''enchant'':36B ''enemi'':59B ''energi'':48B ''enslav'':31B,99B,121B ''even'':63B ''fearsom'':70B ''foe'':77B ''forg'':118B ''formid'':76B ''frequent'':135B ''grant'':136B ''invok'':172B ''known'':11B ''leav'':153B ''mace'':1A,6B,16B,79B,104B,133B,169B ''magicka'':42B ''make'':67B ''master'':167B ''molag'':3A,8B,23B,87B,111B,142B,159B ''mortal'':138B ''oath'':178B ''oblivion'':131B ''often'':81B,171B ''orcish'':115B ''origin'':101B ''plane'':129B ''power'':33B,90B ''prayer'':176B ''princ'':27B,127B ''refer'':161B ''relish'':145B ''sap'':57B ''soul'':66B ''stamina'':40B ''strength'':61B ''symbol'':85B ''trace'':107B ''trail'':147B ''transfer'':46B ''trap'':64B ''trick'':113B ''vampir'':14B ''victim'':45B ''wake'':156B ''weapon'':34B,71B,164B ''wielder'':51B ''wizard'':73B ''worshipp'':157B ''worthi'':140B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
The Mace of Molag Bal is a Daedric artifact that drains stamina and magicka, traps souls, and embodies Molag Bal''s power and cruelty. Forged through deceit, it is a symbol of domination and destruction.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('spear_of_bitter_mercy', '
The Spear of Bitter Mercy is a mysterious artifact believed to be of Daedric origin, originally forged by Mehrunes Dagon and later associated with Hircine, earning him the Reachfolk title "Spear with Five Points." Imbued with powerful energies capable of instantly killing all but High Daedra Lords, the Spear is central to Hircine''s Great Hunt and can only be wielded by those sanctified to its rules. Though once in Sheogorath''s possession, its history remains enigmatic, and it is known to reject unworthy wielders outside its intended purpose.', '''artifact'':13B ''associ'':27B ''believ'':14B ''bitter'':3A,8B ''capabl'':43B ''central'':55B ''daedra'':50B ''daedric'':18B ''dagon'':24B ''earn'':30B ''energi'':42B ''enigmat'':81B ''five'':37B ''forg'':21B ''great'':59B ''high'':49B ''hircin'':29B,57B ''histori'':79B ''hunt'':60B ''imbu'':39B ''instant'':45B ''intend'':92B ''kill'':46B ''known'':85B ''later'':26B ''lord'':51B ''mehrun'':23B ''merci'':4A,9B ''mysteri'':12B ''origin'':19B,20B ''outsid'':90B ''point'':38B ''possess'':77B ''power'':41B ''purpos'':93B ''reachfolk'':33B ''reject'':87B ''remain'':80B ''rule'':71B ''sanctifi'':68B ''sheogorath'':75B ''spear'':1A,6B,35B,53B ''though'':72B ''titl'':34B ''unworthi'':88B ''wield'':65B ''wielder'':89B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
The Spear of Bitter Mercy is a powerful artifact originally forged by Mehrunes Dagon and later associated with Hircine. Imbued with deadly energies, it can only be wielded by those sanctioned to participate in Hircine''s Great Hunt and rejects unworthy wielders.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('banish_daedra', 'Banish Daedra is a Conjuration spell that sends a summoned Daedra back to Oblivion, effectively dispelling it. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':23B ''back'':14B ''banish'':1A,3B ''cast'':27B ''conjur'':7B ''daedra'':2A,4B,13B ''dispel'':18B ''effect'':17B ''level'':25B ''oblivion'':16B ''requir'':21B ''send'':10B ''skill'':24B ''spell'':8B ''summon'':12B', 'mage', '
Banish Daedra is a spell that sends a summoned Daedra back to Oblivion, banishing it from the caster''s presence. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('studded_armor', 'Studded Armor is a basic studded hide chest piece with little protection quality. Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides and iron studs bound together with crude stitching. To craft it: 1 Iron Ingot, 4 leather and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge.  A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''1'':40B ''3'':46B ''4'':43B ''anim'':27B ''armor'':2A,4B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':51B ''bound'':32B ''chest'':10B ''craft'':38B,57B ''crude'':35B ''design'':18B ''forg'':52B ''hide'':9B,28B ''ingot'':42B ''iron'':30B,41B,65B ''leather'':44B,47B ''light'':25B ''littl'':13B ''made'':23B ''novic'':54B ''piec'':11B ''primit'':22B ''protect'':14B ''qualiti'':15B ''rough'':20B ''smith'':55B ''stitch'':36B ''strip'':48B ''stud'':1A,3B,8B,31B ''tan'':26B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''togeth'':33B ''use'':64B ''visual'':17B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Studded Armor is a basic studded hide chest piece with little protection quality. Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides and iron studs bound together with crude stitching. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sacellum_of_boethiah', 'The Sacellum of Boethiah is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince Boethiah, located in the mountains east-southeast of Windhelm and south of Traitor''s Post in Eastmarch. There are rumours of dangerous dark rituals taking place here.', '''boethiah'':3A,7B,16B ''daedric'':14B ''danger'':38B ''dark'':39B ''dedic'':11B ''east'':22B ''east-southeast'':21B ''eastmarch'':33B ''locat'':17B ''mountain'':20B ''place'':42B ''post'':31B ''princ'':15B ''ritual'':40B ''rumour'':36B ''sacellum'':1A,5B ''shrine'':10B ''south'':27B ''southeast'':23B ''take'':41B ''traitor'':29B ''windhelm'':25B', 'eastmarch, daedric, daedra', 'The Sacellum of Boethiah is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince Boethiah, located in the mountains east-southeast of Windhelm in Eastmarch. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fork_of_horripilation', 'The Fork of Horripilation is a cursed artifact of Sheogorath, appearing as a simple iron fork with enchantments that excite magicka and curse its wielder with magicka-draining effects. Fondly called "Forky" by Sheogorath, it is often used by the Mad God to torment mortals by forcing them to wield it as a weapon. The Fork has a strange history, including being "lost" during Sheogorath''s visit to the Dragon Priest Korthor in the Merethic Era and later recovered by the Vestige in various Sheogorath-related trials. Notably, it smells faintly of roast beef, adding to its bizarre nature.', '''ad'':100B ''appear'':14B ''artifact'':11B ''beef'':99B ''bizarr'':103B ''call'':35B ''curs'':10B,26B ''dragon'':74B ''drain'':32B ''effect'':33B ''enchant'':21B ''era'':80B ''excit'':23B ''faint'':96B ''fond'':34B ''forc'':51B ''fork'':1A,5B,19B,60B ''forki'':36B ''god'':46B ''histori'':64B ''horripil'':3A,7B ''includ'':65B ''iron'':18B ''korthor'':76B ''later'':82B ''lost'':67B ''mad'':45B ''magicka'':24B,31B ''magicka-drain'':30B ''mereth'':79B ''mortal'':49B ''natur'':104B ''notabl'':93B ''often'':41B ''priest'':75B ''recov'':83B ''relat'':91B ''roast'':98B ''sheogorath'':13B,38B,69B,90B ''sheogorath-rel'':89B ''simpl'':17B ''smell'':95B ''strang'':63B ''torment'':48B ''trial'':92B ''use'':42B ''various'':88B ''vestig'':86B ''visit'':71B ''weapon'':58B ''wield'':54B ''wielder'':28B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
The Fork of Horripilation is a cursed artifact of Sheogorath, appearing as a simple iron fork that drains magicka and torments its wielder. Known as "Forky," it has a bizarre history and is often used by Sheogorath to torment mortals, smelling faintly of roast beef.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stalhrim_gauntlets', 'Stalhrim Gauntlets have fantastic protection quality. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding. To craft it: 3 stalhrim, 1 quicksilver ingot, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using stalhrim at a workbench.', '''1'':31B ''2'':35B ''3'':29B ''appear'':22B ''blacksmith'':40B ''blue'':19B ''cold'':23B ''craft'':27B,46B ''crystallin'':15B ''design'':11B ''expert'':43B ''fantast'':6B ''forg'':41B ''frosti'':18B ''gauntlet'':2A,4B ''ici'':13B ''ingot'':33B ''leather'':36B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''quicksilv'':32B ''sheen'':20B ''smith'':44B ''stalhrim'':1A,3B,30B,54B ''strip'':37B ''tempered/improved'':51B ''unyield'':25B ''use'':53B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':57B', 'blacksmith', 'Stalhrim Gauntlets have fantastic protection quality. Its visual design is icy and crystalline, with a frosty blue sheen that appears cold and unyielding. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hide_armor', 'Hide Armor is a basic hide chest piece with little protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides bound together with crude stitching. To craft it: 4 leather and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Novice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''3'':39B ''4'':36B ''anim'':26B ''armor'':2A,4B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':44B ''bound'':28B ''chest'':9B ''craft'':34B,50B ''crude'':31B ''design'':17B ''forg'':45B ''hide'':1A,3B,8B,27B ''leather'':37B,40B,58B ''light'':24B ''littl'':12B ''made'':22B ''novic'':47B ''piec'':10B ''primit'':21B ''protect'':13B ''qualiti'':14B ''rough'':19B ''smith'':48B ''stitch'':32B ''strip'':41B ''tan'':25B ''tempered/improved'':55B ''togeth'':29B ''use'':57B ''visual'':16B ''workbench'':61B', 'blacksmith', 'Hide Armor is a basic hide chest piece with little protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides bound together with crude stitching. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hide_bracers', 'Hide Bracers are are a pair of hide bracers with little protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides bound together with crude stitching. To craft it: 1 leather and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge.  A Novice smith can craft it.  It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''1'':37B ''2'':40B ''anim'':27B ''blacksmith'':45B ''bound'':29B ''bracer'':2A,4B,11B ''craft'':35B,51B ''crude'':32B ''design'':18B ''forg'':46B ''hide'':1A,3B,10B,28B ''leather'':38B,41B,59B ''light'':25B ''littl'':13B ''made'':23B ''novic'':48B ''pair'':8B ''primit'':22B ''protect'':14B ''qualiti'':15B ''rough'':20B ''smith'':49B ''stitch'':33B ''strip'':42B ''tan'':26B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''togeth'':30B ''use'':58B ''visual'':17B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Hide Bracers are are a pair of hide bracers with little protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and primitive, made of light, tanned animal hides bound together with crude stitching.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_glibness', 'This potion sharpens wit and charm, granting the drinker an edge in persuasion, negotiation, and intimidation. Grants a slight improvement to Speechcraft, with higher-tier potions greatly enhancing persuasion abilities. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''abil'':34B ''alchemist'':46B ''charm'':9B ''draught'':56B ''drinker'':12B ''edg'':14B ''elixir'':59B ''enhanc'':32B ''found'':39B ''glib'':3A ''grant'':10B,20B ''great'':31B ''higher'':28B ''higher-ti'':27B ''improv'':23B ''intimid'':19B ''loot'':42B ''negoti'':17B ''persuas'':16B,33B ''philter'':57B ''potion'':1A,5B,30B,36B,55B ''purchas'':44B ''random'':41B ''sever'':49B ''sharpen'':6B ''slight'':22B ''speechcraft'':25B ''strongest'':54B ''tier'':29B,50B ''weakest'':52B ''wit'':7B', 'merchant, alchemist, bard, noble, traveler', 'The Potion of Glibness improves persuasion, making speechcraft more effective. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_waterbreathing', 'This potion grants the ability to breathe underwater, a boon for adventurers exploring submerged ruins or evading danger beneath the surface. Allows the user to breathe underwater for a brief duration, with higher-tier potions extending the time significantly. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''abil'':8B ''adventur'':15B ''alchemist'':55B ''allow'':25B ''beneath'':22B ''boon'':13B ''breath'':10B,29B ''brief'':33B ''danger'':21B ''draught'':65B ''durat'':34B ''elixir'':68B ''evad'':20B ''explor'':16B ''extend'':40B ''found'':48B ''grant'':6B ''higher'':37B ''higher-ti'':36B ''loot'':51B ''philter'':66B ''potion'':1A,5B,39B,45B,64B ''purchas'':53B ''random'':50B ''ruin'':18B ''sever'':58B ''signific'':43B ''strongest'':63B ''submerg'':17B ''surfac'':24B ''tier'':38B,59B ''time'':42B ''underwat'':11B,30B ''user'':27B ''waterbreath'':3A ''weakest'':61B', 'alchemist, traveler, hunter, fisherman, sailor', 'The Potion of Waterbreathing allows the user to breathe underwater temporarily. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frostbite_venom', 'Frostbite Venom is a common poison harvested from Frostbite Spiders. It is known to weaken an enemy’s vitality and endurance by delivering a chilling, debilitating effect. The venom is frequently dropped by Frostbite Spiders and their larger kin, Giant Frostbite Spiders.', '''chill'':26B ''common'':7B ''debilit'':27B ''deliv'':24B ''drop'':33B ''effect'':28B ''endur'':22B ''enemy’'':19B ''frequent'':32B ''frostbit'':1A,3B,11B,35B,42B ''giant'':41B ''harvest'':9B ''kin'':40B ''known'':15B ''larger'':39B ''poison'':8B ''spider'':12B,36B,43B ''venom'':2A,4B,30B ''vital'':20B ''weaken'':17B', 'hunter, alchemist, scholar', 'You know that this venom is associated with Frostbite Spiders and may weaken those it infects, but you lack specific details.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('faas_ru_maar', 'Dismay is a Shout that causes fear, making the weak flee in terror before the power of the Thu''um. The three words of power in this Shout are Faas (Fear), which instills dread in the hearts of enemies; Ru (Run), which compels them to flee in panic; and Maar (Terror), which deepens their fear, causing them to flee in absolute terror.', '''absolut'':64B ''caus'':9B,59B ''compel'':46B ''deepen'':56B ''dismay'':4B ''dread'':37B ''enemi'':42B ''faa'':1A,33B ''fear'':10B,34B,58B ''flee'':14B,49B,62B ''heart'':40B ''instil'':36B ''maar'':3A,53B ''make'':11B ''panic'':51B ''power'':19B,28B ''ru'':2A,43B ''run'':44B ''shout'':7B,31B ''terror'':16B,54B,65B ''three'':25B ''thu'':22B ''um'':23B ''weak'':13B ''word'':26B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thalmor_robes', 'Thalmor Robes have basic protection quality. Their visual design is formal and authoritative, featuring black fabric with gold trim and a high collar. They can not be crafted. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using refined moonstone at a workbench.', '''adept'':32B ''authorit'':15B ''basic'':6B ''black'':17B ''collar'':25B ''craft'':30B,35B ''design'':11B ''fabric'':18B ''featur'':16B ''formal'':13B ''gold'':20B ''high'':24B ''it.it'':36B ''moonston'':43B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''refin'':42B ''robe'':2A,4B ''smith'':33B ''tempered/improved'':39B ''thalmor'':1A,3B ''trim'':21B ''use'':41B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':46B', 'blacksmith', 'Thalmor Robes have basic protection quality. Their visual design is formal and authoritative, featuring black fabric with gold trim and a high collar. They can not be crafted. An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using refined moonstone at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_health', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration abilities that increase the caster;s maximum health, improving their resilience and ability to endure greater damage. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted gear. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Fortify Health effect: Bear Claws, Blue Mountain Flower, Giant''s Toe, Glowing Mushroom, Hanging Moss, Wheat', '''abil'':11B,23B ''also'':45B ''appli'':47B ''avail'':31B ''bear'':74B ''blue'':76B ''brew'':39B ''caster'':15B ''claw'':75B ''combin'':52B ''craft'':35B ''creat'':66B ''custom'':41B ''damag'':27B ''effect'':5B,29B,64B,73B ''enchant'':49B ''endur'':25B ''flower'':78B ''focus'':9B ''follow'':58B ''fortifi'':1A,71B ''gear'':50B ''general'':51B ''giant'':79B ''glow'':82B ''greater'':26B ''hang'':84B ''health'':2A,18B,72B ''improv'':19B ''increas'':13B ''ingredi'':59B ''least'':54B ''magic'':4B ''maximum'':17B ''moss'':85B ''mountain'':77B ''mushroom'':83B ''potion'':36B,42B,68B ''pre'':34B ''pre-craft'':33B ''provid'':60B ''resili'':21B ''restor'':10B ''share'':62B ''toe'':81B ''two'':55B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B ''wheat'':86B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic increases your health, making it easier to survive in battles. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('goldfish', 'Goldfish are a orange and gold coloured fish found in temperate lakes. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Restore Stamina, Fortify Heavy Armor, Waterbreathing and Resist Frost.', '''armor'':31B ''colour'':8B ''effect'':24B ''fish'':9B ''fortifi'':29B ''found'':10B ''frost'':35B ''gold'':7B ''goldfish'':1A,2B ''heavi'':30B ''ingredi'':18B ''lake'':13B ''make'':21B ''offer'':23B ''orang'':5B ''potion'':20B ''resist'':34B ''restor'':27B ''stamina'':28B ''temper'':12B ''use'':15B ''waterbreath'':32B', 'fisher', 'Goldfish are a orange and gold coloured fish. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hysteria', 'Hysteria is an Illusion spell that causes enemies within its area of effect to become terrified and flee in panic. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''area'':12B ''becom'':16B ''cast'':29B ''caus'':8B ''effect'':14B ''enemi'':9B ''expert'':25B ''flee'':19B ''hysteria'':1A,2B ''illus'':5B ''level'':27B ''panic'':21B ''requir'':23B ''skill'':26B ''spell'':6B ''terrifi'':17B ''within'':10B', 'mage', '
Hysteria is a spell that causes enemies within its area of effect to become terrified and flee in panic. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('summon_unbound_dremora', 'Summon Unbound Dremora is a Conjuration spell that summons an unbound Dremora, which may not be under the caster''s control and can act independently. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''act'':27B ''adept'':32B ''cast'':36B ''caster'':22B ''conjur'':9B ''control'':24B ''dremora'':3A,6B,15B ''independ'':28B ''level'':34B ''may'':17B ''requir'':30B ''skill'':33B ''spell'':10B ''summon'':1A,4B,12B ''unbound'':2A,5B,14B', 'mage', 'Summon Unbound Dremora is a spell that summons an unbound Dremora, which may not be under the caster''s control and could act independently. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bloodgrass', 'Bloodgrass is an ingredient harvested from the Deadlands. Alchemy effects: Invisibility, Resist Poison, Slow, and Fortify Health.', '''alchemi'':10B ''bloodgrass'':1A,2B ''deadland'':9B ''effect'':11B ''fortifi'':17B ''harvest'':6B ''health'':18B ''ingredi'':5B ''invis'':12B ''poison'':14B ''resist'':13B ''slow'':15B', 'alchemist', 'Bloodgrass is an ingredient harvested from the Deadlands. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('whirlwind_sprint', 'Whirlwind Sprint is a Shout that propels you forward with the speed of a tempest, allowing you to rush ahead in the blink of an eye. The three words of power in this Shout are Wuld (Whirlwind), which summons the rushing wind; Nah (Fury), which intensifies the speed and force of the wind; and Kest (Tempest), which carries you swiftly forward, like a powerful storm.', '''ahead'':22B ''allow'':18B ''blink'':25B ''carri'':60B ''eye'':28B ''forc'':52B ''forward'':11B,63B ''furi'':46B ''intensifi'':48B ''kest'':57B ''like'':64B ''nah'':45B ''power'':33B,66B ''propel'':9B ''rush'':21B,43B ''shout'':7B,36B ''speed'':14B,50B ''sprint'':2A,4B ''storm'':67B ''summon'':41B ''swift'':62B ''tempest'':17B,58B ''three'':30B ''whirlwind'':1A,3B,39B ''wind'':44B,55B ''word'':31B ''wuld'':38B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('father_of_the_niben', 'Father of the Niben, written by Florin Jaliil, is a translation of the fragmented journal of Topal the Pilot, an Aldmeri explorer from the Merethic Era. The account chronicles Topal’s journey, during which he sails across Tamriel with a crew, tasked with finding a way back to Old Ehlnofey and discovering new lands. Throughout his voyages, Topal encounters many wonders, including strange islands, dangerous creatures, and various tribes. However, his journey is marred by miscalculations, mistaken turns, and a failure to reach his intended destination, Firsthold. The account is fragmented, leaving readers with more questions than answers, particularly regarding Topal’s encounters with ancient Khajiit, Orcs, and other civilizations, which would later become extinct or forgotten.

The themes of the story revolve around exploration, failure, and the uncertainty of discovery. Topal’s journey is one of ambition and perseverance, yet ultimately, he fails to achieve his initial goals, though he leaves behind maps that contribute significantly to later understanding of Tamriel’s geography. His encounters with different cultures highlight the diversity of Tamriel, while his miscalculations serve as a reminder of the unpredictable nature of exploration. This text, based on only four surviving fragments, offers a rare glimpse into a world long gone, revealing the tragic beauty of lost knowledge and unfulfilled quests.', '''account'':32B,92B ''achiev'':147B ''across'':40B ''aldmeri'':25B ''ambit'':139B ''ancient'':107B ''answer'':101B ''around'':126B ''back'':50B ''base'':190B ''beauti'':208B ''becom'':116B ''behind'':154B ''chronicl'':33B ''civil'':112B ''contribut'':157B ''creatur'':69B ''crew'':44B ''cultur'':169B ''danger'':68B ''destin'':89B ''differ'':168B ''discov'':55B ''discoveri'':133B ''divers'':172B ''ehlnofey'':53B ''encount'':62B,105B,166B ''era'':30B ''explor'':26B,127B,187B ''extinct'':117B ''fail'':145B ''failur'':84B,128B ''father'':1A,5B ''find'':47B ''firsthold'':90B ''florin'':11B ''forgotten'':119B ''four'':193B ''fragment'':18B,94B,195B ''geographi'':164B ''glimps'':199B ''goal'':150B ''gone'':204B ''highlight'':170B ''howev'':73B ''includ'':65B ''initi'':149B ''intend'':88B ''island'':67B ''jaliil'':12B ''journal'':19B ''journey'':35B,75B,135B ''khajiit'':108B ''knowledg'':211B ''land'':57B ''later'':115B,160B ''leav'':95B,153B ''long'':203B ''lost'':210B ''mani'':63B ''map'':155B ''mar'':77B ''mereth'':29B ''miscalcul'':79B,177B ''mistaken'':80B ''natur'':185B ''new'':56B ''niben'':4A,8B ''offer'':196B ''old'':52B ''one'':137B ''orc'':109B ''particular'':102B ''persever'':141B ''pilot'':23B ''quest'':214B ''question'':99B ''rare'':198B ''reach'':86B ''reader'':96B ''regard'':103B ''remind'':181B ''reveal'':205B ''revolv'':125B ''sail'':39B ''serv'':178B ''signific'':158B ''stori'':124B ''strang'':66B ''surviv'':194B ''tamriel'':41B,174B ''tamriel’'':163B ''task'':45B ''text'':189B ''theme'':121B ''though'':151B ''throughout'':58B ''topal'':21B,61B ''topal’'':34B,104B,134B ''tragic'':207B ''translat'':15B ''tribe'':72B ''turn'':81B ''ultim'':143B ''uncertainti'':131B ''understand'':161B ''unfulfil'':213B ''unpredict'':184B ''various'':71B ''voyag'':60B ''way'':49B ''wonder'':64B ''world'':202B ''would'':114B ''written'':9B ''yet'':142B', 'scholar', '
Father of the Niben, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, is a translation of the fragmented journal of Topal the Pilot, chronicling his failed exploration of Tamriel and his encounters with ancient civilizations. The book explores themes of exploration, failure, and the uncertainty of discovery, highlighting the ambition and perseverance of explorers amidst the unpredictability of their journeys.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('flame_atronach', 'Flame Atronachs are elemental Daedra originating from the realm of Infernace, a fiery domain composed of lava and flames. These beings appear to be made entirely of fire and can be found either unbound in the wild or summoned by skilled mages to serve various roles, such as guards or laborers. The process of summoning Flame Atronachs typically involves the spell known as Koron''s Peremptory Summons, which allows conjurers to customize the specifics of the summon, including the Daedric form and the plane from which they are called.', '''allow'':71B ''appear'':24B ''atronach'':2A,4B,59B ''be'':23B ''call'':91B ''compos'':17B ''conjur'':72B ''custom'':74B ''daedra'':7B ''daedric'':82B ''domain'':16B ''either'':35B ''element'':6B ''entir'':28B ''fieri'':15B ''fire'':30B ''flame'':1A,3B,21B,58B ''form'':83B ''found'':34B ''guard'':51B ''includ'':80B ''infernac'':13B ''involv'':61B ''known'':64B ''koron'':66B ''labor'':53B ''lava'':19B ''made'':27B ''mage'':44B ''origin'':8B ''peremptori'':68B ''plane'':86B ''process'':55B ''realm'':11B ''role'':48B ''serv'':46B ''skill'':43B ''specif'':76B ''spell'':63B ''summon'':41B,57B,69B,79B ''typic'':60B ''unbound'':36B ''various'':47B ''wild'':39B', 'mage, daedra, daedric, scholar', 'Flame Atronachs are elemental Daedra. These beings appear to be made entirely of fire and can be found either unbound in the wild.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('black_briar', 'The Black-Briars are a powerful and influential family faction based in Riften, Skyrim, with far-reaching control over the city''s affairs and beyond. Led by the ruthless Maven Black-Briar, the family dominates local politics, industry, and the criminal underworld. Maven, the matriarch, is known for her cunning and willingness to use whatever means necessary to expand her wealth and influence, including leveraging the Thieves Guild, the Dark Brotherhood, and even the Thalmor. Through manipulation and bribery, she keeps Riften''s guards and Jarl Laila Law-Giver in her pocket, ensuring the family’s dominance in the region. The family’s primary business, Black-Briar Meadery, is a significant source of their power, with aspirations of expanding its reach across Tamriel.

The Black-Briar family consists of four main members, each with their own ambitions and flaws. Hemming Black-Briar, Maven''s loyal son, is pompous and ambitious, aiming to spread the family''s meadery empire far and wide. Sibbi Black-Briar, the disgraced son, tarnishes the family name with his crimes, including murder and adultery, and currently resides in a luxurious prison cell in Mistveil Watch. Ingun Black-Briar, the eccentric daughter, distances herself from the family’s scheming, focusing instead on her passion for alchemy, fascinated by the delicate balance between life and death. Together, the Black-Briars represent a dark yet formidable force within Skyrim, their alliances and cunning ensuring their influence extends well beyond the walls of Riften.', '''across'':127B ''adulteri'':186B ''affair'':27B ''aim'':158B ''alchemi'':217B ''allianc'':241B ''ambit'':143B ''ambiti'':157B ''aspir'':122B ''balanc'':222B ''base'':14B ''beyond'':29B,249B ''black'':1A,5B,36B,111B,131B,148B,171B,200B,230B ''black-briar'':4B,35B,110B,130B,147B,170B,199B,229B ''briar'':2A,6B,37B,112B,132B,149B,172B,201B,231B ''briberi'':84B ''brotherhood'':76B ''busi'':109B ''cell'':194B ''citi'':25B ''consist'':134B ''control'':22B ''crime'':182B ''crimin'':46B ''cun'':55B,243B ''current'':188B ''dark'':75B,234B ''daughter'':204B ''death'':226B ''delic'':221B ''disgrac'':174B ''distanc'':205B ''domin'':40B,102B ''eccentr'':203B ''empir'':165B ''ensur'':99B,244B ''even'':78B ''expand'':64B,124B ''extend'':247B ''faction'':13B ''famili'':12B,39B,133B,162B,178B ''family’'':101B,107B,209B ''far'':20B,166B ''far-reach'':19B ''fascin'':218B ''flaw'':145B ''focus'':211B ''forc'':237B ''formid'':236B ''four'':136B ''giver'':95B ''guard'':89B ''guild'':73B ''hem'':146B ''includ'':69B,183B ''industri'':43B ''influenc'':68B,246B ''influenti'':11B ''ingun'':198B ''instead'':212B ''jarl'':91B ''keep'':86B ''known'':52B ''laila'':92B ''law'':94B ''law-giv'':93B ''led'':30B ''leverag'':70B ''life'':224B ''local'':41B ''loyal'':152B ''luxuri'':192B ''main'':137B ''manipul'':82B ''matriarch'':50B ''maven'':34B,48B,150B ''meaderi'':113B,164B ''mean'':61B ''member'':138B ''mistveil'':196B ''murder'':184B ''name'':179B ''necessari'':62B ''passion'':215B ''pocket'':98B ''polit'':42B ''pompous'':155B ''power'':9B,120B ''primari'':108B ''prison'':193B ''reach'':21B,126B ''region'':105B ''repres'':232B ''resid'':189B ''riften'':16B,87B,253B ''ruthless'':33B ''scheme'':210B ''sibbi'':169B ''signific'':116B ''skyrim'':17B,239B ''son'':153B,175B ''sourc'':117B ''spread'':160B ''tamriel'':128B ''tarnish'':176B ''thalmor'':80B ''thiev'':72B ''togeth'':227B ''underworld'':47B ''use'':59B ''wall'':251B ''watch'':197B ''wealth'':66B ''well'':248B ''whatev'':60B ''wide'':168B ''willing'':57B ''within'':238B ''yet'':235B', 'rift, innkeeper, noble', 'The Black-Briars are a powerful family in Riften, Skyrim, led by the ruthless Maven Black-Briar, who controls local politics, industry, and the criminal underworld. Through manipulation, bribery, and alliances with groups like the Thieves Guild and the Dark Brotherhood, Maven ensures the family''s dominance, particularly through their profitable business, Black-Briar Meadery. The family includes Maven''s loyal son Hemming, the disgraced Sibbi, and the eccentric Ingun, who focuses on alchemy rather than the family''s schemes. The Black-Briars are a formidable force in Skyrim, with their influence extending far beyond Riften.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('drelas_cottage', 'Drelas'' Cottage is an isolated dwelling nestled at the foot of a mountain in northern Whiterun Hold, south of Morthal and northwest of Dustman’s Cairn. Surrounded by rugged terrain and far from any settlements, the cottage exudes an air of quiet seclusion.

The cottage is home to Drelas, a reclusive and formidable elemental mage who fiercely guards his solitude, attacking any who dare to intrude.', '''air'':41B ''attack'':62B ''cairn'':27B ''cottag'':2A,4B,38B,46B ''dare'':65B ''drela'':1A,3B,50B ''dustman’'':26B ''dwell'':8B ''element'':55B ''exud'':39B ''far'':33B ''fierc'':58B ''foot'':12B ''formid'':54B ''guard'':59B ''hold'':19B ''home'':48B ''intrud'':67B ''isol'':7B ''mage'':56B ''morthal'':22B ''mountain'':15B ''nestl'':9B ''northern'':17B ''northwest'':24B ''quiet'':43B ''reclus'':52B ''rug'':30B ''seclus'':44B ''settlement'':36B ''solitud'':61B ''south'':20B ''surround'':28B ''terrain'':31B ''whiterun'':18B', 'whiterun', 'Drelas'' Cottage is an isolated dwelling nestled at the foot of a mountain in northern Whiterun Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stallions_potion', 'The Stallion''s Potion is a unique potion that boosts stamina for an extended period and is often associated with physical endurance.', '''associ'':21B ''boost'':12B ''endur'':24B ''extend'':16B ''often'':20B ''period'':17B ''physic'':23B ''potion'':2A,6B,10B ''stallion'':1A,4B ''stamina'':13B ''uniqu'':9B', 'bothela', 'You assume it must be endurance-enhancing by the name but know nothing else about its origins. You have heard it most often in association with Markarth.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skyforge', 'Skyforge is an ancient and mystical forge located atop a rocky outcrop in Whiterun, near the Companions'' hall, Jorrvaskr. Renowned for its unparalleled craftsmanship, it is tended by Eorlund Gray-Mane, widely regarded as the finest blacksmith in Skyrim. The forge’s searing heat is used to craft powerful weapons and armor, as well as to light the funeral pyres of fallen Companions, intertwining its purpose with the traditions and legacy of the order.

Legend holds that the Skyforge predates human settlement in the area. The ancient elves believed it to be a relic of the gods, an artifact so sacred that they avoided it entirely. When Ysgramor and his Five Hundred Companions arrived, they claimed the forge as their own, building Jorrvaskr nearby to honor its power. This act marked the beginning of human settlement in the region, eventually giving rise to the city of Whiterun.', '''act'':131B ''ancient'':5B,88B ''area'':86B ''armor'':53B ''arriv'':115B ''artifact'':100B ''atop'':10B ''avoid'':105B ''begin'':134B ''believ'':90B ''blacksmith'':39B ''build'':123B ''citi'':146B ''claim'':117B ''companion'':18B,64B,114B ''craft'':49B ''craftsmanship'':25B ''elv'':89B ''entir'':107B ''eorlund'':30B ''eventu'':141B ''fallen'':63B ''finest'':38B ''five'':112B ''forg'':8B,119B ''forge’'':43B ''funer'':60B ''give'':142B ''god'':98B ''gray'':32B ''gray-man'':31B ''hall'':19B ''heat'':45B ''hold'':77B ''honor'':127B ''human'':82B,136B ''hundr'':113B ''intertwin'':65B ''jorrvaskr'':20B,124B ''legaci'':72B ''legend'':76B ''light'':58B ''locat'':9B ''mane'':33B ''mark'':132B ''mystic'':7B ''near'':16B ''nearbi'':125B ''order'':75B ''outcrop'':13B ''power'':50B,129B ''predat'':81B ''purpos'':67B ''pyre'':61B ''regard'':35B ''region'':140B ''relic'':95B ''renown'':21B ''rise'':143B ''rocki'':12B ''sacr'':102B ''sear'':44B ''settlement'':83B,137B ''skyforg'':1A,2B,80B ''skyrim'':41B ''tend'':28B ''tradit'':70B ''unparallel'':24B ''use'':47B ''weapon'':51B ''well'':55B ''whiterun'':15B,148B ''wide'':34B ''ysgramor'':109B', 'whiterun, companions', 'Skyforge is an ancient and mystical forge located atop a rocky outcrop in Whiterun, near the Companions'' hall, Jorrvaskr. Renowned for its unparalleled craftsmanship, it is tended by Eorlund Gray-Mane, widely regarded as the finest blacksmith in Skyrim. The forge’s searing heat is used to craft powerful weapons and armor, as well as to light the funeral pyres of fallen Companions, intertwining its purpose with the traditions and legacy of the order.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('twilight_sepulcher', 'The Twilight Sepulcher is a sacred Nordic ruin located west of Falkreath and south of Knifepoint Ridge in Falkreath Hold. It is the final resting place of Nocturnal''s Ebonmere portal and the Skeleton Key, accessible through the Pilgrim''s Path.', '''access'':38B ''ebonmer'':32B ''falkreath'':14B,21B ''final'':26B ''hold'':22B ''key'':37B ''knifepoint'':18B ''locat'':11B ''nocturn'':30B ''nordic'':9B ''path'':43B ''pilgrim'':41B ''place'':28B ''portal'':33B ''rest'':27B ''ridg'':19B ''ruin'':10B ''sacr'':8B ''sepulch'':2A,5B ''skeleton'':36B ''south'':16B ''twilight'':1A,4B ''west'':12B', 'katriah', 'The Twilight Sepulcher is a sacred Nordic ruin rumored located somewhere in southern Skyrim.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cowflop_farm', 'Cowflop Farm is located just outside Whiterun, a short walk from the city, situated between Whiterun and Rorikstead. The farm is run by a somewhat quirky and down-to-earth Nord named Sigrid, who, with her husband, makes a modest living off the land. As with many Skyrim farmers, their lives are filled with simple, daily chores and the occasional struggle with local wildlife, like wolves or sabre cats, which can disrupt the farm’s routine.', '''cat'':72B ''chore'':60B ''citi'':15B ''cowflop'':1A,3B ''daili'':59B ''disrupt'':75B ''down-to-earth'':30B ''earth'':33B ''farm'':2A,4B,22B ''farmer'':52B ''farm’'':77B ''fill'':56B ''husband'':40B ''land'':47B ''like'':68B ''live'':44B,54B ''local'':66B ''locat'':6B ''make'':41B ''mani'':50B ''modest'':43B ''name'':35B ''nord'':34B ''occasion'':63B ''outsid'':8B ''quirki'':28B ''rorikstead'':20B ''routin'':78B ''run'':24B ''sabr'':71B ''short'':11B ''sigrid'':36B ''simpl'':58B ''situat'':16B ''skyrim'':51B ''somewhat'':27B ''struggl'':64B ''walk'':12B ''whiterun'':9B,18B ''wildlif'':67B ''wolv'':69B', 'whiterun', 'Cowflop Farm is located just outside Whiterun. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', '');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stalhrim_source', 'The Stalhrim Source is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located east of Broken Tusk Mine and southwest of Mortrag Peak on Solstheim. This site is of particular importance due to its abundance of stalhrim, a rare and ancient material used by the Nords to craft powerful weapons and armor.', '''abund'':34B ''ancient'':40B ''armor'':51B ''broken'':15B ''craft'':47B ''due'':31B ''east'':13B ''import'':30B ''locat'':12B ''materi'':41B ''mine'':17B ''mortrag'':21B ''nord'':45B ''nordic'':10B ''outdoor'':9B ''particular'':29B ''peak'':22B ''power'':48B ''rare'':38B ''ruin'':11B ''site'':26B ''small'':8B ''solstheim'':24B ''sourc'':2A,5B ''southwest'':19B ''stalhrim'':1A,4B,36B ''tusk'':16B ''use'':42B ''weapon'':49B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ruins_of_bthalft', 'The Ruins of Bthalft are a small Dwarven ruin located south of Ivarstead in the Rift. It is known to be occupied by bandits, who seem to be searching for something here.', '''bandit'':27B ''bthalft'':3A,7B ''dwarven'':11B ''ivarstead'':16B ''known'':22B ''locat'':13B ''occupi'':25B ''rift'':19B ''ruin'':1A,5B,12B ''search'':32B ''seem'':29B ''small'':10B ''someth'':34B ''south'':14B', 'rift, dwemer', 'The Ruins of Bthalft are a small Dwarven ruin located south of Ivarstead in the Rift.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hunter''s_rest', 'Hunter''s Rest is a small shack located in the hills west of Half-Moon Mill, roughly midway between Falkreath and Rorikstead in Falkreath Hold. The shelter is near Moss Mother Cavern and serves as a home for hunters who poach game in the surrounding wilderness.', '''cavern'':36B ''falkreath'':24B,28B ''game'':46B ''half'':18B ''half-moon'':17B ''hill'':14B ''hold'':29B ''home'':41B ''hunter'':1A,4B,43B ''locat'':11B ''midway'':22B ''mill'':20B ''moon'':19B ''moss'':34B ''mother'':35B ''near'':33B ''poach'':45B ''rest'':3A,6B ''rorikstead'':26B ''rough'':21B ''serv'':38B ''shack'':10B ''shelter'':31B ''small'':9B ''surround'':49B ''west'':15B ''wilder'':50B', 'falkreath', 'Hunter''s Rest is a small shack located roughly midway between Falkreath and Rorikstead in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('atheron_residence', 'The Atheron Residence is the home of the Atheron family, located in the lower Gray Quarter of Windhelm, directly across the street from the New Gnisis Cornerclub. The residence is modest and consists of a single area.

The house is inhabited by Aval Atheron, a street vendor; Faryl Atheron, who works as a farm laborer; and their sister, Suvaris Atheron.', '''across'':22B ''area'':39B ''atheron'':1A,4B,11B,46B,51B,62B ''aval'':45B ''consist'':35B ''cornerclub'':29B ''direct'':21B ''famili'':12B ''farm'':56B ''faryl'':50B ''gnisi'':28B ''gray'':17B ''home'':8B ''hous'':41B ''inhabit'':43B ''labor'':57B ''locat'':13B ''lower'':16B ''modest'':33B ''new'':27B ''quarter'':18B ''resid'':2A,5B,31B ''singl'':38B ''sister'':60B ''street'':24B,48B ''suvari'':61B ''vendor'':49B ''windhelm'':20B ''work'':53B', 'eastmarch', 'The Atheron Residence is the home of the Atheron family, located in the lower Gray Quarter of Windhelm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brunwulf_free-winter''s_house', 'Brunwulf Free-Winter''s House is a one-story home with a partial loft, located in Windhelm near the main entrance. Positioned next to the Aretino Residence and almost directly across from Calixto''s House of Curiosities, it is easily recognizable.

The house belongs to Brunwulf Free-Winter, a Nord known for his progressive views and advocacy for equality among Windhelm''s diverse inhabitants.', '''across'':39B ''advocaci'':66B ''almost'':37B ''among'':69B ''aretino'':34B ''belong'':52B ''brunwulf'':1A,7B,54B ''calixto'':41B ''curios'':45B ''direct'':38B ''divers'':72B ''easili'':48B ''entranc'':29B ''equal'':68B ''free'':3A,9B,56B ''free-wint'':2A,8B,55B ''home'':18B ''hous'':6A,12B,43B,51B ''inhabit'':73B ''known'':60B ''locat'':23B ''loft'':22B ''main'':28B ''near'':26B ''next'':31B ''nord'':59B ''one'':16B ''one-stori'':15B ''partial'':21B ''posit'':30B ''progress'':63B ''recogniz'':49B ''resid'':35B ''stori'':17B ''view'':64B ''windhelm'':25B,70B ''winter'':4A,10B,57B', 'eastmarch', 'Brunwulf Free-Winter''s House is a one-story home with a partial loft, located in Windhelm near the main entrance.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falkreath_hold', 'Falkreath Hold is a location in southern Skyrim, bordered by Cyrodiil to the south across the Jerall Mountains and Hammerfell to the west. It is the second southernmost hold in Skyrim, after the Rift. Its capital, Falkreath, lies nestled amidst dense pine forests, while the hold’s only other notable town, Helgen, is infamous as the site of the first dragon attack in Skyrim.

The hold is renowned for its mist-shrouded landscapes, giving it a timeless and seasonless quality. Towering snow-capped mountains contrast sharply with the verdant forests below, and Lake Ilinalta dominates the central region, serving as the source of the White River. Falkreath also holds Skyrim’s largest cemetery, a reflection of its bloody history of battles, and this heritage influences the names of many local shops and farms.

The region’s flora includes abundant thistles, mora tapinella, and mountain flowers, while nightshade grows more commonly here than in other parts of Skyrim. Lake Ilinalta teems with fish, and snowberry bushes thrive in the snowy eastern areas. Under Jarl Siddgeir’s rule, Falkreath retains its Imperial allegiance, though its control can shift during Skyrim’s civil conflict.', '''abund'':140B ''across'':17B ''allegi'':181B ''also'':111B ''amidst'':42B ''area'':172B ''attack'':63B ''battl'':123B ''bloodi'':120B ''border'':11B ''bush'':166B ''cap'':86B ''capit'':38B ''cemeteri'':115B ''central'':100B ''civil'':189B ''common'':151B ''conflict'':190B ''contrast'':88B ''control'':184B ''cyrodiil'':13B ''dens'':43B ''domin'':98B ''dragon'':62B ''eastern'':171B ''falkreath'':1A,3B,39B,110B,177B ''farm'':135B ''first'':61B ''fish'':163B ''flora'':138B ''flower'':146B ''forest'':45B,93B ''give'':76B ''grow'':149B ''hammerfel'':22B ''helgen'':53B ''heritag'':126B ''histori'':121B ''hold'':2A,4B,31B,67B,112B ''hold’'':48B ''ilinalta'':97B,160B ''imperi'':180B ''includ'':139B ''infam'':55B ''influenc'':127B ''jarl'':174B ''jeral'':19B ''lake'':96B,159B ''landscap'':75B ''largest'':114B ''lie'':40B ''local'':132B ''locat'':7B ''mani'':131B ''mist'':73B ''mist-shroud'':72B ''mora'':142B ''mountain'':20B,87B,145B ''name'':129B ''nestl'':41B ''nightshad'':148B ''notabl'':51B ''part'':156B ''pine'':44B ''qualiti'':82B ''reflect'':117B ''region'':101B ''region’'':137B ''renown'':69B ''retain'':178B ''rift'':36B ''river'':109B ''rule'':176B ''seasonless'':81B ''second'':29B ''serv'':102B ''sharpli'':89B ''shift'':186B ''shop'':133B ''shroud'':74B ''siddgeir’'':175B ''site'':58B ''skyrim'':10B,33B,65B,158B ''skyrim’'':113B,188B ''snow'':85B ''snow-cap'':84B ''snowberri'':165B ''snowi'':170B ''sourc'':105B ''south'':16B ''southern'':9B ''southernmost'':30B ''tapinella'':143B ''teem'':161B ''thistl'':141B ''though'':182B ''thrive'':167B ''timeless'':79B ''tower'':83B ''town'':52B ''verdant'':92B ''west'':25B ''white'':108B', 'falkreath, noble, scholar', 'Falkreath Hold is a location in southern Skyrim, bordered by Cyrodiil to the south across the Jerall Mountains and Hammerfell to the west. It is the second southernmost hold in Skyrim, after the Rift. Its capital, Falkreath, lies nestled amidst dense pine forests, while the hold’s only other notable town, Helgen, is infamous as the site of the first dragon attack in Skyrim.

The hold is renowned for its mist-shrouded landscapes, giving it a timeless and seasonless quality. Towering snow-capped mountains contrast sharply with the verdant forests below, and Lake Ilinalta dominates the central region, serving as the source of the White River. Falkreath also holds Skyrim’s largest cemetery, a reflection of its bloody history of battles, and this heritage influences the names of many local shops and farms.', '', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('clan_shatter-shield_office', 'The Clan Shatter-Shield Office is a small but important establishment located on Windhelm''s docks, nestled between the Argonian Assemblage and the East Empire Company regional office. It serves as the base of operations for Clan Shatter-Shield''s shipping endeavors, overseeing the family''s commercial ventures.

This office plays a key role in managing the family''s business interests, particularly in trade and shipping, which are vital to Windhelm''s economy. ', '''argonian'':26B ''assemblag'':27B ''base'':39B ''busi'':67B ''clan'':1A,7B,43B ''commerci'':54B ''compani'':32B ''dock'':22B ''east'':30B ''economi'':80B ''empir'':31B ''endeavor'':49B ''establish'':17B ''famili'':52B,65B ''import'':16B ''interest'':68B ''key'':60B ''locat'':18B ''manag'':63B ''nestl'':23B ''offic'':5A,11B,34B,57B ''oper'':41B ''overse'':50B ''particular'':69B ''play'':58B ''region'':33B ''role'':61B ''serv'':36B ''shatter'':3A,9B,45B ''shatter-shield'':2A,8B,44B ''shield'':4A,10B,46B ''ship'':48B,73B ''small'':14B ''trade'':71B ''ventur'':55B ''vital'':76B ''windhelm'':20B,78B', 'eastmarch, noble', 'The Clan Shatter-Shield Office is a small but important establishment located on Windhelm''s docks, nestled between the Argonian Assemblage and the East Empire Company regional office.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pearl', 'Pearls, including small pearls, are found in clams and pearl oysters, prized for their use in various alchemical mixtures. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Fortify Block, Restore Magicka, and Resist Shock.', '''alchem'':19B ''alchemi'':21B ''block'':26B ''clam'':9B ''effect'':22B ''fortifi'':25B ''found'':7B ''includ'':3B ''magicka'':28B ''mixtur'':20B ''oyster'':12B ''pearl'':1A,2B,5B,11B ''prize'':13B ''resist'':30B ''restor'':23B,27B ''shock'':31B ''small'':4B ''stamina'':24B ''use'':16B ''various'':18B', 'alchemist', 'Pearls, including small pearls, are found in clams and pearl oysters, prized for their use in various alchemical mixtures. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falkreath', 'Falkreath is a city in the south of Skyrim and serves as the capital of Falkreath Hold. Situated near the borders of Cyrodiil and Hammerfell, it was historically considered part of Cyrodiil but is now firmly within Skyrim''s boundaries. Governed by Jarl Siddgeir, Falkreath is initially aligned with the Empire, though its allegiance may shift during Skyrim''s civil war.

The city''s economy thrives on lumber harvested from its expansive surrounding forests. Falkreath''s most notable feature is its vast cemetery, the largest in Skyrim, which holds generations of the dead. This burial ground is a cultural cornerstone for its residents, influencing the names of many local businesses and homes. The cemetery symbolizes Falkreath''s deep connection to its history and the legacy of its fallen.

Falkreath Hold is a location in southern Skyrim, bordered by Cyrodiil to the south across the Jerall Mountains and Hammerfell to the west. It is the second southernmost hold in Skyrim, after the Rift. Its capital, Falkreath, lies nestled amidst dense pine forests, while the hold’s only other notable town, Helgen, is infamous as the site of the first dragon attack in Skyrim.', '''across'':144B ''align'':49B ''allegi'':55B ''amidst'':169B ''attack'':190B ''border'':22B,138B ''boundari'':41B ''burial'':96B ''busi'':111B ''capit'':15B,165B ''cemeteri'':84B,115B ''citi'':5B,64B ''civil'':61B ''connect'':120B ''consid'':30B ''cornerston'':101B ''cultur'':100B ''cyrodiil'':24B,33B,140B ''dead'':94B ''deep'':119B ''dens'':170B ''dragon'':189B ''economi'':66B ''empir'':52B ''expans'':73B ''falkreath'':1A,2B,17B,46B,76B,117B,130B,166B ''fallen'':129B ''featur'':80B ''firm'':37B ''first'':188B ''forest'':75B,172B ''generat'':91B ''govern'':42B ''ground'':97B ''hammerfel'':26B,149B ''harvest'':70B ''helgen'':180B ''histor'':29B ''histori'':123B ''hold'':18B,90B,131B,158B ''hold’'':175B ''home'':113B ''infam'':182B ''influenc'':105B ''initi'':48B ''jarl'':44B ''jeral'':146B ''largest'':86B ''legaci'':126B ''lie'':167B ''local'':110B ''locat'':134B ''lumber'':69B ''mani'':109B ''may'':56B ''mountain'':147B ''name'':107B ''near'':20B ''nestl'':168B ''notabl'':79B,178B ''part'':31B ''pine'':171B ''resid'':104B ''rift'':163B ''second'':156B ''serv'':12B ''shift'':57B ''siddgeir'':45B ''site'':185B ''situat'':19B ''skyrim'':10B,39B,59B,88B,137B,160B,192B ''south'':8B,143B ''southern'':136B ''southernmost'':157B ''surround'':74B ''symbol'':116B ''though'':53B ''thrive'':67B ''town'':179B ''vast'':83B ''war'':62B ''west'':152B ''within'':38B', 'falkreath, noble, scholar', 'Falkreath is a city in the south of Skyrim and serves as the capital of Falkreath Hold. Situated near the borders of Cyrodiil and Hammerfell, it was historically considered part of Cyrodiil but is now firmly within Skyrim''s boundaries. Governed by Jarl Siddgeir, Falkreath is initially aligned with the Empire, though its allegiance may shift during Skyrim''s civil war.

The city''s economy thrives on lumber harvested from its expansive surrounding forests. Falkreath''s most notable feature is its vast cemetery, the largest in Skyrim, which holds generations of the dead. This burial ground is a cultural cornerstone for its residents, influencing the names of many local businesses and homes. The cemetery symbolizes Falkreath''s deep connection to its history and the legacy of its fallen.

Falkreath Hold is a location in southern Skyrim, bordered by Cyrodiil to the south across the Jerall Mountains and Hammerfell to the west. It is the second southernmost hold in Skyrim, after the Rift. Its capital, Falkreath, lies nestled amidst dense pine forests, while the hold’s only other notable town, Helgen, is infamous as the site of the first dragon attack in Skyrim.', '', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('grave_concoctions', 'Grave Concoctions is an alchemy shop located in Falkreath, between Lod''s House and Falkreath Barracks, opposite the Jarl''s Longhouse. The store is run by Zaria, a Redguard immigrant with a passion for crafting poisons and other alchemical goods.

The shop''s name pays homage to Falkreath''s large cemetery, a tradition shared by many local businesses such as Corpselight Farm and Dead Man''s Drink.', '''alchem'':41B ''alchemi'':7B ''barrack'':18B ''busi'':60B ''cemeteri'':53B ''concoct'':2A,4B ''corpselight'':63B ''craft'':37B ''dead'':66B ''drink'':69B ''falkreath'':11B,17B,50B ''farm'':64B ''good'':42B ''grave'':1A,3B ''homag'':48B ''hous'':15B ''immigr'':32B ''jarl'':21B ''larg'':52B ''local'':59B ''locat'':9B ''lod'':13B ''longhous'':23B ''man'':67B ''mani'':58B ''name'':46B ''opposit'':19B ''passion'':35B ''pay'':47B ''poison'':38B ''redguard'':31B ''run'':27B ''share'':56B ''shop'':8B,44B ''store'':25B ''tradit'':55B ''zaria'':29B', 'falkreath', 'Grave Concoctions is an alchemy shop located in Falkreath, in Falkreath Hold. You do not know who runs the shop.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bilegulch_mine', 'Bilegulch Mine is a location northwest of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold, situated south-southwest of Fort Sungard. It is a small orichalcum mine occupied by a group of Orc bandits and features a single zone.

The mine''s camp is fortified with barricades and includes several Orc-style outbuildings.', '''bandit'':33B ''barricad'':46B ''bilegulch'':1A,3B ''camp'':42B ''falkreath'':10B,12B ''featur'':35B ''fort'':19B ''fortifi'':44B ''group'':30B ''hold'':13B ''includ'':48B ''locat'':7B ''mine'':2A,4B,26B,40B ''northwest'':8B ''occupi'':27B ''orc'':32B,51B ''orc-styl'':50B ''orichalcum'':25B ''outbuild'':53B ''sever'':49B ''singl'':37B ''situat'':14B ''small'':24B ''south'':16B ''south-southwest'':15B ''southwest'':17B ''style'':52B ''sungard'':20B ''zone'':38B', 'falkreath', 'Bilegulch Mine is a location northwest of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('meeko''s_shack', 'Meeko''s Shack is a dwelling located on the edge of the Hjaalmarch marshlands, west-northwest of Morthal and Fort Snowhawk. It sits a short distance from the road connecting Morthal to Dragon Bridge. It is rumored that the owner of the house, a Nord who you do not know the name of, has not been heard from in weeks.', '''bridg'':38B ''connect'':34B ''distanc'':30B ''dragon'':37B ''dwell'':9B ''edg'':13B ''fort'':24B ''heard'':61B ''hjaalmarch'':16B ''hous'':47B ''know'':54B ''locat'':10B ''marshland'':17B ''meeko'':1A,4B ''morthal'':22B,35B ''name'':56B ''nord'':49B ''northwest'':20B ''owner'':44B ''road'':33B ''rumor'':41B ''shack'':3A,6B ''short'':29B ''sit'':27B ''snowhawk'':25B ''week'':64B ''west'':19B ''west-northwest'':18B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Meeko''s Shack is a dwelling located on the edge of the Hjaalmarch marshlands, west-northwest of Morthal. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('calm', 'Calm is an Illusion spell that pacifies a target, reducing their hostility and preventing them from attacking. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':22B ''attack'':18B ''calm'':1A,2B ''cast'':26B ''hostil'':13B ''illus'':5B ''level'':24B ''pacifi'':8B ''prevent'':15B ''reduc'':11B ''requir'':20B ''skill'':23B ''spell'':6B ''target'':10B', 'mage', 'Calm is a spell that pacifies a target, reducing their hostility and stopping them from attacking. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('burnt_spriggan_wood', 'Burnt Spriggan Wood is an ingredient dropped by burnt spriggans, known for its fiery and defensive properties. Alchemy effects: Weakness to Fire, Fortify Alteration, Damage Magicka Regen, and Slow.', '''alchemi'':21B ''alter'':27B ''burnt'':1A,4B,12B ''damag'':28B ''defens'':19B ''drop'':10B ''effect'':22B ''fieri'':17B ''fire'':25B ''fortifi'':26B ''ingredi'':9B ''known'':14B ''magicka'':29B ''properti'':20B ''regen'':30B ''slow'':32B ''spriggan'':2A,5B,13B ''weak'':23B ''wood'':3A,6B', 'alchemist', 'Burnt Spriggan Wood is an ingredient dropped by burnt spriggans, known for its fiery and defensive properties.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('juvenile_mudcrab', 'Juvenile Mudcrabs are a small handheld mudcrab with a grey coloured shell. They can be found in any water source. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Regenerate Stamina, Fortify Carry Weight, Cure Disease and Fortify Two-Handed.', '''carri'':39B ''colour'':13B ''cure'':41B ''diseas'':42B ''effect'':33B ''fortifi'':38B,44B ''found'':18B ''grey'':12B ''hand'':47B ''handheld'':8B ''ingredi'':27B ''juvenil'':1A,3B ''make'':30B ''mudcrab'':2A,4B,9B ''offer'':32B ''potion'':29B ''regener'':36B ''shell'':14B ''small'':7B ''sourc'':22B ''stamina'':37B ''two'':46B ''two-hand'':45B ''use'':24B ''water'':21B ''weight'':40B', 'fisher', 'Juvenile Mudcrabs are a small handheld mudcrab with a grey coloured shell. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('crimson_nirnroot', 'Crimson Nirnroot is a rare red variant of nirnroot found exclusively in Blackreach, known for its powerful effects. Alchemy effects: Damage Health , Damage Stamina Invisibility, and Resist Magic.', '''alchemi'':21B ''blackreach'':15B ''crimson'':1A,3B ''damag'':23B,25B ''effect'':20B,22B ''exclus'':13B ''found'':12B ''health'':24B ''invis'':27B ''known'':16B ''magic'':30B ''nirnroot'':2A,4B,11B ''power'':19B ''rare'':7B ''red'':8B ''resist'':29B ''stamina'':26B ''variant'':9B', 'alchemist', 'Crimson Nirnroot is a rare red variant of nirnroot found exclusively in Blackreach, known for its powerful effects.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tumble_arch_pass', 'Tumble Arch Pass is a giant camp located northeast of Whiterun and south-southwest of Nightgate Inn in The Pale. The camp is home to giants and features the usual elements of a giant encampment, including mammoth bones and a cooking fire', '''arch'':2A,5B ''bone'':42B ''camp'':10B,26B ''cook'':45B ''element'':35B ''encamp'':39B ''featur'':32B ''fire'':46B ''giant'':9B,30B,38B ''home'':28B ''includ'':40B ''inn'':21B ''locat'':11B ''mammoth'':41B ''nightgat'':20B ''northeast'':12B ''pale'':24B ''pass'':3A,6B ''south'':17B ''south-southwest'':16B ''southwest'':18B ''tumbl'':1A,4B ''usual'':34B ''whiterun'':14B', 'pale', 'Tumble Arch Pass is a giant camp located northeast of Whiterun and south-southwest of Nightgate Inn in The Pale.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('heal_other', 'Heal Other is a Restoration spell that allows the caster to restore health to another person, healing them over time. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':25B ''allow'':9B ''anoth'':16B ''cast'':29B ''caster'':11B ''heal'':1A,2B,18B ''health'':14B ''level'':27B ''person'':17B ''requir'':23B ''restor'':6B,13B ''skill'':26B ''spell'':7B ''time'':21B', 'mage', '
Heal Other is a spell that allows the caster to restore health to another person, healing them over time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frost_thrall', 'Frost Thrall is a Conjuration spell that permanently summons a Frost Atronach to fight for the caster until it is defeated. It requires a Master skill level to cast.', '''atronach'':14B ''cast'':31B ''caster'':19B ''conjur'':7B ''defeat'':23B ''fight'':16B ''frost'':1A,3B,13B ''level'':29B ''master'':27B ''perman'':10B ''requir'':25B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':8B ''summon'':11B ''thrall'':2A,4B', 'mage', '
Frost Thrall is a spell that permanently summons a Frost Atronach to fight for the caster until it is defeated. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sundered_towers', 'Sundered Towers is a small complex of two linked ruined Nordic towers located southeast of Karthwasten and northeast of Red Eagle Redoubt in the Reach. The towers are inhabited by Forsworn and hagravens, presenting a significant challenge to those who venture near.

The towers sit atop a series of stone staircases and winding paths interspersed with landings.', '''atop'':48B ''challeng'':39B ''complex'':8B ''eagl'':23B ''forsworn'':33B ''hagraven'':35B ''inhabit'':31B ''interspers'':57B ''karthwasten'':18B ''land'':59B ''link'':11B ''locat'':15B ''near'':44B ''nordic'':13B ''northeast'':20B ''path'':56B ''present'':36B ''reach'':27B ''red'':22B ''redoubt'':24B ''ruin'':12B ''seri'':50B ''signific'':38B ''sit'':47B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':16B ''staircas'':53B ''stone'':52B ''sunder'':1A,3B ''tower'':2A,4B,14B,29B,46B ''two'':10B ''ventur'':43B ''wind'':55B', 'reach', 'Sundered Towers is a small complex of two linked ruined Nordic towers located southeast of Karthwasten in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('silver-blood_inn', 'Silver-Blood Inn is located in the city of Markarth, opposite the entrance and next to the market stalls. The inn is owned by the powerful Silver-Blood clan, although the family members are rarely seen in the building. Instead, the inn is managed by Kleppr, who oversees the renting of rooms and the sale of food and drink.

Kleppr''s wife, Frabbi, works at the inn as well, though she is often found arguing with her husband.  Their two children, Hreinn and Hroki, also help with various tasks around the inn. Despite the occasional family drama, Silver-Blood Inn remains a popular stop for travelers in Markarth.', '''also'':91B ''although'':36B ''argu'':81B ''around'':96B ''blood'':3A,7B,34B,106B ''build'':45B ''children'':87B ''citi'':13B ''clan'':35B ''despit'':99B ''drama'':103B ''drink'':65B ''entranc'':18B ''famili'':38B,102B ''food'':63B ''found'':80B ''frabbi'':69B ''help'':92B ''hreinn'':88B ''hroki'':90B ''husband'':84B ''inn'':4A,8B,26B,48B,73B,98B,107B ''instead'':46B ''kleppr'':52B,66B ''locat'':10B ''manag'':50B ''markarth'':15B,115B ''market'':23B ''member'':39B ''next'':20B ''occasion'':101B ''often'':79B ''opposit'':16B ''overse'':54B ''own'':28B ''popular'':110B ''power'':31B ''rare'':41B ''remain'':108B ''rent'':56B ''room'':58B ''sale'':61B ''seen'':42B ''silver'':2A,6B,33B,105B ''silver-blood'':1A,5B,32B,104B ''stall'':24B ''stop'':111B ''task'':95B ''though'':76B ''travel'':113B ''two'':86B ''various'':94B ''well'':75B ''wife'':68B ''work'':70B', 'reach, innkeeper, traveler', 'Silver-Blood Inn is located in the city of Markarth, opposite the entrance and next to the market stalls. The inn is owned by the powerful Silver-Blood clan, though you do not know exactlly who works here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('temple_of_dibella', 'The Temple of Dibella is a small Aedric temple located in the heart of Markarth, dedicated to Dibella, the Aedric goddess of love, beauty, and artistry. The temple is situated above the Shrine of Talos and can be accessed by climbing numerous flights of stairs, offering a peaceful and serene atmosphere above the bustling city below.

The temple is home to the priestesses of Dibella, with Hamal serving as their leader. Other notable priestesses include Anwen, a Redguard, Orla, a Nord, and Senna, a Breton.', '''access'':42B ''aedric'':11B,23B ''anwen'':79B ''artistri'':29B ''atmospher'':54B ''beauti'':27B ''breton'':88B ''bustl'':57B ''citi'':58B ''climb'':44B ''dedic'':19B ''dibella'':3A,7B,21B,68B ''flight'':46B ''goddess'':24B ''hamal'':70B ''heart'':16B ''home'':63B ''includ'':78B ''leader'':74B ''locat'':13B ''love'':26B ''markarth'':18B ''nord'':84B ''notabl'':76B ''numer'':45B ''offer'':49B ''orla'':82B ''peac'':51B ''priestess'':66B,77B ''redguard'':81B ''senna'':86B ''seren'':53B ''serv'':71B ''shrine'':36B ''situat'':33B ''small'':10B ''stair'':48B ''talo'':38B ''templ'':1A,5B,12B,31B,61B', 'reach, priest, scholar', 'The Temple of Dibella is a small Aedric temple located in the heart of Markarth, dedicated to Dibella, the Aedric goddess of love, beauty, and artistry. The temple is situated above the Shrine of Talos . You do not know who runs the temple.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('whistling_mine', 'Whistling Mine is a small iron mine and settlement located southeast of Winterhold, along the southern road that connects Winterhold to Windhelm, at the base of the mountains. The mine is nestled near the northern edge of Stillborn Cave. The settlement is home to a handful of Nord warriors who are trying to make a living through mining, though they face the harsh conditions of the region.

Among the residents are Angvid, Badnir, Gunding, and Horgar—each Nords attempting to carve out a livelihood in the tough and unforgiving environment of Whistling Mine. The mine itself serves as a modest source of iron, though the locals'' struggles to thrive in the area highlight the challenges posed by the surrounding terrain and climate.', '''along'':16B ''among'':70B ''angvid'':74B ''area'':113B ''attempt'':80B ''badnir'':75B ''base'':27B ''carv'':82B ''cave'':41B ''challeng'':116B ''climat'':123B ''condit'':66B ''connect'':21B ''edg'':38B ''environ'':91B ''face'':63B ''gund'':76B ''hand'':48B ''harsh'':65B ''highlight'':114B ''home'':45B ''horgar—each'':78B ''iron'':8B,104B ''live'':58B ''livelihood'':85B ''local'':107B ''locat'':12B ''make'':56B ''mine'':2A,4B,9B,32B,60B,94B,96B ''modest'':101B ''mountain'':30B ''near'':35B ''nestl'':34B ''nord'':50B,79B ''northern'':37B ''pose'':117B ''region'':69B ''resid'':72B ''road'':19B ''serv'':98B ''settlement'':11B,43B ''small'':7B ''sourc'':102B ''southeast'':13B ''southern'':18B ''stillborn'':40B ''struggl'':108B ''surround'':120B ''terrain'':121B ''though'':61B,105B ''thrive'':110B ''tough'':88B ''tri'':54B ''unforgiv'':90B ''warrior'':51B ''whistl'':1A,3B,93B ''windhelm'':24B ''winterhold'':15B,22B', 'winterhold', 'Whistling Mine is a small iron mine and settlement located southeast of Winterhold. You do not know who works here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('alftand', 'Alftand is a large Dwarven ruin located southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and east of Driftshade Refuge. This ancient and sprawling ruin is one of many remnants of the Dwarven civilization, now abandoned and overrun by various dangerous creatures.

The ruin is filled with the remnants of Dwarven architecture and technology, showcasing the advanced craftsmanship of the long-lost Dwemer.', '''abandon'':36B ''advanc'':57B ''alftand'':1A,2B ''ancient'':22B ''architectur'':52B ''civil'':34B ''craftsmanship'':58B ''creatur'':42B ''danger'':41B ''driftshad'':19B ''dwarven'':6B,33B,51B ''dwemer'':64B ''east'':17B ''fill'':46B ''larg'':5B ''locat'':8B ''long'':62B ''long-lost'':61B ''lost'':63B ''mani'':29B ''one'':27B ''overrun'':38B ''refug'':20B ''region'':15B ''remnant'':30B,49B ''ruin'':7B,25B,44B ''showcas'':55B ''southwest'':9B ''sprawl'':24B ''technolog'':54B ''various'':40B ''winterhold'':11B,14B', 'winterhold', 'Alftand is a large Dwarven ruin located southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fort_fellhammer', 'Fort Fellhammer is a medium-sized fort and iron mine located south of Dawnstar, in the Winterhold region. It sits off the paved road that leads southwest to Fort Dunstad, near the point where the road turns east after passing Red Road Pass. A dirt path branches off from the road at this turn, leading eastward to the fort.

Once a strategic military outpost, the fort is now occupied by a group of bandits who have taken over the iron mine and its surrounding area. These bandits use the fort as a hideout.', '''area'':88B ''bandit'':77B,90B ''branch'':50B ''dawnstar'':17B ''dirt'':48B ''dunstad'':33B ''east'':41B ''eastward'':59B ''fellhamm'':2A,4B ''fort'':1A,3B,10B,32B,62B,69B,93B ''group'':75B ''hideout'':96B ''iron'':12B,83B ''lead'':29B,58B ''locat'':14B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''militari'':66B ''mine'':13B,84B ''near'':34B ''occupi'':72B ''outpost'':67B ''pass'':43B,46B ''path'':49B ''pave'':26B ''point'':36B ''red'':44B ''region'':21B ''road'':27B,39B,45B,54B ''sit'':23B ''size'':9B ''south'':15B ''southwest'':30B ''strateg'':65B ''surround'':87B ''taken'':80B ''turn'':40B,57B ''use'':91B ''winterhold'':20B', 'winterhold, legion, stormcloak', 'Fort Fellhammer is a medium-sized fort and iron mine located south of Dawnstar, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('saarthal', 'Saarthal is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southwest of Winterhold. As the first Nord settlement in Skyrim, Saarthal holds significant historical and archaeological value, particularly to the College of Winterhold, who is actively excavating the site in search of ancient artifacts. The ruins are believed to have a deeper significance, potentially tied to a powerful past.

The original settlement of Saarthal was destroyed during the Merethic Era in an event known as the Night of Tears, where elves launched a brutal attack on the city. The incident, as detailed in the book Night of Tears, suggests that the elven assault was driven by a desire to control a powerful item hidden beneath the city. ', '''activ'':36B ''ancient'':43B ''archaeolog'':26B ''artifact'':44B ''assault'':103B ''attack'':85B ''believ'':48B ''beneath'':115B ''book'':95B ''brutal'':84B ''citi'':88B,117B ''colleg'':31B ''control'':110B ''deeper'':52B ''desir'':108B ''destroy'':66B ''detail'':92B ''driven'':105B ''elv'':81B ''elven'':102B ''era'':70B ''event'':73B ''excav'':37B ''first'':16B ''hidden'':114B ''histor'':24B ''hold'':22B ''incid'':90B ''item'':113B ''known'':74B ''launch'':82B ''locat'':10B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''mereth'':69B ''night'':77B,96B ''nord'':17B ''nordic'':8B ''origin'':61B ''particular'':28B ''past'':59B ''potenti'':54B ''power'':58B,112B ''ruin'':9B,46B ''saarthal'':1A,2B,21B,64B ''search'':41B ''settlement'':18B,62B ''signific'':23B,53B ''site'':39B ''size'':7B ''skyrim'':20B ''southwest'':11B ''suggest'':99B ''tear'':79B,98B ''tie'':55B ''valu'':27B ''winterhold'':13B,33B', 'collegeofwinterhold, scholar', 'Saarthal is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southwest of Winterhold, As the first Nord settlement in Skyrim, Saarthal holds significant historical and archaeological value, particularly to the College of Winterhold, who is actively excavating the site in search of ancient artifacts. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch, winterhold', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('snow_veil_sanctum', 'Snow Veil Sanctum is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located north-northeast of Windhelm, in the Winterhold region, and south of Bleakcoast Cave. The ruin is home to draugr, the ancient undead guardians that protect Nordic tombs, making it a dangerous and foreboding site for any who dare enter.', '''ancient'':36B ''bleakcoast'':27B ''cave'':28B ''danger'':46B ''dare'':53B ''draugr'':34B ''enter'':54B ''forebod'':48B ''guardian'':38B ''home'':32B ''locat'':14B ''make'':43B ''medium'':10B ''medium-s'':9B ''nordic'':12B,41B ''north'':16B ''north-northeast'':15B ''northeast'':17B ''protect'':40B ''region'':23B ''ruin'':13B,30B ''sanctum'':3A,6B ''site'':49B ''size'':11B ''snow'':1A,4B ''south'':25B ''tomb'':42B ''undead'':37B ''veil'':2A,5B ''windhelm'':19B ''winterhold'':22B', 'winterhold', 'Snow Veil Sanctum is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located north-northeast of Windhelm, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skytemple_ruins', 'Skytemple Ruins is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located north of the College of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and east of Ysgramor''s Tomb. The ruins are perched atop a large glacial mound on an island off the northern coast of Skyrim, offering a dramatic and isolated setting.

The sparse remains of the temple are home to draugr and skeletons, the undead guardians of the site, making it a dangerous location for those who venture into its depths.', '''atop'':32B ''coast'':43B ''colleg'':15B ''danger'':73B ''depth'':81B ''dramat'':48B ''draugr'':61B ''east'':23B ''glacial'':35B ''guardian'':66B ''home'':59B ''island'':39B ''isol'':50B ''larg'':34B ''locat'':11B,74B ''make'':70B ''mound'':36B ''nordic'':9B ''north'':12B ''northern'':42B ''offer'':46B ''outdoor'':8B ''perch'':31B ''region'':21B ''remain'':54B ''ruin'':2A,4B,10B,29B ''set'':51B ''site'':69B ''skeleton'':63B ''skyrim'':45B ''skytempl'':1A,3B ''small'':7B ''spars'':53B ''templ'':57B ''tomb'':27B ''undead'':65B ''ventur'':78B ''winterhold'':17B,20B ''ysgramor'':25B', 'winterhold', 'Skytemple Ruins is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located north of the College of Winterhold.You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pilgrim''s_trench', 'Pilgrim''s Trench is a deep underwater ravine located northwest of Winterhold, along the coast. The trench is known for containing four submerged shipwrecks, remnants of vessels that met their untimely end in the treacherous waters of the Sea of Ghosts.  It is recommended to bring an underwater breathing potion if you wish to explore the wrecks.', '''along'':16B ''breath'':52B ''bring'':49B ''coast'':18B ''contain'':24B ''deep'':9B ''end'':35B ''explor'':58B ''four'':25B ''ghost'':44B ''known'':22B ''locat'':12B ''met'':32B ''northwest'':13B ''pilgrim'':1A,4B ''potion'':53B ''ravin'':11B ''recommend'':47B ''remnant'':28B ''sea'':42B ''shipwreck'':27B ''submerg'':26B ''treacher'':38B ''trench'':3A,6B,20B ''underwat'':10B,51B ''untim'':34B ''vessel'':30B ''water'':39B ''winterhold'':15B ''wish'':56B ''wreck'':60B', 'winterhold, sailor', 'Pilgrim''s Trench is a deep underwater ravine located northwest of Winterhold, along the coast. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arniel''s_convection', 'Arniel''s Convection is a Destruction spell that creates a stream of fire around the caster, dealing fire damage to nearby enemies over time. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':31B ''arniel'':1A,4B ''around'':17B ''cast'':35B ''caster'':19B ''convect'':3A,6B ''creat'':12B ''damag'':22B ''deal'':20B ''destruct'':9B ''enemi'':25B ''fire'':16B,21B ''level'':33B ''nearbi'':24B ''requir'':29B ''skill'':32B ''spell'':10B ''stream'':14B ''time'':27B', 'mage', 'Arniel''s Convection is a spell that creates a stream of fire around the caster, dealing fire damage to nearby enemies over time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('birna''s_oddments', 'Birna''s Oddments is a general goods store located in the heart of Winterhold, nestled between the Jarl''s Longhouse and Kraldar''s House. This two-story building is run by Birna, a Nord pawnbroker known for her wide range of goods, from mundane items to rare treasures.

Birna lives in the store with her brother, Ranmir, a troubled Nord citizen of Winterhold. While Birna focuses on her business, Ranmir spends much of his time drinking away his sorrows in The Frozen Hearth, the local tavern.', '''away'':81B ''birna'':1A,4B,36B,53B,69B ''brother'':60B ''build'':32B ''busi'':73B ''citizen'':65B ''drink'':80B ''focus'':70B ''frozen'':86B ''general'':9B ''good'':10B,46B ''heart'':15B ''hearth'':87B ''hous'':27B ''item'':49B ''jarl'':21B ''known'':40B ''kraldar'':25B ''live'':54B ''local'':89B ''locat'':12B ''longhous'':23B ''much'':76B ''mundan'':48B ''nestl'':18B ''nord'':38B,64B ''oddment'':3A,6B ''pawnbrok'':39B ''rang'':44B ''ranmir'':61B,74B ''rare'':51B ''run'':34B ''sorrow'':83B ''spend'':75B ''store'':11B,57B ''stori'':31B ''tavern'':90B ''time'':79B ''treasur'':52B ''troubl'':63B ''two'':30B ''two-stori'':29B ''wide'':43B ''winterhold'':17B,67B', 'winterhold', 'Birna''s Oddments is a general goods store located in the heart of Winterhold. You only know Birna runs the store.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falion''s_house', 'Falion''s House is the residence and shop of the town wizard, Falion, in Morthal. Located along the jetty, it sits behind the Thaumaturgist''s Hut and is situated on the edge of the water, just a short distance from Alva''s house. Falion lives there with his child apprentice, Agni.', '''agni'':54B ''along'':20B ''alva'':44B ''apprentic'':53B ''behind'':25B ''child'':52B ''distanc'':42B ''edg'':35B ''falion'':1A,4B,16B,47B ''hous'':3A,6B,46B ''hut'':29B ''jetti'':22B ''live'':48B ''locat'':19B ''morthal'':18B ''resid'':9B ''shop'':11B ''short'':41B ''sit'':24B ''situat'':32B ''thaumaturgist'':27B ''town'':14B ''water'':38B ''wizard'':15B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Falion''s House is the residence in Morthal. You do not know who Falion is.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('light', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Alteration spells that summon a hovering orb of light to illuminate dark areas, making exploration in caves and dungeons easier. In addition to being available as a spell, this effect can also be found on enchanted items, offering a practical light source for non-magic users.', '''addit'':30B ''also'':40B ''alter'':9B ''area'':21B ''avail'':33B ''cave'':25B ''dark'':20B ''dungeon'':27B ''easier'':28B ''effect'':4B,38B ''enchant'':44B ''explor'':23B ''focus'':8B ''found'':42B ''hover'':14B ''illumin'':19B ''item'':45B ''light'':1A,17B,49B ''magic'':3B,54B ''make'':22B ''non'':53B ''non-mag'':52B ''offer'':46B ''orb'':15B ''practic'':48B ''sourc'':50B ''spell'':10B,36B ''summon'':12B ''user'':55B ''util'':7B ''utility-focus'':6B', 'mage', 'It makes a floating light that follows you around, brightening dark places. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fahlbtharz', 'Fahlbtharz is a large Dwarven ruin located east of the Water Stone and northwest of Frostmoon Crag on Solstheim. The ancient ruin, like many remnants of the Dwemer civilization, is an intricate labyrinth of machinery and traps, showcasing the advanced engineering of the long-lost dwarves.', '''advanc'':41B ''ancient'':22B ''civil'':30B ''crag'':18B ''dwarv'':48B ''dwarven'':6B ''dwemer'':29B ''east'':9B ''engin'':42B ''fahlbtharz'':1A,2B ''frostmoon'':17B ''intric'':33B ''labyrinth'':34B ''larg'':5B ''like'':24B ''locat'':8B ''long'':46B ''long-lost'':45B ''lost'':47B ''machineri'':36B ''mani'':25B ''northwest'':15B ''remnant'':26B ''ruin'':7B,23B ''showcas'':39B ''solstheim'':20B ''stone'':13B ''trap'':38B ''water'':12B', 'solstheim, dwemer', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('esberns_potion', 'Esbern''s Potion is a secret concoction created by the Blades to combat dragons. It is known only to Esbern and is said to bolster one''s defenses against dragon attacks.', '''attack'':33B ''blade'':13B ''bolster'':27B ''combat'':15B ''concoct'':9B ''creat'':10B ''defens'':30B ''dragon'':16B,32B ''esbern'':1A,3B,22B ''known'':19B ''one'':28B ''potion'':2A,5B ''said'':25B ''secret'':8B', 'esbern, dragon', 'You know nothing about this potion or its purpose.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('raldbthar', 'Raldbthar is a medium-sized Dwarven ruin located west-southwest of Windhelm in The Pale. The ruin is filled with ancient Dwemer machinery, traps, and automatons, making it a challenging destination for adventurers. Bandits have taken refugee in the area.', '''adventur'':36B ''ancient'':24B ''area'':43B ''automaton'':29B ''bandit'':37B ''challeng'':33B ''destin'':34B ''dwarven'':8B ''dwemer'':25B ''fill'':22B ''locat'':10B ''machineri'':26B ''make'':30B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''pale'':18B ''raldbthar'':1A,2B ''refuge'':40B ''ruin'':9B,20B ''size'':7B ''southwest'':13B ''taken'':39B ''trap'':27B ''west'':12B ''west-southwest'':11B ''windhelm'':15B', 'pale, dwemer', 'Raldbthar is a medium-sized Dwarven ruin located west-southwest of Windhelm in The Pale. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mace_of_the_crusader', '
The Mace of the Crusader, also known as the Mace of Zenithar, is a holy artifact crafted by Zenithar, imbued with the power to burn foes with holy flames and turn the undead. According to legend, after Pelinal Whitestrake''s death, the mace was brought to Leyawiin, where it inspired the creation of the Great Chapel of Zenithar by Saint Kaladas.', '''accord'':38B ''also'':10B ''artifact'':20B ''brought'':49B ''burn'':29B ''chapel'':60B ''craft'':21B ''creation'':56B ''crusad'':4A,9B ''death'':45B ''flame'':33B ''foe'':30B ''great'':59B ''holi'':19B,32B ''imbu'':24B ''inspir'':54B ''kalada'':65B ''known'':11B ''legend'':40B ''leyawiin'':51B ''mace'':1A,6B,14B,47B ''pelin'':42B ''power'':27B ''saint'':64B ''turn'':35B ''undead'':37B ''whitestrak'':43B ''zenithar'':16B,23B,62B', 'scholar, imperial', 'The Mace of the Crusader, or Mace of Zenithar, is a holy artifact crafted by Zenithar that burns foes with holy flames and turns the undead. It inspired the creation of Leyawiin''s Great Chapel of Zenithar after being brought there following Pelinal Whitestrake''s death.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('golden_saint', 'Golden Saints, also known as the Aureal, are a race of golden-skinned Daedra aligned with the Daedric Prince Sheogorath. They are known for their striking golden appearance, often donning avian-themed armor and wielding powerful weapons. Highly intelligent and formidable in combat, the Golden Saints are both proud and fiercely loyal to their master. However, their pride can make them arrogant, and they are known for being quick to anger and harsh in their judgments.', '''align'':18B ''also'':5B ''anger'':75B ''appear'':31B ''armor'':37B ''arrog'':66B ''aureal'':9B ''avian'':35B ''avian-them'':34B ''combat'':47B ''daedra'':17B ''daedric'':21B ''don'':33B ''fierc'':55B ''formid'':45B ''golden'':1A,3B,15B,30B,49B ''golden-skin'':14B ''harsh'':77B ''high'':42B ''howev'':60B ''intellig'':43B ''judgment'':80B ''known'':6B,26B,70B ''loyal'':56B ''make'':64B ''master'':59B ''often'':32B ''power'':40B ''pride'':62B ''princ'':22B ''proud'':53B ''quick'':73B ''race'':12B ''saint'':2A,4B,50B ''sheogorath'':23B ''skin'':16B ''strike'':29B ''theme'':36B ''weapon'':41B ''wield'':39B', 'daedric, daedra scholar', '
Golden Saints, or Aureal, are golden-skinned Daedra aligned with Sheogorath, the Daedric Prince of Madness. Recognizable by their striking appearance and avian-themed armor, they are highly intelligent and skilled in combat. Fiercely loyal to Sheogorath, they exhibit immense pride, which can lead to arrogance and a quick temper. Their harsh judgments and unwavering dedication make them both formidable allies and fearsome opponents.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sabre_cat_tooth', 'Sabre Cat Teeth are dropped by sabre cats, who always drop either a tooth or an eye of sabre cat, along with a sabre cat pelt. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Fortify Heavy Armor, Fortify Smithing, and Weakness to Poison.', '''alchemi'':30B ''along'':24B ''alway'':13B ''armor'':36B ''cat'':2A,5B,11B,23B,28B ''drop'':8B,14B ''effect'':31B ''either'':15B ''eye'':20B ''fortifi'':34B,37B ''heavi'':35B ''pelt'':29B ''poison'':42B ''restor'':32B ''sabr'':1A,4B,10B,22B,27B ''smith'':38B ''stamina'':33B ''teeth'':6B ''tooth'':3A,17B ''weak'':40B', 'alchemist', 'Sabre Cat Teeth are dropped by sabre cats, who always drop either a tooth or an eye of sabre cat, along with a sabre cat pelt. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('philter_of_the_phantom', 'The Philter of the Phantom grants a ghostly appearance to its user for a short time. It is believed to hold the essence of restless spirits, and is rumored to be obtainable only from Shroud Hearth Barrow.', '''appear'':13B ''barrow'':41B ''believ'':23B ''essenc'':27B ''ghost'':12B ''grant'':10B ''hearth'':40B ''hold'':25B ''obtain'':36B ''phantom'':4A,9B ''philter'':1A,6B ''restless'':29B ''rumor'':33B ''short'':19B ''shroud'':39B ''spirit'':30B ''time'':20B ''user'':16B', 'alchemist', 'You know nothing about this potion or its effects. Maybe an alchemist might though.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('thaumaturgist''s_hut', 'The Thaumaturgist''s Hut is an alchemy shop located across from Highmoon Hall in Morthal. The shop is run by Lami, who manages the business during normal hours from 8 AM to 8 PM. ', '''8'':33B,36B ''across'':13B ''alchemi'':10B ''busi'':28B ''hall'':16B ''highmoon'':15B ''hour'':31B ''hut'':3A,7B ''lami'':24B ''locat'':12B ''manag'':26B ''morthal'':18B ''normal'':30B ''pm'':37B ''run'':22B ''shop'':11B,20B ''thaumaturgist'':1A,5B', 'hjaalmarch', 'The Thaumaturgist''s Hut is an alchemy shop located in Morthal. You do not know who runs the shop.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('halldir''s_cairn', 'Halldir''s Cairn is a small cave located southwest of Falkreath and southeast of Cracked Tusk Keep in Falkreath Hold. The cave is inhabited by draugr and ghosts.', '''cairn'':3A,6B ''cave'':10B,25B ''crack'':18B ''draugr'':29B ''falkreath'':14B,22B ''ghost'':31B ''halldir'':1A,4B ''hold'':23B ''inhabit'':27B ''keep'':20B ''locat'':11B ''small'':9B ''southeast'':16B ''southwest'':12B ''tusk'':19B', 'falkreath', 'Halldir''s Cairn is a small cave located southwest of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dreugh_wax', 'Dreugh Wax, a grey wax originating from Vvardenfell''s dreughs or Cyrodiil''s land dreughs, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Weakness to Magic, Frenzy, Fortify Enchanting, and Fortify Smithing.', '''alchemi'':28B ''caravan'':27B ''cyrodiil'':14B ''dreugh'':1A,3B,12B,17B ''effect'':29B ''enchant'':35B ''fortifi'':34B,37B ''frenzi'':33B ''grey'':6B ''ingredi'':20B ''khajiit'':26B ''land'':16B ''magic'':32B ''origin'':8B ''purchas'':24B ''smith'':38B ''vvardenfel'':10B ''wax'':2A,4B,7B ''weak'':30B', 'alchemist', 'Dreugh Wax, a grey wax originating from Vvardenfell''s dreughs or Cyrodiil''s land dreughs, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('roobrush', 'Roobrush, originating from Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Cure Poison, Weakness to Magic, Fortify Sneak, and Lingering Damage Health.', '''alchemi'':16B ''caravan'':15B ''cure'':18B ''damag'':27B ''effect'':17B ''fortifi'':23B ''health'':28B ''ingredi'':8B ''khajiit'':14B ''linger'':26B ''magic'':22B ''origin'':3B ''poison'':19B ''purchas'':12B ''roobrush'':1A,2B ''sneak'':24B ''vvardenfel'':5B ''weak'':20B', 'alchemist', 'Roobrush, originating from Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glass_catfish', 'Glass Catfish are large translucent fish found in underground fishing spots. They can be eaten with a rather stale taste.', '''catfish'':2A,4B ''eaten'':17B ''fish'':8B,12B ''found'':9B ''glass'':1A,3B ''larg'':6B ''rather'':20B ''spot'':13B ''stale'':21B ''tast'':22B ''transluc'':7B ''underground'':11B', 'fisher', 'Glass Catfish are large translucent fish. They can be eaten with a rather stale taste. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('crystaldrift_cave', 'Crystaldrift Cave is a small cave southwest of Riften and northeast of the Ruins of Rkund. There are rumours of haunting animal screams coming from this cave late at night.', '''anim'':24B ''cave'':2A,4B,8B,29B ''come'':26B ''crystaldrift'':1A,3B ''haunt'':23B ''late'':30B ''night'':32B ''northeast'':13B ''riften'':11B ''rkund'':18B ''ruin'':16B ''rumour'':21B ''scream'':25B ''small'':7B ''southwest'':9B', 'rift', 'Crystaldrift Cave is a small cave southwest of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('stony_creek_cave', 'Stony Creek Cave is a small cave located southeast of Windhelm and north of Ansilvund in Eastmarch. The cave is rumoured to be occupied by bandits.', '''ansilvund'':18B ''bandit'':29B ''cave'':3A,6B,10B,22B ''creek'':2A,5B ''eastmarch'':20B ''locat'':11B ''north'':16B ''occupi'':27B ''rumour'':24B ''small'':9B ''southeast'':12B ''stoni'':1A,4B ''windhelm'':14B', 'eastmarch', 'Stony Creek Cave is a small cave located southeast of Windhelm in Eastmarch. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('salt_pile', 'Salt Piles are more commonly valued for cooking, as they are essential in many recipes, though they also have some alchemical uses. Alchemy effects: Weakness to Magic, Fortify Restoration, Slow, and Regenerate Magicka.', '''alchem'':23B ''alchemi'':25B ''also'':20B ''common'':7B ''cook'':10B ''effect'':26B ''essenti'':14B ''fortifi'':30B ''magic'':29B ''magicka'':35B ''mani'':16B ''pile'':2A,4B ''recip'':17B ''regener'':34B ''restor'':31B ''salt'':1A,3B ''slow'':32B ''though'':18B ''use'':24B ''valu'':8B ''weak'':27B', 'alchemist', 'Salt Piles are more commonly valued for cooking, as they are essential in many recipes, though they also have some alchemical uses. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sadrith_mora', 'Sadrith Mora, meaning "Mushroom Forest" in Dark Elvish, was the seat of power for Great House Telvanni on the island of Vvardenfell. Situated on an island in the Zafirbel Bay, it was accessible primarily by boat or teleportation, and entry required a certification of hospitality. Dominated by Tel Naga, the central Telvanni tower and home of the local councilor, Sadrith Mora was characterized by its mushroom-inspired architecture, sprawling markets, and strict governance by House Telvanni. The city also hosted the Telvanni Council House and Wolverine Hall, an Imperial bastion incongruously located in Telvanni territory. Known for its exclusive culture, the city exemplified Telvanni independence and disdain for outside influence.

In its history, Sadrith Mora played a critical role in Telvanni politics and magical innovation. During the Second Era, Archmagister Nelos Otheri advanced the House’s magical capabilities, including the creation of the Spore Steed. By the Third Era, the city was ruled by the eccentric Magister Neloth, who gave his support to the Nerevarine during their quest to fulfill prophecy. Sadrith Mora was devastated during the Red Year in 4E 5, when the eruption of Red Mountain destroyed much of Vvardenfell. Though its fate afterward remains unclear, the city''s legacy endures as a symbol of Telvanni magical prowess and defiance of convention.', '''4e'':183B ''5'':184B ''access'':35B ''advanc'':136B ''afterward'':198B ''also'':82B ''architectur'':71B ''archmagist'':133B ''bastion'':93B ''bay'':32B ''boat'':38B ''capabl'':140B ''central'':53B ''certif'':45B ''character'':65B ''citi'':81B,105B,153B,202B ''convent'':216B ''council'':86B ''councilor'':61B ''creation'':143B ''critic'':121B ''cultur'':103B ''dark'':9B ''defianc'':214B ''destroy'':191B ''devast'':177B ''disdain'':110B ''domin'':48B ''eccentr'':158B ''elvish'':10B ''endur'':205B ''entri'':42B ''era'':132B,151B ''erupt'':187B ''exclus'':102B ''exemplifi'':106B ''fate'':197B ''forest'':7B ''fulfil'':172B ''gave'':162B ''govern'':76B ''great'':17B ''hall'':90B ''histori'':116B ''home'':57B ''hospit'':47B ''host'':83B ''hous'':18B,78B,87B ''house’'':138B ''imperi'':92B ''includ'':141B ''incongru'':94B ''independ'':108B ''influenc'':113B ''innov'':128B ''inspir'':70B ''island'':22B,28B ''known'':99B ''legaci'':204B ''local'':60B ''locat'':95B ''magic'':127B,139B,211B ''magist'':159B ''market'':73B ''mean'':5B ''mora'':2A,4B,63B,118B,175B ''mountain'':190B ''much'':192B ''mushroom'':6B,69B ''mushroom-inspir'':68B ''naga'':51B ''nelo'':134B ''neloth'':160B ''nerevarin'':167B ''otheri'':135B ''outsid'':112B ''play'':119B ''polit'':125B ''power'':15B ''primarili'':36B ''propheci'':173B ''prowess'':212B ''quest'':170B ''red'':180B,189B ''remain'':199B ''requir'':43B ''role'':122B ''rule'':155B ''sadrith'':1A,3B,62B,117B,174B ''seat'':13B ''second'':131B ''situat'':25B ''spore'':146B ''sprawl'':72B ''steed'':147B ''strict'':75B ''support'':164B ''symbol'':208B ''tel'':50B ''teleport'':40B ''telvanni'':19B,54B,79B,85B,97B,107B,124B,210B ''territori'':98B ''third'':150B ''though'':195B ''tower'':55B ''unclear'':200B ''vvardenfel'':24B,194B ''wolverin'':89B ''year'':181B ''zafirbel'':31B', 'scholar, darkelf', '
Sadrith Mora, meaning "Mushroom Forest" in Dark Elvish, was the seat of House Telvanni''s power on Vvardenfell, located on an island in Zafirbel Bay. Known for its mushroom-inspired architecture and strict Telvanni governance, the city was dominated by the central Tel Naga tower and featured notable structures like the Telvanni Council House and Wolverine Hall. Sadrith Mora played a crucial role in Telvanni politics and magical advancements, especially under Archmagister Nelos Otheri and Magister Neloth in later years. Devastated during the Red Year by the eruption of Red Mountain, its fate remains uncertain, but it remains a symbol of Telvanni''s magical prowess and independence.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragon_bridge', 'Dragon Bridge is a small town located in northwestern Skyrim, near the iconic Dragon Bridge, southwest of the Statue to Meridia and east-southeast of Deepwood Redoubt. The town and its famous bridge are of strategic importance in the civil war, as both the Stormcloaks and Imperials view it as a key location.', '''bridg'':2A,4B,17B,36B ''civil'':43B ''deepwood'':29B ''dragon'':1A,3B,16B ''east'':26B ''east-southeast'':25B ''famous'':35B ''icon'':15B ''imperi'':50B ''import'':40B ''key'':55B ''locat'':9B,56B ''meridia'':23B ''near'':13B ''northwestern'':11B ''redoubt'':30B ''skyrim'':12B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':27B ''southwest'':18B ''statu'':21B ''stormcloak'':48B ''strateg'':39B ''town'':8B,32B ''view'':51B ''war'':44B', 'haafingar, scholar', 'Dragon Bridge is a small town located in northwestern Skyrim, near the iconic Dragon Bridge, south of Solitude. The town and its famous bridge are of strategic importance in the civil war, as both the Stormcloaks and Imperials view it as a key location.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('spider_egg', 'Spider Eggs are light greenish eggs that can be acquired by harvesting the egg sacs of frostbite spiders. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina, Damage Magicka Regen, Fortify Lockpicking, and Fortify Marksman.', '''acquir'':12B ''alchemi'':21B ''damag'':23B,25B ''effect'':22B ''egg'':2A,4B,8B,16B ''fortifi'':28B,31B ''frostbit'':19B ''greenish'':7B ''harvest'':14B ''light'':6B ''lockpick'':29B ''magicka'':26B ''marksman'':32B ''regen'':27B ''sac'':17B ''spider'':1A,3B,20B ''stamina'':24B', 'alchemist', 'Spider Eggs are light greenish eggs that can be acquired by harvesting the egg sacs of frostbite spiders. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('conjure_flame_atronach', 'Conjure Flame Atronach is a Conjuration spell that summons a Flame Atronach to fight for the caster for a limited time. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':28B ''atronach'':3A,6B,15B ''cast'':32B ''caster'':20B ''conjur'':1A,4B,9B ''fight'':17B ''flame'':2A,5B,14B ''level'':30B ''limit'':23B ''requir'':26B ''skill'':29B ''spell'':10B ''summon'':12B ''time'':24B', 'mage', 'Conjure Flame Atronach is a spell that summons a Flame Atronach, a fiery creature, to fight for the caster for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('heart_of_order', 'Heart of Order, a large white crystal originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Restore Health, Fortify Health, Fortify One-handed, and Fortify Two-handed.', '''alchemi'':26B ''caravan'':25B ''crystal'':10B ''effect'':27B ''fortifi'':30B,32B,37B ''hand'':35B,40B ''health'':29B,31B ''heart'':1A,4B ''ingredi'':18B ''isl'':15B ''khajiit'':24B ''larg'':8B ''one'':34B ''one-hand'':33B ''order'':3A,6B ''origin'':11B ''purchas'':22B ''restor'':28B ''shiver'':14B ''two'':39B ''two-hand'':38B ''white'':9B', 'alchemist', 'Heart of Order, a large white crystal originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skeleton_key', 'The Skeleton Key is a powerful Daedric artifact linked to Nocturnal, the Daedric Prince of Night and Shadows. Though typically appearing as a key or lockpick, its form can vary. The Skeleton Key is renowned for its ability to unlock any lock, making it a coveted tool for thieves and adventurers alike. When it manifests as a lockpick, it is nearly indestructible, bypassing even the toughest barriers. However, some wizards, seeking to limit its power, placed restrictions on the Key, such as limiting its use to once per day and ensuring it never stays in the possession of one thief for long, eventually disappearing.', '''abil'':40B ''adventur'':53B ''alik'':54B ''appear'':23B ''artifact'':10B ''barrier'':69B ''bypass'':65B ''covet'':48B ''daedric'':9B,15B ''day'':91B ''disappear'':106B ''ensur'':93B ''even'':66B ''eventu'':105B ''form'':30B ''howev'':70B ''indestruct'':64B ''key'':2A,5B,26B,35B,82B ''limit'':75B,85B ''link'':11B ''lock'':44B ''lockpick'':28B,60B ''long'':104B ''make'':45B ''manifest'':57B ''near'':63B ''never'':95B ''night'':18B ''nocturn'':13B ''one'':101B ''per'':90B ''place'':78B ''possess'':99B ''power'':8B,77B ''princ'':16B ''renown'':37B ''restrict'':79B ''seek'':73B ''shadow'':20B ''skeleton'':1A,4B,34B ''stay'':96B ''thief'':102B ''thiev'':51B ''though'':21B ''tool'':49B ''toughest'':68B ''typic'':22B ''unlock'':42B ''use'':87B ''vari'':32B ''wizard'':72B', 'daedric, daedra, thievesguild, scholar', 'The Skeleton Key is a Daedric artifact of Nocturnal, known for its ability to unlock any lock. ', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('morvunskar', 'Morvunskar is a small fort located southwest of Windhelm and north of Riverside Shack in Eastmarch. It is rumoured to be occupied by dangerous warlocks.

Strategically positioned on a hill, the fort offers a commanding view of the surrounding area, including Windhelm to the northeast, Kynesgrove to the southeast, and several main roads visible from its towers.', '''area'':41B ''command'':36B ''danger'':25B ''eastmarch'':17B ''fort'':6B,33B ''hill'':31B ''includ'':42B ''kynesgrov'':47B ''locat'':7B ''main'':53B ''morvunskar'':1A,2B ''north'':12B ''northeast'':46B ''occupi'':23B ''offer'':34B ''posit'':28B ''riversid'':14B ''road'':54B ''rumour'':20B ''sever'':52B ''shack'':15B ''small'':5B ''southeast'':50B ''southwest'':8B ''strateg'':27B ''surround'':40B ''tower'':58B ''view'':37B ''visibl'':55B ''warlock'':26B ''windhelm'':10B,43B', 'eastmarch', 'Morvunskar is a small fort located southwest of Windhelm in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('transmute_mineral_ore', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Alteration spells that transform iron ore into silver ore and silver ore into gold ore. This effect is only available as a spell, offering resourceful adventurers a way to increase the value of raw materials for crafting or trade.', '''adventur'':36B ''alter'':11B ''avail'':30B ''craft'':47B ''effect'':6B,27B ''focus'':10B ''gold'':24B ''increas'':40B ''iron'':15B ''magic'':5B ''materi'':45B ''miner'':2A ''offer'':34B ''ore'':3A,16B,19B,22B,25B ''raw'':44B ''resourc'':35B ''silver'':18B,21B ''spell'':12B,33B ''trade'':49B ''transform'':14B ''transmut'':1A ''util'':9B ''utility-focus'':8B ''valu'':42B ''way'':38B', 'mage', 'This spell turns iron into silver and silver into gold, useful for making money or fancy things. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonscale_shield', 'Dragonscale Shield has brilliant protection quality. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. To craft it: 4 dragon scales, 2 iron ingots, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dragonbone at a workbench.', '''2'':31B,35B ''4'':28B ''appear'':24B ''blacksmith'':40B ''bone'':19B ''brilliant'':6B ''craft'':16B,26B,46B ''design'':11B ''dragon'':18B,29B ''dragonbon'':54B ''dragonscal'':1A,3B ''forg'':41B ''ingot'':33B ''iron'':32B ''jag'':15B ''leather'':36B ''master'':43B ''organ'':23B ''pale'':13B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''rough'':22B ''scale'':30B ''shield'':2A,4B ''smith'':44B ''strip'':37B ''tempered/improved'':51B ''use'':53B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':57B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragonscale Shield has brilliant protection quality. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('turn_greater_undead', 'Turn Greater Undead is a Restoration spell that causes powerful undead creatures, such as Draugr Deathlords and Liches, to flee in terror, rendering them temporarily neutralized. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''cast'':37B ''caus'':12B ''creatur'':15B ''deathlord'':19B ''draugr'':18B ''expert'':33B ''flee'':23B ''greater'':2A,5B ''level'':35B ''lich'':21B ''neutral'':29B ''power'':13B ''render'':26B ''requir'':31B ''restor'':9B ''skill'':34B ''spell'':10B ''temporarili'':28B ''terror'':25B ''turn'':1A,4B ''undead'':3A,6B,14B', 'mage', 'Repel Undead is a spell that forces undead creatures to flee in terror, effectively neutralizing them for a short period. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_unarmed_damage', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration enchantments that increase the damage dealt with unarmed attacks. This effect is available through custom enchanting and can also be found on enchanted gear, making it highly sought after by brawlers and monks who rely on their fists in combat.', '''also'':30B ''attack'':20B ''avail'':24B ''brawler'':42B ''combat'':51B ''custom'':26B ''damag'':3A,16B ''dealt'':17B ''effect'':6B,22B ''enchant'':12B,27B,34B ''fist'':49B ''focus'':10B ''fortifi'':1A ''found'':32B ''gear'':35B ''high'':38B ''increas'':14B ''magic'':5B ''make'':36B ''monk'':44B ''reli'':46B ''restor'':11B ''sought'':39B ''unarm'':2A,19B ''util'':9B ''utility-focus'':8B', 'mage', 'This magic makes unarmed attacks stronger, useful for brawlers who fight with their fists. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('goat', '
Goats are non-aggressive animals found on mountain slopes in Skyrim. Goats are hunted for their hides, meat, and horns.', '''aggress'':6B ''anim'':7B ''found'':8B ''goat'':1A,2B,14B ''hide'':19B ''horn'':22B ''hunt'':16B ''meat'':20B ''mountain'':10B ''non'':5B ''non-aggress'':4B ''skyrim'':13B ''slope'':11B', 'hunter', 'Goats are non-aggressive animals found on mountain slopes in Skyrim.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('unknown_potion', 'This is a mysterious potion that appears when mixing ingredients with unknown effects. Its purpose is experimental, and it cannot be obtained normally.', '''appear'':9B ''cannot'':22B ''effect'':15B ''experiment'':19B ''ingredi'':12B ''mix'':11B ''mysteri'':6B ''normal'':25B ''obtain'':24B ''potion'':2A,7B ''purpos'':17B ''unknown'':1A,14B', 'blocked', 'You have no knowledge of this potion or its effects. You guess that''s why it''s called ''unknown''.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ustengrav_puzzle', 'Three rounded stones are found in a staggered row in front of a portcullis gate. The stones glow red and making a chiming noise when you stand close to them. When all three stones are active, the portcullis opens for a few seconds.
Solution: You must use the Whirlwind Sprint shout to move quickly enough to pass under the portcullis before it closes.', '''activ'':38B ''chime'':25B ''close'':30B,65B ''enough'':57B ''found'':7B ''front'':13B ''gate'':17B ''glow'':20B ''make'':23B ''move'':55B ''must'':48B ''nois'':26B ''open'':41B ''pass'':59B ''portculli'':16B,40B,62B ''puzzl'':2A ''quick'':56B ''red'':21B ''round'':4B ''row'':11B ''second'':45B ''shout'':53B ''solut'':46B ''sprint'':52B ''stagger'':10B ''stand'':29B ''stone'':5B,19B,36B ''three'':3B,35B ''use'':49B ''ustengrav'':1A ''whirlwind'':51B', 'scholar', 'You have no idea what this puzzle is or how to solze it.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mount_moesring', 'Mount Moesring is one of the highest and most prominent peaks on Solstheim, located south of Moesring Pass. The mountain dominates the surrounding landscape, offering a striking view of Solstheim''s rugged terrain and snow-covered wilderness.', '''cover'':39B ''domin'':23B ''highest'':9B ''landscap'':26B ''locat'':16B ''moesr'':2A,4B,19B ''mount'':1A,3B ''mountain'':22B ''offer'':27B ''one'':6B ''pass'':20B ''peak'':13B ''promin'':12B ''rug'':34B ''snow'':38B ''snow-cov'':37B ''solstheim'':15B,32B ''south'':17B ''strike'':29B ''surround'':25B ''terrain'':35B ''view'':30B ''wilder'':40B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('headwaters_of_harstrad', 'The Headwaters of Harstrad are the source of the Harstrad River, located in the northeastern region of Solstheim. The headwaters can be found a short distance downhill to the southeast from the entrance to Benkongerike or by following the river upstream from the Wind Stone, situated to the west-southwest.', '''benkongerik'':38B ''distanc'':29B ''downhil'':30B ''entranc'':36B ''follow'':41B ''found'':26B ''harstrad'':3A,7B,13B ''headwat'':1A,5B,23B ''locat'':15B ''northeastern'':18B ''region'':19B ''river'':14B,43B ''short'':28B ''situat'':49B ''solstheim'':21B ''sourc'':10B ''southeast'':33B ''southwest'':54B ''stone'':48B ''upstream'':44B ''west'':53B ''west-southwest'':52B ''wind'':47B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('resist_shock', 'These magical effects are defensive Restoration abilities that reduce damage taken from shock-based attacks, shielding the caster from electrical energy. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted items. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Resist Shock effect: Glow Dust, Glowing Mushroom, Hawk Feathers, Snowberries', '''abil'':9B ''also'':42B ''appli'':44B ''attack'':18B ''avail'':28B ''base'':17B ''brew'':36B ''caster'':21B ''combin'':49B ''craft'':32B ''creat'':63B ''custom'':38B ''damag'':12B ''defens'':7B ''dust'':72B ''effect'':5B,26B,61B,70B ''electr'':23B ''enchant'':46B ''energi'':24B ''feather'':76B ''follow'':55B ''general'':48B ''glow'':71B,73B ''hawk'':75B ''ingredi'':56B ''item'':47B ''least'':51B ''magic'':4B ''mushroom'':74B ''potion'':33B,39B,65B ''pre'':31B ''pre-craft'':30B ''provid'':57B ''reduc'':11B ''resist'':1A,68B ''restor'':8B ''share'':59B ''shield'':19B ''shock'':2A,16B,69B ''shock-bas'':15B ''snowberri'':77B ''taken'':13B ''two'':52B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic protects you from shock damage, keeping you safe from lightning attacks. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nchardak', 'Nchardak is a large and historically significant Dwarven ruin located north-northeast of Tel Mithryn and east of Ashfallow Citadel on Solstheim. Once known as the "City of a Hundred Towers," Nchardak was the largest and most advanced of the great Dwemer archives, renowned for its ingenuity and the scale of its operations.

According to legend, when Nords besieged the city, the Dwemer used their technological prowess to submerge the entire complex beneath the sea, forcing the Nords to abandon their siege. At its peak, the great workshops of Nchardak were capable of producing a complete automaton each day, supplying much of the Dwemer army that fought in the Battle of Red Mountain.

Today, much of Nchardak remains flooded, but its ancient mechanisms can still be activated using control cubes found within the ruin. These mechanisms, including the pumps that can drain water from key sections of the complex, reveal glimpses of the Dwemer’s unparalleled engineering. ', '''abandon'':82B ''accord'':56B ''activ'':129B ''advanc'':40B ''ancient'':124B ''archiv'':45B ''armi'':107B ''ashfallow'':21B ''automaton'':99B ''battl'':112B ''beneath'':75B ''besieg'':61B ''capabl'':94B ''citadel'':22B ''citi'':29B,63B ''complet'':98B ''complex'':74B,151B ''control'':131B ''cube'':132B ''day'':101B ''drain'':144B ''dwarven'':9B ''dwemer'':44B,65B,106B ''dwemer’'':156B ''east'':19B ''engin'':158B ''entir'':73B ''flood'':121B ''forc'':78B ''fought'':109B ''found'':133B ''glimps'':153B ''great'':43B,89B ''histor'':7B ''hundr'':32B ''includ'':139B ''ingenu'':49B ''key'':147B ''known'':26B ''larg'':5B ''largest'':37B ''legend'':58B ''locat'':11B ''mechan'':125B,138B ''mithryn'':17B ''mountain'':115B ''much'':103B,117B ''nchardak'':1A,2B,34B,92B,119B ''nord'':60B,80B ''north'':13B ''north-northeast'':12B ''northeast'':14B ''oper'':55B ''peak'':87B ''produc'':96B ''prowess'':69B ''pump'':141B ''red'':114B ''remain'':120B ''renown'':46B ''reveal'':152B ''ruin'':10B,136B ''scale'':52B ''sea'':77B ''section'':148B ''sieg'':84B ''signific'':8B ''solstheim'':24B ''still'':127B ''submerg'':71B ''suppli'':102B ''technolog'':68B ''tel'':16B ''today'':116B ''tower'':33B ''unparallel'':157B ''use'':66B,130B ''water'':145B ''within'':134B ''workshop'':90B', 'solstheim, dwemer, scholar', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ysolda''s_house', 'Ysolda''s House is a modest residence in Whiterun, tucked behind Arcadia''s Cauldron and Belethor''s General Goods. This simple home belongs to Ysolda, an ambitious local aspiring to become a prominent merchant in the city. She lives here alone, reflecting her independent and determined nature.', '''alon'':44B ''ambiti'':30B ''arcadia'':15B ''aspir'':32B ''becom'':34B ''behind'':14B ''belethor'':19B ''belong'':26B ''cauldron'':17B ''citi'':40B ''determin'':49B ''general'':21B ''good'':22B ''home'':25B ''hous'':3A,6B ''independ'':47B ''live'':42B ''local'':31B ''merchant'':37B ''modest'':9B ''natur'':50B ''promin'':36B ''reflect'':45B ''resid'':10B ''simpl'':24B ''tuck'':13B ''whiterun'':12B ''ysolda'':1A,4B,28B', 'whiterun', 'Ysolda''s House is a modest residence in Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falkreath_imperial_camp', 'Falkreath Imperial Camp is a military encampment located east-northeast of Glenmoril Coven and north of Knifepoint Ridge in Falkreath Hold. ', '''camp'':3A,6B ''coven'':17B ''east'':13B ''east-northeast'':12B ''encamp'':10B ''falkreath'':1A,4B,24B ''glenmoril'':16B ''hold'':25B ''imperi'':2A,5B ''knifepoint'':21B ''locat'':11B ''militari'':9B ''north'':19B ''northeast'':14B ''ridg'':22B', 'falkreath, legion', 'Falkreath Imperial Camp is a military encampment in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('peak''s_shade_tower', 'Peak''s Shade Tower is a small, ruined Nordic tower located east of Falkreath and southwest of Pinewatch in Falkreath Hold.', '''east'':16B ''falkreath'':18B,24B ''hold'':25B ''locat'':15B ''nordic'':13B ''peak'':1A,5B ''pinewatch'':22B ''ruin'':12B ''shade'':3A,7B ''small'':11B ''southwest'':20B ''tower'':4A,8B,14B', 'falkreath', 'Peak''s Shade Tower is a small, ruined Nordic tower located east of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('goldbrand', 'Goldbrand is a legendary golden katana created by the dragons of the North and imbued with the power of the Daedric Prince Boethiah, capable of burning those it strikes. First bestowed upon the Nordic warrior Sivdur, an ancestor of the Battle-Born clan, the blade has been revered through history, with its significance documented by Yagrum Bagarn in Tamrielic Lore, spreading its legend across Tamriel.', '''across'':66B ''ancestor'':39B ''bagarn'':59B ''battl'':43B ''battle-born'':42B ''bestow'':32B ''blade'':47B ''boethiah'':24B ''born'':44B ''burn'':27B ''capabl'':25B ''clan'':45B ''creat'':8B ''daedric'':22B ''document'':56B ''dragon'':11B ''first'':31B ''goldbrand'':1A,2B ''golden'':6B ''histori'':52B ''imbu'':16B ''katana'':7B ''legend'':65B ''legendari'':5B ''lore'':62B ''nordic'':35B ''north'':14B ''power'':19B ''princ'':23B ''rever'':50B ''signific'':55B ''sivdur'':37B ''spread'':63B ''strike'':30B ''tamriel'':61B,67B ''upon'':33B ''warrior'':36B ''yagrum'':58B', 'daedra, daedric, scholar', '
Goldbrand is a legendary golden katana created by Northern dragons and imbued with Boethiah''s power, capable of burning enemies. First given to the Nordic warrior Sivdur, its legacy is documented in Tamrielic Lore and revered across Tamriel.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('geirmund''s_hall', 'Geirmund''s Hall is a small Nordic ruin located on an island in the middle of Lake Geir, east of Ivarstead and west-southwest of Nilheim in the Rift. ', '''east'':22B ''geir'':21B ''geirmund'':1A,4B ''hall'':3A,6B ''island'':15B ''ivarstead'':24B ''lake'':20B ''locat'':12B ''middl'':18B ''nilheim'':30B ''nordic'':10B ''rift'':33B ''ruin'':11B ''small'':9B ''southwest'':28B ''west'':27B ''west-southwest'':26B', 'rift', 'Geirmund''s Hall is a small Nordic ruin located on an island in the middle of Lake Geir. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
