INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('eastmarch', 'Eastmarch is a hold in eastern Skyrim, with its capital in Windhelm, located in the northeastern corner of the province. It is bordered by Winterhold to the northwest, the Pale and Whiterun Hold to the west, the Throat of the World to the southwest, and the Rift to the south. The eastern border connects to Morrowind via the Velothi Mountain passes, making Eastmarch an important gateway for trade and migration. Since the Red Year, the hold has seen an increased presence of Dunmer, especially in Windhelm.

The hold is home to Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak, leader of the Stormcloak rebellion. Eastmarch''s diverse landscape includes sulfur pools and rocky crags in the central and southern regions, bordered by the Velothi Mountains, while the northern parts feature snowy tundra and icy terrain. The Darkwater and White Rivers carve through the hold, converging at Windhelm before flowing into the Sea of Ghosts.

Flora and fauna in Eastmarch reflect its varied geography. The sulfur pools are home to creatures like giants, sabre cats, and Jazbay grapes, while the snowy regions feature frost trolls, snowy sabre cats, and snowberry bushes. Pine forests and shrublands surrounding the pools host thistle, mountain flowers, and mora tapinella. Key roads form a north-south loop skirting the sulfur pools, with branches leading to the Rift, Whiterun, and beyond. Eastmarch''s harsh beauty, rich resources, and strategic position make it a vital and contested region in Skyrim.', '''beauti'':225B ''beyond'':221B ''border'':24B,54B,117B ''branch'':214B ''bush'':186B ''capit'':11B ''carv'':137B ''cat'':170B,183B ''central'':113B ''connect'':55B ''contest'':236B ''converg'':141B ''corner'':18B ''crag'':110B ''creatur'':166B ''darkwat'':133B ''divers'':103B ''dunmer'':84B ''eastern'':7B,53B ''eastmarch'':1A,2B,64B,101B,155B,222B ''especi'':85B ''fauna'':153B ''featur'':126B,178B ''flora'':151B ''flow'':145B ''flower'':197B ''forest'':188B ''form'':203B ''frost'':179B ''gateway'':67B ''geographi'':159B ''ghost'':150B ''giant'':168B ''grape'':173B ''harsh'':224B ''hold'':5B,34B,77B,89B,140B ''home'':91B,164B ''host'':194B ''ici'':130B ''import'':66B ''includ'':105B ''increas'':81B ''jarl'':93B ''jazbay'':172B ''key'':201B ''landscap'':104B ''lead'':215B ''leader'':96B ''like'':167B ''locat'':14B ''loop'':208B ''make'':63B,231B ''migrat'':71B ''mora'':199B ''morrowind'':57B ''mountain'':61B,121B,196B ''north'':206B ''north-south'':205B ''northeastern'':17B ''northern'':124B ''northwest'':29B ''pale'':31B ''part'':125B ''pass'':62B ''pine'':187B ''pool'':107B,162B,193B,212B ''posit'':230B ''presenc'':82B ''provinc'':21B ''rebellion'':100B ''red'':74B ''reflect'':156B ''region'':116B,177B,237B ''resourc'':227B ''rich'':226B ''rift'':48B,218B ''river'':136B ''road'':202B ''rocki'':109B ''sabr'':169B,182B ''sea'':148B ''seen'':79B ''shrubland'':190B ''sinc'':72B ''skirt'':209B ''skyrim'':8B,239B ''snowberri'':185B ''snowi'':127B,176B,181B ''south'':51B,207B ''southern'':115B ''southwest'':45B ''stormcloak'':95B,99B ''strateg'':229B ''sulfur'':106B,161B,211B ''surround'':191B ''tapinella'':200B ''terrain'':131B ''thistl'':195B ''throat'':39B ''trade'':69B ''troll'':180B ''tundra'':128B ''ulfric'':94B ''vari'':158B ''velothi'':60B,120B ''via'':58B ''vital'':234B ''west'':37B ''white'':135B ''whiterun'':33B,219B ''windhelm'':13B,87B,143B ''winterhold'':26B ''world'':42B ''year'':75B', 'eastmarch, noble, scholar', 'Eastmarch is a hold in northeastern Skyrim, with Windhelm as its capital. It borders Winterhold to the northwest, the Pale and Whiterun Hold to the west, the Throat of the World to the southwest, and the Rift to the south. Its eastern border connects to Morrowind, making it a key area for trade and migration, especially after the Red Year when the presence of Dunmer increased, particularly in Windhelm.

The landscape of Eastmarch is diverse, featuring sulfur pools, rocky crags, and snowy tundra. The region is home to Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak and is traversed by the Darkwater and White Rivers, which converge at Windhelm before flowing into the Sea of Ghosts. Eastmarch''s wildlife includes giants, sabre cats, frost trolls, and snowberry bushes. The roads connect key areas, including the Rift and Whiterun, highlighting Eastmarch’s strategic importance in Skyrim.', '', '', 'eastmarch');
