Varieties of Faith in the Empire, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, explores the pantheons and deities worshiped across Tamriel''s cultures, examining their significance and varying roles in different societies. The book delves into themes of divine hierarchy, cultural influence, and the fluidity of religious beliefs, highlighting the complexity and diversity of faith throughout the Empire.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('yngol_and_the_sea-ghosts', 'Yngol and the Sea-Ghosts, written by an unknown author, is a tale that recounts Ysgramor''s first adventure in Tamriel, focusing on the tragic fate of his kinsman Yngol. The story begins with Ysgramor and his people landing on the rocky shores of Hsaarik Head, having traveled from Atmora. However, Ysgramor’s kin, including Yngol, are taken by the mysterious and vengeful sea-ghosts. Determined to rescue his people, Ysgramor rows into a violent storm, battling the spirits of the sea for two weeks. Eventually, the storm subsides, but Yngol and his companions are lost, their bodies found washed ashore.

The book explores themes of grief, vengeance, and the harsh realities of the world Ysgramor and his people inhabited. It also touches on the bonds of kinship and the early struggles of the Nords as they set foot in Tamriel. Ysgramor’s grief drives him to avenge his fallen kin by slaying beasts and giving them a proper burial, honoring the tradition of his people. This tale is part of the larger history of Ysgramor’s early days in Tamriel and serves as a pivotal moment in the mythic history of the Nords. It is contained within a single volume.', '''adventur'':26B ''also'':129B ''ashor'':108B ''atmora'':57B ''author'':17B ''aveng'':154B ''battl'':84B ''beast'':160B ''begin'':40B ''bodi'':105B ''bond'':133B ''book'':110B ''burial'':166B ''companion'':101B ''contain'':202B ''day'':184B ''determin'':73B ''drive'':151B ''earli'':138B,183B ''eventu'':93B ''explor'':111B ''fallen'':156B ''fate'':33B ''first'':25B ''focus'':29B ''foot'':146B ''found'':106B ''ghost'':6A,12B,72B ''give'':162B ''grief'':114B,150B ''harsh'':118B ''head'':53B ''histori'':180B,196B ''honor'':167B ''howev'':58B ''hsaarik'':52B ''includ'':61B ''inhabit'':127B ''kin'':60B,157B ''kinship'':135B ''kinsman'':36B ''land'':46B ''larger'':179B ''lost'':103B ''moment'':192B ''mysteri'':67B ''mythic'':195B ''nord'':142B,199B ''part'':176B ''peopl'':45B,77B,126B,172B ''pivot'':191B ''proper'':165B ''realiti'':119B ''recount'':22B ''rescu'':75B ''rocki'':49B ''row'':79B ''sea'':5A,11B,71B,89B ''sea-ghost'':4A,10B,70B ''serv'':188B ''set'':145B ''shore'':50B ''singl'':205B ''slay'':159B ''spirit'':86B ''stori'':39B ''storm'':83B,95B ''struggl'':139B ''subsid'':96B ''taken'':64B ''tale'':20B,174B ''tamriel'':28B,148B,186B ''theme'':112B ''touch'':130B ''tradit'':169B ''tragic'':32B ''travel'':55B ''two'':91B ''unknown'':16B ''veng'':69B ''vengeanc'':115B ''violent'':82B ''volum'':206B ''wash'':107B ''week'':92B ''within'':203B ''world'':122B ''written'':13B ''yngol'':1A,7B,37B,62B,98B ''ysgramor'':23B,42B,78B,123B ''ysgramor’'':59B,149B,182B', 'scholar', '
Yngol and the Sea-Ghosts, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, delves into themes of grief, vengeance, and kinship, recounting Ysgramor''s tragic loss of his kinsman Yngol to vengeful sea-ghosts. The tale highlights the early struggles of the Nords in Tamriel and their enduring traditions of honor and remembrance.', '', '', 'lore');
