Sithis is a primordial force of chaos and change, worshiped mainly by the Dark Brotherhood, who believe that the souls of those killed in his name are sent to the Void. He is the personification of the Void and plays a key role in creation myths, including the birth of the world and Lorkhan. ', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cats_of_skyrim', '
Cats of Skyrim, written by Aldetuile, offers an account of the few feline species that inhabit the cold wilderness of Skyrim. The author’s primary focus is on the indigenous sabrecat, a large and dangerous predator with distinct physical adaptations, such as sharp front teeth and varied fur patterns. The common sabrecat features reddish-brown fur, while its snowy counterpart has spotted white fur, likely for stalking prey in snow-covered regions. These creatures use a combination of biting, clawing, and pouncing in their attacks.

The book also briefly mentions Khajiit outcasts living in Skyrim, though they remain elusive and unhelpful to the author’s research. The text highlights the practical uses of sabrecat pelts and teeth, which can be salvaged for crafting and alchemical purposes, such as creating stamina-restoring potions. Themes of adaptation, survival, and utility underscore this brief treatise, as the author reflects on the harsh and unwelcoming environment that shapes both predator and prey in Skyrim.', '''account'':12B ''adapt'':42B,139B ''alchem'':128B ''aldetuil'':9B ''also'':92B ''attack'':89B ''author'':149B ''author’'':26B,108B ''bite'':83B ''book'':91B ''brief'':145B ''briefli'':93B ''brown'':58B ''cat'':1A,4B ''claw'':84B ''cold'':21B ''combin'':81B ''common'':53B ''counterpart'':63B ''cover'':75B ''craft'':126B ''creat'':132B ''creatur'':78B ''danger'':37B ''distinct'':40B ''elus'':103B ''environ'':156B ''featur'':55B ''felin'':16B ''focus'':28B ''front'':46B ''fur'':50B,59B,67B ''harsh'':153B ''highlight'':112B ''indigen'':32B ''inhabit'':19B ''khajiit'':95B ''larg'':35B ''like'':68B ''live'':97B ''mention'':94B ''offer'':10B ''outcast'':96B ''pattern'':51B ''pelt'':118B ''physic'':41B ''potion'':136B ''pounc'':86B ''practic'':114B ''predat'':38B,160B ''prey'':71B,162B ''primari'':27B ''purpos'':129B ''reddish'':57B ''reddish-brown'':56B ''reflect'':150B ''region'':76B ''remain'':102B ''research'':109B ''restor'':135B ''sabrecat'':33B,54B,117B ''salvag'':124B ''shape'':158B ''sharp'':45B ''skyrim'':3A,6B,24B,99B,164B ''snow'':74B ''snow-cov'':73B ''snowi'':62B ''speci'':17B ''spot'':65B ''stalk'':70B ''stamina'':134B ''stamina-restor'':133B ''surviv'':140B ''teeth'':47B,120B ''text'':111B ''theme'':137B ''though'':100B ''treatis'':146B ''underscor'':143B ''unhelp'':105B ''unwelcom'':155B ''use'':79B,115B ''util'':142B ''vari'':49B ''white'':66B ''wilder'':22B ''written'':7B', 'scholar', '
Cats of Skyrim, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, provides an account of feline species in Skyrim, focusing on the sabrecat and its adaptations to the harsh environment. Themes of adaptation, survival, and the practical utility of these creatures for crafting and alchemy are explored throughout the text.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('proudspire_manor', 'Proudspire Manor is a three-story house located in Solitude, and it is the most expensive house available for purchase in Skyrim. The manor offers expansive living space, with elegant furnishings and a prime location within the city, overlooking the surrounding area.', '''area'':45B ''avail'':21B ''citi'':41B ''eleg'':33B ''expans'':29B ''expens'':19B ''furnish'':34B ''hous'':10B,20B ''live'':30B ''locat'':11B,38B ''manor'':2A,4B,27B ''offer'':28B ''overlook'':42B ''prime'':37B ''proudspir'':1A,3B ''purchas'':23B ''skyrim'':25B ''solitud'':13B ''space'':31B ''stori'':9B ''surround'':44B ''three'':8B ''three-stori'':7B ''within'':39B', 'haafingar', 'Proudspire Manor is a three-story house located in Solitude, and it is the most expensive house available for purchase in Skyrim. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('temple_of_the_divines', 'The Temple of the Divines is the main temple of Solitude and Skyrim, housing shrines dedicated to the Eight Divines. The temple serves as a place of worship and is an important religious site in the city.

It is located on the eastern side of Castle Dour''s courtyard, northwest of the Blue Palace in Solitude. The temple is a central location for those seeking spiritual guidance or wishing to honor the Divines, and it is a peaceful contrast to the bustling political and military activity surrounding Castle Dour.', '''activ'':90B ''blue'':57B ''bustl'':86B ''castl'':50B,92B ''central'':65B ''citi'':41B ''contrast'':83B ''courtyard'':53B ''dedic'':20B ''divin'':4A,9B,24B,77B ''dour'':51B,93B ''eastern'':47B ''eight'':23B ''guidanc'':71B ''honor'':75B ''hous'':18B ''import'':36B ''locat'':44B,66B ''main'':12B ''militari'':89B ''northwest'':54B ''palac'':58B ''peac'':82B ''place'':30B ''polit'':87B ''religi'':37B ''seek'':69B ''serv'':27B ''shrine'':19B ''side'':48B ''site'':38B ''skyrim'':17B ''solitud'':15B,60B ''spiritu'':70B ''surround'':91B ''templ'':1A,6B,13B,26B,62B ''wish'':73B ''worship'':32B', 'haafingar, priest', 'The Temple of the Divines is the main temple of Solitude and Skyrim, housing shrines dedicated to the Eight Divines. The temple serves as a place of worship and is an important religious site in the city. You do not know who runs the temples.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nightgate_inn', 'Nightgate Inn is a remote inn located west of Windhelm and east of Shrouded Grove in The Pale

The inn is run by Hadring, a Nord warrior who serves as its proprietor. Nightgate Inn is a quiet, secluded location, offering respite to travelers navigating the harsh, snowy terrain of the region. Its isolation adds to its charm, providing a peaceful retreat far from the hustle and bustle of Skyrim''s cities.', '''add'':56B ''bustl'':69B ''charm'':59B ''citi'':73B ''east'':14B ''far'':64B ''grove'':17B ''hadr'':26B ''harsh'':48B ''hustl'':67B ''inn'':2A,4B,8B,22B,36B ''isol'':55B ''locat'':9B,41B ''navig'':46B ''nightgat'':1A,3B,35B ''nord'':28B ''offer'':42B ''pale'':20B ''peac'':62B ''proprietor'':34B ''provid'':60B ''quiet'':39B ''region'':53B ''remot'':7B ''respit'':43B ''retreat'':63B ''run'':24B ''seclud'':40B ''serv'':31B ''shroud'':16B ''skyrim'':71B ''snowi'':49B ''terrain'':50B ''travel'':45B ''warrior'':29B ''west'':10B ''windhelm'':12B', 'pale, traveler, innkeeper', '"Nightgate Inn is a remote inn located west of Windhelm  in The Pale. You do not know who runs the inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('resist_frost', 'These magical effects are defensive Restoration abilities that reduce damage taken from frost-based attacks, offering vital protection in Skyrim;s icy environments. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted items. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Resist Frost effect: Frost Mirriam, Frost Salts, Purple Mountain Flower, Snowberries, Thistle Branch', '''abil'':9B ''also'':44B ''appli'':46B ''attack'':18B ''avail'':30B ''base'':17B ''branch'':82B ''brew'':38B ''combin'':51B ''craft'':34B ''creat'':65B ''custom'':40B ''damag'':12B ''defens'':7B ''effect'':5B,28B,63B,72B ''enchant'':48B ''environ'':26B ''flower'':79B ''follow'':57B ''frost'':2A,16B,71B,73B,75B ''frost-bas'':15B ''general'':50B ''ici'':25B ''ingredi'':58B ''item'':49B ''least'':53B ''magic'':4B ''mirriam'':74B ''mountain'':78B ''offer'':19B ''potion'':35B,41B,67B ''pre'':33B ''pre-craft'':32B ''protect'':21B ''provid'':59B ''purpl'':77B ''reduc'':11B ''resist'':1A,70B ''restor'':8B ''salt'':76B ''share'':61B ''skyrim'':23B ''snowberri'':80B ''taken'':13B ''thistl'':81B ''two'':54B ''vital'':20B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic protects you from frost damage, helping you stay safe in icy areas. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('windpeak_inn', 'Windpeak Inn is a cozy inn located in Dawnstar, conveniently situated as the first building you''ll encounter when entering the town from the main road. The inn is run by Thoring, who manages the establishment, rents out rooms, and offers food and drinks to travelers and locals alike.

Karita, Thoring''s daughter, serves as the inn''s bard, providing music and entertainment to patrons. ', '''alik'':51B ''bard'':61B ''build'':17B ''conveni'':12B ''cozi'':7B ''daughter'':55B ''dawnstar'':11B ''drink'':46B ''encount'':20B ''enter'':22B ''entertain'':65B ''establish'':38B ''first'':16B ''food'':44B ''inn'':2A,4B,8B,30B,59B ''karita'':52B ''ll'':19B ''local'':50B ''locat'':9B ''main'':27B ''manag'':36B ''music'':63B ''offer'':43B ''patron'':67B ''provid'':62B ''rent'':39B ''road'':28B ''room'':41B ''run'':32B ''serv'':56B ''situat'':13B ''thore'':34B,53B ''town'':24B ''travel'':48B ''windpeak'':1A,3B', 'pale, innkeeper, traveler', 'Windpeak Inn is an inn located in Dawnstar. You do not know who runs the Inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('firebolt', 'Firebolt is a Destruction spell that hurls a single bolt of fire at a target, dealing immediate fire damage upon impact. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':26B ''bolt'':11B ''cast'':30B ''damag'':20B ''deal'':17B ''destruct'':5B ''fire'':13B,19B ''firebolt'':1A,2B ''hurl'':8B ''immedi'':18B ''impact'':22B ''level'':28B ''requir'':24B ''singl'':10B ''skill'':27B ''spell'':6B ''target'':16B ''upon'':21B', 'mage', 'Firebolt is a spell that launches a single bolt of fire at a target, causing immediate fire damage upon impact. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('malachite', 'Malachite is a rare volcanic crystal known for its distinctive milky translucent green color and its ability to absorb magicka under certain conditions. It is primarily utilized in crafting lightweight yet strong armor and weapons, making it a favored material among skilled artisans. Though less durable than ebony, malachite boasts a higher melting point and is significantly stronger than common glass, which it is often mistakenly associated with. The most abundant sources of malachite are found on the volcanic island of Vvardenfell in Morrowind, but ore veins are also distributed across Tamriel.', '''abil'':18B ''absorb'':20B ''abund'':72B ''across'':92B ''also'':90B ''among'':42B ''armor'':34B ''artisan'':44B ''associ'':68B ''boast'':51B ''certain'':23B ''color'':15B ''common'':61B ''condit'':24B ''craft'':30B ''crystal'':7B ''distinct'':11B ''distribut'':91B ''durabl'':47B ''eboni'':49B ''favor'':40B ''found'':77B ''glass'':62B ''green'':14B ''higher'':53B ''island'':81B ''known'':8B ''less'':46B ''lightweight'':31B ''magicka'':21B ''make'':37B ''malachit'':1A,2B,50B,75B ''materi'':41B ''melt'':54B ''milki'':12B ''mistaken'':67B ''morrowind'':85B ''often'':66B ''ore'':87B ''point'':55B ''primarili'':27B ''rare'':5B ''signific'':58B ''skill'':43B ''sourc'':73B ''strong'':33B ''stronger'':59B ''tamriel'':93B ''though'':45B ''transluc'':13B ''util'':28B ''vein'':88B ''volcan'':6B,80B ''vvardenfel'':83B ''weapon'':36B ''yet'':32B', 'blacksmith, darkelf', 'Malachite is a rare volcanic crystal known for its distinctive milky translucent green color and its ability to absorb magicka. I.t is primarily utilized in crafting lightweight yet strong armor and weapons.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bthardamz', 'Bthardamz is a large Dwarven ruin located west-northwest of Karthwasten and south-southeast of Deep Folk Crossing in the Reach. The ruin is inhabited by the Afflicted, followers of Peryite. To reach Bthardamz from the Shrine to Peryite, head west to find a path, then follow it north, west, and finally south. The entrance is marked by two wide stairways leading to a winding corridor that descends into the ruin', '''afflict'':31B ''bthardamz'':1A,2B,37B ''corridor'':69B ''cross'':21B ''deep'':19B ''descend'':71B ''dwarven'':6B ''entranc'':58B ''final'':55B ''find'':46B ''folk'':20B ''follow'':32B,50B ''head'':43B ''inhabit'':28B ''karthwasten'':13B ''larg'':5B ''lead'':65B ''locat'':8B ''mark'':60B ''north'':52B ''northwest'':11B ''path'':48B ''peryit'':34B,42B ''reach'':24B,36B ''ruin'':7B,26B,74B ''shrine'':40B ''south'':16B,56B ''south-southeast'':15B ''southeast'':17B ''stairway'':64B ''two'':62B ''west'':10B,44B,53B ''west-northwest'':9B ''wide'':63B ''wind'':68B', 'reach, dwemer', 'Bthardamz is a large Dwarven ruin located west-northwest of Karthwasten in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chillwind_depths', 'Chillwind Depths is a medium-sized cave located south of Dragon Bridge in Hjaalmarch. Nestled beside a small waterfall and pond, the cave is occupied by Falmer, making it a dangerous place for travelers.', '''besid'':19B ''bridg'':15B ''cave'':10B,26B ''chillwind'':1A,3B ''danger'':34B ''depth'':2A,4B ''dragon'':14B ''falmer'':30B ''hjaalmarch'':17B ''locat'':11B ''make'':31B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''nestl'':18B ''occupi'':28B ''place'':35B ''pond'':24B ''size'':9B ''small'':21B ''south'':12B ''travel'':37B ''waterfal'':22B', 'reach', 'Chillwind Depths is a medium-sized cave located south of Dragon Bridge in Hjaalmarch. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_lockpicking', 'A thief''s ally, this potion sharpens focus and dexterity, making locks yield more easily to a skilled hand. Slightly improves lockpicking ease, with higher-tier potions granting significant dexterity boosts. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':47B ''alli'':7B ''boost'':35B ''dexter'':13B,34B ''draught'':57B ''eas'':26B ''easili'':18B ''elixir'':60B ''focus'':11B ''found'':40B ''grant'':32B ''hand'':22B ''higher'':29B ''higher-ti'':28B ''improv'':24B ''lock'':15B ''lockpick'':3A,25B ''loot'':43B ''make'':14B ''philter'':58B ''potion'':1A,9B,31B,37B,56B ''purchas'':45B ''random'':42B ''sever'':50B ''sharpen'':10B ''signific'':33B ''skill'':21B ''slight'':23B ''strongest'':55B ''thief'':5B ''tier'':30B,51B ''weakest'':53B ''yield'':16B', 'thief, alchemist, darkbrotherhood, traveler, bard', 'The Potion of Lockpicking makes opening locks easier for a short time. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_true_shot', 'Beloved by archers, this potion increases bow damage, allowing for more lethal strikes from a distance. Enhances bow damage slightly, with higher tiers enabling more devastating ranged attacks. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':44B ''allow'':13B ''archer'':7B ''attack'':32B ''belov'':5B ''bow'':11B,22B ''damag'':12B,23B ''devast'':30B ''distanc'':20B ''draught'':54B ''elixir'':57B ''enabl'':28B ''enhanc'':21B ''found'':37B ''higher'':26B ''increas'':10B ''lethal'':16B ''loot'':40B ''philter'':55B ''potion'':1A,9B,34B,53B ''purchas'':42B ''random'':39B ''rang'':31B ''sever'':47B ''shot'':4A ''slight'':24B ''strike'':17B ''strongest'':52B ''tier'':27B,48B ''true'':3A ''weakest'':50B', 'archer, alchemist, hunter, companions, thief', 'The Potion of True Shot increases bow damage, making archers more deadly. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vision_of_the_tenth_eye', 'Vision of the Tenth Eye is an Alteration spell that allows the caster to see through solid walls, revealing hidden enemies and objects in their line of sight. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''allow'':16B ''alter'':13B ''cast'':41B ''caster'':18B ''enemi'':26B ''expert'':37B ''eye'':5A,10B ''hidden'':25B ''level'':39B ''line'':31B ''object'':28B ''requir'':35B ''reveal'':24B ''see'':20B ''sight'':33B ''skill'':38B ''solid'':22B ''spell'':14B ''tenth'':4A,9B ''vision'':1A,6B ''wall'':23B', 'mage', 'Vision of the Tenth Eye is a spell that allows the caster to see through solid walls, revealing hidden enemies and objects in their line of sight. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('smelter_overseer''s_house', 'Smelter Overseer''s House is a small residence in Markarth, home to Mulush gro-Shugurz, the Smelter Overseer, and his wife Urzoga gra-Shugurz. The house is tucked away behind a rocky outcropping, making it easy to miss, especially while standing in the smelting area.', '''area'':51B ''away'':35B ''behind'':36B ''easi'':42B ''especi'':45B ''gra'':29B ''gra-shugurz'':28B ''gro'':19B ''gro-shugurz'':18B ''home'':15B ''hous'':4A,8B,32B ''make'':40B ''markarth'':14B ''miss'':44B ''mulush'':17B ''outcrop'':39B ''overs'':2A,6B,23B ''resid'':12B ''rocki'':38B ''shugurz'':20B,30B ''small'':11B ''smelt'':50B ''smelter'':1A,5B,22B ''stand'':47B ''tuck'':34B ''urzoga'':27B ''wife'':26B', 'reach', 'Smelter Overseer''s House is a small residence in Markarth, you do not know who lives here.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_warrens', '
The Warrens is a shelter for the sick and homeless located in Markarth, hidden just a few feet from the Markarth Smelter. This area is home to the extreme lower-class citizens of the city, including miners, smelters, and those suffering from illness or injury.', '''area'':26B ''citi'':38B ''citizen'':35B ''class'':34B ''extrem'':31B ''feet'':20B ''hidden'':16B ''home'':28B ''homeless'':12B ''ill'':46B ''includ'':39B ''injuri'':48B ''locat'':13B ''lower'':33B ''lower-class'':32B ''markarth'':15B,23B ''miner'':40B ''shelter'':7B ''sick'':10B ''smelter'':24B,41B ''suffer'':44B ''warren'':2A,4B', 'reach', 'The Warrens is a shelter for the sick and homeless located in Markarth. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vlindrel_hall', 'Vlindrel Hall is a location at the southern edge of Markarth, nestled within the city''s towering stone structures. It sits on the second terrace, offering stunning views of the surrounding Reach and the bustling city below. The house is available for purchase.', '''avail'':43B ''bustl'':37B ''citi'':17B,38B ''edg'':11B ''hall'':2A,4B ''hous'':41B ''locat'':7B ''markarth'':13B ''nestl'':14B ''offer'':28B ''purchas'':45B ''reach'':34B ''second'':26B ''sit'':23B ''southern'':10B ''stone'':20B ''structur'':21B ''stun'':29B ''surround'':33B ''terrac'':27B ''tower'':19B ''view'':30B ''vlindrel'':1A,3B ''within'':15B', 'reach', 'Vlindrel Hall is a location at the southern edge of Markarth, nestled within the city''s towering stone structures. The house is available for purchase you have heard.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('morokei', '
Morokei, also known as the Deathless, was a powerful Dragon Priest in the Merethic Era who achieved lichdom through the worship of his draugr servants. Gifted a magical moonstone mask by his dragon overlord, he was immune to death except by the Thu''um of a dragon. After the Dragon War, he was sealed in the ruins of Bromjunaar, later known as Labyrinthian, by sacred fires to prevent him from seeking vengeance. Morokei was ultimately destroyed around 4E 201.', '''201'':80B ''4e'':79B ''achiev'':18B ''also'':3B ''around'':78B ''bromjunaar'':60B ''death'':40B ''deathless'':7B ''destroy'':77B ''dragon'':11B,34B,48B,51B ''draugr'':25B ''era'':16B ''except'':41B ''fire'':67B ''gift'':27B ''immun'':38B ''known'':4B,62B ''labyrinthian'':64B ''later'':61B ''lichdom'':19B ''magic'':29B ''mask'':31B ''mereth'':15B ''moonston'':30B ''morokei'':1A,2B,74B ''overlord'':35B ''power'':10B ''prevent'':69B ''priest'':12B ''ruin'':58B ''sacr'':66B ''seal'':55B ''seek'':72B ''servant'':26B ''thu'':44B ''ultim'':76B ''um'':45B ''vengeanc'':73B ''war'':52B ''worship'':22B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Morokei, must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('guardian_circle', 'Guardian Circle is a Restoration spell that creates a protective circle on the ground, healing allies within its area and damaging nearby undead. It requires a Master skill level to cast.', '''alli'':18B ''area'':21B ''cast'':33B ''circl'':2A,4B,13B ''creat'':10B ''damag'':23B ''ground'':16B ''guardian'':1A,3B ''heal'':17B ''level'':31B ''master'':29B ''nearbi'':24B ''protect'':12B ''requir'':27B ''restor'':7B ''skill'':30B ''spell'':8B ''undead'':25B ''within'':19B', 'mage', 'Guardian Circle is a spell that creates a protective circle on the ground, healing allies within its area and damaging nearby undead. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elsweyr', '
Elsweyr is a southern coastal region of Tamriel and the homeland of the feline Khajiit. The province is divided into two distinct climates: the dry savannahs and badlands of Anequina in the north, and the fertile jungles and rainforests of Pellitine in the south. Historically, the land was home to sixteen Khajiiti clans, which evolved into kingdoms named after their regions, but hardships such as the Thrassian Plague led to their consolidation into the two kingdoms of Anequina and Pellitine. These eventually united as the Elsweyr Confederacy, only to split again during the Third Aldmeri Dominion.

Elsweyr shares borders with Valenwood to the west, Cyrodiil to the north and east, and has access to Topal Bay and the Southern Sea to the south. Notable geographic features include Lake Vread in the eastern region and Khenarthi''s Roost, an island in the Southern Sea that is part of the province. The Khajiit’s unique culture and connection to their homeland make Elsweyr a vital and enigmatic part of Tamriel.', '''access'':114B ''aldmeri'':96B ''anequina'':31B,79B ''badland'':29B ''bay'':117B ''border'':100B ''clan'':54B ''climat'':24B ''coastal'':6B ''confederaci'':88B ''connect'':156B ''consolid'':73B ''cultur'':154B ''cyrodiil'':106B ''distinct'':23B ''divid'':20B ''dominion'':97B ''dri'':26B ''east'':111B ''eastern'':133B ''elsweyr'':1A,2B,87B,98B,161B ''enigmat'':165B ''eventu'':83B ''evolv'':56B ''featur'':127B ''felin'':15B ''fertil'':37B ''geograph'':126B ''hardship'':64B ''histor'':46B ''home'':50B ''homeland'':12B,159B ''includ'':128B ''island'':140B ''jungl'':38B ''khajiit'':16B ''khajiiti'':53B ''khajiit’'':152B ''khenarthi'':136B ''kingdom'':58B,77B ''lake'':129B ''land'':48B ''led'':70B ''make'':160B ''name'':59B ''north'':34B,109B ''notabl'':125B ''part'':147B,166B ''pellitin'':42B,81B ''plagu'':69B ''provinc'':18B,150B ''rainforest'':40B ''region'':7B,62B,134B ''roost'':138B ''savannah'':27B ''sea'':121B,144B ''share'':99B ''sixteen'':52B ''south'':45B,124B ''southern'':5B,120B,143B ''split'':91B ''tamriel'':9B,168B ''third'':95B ''thrassian'':68B ''topal'':116B ''two'':22B,76B ''uniqu'':153B ''unit'':84B ''valenwood'':102B ''vital'':163B ''vread'':130B ''west'':105B', 'scholar, khajiit', '
Elsweyr is a southern province of Tamriel, home to the feline Khajiit, divided into two regions: the dry savannahs of Anequina and the fertile jungles of Pellitine. Historically, the region was made up of sixteen Khajiiti clans that later merged into the kingdoms of Anequina and Pellitine, and eventually the Elsweyr Confederacy. The province shares borders with Valenwood, Cyrodiil, and the Southern Sea, and features landmarks like Lake Vread and Khenarthi''s Roost. Elsweyr’s unique culture and geography make it an important and mysterious part of Tamriel.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('markarth', 'Markarth is a major city located in the southwest of Skyrim, near the border of High Rock, and serves as the capital of the Reach. Built within an ancient Dwemer city, its architecture is strikingly unique, with much of it carved into the surrounding rock. Jarl Igmund, the ruler, struggles with the Forsworn, a militant group that infests the surrounding countryside, attacking travelers and threatening the hold. The people of Markarth are wary of outsiders, with the city guards treating them with suspicion and hostility.

The Silver-Blood family holds significant influence in Markarth, owning half the city, including the Silver-Blood Inn and Cidhna Mine, a notorious prison considered the most secure in Skyrim. The city’s poor live in The Warrens, a cliffside area of extreme poverty, with many working in the mines and smelters. Near the city entrance, an open-air marketplace hosts several shops, while the guards are stationed in a Dwemer dormitory beneath the central Guard Tower.

Markarth is also home to Understone Keep, the ancient Dwemer castle and seat of government located at the western end of the city. Other notable locations include the Temple of Dibella, the Hag''s Cure, Arnleif and Sons Trading Company, and Salvius Farm. ', '''air'':147B ''also'':168B ''ancient'':30B,174B ''architectur'':34B ''area'':128B ''arnleif'':201B ''attack'':63B ''beneath'':161B ''blood'':90B,105B ''border'':15B ''built'':27B ''capit'':23B ''carv'':42B ''castl'':176B ''central'':163B ''cidhna'':108B ''citi'':6B,32B,79B,100B,142B,188B ''city’'':120B ''cliffsid'':127B ''compani'':205B ''consid'':113B ''countrysid'':62B ''cure'':200B ''dibella'':196B ''dormitori'':160B ''dwemer'':31B,159B,175B ''end'':185B ''entranc'':143B ''extrem'':130B ''famili'':91B ''farm'':208B ''forsworn'':54B ''govern'':180B ''group'':57B ''guard'':80B,154B,164B ''hag'':198B ''half'':98B ''high'':17B ''hold'':68B,92B ''home'':169B ''host'':149B ''hostil'':86B ''igmund'':48B ''includ'':101B,192B ''infest'':59B ''influenc'':94B ''inn'':106B ''jarl'':47B ''keep'':172B ''live'':122B ''locat'':7B,181B,191B ''major'':5B ''mani'':133B ''markarth'':1A,2B,72B,96B,166B ''marketplac'':148B ''milit'':56B ''mine'':109B,137B ''much'':39B ''near'':13B,140B ''notabl'':190B ''notori'':111B ''open'':146B ''open-air'':145B ''outsid'':76B ''own'':97B ''peopl'':70B ''poor'':121B ''poverti'':131B ''prison'':112B ''reach'':26B ''rock'':18B,46B ''ruler'':50B ''salvius'':207B ''seat'':178B ''secur'':116B ''serv'':20B ''sever'':150B ''shop'':151B ''signific'':93B ''silver'':89B,104B ''silver-blood'':88B,103B ''skyrim'':12B,118B ''smelter'':139B ''son'':203B ''southwest'':10B ''station'':156B ''strike'':36B ''struggl'':51B ''surround'':45B,61B ''suspicion'':84B ''templ'':194B ''threaten'':66B ''tower'':165B ''trade'':204B ''travel'':64B ''treat'':81B ''underston'':171B ''uniqu'':37B ''wari'':74B ''warren'':125B ''western'':184B ''within'':28B ''work'':134B', 'reach, noble, scholar', 'Markarth is a major city located in the southwest of Skyrim, near the border of High Rock, and serves as the capital of the Reach. Built within an ancient Dwemer city, its architecture is strikingly unique, with much of it carved into the surrounding rock. Jarl Igmund, the ruler, struggles with the Forsworn, a militant group that infests the surrounding countryside, attacking travelers and threatening the hold. The people of Markarth are wary of outsiders, with the city guards treating them with suspicion and hostility.

The Silver-Blood family holds significant influence in Markarth, owning half the city, including the Silver-Blood Inn and Cidhna Mine, a notorious prison considered the most secure in Skyrim. The city’s poor live in The Warrens, a cliffside area of extreme poverty, with many working in the mines and smelters. Near the city entrance, an open-air marketplace hosts several shops, while the guards are stationed in a Dwemer dormitory beneath the central Guard Tower.

Markarth is also home to Understone Keep, the ancient Dwemer castle and seat of government located at the western end of the city.', '', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('restore_magicka', 'These magical effects are restorative Restoration abilities that instantly replenish the caster;s magicka reserves, enabling continued spellcasting. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions and can also be brewed into custom potions, making it vital for mages in prolonged encounters. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Restore Magicka effect: Briar Heart, Ectoplasm, Elves Ear, Fire Salts, Frost Salts, Garlic, Glow Dust, Grass Pod, Human Flesh, Red Mountain Flower, Taproot, Tundra Cotton, Void Salts', '''abil'':9B ''also'':32B ''avail'':24B ''brew'':34B ''briar'':69B ''caster'':14B ''combin'':47B ''continu'':19B ''cotton'':90B ''craft'':28B ''creat'':61B ''custom'':36B ''dust'':80B ''ear'':73B ''ectoplasm'':71B ''effect'':5B,22B,59B,68B ''elv'':72B ''enabl'':18B ''encount'':45B ''fire'':74B ''flesh'':84B ''flower'':87B ''follow'':53B ''frost'':76B ''garlic'':78B ''general'':46B ''glow'':79B ''grass'':81B ''heart'':70B ''human'':83B ''ingredi'':54B ''instant'':11B ''least'':49B ''mage'':42B ''magic'':4B ''magicka'':2A,16B,67B ''make'':38B ''mountain'':86B ''pod'':82B ''potion'':29B,37B,63B ''pre'':27B ''pre-craft'':26B ''prolong'':44B ''provid'':55B ''red'':85B ''replenish'':12B ''reserv'':17B ''restor'':1A,7B,8B,66B ''salt'':75B,77B,92B ''share'':57B ''spellcast'':20B ''taproot'':88B ''tundra'':89B ''two'':50B ''vital'':40B ''void'':91B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic restores magicka quickly, helping you cast more spells when needed. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elemental_fury', 'Elemental Fury is a Shout that imbues your arms with the speed of wind, allowing for faster weapon strikes. The three words of power in this Shout are Su (Air), which grants you the swiftness of wind; Grah (Battle), which enhances your combat prowess; and Dun (Grace), which allows for more fluid and rapid attacks.', '''air'':32B ''allow'':17B,51B ''arm'':11B ''attack'':57B ''battl'':41B ''combat'':45B ''dun'':48B ''element'':1A,3B ''enhanc'':43B ''faster'':19B ''fluid'':54B ''furi'':2A,4B ''grace'':49B ''grah'':40B ''grant'':34B ''imbu'':9B ''power'':26B ''prowess'':46B ''rapid'':56B ''shout'':7B,29B ''speed'':14B ''strike'':21B ''su'':31B ''swift'':37B ''three'':23B ''weapon'':20B ''wind'':16B,39B ''word'':24B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('equilibrium', 'Equilibrium is an Alteration spell that converts the caster''s health into magicka at a steady rate, allowing for sustained casting at the cost of vitality. It requires a Novice skill level to cast.', '''allow'':19B ''alter'':5B ''cast'':22B,35B ''caster'':10B ''convert'':8B ''cost'':25B ''equilibrium'':1A,2B ''health'':12B ''level'':33B ''magicka'':14B ''novic'':31B ''rate'':18B ''requir'':29B ''skill'':32B ''spell'':6B ''steadi'':17B ''sustain'':21B ''vital'':27B', 'mage', 'Equilibrium is a spell that drains the caster''s health to refill their magicka, letting them cast more spells but weakening their body. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fast', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Illusion enchantments that enhance the caster;s speed, allowing for quicker movement and evasion. This effect is available only on enchanted items, making it a rare boon for those prioritizing agility.', '''agil'':39B ''allow'':17B ''avail'':26B ''boon'':35B ''caster'':14B ''effect'':4B,24B ''enchant'':10B,29B ''enhanc'':12B ''evas'':22B ''fast'':1A ''focus'':8B ''illus'':9B ''item'':30B ''magic'':3B ''make'':31B ''movement'':20B ''priorit'':38B ''quicker'':19B ''rare'':34B ''speed'':16B ''util'':7B ''utility-focus'':6B', 'mage', 'This enchantment makes you faster, helping you move quickly and avoid danger. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fear', 'These magical effects are offensive Illusion spells that cause the target to flee in terror, exploiting their deepest insecurities. This effect is widely available as a spell, can be found in pre-crafted potions, brewed into custom potions, or applied as an enchantment to weapons or armor. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Fear effect: Blue Dartwing, Namira''s Rot, Powdered Mammoth Tusk, Sabre Cat Eye', '''appli'':42B ''armor'':49B ''avail'':25B ''blue'':72B ''brew'':37B ''cat'':81B ''caus'':10B ''combin'':51B ''craft'':35B ''creat'':65B ''custom'':39B ''dartw'':73B ''deepest'':19B ''effect'':4B,22B,63B,71B ''enchant'':45B ''exploit'':17B ''eye'':82B ''fear'':1A,70B ''flee'':14B ''follow'':57B ''found'':31B ''general'':50B ''illus'':7B ''ingredi'':58B ''insecur'':20B ''least'':53B ''magic'':3B ''mammoth'':78B ''namira'':74B ''offens'':6B ''potion'':36B,40B,67B ''powder'':77B ''pre'':34B ''pre-craft'':33B ''provid'':59B ''rot'':76B ''sabr'':80B ''share'':61B ''spell'':8B,28B ''target'':12B ''terror'':16B ''tusk'':79B ''two'':54B ''weapon'':47B ''wide'':24B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This spell makes enemies so scared they run away and won;t fight for a while. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_archery', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration abilities that improve the precision and damage of bow attacks. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted gear, making it indispensable for marksmen and hunters. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Fortify Archery effect: Canis Root, Elves Ear, Juniper Berries, Spider Egg', '''abil'':11B ''also'':38B ''appli'':40B ''archeri'':2A,72B ''attack'':20B ''avail'':24B ''berri'':79B ''bow'':19B ''brew'':32B ''cani'':74B ''combin'':52B ''craft'':28B ''creat'':66B ''custom'':34B ''damag'':17B ''ear'':77B ''effect'':5B,22B,64B,73B ''egg'':81B ''elv'':76B ''enchant'':42B ''focus'':9B ''follow'':58B ''fortifi'':1A,71B ''gear'':43B ''general'':51B ''hunter'':50B ''improv'':13B ''indispens'':46B ''ingredi'':59B ''junip'':78B ''least'':54B ''magic'':4B ''make'':44B ''marksmen'':48B ''potion'':29B,35B,68B ''pre'':27B ''pre-craft'':26B ''precis'':15B ''provid'':60B ''restor'':10B ''root'':75B ''share'':62B ''spider'':80B ''two'':55B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This enchantment improves your aim and the damage of your bow attacks, useful for hunters. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_carry_weight', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration abilities that increase the caster;s carrying capacity, allowing them to transport more items without becoming encumbered. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted gear, making it invaluable for adventurers and traders. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Fortify Carry Weight effect: Creep Cluster, Giant''s Toe, Hawk Beak, River Betty, Scaly Pholiota, Wisp Wrappings', '''abil'':12B ''adventur'':56B ''allow'':20B ''also'':46B ''appli'':48B ''avail'':32B ''beak'':89B ''becom'':27B ''betti'':91B ''brew'':40B ''capac'':19B ''carri'':2A,18B,80B ''caster'':16B ''cluster'':84B ''combin'':60B ''craft'':36B ''creat'':74B ''creep'':83B ''custom'':42B ''effect'':6B,30B,72B,82B ''enchant'':50B ''encumb'':28B ''focus'':10B ''follow'':66B ''fortifi'':1A,79B ''gear'':51B ''general'':59B ''giant'':85B ''hawk'':88B ''increas'':14B ''ingredi'':67B ''invalu'':54B ''item'':25B ''least'':62B ''magic'':5B ''make'':52B ''pholiota'':93B ''potion'':37B,43B,76B ''pre'':35B ''pre-craft'':34B ''provid'':68B ''restor'':11B ''river'':90B ''scali'':92B ''share'':70B ''toe'':87B ''trader'':58B ''transport'':23B ''two'':63B ''util'':9B ''utility-focus'':8B ''weight'':3A,81B ''wisp'':94B ''without'':26B ''wrap'':95B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This enchantment lets you carry more items without being slowed down. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_illusion', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration abilities that strengthen the caster;s skill in Illusion magic, increasing the duration and potency of spells that manipulate the minds of others. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted gear. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Fortify Illusion effect: Dwarven Oil, Fire Salts, Taproot', '''abil'':11B ''also'':51B ''appli'':53B ''avail'':37B ''brew'':45B ''caster'':15B ''combin'':58B ''craft'':41B ''creat'':72B ''custom'':47B ''durat'':23B ''dwarven'':80B ''effect'':5B,35B,70B,79B ''enchant'':55B ''fire'':82B ''focus'':9B ''follow'':64B ''fortifi'':1A,77B ''gear'':56B ''general'':57B ''illus'':2A,19B,78B ''increas'':21B ''ingredi'':65B ''least'':60B ''magic'':4B,20B ''manipul'':29B ''mind'':31B ''oil'':81B ''other'':33B ''potenc'':25B ''potion'':42B,48B,74B ''pre'':40B ''pre-craft'':39B ''provid'':66B ''restor'':10B ''salt'':83B ''share'':68B ''skill'':17B ''spell'':27B ''strengthen'':13B ''taproot'':84B ''two'':61B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic makes Illusion spells stronger, improving their ability to trick or calm enemies. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arctic_grayling', 'Arctic Grayling are long grey fish with a big top fin commonly found in freezing waters. They can be eaten and have are a white-fleshed fish with flaky meat that some say is delicious and versatile.', '''arctic'':1A,3B ''big'':11B ''common'':14B ''delici'':38B ''eaten'':22B ''fin'':13B ''fish'':8B,30B ''flaki'':32B ''flesh'':29B ''found'':15B ''freez'':17B ''grayl'':2A,4B ''grey'':7B ''long'':6B ''meat'':33B ''say'':36B ''top'':12B ''versatil'':40B ''water'':18B ''white'':28B ''white-flesh'':27B', 'fisher', 'Arctic Grayling are long grey fish with a big top fin commonly found in freezing waters. They can be eaten and have are a white-fleshed fish with flaky meat that some say is delicious and versatile. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bruca''s_leap_redoubt', 'Bruca''s Leap Redoubt is a small cave located southwest of Dragon Bridge in the Reach. The cave is inhabited by Forsworn, making it a dangerous destination for travelers and adventurers in the area.', '''adventur'':35B ''area'':38B ''bridg'':17B ''bruca'':1A,5B ''cave'':12B,22B ''danger'':30B ''destin'':31B ''dragon'':16B ''forsworn'':26B ''inhabit'':24B ''leap'':3A,7B ''locat'':13B ''make'':27B ''reach'':20B ''redoubt'':4A,8B ''small'':11B ''southwest'':14B ''travel'':33B', 'reach', 'Bruca''s Leap Redoubt is a small cave located southwest of Dragon Bridge in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rebel''s_cairn', 'Rebel''s Cairn is a small cave located northwest of Rorikstead and southeast of Sundered Towers in the Reach.  Rebel''s Cairn is tied to the legend of Red Eagle, a hero of the Reach, and serves as the final resting place for the Forsworn''s most revered weapon, Red Eagles Bane.', '''bane'':55B ''cairn'':3A,6B,25B ''cave'':10B ''eagl'':33B,54B ''final'':43B ''forsworn'':48B ''hero'':35B ''legend'':30B ''locat'':11B ''northwest'':12B ''place'':45B ''reach'':22B,38B ''rebel'':1A,4B,23B ''red'':32B,53B ''rest'':44B ''rever'':51B ''rorikstead'':14B ''serv'':40B ''small'':9B ''southeast'':16B ''sunder'':18B ''tie'':27B ''tower'':19B ''weapon'':52B', 'reach, scholar, traveler', 'Rebel''s Cairn is a small cave located northwest in the Reach.  You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frenzy', 'These magical effects are offensive Illusion spells that induce uncontrollable aggression in the target, causing them to attack anything nearby. This effect is available as a spell, can be found in pre-crafted potions, brewed into custom potions, and is also found on enchanted items, making it a chaotic choice for combat mages. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Frenzy effect: Blisterwort, Hagraven Claw, Human Heart, Troll Fat', '''aggress'':12B ''also'':43B ''anyth'':20B ''attack'':19B ''avail'':25B ''blisterwort'':78B ''brew'':37B ''caus'':16B ''chaotic'':51B ''choic'':52B ''claw'':80B ''combat'':54B ''combin'':57B ''craft'':35B ''creat'':71B ''custom'':39B ''effect'':4B,23B,69B,77B ''enchant'':46B ''fat'':84B ''follow'':63B ''found'':31B,44B ''frenzi'':1A,76B ''general'':56B ''hagraven'':79B ''heart'':82B ''human'':81B ''illus'':7B ''induc'':10B ''ingredi'':64B ''item'':47B ''least'':59B ''mage'':55B ''magic'':3B ''make'':48B ''nearbi'':21B ''offens'':6B ''potion'':36B,40B,73B ''pre'':34B ''pre-craft'':33B ''provid'':65B ''share'':67B ''spell'':8B,28B ''target'':15B ''troll'':83B ''two'':60B ''uncontrol'':11B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This spell makes enemies go wild, attacking anything nearby, even their allies. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('salmon', 'Salmon are long blue and white fish commonly found everywhere. They can be eaten and made into a delicous Salmon Steak.', '''blue'':5B ''common'':9B ''delic'':20B ''eaten'':15B ''everywher'':11B ''fish'':8B ''found'':10B ''long'':4B ''made'':17B ''salmon'':1A,2B,21B ''steak'':22B ''white'':7B', 'fisher', 'Salmon are long blue and white fish commonly found everywhere.  You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bujold''s_retreat', 'Bujold''s Retreat is a camp located east of Thirsk Mead Hall and south-southeast of Skaal Village on Solstheim. The camp is home to a group of Nords who have been exiled from Thirsk Mead Hall after it was taken over by a tribe of rieklings.

Led by Bujold the Unworthy, the Nords at the retreat are determined to reclaim their ancestral hall from the invading rieklings.', '''ancestr'':67B ''bujold'':1A,4B,54B ''camp'':9B,26B ''determin'':63B ''east'':11B ''exil'':37B ''group'':31B ''hall'':15B,41B,68B ''home'':28B ''invad'':71B ''led'':52B ''locat'':10B ''mead'':14B,40B ''nord'':33B,58B ''reclaim'':65B ''retreat'':3A,6B,61B ''riekl'':51B,72B ''skaal'':21B ''solstheim'':24B ''south'':18B ''south-southeast'':17B ''southeast'':19B ''taken'':45B ''thirsk'':13B,39B ''tribe'':49B ''unworthi'':56B ''villag'':22B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('haknir''s_shoal', 'Haknir''s Shoal is a small pirate camp located north-northwest of Skaal Village and east of Benkongerike on Solstheim. The camp is situated along the rugged northern coastline, making it a secluded and strategic hideout for its pirate inhabitants.', '''along'':29B ''benkongerik'':22B ''camp'':11B,26B ''coastlin'':33B ''east'':20B ''haknir'':1A,4B ''hideout'':40B ''inhabit'':44B ''locat'':12B ''make'':34B ''north'':14B ''north-northwest'':13B ''northern'':32B ''northwest'':15B ''pirat'':10B,43B ''rug'':31B ''seclud'':37B ''shoal'':3A,6B ''situat'':28B ''skaal'':17B ''small'':9B ''solstheim'':24B ''strateg'':39B ''villag'':18B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_light_feet', 'Favored by sneaks and scouts, this potion aids in evasion by reducing the chance of being detected. Slightly reduces detectability, with stronger potions providing significant stealth advantages. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''advantag'':31B ''aid'':12B ''alchemist'':43B ''chanc'':18B ''detect'':21B,24B ''draught'':53B ''elixir'':56B ''evas'':14B ''favor'':5B ''feet'':4A ''found'':36B ''light'':3A ''loot'':39B ''philter'':54B ''potion'':1A,11B,27B,33B,52B ''provid'':28B ''purchas'':41B ''random'':38B ''reduc'':16B,23B ''scout'':9B ''sever'':46B ''signific'':29B ''slight'':22B ''sneak'':7B ''stealth'':30B ''stronger'':26B ''strongest'':51B ''tier'':47B ''weakest'':49B', 'thief, alchemist, hunter, darkbrotherhood, bard', 'The Potion of Light Feet helps sneaks move more quietly and avoid detection. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('alinor', 'Alinor, the ancient capital of the Summerset Isles, is a shining symbol of High Elven civilization, renowned for its towering, light-catching architecture and its position as the seat of the High Kingship for millennia. Nestled on the Oleander Coast between verdant mountains and idyllic beaches, Alinor boasts a sophisticated layout, from bustling lower streets and marketplaces to the majestic Royal Palace that overlooks the city. Known as the "forest city of Summerset," it is surrounded by vineyards and features the Alinor Docks, a hub for trade despite its landlocked location. Alinor''s sister city, Sunhold, lies just beyond the mountains, and together they form the cultural heart of the Altmer. The city has long been a focal point for diplomacy, art, and governance, maintaining its grandeur through eras of isolation and global engagement.

Throughout its history, Alinor has been central to major events shaping Tamriel. It has weathered conflicts with Maormer and Sload, contributed to the All Flags Navy, and led the formation of the Aldmeri Dominions under leaders like Queen Ayrenn. The city played a pivotal role in resisting Tiber Septim''s conquests, though it ultimately fell to the Numidium, leading to the integration of Summerset into the Third Empire. By the Fourth Era, Alinor was transformed under Thalmor rule, as the monarchy was abolished and the province was renamed "Alinor" to evoke its ancient past. Despite periods of turmoil, the city''s enduring legacy as a beacon of Altmeri culture and innovation remains unchallenged.', '''abolish'':219B ''aldmeri'':169B ''alinor'':1A,2B,49B,84B,94B,140B,209B,225B ''altmer'':113B ''altmeri'':244B ''ancient'':4B,229B ''architectur'':25B ''art'':124B ''ayrenn'':175B ''beach'':48B ''beacon'':242B ''beyond'':101B ''boast'':50B ''bustl'':55B ''capit'':5B ''catch'':24B ''central'':143B ''citi'':68B,73B,97B,115B,177B,236B ''civil'':17B ''coast'':42B ''conflict'':152B ''conquest'':187B ''contribut'':157B ''cultur'':109B,245B ''despit'':90B,231B ''diplomaci'':123B ''dock'':85B ''dominion'':170B ''elven'':16B ''empir'':204B ''endur'':238B ''engag'':136B ''era'':131B,208B ''event'':146B ''evok'':227B ''featur'':82B ''fell'':191B ''flag'':161B ''focal'':120B ''forest'':72B ''form'':107B ''format'':166B ''fourth'':207B ''global'':135B ''govern'':126B ''grandeur'':129B ''heart'':110B ''high'':15B,34B ''histori'':139B ''hub'':87B ''idyl'':47B ''innov'':247B ''integr'':198B ''isl'':9B ''isol'':133B ''kingship'':35B ''known'':69B ''landlock'':92B ''layout'':53B ''lead'':195B ''leader'':172B ''led'':164B ''legaci'':239B ''lie'':99B ''light'':23B ''light-catch'':22B ''like'':173B ''locat'':93B ''long'':117B ''lower'':56B ''maintain'':127B ''majest'':62B ''major'':145B ''maormer'':154B ''marketplac'':59B ''millennia'':37B ''monarchi'':217B ''mountain'':45B,103B ''navi'':162B ''nestl'':38B ''numidium'':194B ''oleand'':41B ''overlook'':66B ''palac'':64B ''past'':230B ''period'':232B ''pivot'':180B ''play'':178B ''point'':121B ''posit'':28B ''provinc'':222B ''queen'':174B ''remain'':248B ''renam'':224B ''renown'':18B ''resist'':183B ''role'':181B ''royal'':63B ''rule'':214B ''seat'':31B ''septim'':185B ''shape'':147B ''shine'':12B ''sister'':96B ''sload'':156B ''sophist'':52B ''street'':57B ''summerset'':8B,75B,200B ''sunhold'':98B ''surround'':78B ''symbol'':13B ''tamriel'':148B ''thalmor'':213B ''third'':203B ''though'':188B ''throughout'':137B ''tiber'':184B ''togeth'':105B ''tower'':21B ''trade'':89B ''transform'':211B ''turmoil'':234B ''ultim'':190B ''unchalleng'':249B ''verdant'':44B ''vineyard'':80B ''weather'':151B', 'scholar,  highelf', '
Alinor, the ancient capital of the Summerset Isles, is a symbol of High Elven civilization known for its striking architecture and central role in the Altmer culture. Situated between mountains and beaches, the city boasts a sophisticated layout with bustling streets and the majestic Royal Palace. Historically, Alinor has been a hub for diplomacy, art, and governance, playing a significant role in events such as conflicts with the Maormer, the formation of the Aldmeri Dominion, and resistance to Tiber Septim''s conquest. By the Fourth Era, it was transformed under Thalmor rule, though it remains a key center of Altmeri culture and innovation.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('balgruuf', 'Balgruuf the Greater is the Jarl of Whiterun and a direct descendant of King Olaf One-Eye. Known for his prowess as a Nord warrior, he has a deep respect for the Greybeards and made the pilgrimage to High Hrothgar in his youth. Throughout his life, Balgruuf has maintained a rivalry with Ulfric Stormcloak, which has roots in their shared upbringing.', '''balgruuf'':1A,2B,49B ''deep'':31B ''descend'':13B ''direct'':12B ''eye'':19B ''greater'':4B ''greybeard'':35B ''high'':41B ''hrothgar'':42B ''jarl'':7B ''king'':15B ''known'':20B ''life'':48B ''made'':37B ''maintain'':51B ''nord'':26B ''olaf'':16B ''one'':18B ''one-ey'':17B ''pilgrimag'':39B ''prowess'':23B ''respect'':32B ''rivalri'':53B ''root'':59B ''share'':62B ''stormcloak'':56B ''throughout'':46B ''ulfric'':55B ''upbring'':63B ''warrior'':27B ''whiterun'':9B ''youth'':45B', 'scholar, noble', 'Balgruuf the Greater is the Jarl of Whiterun and a direct descendant of King Olaf One-Eye. A skilled Nord warrior, he respects the Greybeards and made the pilgrimage to High Hrothgar in his youth. Balgruuf has a longstanding rivalry with Ulfric Stormcloak, rooted in their shared upbringing.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orchish_dagger', 'Orcish Dagger is a light Orcish weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is heavy and brutal, with a rough, greenish hue and primitive, rugged details that emphasize raw strength. To craft it: 1 orichalcum ingot, 1 iron ingot, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using orichalcum at a workbench.', '''1'':37B,40B,44B ''adept'':52B ''blacksmith'':49B ''brutal'':20B ''craft'':35B,55B ''dagger'':2A,4B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''detail'':29B ''emphas'':31B ''forg'':50B ''good'':12B ''greenish'':24B ''heavi'':18B ''hue'':25B ''ingot'':39B,42B ''iron'':41B ''leather'':45B ''light'':7B ''orchish'':1A ''orcish'':3B,8B ''orichalcum'':38B,63B ''primit'':27B ''raw'':32B ''rough'':23B ''rug'':28B ''smith'':53B ''strength'':33B ''strip'':46B ''tempered/improved'':60B ''use'':62B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':66B', 'blacksmith', 'Orcish Dagger is a light Orcish weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is heavy and brutal, with a rough, greenish hue and primitive, rugged details that emphasize raw strength. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_bolt', 'Steel Bolt is an bolt that deals good damage. 
Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished steel shaft, a sharp metal tip, and minimal ornamentation. It can be crafted by an adept smith at a forge. 1 steel ingot, 1 firewood = 10 bolts.', '''1'':42B,45B ''10'':47B ''adept'':37B ''bolt'':2A,4B,7B,48B ''craft'':34B ''damag'':11B ''deal'':9B ''design'':14B ''firewood'':46B ''forg'':41B ''function'':18B ''good'':10B ''ingot'':44B ''metal'':26B ''minim'':29B ''ornament'':30B ''polish'':21B ''shaft'':23B ''sharp'':25B ''smith'':38B ''steel'':1A,3B,22B,43B ''straightforward'':16B ''tip'':27B ''visual'':13B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel Bolt is an bolt that deals good damage. 
Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished steel shaft, a sharp metal tip, and minimal ornamentation. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('repel_lesser_undead', 'Repel Lesser Undead is a Restoration spell that causes weaker undead creatures to flee from the caster, temporarily banishing them. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':27B ''banish'':22B ''cast'':31B ''caster'':20B ''caus'':12B ''creatur'':15B ''flee'':17B ''lesser'':2A,5B ''level'':29B ''repel'':1A,4B ''requir'':25B ''restor'':9B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':10B ''temporarili'':21B ''undead'':3A,6B,14B ''weaker'':13B', 'mage', 'Repel Lesser Undead is a spell that causes weaker undead creatures to flee from the caster, temporarily banishing them. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('angler_larvae', 'Angler Larvae are very small pink fish covered in a translucent embryo commonly found in freezing waters. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Lingering Damage Health, Regenerate Stamina, Waterbreathing and Fortify Two-Handed.', '''angler'':1A,3B ''common'':15B ''cover'':10B ''damag'':34B ''effect'':30B ''embryo'':14B ''fish'':9B ''fortifi'':40B ''found'':16B ''freez'':18B ''hand'':43B ''health'':35B ''ingredi'':24B ''larva'':2A,4B ''linger'':33B ''make'':27B ''offer'':29B ''pink'':8B ''potion'':26B ''regener'':36B ''small'':7B ''stamina'':37B ''transluc'':13B ''two'':42B ''two-hand'':41B ''use'':21B ''water'':19B ''waterbreath'':38B', 'fisher', 'Angler Larvae are very small pink fish covered in a translucent embryo .You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('olava_the_feeble''s_house', 'Olava the Feeble''s House is a quaint, modest home located in the southern part of Whiterun, tucked away directly behind Breezehome. This small residence serves as the dwelling of Olava the Feeble, an elderly seer known for her wisdom and mystical insights.', '''away'':24B ''behind'':26B ''breezehom'':27B ''direct'':25B ''dwell'':34B ''elder'':40B ''feebl'':3A,8B,38B ''home'':15B ''hous'':5A,10B ''insight'':48B ''known'':42B ''locat'':16B ''modest'':14B ''mystic'':47B ''olava'':1A,6B,36B ''part'':20B ''quaint'':13B ''resid'':30B ''seer'':41B ''serv'':31B ''small'':29B ''southern'':19B ''tuck'':23B ''whiterun'':22B ''wisdom'':45B', 'whiterun', 'Olava the Feeble''s House is a quaint, modest home located in the southern part of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('oblivion', 'Oblivion, often referred to as Hell or the Outer Realms, is a vast and complex realm within the Aurbis, primarily inhabited by the Daedra, who are et''Ada that did not participate in the creation of the Mundus. It encompasses at least sixteen major Planes, each presided over by a Daedric Prince, and contains over 37,000 documented planes, including various chaos realms and pocket realities. While many of these realms are governed by powerful Daedra, some are ruled by mortals who have achieved immortality.

Oblivion is considered a distinct universe separate from Mundus, with its landscapes shaped by the perceptions of those who enter, often creating illusions that resemble familiar earthly elements. The nature of each Daedric realm varies widely, ranging from the serene and beautiful to the bizarre and desolate. For instance, notable realms include Apocrypha, ruled by Hermaeus Mora; Coldharbour, ruled by Molag Bal; and the Shivering Isles, formerly ruled by Jyggalag and now by Sheogorath. Each realm reflects the character and essence of its ruler, embodying the chaotic and ever-changing nature of Oblivion itself.', '''000'':58B ''37'':57B ''achiev'':85B ''ada'':29B ''apocrypha'':139B ''aurbi'':20B ''bal'':148B ''beauti'':128B ''bizarr'':131B ''chang'':177B ''chao'':63B ''chaotic'':173B ''charact'':165B ''coldharbour'':144B ''complex'':16B ''consid'':89B ''contain'':55B ''creat'':108B ''creation'':36B ''daedra'':25B,77B ''daedric'':52B,119B ''desol'':133B ''distinct'':91B ''document'':59B ''earth'':113B ''element'':114B ''embodi'':171B ''encompass'':41B ''enter'':106B ''essenc'':167B ''et'':28B ''ever'':176B ''ever-chang'':175B ''familiar'':112B ''former'':153B ''govern'':74B ''hell'':7B ''hermaeus'':142B ''illus'':109B ''immort'':86B ''includ'':61B,138B ''inhabit'':22B ''instanc'':135B ''isl'':152B ''jyggalag'':156B ''landscap'':98B ''least'':43B ''major'':45B ''mani'':69B ''molag'':147B ''mora'':143B ''mortal'':82B ''mundus'':39B,95B ''natur'':116B,178B ''notabl'':136B ''oblivion'':1A,2B,87B,180B ''often'':3B,107B ''outer'':10B ''particip'':33B ''percept'':102B ''plane'':46B,60B ''pocket'':66B ''power'':76B ''presid'':48B ''primarili'':21B ''princ'':53B ''rang'':123B ''realiti'':67B ''realm'':11B,17B,64B,72B,120B,137B,162B ''refer'':4B ''reflect'':163B ''resembl'':111B ''rule'':80B,140B,145B,154B ''ruler'':170B ''separ'':93B ''seren'':126B ''shape'':99B ''sheogorath'':160B ''shiver'':151B ''sixteen'':44B ''univers'':92B ''vari'':121B ''various'':62B ''vast'':14B ''wide'':122B ''within'':18B', 'scholar, daedra, daedric', 'Oblivion, also known as Hell or the Outer Realms, is a vast and chaotic realm within the Aurbis, primarily inhabited by Daedra, beings who did not partake in the creation of the Mundus. It consists of at least sixteen major planes, each ruled by a Daedric Prince, and thousands of other realms shaped by the perceptions of those who enter. These realms vary widely in nature, from serene to bizarre and desolate. Notable realms include Apocrypha, Coldharbour, and the Shivering Isles, each reflecting the essence of their respective rulers, and Oblivion itself embodies chaos and constant change.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mount_anthor', 'Mount Anthor is a dragon lair located on a mountaintop south-southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region. The lair is perched high on the mountain, offering a commanding view of the surrounding landscape. It lies north of Yorgrim Overlook, making it accessible through the rugged terrain of the region.', '''access'':46B ''anthor'':2A,4B ''command'':32B ''dragon'':7B ''high'':26B ''lair'':8B,23B ''landscap'':37B ''lie'':39B ''locat'':9B ''make'':44B ''mount'':1A,3B ''mountain'':29B ''mountaintop'':12B ''north'':40B ''offer'':30B ''overlook'':43B ''perch'':25B ''region'':21B,53B ''rug'':49B ''south'':14B ''south-southwest'':13B ''southwest'':15B ''surround'':36B ''terrain'':50B ''view'':33B ''winterhold'':17B,20B ''yorgrim'':42B', 'winterhold, dragon', 'Mount Anthor is a dragon lair located on a mountaintop south-southwest of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region. You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cyrodiil', '
Cyrodiil, the heartland of Tamriel and home to the Imperials, serves as the seat of the Empire and the location of its capital, the Imperial City. Dominated by the iconic White-Gold Tower, Cyrodiil is central to Tamriel''s history and culture. Though initially described as a jungle, its climate is temperate, possibly altered by Emperor Tiber Septim. The province''s early history is marked by the rule of the Ayleids, who enslaved the native Nedic people. The rebellion led by Alessia in 1E 242 ended Ayleid dominance, establishing the Alessian Empire and shaping Cyrodiil into a center of human governance and culture. The Alessians expanded westward, influenced by the prophet Marukh''s teachings, which codified much of Tamriel’s religion.

Cyrodiil’s history is defined by cycles of conquest and upheaval, from the Akaviri invasion of 1E 2703, which united Tamriel under Emperor Reman I, to the eventual collapse of the Second Empire. The chaos of the Interregnum ended with Tiber Septim''s rise, uniting Tamriel under the Third Empire. The Fourth Era brought new challenges, including the Great War against the Aldmeri Dominion, marked by the brutal Battle of the Red Ring and the controversial White-Gold Concordat. While Cyrodiil remains the seat of the Empire, these events have left a lasting impact, straining relations with Skyrim and reshaping the political landscape of Tamriel.', '''1e'':86B,138B ''242'':87B ''2703'':139B ''akaviri'':135B ''aldmeri'':184B ''alessia'':84B ''alessian'':93B,107B ''alter'':56B ''ayleid'':73B,89B ''battl'':190B ''brought'':175B ''brutal'':189B ''capit'':24B ''center'':100B ''central'':38B ''challeng'':177B ''chao'':156B ''citi'':27B ''climat'':52B ''codifi'':118B ''collaps'':150B ''concordat'':201B ''conquest'':130B ''controversi'':197B ''cultur'':44B,105B ''cycl'':128B ''cyrodiil'':1A,2B,36B,97B,203B ''cyrodiil’'':123B ''defin'':126B ''describ'':47B ''domin'':28B,90B ''dominion'':185B ''earli'':64B ''emperor'':58B,144B ''empir'':18B,94B,154B,171B,209B ''end'':88B,160B ''enslav'':75B ''era'':174B ''establish'':91B ''event'':211B ''eventu'':149B ''expand'':108B ''fourth'':173B ''gold'':34B,200B ''govern'':103B ''great'':180B ''heartland'':4B ''histori'':42B,65B,124B ''home'':8B ''human'':102B ''icon'':31B ''impact'':216B ''imperi'':11B,26B ''includ'':178B ''influenc'':110B ''initi'':46B ''interregnum'':159B ''invas'':136B ''jungl'':50B ''landscap'':225B ''last'':215B ''led'':82B ''left'':213B ''locat'':21B ''mark'':67B,186B ''marukh'':114B ''much'':119B ''nativ'':77B ''nedic'':78B ''new'':176B ''peopl'':79B ''polit'':224B ''possibl'':55B ''prophet'':113B ''provinc'':62B ''rebellion'':81B ''red'':193B ''relat'':218B ''religion'':122B ''remain'':204B ''reman'':145B ''reshap'':222B ''ring'':194B ''rise'':165B ''rule'':70B ''seat'':15B,206B ''second'':153B ''septim'':60B,163B ''serv'':12B ''shape'':96B ''skyrim'':220B ''strain'':217B ''tamriel'':6B,40B,142B,167B,227B ''tamriel’'':121B ''teach'':116B ''temper'':54B ''third'':170B ''though'':45B ''tiber'':59B,162B ''tower'':35B ''unit'':141B,166B ''upheav'':132B ''war'':181B ''westward'':109B ''white'':33B,199B ''white-gold'':32B,198B', 'scholar, imperial, noble', '
Cyrodiil, the heart of Tamriel and the seat of the Empire, is home to the Imperial City and the White-Gold Tower. Initially a jungle, its climate was possibly changed by Emperor Tiber Septim. Its early history was marked by Ayleid rule, which ended with the Alessian Rebellion in 1E 242. The province''s history includes cycles of conquest, such as the Akaviri invasion and the rise of Tiber Septim, who unified Tamriel under the Third Empire. The Fourth Era brought challenges, including the Great War with the Aldmeri Dominion and the controversial White-Gold Concordat, shaping Cyrodiil''s political landscape.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frost_mirriam', 'Frost Mirriam is an yellow herb commonly found hanging to dry in homes, often alongside garlic and Elves Ear. Alchemy effects: Resist Frost, Fortify Sneak, Ravage Magicka, and Damage Stamina Regen.', '''alchemi'':22B ''alongsid'':17B ''common'':9B ''damag'':31B ''dri'':13B ''ear'':21B ''effect'':23B ''elv'':20B ''fortifi'':26B ''found'':10B ''frost'':1A,3B,25B ''garlic'':18B ''hang'':11B ''herb'':8B ''home'':15B ''magicka'':29B ''mirriam'':2A,4B ''often'':16B ''ravag'':28B ''regen'':33B ''resist'':24B ''sneak'':27B ''stamina'':32B ''yellow'':7B', 'alchemist', 'Frost Mirriam is an yellow herb commonly found hanging to dry in homes, often alongside garlic and Elves Ear.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ice_wraith', 'Ice Wraiths are ethereal, serpentine spirits composed entirely of ice, commonly found in the frigid landscapes and mountain ranges of Skyrim, as well as in regions of High Rock and Cyrodiil. These magical beings possess the ability to blend seamlessly with their snowy surroundings, rendering them nearly invisible to unsuspecting prey. Ice Wraiths are known for their swift and lethal attacks, lunging at victims to inflict fatal bites, and they can transmit Witbane, a disease that impairs mental acuity. Notably, they are immune to paralysis, making them challenging opponents in combat.', '''abil'':39B ''acuiti'':81B ''attack'':63B ''be'':36B ''bite'':70B ''blend'':41B ''challeng'':90B ''combat'':93B ''common'':13B ''compos'':9B ''cyrodiil'':33B ''diseas'':77B ''entir'':10B ''ether'':6B ''fatal'':69B ''found'':14B ''frigid'':17B ''high'':30B ''ice'':1A,3B,12B,54B ''immun'':85B ''impair'':79B ''inflict'':68B ''invis'':50B ''known'':57B ''landscap'':18B ''lethal'':62B ''lung'':64B ''magic'':35B ''make'':88B ''mental'':80B ''mountain'':20B ''near'':49B ''notabl'':82B ''oppon'':91B ''paralysi'':87B ''possess'':37B ''prey'':53B ''rang'':21B ''region'':28B ''render'':47B ''rock'':31B ''seamless'':42B ''serpentin'':7B ''skyrim'':23B ''snowi'':45B ''spirit'':8B ''surround'':46B ''swift'':60B ''transmit'':74B ''unsuspect'':52B ''victim'':66B ''well'':25B ''witban'':75B ''wraith'':2A,4B,55B', 'nord, hunter', 'Ice Wraiths are ethereal, ice-based spirits found in Skyrim and surrounding regions, blending with their snowy surroundings to ambush prey. Known for their swift attacks and ability to transmit Witbane.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('magicka_poison', 'Designed to cripple spellcasters, this poison drains the target''s magicka, preventing them from casting powerful spells. Stronger variants drain more magicka, making them effective against mages. These poisons can be found in random loot, purchased from apothecaries, or crafted using alchemy. Tiers: weak, standard, potent, virulent, deadly.', '''alchemi'':44B ''apothecari'':40B ''cast'':17B ''craft'':42B ''crippl'':5B ''dead'':50B ''design'':3B ''drain'':9B,22B ''effect'':27B ''found'':34B ''loot'':37B ''mage'':29B ''magicka'':1A,13B,24B ''make'':25B ''poison'':2A,8B,31B ''potent'':48B ''power'':18B ''prevent'':14B ''purchas'':38B ''random'':36B ''spell'':19B ''spellcast'':6B ''standard'':47B ''stronger'':20B ''target'':11B ''tier'':45B ''use'':43B ''variant'':21B ''virul'':49B ''weak'':46B', 'mage, alchemist, scholar, collegeofwinterhold', 'This poison drains magicka, hindering a mage''s ability to cast spells. You do not know the full effects or details of this poison. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ice_wraith_teeth', 'Ice Wraith Teeth are dropped by ice wraiths, known for their ability to enhance defense and manipulate elemental effects. Alchemy effects: Weakness to Frost, Fortify Heavy Armor, Invisibility, and Weakness to Fire.', '''abil'':15B ''alchemi'':23B ''armor'':30B ''defens'':18B ''drop'':8B ''effect'':22B,24B ''element'':21B ''enhanc'':17B ''fire'':35B ''fortifi'':28B ''frost'':27B ''heavi'':29B ''ice'':1A,4B,10B ''invis'':31B ''known'':12B ''manipul'':20B ''teeth'':3A,6B ''weak'':25B,33B ''wraith'':2A,5B,11B', 'alchemist', 'Ice Wraith Teeth are dropped by ice wraiths, known for their ability to enhance defense and manipulate elemental effects. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
