INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vampire''s_bane', 'Vampire''s Bane is a Restoration spell that unleashes a burst of light, dealing damage to vampires and healing the caster if the target is a vampire. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':34B ''bane'':3A,6B ''burst'':14B ''cast'':38B ''caster'':24B ''damag'':18B ''deal'':17B ''heal'':22B ''level'':36B ''light'':16B ''requir'':32B ''restor'':9B ''skill'':35B ''spell'':10B ''target'':27B ''unleash'':12B ''vampir'':1A,4B,20B,30B', 'mage', 'Vampire''s Bane is a spell that releases a burst of light, dealing damage to vampires and healing the caster if the target is a vampire. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rout', 'Rout is an Illusion spell that causes a target to flee in terror, forcing them to run away from the caster and their allies. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':29B ''alli'':25B ''away'':19B ''cast'':33B ''caster'':22B ''caus'':8B ''flee'':12B ''forc'':15B ''illus'':5B ''level'':31B ''requir'':27B ''rout'':1A,2B ''run'':18B ''skill'':30B ''spell'':6B ''target'':10B ''terror'':14B', 'mage', '
Rout is a spell that causes a target to flee in terror, forcing them to run away from the caster and their allies. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dead_thrall', 'Dead Thrall is a Conjuration spell that permanently reanimates a powerful dead body to fight for the caster until it is destroyed. It requires a Master skill level to cast.', '''bodi'':15B ''cast'':32B ''caster'':20B ''conjur'':7B ''dead'':1A,3B,14B ''destroy'':24B ''fight'':17B ''level'':30B ''master'':28B ''perman'':10B ''power'':13B ''reanim'':11B ''requir'':26B ''skill'':29B ''spell'':8B ''thrall'':2A,4B', 'mage', '
Dead Thrall is a spell that permanently reanimates a powerful dead body, bringing it back to fight for the caster until it is destroyed. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('cold_rock_pass', 'Cold Rock Pass is a small mountain passage located south-southwest of Morthal and north of Rannveig''s Fast in Whiterun Hold. The pass is home to a frost troll and provides a treacherous but convenient shortcut through the mountainous terrain."', '''cold'':1A,4B ''conveni'':40B ''fast'':23B ''frost'':33B ''hold'':26B ''home'':30B ''locat'':12B ''morthal'':17B ''mountain'':10B,44B ''north'':19B ''pass'':3A,6B,28B ''passag'':11B ''provid'':36B ''rannveig'':21B ''rock'':2A,5B ''shortcut'':41B ''small'':9B ''south'':14B ''south-southwest'':13B ''southwest'':15B ''terrain'':45B ''treacher'':38B ''troll'':34B ''whiterun'':25B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Cold Rock Pass is a small mountain passage located south-southwest of Morthalin Whiterun Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wolf', '
Wolves are, hostile canines commonly found in the wilds of Skyrim and Solstheim, often encountered alone or in small packs. They are known for circling around their prey and can infect you with the disease Rockjoint through their bite. Wolves typically do not attack werewolves in beast form unless provoked.', '''alon'':17B ''around'':27B ''attack'':45B ''beast'':48B ''bite'':40B ''canin'':5B ''circl'':26B ''common'':6B ''diseas'':36B ''encount'':16B ''form'':49B ''found'':7B ''hostil'':4B ''infect'':32B ''known'':24B ''often'':15B ''pack'':21B ''prey'':29B ''provok'':51B ''rockjoint'':37B ''skyrim'':12B ''small'':20B ''solstheim'':14B ''typic'':42B ''unless'':50B ''werewolv'':46B ''wild'':10B ''wolf'':1A ''wolv'':2B,41B', 'hunter', '
Wolves are, hostile canines commonly found in the wilds of Skyrim and Solstheim, often encountered alone or in small packs. ', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('reachwater_rock', 'Reachwater Rock is a small cave located east-southeast of Markarth and south of Karthspire in the Reach. The cave is inhabited by draugr. To reach the cave, take the road southeast toward Falkreath and look for a path on the right just before crossing the final bridge near the turnoff for Karthspire Camp. It is rumored that a powerful Breton Conjurer, though you do not know who, is buried here. ', '''breton'':64B ''bridg'':51B ''buri'':73B ''camp'':57B ''cave'':8B,23B,31B ''conjur'':65B ''cross'':48B ''draugr'':27B ''east'':11B ''east-southeast'':10B ''falkreath'':37B ''final'':50B ''inhabit'':25B ''karthspir'':18B,56B ''know'':70B ''locat'':9B ''look'':39B ''markarth'':14B ''near'':52B ''path'':42B ''power'':63B ''reach'':21B,29B ''reachwat'':1A,3B ''right'':45B ''road'':34B ''rock'':2A,4B ''rumor'':60B ''small'':7B ''south'':16B ''southeast'':12B,35B ''take'':32B ''though'':66B ''toward'':36B ''turnoff'':54B', 'reach', 'Reachwater Rock is a small cave located east-southeast of Markarth in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('soul_husk_extract', 'This extract protects against magical attacks and interrupts the soul drain effect within the Soul Cairn. Valerica can craft it in exchange for Soul Husks. Alchemists speculate its properties come from the unique magical environment of the Soul Cairn, where the laws of magic differ from Tamriel.', '''alchemist'':29B ''attack'':9B ''cairn'':19B,42B ''come'':33B ''craft'':22B ''differ'':48B ''drain'':14B ''effect'':15B ''environ'':38B ''exchang'':25B ''extract'':3A,5B ''husk'':2A,28B ''interrupt'':11B ''law'':45B ''magic'':8B,37B,47B ''properti'':32B ''protect'':6B ''soul'':1A,13B,18B,27B,41B ''specul'':30B ''tamriel'':50B ''uniqu'':36B ''valerica'':20B ''within'':16B', 'valerica, vampire', 'You have heard that it is related to vampires but know nothing more.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pine_thrush_egg', 'Pine Thrush Eggs can be harvested from birds'' nests found in forested regions, especially throughout The Rift. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Fortify Lockpicking, Weakness to Poison, and Resist Shock.', '''alchemi'':21B ''bird'':11B ''effect'':22B ''egg'':3A,6B ''especi'':17B ''forest'':15B ''fortifi'':25B ''found'':13B ''harvest'':9B ''lockpick'':26B ''nest'':12B ''pine'':1A,4B ''poison'':29B ''region'':16B ''resist'':31B ''restor'':23B ''rift'':20B ''shock'':32B ''stamina'':24B ''throughout'':18B ''thrush'':2A,5B ''weak'':27B', 'alchemist', 'Pine Thrush Eggs can be harvested from birds'' nests found in forested regions, especially throughout The Rift.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_warhammer', 'Dwarven Warhammer is a massive dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. To craft it: 2 dwarven metal ingots, 2 steel ingots, 1 iron ingot, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dwarvern ingot at a workbench.', '''1'':41B ''2'':34B,38B ''3'':45B ''adept'':53B ''angular'':18B ''blacksmith'':50B ''bronz'':25B ''craft'':32B,56B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,8B,35B ''dwarvern'':64B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':51B ''golden'':24B ''golden-bronz'':23B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':37B,40B,43B,65B ''intric'':28B ''iron'':42B ''leather'':46B ''massiv'':7B ''mechan'':29B ''metal'':36B ''ornat'':20B ''pattern'':30B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':39B ''strip'':47B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''warhamm'':2A,4B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Dwarven Warhammer is a massive dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('disguised_invisibility_potion', 'This potion grants invisibility for a brief time but cannot be consumed, as it is marked as a quest item during the events of ''Clear-Headed.'' Its purpose seems tied to unique circumstances, possibly as part of a deceptive scheme.', '''brief'':10B ''cannot'':13B ''circumst'':37B ''clear'':29B ''clear-head'':28B ''consum'':15B ''decept'':43B ''disguis'':1A ''event'':26B ''grant'':6B ''head'':30B ''invis'':2A,7B ''item'':23B ''mark'':19B ''part'':40B ''possibl'':38B ''potion'':3A,5B ''purpos'':32B ''quest'':22B ''scheme'':44B ''seem'':33B ''tie'':34B ''time'':11B ''uniqu'':36B', 'blocked', 'You have no knowledge of this potion or its purpose.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ravage_magicka', 'These magical effects are offensive Destruction abilities that permanently reduce the target;s maximum magicka, crippling their ability to cast higher-level spells. This effect can only be brewed into custom potions, making it a tactical tool against mages. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Ravage Magicka effect: Alocasia Fruit, Frost Mirriam, Grass Pod, Lavender, Orange Dartwing, Red Mountain Flower, Scathecraw, Spawn Ash, White Cap', '''abil'':9B,20B ''alocasia'':66B ''ash'':80B ''brew'':32B ''cap'':82B ''cast'':22B ''combin'':44B ''creat'':58B ''crippl'':18B ''custom'':34B ''dartw'':74B ''destruct'':8B ''effect'':5B,28B,56B,65B ''flower'':77B ''follow'':50B ''frost'':68B ''fruit'':67B ''general'':43B ''grass'':70B ''higher'':24B ''higher-level'':23B ''ingredi'':51B ''lavend'':72B ''least'':46B ''level'':25B ''mage'':42B ''magic'':4B ''magicka'':2A,17B,64B ''make'':36B ''maximum'':16B ''mirriam'':69B ''mountain'':76B ''offens'':7B ''orang'':73B ''perman'':11B ''pod'':71B ''potion'':35B,60B ''provid'':52B ''ravag'':1A,63B ''red'':75B ''reduc'':12B ''scathecraw'':78B ''share'':54B ''spawn'':79B ''spell'':26B ''tactic'':39B ''target'':14B ''tool'':40B ''two'':47B ''white'':81B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic reduces how much magicka an enemy can have, making it harder for them to cast spells. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sun_fire', 'Sun Fire is a Restoration spell that unleashes a burst of fiery light, dealing damage to undead and healing the caster if the target is undead. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':32B ''burst'':12B ''cast'':36B ''caster'':23B ''damag'':17B ''deal'':16B ''fieri'':14B ''fire'':2A,4B ''heal'':21B ''level'':34B ''light'':15B ''requir'':30B ''restor'':7B ''skill'':33B ''spell'':8B ''sun'':1A,3B ''target'':26B ''undead'':19B,28B ''unleash'':10B', 'mage', 'Sun Fire is a spell that releases a burst of fiery light, dealing damage to undead and healing the caster if the target is undead. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('telekinesis_arrow', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Alteration spells that allow the caster to control and fire arrows using telekinetic energy, removing the need for a physical bow. This effect is only accessible as a spell, providing a unique combination of magic and archery.', '''access'':35B ''allow'':13B ''alter'':10B ''archeri'':46B ''arrow'':2A,20B ''bow'':30B ''caster'':15B ''combin'':42B ''control'':17B ''effect'':5B,32B ''energi'':23B ''fire'':19B ''focus'':9B ''magic'':4B,44B ''need'':26B ''physic'':29B ''provid'':39B ''remov'':24B ''spell'':11B,38B ''telekinesi'':1A ''telekinet'':22B ''uniqu'':41B ''use'':21B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B', 'mage', 'This spell lets you shoot arrows without needing a bow, using magic instead. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('diamond_claw', 'Combination: Fox—Moth—Dragon', '''claw'':2A ''combin'':3B ''diamond'':1A ''fox—moth—dragon'':4B', 'puzzle', 'You have no idea what the claw is or how to solze its puzzle.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ignite', 'Ignite is a Destruction spell that causes a target to burst into flames, dealing fire damage over time. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':23B ''burst'':12B ''cast'':27B ''caus'':8B ''damag'':17B ''deal'':15B ''destruct'':5B ''fire'':16B ''flame'':14B ''ignit'':1A,2B ''level'':25B ''requir'':21B ''skill'':24B ''spell'':6B ''target'':10B ''time'':19B', 'mage', 'Ignite is a spell that causes a target to catch fire, dealing fire damage over time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('riverside_shack', 'Riverside Shack is a small, derelict shack located along the eastern bank of the White River, east of Gallows Rock and west-southwest of Kynesgrove in Eastmarch. The shack is in a state of disrepair, with holes in its roof and walls, and is missing a front door and windows.', '''along'':11B ''bank'':14B ''derelict'':8B ''disrepair'':38B ''door'':51B ''east'':19B ''eastern'':13B ''eastmarch'':30B ''front'':50B ''gallow'':21B ''hole'':40B ''kynesgrov'':28B ''locat'':10B ''miss'':48B ''river'':18B ''riversid'':1A,3B ''rock'':22B ''roof'':43B ''shack'':2A,4B,9B,32B ''small'':7B ''southwest'':26B ''state'':36B ''wall'':45B ''west'':25B ''west-southwest'':24B ''white'':17B ''window'':53B', 'eastmarch', 'iverside Shack is a small, derelict shack located along the eastern bank of the White River in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('blacksmiths_potion', 'A craftsman''s aid, this potion enhances the skill of tempering weapons and armor, resulting in superior upgrades. Slightly improves smithing abilities, with higher tiers granting greater enhancement to weapon and armor improvements. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''abil'':24B ''aid'':6B ''alchemist'':47B ''armor'':16B,34B ''blacksmith'':1A ''craftsman'':4B ''draught'':57B ''elixir'':60B ''enhanc'':9B,30B ''found'':40B ''grant'':28B ''greater'':29B ''higher'':26B ''improv'':22B,35B ''loot'':43B ''philter'':58B ''potion'':2A,8B,37B,56B ''purchas'':45B ''random'':42B ''result'':17B ''sever'':50B ''skill'':11B ''slight'':21B ''smith'':23B ''strongest'':55B ''superior'':19B ''temper'':13B ''tier'':27B,51B ''upgrad'':20B ''weakest'':53B ''weapon'':14B,32B', 'blacksmith, alchemist, warrior, companions', 'The Blacksmith''s Potion enhances smithing skills, improving weapon and armor upgrades. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wreck_of_the_strident_squall', 'The Wreck of the Strident Squall is a battered shipwreck resting south-southeast of Raven Rock, off the southern coast of Solstheim. Located southwest of Hrodulf''s House, this forlorn vessel lies amidst jagged rocks and icy waters,.', '''amidst'':39B ''batter'':14B ''coast'':26B ''forlorn'':36B ''hous'':34B ''hrodulf'':32B ''ici'':43B ''jag'':40B ''lie'':38B ''locat'':29B ''raven'':21B ''rest'':16B ''rock'':22B,41B ''shipwreck'':15B ''solstheim'':28B ''south'':18B ''south-southeast'':17B ''southeast'':19B ''southern'':25B ''southwest'':30B ''squall'':5A,11B ''strident'':4A,10B ''vessel'':37B ''water'':44B ''wreck'':1A,7B', 'solstheim, sailor', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orchish_war_axe', 'Orcish War Axe is a sturdy Orcish weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is heavy and brutal, with a rough, greenish hue and primitive, rugged details that emphasize raw strength. To craft it: 2 orichalcum ingots, 1 iron ingot, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using orichalcum at a workbench.', '''1'':42B ''2'':39B,46B ''adept'':54B ''axe'':3A,6B ''blacksmith'':51B ''brutal'':22B ''craft'':37B,57B ''damag'':15B ''deal'':13B ''design'':18B ''detail'':31B ''emphas'':33B ''forg'':52B ''good'':14B ''greenish'':26B ''heavi'':20B ''hue'':27B ''ingot'':41B,44B ''iron'':43B ''leather'':47B ''orchish'':1A ''orcish'':4B,10B ''orichalcum'':40B,65B ''primit'':29B ''raw'':34B ''rough'':25B ''rug'':30B ''smith'':55B ''strength'':35B ''strip'':48B ''sturdi'':9B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''use'':64B ''visual'':17B ''war'':2A,5B ''weapon'':11B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Orcish War Axe is a sturdy Orcish weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is heavy and brutal, with a rough, greenish hue and primitive, rugged details that emphasize raw strength. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ancestor_moth_wing', 'Ancestor Moth Wing is a delicate brownish ingredient that is prized for its magical properties, especially in enhancing conjuration and enchanting abilities. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina, Fortify Conjuration, Damage Magicka Regen, and Fortify Enchanting.', '''abil'':25B ''alchemi'':26B ''ancestor'':1A,4B ''brownish'':10B ''conjur'':22B,31B ''damag'':28B,32B ''delic'':9B ''effect'':27B ''enchant'':24B,37B ''enhanc'':21B ''especi'':19B ''fortifi'':30B,36B ''ingredi'':11B ''magic'':17B ''magicka'':33B ''moth'':2A,5B ''prize'':14B ''properti'':18B ''regen'':34B ''stamina'':29B ''wing'':3A,6B', 'alchemist', 'Ancestor Moth Wing is a delicate brownish ingredient that is prized for its magical properties, especially in enhancing conjuration and enchanting abilities.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_ultimate_stamina', 'The ultimate stamina elixir, this potion fully replenishes stamina, vital for overcoming the most exhausting challenges. Fully restores stamina, ensuring peak performance during the most taxing endeavors. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists.', '''alchemist'':43B ''challeng'':20B ''elixir'':8B ''endeavor'':31B ''ensur'':24B ''exhaust'':19B ''found'':36B ''fulli'':11B,21B ''loot'':39B ''overcom'':16B ''peak'':25B ''perform'':26B ''potion'':1A,10B,33B ''purchas'':41B ''random'':38B ''replenish'':12B ''restor'':22B ''stamina'':4A,7B,13B,23B ''tax'':30B ''ultim'':3A,6B ''vital'':14B', 'alchemist, hunter, warrior, companions, traveler', 'The Potion of Ultimate Stamina fully restores stamina, essential for overcoming exhaustive challenges. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lavender', 'Lavender is an herb that thrives in cold steppe climates, particularly in Whiterun Hold, and is found in several other holds as well. Alchemy effects: Resist Magic, Fortify Stamina, Ravage Magicka, and Fortify Conjuration.', '''alchemi'':25B ''climat'':11B ''cold'':9B ''conjur'':35B ''effect'':26B ''fortifi'':29B,34B ''found'':18B ''herb'':5B ''hold'':15B,22B ''lavend'':1A,2B ''magic'':28B ''magicka'':32B ''particular'':12B ''ravag'':31B ''resist'':27B ''sever'':20B ''stamina'':30B ''stepp'':10B ''thrive'':7B ''well'':24B ''whiterun'':14B', 'alchemist', 'Lavender is an herb that thrives in cold steppe climates, particularly in Whiterun Hold, and is found in several other holds as well. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rockjoint', 'Rockjoint is an acute disease that affects a victim''s manual dexterity and ability to use melee weapons, causing painful swelling and immobility of the joints. It can be contracted from wolves, alit, zombies, and domesticated guar. As the disease progresses, it severely diminishes the effectiveness of one-handed and two-handed weapon damage, limiting the victim''s combat capabilities.', '''abil'':15B ''acut'':5B ''affect'':8B ''alit'':34B ''capabl'':63B ''caus'':20B ''combat'':62B ''contract'':31B ''damag'':57B ''dexter'':13B ''diminish'':45B ''diseas'':6B,41B ''domest'':37B ''effect'':47B ''guar'':38B ''hand'':51B,55B ''immobl'':24B ''joint'':27B ''limit'':58B ''manual'':12B ''mele'':18B ''one'':50B ''one-hand'':49B ''pain'':21B ''progress'':42B ''rockjoint'':1A,2B ''sever'':44B ''swell'':22B ''two'':54B ''two-hand'':53B ''use'':17B ''victim'':10B,60B ''weapon'':19B,56B ''wolv'':33B ''zombi'':35B', 'alchemist', 'Rockjoint is an acute disease that affects a victim''s manual dexterity and ability to use melee weapons, causing painful swelling and immobility of the joints. It can be contracted from wolves, alit, zombies, and domesticated guar. You do not know much else about this disease, but an alchemist would.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shield_of_ysgramor', '
The Shield of Ysgramor is a legendary artifact buried with the famed Nord hero Ysgramor in his tomb during the Late Merethic Era. While it is unclear if Ysgramor used the shield in battle, it grants its wielder enhanced durability and resistance to magic, making it a prized relic of Nordic heritage.', '''artifact'':11B ''battl'':37B ''buri'':12B ''durabl'':43B ''enhanc'':42B ''era'':26B ''fame'':15B ''grant'':39B ''heritag'':55B ''hero'':17B ''late'':24B ''legendari'':10B ''magic'':47B ''make'':48B ''mereth'':25B ''nord'':16B ''nordic'':54B ''prize'':51B ''relic'':52B ''resist'':45B ''shield'':1A,5B,35B ''tomb'':21B ''unclear'':30B ''use'':33B ''wielder'':41B ''ysgramor'':3A,7B,18B,32B', 'scholar', 'The Shield of Ysgramor is a legendary artifact from the Late Merethic Era, granting enhanced durability and resistance to magic. Buried with the Nord hero Ysgramor, it is a treasured relic of Nordic heritage.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vampire', 'Vampires are preternatural beings in Tamriel, often regarded as undead creatures that feed on the blood of the living. This condition arises from the curse of vampirism, which can make individuals into feared and misunderstood abominations. While some vampires view their state as a curse, others might perceive it as a blessing, struggling with their primal instincts or seeking to overcome the disease that has transformed them. Despite their potential for power and agility, they are widely hunted and despised by society, especially in Imperial culture, which labels them as destructive monsters.', '''abomin'':37B ''agil'':75B ''aris'':23B ''be'':5B ''bless'':53B ''blood'':17B ''condit'':22B ''creatur'':12B ''cultur'':87B ''curs'':26B,46B ''despis'':81B ''despit'':69B ''destruct'':92B ''diseas'':64B ''especi'':84B ''fear'':34B ''feed'':14B ''hunt'':79B ''imperi'':86B ''individu'':32B ''instinct'':58B ''label'':89B ''live'':20B ''make'':31B ''might'':48B ''misunderstood'':36B ''monster'':93B ''often'':8B ''other'':47B ''overcom'':62B ''perceiv'':49B ''potenti'':71B ''power'':73B ''preternatur'':4B ''primal'':57B ''regard'':9B ''seek'':60B ''societi'':83B ''state'':43B ''struggl'':54B ''tamriel'':7B ''transform'':67B ''undead'':11B ''vampir'':1A,2B,28B,40B ''view'':41B ''wide'':78B', 'vampire, dawnguard, priest, snowelf', 'Vampires are preternatural beings in Tamriel, often regarded as undead creatures that feed on the blood of the living. Despite their potential for power and agility, they are widely hunted and despised by society, especially in Imperial culture, which labels them as destructive monsters.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('histcarp', 'Histcarp are long dark orange fish found around Skyrim that can be caught with your hands. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Restore Stamina, Fortify Magicka, Damage Stamina Regen and Waterbreathing.', '''around'':9B ''caught'':14B ''damag'':35B ''dark'':5B ''effect'':28B ''fish'':7B ''fortifi'':33B ''found'':8B ''hand'':17B ''histcarp'':1A,2B ''ingredi'':22B ''long'':4B ''magicka'':34B ''make'':25B ''offer'':27B ''orang'':6B ''potion'':24B ''regen'':37B ''restor'':31B ''skyrim'':10B ''stamina'':32B,36B ''use'':19B ''waterbreath'':39B', 'fisher', 'Histcarp are long dark orange fish found around Skyrim. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dead_men''s_respite', 'Dead Men''s Respite is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southwest of Morthal in Hjaalmarch. The ruin is inhabited by draugr. It is rummored that the a Verse from the Poetic Edda is hidden somehwere in the ruin.', '''dead'':1A,5B ''draugr'':27B ''edda'':38B ''hidden'':40B ''hjaalmarch'':21B ''inhabit'':25B ''locat'':16B ''medium'':12B ''medium-s'':11B ''men'':2A,6B ''morthal'':19B ''nordic'':14B ''poetic'':37B ''respit'':4A,8B ''ruin'':15B,23B,44B ''rummor'':30B ''size'':13B ''somehwer'':41B ''southwest'':17B ''vers'':34B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Dead Men''s Respite is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southwest of Morthal in Hjaalmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('glass_arrow', 'Glass Arrow is an arrow that deals great damage. 
Its visual design is sleek and translucent, featuring a greenish shaft, a sharp, crystalline tip, and fine feathered fletching  It can be crafted by an expert smith at a forge. 1 malachite, 1 firewood = 24 arrows."', '''1'':42B,44B ''24'':46B ''arrow'':2A,4B,7B,47B ''craft'':34B ''crystallin'':25B ''damag'':11B ''deal'':9B ''design'':14B ''expert'':37B ''feather'':29B ''featur'':19B ''fine'':28B ''firewood'':45B ''fletch'':30B ''forg'':41B ''glass'':1A,3B ''great'':10B ''greenish'':21B ''malachit'':43B ''shaft'':22B ''sharp'':24B ''sleek'':16B ''smith'':38B ''tip'':26B ''transluc'':18B ''visual'':13B', 'blacksmith', 'Glass Arrow is an arrow that deals great damage. 
Its visual design is sleek and translucent, featuring a greenish shaft, a sharp, crystalline tip, and fine feathered fletching  You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('frenzy_poison', 'A chaotic choice, this poison induces frenzy, causing targets to attack anything nearby. Higher potency affects stronger enemies. These poisons can be found in random loot, purchased from apothecaries, or crafted using alchemy. Tiers: weak, standard, potent, virulent, deadly.', '''affect'':18B ''alchemi'':35B ''anyth'':14B ''apothecari'':31B ''attack'':13B ''caus'':10B ''chaotic'':4B ''choic'':5B ''craft'':33B ''dead'':41B ''enemi'':20B ''found'':25B ''frenzi'':1A,9B ''higher'':16B ''induc'':8B ''loot'':28B ''nearbi'':15B ''poison'':2A,7B,22B ''potenc'':17B ''potent'':39B ''purchas'':29B ''random'':27B ''standard'':38B ''stronger'':19B ''target'':11B ''tier'':36B ''use'':34B ''virul'':40B ''weak'':37B', 'alchemist, mage, thief, bard, witch, darkbrotherhood, collegeofwinterhold', 'This poison causes frenzy, making enemies attack randomly. You do not know the full effects or details of this poison. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('aversion_to_fire', 'This poison exploits a target''s weakness to fire, increasing the damage they take from fire-based attacks. Stronger potions amplify this effect. These poisons can be found in random loot, purchased from apothecaries, or crafted using alchemy. Tiers: weak, standard, potent, virulent, deadly.', '''alchemi'':42B ''amplifi'':25B ''apothecari'':38B ''attack'':22B ''avers'':1A ''base'':21B ''craft'':40B ''damag'':15B ''dead'':48B ''effect'':27B ''exploit'':6B ''fire'':3A,12B,20B ''fire-bas'':19B ''found'':32B ''increas'':13B ''loot'':35B ''poison'':5B,29B ''potent'':46B ''potion'':24B ''purchas'':36B ''random'':34B ''standard'':45B ''stronger'':23B ''take'':17B ''target'':8B ''tier'':43B ''use'':41B ''virul'':47B ''weak'':10B,44B', 'alchemist, mage, scholar, witch, psijic, collegeofwinterhold', 'This poison increases a target''s vulnerability to fire. You do not know the full effects or details of this poison. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('absorb_magicka', 'These magical effects are offensive Destruction enchantments that siphon magicka from the target, replenishing the wielder;s reserves. This effect can be applied through custom enchanting and is also found on enchanted items, making it particularly effective against enemy spellcasters.', '''absorb'':1A ''also'':31B ''appli'':25B ''custom'':27B ''destruct'':8B ''effect'':5B,22B,39B ''enchant'':9B,28B,34B ''enemi'':41B ''found'':32B ''item'':35B ''magic'':4B ''magicka'':2A,12B ''make'':36B ''offens'':7B ''particular'':38B ''replenish'':16B ''reserv'':20B ''siphon'':11B ''spellcast'':42B ''target'':15B ''wielder'':18B', 'mage', 'This effect steals magicka from the target, giving it to whoever is wielding the enchanted item. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('flames', 'Flames is a Destruction spell that projects a continuous stream of fire, dealing fire damage to health and stamina. It requires a Novice skill level to cast.', '''cast'':28B ''continu'':10B ''damag'':16B ''deal'':14B ''destruct'':5B ''fire'':13B,15B ''flame'':1A,2B ''health'':18B ''level'':26B ''novic'':24B ''project'':8B ''requir'':22B ''skill'':25B ''spell'':6B ''stamina'':20B ''stream'':11B', 'mage', 'Flames is a spell that releases a continuous stream of fire, burning enemies and draining their health and stamina. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('poison', 'Poisons inflict harm, dealing damage to an target''s health over time. The potency increases with each tier, making them versatile tools for combat. These poisons can be found in random loot, purchased from apothecaries, or crafted using alchemy. Tiers: weak, standard, potent, virulent, deadly.', '''alchemi'':40B ''apothecari'':36B ''combat'':25B ''craft'':38B ''damag'':6B ''dead'':46B ''deal'':5B ''found'':30B ''harm'':4B ''health'':11B ''increas'':16B ''inflict'':3B ''loot'':33B ''make'':20B ''poison'':1A,2B,27B ''potenc'':15B ''potent'':44B ''purchas'':34B ''random'':32B ''standard'':43B ''target'':9B ''tier'':19B,41B ''time'':13B ''tool'':23B ''use'':39B ''versatil'':22B ''virul'':45B ''weak'':42B', 'alchemist, thief, darkbrotherhood, hunter, mage, scholar', 'This poison causes harm to the target''s health over time. You do not know the full effects or details of this poison. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('iron_warhammer', 'Iron Warhammer is a massive iron weapon which deals low damage. Its visual design is crude and basic, with a dark, weathered appearance and simple, utilitarian shapes. To craft it: 4 iron ingots and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Novice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''3'':37B ''4'':33B ''appear'':25B ''basic'':20B ''blacksmith'':42B ''craft'':31B,48B ''crude'':18B ''damag'':13B ''dark'':23B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''forg'':43B ''ingot'':35B ''iron'':1A,3B,8B,34B,56B ''leather'':38B ''low'':12B ''massiv'':7B ''novic'':45B ''shape'':29B ''simpl'':27B ''smith'':46B ''strip'':39B ''tempered/improved'':53B ''use'':55B ''utilitarian'':28B ''visual'':15B ''warhamm'':2A,4B ''weapon'':9B ''weather'':24B ''workbench'':59B', 'blacksmith', 'Iron Warhammer is a massive iron weapon which deals low damage. Its visual design is crude and basic, with a dark, weathered appearance and simple, utilitarian shapes.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('steel_dagger', 'Steel Dagger is a light steel weapon which deals average damage. Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished silver-gray finish and minimal ornamentation focused on practicality. To craft it: 1 steel ingot, 1 iron ingot, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''1'':37B,40B,44B ''adept'':52B ''averag'':12B ''blacksmith'':49B ''craft'':35B,55B ''dagger'':2A,4B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''finish'':27B ''focus'':31B ''forg'':50B ''function'':20B ''gray'':26B ''ingot'':39B,42B ''iron'':41B ''leather'':45B ''light'':7B ''minim'':29B ''ornament'':30B ''polish'':23B ''practic'':33B ''silver'':25B ''silver-gray'':24B ''smith'':53B ''steel'':1A,3B,8B,38B,63B ''straightforward'':18B ''strip'':46B ''tempered/improved'':60B ''use'':62B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':66B', 'blacksmith', 'Steel Dagger is a light steel weapon which deals average damage. Its visual design is straightforward and functional, with a polished silver-gray finish and minimal ornamentation focused on practicality. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('aster_bloom_core', 'Aster Bloom Core is a red, spiky plant that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Resist Magic, Fortify Light Armor, Fortify Block, and Paralysis.', '''alchemi'':19B ''armor'':25B ''aster'':1A,4B ''block'':27B ''bloom'':2A,5B ''caravan'':18B ''core'':3A,6B ''effect'':20B ''fortifi'':23B,26B ''khajiit'':17B ''light'':24B ''magic'':22B ''paralysi'':29B ''plant'':11B ''purchas'':15B ''red'':9B ''resist'':21B ''spiki'':10B', 'alchemist', 'Aster Bloom Core is a red, spiky plant that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ice_wraith_bane', 'Ice Wraith Bane is a potent poison specifically crafted to harm Ice Wraiths. Known to be issued to those joining the Stormcloaks, its formulation is highly effective against these spectral creatures, though its use is limited to such foes.', '''bane'':3A,6B ''craft'':12B ''creatur'':34B ''effect'':30B ''foe'':42B ''formul'':27B ''harm'':14B ''high'':29B ''ice'':1A,4B,15B ''issu'':20B ''join'':23B ''known'':17B ''limit'':39B ''poison'':10B ''potent'':9B ''specif'':11B ''spectral'':33B ''stormcloak'':25B ''though'':35B ''use'':37B ''wraith'':2A,5B,16B', 'stormcloak, alchemist, scholar', 'You know this poison is meant to combat Ice Wraiths and is tied to the Stormcloak cause, but its details remain unclear.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skuldafn', 'Skuldafn is a vast Nordic ruin located in Eastmarch, notable for containing a portal to Sovngarde. Guarded by powerful draugr, dragons, and the formidable dragon priest Nahkriin, it is a site of immense historical and mythical significance. ', '''contain'':13B ''dragon'':22B,26B ''draugr'':21B ''eastmarch'':10B ''formid'':25B ''guard'':18B ''histor'':35B ''immens'':34B ''locat'':8B ''mythic'':37B ''nahkriin'':28B ''nordic'':6B ''notabl'':11B ''portal'':15B ''power'':20B ''priest'':27B ''ruin'':7B ''signific'':38B ''site'':32B ''skuldafn'':1A,2B ''sovngard'':17B ''vast'':5B', 'eastmarch', 'Skuldafn is a vast Nordic ruin located in Eastmarch, notable for containing a portal to Sovngarde. It is umreachable by normal means.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('blue_butterfly_wing', 'Blue Butterfly Wings are delicate, vibrant wings that can be caught from blue butterflies fluttering around Skyrim. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina, Fortify Conjuration, Damage Magicka Regen, and Fortify Enchanting.', '''alchemi'':21B ''around'':19B ''blue'':1A,4B,16B ''butterfli'':2A,5B,17B ''caught'':14B ''conjur'':26B ''damag'':23B,27B ''delic'':8B ''effect'':22B ''enchant'':32B ''flutter'':18B ''fortifi'':25B,31B ''magicka'':28B ''regen'':29B ''skyrim'':20B ''stamina'':24B ''vibrant'':9B ''wing'':3A,6B,10B', 'alchemist', 'Blue Butterfly Wings are delicate, vibrant wings that can be caught from blue butterflies fluttering around Skyrim.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_cake_and_the_diamond', '
The Cake and the Diamond, written by Athyn Muendil, tells the clever tale of Abelle Chriditte, an alchemist who outwits a group of would-be thieves in Ald’ruhn. Posing as a wandering old woman in need of transportation funds, Abelle offers to create potions of invisibility in exchange for a stolen diamond. Through subtle trickery, including enchanting wine to compel honesty and manipulating the diamond dust on a knife, she vanishes with the valuable gem while leaving her would-be attackers duped. The story highlights themes of cunning, deception, and poetic justice.

This single-volume tale cleverly portrays the interplay of greed and wit, emphasizing the consequences of underestimating others, especially those with hidden skills. The humorous and ironic conclusion leaves the thieves humiliated while demonstrating Abelle’s mastery of both alchemy and manipulation.', '''abell'':20B,46B ''abelle’'':135B ''alchemi'':139B ''alchemist'':23B ''ald’ruhn'':34B ''athyn'':13B ''attack'':88B ''cake'':2A,7B ''chriditt'':21B ''clever'':17B,105B ''compel'':66B ''conclus'':128B ''consequ'':115B ''creat'':49B ''cun'':95B ''decept'':96B ''demonstr'':134B ''diamond'':5A,10B,58B,71B ''dupe'':89B ''dust'':72B ''emphas'':113B ''enchant'':63B ''especi'':119B ''exchang'':54B ''fund'':45B ''gem'':81B ''greed'':110B ''group'':27B ''hidden'':122B ''highlight'':92B ''honesti'':67B ''humili'':132B ''humor'':125B ''includ'':62B ''interplay'':108B ''invis'':52B ''iron'':127B ''justic'':99B ''knife'':75B ''leav'':83B,129B ''manipul'':69B,141B ''masteri'':136B ''muendil'':14B ''need'':42B ''offer'':47B ''old'':39B ''other'':118B ''outwit'':25B ''poetic'':98B ''portray'':106B ''pose'':35B ''potion'':50B ''singl'':102B ''single-volum'':101B ''skill'':123B ''stolen'':57B ''stori'':91B ''subtl'':60B ''tale'':18B,104B ''tell'':15B ''theme'':93B ''thiev'':32B,131B ''transport'':44B ''trickeri'':61B ''underestim'':117B ''valuabl'':80B ''vanish'':77B ''volum'':103B ''wander'':38B ''wine'':64B ''wit'':112B ''woman'':40B ''would'':30B,86B ''would-b'':29B,85B ''written'':11B', 'scholar', 'The Cake and the Diamond, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, tells the story of Abelle Chriditte, an alchemist who outsmarts thieves through cunning and deception, ultimately stealing a diamond while leaving her attackers humiliated. Themes of trickery, greed, and poetic justice are central, showcasing how underestimating others can lead to unexpected consequences.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sload', 'The Sload, also known as Slugmen or slug-folk, are a race of slug-like beastfolk hailing from the Coral Kingdoms of Thras, located southwest of Tamriel. These semi-aquatic, corpulent beings can grow to significant sizes and are primarily known for their necromantic culture.

Described by the Khajiit explorer Ja''dasha as some of the most dangerous sea creatures, the Sload are often mentioned alongside krakens and sea serpents. Their notoriety escalated dramatically in 1E 2260 when they released the Thrassian Plague upon Tamriel, a catastrophic event that resulted in the deaths of over half the continent''s population, further solidifying their reputation as a significant threat in the region.', '''1e'':80B ''2260'':81B ''alongsid'':70B ''also'':4B ''aquat'':34B ''be'':36B ''beastfolk'':19B ''catastroph'':91B ''contin'':102B ''coral'':23B ''corpul'':35B ''creatur'':64B ''cultur'':49B ''danger'':62B ''dasha'':56B ''death'':97B ''describ'':50B ''dramat'':78B ''escal'':77B ''event'':92B ''explor'':54B ''folk'':11B ''grow'':38B ''hail'':20B ''half'':100B ''ja'':55B ''khajiit'':53B ''kingdom'':24B ''known'':5B,45B ''kraken'':71B ''like'':18B ''locat'':27B ''mention'':69B ''necromant'':48B ''notorieti'':76B ''often'':68B ''plagu'':87B ''popul'':104B ''primarili'':44B ''race'':14B ''region'':115B ''releas'':84B ''reput'':108B ''result'':94B ''sea'':63B,73B ''semi'':33B ''semi-aquat'':32B ''serpent'':74B ''signific'':40B,111B ''size'':41B ''sload'':1A,3B,66B ''slug'':10B,17B ''slug-folk'':9B ''slug-lik'':16B ''slugmen'':7B ''solidifi'':106B ''southwest'':28B ''tamriel'':30B,89B ''thras'':26B ''thrassian'':86B ''threat'':112B ''upon'':88B', 'scholar', '
The Sload, or Slugmen, are a slug-like race from the Coral Kingdoms of Thras, southwest of Tamriel. Known for their necromantic culture and semi-aquatic nature, they are infamous for their role in unleashing the Thrassian Plague in 1E 2260, which decimated over half of Tamriel''s population. Described as highly dangerous by explorers, they are often compared to krakens and sea serpents, cementing their reputation as a significant threat to the region.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ebony_dagger', 'Ebony Dagger is a light ebony weapon which deals fantastic damage. 
Its visual design is sleek and black, with smooth, angular lines and silver accents that give it a refined yet intimidating appearance. To craft it: 1 ebony ingot and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Expert smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using ebony at a workbench.', '''1'':39B,43B ''accent'':27B ''angular'':23B ''appear'':35B ''black'':20B ''blacksmith'':48B ''craft'':37B,54B ''dagger'':2A,4B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''eboni'':1A,3B,8B,40B,62B ''expert'':51B ''fantast'':12B ''forg'':49B ''give'':29B ''ingot'':41B ''intimid'':34B ''leather'':44B ''light'':7B ''line'':24B ''refin'':32B ''silver'':26B ''sleek'':18B ''smith'':52B ''smooth'':22B ''strip'':45B ''tempered/improved'':59B ''use'':61B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':65B ''yet'':33B', 'blacksmith', 'Ebony Dagger is a light ebony weapon which deals fantastic damage. 
Its visual design is sleek and black, with smooth, angular lines and silver accents that give it a refined yet intimidating appearance. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mass_paralysis', 'Mass Paralysis is an Alteration spell that immobilizes all targets in a large area around the caster for a short duration. It requires a Master skill level to cast.', '''alter'':7B ''area'':16B ''around'':17B ''cast'':31B ''caster'':19B ''durat'':23B ''immobil'':10B ''larg'':15B ''level'':29B ''mass'':1A,3B ''master'':27B ''paralysi'':2A,4B ''requir'':25B ''short'':22B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':8B ''target'':12B', 'mage', 'Mass Paralysis is a spell that freezes everyone in a large area, making all targets unable to move for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('angler', 'The elusive Angler is a very small, rare fish found exclusively in freezing waters when using an Argonian Fishing Rod. It has large teeth, a glowing lantern on its head, and dark slimey scales. It can be eaten though it has a rather horrible smell.', '''angler'':1A,4B ''argonian'':19B ''dark'':33B ''eaten'':39B ''elus'':3B ''exclus'':12B ''fish'':10B,20B ''found'':11B ''freez'':14B ''glow'':27B ''head'':31B ''horribl'':45B ''lantern'':28B ''larg'':24B ''rare'':9B ''rather'':44B ''rod'':21B ''scale'':35B ''slimey'':34B ''small'':8B ''smell'':46B ''teeth'':25B ''though'':40B ''use'':17B ''water'':15B', 'fisher', 'The elusive Angler is a very small, rare fish. It has large teeth, a glowing lantern on its head, and dark slimey scales. It can be eaten though it has a rather horrible smell. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pogfish', 'Pogfish are a large long blue fish found in temperate rivers. They can be eaten but they have a rather funny taste, but you cant put your finger on what it tastes funny.', '''blue'':7B ''cant'':26B ''eaten'':16B ''finger'':29B ''fish'':8B ''found'':9B ''funni'':22B,34B ''larg'':5B ''long'':6B ''pogfish'':1A,2B ''put'':27B ''rather'':21B ''river'':12B ''tast'':23B,33B ''temper'':11B', 'fisher', 'Pogfish are a large long blue fish. They can be eaten but they have a rather funny taste, but you cant put your finger on what it tastes funny. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chokeberry', 'Chokeberry, originating from Cyrodiil, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Damage Health, Ravage Health, Lingering Damage Health, and Weakness to Poison.', '''alchemi'':16B ''caravan'':15B ''chokeberri'':1A,2B ''cyrodiil'':5B ''damag'':18B,23B ''effect'':17B ''health'':19B,21B,24B ''ingredi'':8B ''khajiit'':14B ''linger'':22B ''origin'':3B ''poison'':28B ''purchas'':12B ''ravag'':20B ''weak'':26B', 'alchemist', 'Chokeberry, originating from Cyrodiil, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. A
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('boulderfall_cave', 'Boulderfall Cave is a small, remote cave northwest of Riften and southeast of Clearspring Tarn, inhabited by necromancers. Marked by a flagpost fluttering above the entrance, the cave is accessible via a path branching from a game trail in the wilderness. It is rumoured that necromancers have taken over the cave.', '''access'':32B ''boulderfal'':1A,3B ''branch'':36B ''cave'':2A,4B,9B,30B,53B ''clearspr'':16B ''entranc'':28B ''flagpost'':24B ''flutter'':25B ''game'':39B ''inhabit'':18B ''mark'':21B ''necromanc'':20B,48B ''northwest'':10B ''path'':35B ''remot'':8B ''riften'':12B ''rumour'':46B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':14B ''taken'':50B ''tarn'':17B ''trail'':40B ''via'':33B ''wilder'':43B', 'rift', 'Boulderfall Cave is a small, remote cave northwest of Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('clearspring_tarn', 'Clearspring Tarn is a serene mountain pool located on a cliff in the Rift, overlooking Eastmarch. It lies due east of Snapleg Cave and west of Shor''s Stone. Nestled in the rugged terrain, this tranquil spot offers a peaceful yet remote setting.', '''cave'':25B ''clearspr'':1A,3B ''cliff'':13B ''due'':21B ''east'':22B ''eastmarch'':18B ''lie'':20B ''locat'':10B ''mountain'':8B ''nestl'':32B ''offer'':40B ''overlook'':17B ''peac'':42B ''pool'':9B ''remot'':44B ''rift'':16B ''rug'':35B ''seren'':7B ''set'':45B ''shor'':29B ''snapleg'':24B ''spot'':39B ''stone'':31B ''tarn'':2A,4B ''terrain'':36B ''tranquil'':38B ''west'':27B ''yet'':43B', 'rift', 'Clearspring Tarn is a serene mountain pool located on a cliff in the Rift.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bloated_man''s_grotto', 'Bloated Man''s Grotto is a small, picturesque cave located north of Falkreath and south of Sleeping Tree Camp in Falkreath Hold. Known for its serene atmosphere and natural beauty. It is rumoured that hunters from around Skyrim are travling to this place for whatever reason. It is usally inhabited by animals and Spriggans.', '''anim'':56B ''around'':41B ''atmospher'':31B ''beauti'':34B ''bloat'':1A,5B ''camp'':23B ''cave'':13B ''falkreath'':17B,25B ''grotto'':4A,8B ''hold'':26B ''hunter'':39B ''inhabit'':54B ''known'':27B ''locat'':14B ''man'':2A,6B ''natur'':33B ''north'':15B ''picturesqu'':12B ''place'':47B ''reason'':50B ''rumour'':37B ''seren'':30B ''skyrim'':42B ''sleep'':21B ''small'':11B ''south'':19B ''spriggan'':58B ''travl'':44B ''tree'':22B ''usal'':53B ''whatev'':49B', 'falkreath', 'Bloated Man''s Grotto is a small, picturesque cave located north of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('broken_oar_grotto', 'Broken Oar Grotto is a small cave located north of Solitude, northwest of Brinewater Grotto, along the northern tip of the coastline in Haafingar. The entrance to the cave is marked by a landslide, next to a small cave opening, with a crushed longboat visible among the rubble, rocks, and broken trees.

Inside, the cave is inhabited by the Blackblood Marauders, a group of bandits led by Captain Hargar.', '''along'':19B ''among'':49B ''bandit'':68B ''blackblood'':63B ''brinewat'':17B ''broken'':1A,4B,54B ''captain'':71B ''cave'':10B,32B,42B,58B ''coastlin'':25B ''crush'':46B ''entranc'':29B ''grotto'':3A,6B,18B ''group'':66B ''haafingar'':27B ''hargar'':72B ''inhabit'':60B ''insid'':56B ''landslid'':37B ''led'':69B ''locat'':11B ''longboat'':47B ''maraud'':64B ''mark'':34B ''next'':38B ''north'':12B ''northern'':21B ''northwest'':15B ''oar'':2A,5B ''open'':43B ''rock'':52B ''rubbl'':51B ''small'':9B,41B ''solitud'':14B ''tip'':22B ''tree'':55B ''visibl'':48B', 'haafingar', 'Broken Oar Grotto is a small cave located north of Solitude in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('honeystrand_cave', 'Honeystrand Cave is a small cave located south of Ivarstead and northeast of the Alchemist''s Shack in the Rift. There are rumours of a bear that lives here.', '''alchemist'':17B ''bear'':28B ''cave'':2A,4B,8B ''honeystrand'':1A,3B ''ivarstead'':12B ''live'':30B ''locat'':9B ''northeast'':14B ''rift'':22B ''rumour'':25B ''shack'':19B ''small'':7B ''south'':10B', 'rift', 'Honeystrand Cave is a small cave located south of Ivarstead.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('beast_stone', 'The Beast Stone is one of the All-Maker Stones found on Solstheim, located west of Thirsk Mead Hall and east-southeast of the Temple of Miraak. This sacred stone holds spiritual significance for the Skaal people.', '''all-mak'':10B ''beast'':1A,4B ''east'':25B ''east-southeast'':24B ''found'':14B ''hall'':22B ''hold'':35B ''locat'':17B ''maker'':12B ''mead'':21B ''miraak'':31B ''one'':7B ''peopl'':41B ''sacr'':33B ''signific'':37B ''skaal'':40B ''solstheim'':16B ''southeast'':26B ''spiritu'':36B ''stone'':2A,5B,13B,34B ''templ'':29B ''thirsk'':20B ''west'':18B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('windhelm_stables', 'Windhelm Stables is located just outside the city of Windhelm in Eastmarch. Accessible by two flights of stairs—one from the stony path leading to the city and another from the nearby carriage stop—the stables feature a small, stony yard in front of the stable house.', '''access'':15B ''anoth'':30B ''carriag'':34B ''citi'':10B,28B ''eastmarch'':14B ''featur'':37B ''flight'':18B ''front'':43B ''hous'':47B ''lead'':25B ''locat'':6B ''nearbi'':33B ''outsid'':8B ''path'':24B ''small'':39B ''stabl'':2A,4B,36B,46B ''stairs—on'':20B ''stoni'':23B,40B ''stop—th'':35B ''two'':17B ''windhelm'':1A,3B,12B ''yard'':41B', 'eastmarch', 'Windhelm Stables is located just outside the city of Windhelm in Eastmarch.  You do not know who runs the stables.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gray_quarter', 'The Gray Quarter is a district in Windhelm, home to the city''s sizable population of Dark Elves, or Dunmer, who sought refuge in Skyrim after the eruption of Red Mountain. Once known as the Snow Quarter, it is a cramped and impoverished area, where the Dunmer face suspicion and xenophobia from the Nords, who view them with disdain. Although they are not openly persecuted, the Dunmer live in difficult conditions, with little support from Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak, who largely ignores their plight.

The Gray Quarter reflects the tension between Windhelm''s native Nords and the immigrant Dunmer, who are forced to live in this slum on the city''s outskirts. Additionally, Argonians, who also reside in Windhelm, are prohibited from entering the city itself and are confined to the docks outside the city walls.', '''addit'':114B ''also'':117B ''although'':62B ''area'':46B ''argonian'':115B ''citi'':14B,111B,126B,136B ''condit'':73B ''confin'':130B ''cramp'':43B ''dark'':19B ''difficult'':72B ''disdain'':61B ''district'':8B ''dock'':133B ''dunmer'':22B,49B,69B,100B ''elv'':20B ''enter'':124B ''erupt'':30B ''face'':50B ''forc'':103B ''gray'':1A,4B,87B ''home'':11B ''ignor'':83B ''immigr'':99B ''impoverish'':45B ''jarl'':78B ''known'':35B ''larg'':82B ''littl'':75B ''live'':70B,105B ''mountain'':33B ''nativ'':95B ''nord'':56B,96B ''open'':66B ''outsid'':134B ''outskirt'':113B ''persecut'':67B ''plight'':85B ''popul'':17B ''prohibit'':122B ''quarter'':2A,5B,39B,88B ''red'':32B ''reflect'':89B ''refug'':25B ''resid'':118B ''sizabl'':16B ''skyrim'':27B ''slum'':108B ''snow'':38B ''sought'':24B ''stormcloak'':80B ''support'':76B ''suspicion'':51B ''tension'':91B ''ulfric'':79B ''view'':58B ''wall'':137B ''windhelm'':10B,93B,120B ''xenophobia'':53B', 'eastmarch', 'The Gray Quarter is a district in Windhelm, home to the city''s sizable population of Dark Elves, or Dunmer, who sought refuge in Skyrim after the eruption of Red Mountain. Once known as the Snow Quarter, it is a cramped and impoverished area, where the Dunmer face suspicion and xenophobia from the Nords, who view them with disdainYou do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pinewatch', 'Pinewatch is a small shack located northeast of Falkreath and west of Helgen in Falkreath Hold. While it appears unassuming from the outside, it conceals a secret underground cave system, known as the Pinewatch Bandit''s Sanctuary, making it a hideout for bandits.', '''appear'':20B ''bandit'':36B,44B ''cave'':30B ''conceal'':26B ''falkreath'':10B,16B ''helgen'':14B ''hideout'':42B ''hold'':17B ''known'':32B ''locat'':7B ''make'':39B ''northeast'':8B ''outsid'':24B ''pinewatch'':1A,2B,35B ''sanctuari'':38B ''secret'':28B ''shack'':6B ''small'':5B ''system'':31B ''unassum'':21B ''underground'':29B ''west'':12B', 'falkreath', 'Pinewatch is a small shack located northeast of Falkreath and west of Helgen in Falkreath Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
