You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_vigorous_healing', 'This robust potion provides vigorous healing, capable of mending even substantial wounds with ease. Restores a substantial amount of health, allowing for quick recovery from critical wounds. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists.', '''alchemist'':43B ''allow'':25B ''amount'':22B ''capabl'':11B ''critic'':30B ''eas'':18B ''even'':14B ''found'':36B ''heal'':4A,10B ''health'':24B ''loot'':39B ''mend'':13B ''potion'':1A,7B,33B ''provid'':8B ''purchas'':41B ''quick'':27B ''random'':38B ''recoveri'':28B ''restor'':19B ''robust'':6B ''substanti'':15B,21B ''vigor'':3A,9B ''wound'':16B,31B', 'alchemist, healer, priest, warrior, companions', 'The Potion of Vigorous Healing restores a substantial amount of health for critical wounds. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('north_cold_rock_pass', 'Cold Rock Pass is a small mountain passage located south-southwest of Morthal and north of Rannveig''s Fast in Whiterun Hold. The pass is home to a frost troll and provides a treacherous but convenient shortcut through the mountainous terrain.', '''cold'':2A,5B ''conveni'':41B ''fast'':24B ''frost'':34B ''hold'':27B ''home'':31B ''locat'':13B ''morthal'':18B ''mountain'':11B,45B ''north'':1A,20B ''pass'':4A,7B,29B ''passag'':12B ''provid'':37B ''rannveig'':22B ''rock'':3A,6B ''shortcut'':42B ''small'':10B ''south'':15B ''south-southwest'':14B ''southwest'':16B ''terrain'':46B ''treacher'':39B ''troll'':35B ''whiterun'':26B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Cold Rock Pass is a small mountain passage located south-southwest of Morthalin Whiterun Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('riften_stables', 'Riften Stables is located just outside the northern entrance to Riften. Owned and operated by Hofgrir Horse-Crusher, with assistance from Shadr, the stables provide horse rentals and sales for travelers and adventurers.', '''adventur'':36B ''assist'':23B ''crusher'':21B ''entranc'':11B ''hofgrir'':18B ''hors'':20B,29B ''horse-crush'':19B ''locat'':6B ''northern'':10B ''oper'':16B ''outsid'':8B ''own'':14B ''provid'':28B ''rental'':30B ''riften'':1A,3B,13B ''sale'':32B ''shadr'':25B ''stabl'':2A,4B,27B ''travel'':34B', 'rift', 'Riften Stables is located just outside the northern entrance to Riften.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mossy_glen_cave', 'Mossy Glen Cave is a small,bear den located within Dayspring Canyon, accessible only via the canyon itself. The natural cave is adorned with stone pillars and plants.', '''access'':16B ''adorn'':26B ''bear'':10B ''canyon'':15B,20B ''cave'':3A,6B,24B ''dayspr'':14B ''den'':11B ''glen'':2A,5B ''locat'':12B ''mossi'':1A,4B ''natur'':23B ''pillar'':29B ''plant'':31B ''small'':9B ''stone'':28B ''via'':18B ''within'':13B', 'rift', 'Mossy Glen Cave is a small,bear den located within Dayspring Canyon.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brothers_of_darkness', 'The Brothers of Darkness, written by Pellarne Assi, explores the enigmatic origins and evolution of the Dark Brotherhood, Tamriel''s infamous guild of assassins. The text traces their roots to the Morag Tong, a Second Era religious cult devoted to the Daedric Prince Mephala. The Morag Tong''s shift to the Dark Brotherhood marked a significant transformation, as they transitioned from ritualistic murder to a profit-driven organization serving rulers and wealthy patrons. This shift solidified their role as both a feared cult and a necessary, albeit unlawful, institution across Tamriel.

The book highlights key historical moments, such as the assassination of Potentate Versidue-Shaie in 2E 324 and the infamous massacre of Emperor-Potentate Savirien-Chorak and his heirs in 2E 430. Themes of secrecy, power, and moral ambiguity run throughout, emphasizing the Brotherhood''s dual identity as both a cult and a business. Though officially condemned, their services remain widely tolerated, securing their position as a shadowy yet indispensable force in Tamriel''s political landscape.', '''2e'':112B,129B ''324'':113B ''430'':130B ''across'':94B ''albeit'':91B ''ambigu'':137B ''assassin'':27B,105B ''assi'':11B ''book'':97B ''brother'':1A,5B ''brotherhood'':21B,56B,142B ''busi'':152B ''chorak'':124B ''condemn'':155B ''cult'':41B,87B,149B ''daedric'':45B ''dark'':3A,7B,20B,55B ''devot'':42B ''driven'':71B ''dual'':144B ''emperor'':120B ''emperor-potent'':119B ''emphas'':140B ''enigmat'':14B ''era'':39B ''evolut'':17B ''explor'':12B ''fear'':86B ''forc'':169B ''guild'':25B ''heir'':127B ''highlight'':98B ''histor'':100B ''ident'':145B ''indispens'':168B ''infam'':24B,116B ''institut'':93B ''key'':99B ''landscap'':174B ''mark'':57B ''massacr'':117B ''mephala'':47B ''moment'':101B ''morag'':35B,49B ''moral'':136B ''murder'':66B ''necessari'':90B ''offici'':154B ''organ'':72B ''origin'':15B ''patron'':77B ''pellarn'':10B ''polit'':173B ''posit'':163B ''potent'':107B,121B ''power'':134B ''princ'':46B ''profit'':70B ''profit-driven'':69B ''religi'':40B ''remain'':158B ''ritualist'':65B ''role'':82B ''root'':32B ''ruler'':74B ''run'':138B ''savirien'':123B ''savirien-chorak'':122B ''second'':38B ''secreci'':133B ''secur'':161B ''serv'':73B ''servic'':157B ''shadowi'':166B ''shaie'':110B ''shift'':52B,79B ''signific'':59B ''solidifi'':80B ''tamriel'':22B,95B,171B ''text'':29B ''theme'':131B ''though'':153B ''throughout'':139B ''toler'':160B ''tong'':36B,50B ''trace'':30B ''transform'':60B ''transit'':63B ''unlaw'':92B ''versidu'':109B ''versidue-shai'':108B ''wealthi'':76B ''wide'':159B ''written'':8B ''yet'':167B', 'scholar', '
The Brothers of Darkness, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, explores the origins and evolution of the Dark Brotherhood, tracing its roots from the Morag Tong cult to a profit-driven assassin organization. The book highlights themes of secrecy, power, and moral ambiguity, emphasizing the Brotherhood’s dual identity as both a feared cult and a necessary force in Tamriel''s political landscape.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_waterwalking', 'This legandary potion purportedly allows the user to walk across the surface of water for a short duration. Only a few of these potions exist, hidden deep within Raven Rock Mine.', '''across'':13B ''allow'':8B ''deep'':30B ''durat'':21B ''exist'':28B ''hidden'':29B ''legandari'':5B ''mine'':34B ''potion'':1A,6B,27B ''purport'':7B ''raven'':32B ''rock'':33B ''short'':20B ''surfac'':15B ''user'':10B ''walk'':12B ''water'':17B ''waterwalk'':3A ''within'':31B', 'alchemist', 'You know nothing about this potion or its origin but an alchemist might know more.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wreck_of_the_pride_of_tel_vos', 'The Wreck of The Pride of Tel Vos is a shipwreck located on a small island east of Winterhold, due east of the city. The wreck is home to a small group of bandits who have set up camp around the ruined vessel, using it as their hideout. ', '''around'':47B ''bandit'':41B ''camp'':46B ''citi'':31B ''due'':27B ''east'':24B,28B ''group'':39B ''hideout'':55B ''home'':35B ''island'':23B ''locat'':19B ''pride'':4A,12B ''ruin'':49B ''set'':44B ''shipwreck'':18B ''small'':22B,38B ''tel'':6A,14B ''use'':51B ''vessel'':50B ''vos'':7A,15B ''winterhold'':26B ''wreck'':1A,9B,33B', 'winterhold, sailor', 'The Wreck of The Pride of Tel Vos is a shipwreck located on a small island east of Winterhold, due east of the city. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hall_of_the_elements', 'The Hall of the Elements is a grand training and meeting space within the College of Winterhold, designed for the study and practice of magical arts. This large, circular room is used not only for spell casting training but also for classes, lectures, and official meetings among the College''s faculty and students. A pair of massive wooden doors serve as the main entrance, leading into an antechamber. From there, one can access the Arch-Mage''s Quarters to the northwest or the Arcanaeum, the College’s renowned library, to the southeast.

The hall itself boasts a high ceiling supported by a ring of imposing pillars, with a series of wooden benches surrounding the perimeter for seating. Small light spheres are placed between every two benches, illuminating the room with a soft glow. At the center of the hall is a powerful focus point, where magical energy rises upward toward the ceiling, acting as a visual representation of the College’s profound connection to the arcane. The College symbol is intricately worked into the design of the gates, further emphasizing the importance of this space within the institution.', '''access'':77B ''act'':157B ''also'':44B ''among'':51B ''antechamb'':72B ''arcan'':169B ''arcanaeum'':89B ''arch'':80B ''arch-mag'':79B ''art'':30B ''bench'':116B,130B ''boast'':100B ''cast'':41B ''ceil'':103B,156B ''center'':140B ''circular'':33B ''class'':46B ''colleg'':19B,53B,171B ''college’'':91B,164B ''connect'':166B ''design'':22B,178B ''door'':63B ''element'':4A,9B ''emphas'':183B ''energi'':151B ''entranc'':68B ''everi'':128B ''faculti'':55B ''focus'':147B ''gate'':181B ''glow'':137B ''grand'':12B ''hall'':1A,6B,98B,143B ''high'':102B ''illumin'':131B ''import'':185B ''impos'':109B ''institut'':191B ''intric'':174B ''larg'':32B ''lead'':69B ''lectur'':47B ''librari'':93B ''light'':123B ''mage'':81B ''magic'':29B,150B ''main'':67B ''massiv'':61B ''meet'':15B,50B ''northwest'':86B ''offici'':49B ''one'':75B ''pair'':59B ''perimet'':119B ''pillar'':110B ''place'':126B ''point'':148B ''power'':146B ''practic'':27B ''profound'':165B ''quarter'':83B ''renown'':92B ''represent'':161B ''ring'':107B ''rise'':152B ''room'':34B,133B ''seat'':121B ''seri'':113B ''serv'':64B ''small'':122B ''soft'':136B ''southeast'':96B ''space'':16B,188B ''spell'':40B ''sphere'':124B ''student'':57B ''studi'':25B ''support'':104B ''surround'':117B ''symbol'':172B ''toward'':154B ''train'':13B,42B ''two'':129B ''upward'':153B ''use'':36B ''visual'':160B ''winterhold'':21B ''within'':17B,189B ''wooden'':62B,11