INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dread_zombie', 'Dread Zombie is a Conjuration spell that reanimates a very powerful dead body to fight for the caster for a limited time. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''bodi'':15B ''cast'':32B ''caster'':20B ''conjur'':7B ''dead'':14B ''dread'':1A,3B ''expert'':28B ''fight'':17B ''level'':30B ''limit'':23B ''power'':13B ''reanim'':10B ''requir'':26B ''skill'':29B ''spell'':8B ''time'':24B ''zombi'':2A,4B', 'mage', '
Dread Zombie is a spell that reanimates a very powerful dead body, bringing it back to life to fight for the caster for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('moesring_pass', 'Moesring Pass is a rugged mountain pass located in the frozen wilds of northwestern Solstheim. Positioned due northwest of the Temple of Miraak and east-northeast of Fahlbtharz, this icy thoroughfare cuts through the harsh terrain, offering a route steeped in peril and natural beauty. The pass, surrounded by snow-draped peaks and windswept valleys, is as treacherous as it is picturesque.Snowclad Ruins is a small outdoor Nordic ruin situated in the icy wilderness of Solstheim. Located northwest of the Temple of Miraak and southeast of Hrothmund''s Barrow, this site is perched amidst snow-covered terrain, exuding an eerie and ancient atmosphere. ', '''amidst'':98B ''ancient'':107B ''atmospher'':108B ''barrow'':93B ''beauti'':48B ''cover'':101B ''cut'':35B ''drape'':55B ''due'':19B ''east'':28B ''east-northeast'':27B ''eeri'':105B ''exud'':103B ''fahlbtharz'':31B ''frozen'':13B ''harsh'':38B ''hrothmund'':91B ''ici'':33B,77B ''locat'':10B,81B ''miraak'':25B,87B ''moesr'':1A,3B ''mountain'':8B ''natur'':47B ''nordic'':72B ''northeast'':29B ''northwest'':20B,82B ''northwestern'':16B ''offer'':40B ''outdoor'':71B ''pass'':2A,4B,9B,50B ''peak'':56B ''perch'':97B ''peril'':45B ''picturesque.snowclad'':66B ''posit'':18B ''rout'':42B ''rug'':7B ''ruin'':67B,73B ''site'':95B ''situat'':74B ''small'':70B ''snow'':54B,100B ''snow-cov'':99B ''snow-drap'':53B ''solstheim'':17B,80B ''southeast'':89B ''steep'':43B ''surround'':51B ''templ'':23B,85B ''terrain'':39B,102B ''thoroughfar'':34B ''treacher'':62B ''valley'':59B ''wild'':14B ''wilder'':78B ''windswept'':58B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('snowclad_ruins', 'Snowclad Ruins is a small outdoor Nordic ruin situated in the icy wilderness of Solstheim. Located northwest of the Temple of Miraak and southeast of Hrothmund''s Barrow. The ruins are home to werebears, fearsome lycanthropic creatures with the ferocity of a bear and the cunning of a man. ', '''barrow'':30B ''bear'':45B ''creatur'':39B ''cun'':48B ''fearsom'':37B ''feroc'':42B ''home'':34B ''hrothmund'':28B ''ici'':14B ''locat'':18B ''lycanthrop'':38B ''man'':51B ''miraak'':24B ''nordic'':9B ''northwest'':19B ''outdoor'':8B ''ruin'':2A,4B,10B,32B ''situat'':11B ''small'':7B ''snowclad'':1A,3B ''solstheim'':17B ''southeast'':26B ''templ'':22B ''werebear'':36B ''wilder'':15B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('broken_tusk_mine', '
Broken Tusk Mine is a small heart stone mine located north of Raven Rock and southeast of Bristleback Cave on Solstheim. The mine is inhabited by rieklings, who have taken over the site and claimed it as their own.', '''bristleback'':21B ''broken'':1A,4B ''cave'':22B ''claim'':38B ''heart'':10B ''inhabit'':28B ''locat'':13B ''mine'':3A,6B,12B,26B ''north'':14B ''raven'':16B ''riekl'':30B ''rock'':17B ''site'':36B ''small'':9B ''solstheim'':24B ''southeast'':19B ''stone'':11B ''taken'':33B ''tusk'':2A,5B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fur_bracers', 'Fur Bracers have basic protection quality. Their visual design is minimal, with strips of fur and leather bound for light coverage. They can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '''basic'':6B ''bound'':20B ''bracer'':2A,4B ''coverag'':23B ''craft'':28B ''design'':11B ''fur'':1A,3B,17B ''leather'':19B,35B ''light'':22B ''minim'':13B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''strip'':15B ''tempered/improved'':32B ''use'':34B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':38B', 'blacksmith', 'Fur Bracers have basic protection quality. Their visual design is minimal, with strips of fur and leather bound for light coverage. They can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using leather at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('creep_cluster', 'Creep Cluster is a mass of orange-brown roots found growing over rocks in the sulfur-rich region of Eastmarch. Alchemy effects: Restore Magicka, Damage Stamina Regen, Fortify Carry Weight, and Weakness to Magic.', '''alchemi'':25B ''brown'':11B ''carri'':33B ''cluster'':2A,4B ''creep'':1A,3B ''damag'':29B ''eastmarch'':24B ''effect'':26B ''fortifi'':32B ''found'':13B ''grow'':14B ''magic'':38B ''magicka'':28B ''mass'':7B ''orang'':10B ''orange-brown'':9B ''regen'':31B ''region'':22B ''restor'':27B ''rich'':21B ''rock'':16B ''root'':12B ''stamina'':30B ''sulfur'':20B ''sulfur-rich'':19B ''weak'':36B ''weight'':34B', 'alchemist', 'Creep Cluster is a mass of orange-brown roots found growing over rocks in the sulfur-rich region of Eastmarch. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('coldharbour', 'Coldharbour is a bleak and desolate realm of Oblivion, presided over by Molag Bal, the Daedric Prince of Domination. This realm serves as a twisted reflection of Nirn, constructed through a combination of mocking imitation and the outright appropriation of its features. Coldharbour is characterized by its lifeless landscape and is populated by Daedra as well as the Soul Shriven, mortals condemned to eternal torment. Those who have made pacts with Molag Bal can also be found residing within this grim plane, while the souls of vampires are directed to Coldharbour upon their death.', '''also'':76B ''appropri'':40B ''bal'':15B,74B ''bleak'':5B ''character'':46B ''coldharbour'':1A,2B,44B,92B ''combin'':33B ''condemn'':63B ''construct'':30B ''daedra'':55B ''daedric'':17B ''death'':95B ''desol'':7B ''direct'':90B ''domin'':20B ''etern'':65B ''featur'':43B ''found'':78B ''grim'':82B ''imit'':36B ''landscap'':50B ''lifeless'':49B ''made'':70B ''mock'':35B ''molag'':14B,73B ''mortal'':62B ''nirn'':29B ''oblivion'':10B ''outright'':39B ''pact'':71B ''plane'':83B ''popul'':53B ''presid'':11B ''princ'':18B ''realm'':8B,22B ''reflect'':27B ''resid'':79B ''serv'':23B ''shriven'':61B ''soul'':60B,86B ''torment'':66B ''twist'':26B ''upon'':93B ''vampir'':88B ''well'':57B ''within'':80B', 'scholar, daedra, daedric', '
Coldharbour is a bleak realm of Oblivion ruled by Molag Bal, the Daedric Prince of Domination. It mirrors Nirn in a twisted and mocking way, with a lifeless landscape populated by Daedra and the Soul Shriven—mortals condemned to eternal torment. Those who make pacts with Molag Bal, as well as the souls of vampires, are sent to Coldharbour after death.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hell', 'Oblivion, often referred to as Hell or the Outer Realms, is a vast and complex realm within the Aurbis, primarily inhabited by the Daedra, who are et''Ada that did not participate in the creation of the Mundus. It encompasses at least sixteen major Planes, each presided over by a Daedric Prince, and contains over 37,000 documented planes, including various chaos realms and pocket realities. While many of these realms are governed by powerful Daedra, some are ruled by mortals who have achieved immortality.

Oblivion is considered a distinct universe separate from Mundus, with its landscapes shaped by the perceptions of those who enter, often creating illusions that resemble familiar earthly elements. The nature of each Daedric realm varies widely, ranging from the serene and beautiful to the bizarre and desolate. For instance, notable realms include Apocrypha, ruled by Hermaeus Mora; Coldharbour, ruled by Molag Bal; and the Shivering Isles, formerly ruled by Jyggalag and now by Sheogorath. Each realm reflects the character and essence of its ruler, embodying the chaotic and ever-changing nature of Oblivion itself.', '''000'':58B ''37'':57B ''achiev'':85B ''ada'':29B ''apocrypha'':139B ''aurbi'':20B ''bal'':148B ''beauti'':128B ''bizarr'':131B ''chang'':177B ''chao'':63B ''chaotic'':173B ''charact'':165B ''coldharbour'':144B ''complex'':16B ''consid'':89B ''contain'':55B ''creat'':108B ''creation'':36B ''daedra'':25B,77B ''daedric'':52B,119B ''desol'':133B ''distinct'':91B ''document'':59B ''earth'':113B ''element'':114B ''embodi'':171B ''encompass'':41B ''enter'':106B ''essenc'':167B ''et'':28B ''ever'':176B ''ever-chang'':175B ''familiar'':112B ''former'':153B ''govern'':74B ''hell'':1A,7B ''hermaeus'':142B ''illus'':109B ''immort'':86B ''includ'':61B,138B ''inhabit'':22B ''instanc'':135B ''isl'':152B ''jyggalag'':156B ''landscap'':98B ''least'':43B ''major'':45B ''mani'':69B ''molag'':147B ''mora'':143B ''mortal'':82B ''mundus'':39B,95B ''natur'':116B,178B ''notabl'':136B ''oblivion'':2B,87B,180B ''often'':3B,107B ''outer'':10B ''particip'':33B ''percept'':102B ''plane'':46B,60B ''pocket'':66B ''power'':76B ''presid'':48B ''primarili'':21B ''princ'':53B ''rang'':123B ''realiti'':67B ''realm'':11B,17B,64B,72B,120B,137B,162B ''refer'':4B ''reflect'':163B ''resembl'':111B ''rule'':80B,140B,145B,154B ''ruler'':170B ''separ'':93B ''seren'':126B ''shape'':99B ''sheogorath'':160B ''shiver'':151B ''sixteen'':44B ''univers'':92B ''vari'':121B ''various'':62B ''vast'':14B ''wide'':122B ''within'':18B', 'scholar, daedra, daedric', 'Oblivion, also known as Hell or the Outer Realms, is a vast and chaotic realm within the Aurbis, primarily inhabited by Daedra, beings who did not partake in the creation of the Mundus. It consists of at least sixteen major planes, each ruled by a Daedric Prince, and thousands of other realms shaped by the perceptions of those who enter. These realms vary widely in nature, from serene to bizarre and desolate. Notable realms include Apocrypha, Coldharbour, and the Shivering Isles, each reflecting the essence of their respective rulers, and Oblivion itself embodies chaos and constant change.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mara''s_eye_pond', 'Mara''s Eye Pond is a small, tranquil lake located due east of Gallows Rock in Eastmarch. At the center of the pond is a small island concealing a trapdoor that leads to Mara''s Eye Den, which is rumoured to be a home to vampires. On the northern shore of the pond lies Gallows Hall, adding another point of interest to the area. ', '''ad'':61B ''anoth'':62B ''area'':68B ''center'':24B ''conceal'':32B ''den'':41B ''due'':15B ''east'':16B ''eastmarch'':21B ''eye'':3A,7B,40B ''gallow'':18B,59B ''hall'':60B ''home'':48B ''interest'':65B ''island'':31B ''lake'':13B ''lead'':36B ''lie'':58B ''locat'':14B ''mara'':1A,5B,38B ''northern'':53B ''point'':63B ''pond'':4A,8B,27B,57B ''rock'':19B ''rumour'':44B ''shore'':54B ''small'':11B,30B ''tranquil'':12B ''trapdoor'':34B ''vampir'':50B', 'eastmarch', 'Mara''s Eye Pond is a small, tranquil lake located due east of Gallows Rock in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('call_dragon', 'Call Dragon is a Shout that summons a dragon to aid you in your time of need, specifically calling upon Odahviing. The three words of power in this Shout are Od (Snow), which represents the call to the dragon; Ah (Hunter), which signifies the summoning of a creature of the wild; and Viing (Wing), which invokes the dragon''s wings to bring it forth.', '''ah'':42B ''aid'':13B ''bring'':64B ''call'':1A,3B,21B,38B ''creatur'':50B ''dragon'':2A,4B,11B,41B,60B ''forth'':66B ''hunter'':43B ''invok'':58B ''need'':19B ''od'':33B ''odahvi'':23B ''power'':28B ''repres'':36B ''shout'':7B,31B ''signifi'':45B ''snow'':34B ''specif'':20B ''summon'':9B,47B ''three'':25B ''time'':17B ''upon'':22B ''vi'':55B ''wild'':53B ''wing'':56B,62B ''word'':26B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('iron_mace', 'Iron Mace is a blunt iron weapon which deals low damage. To craft it: 3 iron ingots and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. A Novice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using iron at a workbench.', '''2'':21B ''3'':17B ''blacksmith'':26B ''blunt'':7B ''craft'':15B,32B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''forg'':27B ''ingot'':19B ''iron'':1A,3B,8B,18B,40B ''leather'':22B ''low'':12B ''mace'':2A,4B ''novic'':29B ''smith'':30B ''strip'':23B ''tempered/improved'':37B ''use'':39B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':43B', 'blacksmith', 'Iron Mace is a blunt iron weapon which deals low damage. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('call_of_valour', 'Call of Valor is a Shout that summons the valiant heroes of Sovngarde to aid you, transcending space and time. The three words of power in this Shout are Hun (Hero), which calls upon the brave souls of heroes; Kaal (Champion), which invokes the might of champions; and Zoor (Legend), which summons legendary figures to fight beside you.', '''aid'':18B ''besid'':60B ''brave'':39B ''call'':1A,4B,36B ''champion'':44B,50B ''fight'':59B ''figur'':57B ''hero'':14B,34B,42B ''hun'':33B ''invok'':46B ''kaal'':43B ''legend'':53B ''legendari'':56B ''might'':48B ''power'':28B ''shout'':9B,31B ''soul'':40B ''sovngard'':16B ''space'':21B ''summon'':11B,55B ''three'':25B ''time'':23B ''transcend'':20B ''upon'':37B ''valiant'':13B ''valor'':6B ''valour'':3A ''word'':26B ''zoor'':52B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('alduin', 'Alduin, often referred to as the World-Eater, is a powerful black dragon revered in Nord mythology as the harbinger of the end times. Known by various titles, including the First Dragon and the Time-Eater, Alduin is believed to periodically destroy the world, making way for a new cycle of existence. He is considered the self-proclaimed First-Born of Akatosh, embodying a malevolent aspect of the deity associated with time and dragons.

The name "Alduin" can be translated in the Dragon Language to mean "Destroyer Devour Master," reflecting his fearsome nature and role as a force of annihilation. Alduin commands a legion of dragons, dragon priests, and draugr, and his return is seen as a sign of impending doom, signaling the end of the current world and the dawn of a new one. His lore intertwines with the beliefs and traditions of the Nords, who view him both as a deity and a harbinger of destruction.', '''akatosh'':67B ''alduin'':1A,2B,40B,82B,106B ''annihil'':105B ''aspect'':71B ''associ'':75B ''belief'':146B ''believ'':42B ''black'':14B ''born'':65B ''command'':107B ''consid'':58B ''current'':132B ''cycl'':53B ''dawn'':136B ''deiti'':74B,158B ''destroy'':45B,92B ''destruct'':163B ''devour'':93B ''doom'':126B ''dragon'':15B,34B,79B,88B,111B,112B ''draugr'':115B ''eater'':10B,39B ''embodi'':68B ''end'':25B,129B ''exist'':55B ''fearsom'':97B ''first'':33B,64B ''first-born'':63B ''forc'':103B ''harbing'':22B,161B ''impend'':125B ''includ'':31B ''intertwin'':143B ''known'':27B ''languag'':89B ''legion'':109B ''lore'':142B ''make'':48B ''malevol'':70B ''master'':94B ''mean'':91B ''mytholog'':19B ''name'':81B ''natur'':98B ''new'':52B,139B ''nord'':18B,151B ''often'':3B ''one'':140B ''period'':44B ''power'':13B ''priest'':113B ''proclaim'':62B ''refer'':4B ''reflect'':95B ''return'':118B ''rever'':16B ''role'':100B ''seen'':120B ''self'':61B ''self-proclaim'':60B ''sign'':123B ''signal'':127B ''time'':26B,38B,77B ''time-eat'':37B ''titl'':30B ''tradit'':148B ''translat'':85B ''various'':29B ''view'':153B ''way'':49B ''world'':9B,47B,133B ''world-eat'':8B', 'scholar, dragon, priest, miraakcult', 'Alduin, the World-Eater, is a powerful black dragon in Nord mythology, known as the harbinger of the end times. Believed to destroy the world periodically, Alduin is considered the First-Born of Akatosh and represents a malevolent aspect of the deity tied to time and dragons. His name, "Alduin," translates to "Destroyer Devour Master" in the Dragon Language, highlighting his destructive nature. He commands dragons, dragon priests, and draugr, with his return signaling the end of the world and the start of a new cycle. Nords view him both as a deity and a force of annihilation.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('high_king_torygg', 'High King Torygg was the ruler of Skyrim and the Jarl of Solitude until his death in 4E 201. The son of Istlod, who had reigned for nearly twenty-five years, Torygg was formally named his successor by the Moot, despite the growing calls for Skyrim''s independence from the influential Ulfric Stormcloak. Torygg respected Ulfric''s passionate stance and sought to engage him in dialogue about his views, unaware that Ulfric had come with the intention of challenging him for the throne.

The encounter between Torygg and Ulfric culminated in tragedy, as Ulfric used his thu''um to overpower the young king and subsequently killed him. While Ulfric viewed the act as a rightful challenge for leadership, many—including the Empire and several Jarls—considered it regicide, noting Torygg''s limited martial training compared to Ulfric''s experience as a war veteran. Following Torygg''s death, his widow, Elisif the Fair, ascended to the position of Jarl of Solitude and aimed to claim the title of High Queen with the support of the Empire. ', '''201'':22B ''4e'':21B ''act'':116B ''aim'':164B ''ascend'':155B ''call'':48B ''challeng'':83B,120B ''claim'':166B ''come'':78B ''compar'':137B ''culmin'':94B ''death'':19B,149B ''despit'':45B ''dialogu'':70B ''elisif'':152B ''empir'':125B,177B ''encount'':89B ''engag'':67B ''experi'':141B ''fair'':154B ''five'':34B ''follow'':146B ''formal'':38B ''grow'':47B ''high'':1A,4B,170B ''independ'':52B ''influenti'':55B ''intent'':81B ''istlod'':26B ''jarl'':14B,160B ''jarls—consid'':128B ''kill'':110B ''king'':2A,5B,107B ''leadership'':122B ''limit'':134B ''many—includ'':123B ''martial'':135B ''moot'':44B ''name'':39B ''near'':31B ''note'':131B ''overpow'':104B ''passion'':62B ''posit'':158B ''queen'':171B ''regicid'':130B ''reign'':29B ''respect'':59B ''right'':119B ''ruler'':9B ''sever'':127B ''skyrim'':11B,50B ''solitud'':16B,162B ''son'':24B ''sought'':65B ''stanc'':63B ''stormcloak'':57B ''subsequ'':109B ''successor'':41B ''support'':174B ''throne'':87B ''thu'':101B ''titl'':168B ''torygg'':3A,6B,36B,58B,91B,132B,147B ''tragedi'':96B ''train'':136B ''twenti'':33B ''twenty-f'':32B ''ulfric'':56B,60B,76B,93B,98B,113B,139B ''um'':102B ''unawar'':74B ''use'':99B ''veteran'':145B ''view'':73B,114B ''war'':144B ''widow'':151B ''year'':35B ''young'':106B', 'nord, scholar', 'High King Torygg was the ruler of Skyrim and the Jarl of Solitude until his death in 4E 201. The son of Istlod, he was named his successor by the Moot, despite Ulfric Stormcloak''s growing calls for Skyrim''s independence. Torygg respected Ulfric’s views and sought dialogue, unaware that Ulfric came to challenge him for the throne. The confrontation ended when Ulfric used his thu''um to kill Torygg, an act many, including the Empire, considered regicide. After his death, his widow, Elisif the Fair, became Jarl of Solitude and sought to claim the title of High Queen with the Empire’s support.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nahkriin', 'Nahkriin is one of the eight high-ranking dragon priests in Skyrim. He was an aloof Dragon priest who did nothing of note during the Dragon war.', '''aloof'':18B ''dragon'':11B,19B,28B ''eight'':7B ''high'':9B ''high-rank'':8B ''nahkriin'':1A,2B ''note'':25B ''noth'':23B ''one'':4B ''priest'':12B,20B ''rank'':10B ''skyrim'':14B ''war'':29B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Nahkriin must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bruma', 'Bruma, a Nibenese city nestled in the Jerall Mountains north of the Imperial City, is known for its Nordic population and snow-covered, cold climate. The city''s architecture reflects its Nordic influence, and its residents practice a mix of traditional Nordic beliefs and the worship of the Divines. The Great Chapel of Talos dominates the city center, and Bruma is connected to other regions by the Silver Road to the Imperial City and the Orange Road to Chorrol. Nearby landmarks include the historic Cloud Ruler Temple, and the city''s underground network of sewers and caves has been the site of significant events, including use by the Mythic Dawn during the Oblivion Crisis.

Bruma has a storied history, playing a key role in various conflicts, such as Varen''s Rebellion and the Oblivion Crisis in 3E 433. The city successfully repelled a Daedric siege during the Crisis, thanks to Martin Septim and reinforcements from other Cyrodiilic cities. Later, Bruma endured attacks from Molag Bal''s forces during the Planemeld in 2E 582 and suffered losses like the destruction of its Mages Guild hall by the Order of the Black Worm. In the Fourth Era, Bruma faced continued challenges, including the destruction of the Dark Brotherhood sanctuary and raids by groups like the Crimson Dirks. Despite these adversities, Bruma remains a resilient and culturally rich city in northern Cyrodiil.', '''2e'':174B ''3e'':139B ''433'':140B ''582'':175B ''advers'':220B ''architectur'':31B ''attack'':164B ''bal'':167B ''belief'':45B ''black'':192B ''brotherhood'':208B ''bruma'':1A,2B,62B,117B,162B,198B,221B ''cave'':99B ''center'':60B ''challeng'':201B ''chapel'':54B ''chorrol'':81B ''citi'':5B,15B,29B,59B,75B,92B,142B,160B,228B ''climat'':27B ''cloud'':87B ''cold'':26B ''conflict'':128B ''connect'':64B ''continu'':200B ''cover'':25B ''crimson'':216B ''crisi'':116B,137B,150B ''cultur'':226B ''cyrodiil'':159B,231B ''daedric'':146B ''dark'':207B ''dawn'':112B ''despit'':218B ''destruct'':181B,204B ''dirk'':217B ''divin'':51B ''domin'':57B ''endur'':163B ''era'':197B ''event'':106B ''face'':199B ''forc'':169B ''fourth'':196B ''great'':53B ''group'':213B ''guild'':185B ''hall'':186B ''histor'':86B ''histori'':121B ''imperi'':14B,74B ''includ'':84B,107B,202B ''influenc'':35B ''jeral'':9B ''key'':124B ''known'':17B ''landmark'':83B ''later'':161B ''like'':179B,214B ''loss'':178B ''mage'':184B ''martin'':153B ''mix'':41B ''molag'':166B ''mountain'':10B ''mythic'':111B ''nearbi'':82B ''nestl'':6B ''network'':95B ''nibenes'':4B ''nordic'':20B,34B,44B ''north'':11B ''northern'':230B ''oblivion'':115B,136B ''orang'':78B ''order'':189B ''planemeld'':172B ''play'':122B ''popul'':21B ''practic'':39B ''raid'':211B ''rebellion'':133B ''reflect'':32B ''region'':67B ''reinforc'':156B ''remain'':222B ''repel'':144B ''resid'':38B ''resili'':224B ''rich'':227B ''road'':71B,79B ''role'':125B ''ruler'':88B ''sanctuari'':209B ''septim'':154B ''sewer'':97B ''sieg'':147B ''signific'':105B ''silver'':70B ''site'':103B ''snow'':24B ''snow-cov'':23B ''stori'':120B ''success'':143B ''suffer'':177B ''talo'':56B ''templ'':89B ''thank'':151B ''tradit'':43B ''underground'':94B ''use'':108B ''varen'':131B ''various'':127B ''worm'':193B ''worship'':48B', 'scholar, imperial', 'Bruma, located in the Jerall Mountains north of the Imperial City, is known for its cold climate and Nordic population. The city''s architecture and religious practices reflect its Nordic influence, with the Great Chapel of Talos at its center. Bruma has played a significant role in Cyrodiil''s history, notably during the Oblivion Crisis and the Planemeld, when it successfully repelled Daedric forces. The city has also faced other challenges, including raids by the Crimson Dirks and the destruction of its Mages Guild hall. Despite these struggles, Bruma remains a resilient and culturally rich city in northern Cyrodiil.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falkreath_stormcloak_camp', 'Falkreath Stormcloak Camp is a military encampment located east of Helgen in Falkreath Hold. It serves as a base for the Stormcloak forces in the region and is typically commanded by Thorygg Sun-Killer.', '''base'':22B ''camp'':3A,6B ''command'':33B ''east'':12B ''encamp'':10B ''falkreath'':1A,4B,16B ''forc'':26B ''helgen'':14B ''hold'':17B ''killer'':38B ''locat'':11B ''militari'':9B ''region'':29B ''serv'':19B ''stormcloak'':2A,5B,25B ''sun'':37B ''sun-kil'':36B ''thorygg'':35B ''typic'':32B', 'falkreath, stormcloak', 'Falkreath Stormcloak Camp is a military encampment located east of Helgen in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('circle_of_protection', 'Circle of Protection is a Restoration spell that creates a protective barrier on the ground, which repels undead and daedra from entering the area while healing allies within it. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''alli'':30B ''area'':27B ''barrier'':15B ''cast'':40B ''circl'':1A,4B ''creat'':12B ''daedra'':23B ''enter'':25B ''expert'':36B ''ground'':18B ''heal'':29B ''level'':38B ''protect'':3A,6B,14B ''repel'':20B ''requir'':34B ''restor'':9B ''skill'':37B ''spell'':10B ''undead'':21B ''within'':31B', 'mage', 'Circle of Protection is a spell that creates a protective barrier on the ground, repelling undead and daedra from entering the area while healing allies within it. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('chitin_helmet', 'Chitin Helmet is a basic chitin helmet with good protection quality. Its visual design is organic and jagged, with dark, shell-like plates and a rough, natural texture. To craft it: 1leather, 1 iron ingot and 3 chitin at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using chitin at a workbench.', '''1'':36B ''1leather'':35B ''3'':40B ''adept'':47B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':44B ''chitin'':1A,3B,8B,41B,58B ''craft'':33B,50B ''dark'':22B ''design'':16B ''forg'':45B ''good'':11B ''helmet'':2A,4B,9B ''ingot'':38B ''iron'':37B ''jag'':20B ''like'':25B ''natur'':30B ''organ'':18B ''plate'':26B ''protect'':12B ''qualiti'':13B ''rough'':29B ''shell'':24B ''shell-lik'':23B ''smith'':48B ''tempered/improved'':55B ''textur'':31B ''use'':57B ''visual'':15B ''workbench'':61B', 'blacksmith', 'Chitin Helmet is a basic chitin helmet with good protection quality. Its visual design is organic and jagged, with dark, shell-like plates and a rough, natural texture. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nirnroot', '
Nirnroot is a bright green plant typically found near water, known for its glowing appearance and the unique chiming sound it emits, making it easier to locate at night. Alchemy effects: Damage Health, Damage Stamina, Invisibility, and Resist Magic.', '''alchemi'':31B ''appear'':16B ''bright'':5B ''chime'':20B ''damag'':33B,35B ''easier'':26B ''effect'':32B ''emit'':23B ''found'':9B ''glow'':15B ''green'':6B ''health'':34B ''invis'':37B ''known'':12B ''locat'':28B ''magic'':40B ''make'':24B ''near'':10B ''night'':30B ''nirnroot'':1A,2B ''plant'':7B ''resist'':39B ''sound'':21B ''stamina'':36B ''typic'':8B ''uniqu'':19B ''water'':11B', 'alchemist', 'Nirnroot is a bright green plant typically found near water, known for its glowing appearance and the unique chiming sound it emits, making it easier to locate at night.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_minor_stamina', 'A simple concoction that restores a small amount of stamina, useful for light exertions and quick recovery. Restores a small amount of stamina, ideal for minor exertions and short bursts of activity. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists.', '''activ'':36B ''alchemist'':48B ''amount'':12B,25B ''burst'':34B ''concoct'':7B ''exert'':18B,31B ''found'':41B ''ideal'':28B ''light'':17B ''loot'':44B ''minor'':3A,30B ''potion'':1A,38B ''purchas'':46B ''quick'':20B ''random'':43B ''recoveri'':21B ''restor'':9B,22B ''short'':33B ''simpl'':6B ''small'':11B,24B ''stamina'':4A,14B,27B ''use'':15B', 'alchemist, hunter, warrior, companions, traveler', 'The Potion of Minor Stamina restores a small amount of stamina for light exertions. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('armor', 'These magical effects are defensive Alteration spells that create barriers around the caster, temporarily increasing their armor rating to reduce incoming physical damage. This effect is only available as a spell, offering a reliable option for mages seeking enhanced protection in combat.', '''alter'':7B ''armor'':1A,18B ''around'':12B ''avail'':29B ''barrier'':11B ''caster'':14B ''combat'':43B ''creat'':10B ''damag'':24B ''defens'':6B ''effect'':4B,26B ''enhanc'':40B ''incom'':22B ''increas'':16B ''mage'':38B ''magic'':3B ''offer'':33B ''option'':36B ''physic'':23B ''protect'':41B ''rate'':19B ''reduc'':21B ''reliabl'':35B ''seek'':39B ''spell'':8B,32B ''temporarili'':15B', 'mage', 'Spells like this make a person harder to hurt, as if they''re wearing invisible armor. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skeever_tail', 'Skeever Tails are dropped by dead skeevers. Alchemy effects: Damage Stamina Regen, Ravage Health, Damage Health, and Fortify Light Armor', '''alchemi'':10B ''armor'':22B ''damag'':12B,17B ''dead'':8B ''drop'':6B ''effect'':11B ''fortifi'':20B ''health'':16B,18B ''light'':21B ''ravag'':15B ''regen'':14B ''skeever'':1A,3B,9B ''stamina'':13B ''tail'':2A,4B', 'alchemist', 'Skeever Tails are dropped by dead skeevers. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('detect_dead', 'Detect Dead is an Alteration spell that highlights nearby undead, Daedra, and automatons with a glowing aura, making them visible through walls. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''alter'':7B ''aura'':19B ''automaton'':15B ''cast'':32B ''daedra'':13B ''dead'':2A,4B ''detect'':1A,3B ''expert'':28B ''glow'':18B ''highlight'':10B ''level'':30B ''make'':20B ''nearbi'':11B ''requir'':26B ''skill'':29B ''spell'':8B ''undead'':12B ''visibl'':22B ''wall'':24B', 'mage', 'Detect Dead is a spell that makes undead, Daedra, and automatons glow, allowing the caster to see them through walls. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('luminous_russula', 'Luminous Russula, a dark brown fungus originating from Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Lingering Damage Stamina, Lingering Damage Health, Waterbreathing, and Fear.', '''alchemi'':22B ''brown'':7B ''caravan'':21B ''damag'':25B,28B ''dark'':6B ''effect'':23B ''fear'':32B ''fungus'':8B ''health'':29B ''ingredi'':14B ''khajiit'':20B ''linger'':24B,27B ''lumin'':1A,3B ''origin'':9B ''purchas'':18B ''russula'':2A,4B ''stamina'':26B ''vvardenfel'':11B ''waterbreath'':30B', 'alchemist', 'Luminous Russula, a dark brown fungus originating from Vvardenfell, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans.
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ebonyflesh', 'Ebonyflesh is an Alteration spell that greatly increases the caster''s armor rating for a short duration, providing substantial protection. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''alter'':5B ''armor'':13B ''cast'':29B ''caster'':11B ''durat'':18B ''ebonyflesh'':1A,2B ''expert'':25B ''great'':8B ''increas'':9B ''level'':27B ''protect'':21B ''provid'':19B ''rate'':14B ''requir'':23B ''short'':17B ''skill'':26B ''spell'':6B ''substanti'':20B', 'mage', 'Ebonyflesh is a spell that makes the caster’s skin as strong as ebony, offering powerful protection for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('honningbrew_meadery', 'Honningbrew Meadery, owned by Sabjorn, is a bustling meadery located southeast of Whiterun and north-northeast of Riverwood, nestled within the fertile plains of Whiterun Hold. Renowned for its production of Honningbrew Mead, it stands as a proud competitor to the famous Black-Briar Meadery of Riften.

The meadery consists of two buildings: the main brewing hall, Honningbrew Meadery, and the adjacent Honningbrew Boilery. Its strategic location near Whiterun makes it a hub for trade and a popular supplier of mead throughout Skyrim. The rich aroma of fermenting honey and the sounds of activity within are a testament to its thriving operation and its ambition to carve a name for itself among the land’s most cherished brewers.', '''activ'':98B ''adjac'':66B ''ambit'':109B ''among'':116B ''aroma'':90B ''black'':47B ''black-briar'':46B ''boileri'':68B ''brew'':60B ''brewer'':121B ''briar'':48B ''build'':57B ''bustl'':10B ''carv'':111B ''cherish'':120B ''competitor'':42B ''consist'':54B ''famous'':45B ''ferment'':92B ''fertil'':25B ''hall'':61B ''hold'':29B ''honey'':93B ''honningbrew'':1A,3B,35B,62B,67B ''hub'':77B ''land’'':118B ''locat'':12B,71B ''main'':59B ''make'':74B ''mead'':36B,85B ''meaderi'':2A,4B,11B,49B,53B,63B ''name'':113B ''near'':72B ''nestl'':22B ''north'':18B ''north-northeast'':17B ''northeast'':19B ''oper'':106B ''own'':5B ''plain'':26B ''popular'':82B ''product'':33B ''proud'':41B ''renown'':30B ''rich'':89B ''riften'':51B ''riverwood'':21B ''sabjorn'':7B ''skyrim'':87B ''sound'':96B ''southeast'':13B ''stand'':38B ''strateg'':70B ''supplier'':83B ''testament'':102B ''thrive'':105B ''throughout'':86B ''trade'':79B ''two'':56B ''whiterun'':15B,28B,73B ''within'':23B,99B', 'whiterun', 'Honningbrew Meadery is a bustling meadery located southeast of Whiterun and north-northeast of Riverwood, nestled within the fertile plains of Whiterun Hold. Renowned for its production of Honningbrew Mead, it stands as a proud competitor to the famous Black-Briar Meadery of Riften. You do not know who owns the meadery.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('clairvoyance', 'Clairvoyance: These magical effects are utility-focused Illusion spells that guide the caster along the correct path to their objective by illuminating a magical trail. This effect is only available as a spell and is commonly used by adventurers to navigate complex terrains or dungeons.', '''adventur'':41B ''along'':16B ''avail'':32B ''caster'':15B ''clairvoy'':1A,2B ''common'':38B ''complex'':44B ''correct'':18B ''dungeon'':47B ''effect'':5B,29B ''focus'':9B ''guid'':13B ''illumin'':24B ''illus'':10B ''magic'':4B,26B ''navig'':43B ''object'':22B ''path'':19B ''spell'':11B,35B ''terrain'':45B ''trail'':27B ''use'':39B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B', 'mage', 'This spell helps you find your way by showing a magical path to your destination. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_minor_healing', 'This simple potion offers a minor boost to vitality, ideal for patching up small wounds in the midst of an adventure. Restores a small amount of health, suitable for minor injuries and light encounters. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists.', '''adventur'':25B ''alchemist'':50B ''amount'':29B ''boost'':11B ''encount'':38B ''found'':43B ''heal'':4A ''health'':31B ''ideal'':14B ''injuri'':35B ''light'':37B ''loot'':46B ''midst'':22B ''minor'':3A,10B,34B ''offer'':8B ''patch'':16B ''potion'':1A,7B,40B ''purchas'':48B ''random'':45B ''restor'':26B ''simpl'':6B ''small'':18B,28B ''suitabl'':32B ''vital'':13B ''wound'':19B', 'alchemist, healer, priest, traveler, peasant', 'The Potion of Minor Healing restores a small amount of health for minor wounds. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('sabre_cat', '
Sabre Cats are large, fast, and powerful felines found in the wilds of Skyrim. Known for their sharp front teeth, they are aggressive hunters that will attack on sight. Sabre cats can carry Witbane, a disease that reduces magicka regeneration. They are stealthy and quick, but can be outmaneuvered by dodging, and dislike water, which can be used to evade them. They can be harvested for their pelt for tanning, and eyes for alchemy.', '''aggress'':25B ''alchemi'':76B ''attack'':29B ''carri'':35B ''cat'':2A,4B,33B ''diseas'':38B ''dislik'':55B ''dodg'':53B ''evad'':62B ''eye'':74B ''fast'':7B ''felin'':10B ''found'':11B ''front'':21B ''harvest'':67B ''hunter'':26B ''known'':17B ''larg'':6B ''magicka'':41B ''outmaneuv'':51B ''pelt'':70B ''power'':9B ''quick'':47B ''reduc'':40B ''regener'':42B ''sabr'':1A,3B,32B ''sharp'':20B ''sight'':31B ''skyrim'':16B ''stealthi'':45B ''tan'':72B ''teeth'':22B ''use'':60B ''water'':56B ''wild'':14B ''witban'':36B', 'hunter', 'Sabre Cats are large, fast, and powerful felines found in the wilds of Skyrim. Known for their sharp front teeth, they are aggressive hunters that will attack on sight. ', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('reanimate_corpse', 'Reanimate Corpse is a Conjuration spell that raises a more powerful dead body to fight for the caster for a limited time. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':28B ''bodi'':15B ''cast'':32B ''caster'':20B ''conjur'':7B ''corps'':2A,4B ''dead'':14B ''fight'':17B ''level'':30B ''limit'':23B ''power'':13B ''rais'':10B ''reanim'':1A,3B ''requir'':26B ''skill'':29B ''spell'':8B ''time'':24B', 'mage', '
Reanimate Corpse is a spell that raises a more powerful dead body, reanimating it to fight for the caster for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('clear_skies', 'Clear Skies is a Shout that causes Skyrim itself to yield before the Thu''um, clearing away fog and inclement weather. The three words of power in this Shout are Lok (Sky), which calls upon the power of the heavens; Vah (Spring), which ushers in clear, refreshing weather; and Koor (Summer), which brings warm, clear skies to the land.', '''away'':19B ''bring'':55B ''call'':36B ''caus'':9B ''clear'':1A,3B,18B,48B,57B ''fog'':20B ''heaven'':42B ''inclement'':22B ''koor'':52B ''land'':61B ''lok'':33B ''power'':28B,39B ''refresh'':49B ''shout'':7B,31B ''sky'':2A,4B,34B,58B ''skyrim'':10B ''spring'':44B ''summer'':53B ''three'':25B ''thu'':16B ''um'':17B ''upon'':37B ''usher'':46B ''vah'':43B ''warm'':56B ''weather'':23B,50B ''word'':26B ''yield'':13B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('poison_rune', 'Poison Rune is an Alteration spell that places a magical rune on the ground, which explodes with a burst of toxic gas, dealing poison damage to any enemies who step on it. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''alter'':7B ''apprentic'':38B ''burst'':21B ''cast'':42B ''damag'':27B ''deal'':25B ''enemi'':30B ''explod'':18B ''gas'':24B ''ground'':16B ''level'':40B ''magic'':12B ''place'':10B ''poison'':1A,3B,26B ''requir'':36B ''rune'':2A,4B,13B ''skill'':39B ''spell'':8B ''step'':32B ''toxic'':23B', 'mage', '
Poison Rune is a spell that places a magical rune on the ground, which detonates with toxic gas, dealing poison damage to any enemies who step on it. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rii_vaaz_zol', 'Soul Tear is a Shout that cuts through flesh and shatters the soul, allowing you to command the will of the fallen. The three words of power in this Shout are Rii (Essence), which targets the essence of the foe; Vaaz (Tear), which rends their soul apart; and Zol (Zombie), which raises the fallen to serve you as a zombie under your control.', '''allow'':17B ''apart'':50B ''command'':20B ''control'':66B ''cut'':10B ''essenc'':36B,40B ''fallen'':25B,57B ''flesh'':12B ''foe'':43B ''power'':30B ''rais'':55B ''rend'':47B ''rii'':1A,35B ''serv'':59B ''shatter'':14B ''shout'':8B,33B ''soul'':4B,16B,49B ''target'':38B ''tear'':5B,45B ''three'':27B ''vaaz'':2A,44B ''word'':28B ''zol'':3A,52B ''zombi'':53B,63B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('storm_call', 'Storm Call is a Shout that summons a destructive storm, calling down lightning to strike your enemies. The three words of power in this Shout are Strun (Storm), which conjures the violent storm; Bah (Wrath), which intensifies the fury of the storm; and Qo (Lightning), which directs the lightning to strike down foes with powerful bolts.', '''bah'':36B ''bolt'':58B ''call'':2A,4B,13B ''conjur'':32B ''destruct'':11B ''direct'':49B ''enemi'':19B ''foe'':55B ''furi'':41B ''intensifi'':39B ''lightn'':15B,47B,51B ''power'':24B,57B ''qo'':46B ''shout'':7B,27B ''storm'':1A,3B,12B,30B,35B,44B ''strike'':17B,53B ''strun'':29B ''summon'':9B ''three'':21B ''violent'':34B ''word'':22B ''wrath'':37B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fenn''s_gulch_mine', 'Fenn''s Gulch Mine is a small silver mine located in the northwestern part of Karthwasten in the Reach.  There is nothing of interest at this location.', '''fenn'':1A,5B ''gulch'':3A,7B ''interest'':28B ''karthwasten'':20B ''locat'':14B,31B ''mine'':4A,8B,13B ''northwestern'':17B ''noth'':26B ''part'':18B ''reach'':23B ''silver'':12B ''small'':11B', 'reach', 'Fenn''s Gulch Mine is a small silver mine located in the northwestern part of Karthwasten in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_centurion', 'Dwarven Centurions, often referred to as Steam Centurions, are imposing and heavily armored constructs that serve as formidable guardians in Dwemer ruins. Equipped with either an extendable mace or hammer on one arm and a spring-loaded blade on the other, they can deliver devastating melee attacks. Some variants are capable of emitting a scalding blast of steam, enhancing their offensive capabilities. While not as common as smaller Dwarven constructs, their presence signifies heightened security within ancient ruins.', '''ancient'':80B ''arm'':35B ''armor'':15B ''attack'':50B ''blade'':41B ''blast'':59B ''capabl'':54B,65B ''centurion'':2A,4B,10B ''common'':69B ''construct'':16B,73B ''deliv'':47B ''devast'':48B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,72B ''dwemer'':23B ''either'':27B ''emit'':56B ''enhanc'':62B ''equip'':25B ''extend'':29B ''formid'':20B ''guardian'':21B ''hammer'':32B ''heavili'':14B ''heighten'':77B ''impos'':12B ''load'':40B ''mace'':30B ''mele'':49B ''offens'':64B ''often'':5B ''one'':34B ''presenc'':75B ''refer'':6B ''ruin'':24B,81B ''scald'':58B ''secur'':78B ''serv'':18B ''signifi'':76B ''smaller'':71B ''spring'':39B ''spring-load'':38B ''steam'':9B,61B ''variant'':52B ''within'':79B', 'dwemer', '
Dwarven Centurions, or Steam Centurions, are heavily armored constructs found in Dwemer ruins,, that will attack anyone foolish enough to enter a dwemer ruin.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('severio_pelagia''s_house', 'Severio Pelagia''s House is a modest residence located in the Plains District of Whiterun, nestled between the Drunken Huntsman and the bustling market stalls. The home serves as the city dwelling of Severio Pelagia, the proprietor of Pelagia Farm, a prominent agricultural holding just outside Whiterun''s walls.', '''agricultur'':47B ''bustl'':27B ''citi'':35B ''district'':17B ''drunken'':23B ''dwell'':36B ''farm'':44B ''hold'':48B ''home'':31B ''hous'':4A,8B ''huntsman'':24B ''locat'':13B ''market'':28B ''modest'':11B ''nestl'':20B ''outsid'':50B ''pelagia'':2A,6B,39B,43B ''plain'':16B ''promin'':46B ''proprietor'':41B ''resid'':12B ''serv'':32B ''severio'':1A,5B,38B ''stall'':29B ''wall'':53B ''whiterun'':19B,51B', 'whiterun', 'Severio Pelagia''s House is a modest residence located in the Plains District of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_conjuration', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration abilities that amplify the caster;s skill in Conjuration magic, extending the power and duration of spells. This effect is available in pre-crafted potions, can be brewed into custom potions, and can also be applied to enchanted gear. Generally combining at least two of the following ingredients, provided they share this effect, will create a potion with the Fortify Conjuration effect: Blue Butterfly Wing, Blue Mountain Flower, Frost Salts', '''abil'':11B ''also'':45B ''amplifi'':13B ''appli'':47B ''avail'':31B ''blue'':74B,77B ''brew'':39B ''butterfli'':75B ''caster'':15B ''combin'':52B ''conjur'':2A,19B,72B ''craft'':35B ''creat'':66B ''custom'':41B ''durat'':25B ''effect'':5B,29B,64B,73B ''enchant'':49B ''extend'':21B ''flower'':79B ''focus'':9B ''follow'':58B ''fortifi'':1A,71B ''frost'':80B ''gear'':50B ''general'':51B ''ingredi'':59B ''least'':54B ''magic'':4B,20B ''mountain'':78B ''potion'':36B,42B,68B ''power'':23B ''pre'':34B ''pre-craft'':33B ''provid'':60B ''restor'':10B ''salt'':81B ''share'':62B ''skill'':17B ''spell'':27B ''two'':55B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B ''wing'':76B', 'alchemist, mage', 'This magic makes Conjuration spells stronger, making summoned creatures more powerful. An alchemist or mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orchish_greatsword', 'Orcish Greatsword is a two-handed Orcish weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is heavy and brutal, with a rough, greenish hue and primitive, rugged details that emphasize raw strength. To craft it: 4 orichalcum ingots, 2 iron ingots, and 3 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using orichalcum at a workbench.', '''2'':42B ''3'':46B ''4'':39B ''adept'':54B ''blacksmith'':51B ''brutal'':22B ''craft'':37B,57B ''damag'':15B ''deal'':13B ''design'':18B ''detail'':31B ''emphas'':33B ''forg'':52B ''good'':14B ''greatsword'':2A,4B ''greenish'':26B ''hand'':9B ''heavi'':20B ''hue'':27B ''ingot'':41B,44B ''iron'':43B ''leather'':47B ''orchish'':1A ''orcish'':3B,10B ''orichalcum'':40B,65B ''primit'':29B ''raw'':34B ''rough'':25B ''rug'':30B ''smith'':55B ''strength'':35B ''strip'':48B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''two'':8B ''two-hand'':7B ''use'':64B ''visual'':17B ''weapon'':11B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Orcish Greatsword is a two-handed Orcish weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is heavy and brutal, with a rough, greenish hue and primitive, rugged details that emphasize raw strength. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ectoplasm', 'Ectoplasm is an uncommon greyish goo ingredient obtained from ghosts, known for its magical and destructive alchemical properties. Alchemy effects: Restore Magicka, Fortify Destruction, Fortify Magicka, and Damage Health.', '''alchem'':18B ''alchemi'':20B ''damag'':29B ''destruct'':17B,25B ''ectoplasm'':1A,2B ''effect'':21B ''fortifi'':24B,26B ''ghost'':11B ''goo'':7B ''greyish'':6B ''health'':30B ''ingredi'':8B ''known'':12B ''magic'':15B ''magicka'':23B,27B ''obtain'':9B ''properti'':19B ''restor'':22B ''uncommon'':5B', 'alchemist', 'Ectoplasm is an uncommon greyish goo ingredient obtained from ghosts, known for its magical and destructive alchemical properties.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('command', 'These magical effects are offensive Conjuration spells that compel a conjured or summoned entity to obey the caster;s will, overriding its natural behavior. This effect is available as a spell and can also be found on enchanted gear, making it indispensable for skilled conjurers managing Daedric allies.', '''alli'':49B ''also'':35B ''avail'':29B ''behavior'':25B ''caster'':19B ''command'':1A ''compel'':10B ''conjur'':7B,12B,46B ''daedric'':48B ''effect'':4B,27B ''enchant'':39B ''entiti'':15B ''found'':37B ''gear'':40B ''indispens'':43B ''magic'':3B ''make'':41B ''manag'':47B ''natur'':24B ''obey'':17B ''offens'':6B ''overrid'':22B ''skill'':45B ''spell'':8B,32B ''summon'':14B', 'mage', 'This spell forces a summoned creature to obey the caster, even if it doesn;t want to. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('redorans_retreat', 'Redoran''s Retreat is a small, concealed cave located west-northwest of Whiterun and south of Dustman’s Cairn, nestled within the open plains of Whiterun Hold. Hidden at the end of a winding path behind a rocky outcrop, the entrance is easily overlooked, blending seamlessly into the rugged landscape.

The cave serves as a hideout for a group of bandits, who have taken up residence.', '''bandit'':63B ''behind'':38B ''blend'':47B ''cairn'':21B ''cave'':10B,54B ''conceal'':9B ''dustman’'':20B ''easili'':45B ''end'':33B ''entranc'':43B ''group'':61B ''hidden'':30B ''hideout'':58B ''hold'':29B ''landscap'':52B ''locat'':11B ''nestl'':22B ''northwest'':14B ''open'':25B ''outcrop'':41B ''overlook'':46B ''path'':37B ''plain'':26B ''redoran'':1A,3B ''resid'':68B ''retreat'':2A,5B ''rocki'':40B ''rug'':51B ''seamless'':48B ''serv'':55B ''small'':8B ''south'':18B ''taken'':66B ''west'':13B ''west-northwest'':12B ''whiterun'':16B,28B ''wind'':36B ''within'':23B', 'whiterun', 'Redoran''s Retreat is a small, concealed cave located west-northwest of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('snow_elf', 'The Snow Elves, also known as the Ancient Falmer or Ice Elves, were a proud and highly magical race of mer who once inhabited much of Skyrim and parts of High Rock. Known for their pale skin, white hair, and long lifespans, Snow Elves possessed a natural resistance to frost, allowing them to thrive in cold, remote regions. Their civilization was advanced, rivalling even the Altmer of the Summerset Isles. However, the Snow Elves were gradually displaced by the Nords during the late Merethic Era and early First Era.', '''advanc'':64B ''allow'':53B ''also'':6B ''altmer'':68B ''ancient'':10B ''civil'':62B ''cold'':58B ''displac'':79B ''earli'':89B ''elf'':2A ''elv'':5B,14B,46B,76B ''era'':87B,91B ''even'':66B ''falmer'':11B ''first'':90B ''frost'':52B ''gradual'':78B ''hair'':41B ''high'':19B,33B ''howev'':73B ''ice'':13B ''inhabit'':26B ''isl'':72B ''known'':7B,35B ''late'':85B ''lifespan'':44B ''long'':43B ''magic'':20B ''mer'':23B ''mereth'':86B ''much'':27B ''natur'':49B ''nord'':82B ''pale'':38B ''part'':31B ''possess'':47B ''proud'':17B ''race'':21B ''region'':60B ''remot'':59B ''resist'':50B ''rival'':65B ''rock'':34B ''skin'':39B ''skyrim'':29B ''snow'':1A,4B,45B,75B ''summerset'':71B ''thrive'':56B ''white'':40B', 'snowelf ,scholar', 'The Snow Elves, or Ancient Falmer, were a magical race of mer who once thrived in Skyrim and parts of High Rock. Distinguished by their pale skin, white hair, and frost resistance, they excelled in magic and lived in advanced civilizations rivaling the Altmer of Summerset. Their long lifespans and resilience allowed them to flourish in cold regions, but they were gradually displaced by the Nords during the late Merethic and early First Eras.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('rally', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Illusion spells that bolster the morale and combat abilities of allies within range, increasing their health and stamina. This effect is available as a spell and can also be found on enchanted items, making it a key spell for inspiring groups during battle.', '''abil'':17B ''alli'':19B ''also'':36B ''avail'':30B ''battl'':51B ''bolster'':12B ''combat'':16B ''effect'':4B,28B ''enchant'':40B ''focus'':8B ''found'':38B ''group'':49B ''health'':24B ''illus'':9B ''increas'':22B ''inspir'':48B ''item'':41B ''key'':45B ''magic'':3B ''make'':42B ''moral'':14B ''ralli'':1A ''rang'':21B ''spell'':10B,33B,46B ''stamina'':26B ''util'':7B ''utility-focus'':6B ''within'':20B', 'mage', 'This magic inspires your allies, giving them more energy and strength to fight. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vaerminas_torpor', 'Vaermina''s Torpor is a unique alchemical creation tied to the Daedric Prince Vaermina. It allows the user to enter ''The Dreamstride,'' a state of altered consciousness used in rituals. Its effects are said to transport the user through memories and dreams, making it a powerful but dangerous substance.', '''alchem'':9B ''allow'':18B ''alter'':28B ''conscious'':29B ''creation'':10B ''daedric'':14B ''danger'':50B ''dream'':44B ''dreamstrid'':24B ''effect'':34B ''enter'':22B ''make'':45B ''memori'':42B ''power'':48B ''princ'':15B ''ritual'':32B ''said'':36B ''state'':26B ''substanc'':51B ''tie'':11B ''torpor'':2A,5B ''transport'':38B ''uniqu'':8B ''use'':30B ''user'':20B,40B ''vaermina'':1A,3B,16B', 'daedra', 'You know nothing about this potion or its unique effects. The name itself is ominous and suggests terrible things.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('torchbug_thorax', 'Torchbug Thoraxes are bright yellow and can be acquired by catching torchbugs, which appear at night in most non-snowy areas. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Lingering Damage Magicka, Weakness to Magic, and Fortify Stamina.', '''acquir'':11B ''alchemi'':25B ''appear'':16B ''area'':24B ''bright'':6B ''catch'':13B ''damag'':30B ''effect'':26B ''fortifi'':36B ''linger'':29B ''magic'':34B ''magicka'':31B ''night'':18B ''non'':22B ''non-snowi'':21B ''restor'':27B ''snowi'':23B ''stamina'':28B,37B ''thorax'':2A,4B ''torchbug'':1A,3B,14B ''weak'':32B ''yellow'':7B', 'alchemist', 'Torchbug Thoraxes are bright yellow and can be acquired by catching torchbugs, which appear at night in most non-snowy areas. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('talking_stone_camp', 'Talking Stone Camp is a giant camp located northeast of Rorikstead and south of Orotheim in Hjaalmarch. The camp is home to giants and their mammoths, with the typical features of a giant camp, including a large bonfire and scattered mammoth bones.', '''bone'':45B ''bonfir'':41B ''camp'':3A,6B,10B,22B,37B ''featur'':33B ''giant'':9B,26B,36B ''hjaalmarch'':20B ''home'':24B ''includ'':38B ''larg'':40B ''locat'':11B ''mammoth'':29B,44B ''northeast'':12B ''orotheim'':18B ''rorikstead'':14B ''scatter'':43B ''south'':16B ''stone'':2A,5B ''talk'':1A,4B ''typic'':32B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Talking Stone Camp is a giant camp located northeast of Rorikstead in Hjaalmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('watchers_eye', 'Watcher''s Eye, a yellow-brown plant originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Night Eye, Fortify Magicka, Fortify Illusion, and Spell Absorption.', '''absorpt'':36B ''alchemi'':26B ''brown'':9B ''caravan'':25B ''effect'':27B ''eye'':2A,5B,29B ''fortifi'':30B,32B ''illus'':33B ''ingredi'':18B ''isl'':15B ''khajiit'':24B ''magicka'':31B ''night'':28B ''origin'':11B ''plant'':10B ''purchas'':22B ''shiver'':14B ''spell'':35B ''watcher'':1A,3B ''yellow'':8B ''yellow-brown'':7B', 'alchemist', 'Watcher''s Eye, a yellow-brown plant originating from the Shivering Isles, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ustengrav', 'Ustengrav is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located northeast of Morthal and south of High Gate Ruins in Hjaalmarch. It is inhabited by a variety of foes, including bandits, warlocks, and draugr. It is rumored that the Horn of Jurgen Windcaller is located here.', '''bandit'':31B ''draugr'':34B ''foe'':29B ''gate'':18B ''high'':17B ''hjaalmarch'':21B ''horn'':40B ''includ'':30B ''inhabit'':24B ''jurgen'':42B ''locat'':10B,45B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''morthal'':13B ''nordic'':8B ''northeast'':11B ''ruin'':9B,19B ''rumor'':37B ''size'':7B ''south'':15B ''ustengrav'':1A,2B ''varieti'':27B ''warlock'':32B ''windcal'':43B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Ustengrav is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located northeast of Morthal and south in Hjaalmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('courage', 'Courage is an Illusion spell that boosts the target''s confidence, increasing their combat abilities and making them more likely to attack enemies. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''abil'':16B ''apprentic'':28B ''attack'':23B ''boost'':8B ''cast'':32B ''combat'':15B ''confid'':12B ''courag'':1A,2B ''enemi'':24B ''illus'':5B ''increas'':13B ''level'':30B ''like'':21B ''make'':18B ''requir'':26B ''skill'':29B ''spell'':6B ''target'':10B', 'mage', 'Courage is a spell that boosts the target''s confidence, enhancing their combat abilities and making them more likely to attack enemies. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('balmora_blue', 'Balmora Blue is a highly illicit and rare substance, known for its invigorating effects and its ties to smuggling operations. Its rarity and illegality make it a prized and dangerous commodity.', '''balmora'':1A,3B ''blue'':2A,4B ''commod'':33B ''danger'':32B ''effect'':16B ''high'':7B ''illeg'':26B ''illicit'':8B ''invigor'':15B ''known'':12B ''make'':27B ''oper'':22B ''prize'':30B ''rare'':10B ''rariti'':24B ''smuggl'':21B ''substanc'':11B ''tie'':19B', 'erikur, thief, thievesguild, darkbrotherhood', 'You have heard whispers of Balmora Blue but know nothing specific about its effects or origins.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('greywater_grotto', 'Greywater Grotto is a small cave located far east of Falkreath and south-southwest of Helgen in Falkreath Hold. The cave is inhabited by predatory animals like bears and sabre cats.', '''anim'':29B ''bear'':31B ''cat'':34B ''cave'':8B,24B ''east'':11B ''falkreath'':13B,21B ''far'':10B ''greywat'':1A,3B ''grotto'':2A,4B ''helgen'':19B ''hold'':22B ''inhabit'':26B ''like'':30B ''locat'':9B ''predatori'':28B ''sabr'':33B ''small'':7B ''south'':16B ''south-southwest'':15B ''southwest'':17B', 'falkreath', 'Greywater Grotto is a small cave located far east of Falkreath and south-southwest of Helgen in Falkreath Hold.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonbone_sword', 'Dragonbone Sword is a basic Dragonbone weapon which deals brilliant damage. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. To craft it: 1 dragon bone, 1 ebony ingot, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. A Master smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dragonbone at a workbench.', '''1'':33B,36B,40B ''appear'':29B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':45B ''bone'':24B,35B ''brilliant'':12B ''craft'':21B,31B,51B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''dragon'':23B,34B ''dragonbon'':1A,3B,8B,59B ''eboni'':37B ''forg'':46B ''ingot'':38B ''jag'':20B ''leather'':41B ''master'':48B ''organ'':28B ''pale'':18B ''rough'':27B ''smith'':49B ''strip'':42B ''sword'':2A,4B ''tempered/improved'':56B ''use'':58B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':62B', 'blacksmith', 'Dragonbone Sword is a basic Dragonbone weapon which deals brilliant damage. Its visual design is pale and jagged, crafted from dragon bones with a rough, organic appearance. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragons_tongue', 'Dragon''s Tongue is a striking yellow-flowered plant found in the volcanic tundra of Eastmarch and is sometimes cultivated as an ornamental plant. Alchemy effects: Resist Fire, Fortify Barter, Fortify Illusion, and Fortify Two-handed.', '''alchemi'':28B ''barter'':33B ''cultiv'':23B ''dragon'':1A,3B ''eastmarch'':19B ''effect'':29B ''fire'':31B ''flower'':11B ''fortifi'':32B,34B,37B ''found'':13B ''hand'':40B ''illus'':35B ''ornament'':26B ''plant'':12B,27B ''resist'':30B ''sometim'':22B ''strike'':8B ''tongu'':2A,5B ''tundra'':17B ''two'':39B ''two-hand'':38B ''volcan'':16B ''yellow'':10B ''yellow-flow'':9B', 'alchemist', 'Dragon''s Tongue is a striking yellow-flowered plant found in the volcanic tundra of Eastmarch and is sometimes cultivated as an ornamental plant.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elves_ear', 'Elves Ear is a small green herb harvested from branches of dried Elves Ear, often found hanging to dry alongside garlic and frost mirriam in homes and buildings. Alchemy effects: Restore Magicka, Fortify Marksman, Weakness to Frost, and Resist Fire.', '''alchemi'':31B ''alongsid'':22B ''branch'':12B ''build'':30B ''dri'':14B,21B ''ear'':2A,4B,16B ''effect'':32B ''elv'':1A,3B,15B ''fire'':42B ''fortifi'':35B ''found'':18B ''frost'':25B,39B ''garlic'':23B ''green'':8B ''hang'':19B ''harvest'':10B ''herb'':9B ''home'':28B ''magicka'':34B ''marksman'':36B ''mirriam'':26B ''often'':17B ''resist'':41B ''restor'':33B ''small'':7B ''weak'':37B', 'alchemist', 'Elves Ear is a small green herb harvested from branches of dried Elves Ear, often found hanging to dry alongside garlic and frost mirriam in homes and buildings.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('conjure_ash_guardian', 'Conjure Ash Guardian is a Conjuration spell from solstheim that summons a powerful Ash Guardian to fight for the caster, requiring a heart stone to remain under control. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''ash'':2A,5B,17B ''cast'':39B ''caster'':23B ''conjur'':1A,4B,9B ''control'':31B ''expert'':35B ''fight'':20B ''guardian'':3A,6B,18B ''heart'':26B ''level'':37B ''power'':16B ''remain'':29B ''requir'':24B,33B ''skill'':36B ''solstheim'':12B ''spell'':10B ''stone'':27B ''summon'':14B', 'mage', 'Conjure Ash Guardian is a spell that summons a powerful Ash Guardian to fight for the caster, but it requires a heart stone to keep the creature under control. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('moorside_inn', 'Moorside Inn is the inn in Morthal, owned and operated by Jonna. Located in the heart of the town. Lurbuk serves as the inn''s bard, though his performances are not particularly well-received, and business at the inn seems slow. Jonna often mentions that the front door sees little traffic. ', '''bard'':28B ''busi'':39B ''door'':51B ''front'':50B ''heart'':18B ''inn'':2A,4B,7B,26B,42B ''jonna'':14B,45B ''littl'':53B ''locat'':15B ''lurbuk'':22B ''mention'':47B ''moorsid'':1A,3B ''morthal'':9B ''often'':46B ''oper'':12B ''own'':10B ''particular'':34B ''perform'':31B ''receiv'':37B ''see'':52B ''seem'':43B ''serv'':23B ''slow'':44B ''though'':29B ''town'':21B ''traffic'':54B ''well'':36B ''well-receiv'':35B', 'hjaalmarch, innkeeper, traveler', 'Moorside Inn is the inn in Morthal. You do not know who runs the Inn.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shriekwind_bastion', 'Shriekwind Bastion is a small Nordic ruin located north of Falkreath and east of Falkreath Watchtower in Falkreath Hold. It is inhabitted by Draugrs and rumors of vampires recently taking residence. ', '''bastion'':2A,4B ''draugr'':26B ''east'':15B ''falkreath'':13B,17B,20B ''hold'':21B ''inhabit'':24B ''locat'':10B ''nordic'':8B ''north'':11B ''recent'':31B ''resid'':33B ''ruin'':9B ''rumor'':28B ''shriekwind'':1A,3B ''small'':7B ''take'':32B ''vampir'':30B ''watchtow'':18B', 'falkreath', 'Shriekwind Bastion is a small Nordic ruin located north of Falkreath in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vahlok_the_jailor', '
Vahlok the Jailor was a Dragon Priest who once ruled Solstheim and was tasked with guarding the traitor Miraak. After uncovering Miraak''s plot against their masters, Vahlok defeated him in a legendary battle and was later entombed in Vahlok''s Tomb in Solstheim.', '''battl'':37B ''defeat'':32B ''dragon'':9B ''entomb'':41B ''guard'':19B ''jailor'':3A,6B ''later'':40B ''legendari'':36B ''master'':30B ''miraak'':22B,25B ''plot'':27B ''priest'':10B ''rule'':13B ''solstheim'':14B,47B ''task'':17B ''tomb'':45B ''traitor'':21B ''uncov'':24B ''vahlok'':1A,4B,31B,43B', 'scholar, dragon, miraakcult', 'Vahlok the Jailor must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Solstheim. You really don''t know much more apart from that. You have a hunch he must of been being a jailor for someone important, but don''t know what.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shadowgreen_cavern', 'Shadowgreen Cavern is a small cave located northwest of Solitude in Haafingar. To reach the cave, follow the road from Solitude toward the Dainty Sload and Solitude Lighthouse, but stay on the main road as it curves north and then west around the mountain.', '''around'':44B ''cave'':8B,18B ''cavern'':2A,4B ''curv'':39B ''dainti'':26B ''follow'':19B ''haafingar'':14B ''lighthous'':30B ''locat'':9B ''main'':35B ''mountain'':46B ''north'':40B ''northwest'':10B ''reach'':16B ''road'':21B,36B ''shadowgreen'':1A,3B ''sload'':27B ''small'':7B ''solitud'':12B,23B,29B ''stay'':32B ''toward'':24B ''west'':43B', 'haafingar', 'Shadowgreen Cavern is a small cave located northwest of Solitude in Haafingar.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('conjure_storm_atronach', 'Conjure Storm Atronach is a Conjuration spell that summons a powerful Storm Atronach to fight for the caster for a limited time. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''atronach'':3A,6B,16B ''cast'':33B ''caster'':21B ''conjur'':1A,4B,9B ''expert'':29B ''fight'':18B ''level'':31B ''limit'':24B ''power'':14B ''requir'':27B ''skill'':30B ''spell'':10B ''storm'':2A,5B,15B ''summon'':12B ''time'':25B', 'mage', 'Conjure Storm Atronach is a spell that summons a powerful Storm Atronach to fight for the caster for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orphan''s_tear', 'Orphan''s Tear is a shipwreck located west of Ravenscar Hollow on the northern coast of Haafingar. The wreck is inhabited by bandits who have made it their hideout.', '''bandit'':26B ''coast'':18B ''haafingar'':20B ''hideout'':32B ''hollow'':14B ''inhabit'':24B ''locat'':10B ''made'':29B ''northern'':17B ''orphan'':1A,4B ''ravenscar'':13B ''shipwreck'':9B ''tear'':3A,6B ''west'':11B ''wreck'':22B', 'haafingar', 'Orphan''s Tear is a shipwreck located on the northern coast of Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.
', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('radiant_raiment', 'Radiant Raiment is a clothing store in Solitude, run by Taarie and her sister Endarie, both High Elves who are skilled tailors. The store is located near the entrance of Solitude, on the right as you enter through the main gate.

Radiant Raiment offers a variety of high-quality clothing and accessories, catering to those with refined tastes. Taarie and Endarie are known for their expertise in tailoring, and their shop is a popular destination for those seeking stylish and elegant outfits in Solitude.', '''accessori'':55B ''cater'':56B ''cloth'':7B,53B ''destin'':78B ''eleg'':84B ''elv'':20B ''endari'':17B,64B ''enter'':39B ''entranc'':31B ''expertis'':69B ''gate'':43B ''high'':19B,51B ''high-qual'':50B ''known'':66B ''locat'':28B ''main'':42B ''near'':29B ''offer'':46B ''outfit'':85B ''popular'':77B ''qualiti'':52B ''radiant'':1A,3B,44B ''raiment'':2A,4B,45B ''refin'':60B ''right'':36B ''run'':11B ''seek'':81B ''shop'':74B ''sister'':16B ''skill'':23B ''solitud'':10B,33B,87B ''store'':8B,26B ''stylish'':82B ''taari'':13B,62B ''tailor'':24B,71B ''tast'':61B ''varieti'':48B', 'haafingar', 'Radiant Raiment is a clothing store in Solitude. You do not know who runs the store.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('pelinal_whitestrake', 'Pelinal Whitestrake is a legendary figure revered as a demigod and champion of Queen Alessia during the early First Era''s Alessian Slave Rebellion. Known for his fierce combat prowess, Pelinal fought against the Ayleid oppressors, wielding the Crusader''s Relics bestowed upon him by the Eight Divines. His name, derived from Pelin-El, meaning "Star-Made Knight," reflects his celestial connection and glory in battle. Throughout his conquests across Tamriel, Pelinal is said to have embodied both heroism and chaos, often succumbing to bouts of madness that drove him to indiscriminately slay enemies and alter the very landscape.

Pelinal is remembered by many titles, including Pelinal the Bloody, the Divine Crusader, and Pelinal Insurgent, with some legends suggesting he had incarnated multiple times. His connection to Queen Alessia was profound, with their names occasionally combined to signify their unity in the fight for freedom. Khajiiti tales recount him as the White Snake, further highlighting his mythic status. Despite his feats, Pelinal''s legacy is complex, as he is equally known for the destruction he wrought, embodying both the hope of liberation and the peril of unchecked power.', '''across'':74B ''alessia'':17B,133B ''alessian'':24B ''alter'':100B ''ayleid'':37B ''battl'':70B ''bestow'':44B ''bloodi'':113B ''bout'':89B ''celesti'':65B ''champion'':14B ''chao'':85B ''combat'':31B ''combin'':140B ''complex'':170B ''connect'':66B,130B ''conquest'':73B ''crusad'':41B,116B ''demigod'':12B ''deriv'':53B ''despit'':163B ''destruct'':178B ''divin'':50B,115B ''drove'':93B ''earli'':20B ''eight'':49B ''el'':57B ''embodi'':81B,181B ''enemi'':98B ''equal'':174B ''era'':22B ''feat'':165B ''fierc'':30B ''fight'':147B ''figur'':8B ''first'':21B ''fought'':34B ''freedom'':149B ''glori'':68B ''heroism'':83B ''highlight'':159B ''hope'':184B ''incarn'':126B ''includ'':110B ''indiscrimin'':96B ''insurg'':119B ''khajiiti'':150B ''knight'':62B ''known'':27B,175B ''landscap'':103B ''legaci'':168B ''legend'':122B ''legendari'':7B ''liber'':186B ''mad'':91B ''made'':61B ''mani'':108B ''mean'':58B ''multipl'':127B ''mythic'':161B ''name'':52B,138B ''occasion'':139B ''often'':86B ''oppressor'':38B ''pelin'':1A,3B,33B,56B,76B,104B,111B,118B,166B ''pelin-el'':55B ''peril'':189B ''power'':192B ''profound'':135B ''prowess'':32B ''queen'':16B,132B ''rebellion'':26B ''recount'':152B ''reflect'':63B ''relic'':43B ''rememb'':106B ''rever'':9B ''said'':78B ''signifi'':142B ''slave'':25B ''slay'':97B ''snake'':157B ''star'':60B ''star-mad'':59B ''status'':162B ''succumb'':87B ''suggest'':123B ''tale'':151B ''tamriel'':75B ''throughout'':71B ''time'':128B ''titl'':109B ''uncheck'':191B ''uniti'':144B ''upon'':45B ''white'':156B ''whitestrak'':2A,4B ''wield'':39B ''wrought'':180B', ' highelf, scholar, imperial, priest', 'Pelinal Whitestrake is a legendary figure, revered as a demigod and champion of Queen Alessia during the Alessian Slave Rebellion. Known for his combat prowess, he fought against the Ayleid oppressors using the Crusader''s Relics bestowed by the Eight Divines. His name, Pelin-El, meaning "Star-Made Knight," reflects his celestial nature. Pelinal is remembered by titles such as Pelinal the Bloody and the Divine Crusader. He had a deep connection to Queen Alessia, and some Khajiiti tales call him the White Snake. Though a hero, Pelinal’s legacy is marked by both the hope of liberation and the destruction he caused.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('deepwood_redoubt', 'Deepwood Redoubt is a large Nordic ruin located west of Dragon Bridge and east of Mor Khazgur in The Reach. The ruin is inhabited by Forsworn, the fierce and rebellious natives of the Reach, who occupy the site as part of their struggle against outsiders.', '''bridg'':14B ''deepwood'':1A,3B ''dragon'':13B ''east'':16B ''fierc'':30B ''forsworn'':28B ''inhabit'':26B ''khazgur'':19B ''larg'':7B ''locat'':10B ''mor'':18B ''nativ'':33B ''nordic'':8B ''occupi'':38B ''outsid'':47B ''part'':42B ''reach'':22B,36B ''rebelli'':32B ''redoubt'':2A,4B ''ruin'':9B,24B ''site'':40B ''struggl'':45B ''west'':11B', 'haafingar', 'Deepwood Redoubt is a large Nordic ruin located west of Dragon Bridge in The Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gallows_rock', 'Gallows Rock is a small fort located southwest of Windhelm and northeast of Cradlecrush Rock in Eastmarch. It is rumoured that the Silver Hand, and their leader occupies the area.', '''area'':32B ''cradlecrush'':16B ''eastmarch'':19B ''fort'':8B ''gallow'':1A,3B ''hand'':26B ''leader'':29B ''locat'':9B ''northeast'':14B ''occupi'':30B ''rock'':2A,4B,17B ''rumour'':22B ''silver'':25B ''small'':7B ''southwest'':10B ''windhelm'':12B', 'eastmarch', 'Gallows Rock is a small fort located southwest of Windhelm in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragon_rend', 'Dragonrend is a Shout that targets a dragon''s very soul, forcing it to land. The three words of power in this Shout are Joor (Mortal), which connects the dragon to the frailty of mortal existence; Zah (Finite), which limits the dragon’s power and forces it to the ground; and Frul (Temporary), which makes the dragon''s flight temporarily impossible, grounding it for a period.', '''connect'':30B ''dragon'':1A,10B,32B,58B ''dragonrend'':3B ''dragon’'':44B ''exist'':38B ''finit'':40B ''flight'':60B ''forc'':14B,47B ''frailti'':35B ''frul'':53B ''ground'':51B,63B ''imposs'':62B ''joor'':27B ''land'':17B ''limit'':42B ''make'':56B ''mortal'':28B,37B ''period'':67B ''power'':22B,45B ''rend'':2A ''shout'':6B,25B ''soul'':13B ''target'':8B ''temporari'':54B ''temporarili'':61B ''three'':19B ''word'':20B ''zah'':39B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dragonhide', 'Dragonhide is an Alteration spell that drastically reduces physical damage taken by the caster for a short duration. It requires a Master skill level to cast.', '''alter'':5B ''cast'':27B ''caster'':15B ''damag'':11B ''dragonhid'':1A,2B ''drastic'':8B ''durat'':19B ''level'':25B ''master'':23B ''physic'':10B ''reduc'':9B ''requir'':21B ''short'':18B ''skill'':24B ''spell'':6B ''taken'':12B', 'mage', 'Dragonhide is a spell that makes the caster''s skin as tough as a dragon''s, greatly reducing the damage they take for a short time. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('korvanjund', 'Korvanjund is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located northeast of Whiterun and south of Silverdrift Lair in The Pale. The ruin is inhabited by draugr.', '''draugr'':27B ''inhabit'':25B ''korvanjund'':1A,2B ''lair'':18B ''locat'':10B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''nordic'':8B ''northeast'':11B ''pale'':21B ''ruin'':9B,23B ''silverdrift'':17B ''size'':7B ''south'':15B ''whiterun'':13B', 'pale', 'Korvanjund is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located northeast of Whiterun in The Pale. .You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_alteration', 'This potion enhances the duration of alteration magic, a school of spells that manipulate the physical world and natural properties. Often used by mages for utility and defense. Grants alteration spells a slight improvement, with effects lasting longer as the potion increases in potency. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':59B ''alter'':3A,10B,33B ''defens'':31B ''draught'':69B ''durat'':8B ''effect'':39B ''elixir'':72B ''enhanc'':6B ''found'':52B ''grant'':32B ''improv'':37B ''increas'':45B ''last'':40B ''longer'':41B ''loot'':55B ''mage'':27B ''magic'':11B ''manipul'':17B ''natur'':22B ''often'':24B ''philter'':70B ''physic'':19B ''potenc'':47B ''potion'':1A,5B,44B,49B,68B ''properti'':23B ''purchas'':57B ''random'':54B ''school'':13B ''sever'':62B ''slight'':36B ''spell'':15B,34B ''strongest'':67B ''tier'':63B ''use'':25B ''util'':29B ''weakest'':65B ''world'':20B', 'mage, alchemist, scholar, collegeofwinterhold, psijic', 'The Potion of Alteration enhances the duration of alteration spells. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_haggling', 'A merchant''s best friend, this potion enhances one''s silver tongue, allowing better negotiation and lower prices for a brief time. Provides a slight advantage in haggling, with greater bargaining power as the potion becomes stronger. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''advantag'':29B ''alchemist'':52B ''allow'':16B ''bargain'':34B ''becom'':39B ''best'':7B ''better'':17B ''brief'':24B ''draught'':62B ''elixir'':65B ''enhanc'':11B ''found'':45B ''friend'':8B ''greater'':33B ''haggl'':3A,31B ''loot'':48B ''lower'':20B ''merchant'':5B ''negoti'':18B ''one'':12B ''philter'':63B ''potion'':1A,10B,38B,42B,61B ''power'':35B ''price'':21B ''provid'':26B ''purchas'':50B ''random'':47B ''sever'':55B ''silver'':14B ''slight'':28B ''stronger'':40B ''strongest'':60B ''tier'':56B ''time'':25B ''tongu'':15B ''weakest'':58B', 'merchant, alchemist, noble, bard, traveler', 'The Potion of Haggling improves your ability to negotiate better deals. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('witchmist_grove', 'Witchmist Grove is a small, eerie grove located north of Bonestrewn Crest and south of Kynesgrove in Eastmarch. The grove is most easily reached by traveling to Kynesgrove and heading directly south.

At its center lies a doorless shack surrounded by sharpened stakes. It is rumoured that hagravens occupy the area. ', '''area'':53B ''bonestrewn'':13B ''center'':37B ''crest'':14B ''direct'':33B ''doorless'':40B ''easili'':25B ''eastmarch'':20B ''eeri'':8B ''grove'':2A,4B,9B,22B ''hagraven'':50B ''head'':32B ''kynesgrov'':18B,30B ''lie'':38B ''locat'':10B ''north'':11B ''occupi'':51B ''reach'':26B ''rumour'':48B ''shack'':41B ''sharpen'':44B ''small'':7B ''south'':16B,34B ''stake'':45B ''surround'':42B ''travel'':28B ''witchmist'':1A,3B', 'eastmarch, witch', 'Witchmist Grove is a small, eerie grove located north of Bonestrewn Crest in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('darkfall_cave', 'Darkfall Cave is a small cave located south of Mor Khazgur and north of Druadach Redoubt in the Reach. The entrance is situated at the end of a mountain meadow that rises to just above the snowline, offering a remote and scenic approach.', '''approach'':45B ''cave'':2A,4B,8B ''darkfal'':1A,3B ''druadach'':17B ''end'':28B ''entranc'':23B ''khazgur'':13B ''locat'':9B ''meadow'':32B ''mor'':12B ''mountain'':31B ''north'':15B ''offer'':40B ''reach'':21B ''redoubt'':18B ''remot'':42B ''rise'':34B ''scenic'':44B ''situat'':25B ''small'':7B ''snowlin'':39B ''south'':10B', 'reach', 'Darkfall Cave is a small cave located south of Mor Khazgur  in the Reach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bonemold_pauldron_armor', 'Bonemold Armor is a basic bonemold chest piece with basic protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. To craft it: 2 netch leather, 1 iron ingots, 10 bonemold, at a blacksmith forge. An Apprentice smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using bonemeal at a workbench.', '''1'':44B ''10'':47B ''2'':41B ''apprentic'':54B ''armor'':3A,5B ''basic'':8B,13B ''bind'':33B ''blacksmith'':51B ''bone'':27B ''bone-lik'':26B ''bonem'':65B ''bonemold'':1A,4B,9B,48B ''chest'':10B ''craft'':39B,57B ''dark'':32B ''design'':18B ''forg'':52B ''ingot'':46B ''iron'':45B ''leather'':43B ''like'':28B ''netch'':42B ''organ'':22B ''pauldron'':2A ''piec'':11B ''protect'':14B ''qualiti'':15B ''reinforc'':30B ''rough'':20B ''shape'':37B ''smith'':55B ''tan'':25B ''tempered/improved'':62B ''textur'':29B ''use'':64B ''utilitarian'':36B ''visual'':17B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Bonemold Armor is a basic bonemold chest piece with basic protection quality. 
Its visual design is rough and organic, with a tan, bone-like texture reinforced by dark bindings and a utilitarian shape. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('winterhold', 'Winterhold is a hold in northeast Skyrim, with its capital in the city of Winterhold, located on the Sea of Ghosts’ coast. The city is aligned with the Stormcloaks under Jarl Korir. Winterhold is the northernmost hold in Skyrim, with harsh weather and bleak landscapes, bordered by Eastmarch to the southeast, the Pale to the south and west, and the Sea of Ghosts to the north. The region is primarily composed of barren tundra, snowy mountains, and rocky coastlines.

Once a prosperous and vibrant city, Winterhold was devastated in the Great Collapse of 4E 122, in which most of the city was swallowed by the Sea of Ghosts. Today, only a few buildings remain standing near the College of Winterhold, which miraculously survived. The College, a fortress-like institution for mages, is perched on a rocky outcropping, sparking rumors among locals that its magical experiments caused the city''s destruction. Despite this, the College maintains that the event was a result of the earthquake in Vivec and the eruption of Red Mountain in Morrowind. The remaining residents can be found at The Frozen Hearth, where they often drown their sorrows. The sparse wildlife of Winterhold includes wolves, snow bears, and the occasional ice wraith, with little plant life beyond snowberry bushes and mountain flowers. The hold is traversed by a single main road leading to the city, with another path leading to the ancient ruins of Saarthal.', '''122'':96B ''4e'':95B ''align'':27B ''among'':142B ''ancient'':236B ''anoth'':231B ''barren'':74B ''bear'':201B ''beyond'':211B ''bleak'':45B ''border'':47B ''build'':114B ''bush'':213B ''capit'':11B ''caus'':148B ''citi'':14B,25B,86B,102B,150B,229B ''coast'':23B ''coastlin'':80B ''collaps'':93B ''colleg'':119B,126B,156B ''compos'':72B ''despit'':153B ''destruct'':152B ''devast'':89B ''drown'':190B ''earthquak'':166B ''eastmarch'':49B ''erupt'':171B ''event'':160B ''experi'':147B ''flower'':216B ''fortress'':129B ''fortress-lik'':128B ''found'':182B ''frozen'':185B ''ghost'':64B,109B ''ghosts’'':22B ''great'':92B ''harsh'':42B ''hearth'':186B ''hold'':5B,38B,218B ''ice'':205B ''includ'':198B ''institut'':131B ''jarl'':32B ''korir'':33B ''landscap'':46B ''lead'':226B,233B ''life'':210B ''like'':130B ''littl'':208B ''local'':143B ''locat'':17B ''mage'':133B ''magic'':146B ''main'':224B ''maintain'':157B ''miracul'':123B ''morrowind'':176B ''mountain'':77B,174B,215B ''near'':117B ''north'':67B ''northeast'':7B ''northernmost'':37B ''occasion'':204B ''often'':189B ''outcrop'':139B ''pale'':54B ''path'':232B ''perch'':135B ''plant'':209B ''primarili'':71B ''prosper'':83B ''red'':173B ''region'':69B ''remain'':115B,178B ''resid'':179B ''result'':163B ''road'':225B ''rocki'':79B,138B ''ruin'':237B ''rumor'':141B ''saarthal'':239B ''sea'':20B,62B,107B ''singl'':223B ''skyrim'':8B,40B ''snow'':200B ''snowberri'':212B ''snowi'':76B ''sorrow'':192B ''south'':57B ''southeast'':52B ''spark'':140B ''spars'':194B ''stand'':116B ''stormcloak'':30B ''surviv'':124B ''swallow'':104B ''today'':110B ''travers'':220B ''tundra'':75B ''vibrant'':85B ''vivec'':168B ''weather'':43B ''west'':59B ''wildlif'':195B ''winterhold'':1A,2B,16B,34B,87B,121B,197B ''wolv'':199B ''wraith'':206B', 'winterhold, noble, scholar', 'Winterhold is a hold in northeast Skyrim, with its capital in the city of Winterhold, located on the Sea of Ghosts’ coast. The city is aligned with the Stormcloaks under Jarl Korir. Winterhold is the northernmost hold in Skyrim, with harsh weather and bleak landscapes, bordered by Eastmarch to the southeast, the Pale to the south and west, and the Sea of Ghosts to the north. The region is primarily composed of barren tundra, snowy mountains, and rocky coastlines.

Once a prosperous and vibrant city, Winterhold was devastated in the Great Collapse of 4E 122, in which most of the city was swallowed by the Sea of Ghosts. Today, only a few buildings remain standing near the College of Winterhold, which miraculously survived. The College, a fortress-like institution for mages, is perched on a rocky outcropping, sparking rumors among locals that its magical experiments caused the city''s destruction.  The hold is traversed by a single main road leading to the city, with another path leading to the ancient ruins of Saarthal.You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fortify_alchemy', 'These magical effects are utility-focused Restoration enchantments that enhance the potency of crafted potions and poisons, maximizing their effects. This effect is available through custom enchanting and is also found on enchanted gear, making it a favored choice for skilled alchemists.', '''alchemi'':2A ''alchemist'':45B ''also'':33B ''avail'':27B ''choic'':42B ''craft'':17B ''custom'':29B ''effect'':5B,23B,25B ''enchant'':11B,30B,36B ''enhanc'':13B ''favor'':41B ''focus'':9B ''fortifi'':1A ''found'':34B ''gear'':37B ''magic'':4B ''make'':38B ''maxim'':21B ''poison'':20B ''potenc'':15B ''potion'':18B ''restor'':10B ''skill'':44B ''util'':8B ''utility-focus'':7B', 'mage', 'This enchantment makes potions and poisons you create stronger and more effective. A mage might know more though.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('feim_zii_gron', 'Become Ethereal is a Shout that transforms your form to one that cannot harm or be harmed, as it reaches out to the Void. The three words of power in this Shout are Feim (Fade), which allows you to slip from the physical world; Zii (Spirit), which grants you a ghostly form; and Gron (Bind), which anchors you in a state where you are untouchable by physical harm.', '''allow'':40B ''anchor'':60B ''becom'':4B ''bind'':58B ''cannot'':16B ''ether'':5B ''fade'':38B ''feim'':1A,37B ''form'':12B,55B ''ghost'':54B ''grant'':51B ''gron'':3A,57B ''harm'':17B,20B,71B ''one'':14B ''physic'':46B,70B ''power'':32B ''reach'':23B ''shout'':8B,35B ''slip'':43B ''spirit'':49B ''state'':64B ''three'':29B ''transform'':10B ''untouch'':68B ''void'':27B ''word'':30B ''world'':47B ''zii'':2A,48B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('journeyman''s_nook', 'Journeyman''s Nook is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located southeast of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region, and northwest of Snow Veil Sanctum. Despite its modest size, the ruin is home to a bandit who has taken shelter within its crumbling walls, using it as a hideout.

The site is relatively isolated, set against the harsh northern landscape, making it a perfect place for the bandit to remain hidden from the law.', '''bandit'':37B,69B ''crumbl'':44B ''despit'':27B ''harsh'':59B ''hidden'':72B ''hideout'':50B ''home'':34B ''isol'':55B ''journeyman'':1A,4B ''landscap'':61B ''law'':75B ''locat'':13B ''make'':62B ''modest'':29B ''nook'':3A,6B ''nordic'':11B ''northern'':60B ''northwest'':22B ''outdoor'':10B ''perfect'':65B ''place'':66B ''region'':20B ''relat'':54B ''remain'':71B ''ruin'':12B,32B ''sanctum'':26B ''set'':56B ''shelter'':41B ''site'':52B ''size'':30B ''small'':9B ''snow'':24B ''southeast'':14B ''taken'':40B ''use'':46B ''veil'':25B ''wall'':45B ''winterhold'':16B,19B ''within'':42B', 'winterhold', 'Journeyman''s Nook is a small outdoor Nordic ruin located southeast of Winterhold, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ancient''s_ascent', 'Ancient''s Ascent is a mountaintop dragon lair located southwest of Helgen and north of Bloodlet Throne in Falkreath Hold. ', '''ancient'':1A,4B ''ascent'':3A,6B ''bloodlet'':19B ''dragon'':10B ''falkreath'':22B ''helgen'':15B ''hold'':23B ''lair'':11B ''locat'':12B ''mountaintop'':9B ''north'':17B ''southwest'':13B ''throne'':20B', 'falkreath, dragon', 'Ancient''s Ascent is a mountaintop dragon lair located southwest of Helgen in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mul_qah_diiv', 'Dragon Aspect is a Shout that allows you to take on the mighty aspect of a dragon once a day, delivering powerful blows, gaining an armored hide, and enhancing your shouts. The three words of power in this Shout are Mul (Strength), which grants you immense power; Qah (Armor), which gives you a protective dragon-like hide; and Diiv (Wyrm), which imbues you with the spirit of a dragon, strengthening your attacks and abilities.', '''abil'':78B ''allow'':10B ''armor'':29B,52B ''aspect'':5B,17B ''attack'':76B ''blow'':26B ''day'':23B ''deliv'':24B ''diiv'':3A,63B ''dragon'':4B,20B,59B,73B ''dragon-lik'':58B ''enhanc'':32B ''gain'':27B ''give'':54B ''grant'':47B ''hide'':30B,61B ''imbu'':66B ''immens'':49B ''like'':60B ''mighti'':16B ''mul'':1A,44B ''power'':25B,39B,50B ''protect'':57B ''qah'':2A,51B ''shout'':8B,34B,42B ''spirit'':70B ''strength'':45B ''strengthen'':74B ''take'':13B ''three'':36B ''word'':37B ''wyrm'':64B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('blind_cliff_cave', 'Blind Cliff Cave is a medium-sized cave located southwest of Karthwasten along the banks of the Karth River in the Reach. The cave is inhabited by Forsworn, making it a dangerous location for adventurers.', '''adventur'':39B ''along'':17B ''bank'':19B ''blind'':1A,4B ''cave'':3A,6B,12B,28B ''cliff'':2A,5B ''danger'':36B ''forsworn'':32B ''inhabit'':30B ''karth'':22B ''karthwasten'':16B ''locat'':13B,37B ''make'':33B ''medium'':10B ''medium-s'':9B ''reach'':26B ''river'':23B ''size'':11B ''southwest'':14B', 'reach', 'Blind Cliff Cave is a medium-sized cave located southwest of Karthwasten along the banks of the Karth River in the Reach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('arkngthamz', 'Arkngthamz is a small Dwarven ruin located southeast of Dushnikh Yal and west of Valthume in Falkreath Hold.  The ruin can be accessed via a path heading east from the Orc stronghold of Dushnikh Yal.', '''access'':24B ''arkngthamz'':1A,2B ''dushnikh'':11B,35B ''dwarven'':6B ''east'':29B ''falkreath'':18B ''head'':28B ''hold'':19B ''locat'':8B ''orc'':32B ''path'':27B ''ruin'':7B,21B ''small'':5B ''southeast'':9B ''stronghold'':33B ''valthum'':16B ''via'':25B ''west'':14B ''yal'':12B,36B', 'reach, dwemer', 'Arkngthamz is a small Dwarven ruin located southeast of Dushnikh Yal in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('enchanters_potion', 'A must-have for aspiring enchanters, this potion enhances the potency of crafted enchantments, imbuing items with greater magical power. Grants a slight increase to enchantment strength, with higher tiers offering more powerful enhancements for magical crafting. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists. There are several tiers: from weakest to strongest: potion, draught, philter, and elixir.', '''alchemist'':52B ''aspir'':8B ''craft'':16B,40B ''draught'':62B ''elixir'':65B ''enchant'':1A,9B,17B,29B ''enhanc'':12B,37B ''found'':45B ''grant'':24B ''greater'':21B ''higher'':32B ''imbu'':18B ''increas'':27B ''item'':19B ''loot'':48B ''magic'':22B,39B ''must'':5B ''must-hav'':4B ''offer'':34B ''philter'':63B ''potenc'':14B ''potion'':2A,11B,42B,61B ''power'':23B,36B ''purchas'':50B ''random'':47B ''sever'':55B ''slight'':26B ''strength'':30B ''strongest'':60B ''tier'':33B,56B ''weakest'':58B', 'alchemist, mage, scholar, collegeofwinterhold, psijic', 'The Enchanter''s Potion enhances the strength of crafted enchantments. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('gyldenhul_barrow', '
Gyldenhul Barrow is a Nordic ruin located east of Skaal Village, on the northwestern shore of Horker Island in Solstheim. The barrow is steeped in legend and intrigue, said to house the spirit and treasure of Haknir Death-Brand, a notorious pirate king whose name strikes fear even in death.', '''barrow'':2A,4B,24B ''brand'':42B ''death'':41B,53B ''death-brand'':40B ''east'':10B ''even'':51B ''fear'':50B ''gyldenhul'':1A,3B ''haknir'':39B ''horker'':19B ''hous'':33B ''intrigu'':30B ''island'':20B ''king'':46B ''legend'':28B ''locat'':9B ''name'':48B ''nordic'':7B ''northwestern'':16B ''notori'':44B ''pirat'':45B ''ruin'':8B ''said'':31B ''shore'':17B ''skaal'':12B ''solstheim'':22B ''spirit'':35B ''steep'':26B ''strike'':49B ''treasur'':37B ''villag'':13B ''whose'':47B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('soljund''s_sinkhole', 'Soljund''s Sinkhole is a small moonstone mine and settlement located east of Markarth and north of Old Hroldan Inn in the Reach. The mine is inhabited by draugr, presenting a challenge for miners and adventurers alike.', '''adventur'':39B ''alik'':40B ''challeng'':35B ''draugr'':32B ''east'':15B ''hroldan'':22B ''inhabit'':30B ''inn'':23B ''locat'':14B ''markarth'':17B ''mine'':11B,28B ''miner'':37B ''moonston'':10B ''north'':19B ''old'':21B ''present'':33B ''reach'':26B ''settlement'':13B ''sinkhol'':3A,6B ''small'':9B ''soljund'':1A,4B', 'reach', 'Soljund''s Sinkhole is a small moonstone mine and settlement located east of Markarth in the Reach. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, whiterun, hjaalmarch, haafingar', '', 'reach');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('mudcrab_chitin', 'Mudcrab Chitin is dropped by mudcrabs and is valued for its defensive and restorative properties. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Cure Disease, Resist Poison, and Resist Fire.', '''alchemi'':18B ''chitin'':2A,4B ''cure'':22B ''defens'':14B ''diseas'':23B ''drop'':6B ''effect'':19B ''fire'':28B ''mudcrab'':1A,3B,8B ''poison'':25B ''properti'':17B ''resist'':24B,27B ''restor'':16B,20B ''stamina'':21B ''valu'':11B', 'alchemist', 'Mudcrab Chitin is dropped by mudcrabs and is valued for its defensive and restorative properties. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elven_arrow', 'Elven Arrow is an arrow that deals good damage. 
Its visual design is elegant and golden, with a slender shaft, a curved, leaf-like arrowhead, and light feathered fletching. It can be crafted by an adept smith at a forge. 1 moonstone, 1 firewood = 24 arrows.', '''1'':44B,46B ''24'':48B ''adept'':39B ''arrow'':2A,4B,7B,49B ''arrowhead'':28B ''craft'':36B ''curv'':24B ''damag'':11B ''deal'':9B ''design'':14B ''eleg'':16B ''elven'':1A,3B ''feather'':31B ''firewood'':47B ''fletch'':32B ''forg'':43B ''golden'':18B ''good'':10B ''leaf'':26B ''leaf-lik'':25B ''light'':30B ''like'':27B ''moonston'':45B ''shaft'':22B ''slender'':21B ''smith'':40B ''visual'':13B', 'blacksmith', 'Elven Arrow is an arrow that deals good damage. 
Its visual design is elegant and golden, with a slender shaft, a curved, leaf-like arrowhead, and light feathered fletching. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_oil', 'Dwarven Oil is an ingredient dropped by Dwarven automatons, sharing similar effects to taproot, allowing for a potent combination of magical properties. Alchemy effects: Weakness to Magic, Fortify Illusion, Regenerate Magicka, and Restore Magicka.', '''alchemi'':25B ''allow'':17B ''automaton'':11B ''combin'':21B ''drop'':8B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,10B ''effect'':14B,26B ''fortifi'':30B ''illus'':31B ''ingredi'':7B ''magic'':23B,29B ''magicka'':33B,36B ''oil'':2A,4B ''potent'':20B ''properti'':24B ''regener'':32B ''restor'':35B ''share'':12B ''similar'':13B ''taproot'':16B ''weak'':27B', 'alchemist', 'Dwarven Oil is an ingredient dropped by Dwarven automatons, sharing similar effects to taproot, allowing for a potent combination of magical properties.  
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('alessian_slave_rebellion', 'The Alessian Slave Rebellion was a landmark conflict in Tamrielic history, spanning from 1E 242 to 1E 243. Led by the Slave-Queen Alessia, the rebellion marked the liberation of the Nedic people from their Ayleid overlords, who had dominated Cyrodiil through a brutal regime of Daedra worship, enslavement, and ritual cruelty. With divine guidance from the Eight Divines and the aid of key allies like Pelinal Whitestrake and Morihaus, Alessia united human slaves and sympathetic Ayleid factions in a desperate uprising. The rebellion culminated in the Siege of White-Gold Tower, where Pelinal slew the demigod Umaril the Unfeathered but fell in battle. This victory dismantled the Ayleid Empire and laid the foundation for the Alessian Empire, ushering in the dominance of men over mer in Cyrodiil.

The rebellion not only freed the Nedic slaves but also began the Ayleids'' gradual decline. Many Daedra-worshipping Ayleids fled to Valenwood and High Rock, while their remaining city-states either integrated into the new Empire as vassals or were annihilated by the Alessian forces. The rebellion’s aftermath saw Alessia crowned as the first Empress of Cyrodiil, the establishment of the Amulet of Kings to protect Mundus from Oblivion, and the rise of the Imperial Pantheon, blending elements of Nordic and Elven faiths. However, centuries later, the rise of the Alessian Order would erase much of the Ayleid presence from Cyrodiil, ensuring the once-mighty Heartland High Elves faded into obscurity. The rebellion marked a critical turning point in Tamriel’s history, redefining its religious, cultural, and political landscape.', '''1e'':17B,20B ''242'':18B ''243'':21B ''aftermath'':183B ''aid'':66B ''alessia'':28B,75B,185B ''alessian'':1A,5B,122B,179B,226B ''alli'':69B ''also'':143B ''amulet'':197B ''annihil'':176B ''ayleid'':40B,81B,114B,146B,153B,233B ''battl'':109B ''began'':144B ''blend'':212B ''brutal'':48B ''centuri'':220B ''citi'':164B ''city-st'':163B ''conflict'':11B ''critic'':252B ''crown'':186B ''cruelti'':56B ''culmin'':89B ''cultur'':261B ''cyrodiil'':45B,133B,192B,236B ''daedra'':51B,151B ''daedra-worship'':150B ''declin'':148B ''demigod'':102B ''desper'':85B ''dismantl'':112B ''divin'':58B,63B ''domin'':44B,127B ''eight'':62B ''either'':166B ''element'':213B ''elv'':244B ''elven'':217B ''empir'':115B,123B,171B ''empress'':190B ''enslav'':53B ''ensur'':237B ''eras'':229B ''establish'':194B ''faction'':82B ''fade'':245B ''faith'':218B ''fell'':107B ''first'':189B ''fled'':154B ''forc'':180B ''foundat'':119B ''freed'':138B ''gold'':96B ''gradual'':147B ''guidanc'':59B ''heartland'':242B ''high'':158B,243B ''histori'':14B,257B ''howev'':219B ''human'':77B ''imperi'':210B ''integr'':167B ''key'':68B ''king'':199B ''laid'':117B ''landmark'':10B ''landscap'':264B ''later'':221B ''led'':22B ''liber'':33B ''like'':70B ''mani'':149B ''mark'':31B,250B ''men'':129B ''mer'':131B ''mighti'':241B ''morihaus'':74B ''much'':230B ''mundus'':202B ''nedic'':36B,140B ''new'':170B ''nordic'':215B ''oblivion'':204B ''obscur'':247B ''once-mighti'':239B ''order'':227B ''overlord'':41B ''pantheon'':211B ''pelin'':71B,99B ''peopl'':37B ''point'':254B ''polit'':263B ''presenc'':234B ''protect'':201B ''queen'':27B ''rebellion'':3A,7B,30B,88B,135B,249B ''rebellion’'':182B ''redefin'':258B ''regim'':49B ''religi'':260B ''remain'':162B ''rise'':207B,223B ''ritual'':55B ''rock'':159B ''saw'':184B ''sieg'':92B ''slave'':2A,6B,26B,78B,141B ''slave-queen'':25B ''slew'':100B ''span'':15B ''state'':165B ''sympathet'':80B ''tamriel'':13B ''tamriel’'':256B ''tower'':97B ''turn'':253B ''umaril'':103B ''unfeath'':105B ''unit'':76B ''upris'':86B ''usher'':124B ''valenwood'':156B ''vassal'':173B ''victori'':111B ''white'':95B ''white-gold'':94B ''whitestrak'':72B ''worship'':52B,152B ''would'':228B', ' highelf, scholar, imperial', 'The Alessian Slave Rebellion, occurring between 1E 242 and 1E 243, was a pivotal conflict in Tamriel''s history, led by the Slave-Queen Alessia. It marked the liberation of the Nedic people from the oppressive Ayleid overlords, who ruled Cyrodiil through Daedra worship and cruelty. With divine guidance from the Eight Divines and support from allies like Pelinal Whitestrake and Morihaus, Alessia led a rebellion that culminated in the Siege of White-Gold Tower. The Ayleids were defeated, and Alessia became the first Empress of Cyrodiil, establishing the Alessian Empire and the Amulet of Kings. The rebellion weakened the Ayleid Empire, causing many Ayleids to flee or be destroyed, and reshaped Cyrodiil’s political, religious, and cultural landscape, marking the rise of men over mer.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_vigorous_magicka', 'This robust potion provides vigorous magicka restoration, enabling sustained spellcasting during intense battles. Restores a substantial amount of magicka, critical for maintaining powerful spells in prolonged combat. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists.', '''alchemist'':43B ''amount'':21B ''battl'':17B ''combat'':31B ''critic'':24B ''enabl'':12B ''found'':36B ''intens'':16B ''loot'':39B ''magicka'':4A,10B,23B ''maintain'':26B ''potion'':1A,7B,33B ''power'':27B ''prolong'':30B ''provid'':8B ''purchas'':41B ''random'':38B ''restor'':11B,18B ''robust'':6B ''spell'':28B ''spellcast'':14B ''substanti'':20B ''sustain'':13B ''vigor'':3A,9B', 'mage, alchemist, scholar, collegeofwinterhold, psijic', 'The Potion of Vigorous Magicka restores a substantial amount of magicka for intense magical encounters. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('shrine_of_mehrunes_dagon', 'The Shrine of Mehrunes Dagon is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon, located in The Pale, south-southeast of Stonehills and southwest of The Lord Stone.

The shrine is best reached by traveling southwest from The Lord Stone, following a winding path that leads to its remote location in the mountainous terrain.', '''best'':38B ''daedric'':16B ''dagon'':4A,9B,19B ''dedic'':13B ''follow'':47B ''lead'':52B ''locat'':20B,56B ''lord'':33B,45B ''mehrun'':3A,8B,18B ''mountain'':59B ''pale'':23B ''path'':50B ''princ'':17B ''reach'':39B ''remot'':55B ''shrine'':1A,6B,12B,36B ''south'':25B ''south-southeast'':24B ''southeast'':26B ''southwest'':30B,42B ''stone'':34B,46B ''stonehil'':28B ''terrain'':60B ''travel'':41B ''wind'':49B', 'pale, daedra, daedric', 'The Shrine of Mehrunes Dagon is a shrine dedicated to the Daedric Prince Mehrunes Dagon, located somewhere near the mountains in south of Dawnstar The Pale.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('valenwood', '
Valenwood is a lush, densely forested province in southwestern Tamriel, renowned for its sprawling rainforests, rolling hills, and mangrove swamps. Home to the Bosmer (Wood Elves), as well as races like Wood Orcs, Imga, and Centaurs, Valenwood is a natural haven often referred to as "Tamriel''s garden." A unique feature of the region is its massive, migratory trees, some of which serve as cities. Among these is Falinesti, a mile-high tree that acts as the capital of Valenwood. The province is bordered by Elsweyr to the east, Cyrodiil to the north, and lies across the sea from the Summerset Isles.

The region is divided into Grahtwood, Greenshade, Malabal Tor, and western Reaper''s March, with its landscapes ranging from coastal mangroves to temperate inland forests nourished by heavy rainfall. The Bosmer inhabit timber clanhouses scattered across Valenwood, blending seamlessly with the natural environment. Despite its beauty, the province''s dense woodlands and remote settlements make travel difficult, with only a few Imperial roads connecting its widely separated communities.', '''across'':98B,140B ''act'':77B ''among'':67B ''beauti'':150B ''blend'':142B ''border'':86B ''bosmer'':25B,135B ''capit'':80B ''centaur'':37B ''citi'':66B ''clanhous'':138B ''coastal'':124B ''communiti'':172B ''connect'':168B ''cyrodiil'':92B ''dens'':6B,154B ''despit'':148B ''difficult'':161B ''divid'':108B ''east'':91B ''elsweyr'':88B ''elv'':27B ''environ'':147B ''falinesti'':70B ''featur'':52B ''forest'':7B,129B ''garden'':49B ''grahtwood'':110B ''greenshad'':111B ''haven'':42B ''heavi'':132B ''high'':74B ''hill'':18B ''home'':22B ''imga'':35B ''imperi'':166B ''inhabit'':136B ''inland'':128B ''isl'':104B ''landscap'':121B ''lie'':97B ''like'':32B ''lush'':5B ''make'':159B ''malab'':112B ''mangrov'':20B,125B ''march'':118B ''massiv'':58B ''migratori'':59B ''mile'':73B ''mile-high'':72B ''natur'':41B,146B ''north'':95B ''nourish'':130B ''often'':43B ''orc'':34B ''provinc'':8B,84B,152B ''race'':31B ''rainfal'':133B ''rainforest'':16B ''rang'':122B ''reaper'':116B ''refer'':44B ''region'':55B,106B ''remot'':157B ''renown'':12B ''road'':167B ''roll'':17B ''scatter'':139B ''sea'':100B ''seamless'':143B ''separ'':171B ''serv'':64B ''settlement'':158B ''southwestern'':10B ''sprawl'':15B ''summerset'':103B ''swamp'':21B ''tamriel'':11B,47B ''temper'':127B ''timber'':137B ''tor'':113B ''travel'':160B ''tree'':60B,75B ''uniqu'':51B ''valenwood'':1A,2B,38B,82B,141B ''well'':29B ''western'':115B ''wide'':170B ''wood'':26B,33B ''woodland'':155B', 'scholar, woodelf', 'Valenwood is a lush, densely forested province in southwestern Tamriel, home to the Bosmer (Wood Elves) and other races like Wood Orcs, Imga, and Centaurs. The region is known for its sprawling rainforests, rolling hills, and mangrove swamps, with unique migratory trees that serve as cities, including Falinesti, the capital. Valenwood is bordered by Elsweyr, Cyrodiil, and the Summerset Isles, and is divided into regions like Grahtwood, Greenshade, and Malabal Tor. The Bosmer live in harmony with nature, in timber clanhouses scattered across the province. Despite its beauty, the province''s remote location and difficult terrain make travel challenging.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bannermist_tower', 'Bannermist Tower is a small, ruined Nordic tower located northwest of Falkreath and south of Hunter''s Rest in Falkreath Hold. The tower is occupied by bandits.', '''bandit'':29B ''bannermist'':1A,3B ''falkreath'':14B,22B ''hold'':23B ''hunter'':18B ''locat'':11B ''nordic'':9B ''northwest'':12B ''occupi'':27B ''rest'':20B ''ruin'':8B ''small'':7B ''south'':16B ''tower'':2A,4B,10B,25B', 'falkreath', 'Bannermist Tower is a small, ruined Nordic tower located northwest of Falkreath and south of Hunter''s Rest in Falkreath Hold. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nordic_battleaxe', 'Nordic Battleaxe is a heavy Nordic weapon which deals good damage.Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship.  To craft it: 2 quicksilver ingots, 5 leather strips, and 1 steel ingot at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using quicksilver at a workbench.', '''1'':44B ''2'':37B ''5'':40B ''adept'':52B ''ancient'':32B ''battleax'':2A,4B ''blacksmith'':49B ''craft'':35B,55B ''craftsmanship'':33B ''damage.its'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':15B ''engrav'':29B ''evok'':31B ''finish'':25B ''forg'':50B ''good'':12B ''gray'':24B ''heavi'':7B ''ingot'':39B,46B ''intric'':27B ''leather'':41B ''nordic'':1A,3B,8B,28B ''quicksilv'':38B,63B ''silver'':23B ''silver-gray'':22B ''smith'':53B ''steel'':45B ''strip'':42B ''sturdi'':17B ''tempered/improved'':60B ''use'':62B ''visual'':14B ''weapon'':9B ''weather'':19B ''workbench'':66B', 'blacksmith', 'Nordic Battleaxe is a heavy Nordic weapon which deals good damage.Its visual design is sturdy and weathered, with a silver-gray finish and intricate Nordic engravings that evoke ancient craftsmanship.  You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bristleback_cave', '
Bristleback Cave is a medium-sized cave located due northwest of Broken Tusk Mine on Solstheim. The cave serves as a stronghold for rieklings and their bristleback companions, both of which fiercely defend their territory from intruders.', '''bristleback'':1A,3B,30B ''broken'':15B ''cave'':2A,4B,10B,21B ''companion'':31B ''defend'':36B ''due'':12B ''fierc'':35B ''intrud'':40B ''locat'':11B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''mine'':17B ''northwest'':13B ''riekl'':27B ''serv'':22B ''size'':9B ''solstheim'':19B ''stronghold'':25B ''territori'':38B ''tusk'':16B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('orchish_gauntlets', 'Orcish Gauntlets are a pair of Orcish gauntlets with great protection quality. Its visual design is heavy and brutal, with a rough, greenish hue and primitive, rugged details that emphasize raw strength. To craft it: 2 orichalcum ingots, 1 iron ingot, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using orichalcum at a workbench.', '''1'':41B ''2'':38B,45B ''adept'':53B ''blacksmith'':50B ''brutal'':21B ''craft'':36B,56B ''design'':17B ''detail'':30B ''emphas'':32B ''forg'':51B ''gauntlet'':2A,4B,10B ''great'':12B ''greenish'':25B ''heavi'':19B ''hue'':26B ''ingot'':40B,43B ''iron'':42B ''leather'':46B ''orchish'':1A ''orcish'':3B,9B ''orichalcum'':39B,64B ''pair'':7B ''primit'':28B ''protect'':13B ''qualiti'':14B ''raw'':33B ''rough'':24B ''rug'':29B ''smith'':54B ''strength'':34B ''strip'':47B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':16B ''workbench'':67B', 'blacksmith', 'Orcish Gauntlets are a pair of Orcish gauntlets with great protection quality. Its visual design is heavy and brutal, with a rough, greenish hue and primitive, rugged details that emphasize raw strength. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('kagrumez', 'Kagrumez is a small Dwarven ruin located south of the Temple of Miraak and north of the Ramshackle Trading Post on Solstheim. ', '''dwarven'':6B ''kagrumez'':1A,2B ''locat'':8B ''miraak'':14B ''north'':16B ''post'':21B ''ramshackl'':19B ''ruin'':7B ''small'':5B ''solstheim'':23B ''south'':9B ''templ'':12B ''trade'':20B', 'solstheim, dwemer', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ashfall''s_tear', 'Ashfall''s Tear is a small, secluded cave located north of Raven Rock and southeast of Bloodskal Barrow on Solstheim. ', '''ashfal'':1A,4B ''barrow'':21B ''bloodskal'':20B ''cave'':11B ''locat'':12B ''north'':13B ''raven'':15B ''rock'':16B ''seclud'':10B ''small'':9B ''solstheim'':23B ''southeast'':18B ''tear'':3A,6B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_extreme_magicka', 'A powerful brew that restores an extreme amount of magicka, essential for powerful mages and taxing spells. Restores an extreme amount of magicka, vital for executing taxing and high-level magical abilities. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists.', '''abil'':37B ''alchemist'':49B ''amount'':12B,25B ''brew'':7B ''essenti'':15B ''execut'':30B ''extrem'':3A,11B,24B ''found'':42B ''high'':34B ''high-level'':33B ''level'':35B ''loot'':45B ''mage'':18B ''magic'':36B ''magicka'':4A,14B,27B ''potion'':1A,39B ''power'':6B,17B ''purchas'':47B ''random'':44B ''restor'':9B,22B ''spell'':21B ''tax'':20B,31B ''vital'':28B', 'mage, alchemist, scholar, collegeofwinterhold, psijic', 'The Potion of Extreme Magicka restores an extreme amount of magicka for taxing magical feats. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lingering_magicka_poison', 'Lingering Magicka Poisons gradually drain a target''s magical reserves, leaving spellcasters vulnerable. Tiers include Lingering, Enduring, Lasting, Persisting, and Unceasing Magicka Poisons, with stronger tiers found in rare locations such as Highpoint Tower and Forsaken Crypt.', '''crypt'':40B ''drain'':8B ''endur'':20B ''forsaken'':39B ''found'':30B ''gradual'':7B ''highpoint'':36B ''includ'':18B ''last'':21B ''leav'':14B ''linger'':1A,4B,19B ''locat'':33B ''magic'':12B ''magicka'':2A,5B,25B ''persist'':22B ''poison'':3A,6B,26B ''rare'':32B ''reserv'':13B ''spellcast'':15B ''stronger'':28B ''target'':10B ''tier'':17B,29B ''tower'':37B ''unceas'':24B ''vulner'':16B', 'alchemist, mage, scholar', 'You know these poisons sap magicka over time, but their creation and sources remain obscure.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('daedroth_teeth', 'Daedroth Teeth, large teeth originating from the planes of Oblivion, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. Alchemy effects: Resist Frost, Light, Damage Magicka Regen, and Regenerate Stamina.', '''alchemi'':23B ''caravan'':22B ''daedroth'':1A,3B ''damag'':28B ''effect'':24B ''frost'':26B ''ingredi'':15B ''khajiit'':21B ''larg'':5B ''light'':27B ''magicka'':29B ''oblivion'':12B ''origin'':7B ''plane'':10B ''purchas'':19B ''regen'':30B ''regener'':32B ''resist'':25B ''stamina'':33B ''teeth'':2A,4B,6B', 'alchemist', 'Daedroth Teeth, large teeth originating from the planes of Oblivion, is an ingredient that can be purchased from Khajiit caravans. 
