INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('bloodworm_helm', '
The Bloodworm Helm is a necromantic artifact crafted by the lich Mannimarco from trollbone, known for its unsettling beauty and dark powers. The helm enhances Conjuration skills, allows the wearer to turn undead, drain enemy essence, and summon a skeletal minion. For undead wearers, it also strengthens their attacks. Mannimarco left the helm behind upon ascending to godhood during the Warp in the West.', '''allow'':30B ''also'':48B ''artifact'':9B ''ascend'':58B ''attack'':51B ''beauti'':21B ''behind'':56B ''bloodworm'':1A,4B ''conjur'':28B ''craft'':10B ''dark'':23B ''drain'':36B ''enemi'':37B ''enhanc'':27B ''essenc'':38B ''godhood'':60B ''helm'':2A,5B,26B,55B ''known'':17B ''left'':53B ''lich'':13B ''mannimarco'':14B,52B ''minion'':43B ''necromant'':8B ''power'':24B ''skelet'':42B ''skill'':29B ''strengthen'':49B ''summon'':40B ''trollbon'':16B ''turn'':34B ''undead'':35B,45B ''unsettl'':20B ''upon'':57B ''warp'':63B ''wearer'':32B,46B ''west'':66B', 'scholar', '
The Bloodworm Helm is a necromantic artifact created by Mannimarco, enhancing Conjuration, turning undead, and summoning minions. Left behind during Mannimarco''s ascent to godhood, it also boosts attacks for undead wearers.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('potion_of_extreme_healing', 'One of the most powerful potions available, this brew restores an extreme amount of health, crucial for dire situations. Restores an extreme amount of health, essential for surviving the most perilous encounters. These potions can be found in random loot or purchased from alchemists.', '''alchemist'':48B ''amount'':17B,27B ''avail'':11B ''brew'':13B ''crucial'':20B ''dire'':22B ''encount'':36B ''essenti'':30B ''extrem'':3A,16B,26B ''found'':41B ''heal'':4A ''health'':19B,29B ''loot'':44B ''one'':5B ''peril'':35B ''potion'':1A,10B,38B ''power'':9B ''purchas'':46B ''random'':43B ''restor'':14B,24B ''situat'':23B ''surviv'':32B', 'alchemist, healer, priest, warrior, companions', 'The Potion of Extreme Healing restores an extreme amount of health for dire situations. You do not know the full effects or details of this potion. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('otar_the_mad', 'Otar the Mad was a high-ranking Dragon Priest in the Merethic Era, once a just ruler who descended into madness, causing the downfall of Ragnvald. He wielded powerful magic and the Thu''um, and was known for his oppressive rule. After being defeated by heroes Saerek and Torsten, he was sealed in Ragnvald''s tomb, with his fate tied to two keys held by his captors. Otar was reawakened in the Fourth Era, still bound by his tomb and his past malevolent power.', '''bound'':80B ''captor'':71B ''caus'':26B ''defeat'':48B ''descend'':23B ''downfal'':28B ''dragon'':12B ''era'':17B,78B ''fate'':63B ''fourth'':77B ''held'':68B ''hero'':50B ''high'':10B ''high-rank'':9B ''key'':67B ''known'':41B ''mad'':3A,6B,25B ''magic'':34B ''malevol'':87B ''mereth'':16B ''oppress'':44B ''otar'':1A,4B,72B ''past'':86B ''power'':33B,88B ''priest'':13B ''ragnvald'':30B,58B ''rank'':11B ''reawaken'':74B ''rule'':45B ''ruler'':21B ''saerek'':51B ''seal'':56B ''still'':79B ''thu'':37B ''tie'':64B ''tomb'':60B,83B ''torsten'':53B ''two'':66B ''um'':38B ''wield'':32B', 'scholar, dragon', 'Otar the Mad must of been one of those Dragon Priests buried around Skyrim. You really don''t know much more apart from that.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ebony_mail', 'The Ebony Mail is a legendary Daedric artifact created by Boethiah, the Daedric Prince of deceit, treachery, and conspiracy. This enchanted ebony armor, typically a cuirass, grants its wearer resistance to fire, magical attacks, and physical blows while enabling stealthy movements and the ability to poison enemies upon close contact. Forged from the blood of Lorkhan after his heart was cast into the sea, the Ebony Mail embodies Boethiah’s cunning and deadly nature. Only individuals chosen by Boethiah can wield the artifact, as the Prince determines both its owner and duration of ownership.', '''abil'':46B ''armor'':25B ''artifact'':10B,84B ''attack'':36B ''blood'':56B ''blow'':39B ''boethiah'':13B,80B ''boethiah’'':71B ''cast'':63B ''chosen'':78B ''close'':51B ''conspiraci'':21B ''contact'':52B ''creat'':11B ''cuirass'':28B ''cun'':72B ''daedric'':9B,15B ''dead'':74B ''deceit'':18B ''determin'':88B ''durat'':93B ''eboni'':1A,4B,24B,68B ''embodi'':70B ''enabl'':41B ''enchant'':23B ''enemi'':49B ''fire'':34B ''forg'':53B ''grant'':29B ''heart'':61B ''individu'':77B ''legendari'':8B ''lorkhan'':58B ''magic'':35B ''mail'':2A,5B,69B ''movement'':43B ''natur'':75B ''owner'':91B ''ownership'':95B ''physic'':38B ''poison'':48B ''princ'':16B,87B ''resist'':32B ''sea'':66B ''stealthi'':42B ''treacheri'':19B ''typic'':26B ''upon'':50B ''wearer'':31B ''wield'':82B', 'daedric, daedra, scholar', '
The Ebony Mail is a powerful Daedric artifact created by Boethiah thought to  grant its wearer extra powers.', '', '', 'artifacts');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('large_antlers', 'Large Antlers may be dropped by male deer and elk, while female elk drop small antlers. Alchemy effects: Restore Stamina, Fortify Stamina, Slow, and Damage Stamina Regen.', '''alchemi'':19B ''antler'':2A,4B,18B ''damag'':27B ''deer'':10B ''drop'':7B,16B ''effect'':20B ''elk'':12B,15B ''femal'':14B ''fortifi'':23B ''larg'':1A,3B ''male'':9B ''may'':5B ''regen'':29B ''restor'':21B ''slow'':25B ''small'':17B ''stamina'':22B,24B,28B', 'alchemist', 'Large Antlers may be dropped by male deer and elk, while female elk drop small antlers. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_shield', 'Dwarven Shield is a basic dwarven shield with good protection quality. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. To craft it: 2 dwarven metal ingots, 1 iron ingot, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dwarvern ingot at a workbench.', '''1'':38B,42B ''2'':34B ''adept'':50B ''angular'':18B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':47B ''bronz'':25B ''craft'':32B,53B ''design'':16B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,8B,35B ''dwarvern'':61B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':48B ''golden'':24B ''golden-bronz'':23B ''good'':11B ''ingot'':37B,40B,62B ''intric'':28B ''iron'':39B ''leather'':43B ''mechan'':29B ''metal'':36B ''ornat'':20B ''pattern'':30B ''protect'':12B ''qualiti'':13B ''shield'':2A,4B,9B ''smith'':51B ''strip'':44B ''tempered/improved'':58B ''use'':60B ''visual'':15B ''workbench'':65B', 'blacksmith', 'Dwarven Shield is a basic dwarven shield with good protection quality. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('expel_daedra', 'Expel Daedra is a Conjuration spell that banishes a summoned Daedra back to Oblivion and works on more powerful Daedra than the standard banishment spells. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''back'':14B ''banish'':10B,26B ''cast'':35B ''conjur'':7B ''daedra'':2A,4B,13B,22B ''expel'':1A,3B ''expert'':31B ''level'':33B ''oblivion'':16B ''power'':21B ''requir'':29B ''skill'':32B ''spell'':8B,27B ''standard'':25B ''summon'':12B ''work'':18B', 'mage', 'Expel Daedra is a spell that banishes a summoned Daedra back to Oblivion, and it is effective against more powerful Daedra than the standard banishment spells. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fort_greymoor', 'Fort Greymoor is a medium-sized stronghold located west of Whiterun and south of Redoran''s Retreat, strategically positioned on the plains of Whiterun Hold. It is occupied by bandits.

The fort consists of two distinct zones: the main structure, Fort Greymoor, and its adjoining prison. Surrounded by crumbling walls and guarded by towers, the fort serves as both a defensive position and a staging ground for its occupants. ', '''adjoin'':48B ''bandit'':33B ''consist'':36B ''crumbl'':52B ''defens'':64B ''distinct'':39B ''fort'':1A,3B,35B,44B,59B ''greymoor'':2A,4B,45B ''ground'':69B ''guard'':55B ''hold'':28B ''locat'':11B ''main'':42B ''medium'':8B ''medium-s'':7B ''occup'':72B ''occupi'':31B ''plain'':25B ''posit'':22B,65B ''prison'':49B ''redoran'':18B ''retreat'':20B ''serv'':60B ''size'':9B ''south'':16B ''stage'':68B ''strateg'':21B ''stronghold'':10B ''structur'':43B ''surround'':50B ''tower'':57B ''two'':38B ''wall'':53B ''west'':12B ''whiterun'':14B,27B ''zone'':40B', 'whiterun, legion, stormcloak', 'Fort Greymoor is a medium-sized stronghold located west of Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('yol_toor_shul', 'Fire Breath is a Shout that allows you to inhale air and exhale a powerful flame, creating an inferno. The three words of power in this Shout are Yol (Fire), which conjures the flames; Toor (Inferno), which intensifies the blaze into a fiery eruption; and Shul (Sun), which amplifies the heat and power of the flames to scorch your enemies.', '''air'':14B ''allow'':10B ''amplifi'':52B ''blaze'':43B ''breath'':5B ''conjur'':35B ''creat'':20B ''enemi'':63B ''erupt'':47B ''exhal'':16B ''fieri'':46B ''fire'':4B,33B ''flame'':19B,37B,59B ''heat'':54B ''inferno'':22B,39B ''inhal'':13B ''intensifi'':41B ''power'':18B,27B,56B ''scorch'':61B ''shout'':8B,30B ''shul'':3A,49B ''sun'':50B ''three'':24B ''toor'':2A,38B ''word'':25B ''yol'':1A,32B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('forelhost', 'Forelhost is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southeast of Riften and west of Stendarr''s Beacon in the Rift. It is home to a large amount of draugr. Rumours of a Dragon Priest live in the ruins.', '''amount'':29B ''beacon'':19B ''dragon'':35B ''draugr'':31B ''forelhost'':1A,2B ''home'':25B ''larg'':28B ''live'':37B ''locat'':10B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''nordic'':8B ''priest'':36B ''rift'':22B ''riften'':13B ''ruin'':9B,40B ''rumour'':32B ''size'':7B ''southeast'':11B ''stendarr'':17B ''west'':15B', 'rift', 'Forelhost is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southeast of Riften and west of Stendarr''s Beacon in the Rift.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('lyretail_anthias', 'Lyretail Anthias are a small orange,yellow and purple fish found at small streams by using an Alikri fishing rod. When used as an ingredient for potion making, they offer effects such as Restore Magicka, Fortify Alteration, Fortify Conjuration and Fortify Carry Weight.', '''alikri'':20B ''alter'':39B ''anthia'':2A,4B ''carri'':44B ''conjur'':41B ''effect'':33B ''fish'':12B,21B ''fortifi'':38B,40B,43B ''found'':13B ''ingredi'':27B ''lyretail'':1A,3B ''magicka'':37B ''make'':30B ''offer'':32B ''orang'':8B ''potion'':29B ''purpl'':11B ''restor'':36B ''rod'':22B ''small'':7B,15B ''stream'':16B ''use'':18B,24B ''weight'':45B ''yellow'':9B', 'fisher', 'Lyretail Anthias are a small orange,yellow and purple fish. You do not know much more about the fish, but a fisher would.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('wind_stone', 'The Water Stone is one of the All-Maker Stones located on Solstheim, positioned north of Raven Rock and west of Fahlbtharz. This sacred site holds profound importance to the Skaal people, reflecting their spiritual connection to the natural elements and their worship of the All-Maker.', '''all-mak'':10B,49B ''connect'':39B ''element'':43B ''fahlbtharz'':25B ''hold'':29B ''import'':31B ''locat'':14B ''maker'':12B,51B ''natur'':42B ''north'':18B ''one'':7B ''peopl'':35B ''posit'':17B ''profound'':30B ''raven'':20B ''reflect'':36B ''rock'':21B ''sacr'':27B ''site'':28B ''skaal'':34B ''solstheim'':16B ''spiritu'':38B ''stone'':2A,5B,13B ''water'':4B ''west'':23B ''wind'':1A ''worship'':46B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fast_healing', 'Fast Healing is a Restoration spell that rapidly restores a significant amount of health to the target, whether it be the caster or an ally. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''alli'':27B ''amount'':14B ''apprentic'':31B ''cast'':35B ''caster'':24B ''fast'':1A,3B ''heal'':2A,4B ''health'':16B ''level'':33B ''rapid'':10B ''requir'':29B ''restor'':7B,11B ''signific'':13B ''skill'':32B ''spell'':8B ''target'':19B ''whether'':20B', 'mage', '
Fast Healing is a spell that quickly restores a significant amount of health to the target, whether it be the caster or an ally. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('fox', 'Foxes are small, non-aggressive creatures found in Skyrim''s wilderness, often chasing rabbits. They drop pelts upon death, which can be used for tanning. Foxes will flee when approached.', '''aggress'':7B ''approach'':32B ''chase'':15B ''creatur'':8B ''death'':21B ''drop'':18B ''flee'':30B ''found'':9B ''fox'':1A,2B,28B ''non'':6B ''non-aggress'':5B ''often'':14B ''pelt'':19B ''rabbit'':16B ''skyrim'':11B ''small'':4B ''tan'':27B ''upon'':20B ''use'':25B ''wilder'':13B', 'hunter', 'Foxes are small, non-aggressive creatures found in Skyrim''s wilderness.', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('heimskr''s_house', 'Heimskr''s House is a modest dwelling located in Whiterun, near the sacred Gildergreen tree, nestled between Jorrvaskr and the Temple of Kynareth. The home belongs to Heimskr, a fervent priest of Talos known for his impassioned sermons extolling the virtues of the Ninth Divine.
', '''belong'':29B ''divin'':48B ''dwell'':10B ''extol'':42B ''fervent'':33B ''gildergreen'':17B ''heimskr'':1A,4B,31B ''home'':28B ''hous'':3A,6B ''impass'':40B ''jorrvaskr'':21B ''known'':37B ''kynareth'':26B ''locat'':11B ''modest'':9B ''near'':14B ''nestl'':19B ''ninth'':47B ''priest'':34B ''sacr'':16B ''sermon'':41B ''talo'':36B ''templ'':24B ''tree'':18B ''virtu'':44B ''whiterun'':13B', 'whiterun', 'Heimskr''s House is a modest dwelling located in the Winds District in Whiterun.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, falkreath, eastmarch, reach, pale, hjaalmarch', '', 'whiterun');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('incinerate', 'Incinerate is a Destruction spell that launches a concentrated blast of fire, dealing massive fire damage to a target and incinerating them. It requires an Expert skill level to cast.', '''blast'':11B ''cast'':31B ''concentr'':10B ''damag'':17B ''deal'':14B ''destruct'':5B ''expert'':27B ''fire'':13B,16B ''inciner'':1A,2B,22B ''launch'':8B ''level'':29B ''massiv'':15B ''requir'':25B ''skill'':28B ''spell'':6B ''target'':20B', 'mage', '
Incinerate is a spell that releases a concentrated blast of fire, dealing massive fire damage to a target and incinerating them. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('highpoint_tower', 'Highpoint Tower is a small, decrepit fort located east of Raven Rock and north of Fort Frostmoth on Solstheim. The fort has fallen into disrepair and is now overrun by albino spiders, making it a dangerous and eerie place to explore.', '''albino'':33B ''danger'':38B ''decrepit'':8B ''disrepair'':27B ''east'':11B ''eeri'':40B ''explor'':43B ''fallen'':25B ''fort'':9B,18B,23B ''frostmoth'':19B ''highpoint'':1A,3B ''locat'':10B ''make'':35B ''north'':16B ''overrun'':31B ''place'':41B ''raven'':13B ''rock'':14B ''small'':7B ''solstheim'':21B ''spider'':34B ''tower'':2A,4B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dawnguard_heavy_gauntlets', 'Dawnguard Heavy Gauntlets have good protection quality. Their visual design is robust and defensive, with reinforced metal plates over leather for maximum durability. They can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''craft'':31B ''dawnguard'':1A,4B ''defens'':17B ''design'':13B ''durabl'':26B ''gauntlet'':3A,6B ''good'':8B ''heavi'':2A,5B ''leather'':23B ''maximum'':25B ''metal'':20B ''plate'':21B ''protect'':9B ''qualiti'':10B ''reinforc'':19B ''robust'':15B ''steel'':38B ''tempered/improved'':35B ''use'':37B ''visual'':12B ''workbench'':41B', 'blacksmith', 'Dawnguard Heavy Gauntlets have good protection quality. Their visual design is robust and defensive, with reinforced metal plates over leather for maximum durability. They can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('eastmarch_imperial_camp', 'Eastmarch Imperial Camp is an Imperial military outpost located in Eastmarch, southeast of Mzulft and north of Stony Creek Cave. The camp serves as a strategic base for the Imperial Legion''s operations in the region during the Skyrim Civil War.

It is commanded by Legate Hrollod.', '''base'':30B ''camp'':3A,6B,25B ''cave'':23B ''civil'':43B ''command'':47B ''creek'':22B ''eastmarch'':1A,4B,14B ''hrollod'':50B ''imperi'':2A,5B,9B,33B ''legat'':49B ''legion'':34B ''locat'':12B ''militari'':10B ''mzulft'':17B ''north'':19B ''oper'':36B ''outpost'':11B ''region'':39B ''serv'':26B ''skyrim'':42B ''southeast'':15B ''stoni'':21B ''strateg'':29B ''war'':44B', 'eastmarch, legion', 'Eastmarch Imperial Camp is an Imperial military outpost located in Eastmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('grey_quarter', 'The Gray Quarter is a district in Windhelm, home to the city''s sizable population of Dark Elves, or Dunmer, who sought refuge in Skyrim after the eruption of Red Mountain. Once known as the Snow Quarter, it is a cramped and impoverished area, where the Dunmer face suspicion and xenophobia from the Nords, who view them with disdain. Although they are not openly persecuted, the Dunmer live in difficult conditions, with little support from Jarl Ulfric Stormcloak, who largely ignores their plight.

The Gray Quarter reflects the tension between Windhelm''s native Nords and the immigrant Dunmer, who are forced to live in this slum on the city''s outskirts. Additionally, Argonians, who also reside in Windhelm, are prohibited from entering the city itself and are confined to the docks outside the city walls.', '''addit'':114B ''also'':117B ''although'':62B ''area'':46B ''argonian'':115B ''citi'':14B,111B,126B,136B ''condit'':73B ''confin'':130B ''cramp'':43B ''dark'':19B ''difficult'':72B ''disdain'':61B ''district'':8B ''dock'':133B ''dunmer'':22B,49B,69B,100B ''elv'':20B ''enter'':124B ''erupt'':30B ''face'':50B ''forc'':103B ''gray'':4B,87B ''grey'':1A ''home'':11B ''ignor'':83B ''immigr'':99B ''impoverish'':45B ''jarl'':78B ''known'':35B ''larg'':82B ''littl'':75B ''live'':70B,105B ''mountain'':33B ''nativ'':95B ''nord'':56B,96B ''open'':66B ''outsid'':134B ''outskirt'':113B ''persecut'':67B ''plight'':85B ''popul'':17B ''prohibit'':122B ''quarter'':2A,5B,39B,88B ''red'':32B ''reflect'':89B ''refug'':25B ''resid'':118B ''sizabl'':16B ''skyrim'':27B ''slum'':108B ''snow'':38B ''sought'':24B ''stormcloak'':80B ''support'':76B ''suspicion'':51B ''tension'':91B ''ulfric'':79B ''view'':58B ''wall'':137B ''windhelm'':10B,93B,120B ''xenophobia'':53B', 'eastmarch', 'The Gray Quarter is a district in Windhelm, home to the city''s sizable population of Dark Elves, or Dunmer, who sought refuge in Skyrim after the eruption of Red Mountain. Once known as the Snow Quarter, it is a cramped and impoverished area, where the Dunmer face suspicion and xenophobia from the Nords, who view them with disdainYou do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, rift, winterhold, whiterun', '', 'eastmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('corpselight_farm', 'Corpselight Farm is a small farmstead located in the center of Falkreath, directly behind the inn Dead Man''s Drink, in Falkreath Hold. It is run by Mathies and his wife, Indara Caerellia, who are grieving the recent loss of their daughter.

Their daughter was tragically killed by a passing farmhand named Sinding, who went berserk and tore her apart.', '''apart'':62B ''behind'':16B ''berserk'':58B ''caerellia'':35B ''center'':12B ''corpselight'':1A,3B ''daughter'':44B,46B ''dead'':19B ''direct'':15B ''drink'':22B ''falkreath'':14B,24B ''farm'':2A,4B ''farmhand'':53B ''farmstead'':8B ''griev'':38B ''hold'':25B ''indara'':34B ''inn'':18B ''kill'':49B ''locat'':9B ''loss'':41B ''man'':20B ''mathi'':30B ''name'':54B ''pass'':52B ''recent'':40B ''run'':28B ''sind'':55B ''small'':7B ''tore'':60B ''tragic'':48B ''went'':57B ''wife'':33B', 'falkreath', 'Corpselight Farm is a small farmstead located in Falkreath, the town, in Falkreath Hold. You do not know who runs the farm.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, rift reach', '', 'falkreath');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hjaalmarch_stormcloak_camp', 'Hjaalmarch Stormcloak Camp is a Stormcloak military encampment located east of Ustengrav and west of Mzinchaleft in Hjaalmarch. The camp serves as a base of operations for the Stormcloaks in their campaign to gain control of the region.

The camp is typically commanded by Arrald Frozen-Heart.', '''arrald'':48B ''base'':27B ''camp'':3A,6B,23B,43B ''campaign'':35B ''command'':46B ''control'':38B ''east'':13B ''encamp'':11B ''frozen'':50B ''frozen-heart'':49B ''gain'':37B ''heart'':51B ''hjaalmarch'':1A,4B,21B ''locat'':12B ''militari'':10B ''mzinchaleft'':19B ''oper'':29B ''region'':41B ''serv'':24B ''stormcloak'':2A,5B,9B,32B ''typic'':45B ''ustengrav'':15B ''west'':17B', 'hjaalmarch, stormcloak', 'Hjaalmarch Stormcloak Camp is a Stormcloak military encampment located east of Morthal in Hjaalmarch.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ravenscar_hollow', 'Ravenscar Hollow is a small cave located west of the Thalmor Embassy and due east of the Steed Stone in Haafingar. The cave is inhabited by hagravens, making it a perilous location for those who dare to venture inside.

To find the cave, head east along the road that passes Wolfskull Cave, continuing downhill past a switchback. Along the way, you’ll notice two cairns on the left, marking the beginning of a path that winds downhill, passing several more cairns and leading you to the cave’s entrance along the shore. The eerie atmosphere of the cave and its hagraven occupants make it a notable site for adventurers in the region.', '''adventur'':109B ''along'':48B,60B,90B ''atmospher'':95B ''begin'':72B ''cairn'':66B,82B ''cave'':8B,25B,45B,54B,98B ''cave’'':88B ''continu'':55B ''dare'':38B ''downhil'':56B,78B ''due'':16B ''east'':17B,47B ''eeri'':94B ''embassi'':14B ''entranc'':89B ''find'':43B ''haafingar'':23B ''hagraven'':29B,101B ''head'':46B ''hollow'':2A,4B ''inhabit'':27B ''insid'':41B ''lead'':84B ''left'':69B ''locat'':9B,34B ''make'':30B,103B ''mark'':70B ''notabl'':106B ''notic'':64B ''occup'':102B ''pass'':52B,79B ''past'':57B ''path'':75B ''peril'':33B ''ravenscar'':1A,3B ''region'':112B ''road'':50B ''sever'':80B ''shore'':92B ''site'':107B ''small'':7B ''steed'':20B ''stone'':21B ''switchback'':59B ''thalmor'':13B ''two'':65B ''ventur'':40B ''way'':62B ''west'':10B ''wind'':77B ''wolfskul'':53B ''you’ll'':63B', 'haafingar', 'Ravenscar Hollow is a small cave located west of the Thalmor Embassy in Haafingar. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, reach, hjaalmarch', '', 'haafingar');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('falmer_blood_elixir', 'An amazing concoction that can grant your every wish. Only available from Brynjolf for a limited time.', '''amaz'':5B ''avail'':14B ''blood'':2A ''brynjolf'':16B ''concoct'':6B ''elixir'':3A ''everi'':11B ''falmer'':1A ''grant'':9B ''limit'':19B ''time'':20B ''wish'':12B', 'brynjolf', 'You have only heard rumors of this potion supposedly granting any wish one desires. It is supposedly sold by a persuasive merchant, ''Brynjolf'' if you remember correctly, in Riften.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('silverdrift_lair', 'Silverdrift Lair is a small Nordic ruin located south-southeast of Dawnstar and west-northwest of Nightgate Inn in The Pale. The lair is inhabited by draugr.', '''dawnstar'':15B ''draugr'':31B ''inhabit'':29B ''inn'':22B ''lair'':2A,4B,27B ''locat'':10B ''nightgat'':21B ''nordic'':8B ''northwest'':19B ''pale'':25B ''ruin'':9B ''silverdrift'':1A,3B ''small'':7B ''south'':12B ''south-southeast'':11B ''southeast'':13B ''west'':18B ''west-northwest'':17B', 'pale', 'Silverdrift Lair is a small Nordic ruin located south-southeast of Dawnstar in The Pale. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('tower_of_mzark', 'The Tower of Mzark is a small Dwarven tower located in Blackreach, accessible only from within the cavern. It is situated in the southwestern corner of Blackreach, perched on a spire between two waterfalls. A stone bridge crosses the river below, connecting to the northern face of the tower.', '''access'':16B ''blackreach'':15B,30B ''bridg'':40B ''cavern'':21B ''connect'':45B ''corner'':28B ''cross'':41B ''dwarven'':11B ''face'':49B ''locat'':13B ''mzark'':3A,7B ''northern'':48B ''perch'':31B ''river'':43B ''situat'':24B ''small'':10B ''southwestern'':27B ''spire'':34B ''stone'':39B ''tower'':1A,5B,12B,52B ''two'':36B ''waterfal'':37B ''within'':19B', 'pale, dwemer', 'The Tower of Mzark is a small Dwarven tower located in Blackreach.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('folgunthur', 'Folgunthur is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southeast of Solitude and west of the Abandoned Shack in Hjaalmarch. The ruin is inhabited by draugr.', '''abandon'':18B ''draugr'':27B ''folgunthur'':1A,2B ''hjaalmarch'':21B ''inhabit'':25B ''locat'':10B ''medium'':6B ''medium-s'':5B ''nordic'':8B ''ruin'':9B,23B ''shack'':19B ''size'':7B ''solitud'':13B ''southeast'':11B ''west'':15B', 'hjaalmarch', 'Folgunthur is a medium-sized Nordic ruin located southeast of Solitude and west of the Abandoned Shack in Hjaalmarch. You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('heartwood_mill', 'Heartwood Mill is a small, struggling lumber mill located on the shores of Lake Honrich at the mouth of the Treva River, west of Goldenglow Estate in the Rift. The mill is operated by Grosta, who has been left to run it alone after the disappearance of her husband, Leifnarr. She is assisted by their young son, Gralnach, who helps as much as he can.', '''alon'':45B ''assist'':55B ''disappear'':48B ''estat'':28B ''goldenglow'':27B ''gralnach'':60B ''grosta'':37B ''heartwood'':1A,3B ''help'':62B ''honrich'':17B ''husband'':51B ''lake'':16B ''left'':41B ''leifnarr'':52B ''locat'':11B ''lumber'':9B ''mill'':2A,4B,10B,33B ''mouth'':20B ''much'':64B ''oper'':35B ''rift'':31B ''river'':24B ''run'':43B ''shore'':14B ''small'':7B ''son'':59B ''struggl'':8B ''treva'':23B ''west'':25B ''young'':58B', 'rift', 'Heartwood Mill is a small, struggling lumber mill located on the shores of Lake Honrich at the mouth of the Treva River.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('last_vigil', 'Last Vigil is a small, secluded camp located northeast of Riften and southeast of Ruunvald Excavation. It is rumoured that one day a great battle will take place here, between two warriors who have reached the end of their quest.', '''battl'':27B ''camp'':9B ''day'':24B ''end'':39B ''excav'':18B ''great'':26B ''last'':1A,3B ''locat'':10B ''northeast'':11B ''one'':23B ''place'':30B ''quest'':42B ''reach'':37B ''riften'':13B ''rumour'':21B ''ruunvald'':17B ''seclud'':8B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':15B ''take'':29B ''two'':33B ''vigil'':2A,4B ''warrior'':34B', 'rift', 'Last Vigil is a small, secluded camp located northeast of Riften. It is rumoured that one day a great battle will take place here, between two warriors who have reached the end of their quest.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('vahlok''s_tomb', 'Vahlok''s Tomb is a small but formidable Nordic ruin located south-southeast of Thirsk Mead Hall and north-northeast of Ashfallow Citadel, deep within the ash-ridden expanse of Solstheim. This ancient burial site serves as the final resting place of Vahlok the Jailor, a dragon priest of great power and ominous legacy.', '''ancient'':39B ''ash'':33B ''ash-ridden'':32B ''ashfallow'':27B ''burial'':40B ''citadel'':28B ''deep'':29B ''dragon'':53B ''expans'':35B ''final'':45B ''formid'':11B ''great'':56B ''hall'':21B ''jailor'':51B ''legaci'':60B ''locat'':14B ''mead'':20B ''nordic'':12B ''north'':24B ''north-northeast'':23B ''northeast'':25B ''omin'':59B ''place'':47B ''power'':57B ''priest'':54B ''rest'':46B ''ridden'':34B ''ruin'':13B ''serv'':42B ''site'':41B ''small'':9B ''solstheim'':37B ''south'':16B ''south-southeast'':15B ''southeast'':17B ''thirsk'':19B ''tomb'':3A,6B ''vahlok'':1A,4B,49B ''within'':30B', 'solstheim', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dawnguard_full_helmet', 'Dawnguard Full Helmet has good protection quality. Its visual design is heavy and protective, covering the entire head with a solid metal structure and a distinct, angular visor. It can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''angular'':30B ''cover'':18B ''craft'':36B ''dawnguard'':1A,4B ''design'':13B ''distinct'':29B ''entir'':20B ''full'':2A,5B ''good'':8B ''head'':21B ''heavi'':15B ''helmet'':3A,6B ''metal'':25B ''protect'':9B,17B ''qualiti'':10B ''solid'':24B ''steel'':43B ''structur'':26B ''tempered/improved'':40B ''use'':42B ''visor'':31B ''visual'':12B ''workbench'':46B', 'blacksmith', 'Dawnguard Full Helmet has good protection quality. Its visual design is heavy and protective, covering the entire head with a solid metal structure and a distinct, angular visor. It can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('morwen''s_house', 'Morwen''s House is a cozy, well-kept home located on the north side of Skaal Village, positioned between Edla''s House to the west and the Greathall to the southeast. This modest dwelling is the home of Morwen, a dedicated Nord woman living in the village. She works as an apprentice to Baldor Iron-Shaper, the village blacksmith, honing her skills and learning the craft of metalwork during the day.', '''apprentic'':56B ''baldor'':58B ''blacksmith'':64B ''cozi'':9B ''craft'':71B ''day'':76B ''dedic'':45B ''dwell'':38B ''edla'':24B ''greathal'':32B ''home'':13B,41B ''hone'':65B ''hous'':3A,6B,26B ''iron'':60B ''iron-shap'':59B ''kept'':12B ''learn'':69B ''live'':48B ''locat'':14B ''metalwork'':73B ''modest'':37B ''morwen'':1A,4B,43B ''nord'':46B ''north'':17B ''posit'':22B ''shaper'':61B ''side'':18B ''skaal'':20B ''skill'':67B ''southeast'':35B ''villag'':21B,51B,63B ''well'':11B ''well-kept'':10B ''west'':29B ''woman'':47B ''work'':53B', 'skaal', 'You do not know anything about this area.', '', '', 'solstheim');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('high_rock', 'High Rock, located in northwestern Tamriel, is home to the Bretons, who have divided the province into numerous city-states and minor kingdoms. The region also historically housed Orsinium, the Orcs'' City-State. High Rock’s history traces back to the Direnni Hegemony, which once ruled the area before its dissolution in the First Era, leaving behind ruins and a lasting influence on Breton culture. The rugged terrain, including highlands, isolated valleys, and diverse landscapes like temperate forests and snowy mountains, has fostered a strong sense of independence among the Breton clans. Other races, such as Orcs, Snow Elves, and centaurs, have also called High Rock home at various points in its history.

The province is divided into six main regions: Glenumbra, Stormhaven, Rivenspire, the Western Reach, northern Bangkorai, and Wrothgar, alongside numerous islands like Balfiera and Betony. High Rock is bordered by Hammerfell to the southeast and Skyrim to the east, with the Iliac Bay and surrounding seas providing access to its coastal areas. Its unique geography and bardic traditions contribute to a rich cultural heritage, uniting its fiercely independent clans under a shared Breton identity.', '''access'':164B ''alongsid'':135B ''also'':29B,106B ''among'':92B ''area'':51B,168B ''back'':42B ''balfiera'':139B ''bangkorai'':132B ''bardic'':173B ''bay'':159B ''behind'':60B ''betoni'':141B ''border'':145B ''breton'':13B,67B,94B,189B ''call'':107B ''centaur'':104B ''citi'':22B,36B ''city-st'':21B,35B ''clan'':95B,185B ''coastal'':167B ''contribut'':175B ''cultur'':68B,179B ''direnni'':45B ''dissolut'':54B ''divers'':77B ''divid'':16B,120B ''east'':155B ''elv'':102B ''era'':58B ''fierc'':183B ''first'':57B ''forest'':81B ''foster'':86B ''geographi'':171B ''glenumbra'':125B ''hammerfel'':147B ''hegemoni'':46B ''heritag'':180B ''high'':1A,3B,38B,108B,142B ''highland'':73B ''histor'':30B ''histori'':40B,116B ''home'':10B,110B ''hous'':31B ''ident'':190B ''iliac'':158B ''includ'':72B ''independ'':91B,184B ''influenc'':65B ''island'':137B ''isol'':74B ''kingdom'':26B ''landscap'':78B ''last'':64B ''leav'':59B ''like'':79B,138B ''locat'':5B ''main'':123B ''minor'':25B ''mountain'':84B ''northern'':131B ''northwestern'':7B ''numer'':20B,136B ''orc'':34B,100B ''orsinium'':32B ''point'':113B ''provid'':163B ''provinc'':18B,118B ''race'':97B ''reach'':130B ''region'':28B,124B ''rich'':178B ''rivenspir'':127B ''rock'':2A,4B,109B,143B ''rock’'':39B ''rug'':70B ''ruin'':61B ''rule'':49B ''sea'':162B ''sens'':89B ''share'':188B ''six'':122B ''skyrim'':152B ''snow'':101B ''snowi'':83B ''southeast'':150B ''state'':23B,37B ''stormhaven'':126B ''strong'':88B ''surround'':161B ''tamriel'':8B ''temper'':80B ''terrain'':71B ''trace'':41B ''tradit'':174B ''uniqu'':170B ''unit'':181B ''valley'':75B ''various'':112B ''western'':129B ''wrothgar'':134B', 'scholar, breton, noble', 'High Rock, located in northwestern Tamriel, is home to the Bretons and is divided into multiple city-states and minor kingdoms. Historically, it also housed Orsinium, the Orcs'' city-state. The province has a rugged landscape with highlands, valleys, temperate forests, and snowy mountains, fostering a strong sense of independence among its clans. High Rock’s history includes the Direnni Hegemony, which greatly influenced Breton culture. The province is divided into six main regions, including Glenumbra, Stormhaven, and Wrothgar, and is bordered by Hammerfell and Skyrim. Its diverse geography and bardic traditions contribute to a rich cultural heritage.', '', '', 'locationother');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('brood_cavern', 'Brood Cavern is a small cave located southwest of Morthal and southeast of Dead Men''s Respite in Hjaalmarch. The cavern is inhabited by dagnerous animals.', '''anim'':28B ''brood'':1A,3B ''cave'':8B ''cavern'':2A,4B,23B ''dagner'':27B ''dead'':16B ''hjaalmarch'':21B ''inhabit'':25B ''locat'':9B ''men'':17B ''morthal'':12B ''respit'':19B ''small'':7B ''southeast'':14B ''southwest'':10B', 'hjaalmarch, vampire', 'Brood Cavern is a small cave located southwest of Morthal in HjaalmarchYou do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, whiterun, pale, haafingar', '', 'hjaalmarch');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('talos', 'Talos, also known as Tiber Septim, was a legendary figure who rose to prominence as the first Emperor of the unified Tamriel and later ascended to godhood. In life, Talos conquered all of Tamriel, founding the Third Empire and ushering in the Third Era. Born in Atmora, his birth name, Talos, means "Stormcrown" in the ancient Ehlnofey language. Throughout his military and political career, he was also known by other titles, including Ysmir, Dragon of the North, the Grey Wind, and Storm of Kyne. His legendary conquests culminated in the subjugation of the Aldmeri Dominion, leading to his later veneration by humans as the "Hero-God of Mankind." Upon his death in 3E 38, Tiber Septim is believed to have ascended to become the ninth Divine, joining the pantheon of the Eight Divines as Talos.

Talos is revered as the patron of warriors, adventurers, and rulers, symbolizing the virtues of strength, courage, and leadership. His divine status, however, is a point of contention, especially among the Altmer, who view his apotheosis with hostility due to his conquest of their lands. In the Fourth Era, worship of Talos was banned following the White-Gold Concordat between the Aldmeri Dominion and the Empire, which claimed that a man could not achieve godhood. This ban ignited the Skyrim Civil War, with the Stormcloaks, led by Ulfric Stormcloak, rebelling in defense of their right to worship Talos. Despite the ban, Talos remains a powerful symbol of unity and strength for many, particularly among the Nords and other human races. Amulets of Talos, often crafted from dragonbone and scales, are used by his followers to invoke his blessing and strength in their endeavors.', '''38'':116B ''3e'':115B ''achiev'':212B ''adventur'':146B ''aldmeri'':95B,200B ''also'':3B,68B ''altmer'':169B ''among'':167B,252B ''amulet'':259B ''ancient'':57B ''apotheosi'':173B ''ascend'':26B,123B ''atmora'':48B ''ban'':191B,215B,239B ''becom'':125B ''believ'':120B ''birth'':50B ''bless'':276B ''born'':46B ''career'':65B ''civil'':219B ''claim'':206B ''concordat'':197B ''conquer'':32B ''conquest'':88B,179B ''content'':165B ''could'':210B ''courag'':154B ''craft'':263B ''culmin'':89B ''death'':113B ''defens'':230B ''despit'':237B ''divin'':128B,135B,158B ''dominion'':96B,201B ''dragon'':75B ''dragonbon'':265B ''due'':176B ''ehlnofey'':58B ''eight'':134B ''emperor'':19B ''empir'':39B,204B ''endeavor'':281B ''era'':45B,186B ''especi'':166B ''figur'':11B ''first'':18B ''follow'':192B,272B ''found'':36B ''fourth'':185B ''god'':108B ''godhood'':28B,213B ''gold'':196B ''grey'':80B ''hero'':107B ''hero-god'':106B ''hostil'':175B ''howev'':160B ''human'':103B,257B ''ignit'':216B ''includ'':73B ''invok'':274B ''join'':129B ''known'':4B,69B ''kyne'':85B ''land'':182B ''languag'':59B ''later'':25B,100B ''lead'':97B ''leadership'':156B ''led'':224B ''legendari'':10B,87B ''life'':30B ''man'':209B ''mani'':250B ''mankind'':110B ''mean'':53B ''militari'':62B ''name'':51B ''ninth'':127B ''nord'':254B ''north'':78B ''often'':262B ''pantheon'':131B ''particular'':251B ''patron'':143B ''point'':163B ''polit'':64B ''power'':243B ''promin'':15B ''race'':258B ''rebel'':228B ''remain'':241B ''rever'':140B ''right'':233B ''rose'':13B ''ruler'':148B ''scale'':267B ''septim'':7B,118B ''skyrim'':218B ''status'':159B ''storm'':83B ''stormcloak'':223B,227B ''stormcrown'':54B ''strength'':153B,248B,278B ''subjug'':92B ''symbol'':149B,244B ''talo'':1A,2B,31B,52B,137B,138B,189B,236B,240B,261B ''tamriel'':23B,35B ''third'':38B,44B ''throughout'':60B ''tiber'':6B,117B ''titl'':72B ''ulfric'':226B ''unifi'':22B ''uniti'':246B ''upon'':111B ''use'':269B ''usher'':41B ''vener'':101B ''view'':171B ''virtu'':151B ''war'':220B ''warrior'':145B ''white'':195B ''white-gold'':194B ''wind'':81B ''worship'':187B,235B ''ysmir'':74B', 'priest, scholar, companions', '
Talos, also known as Tiber Septim, was the first Emperor of a unified Tamriel and later ascended to godhood, becoming the ninth Divine. Born in Atmora and originally named Talos, meaning "Stormcrown," he founded the Third Empire through military conquest, including subjugating the Aldmeri Dominion, earning him veneration as the "Hero-God of Mankind." Revered for his strength, courage, and leadership, Talos symbolizes unity and the virtues of warriors and rulers. However, his divine status is contested, particularly by the Altmer, and worship of Talos was banned in the Fourth Era under the White-Gold Concordat, sparking the Skyrim Civil War. Despite opposition, Talos remains a powerful symbol of human resilience and faith, especially among the Nords.', '', '', 'figures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('spriggan_sap', 'Spriggan Sap is found randomly around Skyrim, and its origins of creation remain a mystery. Alchemy effects: Damage Magicka Regen, Fortify Enchanting, Fortify Smithing, and Fortify Alteration.', '''alchemi'':18B ''alter'':29B ''around'':8B ''creation'':14B ''damag'':20B ''effect'':19B ''enchant'':24B ''fortifi'':23B,25B,28B ''found'':6B ''magicka'':21B ''mysteri'':17B ''origin'':12B ''random'':7B ''regen'':22B ''remain'':15B ''sap'':2A,4B ''skyrim'':9B ''smith'':26B ''spriggan'':1A,3B', 'alchemist', 'Spriggan Sap is found randomly around Skyrim, and its origins of creation remain a mystery. 
You do not know the alchemical effects of this ingredient. However, an alchemist might.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ironflesh', 'Ironflesh is an Alteration spell that significantly boosts the caster''s armor rating for a short duration, providing enhanced protection. It requires an Adept skill level to cast.', '''adept'':25B ''alter'':5B ''armor'':13B ''boost'':9B ''cast'':29B ''caster'':11B ''durat'':18B ''enhanc'':20B ''ironflesh'':1A,2B ''level'':27B ''protect'':21B ''provid'':19B ''rate'':14B ''requir'':23B ''short'':17B ''signific'':8B ''skill'':26B ''spell'':6B', 'mage', 'Ironflesh is a spell that makes the caster’s skin as strong as iron for a while, offering much better protection from attacks. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dawnguard_shield', 'Dawnguard Shield has good protection quality. Its visual design is solid and reliable, featuring a round metal surface with leather bindings for a defensive look. It can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '''bind'':23B ''craft'':32B ''dawnguard'':1A,3B ''defens'':26B ''design'':11B ''featur'':16B ''good'':6B ''leather'':22B ''look'':27B ''metal'':19B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''reliabl'':15B ''round'':18B ''shield'':2A,4B ''solid'':13B ''steel'':39B ''surfac'':20B ''tempered/improved'':36B ''use'':38B ''visual'':10B ''workbench'':42B', 'blacksmith', 'Dawnguard Shield has good protection quality. Its visual design is solid and reliable, featuring a round metal surface with leather bindings for a defensive look. It can not be crafted. It can be tempered/improved by using steel at a workbench.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('the_sea_squall', 'The Sea Squall is a ship permanently docked in Dawnstar''s Northstar Port. Captain Wayfinder, a Nord owns the ship serves. Among the inhabitants of The Sea Squall are Guthrum, an aging Nord ranger who has made the ship his home, and Ravam Verethi, a Dark Elf.', '''age'':35B ''among'':25B ''captain'':17B ''dark'':49B ''dawnstar'':13B ''dock'':11B ''elf'':50B ''guthrum'':33B ''home'':44B ''inhabit'':27B ''made'':40B ''nord'':20B,36B ''northstar'':15B ''own'':21B ''perman'':10B ''port'':16B ''ranger'':37B ''ravam'':46B ''sea'':2A,5B,30B ''serv'':24B ''ship'':9B,23B,42B ''squall'':3A,6B,31B ''verethi'':47B ''wayfind'':18B', 'pale, sailor', 'The Sea Squall is a ship permanently docked in Dawnstar''s Northstar Port. You do not know who owns the ship.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, winterhold, whiterun, hjaalmarch', '', 'pale');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('college_of_winterhold', 'The College of Winterhold is a renowned school for magic located in the city of Winterhold, perched on a rocky outcrop, and reachable only by crossing a narrow stone bridge after the Great Collapse. Though it functions similarly to the Mages Guild, the College is an independent institution, separate from the Guild, and has a storied history dating back to the First Era. It is believed to have been founded by the legendary mage Shalidor, though this claim, like many others associated with him, is shrouded in mystery. The College boasts documents from as far back as the late Second Era and houses some of Tamriel''s most valuable arcane knowledge.

A selective institution, the College admits only those who prove their aptitude in the magical arts. Once enrolled, students enjoy greater freedom in their studies, including the practice of controversial magic such as Necromancy. The College''s central building, the Hall of the Elements, serves as the site for all types of magical practice and contains the famous Arcanaeum library. The Arch-Mage’s quarters are located within, while students and faculty are housed in separate accommodations. Beneath the College lies the Midden, a mysterious underground area that holds many of the College''s secrets. The Eye of Shalidor, a symbol of the institution, is displayed prominently across the campus, honoring the College''s ancient roots.

Notable residents of the College include the Arch-Mage Savos Aren, Master-Wizard Mirabelle Ervine, and various experts and trainers in different magical disciplines, including Faralda (Destruction), Tolfdir (Alteration), and Phinis Gestor (Conjuration). The College also hosts a range of followers, such as Brelyna Maryon and J''zargo, alongside other figures like Enthir, a general goods vendor, and the enigmatic Ancano, a Thalmor advisor.', '''accommod'':191B ''across'':222B ''admit'':120B ''advisor'':296B ''alongsid'':281B ''also'':268B ''alter'':261B ''ancano'':293B ''ancient'':229B ''aptitud'':126B ''arcan'':113B ''arcanaeum'':173B ''arch'':177B,239B ''arch-mag'':238B ''arch-mage’'':176B ''area'':201B ''aren'':242B ''art'':130B ''associ'':85B ''back'':62B,99B ''believ'':69B ''beneath'':192B ''boast'':94B ''brelyna'':276B ''bridg'':33B ''build'':153B ''campus'':224B ''central'':152B ''citi'':17B ''claim'':81B ''collaps'':37B ''colleg'':1A,5B,47B,93B,119B,150B,194B,207B,227B,235B,267B ''conjur'':265B ''contain'':170B ''controversi'':144B ''cross'':29B ''date'':61B ''destruct'':259B ''differ'':254B ''disciplin'':256B ''display'':220B ''document'':95B ''element'':158B ''enigmat'':292B ''enjoy'':134B ''enrol'':132B ''enthir'':285B ''era'':66B,104B ''ervin'':247B ''expert'':250B ''eye'':211B ''faculti'':186B ''famous'':172B ''far'':98B ''faralda'':258B ''figur'':283B ''first'':65B ''follow'':273B ''found'':73B ''freedom'':136B ''function'':40B ''general'':287B ''gestor'':264B ''good'':288B ''great'':36B ''greater'':135B ''guild'':45B,55B ''hall'':155B ''histori'':60B ''hold'':203B ''honor'':225B ''host'':269B ''hous'':106B,188B ''includ'':140B,236B,257B ''independ'':50B ''institut'':51B,117B,218B ''j'':279B ''knowledg'':114B ''late'':102B ''legendari'':76B ''librari'':174B ''lie'':195B ''like'':82B,284B ''locat'':14B,181B ''mage'':44B,77B,240B ''mage’'':178B ''magic'':13B,129B,145B,167B,255B ''mani'':83B,204B ''maryon'':277B ''master'':244B ''master-wizard'':243B ''midden'':197B ''mirabell'':246B ''mysteri'':91B,199B ''narrow'':31B ''necrom'':148B ''notabl'':231B ''other'':84B ''outcrop'':24B ''perch'':20B ''phini'':263B ''practic'':142B,168B ''promin'':221B ''prove'':124B ''quarter'':179B ''rang'':271B ''reachabl'':26B ''renown'':10B ''resid'':232B ''rocki'':23B ''root'':230B ''savo'':241B ''school'':11B ''second'':103B ''secret'':209B ''select'':116B ''separ'':52B,190B ''serv'':159B ''shalidor'':78B,213B ''shroud'':89B ''similar'':41B ''site'':162B ''stone'':32B ''stori'':59B ''student'':133B,184B ''studi'':139B ''symbol'':215B ''tamriel'':109B ''thalmor'':295B ''though'':38B,79B ''tolfdir'':260B ''trainer'':252B ''type'':165B ''underground'':200B ''valuabl'':112B ''various'':249B ''vendor'':289B ''winterhold'':3A,7B,19B ''within'':182B ''wizard'':245B ''zargo'':280B', 'collegeofwinterhold, scholar, mage', 'The College of Winterhold is a renowned school for magic located in the city of Winterhold, perched on a rocky outcrop, and reachable only by crossing a narrow stone bridge after the Great Collapse. Though it functions similarly to the Mages Guild, the College is an independent institution, separate from the Guild, and has a storied history dating back to the First Era. 

A selective institution, the College admits only those who prove their aptitude in the magical arts. 

You do not know anything else about this area.', '', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('nightshade_extract', 'Nightshade Extract is a subtle but deadly poison derived from the nightshade plant. It causes lingering harm and is often used in covert operations or rituals. Some claim to have obtained it from Wuunferth the Unliving or hidden caches in Windhelm.', '''cach'':41B ''caus'':17B ''claim'':30B ''covert'':25B ''dead'':9B ''deriv'':11B ''extract'':2A,4B ''harm'':19B ''hidden'':40B ''linger'':18B ''nightshad'':1A,3B,14B ''obtain'':33B ''often'':22B ''oper'':26B ''plant'':15B ''poison'':10B ''ritual'':28B ''subtl'':7B ''unliv'':38B ''use'':23B ''windhelm'':43B ''wuunferth'':36B', 'alchemist, darkelf, mage', 'You know this extract is associated with the poisonous nightshade plant and is occasionally linked to underhanded dealings in Windhelm.', '', '', 'items');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ice_spike', 'Ice Spike is a Destruction spell that launches a shard of ice at a target, dealing frost damage upon impact. It requires an Apprentice skill level to cast.', '''apprentic'':26B ''cast'':30B ''damag'':20B ''deal'':18B ''destruct'':7B ''frost'':19B ''ice'':1A,3B,14B ''impact'':22B ''launch'':10B ''level'':28B ''requir'':24B ''shard'':12B ''skill'':27B ''spell'':8B ''spike'':2A,4B ''target'':17B ''upon'':21B', 'mage', 'Ice Spike is a spell that hurls a sharp shard of ice at a target, dealing frost damage upon impact. You do not know much else about this spell.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('skeever', '
Skeevers are small, aggressive, rat-like creatures found in dark areas like caves or dungeons, as well as the wilderness of Skyrim. While they are generally considered weak enemies, they can carry the disease Ataxia, which reduces Lockpicking and Pickpocket skills.', '''aggress'':5B ''area'':13B ''ataxia'':37B ''carri'':34B ''cave'':15B ''consid'':29B ''creatur'':9B ''dark'':12B ''diseas'':36B ''dungeon'':17B ''enemi'':31B ''found'':10B ''general'':28B ''like'':8B,14B ''lockpick'':40B ''pickpocket'':42B ''rat'':7B ''rat-lik'':6B ''reduc'':39B ''skeever'':1A,2B ''skill'':43B ''skyrim'':24B ''small'':4B ''weak'':30B ''well'':19B ''wilder'':22B', 'hunter', 'Skeevers are small, aggressive, rat-like creatures found in dark areas like caves or dungeons, as well as the wilderness of Skyrim. ', '', '', 'creatures');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('a_dance_in_fire', 'A Dance in Fire, written by Waughin Jarth, is a seven-chapter compilation chronicling the misadventures of Decumus Scotti, a middling clerk from the Imperial City, as he navigates the political chaos and wild dangers of Valenwood. Following a dismissal from his stable position at the Atrius Building Commission, Scotti receives an ill-fated invitation from a former colleague, Liodes Jurus, to exploit post-war rebuilding opportunities in Valenwood. Through a series of increasingly perilous events—including encounters with mercenaries, natural disasters, predatory wildlife, and betrayals—Scotti stumbles his way through the Bosmer province, eventually landing an audience with the enigmatic Silvenar, the spiritual leader of Valenwood. The text explores themes of survival, greed, cultural misunderstanding, and the absurdity of imperial ambitions in a foreign land.

The book, divided into seven parts, combines a satirical critique of imperial bureaucracy with an adventurous narrative rich in cultural detail. Scotti’s journey mirrors the chaotic nature of Valenwood itself, with its dense jungles, mystical traditions, and ongoing conflicts with neighboring territories like Elsweyr and Summerset Isle. Despite his lack of skill or heroism, Scotti’s inadvertent cunning allows him to secure contracts that benefit himself and the Imperial Building Commission, albeit at the cost of moral compromise. The story also highlights the absurdities of colonialism, as outsiders profit from a war-torn province’s misfortunes while failing to understand or respect its people. Ultimately, Scotti returns to the Imperial City, only to find that his success comes with eerie consequences, leaving readers to ponder the price of ambition and the dissonance between civilized ideals and the savage reality of conquest.', '''absurd'':124B,214B ''adventur'':147B ''albeit'':202B ''allow'':189B ''also'':211B ''ambit'':127B,259B ''atrius'':52B ''audienc'':103B ''benefit'':195B ''betrayals—scotti'':92B ''book'':133B ''bosmer'':98B ''build'':53B,200B ''bureaucraci'':144B ''chao'':37B ''chaotic'':157B ''chapter'':17B ''chronicl'':19B ''citi'':31B,241B ''civil'':264B ''clerk'':27B ''colleagu'':65B ''coloni'':216B ''combin'':138B ''come'':248B ''commiss'':54B,201B ''compil'':18B ''compromis'':208B ''conflict'':170B ''conquest'':271B ''consequ'':251B ''contract'':193B ''cost'':205B ''critiqu'':141B ''cultur'':120B,151B ''cun'':188B ''danc'':2A,6B ''danger'':40B ''decumus'':23B ''dens'':164B ''despit'':179B ''detail'':152B ''disast'':88B ''dismiss'':45B ''disson'':262B ''divid'':134B ''eeri'':250B ''elsweyr'':175B ''encount'':84B ''enigmat'':106B ''events—includ'':83B ''eventu'':100B ''exploit'':69B ''explor'':115B ''fail'':228B ''fate'':60B ''find'':244B ''fire'':4A,8B ''follow'':43B ''foreign'':130B ''former'':64B ''greed'':119B ''heroism'':185B ''highlight'':212B ''