A Dance in Fire, you do not know the author of the book and have limited knowledge of it, is a satirical adventure chronicling the misadventures of Decumus Scotti, an Imperial clerk, as he navigates the political chaos and dangers of Valenwood. The book explores themes of survival, greed, imperialism, and cultural misunderstanding, critiquing bureaucracy and the absurdity of colonial ambitions in a foreign land.', '', '', 'lore');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('forsworn_arrow', 'Forsworn Arrow is an arrow that deals good damage. 
Its visual design is rough and tribal, with a wooden shaft, a chipped stone tip, and uneven feather fletching bound with sinew. It can not be crafted, but found on the Forsworn in the reach.', '''arrow'':2A,4B,7B ''bound'':31B ''chip'':24B ''craft'':38B ''damag'':11B ''deal'':9B ''design'':14B ''feather'':29B ''fletch'':30B ''forsworn'':1A,3B,43B ''found'':40B ''good'':10B ''reach'':46B ''rough'':16B ''shaft'':22B ''sinew'':33B ''stone'':25B ''tip'':26B ''tribal'':18B ''uneven'':28B ''visual'':13B ''wooden'':21B', 'blacksmith', 'Forsworn Arrow is an arrow that deals good damage. 
Its visual design is rough and tribal, with a wooden shaft, a chipped stone tip, and uneven feather fletching bound with sinew. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('dwarven_sword', 'Dwarven Sword is a basic dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. To craft it: 1 dwarven metal ingot, 1 steel ingot, 1 iron ingot, and 1 leather strip at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it. It can be tempered/improved by using dwarvern ingot at a workbench.', '''1'':34B,38B,41B,45B ''adept'':53B ''angular'':18B ''basic'':7B ''blacksmith'':50B ''bronz'':25B ''craft'':32B,56B ''damag'':13B ''deal'':11B ''design'':16B ''dwarven'':1A,3B,8B,35B ''dwarvern'':64B ''finish'':26B ''forg'':51B ''golden'':24B ''golden-bronz'':23B ''good'':12B ''ingot'':37B,40B,43B,65B ''intric'':28B ''iron'':42B ''leather'':46B ''mechan'':29B ''metal'':36B ''ornat'':20B ''pattern'':30B ''smith'':54B ''steel'':39B ''strip'':47B ''sword'':2A,4B ''tempered/improved'':61B ''use'':63B ''visual'':15B ''weapon'':9B ''workbench'':68B', 'blacksmith', 'Dwarven Sword is a basic dwarven weapon which deals good damage. Its visual design is angular and ornate, with a golden-bronze finish and intricate mechanical patterns. You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('drain_vitality', 'Drain Vitality is a Shout that siphons both magical and mortal energies from your opponent, weakening them. The three words of power in this Shout are Gaan (Stamina), which drains the target''s stamina; Lah (Magicka), which saps their magical energy; and Haas (Health), which steals their life force, leaving them weaker and more vulnerable.', '''drain'':1A,3B,32B ''energi'':14B,43B ''forc'':51B ''gaan'':29B ''haa'':45B ''health'':46B ''lah'':37B ''leav'':52B ''life'':50B ''magic'':11B,42B ''magicka'':38B ''mortal'':13B ''oppon'':17B ''power'':24B ''sap'':40B ''shout'':7B,27B ''siphon'':9B ''stamina'':30B,36B ''steal'':48B ''target'':34B ''three'':21B ''vital'':2A,4B ''vulner'':57B ''weaken'':18B ''weaker'':54B ''word'':22B', 'dragon', 'This is a Dragon Shout. You do not know much about Dragon shouts, or their language.', '', '', 'spells');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('hela''s_folly', 'Hela''s Folly is a shipwreck located northeast of Dawnstar, in the Winterhold region, and northwest of The Tower Stone. The wreck lies along the rugged coast, adding to the eerie and desolate landscape of the area. The ship''s remains are a stark reminder of the dangerous waters off Skyrim''s northern coast. There are rumors of an Argonian who have taken refugee there.', '''ad'':31B ''along'':27B ''area'':40B ''argonian'':63B ''coast'':30B,57B ''danger'':51B ''dawnstar'':13B ''desol'':36B ''eeri'':34B ''folli'':3A,6B ''hela'':1A,4B ''landscap'':37B ''lie'':26B ''locat'':10B ''northeast'':11B ''northern'':56B ''northwest'':19B ''refuge'':67B ''region'':17B ''remain'':44B ''remind'':48B ''rug'':29B ''rumor'':60B ''ship'':42B ''shipwreck'':9B ''skyrim'':54B ''stark'':47B ''stone'':23B ''taken'':66B ''tower'':22B ''water'':52B ''winterhold'':16B ''wreck'':25B', 'winterhold', 'Hela''s Folly is a shipwreck located northeast of Dawnstar, in the Winterhold region.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, pale, eastmarch', '', 'winterhold');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('elven_gauntlets', 'Elven Gauntlets have good protection quality. To craft it: 1 refined moonstone, 1 iron ingot, 1 leather, and 2 leather strips at a blacksmith forge. An Adept smith can craft it.An Adept smith can craft it.It can be tempered/improved by using moonstone at a workbench.', '''1'':12B,15B,18B ''2'':21B ''adept'':29B,34B ''blacksmith'':26B ''craft'':10B,32B,37B ''elven'':1A,3B ''forg'':27B ''gauntlet'':2A,4B ''good'':6B ''ingot'':17B ''iron'':16B ''it.an'':33B ''it.it'':38B ''leather'':19B,22B ''moonston'':14B,44B ''protect'':7B ''qualiti'':8B ''refin'':13B ''smith'':30B,35B ''strip'':23B ''tempered/improved'':41B ''use'':43B ''workbench'':47B', 'blacksmith', 'Elven Gauntlets have good protection quality.You do not know how to craft it, but a blacksmith would.', '', '', 'equipment');
INSERT INTO public.oghma VALUES ('ruunvald', 'Ruunvald Excavation is a medium-sized cave east of Shor''s Stone and northeast of Fort Greenwall, nestled high in the eastern mountains. It is rumoured that it was established by Vigilants of Stendarr led by Moric Sidrey.', '''cave'':9B ''east'':10B ''eastern'':24B ''establish'':32B ''excav'':3B ''fort'':18B ''greenwal'':19B ''high'':21B ''led'':37B ''medium'':7B ''medium-s'':6B ''moric'':39B ''mountain'':25B ''nestl'':20B ''northeast'':16B ''rumour'':28B ''ruunvald'':1A,2B ''shor'':12B ''sidrey'':40B ''size'':8B ''stendarr'':36B ''stone'':14B ''vigil'':34B', 'rift', 'Ruunvald Excavation is a medium-sized cave east of Shor''s Stone and northeast of Fort Greenwall.You do not know anything else about this area.', 'skyrimall, eastmarch, falkreath', '', 'rift');
